{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000488W1', 'answerTime': 'Oct 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413788400, 'question': "I have a tot lok in my kitchen. I have loved it for years but today the magnet won't open the lock. What could be wrong and what can I do to open it", 'answer': 'Chance are there is a little pressure on door due to misalignment or loose hinges. Push in on door while positioning magnet, I am sure this will work. Once door open adjust hinges fully to tighten closing of door.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000488W1', 'answerTime': 'Sep 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409554800, 'question': 'How long are the screws that attach to the door? I am interested in putting this on china cabinet doors - which are a little thinner.', 'answer': "They aren't super long, but long enough to secure it. I heave it installed on a medicine cabinet which is about a quarter thick. They almost penetrated, but didn't. I also might have over tightened. You could very easily get the same type of screws at a very low cost (0.10 cents) at a hardware store. I used to work at one. :-P new I heave ordered two sets now. I love having the hidden lock. I do recommend ordering a backup key though."}
