{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000488W1', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362211200, 'question': 'Would these locks work with a lazy susan cabinet?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'They might, but I doubt it. You would have to put one on both asides of the cabinet and it would depend on the size of the gap between the cabinate face and the side. I also have lazy Susan cabinets and I was never successful in child proofing them :('}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000488W1', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2012', 'unixTime': 1356508800, 'question': 'European cabinets: Does anyone know if the Tot Loks will work on European style cabinets?', 'answer': 'Yes - we installed them onto our Ikea cabinets. For the cabinet doors without a top bar, we just installed the lock sideways and put the catch on the sidewall. For doors that came together in the middle - well, we had a center bar at the top that the doors closed against that was too narrow to afix the catch to, so I just used that piece as a catch. I can send pics if you want. They work just fine, though.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000488W2', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383724800, 'question': 'Will this keep a strong 6 year old out of my cabinets? He has special needs and feels that he can open my cabinets and dump whatever on the floor. I am looking for something that would prevent him to get in my cabinets.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, the locks will keep adults out too. My huband installed the locks and, as other reviewers stated, they can be a pain to install. Very important to remember: KEEP TRACK OF THE MAGNETIC KEY!!! Or, buy an extra one. We found out that our key did work even though it was melted a little (was left on top of hot stove for a few minutes). All-in-all, I believe these locks were well worth the money.'}
