{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00004RA66', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374476400, 'question': 'Hey! I have this play yard for my son. We have it in a rectangle. Any recommendations on securing it? He pulls one side almost all the way down!', 'answer': "It isn't easy to secure but this is what I've done: Put the lower circular connectors on top of one another so they are together. The top parts then go together by pushing the part that sticks up into the groove on the edge of the other side. They then are locked in place."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00004RA66', 'answerTime': 'Jan 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357372800, 'question': 'Instead of buying the 2-panel extension kit, could I purchase another 6-panel set and attach it to the 6-panel set I already have?', 'answer': "Yes, that's what we did... just orient the panels correctly and there is no end to how many 6-panel sets you can attach; it's better to have a few spare panels anyway in case you want to modify the play-yard. Another tip: We recommend that you angle the corners where the panels meet (sort of like in the main product photo), so it is more stable... keeping multiply connected panels in a straight position is not as stable and will bend when baby leans on it; an alternative is to fasten the panels to wall and/or floor."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00004RA66', 'answerTime': 'Jul 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375081200, 'question': 'Can this gate attach to the wall.Do I purchase suction cups or does it have to drill holders into wall?thank you', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Mine did not come with hardware to attach to a wall, and when I looked at it closely, it might be hard to attach a bracket to do that. We have used velcro straps to connect ours to a couple of different things (railings, a piece of furniture) but it isn't really designed for that."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00004RA66', 'answerTime': 'Dec 16, 2012', 'unixTime': 1355644800, 'question': 'May I know the width of each panel in inches please?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The width of each panel is 30 1/2 " across the top edge. If you include the hinge circle (which is part of each section) it measures 32 1/2".'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00004RA66', 'answerTime': 'Nov 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417248000, 'question': 'how long is it stretched out?', 'answer': 'Each of the six panels is about 31"; each of the six movable joints is about 2". The total length of this durable playgate is about 198" or 16\' 5".'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00004RA66', 'answerTime': '3 days ago', 'question': 'I would like to create an L shaped gate to enclose a corner so it makes an enclosed square space for a play area. Will the gate be sturdy in an L?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't believe it would be sturdy on its own in an L shape. However, if you can attach both ends to something, it will be fine. I have done something similar to create a play space and it works because we've been able to stabilize both ends to other furniture."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00004RA66', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422518400, 'question': "Can you take the individual panels apart? I'd like to use 3 panels to set up in the door frame of one door to block access for my 15 month old.Thanks!", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Just go to http://www.amazon.com/North-States-Industries-Superyard-Colorplay/dp/B006NTY1HK/ref=sr_1_3?ie=UTF8&qid=1422571149&sr=8-3&keywords=north+states+baby+play+yard and click on the photo that\'s listed as a video. It clearly explains and demonstrates how to separate the panels. Not user that I wold use a section of the pen to block a door for an 18 month old though. They are not very sturdy as freestanding panels, and a toddler could easily knock them over. You\'d be better off with a product designed to specifically to block a door. There are lots of them out there...get one that is pressure mounted if you don\'t want to mar your walls or mess with screws. I have a nice one made by "Summer" that is quite secure when it\'s installed according to the directions, and it automatically swings shut and latches. Much safer for a toddler and I\'m pretty sure I got it here on Amazon too....'}
