{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000056B86', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388217600, 'question': 'will this car seat fit on top of a bike rack that is permantly attached to the back of a beach cruiser?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'According to mfg spec sheet It should fit most 26"-27" bicycles. However, it hangs from seat post by u- bracket (And because of that is not recommended for bicycles with rear suspension on seatpost) and attaches to two seat supports to the rear fork of the bicycle. I could never install this seat to my mountain bike due to rear forks design are not parallel to the centerline of the bicycle nor parallel to the ground and sort of bow out. It made attaching supports to rear forks difficult. Due to my rear fork design and my rear post suspension design I bought a product that I have never used nor installed. It\'s in the box in my garage. If you can spend the money go for one with the rear carriage design and pull it behind.'}
