{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000056C86', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': 'is there any weight and height limit how high is it from bottom of pen to top and is there a weight limit or age limit for baby?', 'answer': "That question is best directed to Graco -- or Babies R Us who has several floor models by Graco. When our child was two he could see over the railing with his chin at the railing. There probably is a weight limit but it is a sturdy pack n' play with a metal foot base and a thin chipboard floor system that fits snugly in the bottom. Call Graco. Or, test out floor samples at Babies R Us if you have one nearby before purchasing from Amazon. (Usually the only difference is the shape -- square or rectangular.)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000056C86', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Hi! Would this be safe as a temporary crib for an infant for a few months? Looks like the ideal one for infant to tall-toddler transition! Thnx!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It is so colorful and cheery I don't know if it would be conducive to fall asleep in. Plus you would want a thicker mattress pad and I don't know if that size is available. It is a great playpen and somewhere to put the baby when you can't constantly watch it. My grandchild sleeps in a regular size pack and play and I read reviews to find out which mattress pad works in it and also bought the sheets for it. I would think in any pack and play you would want to add a mattress on top of the padding they give you if you plan to sleep the baby in it."}
