{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000056J76', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': 'Did anyone use this seat from the very beginning of potty training or is it better to get the full potty chair version first and transition to this?', 'answer': "It really depends on your kid. My son was afraid of the big potty when he started potty training, so we used the baby Bjorn potty chair to get him started, then transitioned to this seat on the toilet. If your child is not scared of the toilet then I think they would be OK just using the seat. It's definitely secure enough for little ones to use without falling in. I would recommend staying right beside them while they use it until they are used to balancing on the toilet though, because they could still fall off to the side or the front."}
