{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000056JC1', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371711600, 'question': 'Would this work to reduce heartburn from pregnancy?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No, I doubt it would help you at all with your acid reflux. I'd go get myself two pieces of solid boards nailed together (or glued, I suppose) to reach your needed height to keep the acid in your pushed up belly and out of your esophagus. Check with your Dr. but I'd guess between 8 inches and 12 inches should so it. Just have someone lift the top portion of your bed frame and legs and place the board squarely under each top leg. This will pitch your upper body enough for you to get some relief but not 'realize' you are lying at an angle. I tried this pillow for my own reflux and it didn't work, so I asked my husband to go find me two cinder blocks and viola! done! You will slide off of the pillow and will end up right back to flat and reflux waking you up. I use my wedge now in the car, I'm short and it gives me the little lift to see better over the front of my car. Good luck, happy birthing."}
