{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000056OUX', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395730800, 'question': 'Would this product work for (townhome) railing going up the stairs to a second level, a gap in the bannister, and then stairs to a third level?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "hard to say for sure, but it might? It would take some manipulation so possibly some gapping when you're trying to over a new plane. We have ours wrapped around a top banister in an L-shaped fashion and it works great. But we also don't have a kid that tests limits at all. She knows to steer clear of the mesh and it's primarily there to catch any falls or missteps. It can be easily bent or fussed with if you had a really persistent little one."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000056OUX', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387267200, 'question': "Would purchasing one be enough to go around a small third floor apartment balcony, or would I need two or more? I have a 6 month old chihuhua, that I don't want to fit in between the balcony rails.", 'answer': 'If it is a smaller balcony it should be fine with just one.'}
