{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000058CC7', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378969200, 'question': 'Anyone know why this gate is not recommended for top of stairs?', 'answer': "Any gate mounted above stairs needs to be hardware-mounted. This pressure-mounted one eventually can wiggle loose, especially if the surfaces it's pushing up against for mounting are not completely square horizontally. More than once we have stepped to open it and the whole thing dislodged, and we hadn't realized it was that loose."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000058CC7', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392019200, 'question': 'Is it good for stairs?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Gate can only be used at the BOTTOM of a staircase as long as you can securely attach on both sides of the stair case and keep the gate firmly closed. It should never be used at the top of a staircase and we do not use on a staircase in our house - only doorways. I suggest you research further with the manufacturer to see what they recommend. You can contact them @ Tomy International 1-800-704-8697. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000058CC7', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389686400, 'question': 'Would this fit a 35 inch opening? is the extension needed?', 'answer': 'I had my husband measure the gate with the extension screws pulled completely out and it measured 36 1/2 inches. We have ours on a regular bedroom doorway so it may or may not fit on a 35 inch opening.'}
