{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000058CC7', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395212400, 'question': "Has anyone's baby figured out how to open it herself? It looks like it'd be pretty easy for a baby to figure out, not different than a pop-up toy.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'it takes a good hard press on the foot release to get it to open-more that even a child could do! just wondered if it gets easier with age!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000058CC7', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427698800, 'question': 'Anyone know if I can buy replacement screws and stoppers?', 'answer': 'Hello, thank you for your question on the Hands Free Gate. Our customer service department has many replacement parts for our products available. Please contact 800-704-8697 as they may be able to help you with these parts.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000058CC7', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417593600, 'question': 'Do you have to drill holes in your wall to install this?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No you do not. It is secure in place with pressure, you can adjust screws to the rubber ends (that will press against your door frame) for a tight fit. We have had ours in place well over a year, and it is the absolute most sturdy baby gate we have ever had. I am bummed we didn't find it sooner, it would have been a much greater investment than some of the others we purchased. It takes your entire bodyweight to release, so very secure (and not even a lightweight child could open)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000058CC7', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417593600, 'question': 'Question - is it possible to keep this open wide open if I want, or does it have a spring to auto close the gate?', 'answer': "You can leave it open, just like a regular door. We leave ours open all day, then close it when we're home with the baby."}
