{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00005BTNA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421654400, 'question': 'Can these store (expressed) milk in the fridge for a week? Or do the vents on the bottom mean that air gets in and spoils the milk/the milk leaks out?', 'answer': "Well, it will not be hermetically sealed. There always will be some air in the bottle. I think you would be better of with some other containers. A day or two I would say yes. No, they won't leak. Just don't use a bottle warmer because they will leak. Annoying I know. My baby is 8 months and it's the only bottle I use and I only own one! It's easy to clean and assemble. The angle is cool. They only down side is that you can't heat the liquid in the bottle."}
