{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00005JIVI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394607600, 'question': 'Does baby get cold, I am wondering how is he in the water, do you fill the tub or sink up to where it covers his belly and is his head elevated?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I wouldn't recommend this for a sink. The bather soaks up water. The head end is fluffier than the seat end. The seat fills with water. Most of the baby's torso is out of the water. I keep a cup and wash cloth in the bath to keep baby warm. Also don't get their hair or head wet till the very end. Also have a baby bath thermometer. You would be surprised at how warm the normal temp. Should be."}
