{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00005JIVI', 'answerTime': 'Jul 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404284400, 'question': 'Opinions on using this in a standard 14x16 kitchen sink? Looks like the side will bend up to fit? Is it comfy/functional?', 'answer': 'It is very flexible and can be forced into an area that size but greatly reduces area for baby to lay. My recommendation is to us it in you bathtub with only about an inch of warm water in bottom of tub. Push up and down on the bath pad so it absorbs the warm water and your baby will be warmed by it. Just be sure to fold up a towel or rug for under your knees (beside the tub) so mom can be comfy too!'}
