{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000088KGZ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424592000, 'question': 'Mine only shows celsius. Is there a way to change it to fahrenheit? Thank you!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, i'm assuming there is because mine shows Fahrenheit, But it has since I got it. It works great for us. We love it"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000088KGZ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'Does this measures in Celsius grades too?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'yes both'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000088KGZ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'How accurate is this thermometer? To 2/10 or 1/10 of a degree or something else?', 'answer': 'thermometer was accurate and quick but stop working after 3 months!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'Nov 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384848000, 'question': 'Is this treated with flame retardant chemicals?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It appears that they are not. Here is a link to a blog where someone wrote and asked them: ladyplusbaby.com/?tag=halo-response-about-fire-retardant ...it\'s on the ladyplusbaby website and is a post tagged "halo-response-about-fire-retardant"...in case the weblink is blocked. On that page is posted these emails from Halo: Randall, Polyester is a natural flame retardant fabric; therefore all our fleece and comfort mesh items pass the standards with out flame retardant chemicals. Our cotton sleepsacks are made without the chemicals but can only pass the standards in the smaller sizes. This is the reason they are only made in these sizes. The flame resistance standards for children\'s sleepwear gets stricter as the sizes get larger. This is due to the mobility of the child increasing with size. If you have any other questions, please let us know. Christy Halo Innovations Customer Service ---------------------------------------------- Hello Randall, We do not use any flame resistance chemicals on any of our items. They pass the minimum standards for flame resistance without the use of chemicals. The standards are different based upon the size and mobility of the child therefore, the standards for larger or older children are more strict than for infants. This is why some of our products are only available in certain sizes. There are different CPSC levels of FR standards. The SleepSack wearable blanket falls into category 1610 which is for bedding categories. IF we were in a pajama category which is 1615 then the cotton SleepSacks would not pass without treatment. If you would like to learn more about this please visit the CPSC web site. http://www.cpsc.gov/ Regards, Karen Customer Service Halo Innovations Also on the Halosleep FAQ page, they say they are not chemically treated also. Hope that helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396335600, 'question': 'anyone have a tummy sleeper? does the zipper dig into their bodies if they sleep on their tummy?', 'answer': "I don't have a tummy sleeper, but if the zipper is zipped up, the pull is at the very bottom of the sack, probably lower than the feet unless the bag is really small for your baby. At that location, I don't think your baby will have a lot of weight to put on the zipper pull (and causing the dig). As for the zipper itself, it is pretty flat so I don't think it will be a problem. Just a reminder that if your baby is less than 6 month old, he or she should be sleeping on the back all the time to reduce the chance of SIDS."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395644400, 'question': 'Hi! Would this be considered the "summer weight" sleep sac option? Or would this be too thick for the summer?', 'answer': "I plan to use ours in the summer, with onesies underneath. :) I wouldn't consider it too thick."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'Jul 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405407600, 'question': 'What is the Tog rating for this sack?', 'answer': 'according to their website, the 100% cotton sleepsack has a tog rating of 0.5'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417075200, 'question': 'My granddaughter sleeps better with her arms and body swaddled but she is outgrowing her swaddles. Could I zip up this sack with her arms inside?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Technically yes but this sleep sack is loose so her arms would be free to move and likely tangled in the arm holes. I wouldn't recommend it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428908400, 'question': 'How many inches long is the size x large from shoulders to bottom?', 'answer': 'I can\'t get to the sack to measure right now, but I can tell you even in cold water wash and dried on low heat, it has shrunk a lot. My son\'s feet now hit the end of the cotton XL sleepsack and he\'s a total of 33-34ish inches tall. The Fleece version in XL still fits him with room but the cotton ones shrink so much! Too bad... I was hoping to get another cotton one for this spring/summer season but looks like he\'ll be "graduating" early.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 17, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426575600, 'question': 'Does this allow babies to roll over? My little one is 7 months and rolls himself over before sleeping.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes it does. It moves as the baby moves and it's comfortable for them and makes them feel secure. My 20 month old still uses it every now and then when all his pajamas are in the dirty laundry. And he sleeps 10.5-11hrs. Hope that helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425456000, 'question': 'Is there much of a difference between the L and XL besides length? If I put my M size baby in a L or XL would there be a problem?', 'answer': 'XL is definitely bigger, but I have always gone a size up on these because my baby is VERY tall for her height.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00008KWO2', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'Does anyone know the length of the different sizes?', 'answer': "Here is the link to the website's chart. It has the length measurements on it. http://www.halosleep.com/size-chart/"}
