{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420272000, 'question': 'Will it remove raspberry seeds?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Not very well. I made raspberry jam with it last month and found a lot of seeds got through the finest disc. I had to put the puree through a wire mesh sieve after the food mill. But - I did not heat them first and realize now I should have; it may have helped. The smallest screen though, has holes that the seeds can fit through.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'Jul 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404284400, 'question': 'I just received the food mill, and it has no instructions with it. How do I use the food mill and for what fruits and vegetables?', 'answer': 'Hi, simply put sliced up fruit in in the mill, I do no more than half full, and turn so fruit goes under blade. Occasionally you will have to turn backwards to allow room for skins, etc to become dislodged. After that batch is done, empty out skins and repeat until finished. I use fruits like peaches, apples, ones that are solid in nature. usually you will need to soften them by cooking in water until they are soft enough to press through sieve. If you use vegetables, cook them first. Tomatoes, you can just slice, and use course plate to process. I use the course one for apple sauce, but use your preference. Hope this helps.. You can also research on the internet, and see if there are some more ideas. This mill is great for baby food..'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'Feb 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424246400, 'question': "How many quart is this item's capacity? What is the hole size of three Stainless Disks? Made in China?", 'answer': "It is big, I'd say 4 quarts. I'm not where my food mill is, so I have to estimate. Pore size of the three disks is baby food, applesauce, and raw cranberry salad or deseeding size, if that helps. I don't remember where it is made. This is by far the nicest food mill I have ever had. I have worn out two regulation food mills but this one will last longer than me! Hope this helps you&#128038;"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'Oct 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414306800, 'question': 'Has anyone used this to pulp persimmons?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No. I couldn't imagine why it wouldn't work it works perfect for tomatoes. I think it would be fine if you're looking for a persimmons puree"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410246000, 'question': 'what is the capacity of this one? 2 quart?', 'answer': "It doesn't say anywhere maybe a pint"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'Jul 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404284400, 'question': 'I just received the food mill, and it has no instructions with it. How do I use the food mill and for what fruits and vegetables?', 'answer': 'I used it to make potato dumplings. I boiled some white potatoes, cut them into disks, and ran them through the food mill to mix with flour. I formed the potato/flour mixture into dumplings.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'May 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400828400, 'question': "I received this mill as a gift from my son. I assembled it but the handle is difficult to turn. What should I do? I can't use it.", 'answer': 'Mine works very well. Are you sure you have it assembled properly? Be sure the grate is snuggly in place (Raised side up) and the piece that is spring loaded needs to be in in tight.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': 'Do you know if the two discs shown here in the picture are the large and medium holes or the medium and fine ones?', 'answer': "David, they are the large and medium. Works great in qty's of 1 quart."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387094400, 'question': 'Would this be good as a baby food grinder?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This will puree foods very finely. It has three levels of mesh. When I make potatoes with it they are very smooth. It will also leave any peel in the container, it won't go through the mesh. Hope that helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000CFH1K', 'answerTime': 'May 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400742000, 'question': 'What size holes are in each disc?', 'answer': 'The small disc has holes approx. 1/16 of an inch, the medium has holes approx. 1/8 of an inch, large has approx. 1/4 inch holes. The small disc I usually use for egg salad because it is very fine. The medium I usually use for tomatoes and mashed potatoes. The large is used for a salsa where you would want chunks. Hope this helps'}
