{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Sep 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378278000, 'question': 'How tall is this gate? I see one description that liss it at 30" and one that lists it at 11". Help!', 'answer': 'It would be 30". It is really nice. You can attach to an opening and swing it or use the tension option which would be removing the whole thing when passing through. I bought two.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389513600, 'question': 'Is the gate easily opened with ONE hand from top of stairs when holding a baby in the other hand?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes, its very easy to open one handed. You shouldn't have any problem doing so."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388476800, 'question': 'Does this gate swing open and close if pressure mounted? Also, If I hardware mount this gate, can I purchase additional hardware?', 'answer': "In order for it to swing open you have to hardware mount it on the hinge side. The other side can still use the 'pressure' to secure it in place. The gate can be removed completely even if you hardware mount it. The hardware will stay screwed into your frame or wall. You would have to do a search or contact the company for additional hardware."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392969600, 'question': 'Is there somewhere I can buy an extra installation kit for this specific gate so I can hard mount it in multiple places and only have to move gate?', 'answer': 'I have no idea. Maybe contact the First Years manufacturer directly?'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'At top of the stairs, does the hinge mount on the left or right and allow the gate to swing toward you and not over stairs?', 'answer': "You can mount over right or left. That doesn't matter. But you cannot restrict the swing of the door. It swing both in and out."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398582000, 'question': 'Will this gate work with baseboards? The doorway is 30 inches wide at the baseboards, and 32 inches wide at the wall above the baseboards.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "it depends on how you're going to use it. If you'll use the pressure option, yes, you can just mount it higher. If you're planning on mounting it to the wall, you'll need to cut part of the baseboard."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'May 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400655600, 'question': 'If this is hardware mounted in a door frame can the door still be closed?', 'answer': 'I guess it depends on the door frame. It would work with mine.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387094400, 'question': 'Will this gate swing open or just slide?', 'answer': 'We have it hard mounted and it will swing.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Jul 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374130800, 'question': "How wide of an opening will this gate fit? I can't seem to find that anywhere in the description, unless I'm looking right over it!", 'answer': 'I found that info under product information, it goes from 27-1/2" to 42-1/2" wide'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DBHHR', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386662400, 'question': "Would this work between a wall with a tall baseboard and a stair banister? Grandparents here! Don't need all the time!", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "There is an option to pressure mount the gate between two walls. I can't remember if the manual provided an option to install when one side is a banister but I believe as long as there is a flat surface on the banister I don't see why not. I do remember reading in the manual that pressure mounting is only OK for the bottom of a stairs (never for the top). Hope this helps. I have two of these installed to swing open. The top of the stairs had a tall baseboard so I had to install a little higher than the bottom. The gap was not too wide so this was OK. The gap between floor and bottom of the gate should not be wide enough for the little tike to fit body parts through."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416643200, 'question': 'what is this "Ships in certified frustration free packaging"', 'answer': 'upon opening you will not be frustrated'}
