{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386057600, 'question': 'toddler', 'answer': 'Most toddlers I would say yes. My Great Granddaughter, she is 28 months, loves it because she sits up to the table with her parents and eats with them right off the supper table. She does not use the tray.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': 'Jul 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406703600, 'question': 'Would you need a separate high chair for a baby or can you just use this chair?', 'answer': "Yeah, I wouldn't want to put an infant in this seat. Maybe by the time they're a year old it might be different but there's no padding or head support, so I would definitely get something separate for a baby. I used the Fisher Price Space Saver high chair when my little one was really little."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': 'Aug 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408345200, 'question': 'Is the red &amp; white one, truly red or more burgundy like the picture online looks?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think it looks a little more red in person than than the picture but it's definitely not bright red."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416902400, 'question': 'is this ok for a small 2 year old?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': 'Dec 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386921600, 'question': 'Can you set it on the floor, place the baby (who can sit upright) in it and use it for playtime? We would be sitting right next to baby.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Absolutely! This low chair is super safe and the only thing about being on the floor would be tipping over if there was a great force like a pet or another child. It would be safe especially with an adult sitting next to child in the chair. Oh, and because it has the options of three tabletops it is ideal for playing before the child independently is sitting! It's a great product, we love it; mostly for getting our family dinner established young even though our little one is just beginning to eat solids. He sits with us at the table most evenings."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411801200, 'question': 'where is it made from?', 'answer': 'Mine is made in Mexico.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': '10 days ago', 'question': 'at what size does your child "out grow" being able to use the plastic tray?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hmmmm ..... all I can say is our oldest grandchild is 32 months and the tray still works great. Youngest is 14 months, works great for him too.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW8N', 'answerTime': 'Aug 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407826800, 'question': 'Would it be OK to use it outside? On a deck table / chair? Will it be OK to get wet, etc?', 'answer': "Yes, it would work very well outdoors. It's all plastic and the straps are nylon. It's very portable so can be taken indoors quickly and easily also. Would pack well for camping also. I love it!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'Jun 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371970800, 'question': 'what is the measurement of the spaces between the bars?', 'answer': 'It is 3in between each bar.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': "Does anyone have pictures of this gate with the wall-mounted hardware? I don't see how it can work with the pressure mounted clip on the end. thank yo", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I have the "Summer Multi-Use Deco Extra Tall Walk-Thru Gate, Bronze", which is essentially a prior model of this gate. The hardware mount is simply a plastic cup about two inches diameter and 1/4" thick, with a hole in the center for passing a screw into the drywall. The gate still mounts with pressure using the same pressure pads when using the hardware mount, they just sit inside the plastic cups which provide some extra security by prevent the gate from slowly scooting along the wall over time. The wall (or whatever you\'re attaching to) still needs to be strong enough to support the pressure (which is substantial). Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'May 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400655600, 'question': 'Can we get extra extenstions for this gate ? I have this item but the opening I need to close is almost 6 1/2 - 7 feet', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I would not recommend it. I have two of these and have used both bigger extensions on one of the gates. Its a little shaky at the joints. There are longer gates.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426748400, 'question': 'Does anyone know if/where you can get replacement parts? All I need is the adhesive pads and the circles.', 'answer': "Had a hard time finding them myself. Here's the site that I found but they only sell the whole kit. http://www.summerinfant.com/hardwarekit0706007970"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'May 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367996400, 'question': 'with pets', 'answer': 'The gate works just fine with our cat and dog. Our dog is smaller, Jack Russell Terrier, and she cannot get through the slots. The cat can jump over, but does not.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'Mar 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426489200, 'question': 'Does this gate lock at the bottom as well?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it does. It auto locks at the bottom, and you lift it to release as you open it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'Oct 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413788400, 'question': 'Can this gate be used for the top of the stairs? It seems like it would be easy to trip over the bottom mount.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I would not recommend it for the top of the stairs. A gate whereby one side is secured to a wall and not pressure mounted would be safer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407913200, 'question': "I can't get the gate to lock on its own when it closes? I have to physically close it so it latches. Is there a setting to force it to auto lock?", 'answer': "if the gate is a little bit twisted it doesn't close on its own. look very closely from different angles, may need some tweaking on the install. good luck"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'Jul 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404716400, 'question': 'Will this gate work if one side is a stair rail? Is there an adapter?', 'answer': 'Not sure, sorry. We use it at the top of our stairs and it works great! We just place it one step down and it works nice. If you put it one stair down it should go under the railing as did ours.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000DEW91', 'answerTime': 'Jul 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404889200, 'question': 'Are there any gy spindle adapters for this gate?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'According to one of the answered questions, it looks like you could use the KidCo adapters at http://www.amazon.com/Spindle-Gate-Installation-Pack-KidCo/dp/B000GEAKNM/ref=cm_cd_al_qh_dp_t. The manufacturer recommends a maximum of two and only on one side. If the bottom is rectangular then you could get by with a standard pressure pad.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000E2DIE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402383600, 'question': 'How does this mount?', 'answer': 'You need to screw it into the wall/banister at the ends (pays were included I believe). It attached to the banister with zip ties (also included).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000E2DIE', 'answerTime': 'Apr 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396854000, 'question': 'How sturdy is the sheeting? For example, if a dog or cat paws at the installed sheet with any insistence, would it puncture and tear?', 'answer': "I don't think an animal could puncture it. It might get scratched and not look great. It is pretty strong."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000E2DIE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427266800, 'question': 'In one place this ad says the sheet is 3 ft. (36 inches) wide and in another 33 inches. Would someone be kind enough to verify the width?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Well at least for the one I have it was 36" wide. I would assume that they are all the same width otherwise it\'d just be a weird product design.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000E2DIE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425884400, 'question': "Would this work on an all wrought iron banister / it's my understanding it could still tie to the top of the railing?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'This is exactly what I used it for. I have all iron staircase that extends all the way through the second floor in a balcony style. I just wrapped the ends of the sheet around the last iron spingles and tied the ties through both sheets at the very top and then again at bottom. You can improvise with it quite easily.'}
