{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000E2DIE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413356400, 'question': 'Will this material give paper cuts?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It certainly could. It is probably 0.75mm thick. So, you cut the sheet to fit whatever space you are covering and you have a thin sharp edged piece of plastic. That said, you could easily run a piece of electrical tape up the edge of one side and then fold it over onto the other side (thereby covering the edge). Problem solved. That is only one solution, I'm sure there are many more you could come up with. I have yet to have anyone in my family get sliced open by the plastic sheet...."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000E2DIE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411542000, 'question': 'How thick is this material?', 'answer': 'Not thick enough. They give you a childs hole puncher to perforate it so that you can mount it. That should tell exactly how weak it is.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000E2DIE', 'answerTime': 'May 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401087600, 'question': 'Do you think the material would be noisy in a windy environment?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. I think it would be noisy. We noticed that when we had it on our stairs that if it was bumped, even slightly, it made a pretty big rattle/thundery sound which was annoying. The product worked well for keeping our kids from slipping through or getting stuck in our stair banisters and we were glad to have it. But it was nice to get rid of it when our stairs were redone and we didn't need a banister guard anymore."}
