{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0001EM8I2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423555200, 'question': 'What is the dimension of the part that covers the seat itself?', 'answer': 'My advice, which comes from a car seat installation trainer of 20 years, do not buy anything to add to, put under, or put over the car seat. The cas seat manufacturer will not stand behind the safety of their product with additions. Before you dismiss this as cooky "conspiracy knowledge", think logically about our society: would a company look for ways to get out of liability or will they willingly accept liability?'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0001IU5HY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2008', 'unixTime': 1205910000, 'question': 'Has anyone had problems with the motor failing? Has anyone else experienced this same problem?', 'answer': "Yes, we've been using our swing for 7 months and our motor just went today. I called fisher price service center at 1800-432-5437 and they 're sending us a new motor housing for free. All swings are covered for 1 year. When you call have the product# and the date code ready. They can be found on the motor housing opposite side of the battery compartment. They're going to send our part out tomorrow and I should get it in 7-10 business days. If your swing is older than a year, you can order the motor housing at www.service.fisher-price.com for $25.00 NOT including shipping. I hope this helps you!"}
