{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00020L78M', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389859200, 'question': 'Can I use multiple extension kits to make it even larger?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you can, but remember that the more panels has the structure becomes weaker. This is important because when kids push the panels it will yield more easily. Extrapolating: a 3 panels yard (a triangle) would be virtually indestructible while octagons or decahedrons have not been made famous for its resistance. Paradoxically as your children grow you should remove panels of the yard because your yard will be to weak for him. Greetings from Uruguay.'}
