{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002JETPQ', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404198000, 'question': 'Does this gate bend? I need a gate that bends around curved stairs', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Nope. It's all straight lines and solid wood, and not designed to bend."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002JETPQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375513200, 'question': 'How small can this gate get? The descption says 28" wide in one paragraph and 60" wide in the next.', 'answer': 'Amelia, this gate will open wide to approximately 102" When fully expanded. It has four panels that are approximately 28" each. When fully compressed two of the panels butt together at their ends, so the smallest opening it can fit in is approximately 60" with the mounting hardware. If you have an opening less than 60" you will need to use one of the gates that doesn\'t expand as far and has narrower panels. I love this gate. We use it outside on the porch for our two dogs and it works great.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002JETPQ', 'answerTime': 'Jun 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402988400, 'question': 'What the difference between Extrat Wide Swing Gate and Wide Stairway Swing Gate?', 'answer': 'This gate does not swing it slides open. It is extra wide but I do not recommend this gate I have it. It is hard to slide it open when holding a baby because you have to unlatch it with one hand.'}
