{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00068O22S', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396162800, 'question': 'I have a kitchen aid gas stove...does anyone know if these will fit that?', 'answer': 'Just to let you know, the plastic knobs measure about 2 3/4 inches wide in diameter, they protrude from the stove about 2 inches, and the hole in the back is 1 1/4 wide. Just make sure to measure so that if the knobs are in place, that you have room between them. My GE stove has 6 knobs (5 burners and the oven) and they fit perfectly with ample room between them. I hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00068O22S', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389340800, 'question': 'Will this work to prevent animals from turning knobs? A friend of mine has a large dog &amp; non-removable stove knobs.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. The covers spin when my daughter messes with them and I think they would keep a dog from turning the knobs also. That's too funny the dog is messing with the stove! However, you do have to remove the knobs to put them on."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00068O22S', 'answerTime': 'Feb 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391846400, 'question': 'I see all references are for a gas stove, will they work on an electric stove as well??', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'My stove is gas but I would imagine all stoves have the same knob setup. The hole on the back plate of the Safety 1st (where the prong - sorry I don\'t know what it\'s called - from the stove goes in) is pretty big, 1.25 inches wide. You remove the knob off the stove, you put the Safety 1st against the stove in an open position so the prong sticks out thru the 1.25 inch hole, put the stove knob back into the prong that sticks out of the stove, and you can close the Safety 1st. The Safety 1st is 2 inches "tall" so make sure your stove knob doesn\'t protrude that much (with mine there\'s plenty of room inside the Safety 1st). The Safety 1st is just under 3 inches wide on the back so make sure your stove prongs are spaced far enough to accommodate them. With my stove, there\'s plenty of room between the Safety 1st knobs. I hope this helps.'}
