{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00068O22S', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427612400, 'question': 'Are they supposed to fit loosely and spin? This makes them more than a bit of a hassle when actually turning the stove burners on.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I believe that are made to fit loosely and spin. If they were tight and were turned they would have the same effect as the handles on the stove and turn on the gas. I got them because in my small kitchen I often brushed against the knobs and accidently turned on the gas. Now if I brush against the stove the knobs just rotate without causing any problems..'}
