{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0006FHBB0', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409900400, 'question': 'i am looking for a bottle system in case of post-earthquake evacuation. can i use 1 bottle and just use fresh bags &amp; nipples for 3 days, no washing?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "As long as you're using fresh bags and nipples it shouldn't be a problem, although I would get some wipes to clean the bottle and the nipple ring atleast once a day. Either germs from hands/accidental dropping or sometimes milk/formula can pool alittle on the inside of the ring. If you're concerned about chemicals that close to your baby's food source, I know there are wipes that are made with natural subtances for on-the-go cleaning for pacifiers and teething toys (safe for baby) so you can just wipe down and let air dry for a minute. But I have used this system since my 7mos baby was born and I go through a whole day just using the same bottle but changing the nipples and bags for each feeding. No problem."}
