{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006FHBBA', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401951600, 'question': 'what warmer will these fit in?', 'answer': "I used a gumdrop one and they fit. HOWEVER... these bottles have a thick plastic bottom and gets really hot and the steam condenses in that seam between the bottom and the bottle. I found that I had to wrap the bottle in a towel or something and give it a good shake to get all of the VERY hot water off before bringing it near my baby. Plus, it took a good 5 minutes to get the formula warm after coming out of the fridge. I quickly gave up on a warmer and went for a much better trick. Get a small crockpot, put some water in and it and keep it on your countertop on low (or even warm). You can just plop the bottle in and it's ready in a minute or two. We found this to be MUCH easier and faster. With the warmers you have to measure the appropriate amount of water and add it every time. With the crockpot you just drop it in. I put the bottle in and it's ready by the time I'm finished changing her diaper. FAST! When you're holding a crying baby every minute counts!!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0006FHBBA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398495600, 'question': "do the bottles have oz markers on them? It doesn't shoe in the picture...", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes they do!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0006FHBBA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395385200, 'question': 'Do these bottles fit in standard bottle warmers?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, they fit the Muchkin bottle warmer but only partially. You have to leave the bottle warmer cover off. Playtex bottles seemed like a good solution to me at the time for venting air so baby's tummy does not hurt but they are require a lot of cleanup, their nipples are fast flow even though they state slow flow, and they tend to leak at the bottom often. I quit using these and went with the cheaper/standard plastic Gerber baby bottles (BPA free) with Nuk Silicon orthodontic slow flow nipples. They seem to work perfectly for my baby. The Nuk orthodontic nipples also reduce the amount of air being taken in by the baby, so the combo works just as well."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0006FHBBA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389686400, 'question': "do anyone's bottles' bottoms leak? mine 3 bottoms leaked a little when just added water, and then stopped.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "They leaked a bit with just water. Make sure you have the bottoms on completely tight. It wasn't generally a big problem for me."}
