{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006HBS1M', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'Manual pump vs electric pump?', 'answer': "Manual pump - Hand-held - One breast at a time - You have to manually pump yourself which can be quite the workout w your hands! - Convenient for travel bc they're small - Nice to have as a backup in case something goes wrong w your elec pump (I have both manual and elec) Electric pump - Can be plugged in or used w rechargeable battery - Does both breasts at the same time w option to do just one at a time - Saves loads of time - I have the Medela Freestyle electric pump which is also good for travel bc it comes w a nice bag and tiny cooler thing and the device itself is small (others are larger and may/may not be suitable for travel) - Worth every penny! - Insurance is now required to cover part of/all of the expenses of pumps, electric or otherwise. Call your ins co for details."}
