{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0009KF8DU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402988400, 'question': 'I need to fit a 48.5 inch opening. Which extensions should I buy? Many thanks!', 'answer': 'I looked at the different extensions compatible with the gate system. I played with measurement numbers. For instance, start with the longest extension and add another until you exceed the desired number. Then, consider the other shorter extensions until you get as close to 48.5" as possible. Remember, the system comes with arms at the top and bottom that compensate for about 3" on each side. I hope this helps. Best wishes!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0009KF8DU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378450800, 'question': 'I\'m confused about the 57.50" to 60.25" instructions. It says add two 4802s and remove the 4802 that came with it. I have an opening that\'s about 59".', 'answer': 'Well I had a situation much like that. From what you are telling me part 4802 is an extension that came with the base. You are supposed to remove that extensions and add two of them. I am guessing that the gait only came with one extension. part 4802 is Auto-Close Gate 2-Bar Extension (5.75" wide x 30" high). It sounds like you need two extensions ( 2 pieces of 4802 but only one came with you gate. You can look at the website (see link i have included). This will give you part numbers and what they go to. Now that being said. you should be able to extend the posts at the end of the gate (tops and bottoms to make it wide enough. If it were me, lay what you have in the doorway and extend the end attachments. If that does not stretch across the opening, purchase one extension Part 4208 and add it on. It is important to make sure the ends that touch the wall are all the same distance from the gait. If they are not, the gait will not open and close properly. Once the gait is in place and the extensions are all equal the gait should open easily and close on it\'s own It took me several days to get mine done. I had to order an extra part and when it came in, it fit a different gait so i had to order another extension. Now that it is together it keeps my cocker spaniel out of my formal living room very well. So bear with the frustration it will be all worth the effort. http://www.northstatesind.com/two 4802 extensions. I hope this helps... Good luch'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0009PAO2K', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401951600, 'question': 'Do these have the older valve system with one connecter strip or the newer one with two connector strips?', 'answer': 'I purchased mine around September of last year and they have just one connector strip. The cup is only 3 parts total - the cup, the lid and the valve piece that slides in the two holes in the lid. Simple, easy to clean and completely leak proof if you close it correctly. LOVEEE these cups!!'}
