{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000A6OLM2', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415260800, 'question': "Does this make fine purees of things such as peas with skins? My stick blender doesn't so I have to push through a seive to get it fine enough", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Not really. I got a finer puree of peas by using baby peas (petite pois), the skins are softer, but you will still be left with a puree with texture. For things like blueberries you will have to cook them and pass them through a seive if you want a really fine puree. Both my boys were fine with the skins left in but it will depend on what your baby prefers.'}
