{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BN63KC', 'answerTime': 'May 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400050800, 'question': 'is this waterproof?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No it's not waterproof but most changing pads are covered with a plastic or vinyl type material which you can just wipe down if liquids leak through your covers. We also use cloth diapers that you can purchase in packs of 10 or so from Target and Shopko as an additional layer of absorbency under our little ones bum. We set it on top of the cover and fold it a quarter of the way up where the cloth diaper sits under her bum for containing the most mess from accidents and messy diapers while changing. If you're looking for a waterproof covet you might as well just use your changing pad without anything and wipe it off after diaper changes since it's already waterproof and I think most waterproof covers will be plasticky anyway. Hope that helps!"}
