{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BQKWHE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364194800, 'question': 'can this be use instead of a staircase on a door frame???', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If the question is "Can it be used on a door frame that leads to stairs, I would think so, depending on what the door jam looks like. When the door is closed, is there an additional inch or two of flat wood? You would need about an inch of width to mount the door. You would need this space on both sides of the door frame (i.e., the side with your door hinges, and the side the door latches to.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BQKWHE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423123200, 'question': "Does this gate make a loud noise when it's open or closed? Our stairs are next to my son's room, and I don't want the gate to wake him up. Thanks!", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I agree with the other answer. Only a small click. I've actually learned to minimize that click by jamming my thumb into the latch release instead of using the handle."}
