{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BQKWHE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412665200, 'question': 'I have molding at the top of my stairs. Do you attach the gate above the molding or just mount through the molding with spacer adjustment?', 'answer': 'We mounted thru it is a sturdy gate.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BQKWHE', 'answerTime': 'May 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401346800, 'question': 'The description gives the product\'s width, but it doesn\'t state what size openings it supports. Will this work in a 44.5" opening?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I had to cover an opening that size with this gate. I just added a single 2x4 as a spacer on the hinge side, and it works perfectly. My wife runs a daycare, and the gate has been up and solid as a rock for 9 years.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BQKWHE', 'answerTime': 'Apr 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396854000, 'question': 'How does the gate release / catch work?', 'answer': "It doesn't latch automatically. You must press the downward until you hear it click. Then to open it, you squeeze the latch from the top to release it. It actually works best if you squeeze down on the release button while simultaneously pulling up on the gate. Hope that makes sense."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BV9Q80', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408172400, 'question': 'I see some negative reviews about it being to firm, I want a firm but comfy matress for my 11 lb 2 month old..is this it?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It is firm. Not much give to the small weight of a child. It's not as firm as sleeping on a floor but I would consider it as firm as it can get. I chose the firmest I could find as the firmer the better when it comes to safest sleeping (when it comes to SIDS.) We were very satisfied with this mattress. My son used it until he was 2 when he moved to a larger mattress and he slept well on it always. I plan on using it again for future children."}
