{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BXAI08', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2009', 'unixTime': 1253602800, 'question': 'How wide is this? Can anyone tell me how wide the dining chair must be to accommodate this?', 'answer': 'Base that sits on dining chair is 15" side to side and 15" or 16" front to back. Arm rest/tray holders are 11" from the bottom of the base to the top of the tray holder. The tray holders stick out about an inch each wider than the base so the widest part of the chair is 18" side to side. I don\'t think you could use it with a dining chair with arms unless it is quite wide because you need clearance for the tray and the dining chair arms would get covered in food. I seem to have food splatters in a 5\'x5\' area! I have the seat as upright as it can go and it is about even with the back of the base. If you recline the seat the top part where the baby\'s head goes looks to be in line with the base but it is closer to my dining chair seat back. I hope this description makes some sense. I noticed that this year\'s model looks nicer than last year\'s and the vinyl looks easier to clean. I find this seat is soft and comfy but it has a lot of folds where food gets caught. Also, food falls down the slit where the crotch seat belt comes up so you need to clean under the padded cover. Although the padded cover says spot clean only I put it in the washing machine and it came out OK. I am considering buying a hard plastic booster with shoulder harness as it would be easier to clean. My boy doesn\'t sit in the highchair long enough for hard plastic to become uncomfortable. This chair attaches to my dining chair firmly and the harness keeps my boy secure. The tray comes off with one hand.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BXAI08', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2009', 'unixTime': 1235030400, 'question': 'FP space saver high chair and washability? Hi just wondered about the seat cover and machine washability?', 'answer': 'I have washed it on the hand wash cycle without problems, but I would not recommend this seat. There are to many places for food/stuff to get stuck in the arm rest when not using the tray and the cover is to hard to keep stuff out of the corners. I spent $16 on another seat at WalMart and I love it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BXHPEU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403852400, 'question': 'Does this potty seat fit on elongated toilet seats that are often found in public restrooms?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Not well. It feels a little unstable to the child because the part thats suppose to fit snug inside the toilet is sitting on the seat instead. Go with the Potette Plus 2-1 portable potty seat. Its awesome.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BXHPEU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396422000, 'question': 'how comfortable is it since its not cushioned and does it come with a carrying case?', 'answer': "There is no carrying case, I use a ziplock bag (then I can change it out often anyway). It's a firm plastic so I'm sure it's not overly comfortable. I wouldn't have my little one use it at home but for on-the-go situations, I think it's perfect. I also bought one to keep in our motorhome. I have had no issues with it fitting any public restrooms we've used. Key it to put it to the front of the seat, not inside."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BXHPEU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410246000, 'question': "Are the toilet's hinges really effective at eliminating pinches? I've read some conflicting reviews.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have a 27 mo old boy, who squirms off as soon as possible..no pinching, in spite of quick movements.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BXHPEU', 'answerTime': 'Aug 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407999600, 'question': "How often do you clean it? If not after every use, how is it better than a public toilet? Also, doesn't it seem gross going from public toilet to bag?", 'answer': 'I\'m very impressed at the design of the folding mechanism. It\'s made so that the "dirty" side (part that sits on the toilet) is on the inside when folded up to keep any bag you store the seat in clean. Given some practice, it\'s also possible to open and close this seat without ever touch the bottom side. That said, I would still wipe down the seat before setting the cover down to reduce the "ick" factor. I\'m quite picky about the sanitation of public toilets and I\'d still be comfortable cleaning the cover at the end of the day rather than per use because if the thoughtful design. After all, the top side of the seat where it actually touches your child is as clean (or dirty) as his or her bum. :) There\'s also a study that says diseases are not easily transmitted through the natural protective barrier of the skin from the toilet seat, but I still find it comforting to cover the "ick" factor. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BXHPEU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410418800, 'question': 'Can a adult use it', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I would not advise an adult to sit on it, as the maximum weight limit is 40lbs.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000BXHPEU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426489200, 'question': "The description says there is a carrying case included, but from reviews and questions it doesn't sound like there is. Can anyone clarify?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Mine did not come with a carrying case. It came with a plastic ziploc bag. After that bag ripped, I use a gallon ziploc bag. I think disposable ziploc bags are way to go. You can cheaply replace them when they get dirty.'}
