{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000E0P218', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2008', 'unixTime': 1206342000, 'question': 'GRACO TURBO BOOSTER SEAT: DOES ANY ONE KNOW HOW THIS WORKS IN THE MIDDLE OF THE BACK SEAT WHERE THERE IS NO SHOULDER HARNESS?', 'answer': "Modern booster seats *cannot* be used without a shoulder belt. It increases the range of motion of the child's body in an accident as well as the risk of ejection and 'seat belt syndrome'. The seat should either be installed in a vehicle position with a shoulder belt, the vehicle should be retrofitted with a center shoulder belt by the dealership, or an extended harnessing seat (such as the Britax Regent or Sunshine Kids Radian 80) should be used."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000E0P218', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2010', 'unixTime': 1266998400, 'question': 'How do you keep a toddler from opening seat belt latches? Any ideas beside stapling him to the seat?', 'answer': "It's been at least a year since you posted this question, so I hope you've solved the problem by now. My parents had the same fight with me and my brother when we were young and solved it by slamming on the breaks when they saw our seat belts were off (obviously, they made sure the road conditions were safe for this!). I tumbled to the front of our van and my brother hit a cabinet. Then we got yelled at and (probably) spanked. We were unharmed, but very terrified by the experience and NEVER took our seatbelt off again. It's not a solution I can recommend, but it worked on me."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000E0P218', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2007', 'unixTime': 1174546800, 'question': 'Cleaning this chair: Does the seat have a washable removable cover?', 'answer': 'Yes, the whole cover comes off & is machine washable.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000E0P218', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2009', 'unixTime': 1248073200, 'question': 'Graco Booster with high back fairy tale: is this seat acually safe if it does not strap to the vehicle?', 'answer': "I don't think there are any boosters that strap into the car. At 28 pounds though the child should still be in a car seat. The safest thing is a 5 point harness for as long as possible. I just bought this booster for my child who is about to turn 6 and just hit 50 pounds so to heavy for her car seat. I suggest another car seat that goes up to 50 pounds and has a harness the child can't open not this seat."}
