{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000EGZ40G', 'answerTime': 'Feb 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422777600, 'question': 'Are these microwave safe?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I know I'm not answering your question, but you should heat the milk in simmering water and dump it into a bottle after the fat is all dissolved in the milk again. Don't just sit the plastic bottle on the bottom of the pan, swirl it around, it only takes a minute or two. Or get a bottle warmer. I don't think you should microwave breast milk, but I would assume these are OK in the microwave, they are fairly thick. I watched a friend microwave chicken wings in a Styrofoam box once and he didn't die."}
