{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000F0DX7C', 'answerTime': 'Mar 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363417200, 'question': 'do the top and bottom latches need to be exactly parallel? my bannister is smaller on the top than on the bottom, so the bottom will be 3/4" further', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not totally clear on the question. We do have the gate slightly angled at the top of the stairs because of the bannister location so that there is not such a gap between the bottom of the gate and the top of the top step. We have the gate opening currently over the steps because of the space in my house at the top of the stairs. So, the latches are on the wall side--slightly further in than they would be if they were directly across from the locations where the gate is attached on the bannister side. Not sure if this helps. I have loved the gate and feel it is very secure. I have not had any worries about my daughter falling. Plus, with the gate attached further in on the wall side, there is less space for her to try and slide her legs underneath (which she has a couple of times). When I decide to change the direction of the gate opening, I'll just have to move the pins on the latch side so the gate will open into the hallway. (I'll probably do this when my daughter is a little bigger and older and more able to do stairs safely on her own, if the gate remains in use.)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000F0JPRE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388649600, 'question': 'does this strap work in the Target stores shopping cart? My Cart covers do not work in target shoping carts because they have a weird back.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have found a way to make this work on Target carts. I just attach the strap backward - in other words, wrap the strap around your child's back and secure the Velcro straps around the front of the cart, around the divider that goes between your child's legs. It's slightly less secure than attaching it to the back, but I've found it works pretty well (and quite a bit more secure than the belt installed in the cart)."}
