{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000F1OAE6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 20, 2009', 'unixTime': 1253430000, 'question': 'Does this seat make babies hot?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have the Roundabout and Boulevard in Onyx (black) and the material is smooth and doesn\'t overheat as much as others on the market, even during summer months. If you baby "runs hot" (mine can get sweaty just from sleeping anywhere) there is an extra-large "seat chiller" sold at babydagny dot com that you keep in the freezer and place on the car seat minutes before putting your child in to cool it down. I have yet to use it for this car seat (don\'t need it) - it\'s really great inside coolers though!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000F1OAE6', 'answerTime': 'May 22, 2009', 'unixTime': 1242975600, 'question': 'Britax car seat indent damage: Has anyone had a problem of this car seat ripping the cloth?', 'answer': 'Try the "Sunshine Kids Ultra-Mat Ulimate 2-Part Undermat Car Seat Mat" or the "DuoMat 2-in-1 Car Seat and Mat by Kiddopotamus" Look for padded bottom and seat cover, so that it can be used rearfacing and forward facing. Either way they protect well. Skip the ones that only cover the seat because your child will kick the cloth and it won\'t be protected.'}
