{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NUG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408518000, 'question': 'Is this crib JPMA certified? Does it really matter if it isnt?', 'answer': 'JPMA standards include appropriate spacing between crib slats and structural stability. This crib, although not officially endorsed by JPMA, abides by the slat spaces and is very sturdy. I read many, many reviews on cribs and I was pleased with what customers had to say about this one in particular. We are very happy with this product. I believe it was made in Australia. Personally, I would ignore certifications as long as the product meets them.'}
