{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NVA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387094400, 'question': 'too high', 'answer': "The bed is pretty low to the floor so there shouldn't be worry of your toddler falling out. It comes with two guards so that it reflects that of a crib but easy to get in and out of. To be on the safe side, I purchased a cheap area carpet and placed it beside the bed to assure that my daughter wouldn't injure herself. She is a wild sleeper and so far she hasn't had any spills out of the bed. No worries!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NVA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1420012800, 'question': 'Could someone tell me how high is the side rail, the shorter side. The dimentions of it.', 'answer': 'The "short" sides are 23.5 inches in height and 29.5 inches in "width" (the back of the bed to the front). I know you didn\'t ask for the front rail but just so that you know it comes with 2 rails. So, essentially you can have a guard rail on the right or left side of the bed. But it is 19.25 inches high. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT7NVA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420617600, 'question': 'Can you use crib bumpers with this bed?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, but its awkward and loose. I ended up threading a rolled comforter through the slats which worked fine.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NVA', 'answerTime': 'Jul 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404630000, 'question': 'How high is the clearance under the bed? I would want to build a trundle for it to accommodate my twins.', 'answer': 'Kim, my bed is on carpet and measures slightly over 6-1/4" from bottom of front trim to carpet, very slightly but not even close to 6-1/2". I must say I\'ve been very happy with this bed.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT7NVA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410073200, 'question': "The pics are a little unclear. Does this bed convert to a regular twin sized day bed? I can't tell if it just goes straight from toddler bed to full.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It does convert into a twin but it doesn't come with the part needed to convert it. You have to but it separately from the manufacturer"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NVA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359273600, 'question': 'How high is the top of thew mattress (or mattress support) off the ground? And how high is the lower side rail above that?', 'answer': "Honestly, I wouldn't buy this bed if I were you the craftsmanship is horrible. The wood split when I was assembling it it was damaged when it came to my house and I'm constantly having to tighten the screws because they always seem to work themselves out. This bed served its purpose and the price wasn't bad but I will be replacing it with a regular bed soon. To answer your question the mattress is about 6-8 inches off the ground and the lower bedrail is like 1ft to 1.5 ft off the ground."}
{'answer': 'The standard crib/toddler mattress fits.', 'asin': 'B000FT7NVA', 'answerTime': '22 days ago', 'question': 'What size mattress does it need?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NVA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428044400, 'question': 'Does it convert into a twin and a full? or just a full?', 'answer': 'Just a full'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372921200, 'question': "Is this bed ok for shorter people? I'm 5'3 and wondering if it will be hard to bend over and get out the baby (especially because of the front rail)?", 'answer': 'The parents aren\'t tall, and they seem to be OK. I\'m 5\'4", and I find it accessible.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390118400, 'question': 'My sister bought this bed a couple of years ago and when she moved, she lost a few screws and barrel nuts. Where can I get those parts?', 'answer': "Here's the link to the manual I mentioned. It has specifics about the parts you need The instruction manual is here: http://www.davincibaby.com/files/manual/2977/M4791%20-%20Emily%20Crib%20in%20English%20and%20French_05.12.11%20[NF].pdf"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385193600, 'question': 'Do the screws go into wood, or are there metal bushings for the screws so that it can be safely taken apart and put back together multiple times?', 'answer': 'The crib has barrel nuts inside the pre-drilled wood holes and the screw and lock washer are screwed into the barrel nuts. It appears that it could be safely taken apart and put back together as the crib converts to a youth bed. Since I have not actually taken it apart again, I cannot say for certain. I hope this is helpful.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420876800, 'question': "Is this white a true white or is it more cream? Is it bright or flat? I'm trying to match a Graco dresser I have, but they've discontinued the crib.", 'answer': 'I would say the crib is more true white with a satin finish.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372057200, 'question': 'Does this crib have the mattress spring system in lieu of the solid adjustable mattress', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It doesn't come with a mattress but it has the adjustable mattress support and it is with springs. I love this crib and have gotten 2 already."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419667200, 'question': 'Do I need to buy a bigger size matress once the crib is converted into todler bed?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'How difficult is it to convert from a crib to toddler bed with the railing? How long does it take?', 'answer': 'It was easy to do. It took about 20-30 minutes. We had our toddler help so that added time. Make sure you have the little tool you used to put the bed together.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1296115200, 'question': 'When did you lower the mattress? When did you lower the mattress height?', 'answer': "I think we lowered the mattress when our son was able to reach up and grab the bumper - we anticipated that he would be pulling up - sometime before he pulled up on the sides. My second son is 4 months and hasn't rolled over yet, so we haven't lowered it yet. If you have to ask yourself twice, that usually means just do it! You'll feel better. What's it going to hurt? It's better to lower it too early than too late."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2010', 'unixTime': 1291190400, 'question': 'Please help with a mobile that fits this crib: Can someone please share the name of a baby mobile that fits on this crib?', 'answer': 'Well, this may be way too late judging by the post date but my Fisher Price Precious Planet 2-in-1 Projection Mobile fits perfectly.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NYC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420185600, 'question': 'What is included with this purchase? Are all parts included to convert from crib to toddler bed to day bed to full size?', 'answer': "You should look for description. If I understand correctly it has the part to convert the crib to toddler bed, but you have to order one more part to convert to full size (sold separately). I've bought the bed about 7 months ago and that part was available at Amazon also then."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': 'When the mattress platform is at the lowest position what is the height from the platform to the top of the side railing?', 'answer': "Ours measures 27 and 5/16 inches from the platform at it's lowest position to the top of the side rail. Hope that helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411974000, 'question': 'How many mattress positions are there to choose from? Or can you adjust the height to wherever you want?', 'answer': 'HI, There are 4 Mattress Height Positions to choose from. Let me know if you still have any questions. Rishy'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392796800, 'question': 'Does anyone know if the naturepedic mini/portable crib mattress fits with this crib? Im looking for an organic mattress that fits with this crib.', 'answer': 'It did for us 3 years ago!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Aug 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408518000, 'question': 'Is this crib JPMA certified? Does it really matter if it isnt?', 'answer': 'JPMA standards include appropriate spacing between crib slats and structural stability. This crib, although not officially endorsed by JPMA, abides by the slat spaces and is very sturdy. I read many, many reviews on cribs and I was pleased with what customers had to say about this one in particular. We are very happy with this product. I believe it was made in Australia. Personally, I would ignore certifications as long as the product meets them.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423900800, 'question': 'What is the exact measurement length wise. From the outside edge to the other outside edge length. I have a 41" space to put it in. Thank you.', 'answer': "it is 40 inches long 28 inches across and 34 inches high if the space is 41 inches you would have to build it in that spot because moving it won't be an option. and it may not rock unless you have more then 35 inches of floor space for it to rock back and forth."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'I just purchased this crib along with the Naturepedic mattress, but it is too large. What mattress besides the Davinci mattresses work with this?', 'answer': 'I purchesed the "Dream on me 3" spring coil portable crib mattress." it was perfect!!!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1369724400, 'question': 'Is this crib 16 CFR 1220 compliant?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'As far as I found: Yes. All juvenile products are required by federal law to abide by the rules of the CPSC (Consumer Product Safety Commission) in order for them to be sold to consumers. They are manufactured to comply with the federal guidelines and standards set forth by the CPSC, as well as the ASTM (American Society of Testing Materials)"'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394694000, 'question': 'Do the two side panels have plastic teething rails (The manual says they have, but my two orders, including a replacement, do not have)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'mine did not come with teething rails'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 5, 2010', 'unixTime': 1286262000, 'question': 'Wheels? In the picture, it looks like there are wheels on the bottom?', 'answer': "it comes with 4 casters you can use or not. if you put them in, the crib will not rock. there is also a small piece that you can use to lock it into a stationary position so it won't just rock while your little one is sleeping."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IZY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2012', 'unixTime': 1341126000, 'question': 'sheets and bedding: What bedding fits the mini crib????', 'answer': '24" by 38" are the size of the sheets for this bed if you have a 3" mattress and not just the pad. The pad is not good it\'s a thin pad. Mattress is necessary. Amazon has mini crib sheets gerber does too.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396681200, 'question': 'What is the interior depth of the crib measuring from the mattress support to the top of the side rails when the crib is at the lowest height setting?', 'answer': '27 inches.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2012', 'unixTime': 1334300400, 'question': 'Good for petite moms? Is the Kalani good for short moms?', 'answer': 'yes, yes, yes! I\'m 4\'10" so when were looking for cribs I wanted something that was still going to be easy for me to lay baby down in once we had to lower the mattress. My son\'s mattress is on the second to last setting and I can still lay him down with out feeling like I\'m tossing him into the crib.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391760000, 'question': 'What is the distance between the bottom rail and the floor? I would like to use under-the-bed storage and want to be sure something could fit under.', 'answer': 'Approximately 6-10 inches'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359964800, 'question': 'Has anyone used the DaVinci Kalani Crib as a co-sleeper (nestled up next to their own bed like a sidecar)? Does it work well in that capacity?', 'answer': 'Yes it works until unless ur mattress is of standard size by height. My mattress is little bit high than the usual mattress . But it does work and its a beautiful crib. Go for it I am using for my month old son.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379487600, 'question': 'Do I need to buy any bed frame or rail to get it it be a full size bed?', 'answer': 'They conversion rails are sold separately.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2009', 'unixTime': 1256626800, 'question': 'Crib mattress for DaVinci Kalani crib: Do any other Kalani crib owners have a suggestion as to crib mattresses?', 'answer': "Hi Tootsie, we got this crib and the Naturepedic organic 150 mattress. Fits well!The Kalani's metal support is one solid piece & therefore cannot sag in the center."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385107200, 'question': 'What is the mattress size for this bed?', 'answer': "It's a standard size crib mattress. We didn't measure just bought a standard crib mattress."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373526000, 'question': 'Hi two questions: 1) is the mattress height on this adjustable? 2) is there a side rail that be raised/lowered using one hand? thx!', 'answer': "The crib is adjustable for four mattress heights. It does not have a drop rail. I was under the impression that the drop side cribs are now banned due to their not meeting safety standards and the potential for injury or death? The adjustable heights on the mattress work very well and are not a hardship, partly due to the crib itself being built lower to the ground. We transitioned from a drop side to this crib almost two years ago and he is now three and nearly ready to go to the next stage on the crib - removing one side and replacing with the side rail that comes with it. We actually got the new crib because he was so active and energetic and we were afraid the other one would collapse on him. The new DaVinci has been wonderful - no problem in the Cherry finish at all, looks great, and is so sturdy for this extremely active little boy! We're delighted with our choice and plan on a white one for my grand daughter soon."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT7NRO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417075200, 'question': 'Does your company currently in stock and ready to ship in expresso?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, we have it.'}
