{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT9J3U', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412665200, 'question': "Can I change the levels of the bed so I won't bend inside to grab my infant baby?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, the crib has three levels. With a thicker mattress which we purchased as an add on the top level is just below waist level. I am 5'9''."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9J3U', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425542400, 'question': 'Hello, could you tell me the space/distance in the middle between 2 slats of the crib? Thanks a lot', 'answer': "I'm not able to look at the crib since I am not near it right now but I don't think they are more than 2 inches apart. If your worried about the baby falling through or getting stuck it will not happen."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9J3U', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396335600, 'question': 'how portable is the crib? is it easy to roll in and out?', 'answer': 'I had another crib previously that was on wheels and that one was definitely more portable in that it wheeled. I move this one all the time from room to room and it is fairly easy to scoot and/or pull, but not as easy as if it were on wheels. The plus side is that it is extremely solid and sturdy - much more so than some I have seen on wheels.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT9J3U', 'answerTime': 'Feb 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393142400, 'question': 'Will this fit regular size crib sheets?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it will. I actually recommebd using the regular size crib sheets because the mini crib sheets are so tight and barely fit. They were constantly popping off and i had to fix it like everyday. So def go with the regular crib sheets. You can even use the toddler bed sheets. They have more character options. Hope this heps you.'}
