{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IOA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385884800, 'question': 'How high are the edges on either side? Would a 4 inch changing pad work with this table?', 'answer': 'The short sides are 41/2 inches tall. The front is slightly taller and the back is considerably taller. I think a 4 inch changing pad would be just fine.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IOA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385539200, 'question': 'Can anyone give an exact measurement of how much vertical space there is on the shelves? Will a basket 10 inches tall fit?', 'answer': 'I bought bins from Walmart.com (http://www.walmart.com/ip/Household-Essentials-Nested-2-Piece-Box-Set-with-Lids/22866950) that are 8" tall and that\'s about as tall as I would go. There is a lip on the bottom of each shelf so you can\'t just slide the bin out to get what you want. You have to be able to lift them a little.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9IOA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375772400, 'question': 'Is the finish formaldehyde/HAPS and VOC free? Is the glue water soluable? What is the matress pad made of anf covered with ( exact materials as in MDS info please)', 'answer': "Hmmm I have to put my thinking cap on - my grandson is now 4 years old. I do know we bought another mattress pad for the changing table, but can't remember if the finish was formaldehyde/HAPS and VOC free. He loved it and would coo, bit I don't remember the exact materials. Sorry. Janet"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FT9IOA', 'answerTime': 'Jul 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375254000, 'question': 'How much space is there height-wise on the shelves? Wondering how tall baskets,etc. can be and still fit on the shelf.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'There is about 10 inches, plenty of room depending on what kind you get. We have 3 ten by six canvas drawers on one of the shelves with room to spare. The Land of Nod canvas bins were what we used. http://m.landofnod.com/i-think-i-canvas-wide-drawer/f6264'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9J3A', 'answerTime': 'Jul 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372921200, 'question': "Is this bed ok for shorter people? I'm 5'3 and wondering if it will be hard to bend over and get out the baby (especially because of the front rail)?", 'answer': 'The parents aren\'t tall, and they seem to be OK. I\'m 5\'4", and I find it accessible.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9J3A', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390118400, 'question': 'My sister bought this bed a couple of years ago and when she moved, she lost a few screws and barrel nuts. Where can I get those parts?', 'answer': "Here's the link to the manual I mentioned. It has specifics about the parts you need The instruction manual is here: http://www.davincibaby.com/files/manual/2977/M4791%20-%20Emily%20Crib%20in%20English%20and%20French_05.12.11%20[NF].pdf"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9J3A', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385193600, 'question': 'Do the screws go into wood, or are there metal bushings for the screws so that it can be safely taken apart and put back together multiple times?', 'answer': 'The crib has barrel nuts inside the pre-drilled wood holes and the screw and lock washer are screwed into the barrel nuts. It appears that it could be safely taken apart and put back together as the crib converts to a youth bed. Since I have not actually taken it apart again, I cannot say for certain. I hope this is helpful.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FT9J3A', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420876800, 'question': "Is this white a true white or is it more cream? Is it bright or flat? I'm trying to match a Graco dresser I have, but they've discontinued the crib.", 'answer': 'I would say the crib is more true white with a satin finish.'}
