{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000G7TIZA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398582000, 'question': 'If I shoved this into my suitcase so I can transport it as a gift for my cousin, would it hold its shape in a day of travel?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't know whether it would return to it's original shape because I've never tried to fold it in half to fit into a suitcase. However, if you want it to hold it's shape and serve the person well who is changing the baby, I wouldn't recommend you fold it in half. A better option might be to put in a larger, lightweight case, with foam layers around it to protect it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G7TIZA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396162800, 'question': "Is the entire thing machine washable? And this vinyl covering it mentions, does that mean it doesn't require a separate cover?", 'answer': 'No, the pad itself is foam covered in non-removable vinyl. It is hand washable and wipeable, and there are covers you can buy for it that can be machine washed, but the entire thing is not machine washable.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G7TIZA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394780400, 'question': 'Hi, from what kind of material was it made? Does it have PVC ? Thanks.', 'answer': "It's not PVC, but it is a plastic kind of material (almost like a crib mattress?), I recommend getting one of the covers for it. But mine is still in as great of condition as when I first bought it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G7YLZW', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2008', 'unixTime': 1203062400, 'question': '3 Radian carseats in a row: Has anyone tried to fit 3 of the Radian seats side by side in a standard car/small SUV?', 'answer': 'Yes, it does fit. We have a Highlander and two Radian seats along with an infant Chicco rear-facing base/car seat. It is a tight fit but definitely fits.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000G7YLZW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371366000, 'question': 'can sunshine kids radian 80 car seat turn into a booster seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No...the seat folds somewhat flat for transporting (i.e. putting into a large 33" or 36" rolling duffel as checked luggage) but it does not detach. We eventually got tired of shuffling car seats between 2 cars and ended up buying another pair of seats. After researching booster seats and finding out that it is still recommended to have upper body support, we chose the Britax Frontier 85 SICT which can be used as a booster later in the child\'s life. This is a bigger seat than the Radian but is a little lighter and has side impact cushioning for additional safety. See http://www.amazon.com/Britax-Frontier-SICT-Booster-Seat/dp/B004Z4U1QU/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1371401130&sr=8-1&keywords=Britax+Frontier+85+SICT+Booster+Seat'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G7YLZW', 'answerTime': 'Jan 17, 2010', 'unixTime': 1263715200, 'question': 'Sunshine Kids Radian in a 2007 Subaru Impreza Wagon: Does anybody know if a SK Radian will fit in my 2007 Subaru Impreza Wagon rear facing?', 'answer': "You may have already found a solution, but my gut is this won't fit rear facing *and* allow you to use your front passenger seat. Try posting on the www.car-seat.org forum for more confirmation. We have a 2005 Saab 92X (built off of Impreza Wagon during brief joint venture w/Subaru) and had a very difficult time finding a rear-facing model that would fit while allowing us to retain use of the front seat. I was very excited about the Radian originally (due to long term use possibilities and air travel angle), but we realized it would probably not work (and retain use of front seat) rear facing in even our Pontiac Vibe (also Toyota Matrix). In the end we got a Britax Diplomat for rear facing use."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G7YLZW', 'answerTime': 'Nov 21, 2008', 'unixTime': 1227254400, 'question': '3 Radian car seats in a 3rd Row: Does anyone know if 3 Radian car seats can fit in the 3rd row of a Tahoe?', 'answer': "I can fit 3 Radian's across the back of a Volkswagen golf, so I am sure you would be OK."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G80O4I', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': 'Does the chair not rotate at all? After installation, my boon chair can rotate a little bit say 10 degrees. It is normal?', 'answer': "The top chair/seat part does not swivel. However the whole chair swivels easily because of the rollers underneath the chair. It's never been an issue for us, and I think it's safer that the top seat does not swivel. You wouldn't want child to push on the table or under counter and spin itself. :) We have had our boon for 5 years now and has been thru 2 kids and guests and we still LOVE it. Still looks cool and CLEAN and moves easily around on tile and hardwood. :-)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G80O4I', 'answerTime': 'Mar 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394953200, 'question': 'I like the look of the white color but worry that it will easily stain. Does the white stain or will it retain its color with regular cleaning?', 'answer': "I have had white for years now. It's seen me through 3 boys, spaghetti sauce, poo accidents and strawberry stains. All you have to do is spray down w/ a Clorox water mixture & any stain will come out within minutes! So fear not. My chair looks like the day I bought it! (The status come off super easy for deep cleaning as well). This chair is a must have!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G80O4I', 'answerTime': 'Oct 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381388400, 'question': 'Does it really last till 4 years of age or 50 lbs? Seems like the crotch part would be an issue for a bigger child.', 'answer': 'The crotch part is easily removable.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000G80O4I', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422432000, 'question': 'The tray height from the floor seems a little low, has anyone noticed if this highchair sits the same or lower than other highchairs on the market?', 'answer': "it's adjustable on the height, we've had both a high top table and a normal top table and been able to lower it to fit under our normal height and raise it to be really close to our high top....so you can choose where you want it."}
