{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GB0NZA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426316400, 'question': 'Do you think this is a better option than a blender for making homemade baby food?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'This is for " when you make a meal for the family and the baby can eat the same thing". Or when you eat out just share what you are having with your infant. If you make a baby food enmass and want to freeze or store it then a blender makes more sense.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GB0NZA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'Will it puree cooked asparagus since that veggie tends to have strings that need to be removed or would the strings clog it up too fast?', 'answer': "I don't have personal experience with asparagus. The grinding mechanism is metal-on-metal, with a scissor-like action. Asparagus might require some extra pressure, but I bet it would work. Clogging should not be a problem while grinding, afterward you might have to clean the little holes with a brush or something."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GB0NZA', 'answerTime': 'Oct 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413010800, 'question': 'Does the inside bottom part that pushes the food upwards go all the way to the top and push all food through? I had one that left 1/8" food inside...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Since there is about an &#8539;" of blade and shaft below the metal screen, there will be about an &#8539;" of food left inside at the end of the grinding process.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GB0NZA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': 'does this separate or strain skin or seed or bones while grinding? Like berries or chicken?', 'answer': "I don't think so, it's hard grinding soft foods like boiled vege's!"}
