{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GB0NZA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384416000, 'question': 'is it easy to clean or a pain in the butt with many parts?', 'answer': 'The little blue cap on the center post unscrews. You then have two plastic parts and three metal ones. It disassembles sufficiently that it is easy to clean, and you could put it together blindfolded after the first couple of times. I really like this grinder, and so does the baby!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GB0NZA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386316800, 'question': 'can you use it on flax seed?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I wouldn't want to use this little grinder on anything harder than a steamed fruit or veggie. I had some raw green beans that I was trying to grind and it took forever and my arm got tired. Once I steamed the green beans until soft, it was easy and quick."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GB0NZA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409900400, 'question': 'Is this BPA free?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It is BPA free but I wouldn't recommend the product. It was more of a hassle than anything. It was a pain to clean and didn't do a great job grinding the food. And it was a bit hard to actually grind anything harder than a banana. A blender or a baby bullet would be a better pick."}
