{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GBGU4S', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372057200, 'question': 'Would this carrier be suitable for a dog?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Actually, I don't have experience with smaller dogs, I've always had big dogs. But I don't think so. Your dog should have more or less the same size and weight of a regular baby. And unless your pet is really easygoing, I don't think it would be so comfortable for him walking arround in this position. I think those special bags for dogs, which look like a handbag, would be more apropriate. Hope I've helped...."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GBGU4S', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395298800, 'question': 'I am a big guy I wear 2 to 3 X shirts would this fit me?', 'answer': 'i think it would still be fine. i am a 6\'1" woman and wear an xl often before being pregnant and then gained 60 lbs. i was wearing the bjorn soon after my munchkin was born. the carrier has adjustable straps. on a side note i am now using the ergo sport much more. it is for tall and bigger frames and works well :)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GCL5NI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377154800, 'question': "Owners - how have you cleaned up the little crevices on the underside of the lid? I've had to throw three of them away with gummed up milk.", 'answer': "A bottle brush. The sprayer on your sink. Not letting cups sit until milk gets gummy. Several companies make a small set of four different brushes specifically for cleaning sippy cups. Unfortunately, I have yet to find a single brand or style of cup that does not have small crevices in the lid and some are much worse than these. If you've let the cups sit until a bottle or cup brush and hot water will not help, try soaking them for a few hours or overnight in hot water and dish detergent and trying again."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GCL5NI', 'answerTime': 'Sep 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411628400, 'question': 'Is the spout soft or flexible at all?', 'answer': 'For all of these, not just this design, the tops are a fairly hard plastic. While smooth they are not flexible but not sharp or brittle.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GCL5NI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402642800, 'question': 'do these cups fit in car seat cup holders?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I haven't tried yet but think my grandson has used them in his own car seat (in his mother's car). The shorter cups do get lost in the deeper cup holder on his toddler pushcar/stroller, but the taller ones stand up high enough for him to grab the cup out of that one. The shorter cups are easier for a young child to lift up high enough to get the drink out of it. Our family loves these cups, but be sure the piece inside the lid is on tightly each time you fill it or it will cause a leak."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GCL5NI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377414000, 'question': 'Are these cups made in USA or China???', 'answer': 'China'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GCL5NI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375945200, 'question': 'what age or stage are these cups?', 'answer': 'We used them as the first sippy cup around age 7 mos.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GCL5NI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367305200, 'question': 'Do these fit in a bottle warmer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't exactly remember how wide my bottle warmer was, but these are wider than bottles. I don't think they would fit, but I'm not certain about that."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GCL5NI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389859200, 'question': 'Do these cups have valves that have to be separated from the lid and cleaned or is it just the lid and cup? Looking for easy cups to take to daycare!', 'answer': "There is a valve but they're pretty easy to clean. I've never seen a cup that is actually spill proof without a valve. The ones that claim to be always end up leaking."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'Does the Chicco KeyFit 30 carseat attach easily?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it does. You attach the extender/support piece and strap the carseat in.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2012', 'unixTime': 1344236400, 'question': 'Difference between Joovy Caboose and Joovy Ultralight: What am I missing?', 'answer': "I found a video on YouTube from StrollerDepot comparing the two strollers. Apparently there are three differences-- 1) The regular Caboose is 5 pounds heavier than the Ultralight, 2) The canopy on the Ultralight is larger, and 3) the Ultralight comes with the parent tray and the regular Caboose doesn't. Considering you can get a generic, universal parent tray for ~$10, I fail to see why the Ultralight costs SO MUCH more than the regular Caboose!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Aug 15, 2012', 'unixTime': 1345014000, 'question': 'Toddler facing forward on rear seat? Has anyone found a safe way to face a toddler forward in the backseat?', 'answer': "Joovy now makes an insert to turn the back bench into a full seat. It's around $65, and you can order it as an on the Joovy site. It's new."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373439600, 'question': 'Can the older child in the rear bench seat still sit comfortably with the infant car seat installed in the front?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes it car seat faces back and doesn't intrude into the bench at all"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397026800, 'question': 'Is it easy to maneuver this stroller on the subway? We live in Boston in case that gives you a frame of reference for door size on the train! Tx', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't have experience taking mine on a subway. But it is easy to steer and to fold/unfold quickly. For a two-kid stroller it is maneuverable and light... If compared to a single kid stroller, no it is not maneuverable, but we used to have a contours optima tandem stroller and I sold it because it was impossible to get around."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'Has anyone ever taken this on an airplane? Are they willing to gate check this stroller for free, or is it too big?', 'answer': "I have. However I've read that American Airlines is the only airline who won't gate check a stroller heavier than 20 pounds. I guess I'll find out soon because we booked a trip with AA. And I am going to take this stroller. No problem with any other airlines I've travelled (United, Delta)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403247600, 'question': 'Is the 45 lb max for each kid or for both?', 'answer': 'Hey!, Yes it is tested for 45LBS per seat per child. -Joovy'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388217600, 'question': 'can the joovy too seat be used with this model instead of the ultralight?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. It can be used with both models. We have three kids and it can easily be converted from bench to seat on the cheaper model.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Jul 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373871600, 'question': 'Can you travel through the air port easily?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, this stroller is very light weight and easy to maneuver. I wish we had it when we travelled to New Mexico last fall.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GDGV3Q', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384588800, 'question': 'Is it uncomfortable to have the older child sit on the bench when the infant is in a car seat. I have a snug ride 35.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not really... My 2 year old sat hunched over on the bench since the front chair back has to be fully reclined. I ended up purchasing the Caboose Too rear seat so she could have a more comfortable ride back there. It doesn't help that the bench does not lock in place, so her hunched position would get worse as the bench would slide out of place."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GE8VKG', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374044400, 'question': 'is it hard for children to sit on?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "My daughter is 13 months old, and she still doesn't have the coordination to hold the handles and sit up on it by herself. I expect that it will be several months before she can sit up on it and rock by herself, but she also isn't walking yet. If a child can pull his/herself up and walk then I would expect that sitting up on this rocking horse should be no problem."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GE8VKG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415260800, 'question': 'Can a 5 year old fit this?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes my 5 year old is 70lbs. She is built big like her dad and fits fine still. I'm sure your child will fit it to."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GE8VKG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386316800, 'question': 'What kind of fasteners are used to put this item together, and is glue used? How well does it hold together compared to a fully assembled horse?', 'answer': 'Wood screws are included. Upon final assembly as per the included instructions, this rocking horse is solid as a rock. The pieces assembled with the wood screws are counter sunk and keep the screw heads from the child. There is no need for glue in the initial assembly.'}
