{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GGD3O8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377068400, 'question': 'do you lift the gate to open it? Could a 5-year old open it?', 'answer': "It's been a long time since I had a 5 year old, but I think they could learn to open it. The gate closed with a lever-type piece of plastic at the top of the gate that you lift up to disengage the latch. You can lock it by pressing down on the lever firmly after closing, which causes a red piece of plastic to fit over the end. To open after locking takes two hands - one to push the plastic piece to release the lever, and one to lift the lever to open the gate. I think a 5 year old could probably figure it out but I'm not sure if they would be strong enough to unlock and open the gate. But then, kids are clever!"}
