{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GK5XY2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391155200, 'question': 'What foods work well in these feeding bags?', 'answer': 'You can put anything in them. I used to put fresh apples, pears, oranges, frozen cubes of pureed foods such as squash and sweet potatoes; we even put ice chips in to help when she was teething. You can put just about any kind of fresh/frozen fruit or vegetable. Keep in mind these bags are very difficult to clean after a few weeks. I soaked them in hot water after every use and ran them through the dishwasher but food builds up in the seam. Even boiling them did not get it out. If you want to replace every couple weeks these are great, otherwise I would spend a little more for a silicone type.'}
