{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000GX0B3M', 'answerTime': 'May 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399618800, 'question': 'There seems to be conflicting opinion s on what size for what age, my Grandaughter is one just starting to walk, do I buy the small or large one? I', 'answer': 'My granddaughter turned 1 in November. I bought her the small one so she could keep her feet on the ground and push around. She can also lie across the body and scoot. Do not worry that the small one will be too small in a year or so. My three year old grandson has the larger one, but he likes to ride on either one, and gladly rides the smaller one so his 7 year old brother can use the larger one for racing around the house. If your granddaughter likes the toy, she will ride it for many years. "Grandma to 3 in AZ".'}
