{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000H4C6FG', 'answerTime': 'Oct 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412492400, 'question': 'What do you use to clean the surface before applying the velcro? Window cleaner or soap and water?', 'answer': "I used soap and water and then I put some rubbing alcohol to make sure there wasn't any oily residue on it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000H4C6FG', 'answerTime': 'Oct 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412406000, 'question': 'I want my windows to be totally closed and locked. Will these wedges prevent someone from sliding the windows open?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The purpose is so that they will not open but keep in mind these are stuck down, not screwed down and I imagine with some strength and wiggling around these could come off. They work perfectly to not let my kids open the windows and I have a hard time opening them past. But if you are looking to prevent an intruder I would recommend something that is more permanent.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000H4C6FG', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412060400, 'question': 'I have double hung wooden frame windows (built in 1941). Will these wedges work?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hello Richard, I had to Google some pictures of the windows in question :-) These wedges will work with any window that slides up/down or side to side. The trick is, the make sure you clean/dry the surface before you stick the Velcro on the window. Also make sure the wedge is affixed securely to the Velcro. I have two on each window downstairs (split level house) and they hold well. I truly believe that these wedges will give you extra time if an intruder tries to get into your home. Hope this helps.'}
