{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000H4C6NI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397199600, 'question': 'it says it fits a window up to 53" but protects only 21" - what does that mean? i have a casement windows - 2 windows that open out - 51"', 'answer': 'It means that it\'s only 21" tall. If your window is taller than 21", then you\'ll need to purchase two. Install one near the bottom and one near the top. Make sure the space inbetween the two is not too big. Check the instructions for the recommended spacing.'}
