{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HBMVO0', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': 'How do you remove it?', 'answer': 'It is super easy. You simply reverse the process that you use to place it on the stroller. There is a nob that you turn initially and then it slides off in two-three pieces. I have two of these on my double stroller and have had zero issues moving them if I didn\'t like where I initially placed them, etc. In some ways, the directions MIGHT seem a bit tricky but I just studied the product visually, read the directions, and figured it out. You have to use some "force" to really make sure it is tight because the plastic is a bit stiff but, again, I did it twice and have had zero issues.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HBMVO0', 'answerTime': 'May 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399359600, 'question': 'Will this fit on a carseat? (Specifically the Diono)?', 'answer': 'The cup holder comes with a long strap which you can adjust to go around a round object. So think of any sort of round handle, bar, bike frame, which you can strap the cup holder too. The length of the strap is quite long it will go around a pretty large round object maybe up to 3inches in diameter. The strap and the cup holder part can swivel and be adjusted to position the cub level regardless of which way the strap is lashed to the round item you mount it too. We bought two and put them on our Farmers Market Bicycles (Handle Bars) to carry our coffee cups. For a kids car seat you would need a clamp style holder. These are a strap that wrap around an object like a bar or stroller handle etc.'}
