{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000HK6BCE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359792000, 'question': 'Will they work for the top bed on a bunkbed?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Probably. Are there any railings at all? They do slide out a little from out twin bed but I haven't had them push all the way out. I could probably tighten them up a little under the mattress. The problem is the doubles are really designed to fit a bigger bed (double or queen). But if you have any railing at all up there that would hold them in place and they would work great. Also better than nothing. I'm just a little skeptical because if it did push out, that's a long drop. I have one side up against the wall which helps to keep them in place. There is a strap connecting the two sides together. It just is a little loose for the twin. You could probably shorten the strap and they would work fine. OK, I hope this helped. If you have any other questions, let me know and I'll try and help."}
