{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HL2JOC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412060400, 'question': 'If this is for a 9V pump, why does it say 12V on the battery pack itself (imprinted in the plastic)? (It even shows the same on the Medela site.)', 'answer': "I am not sure why it says that, I didn't even notice it till I looked to answer your question. I know when I purchased it said for use with 9v pumps. Mine says the same but it works perfectly withy 9v instyle pump. No issues at all. I absolutely love it and the freedom it gives me to pump anywhere!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HL2JOC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397977200, 'question': 'How many times can you pump on one set of batteries?', 'answer': 'The instructions say you can get 10 hours of pumping time out of a set of batteries. I have done about 5, and still have power, but I do feel the "pump" isn\'t as strong. I doubt it will last 10 hrs, but I am still glad I bought it. Great for on car trips, or when you have to pump in a jam'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HL2JOC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410678000, 'question': 'The instructions say that rechargeable batteries are suggested. Can I use regular AA batteries, or do they have to be the rechargeable kind?', 'answer': "Also for three days straight I pumped 5-6 times per day and didn't need to change out the regular batteries."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HL2JOC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411974000, 'question': 'Can the battery pack case attach to your belt/pants for easy hands-free pumping? (Is there a clip of some sort in the back?)', 'answer': "no belt clip but the pouch it comes with you could probably close over your belt. I don't know what pump you have but I put mine in pump bag & put the pump bag strap over my shoulder. works pretty well for me."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HL2JOC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427612400, 'question': 'Can the battery pack also recharge rechargeable batteries, or do you need a separate charger for that?', 'answer': 'The Medela battery pack does not charge the batteries, but can work with rechargeable batteries that are fully charged. You will have to charge them before using them.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000HL2JOC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426834800, 'question': 'Does the adapter support 220V input power?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No its only 110'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HL2JOC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425884400, 'question': 'Has anyone used both the battery pack and a manual pump? Which do you prefer?', 'answer': "I prefer an electric pump over the manual pump. The electric pump (battery pack or plug) is more consistent and produces more milk for me. The advantage of a manual pump would be that there is no noise. I would use a manual when it's not feasible to use an electric pump, but would not choose that as my sole pump."}
