{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000HZDN9I', 'answerTime': 'Mar 10, 2008', 'unixTime': 1205132400, 'question': 'Is this thing safe? Does anyone else agree with this?', 'answer': "Does a baby jumping on a parents lap pose a hip-damage risk? Probably not. I think you're most likely alright using the jumper for periods of time but sure, don't let your child live in it. I think the old style of jumper that hung from the door jams where the child could swing and bash themselves into the walls would be worse for their hips than anything. If you're concerned, ask your doctor to explain -- or better yet - get a second opinion... but I wouldn't quit using it."}
