{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000I4YA72', 'answerTime': 'Jan 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390032000, 'question': 'how do you change from celcius to farenheit?', 'answer': 'The unit displays F by default. You can change to C and back. In the case of the IRT4520, the manual says: 1) Make sure the thermometer is turned off, 2) Press and hold down the "I/O" button. After about 3 seconds, the display will show [either] "F"/"Set"/ [or] "C"/"Set" ... 3)Release the "I/O" button when the desired temperature scale is shown. There will be a short beep to confirm the new setting, then the thermometer is turned off automatically. The same instructions say in the case of the IRT4020, you use the Start button instead of the I/O button. In case you don\'t want to change the default display, or for old-style/non-changeable display thermometers), here are the formulas: To change from C to F: F = C x 9/5 + 32. To change from F to C: C = (F - 32) x 5/9.'}
