{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000I5HB86', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': 'Could I use this cover with the Baby Jogger Summit X3?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think you probably can although I haven't tried it because I was overall unhappy with this rain cover. It's stiff plastic and that makes it hard to take on and off. Also, it doesn't have a zipper to open and close so you have to lift it on and off to take your baby in and out of the stroller. I ordered the baby jogger brand rain cover to replace this one (I use it on the standard city mini and my summit x3) and I prefer it. It's better quality, easier to take on and off and to store. The only downside to the baby jogger brand one is that the top is black so when it's on you can't see your baby through the little windows in the top of the sun canopy. Still, I'd recommend it over the Sasha brand one."}
