{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000JIINLQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376895600, 'question': 'We are gong to florida so it will be HOT and rainy, will this be too hot for my daughter to be in when its raining?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'If the sun is shining, yes, it is like a greenhouse in there. You can try to open some flaps, but if it is hot outside, it will probably be too hot under the rain shield unless there is a pretty good breeze. The plastic is very thick, which is great for not tearing or breaking, but bad for hot days. I often used mine on sunny winter days to keep the kids warm. Have a great vacation!'}
