{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KCV61U', 'answerTime': 'Jun 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372575600, 'question': 'Can I use this in a plane for my 3 year old toddler?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I used it with my 3 year old on AirTran, but that was 4 years ago. She hated the feel because it was so different from her carseat and she was not used to it. She was comfortable and found asleep on the 6 hour flight. Good luck and God bless.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KCV61U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383811200, 'question': 'Is it FAA approved for air travel?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It is not approved for air travel. The answer is in the customer questions and answers when you scroll down in the web page, you have also the option of purchasing the ride car seat travel vest with the child airplane travel harness (FAA approved).'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KCV61U', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374994800, 'question': "I drove a friend's child who was wearing this vest. She could lean down and put her chin on her knees while wearing it. Is there a way to avoid this?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Were you using the top tether or just a lap/shoulder belt? If the vest was top-tethered I can't picture a kid leaning far down enough to be putting his/her chin to her knees. Some folks who might be better able to help you with this question are the certified child-passenger safety techs at the internet forum http://www.car-seat.org - they're very helpful and knowledgeable. Hope that helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KCV61U', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397545200, 'question': 'My son is autistic and gets out of his seatbelt all the time. He slides underneath the lap belt. Will this vest solve that problem?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It still depends on the seat belt to be secure... But there are 2 more buckles like the seatbelt to secure the vest onto him and one that keeps him from sliding out from under the vest that fastens from back to front between the legs. Once the vest is on and he is seated, the seat belt is secured through the front of the vest w/ metal C clips that keep the seat belt low and in place. At times this can be difficult to undo with a moving child but could help delay his escape for a while. This also should be used w/ the shoulder strap and has Velcro to keep it placed just right- not on his neck, but st his shoulder. My kids would not be able to get out & still attached w/ seat belt at the beginning. The best thing about this is that it looks like a space/ astronaut suit & they learned to tolerate it b/c it was special. The only down side to this is that my kids couldn't see out the window, which is why they wanted out of the seat belt in the first place. We just had special things for them to do in the car when we traveled to keep them safe. Best to you and your family."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000KCV61U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383724800, 'question': 'is this the safe rider 3 or 2?', 'answer': "I'm not sure. The Vest only gives the manufacture date of 2005 March: Model AO10000LGB."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KJBFC8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414738800, 'question': 'Does it work with Britax Boulevard car seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I believe it will because mine is very similar to that one.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KJBFC8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392969600, 'question': 'Has anyone had success using this with the Diono Radian RXT car seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hello, While I haven't used this particular car seat, after looking at pictures of it, I can offer some advice. The Diono seat do not have very high sides, therefore the travel tray will rest directly on the child's lap. Additionally, without fairly tall sides on the car seat, the sides of the tray will be fairly useless. Please let me know if I can answer any additional questions. Cheers, Jason"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KJBFC8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379401200, 'question': 'Does this work with sunshine car seats?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "This comes with a long adjustable strap that I'm sure canfit any car seat. I really like it and stiil use it easy to wipe clean and keeps food off of car floor seats and in tray. My child likes it too . He doesn't lose his cars or colors. Enjoy"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KJBFC8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427007600, 'question': "Does anyone have success using the product according to safety directions and wrapping around the child's waist NOT around the car seat?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I bought the product for our daughter to use with our granddaughter, and she said they put the belt around her waist, as directed, then just unbuckled one side to get her out, although she did say that had their car seat not been so large, she would have been tempted to put it around the car seat itself.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000KJBFC8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409468400, 'question': 'hi, I would like to know if the product works well on airplanes and also does it fold flat?', 'answer': 'Imagine a piece of hard plastic layered with a thin layer of foam for the bottom that rests on the arms of the carseat then add about a 2" inch high foam lip around the top edge that can fold down to put back in the box. This holds in the toys, food, ect. Now to the sides sew a couple of pouches that hang down about 6". Solid on the inside and netting on the outside to hold a bottle, small coloring books or whatever you wish to take with you. The belt that goes behind the car seat to hold it in place against his belly has an adjustable strap with a clip on the end. One short piece on one back side of the tray with half the clip and the other half at the end of the long strap. It is very easy to snap together and adjust it. I bought it for long trips but I actually use it every day. My 2 year old grandson would carry his toy in his hands and they were always dropping and he was wanting me to pick them up as we are driving. (not happening) Now he plays with his cars or whatever other toy and it all stays within his reach. I just love it!!! I kept the almost flat box in the car to put it back after each use but I have never used it again. I just unstrap it, move it to the side of his carseat and it\'s very handy for the next time he gets in the car. Well worth my money!! I don\'t know if it would work on an airplane, I guess you could strap it behind the child if he stays still and allows it to rest on his lap, the pouches could be folded underneath the tray. And yes it folds almost flat to about an inch and a half. Hope this helped.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KJBFC8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415001600, 'question': 'Would this work for a 2 year old on a plane without a car seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you could make some sort of extension for the strap for it to fit all the way around an airplane seat, then it could possibly work. Otherwise, I would say no. You could possibly strap it around your 2 year old, but it isn't a hard surface, it is soft. It would flop around and move whenever your toddler moved. I'd say without a car seat, it wouldn't work very well."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KJBFC8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395558000, 'question': 'Would this work for kids in wheelchairs', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "yes. Depending on the type. It would work best for one with no sides. You know the ones with no armrests. But either way it will work. It you don't need the side pockets because the chair does have sides and armrests, then you could also use a seam ripper and take off the side pockets. It does provide a pretty sturdy surface. I love it. My son has really gotten into note taking (he is 3) he loves to copy what his nurses are doing when they do their paperwork, or even in the car. It is really nice and easy to use. Hope that helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000KJBFC8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410764400, 'question': 'Will this work on a infant car seat? I have a snug fit 40 and a 7 month old who likes to play with toys in the car that fall out of reach. Thanks!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I would think that it would work. The only issue that would be a problem is that the infant seat tilts back more than a forward facing so things might roll back towards him because it tilts. However if you get it and it doesn't work for the infant seat it will definitely work for him when he's a toddler. I have these for my 2 year old twins and they are wonderful for long car rides."}
