{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000KU5A9G', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410850800, 'question': 'Can you put this directly on top of a cot bed, change the baby and trust it wont move around? Or buy a wood cot top changer unit and put this in?', 'answer': "It will move around unless you fasten it with the safety tabs. I have it on a changing table with four sides, and it is a very snug fit, so in my case it doesn't move at all. If you have a changing table like that, then you might be okay."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000KU5A9G', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410678000, 'question': 'Can you put this directly on top of a cot bed and change the baby? Or should I buy a cot top changer unit made of wood and put this in??', 'answer': "It's flat-bottomed, so you could put it directly on any flat surface. However, if you have a roly poly baby and lay it on a surface without securing the bottom of the pad to that surface (such as to a changing table or dresser), the lap belt won't do anything to keep baby from rolling off - he would simply roll off of that surface with the pad buckled to him!"}
