{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LEI82W', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2010', 'unixTime': 1267948800, 'question': 'Will this work for the Chicco Keyfit 30 carseats? Will this work for the Chicco Keyfit 30 carseats?', 'answer': "Baby Trend's website says that it will work with the chicco keyfit and keyfit 30. Based on that information we bought this stroller, and just got two keyfit 30 carseats yesterday. Unfortunately, contrary to the baby trend's website, they DO NOT fit. I cannot find any way to make them secure in this stroller. I have been searching the internet to find out what happened. It turns out that people have used the 1304TW model with chicco's carseats. I believe that is an older model. The 1305TW, which is listed here on amazon and at most other places on the internet, will not work with chiccos. I'm very frustrated with BabyTrend's website. They should not claim compatibility if only their older models which are no longer available are compatible."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000LEI82W', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373007600, 'question': 'Has anybody used Britax B Safe carseats? The salesman tried to snap the car seat on this stroller and it rocked and wabbled tremendously--very unsafe. The salesman said maybe it was missing pieces or not put well together. Has anybody used double...', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'I did not, but there is another piece you can buy - an adapter that may help you. Good luck!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000LEI82W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357891200, 'question': 'Can a Graco quick connect 40 fit?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I don't know for sure, but I used two different styles of Graco car seats and they both fit. This stroller is designed to fit all the popular standard infant car seats, so I don't think you'll run into a problem unless you have an unheard of brand of car seat. If you're really worried about it, call Snap-N-Go."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LEI82W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2011', 'unixTime': 1313478000, 'question': 'Will this fit two Snug Ride 35s? Does the Baby Trend Snap and Go fit two Snug Ride 35s?', 'answer': "I had the opposite experience. I have 2 SnugRide 35s and not only could I not get them to fit but when I called BabyTrend they told me that the double snap n go will fit the Snugride and the Snugride 30, but not the Snugride 35. I found this out too late and ended up having to return by double snap n go and buy the Graco Quattro Tour Duo. It was heavier and not exactly what I wanted but it worked and now that my twins aren't in their infant seats anymore I can still use the stroller because it has seats."}
