{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LNHTZK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 16, 2009', 'unixTime': 1247727600, 'question': 'Pack n Play or Co Sleeper???', 'answer': 'I was also having a hard time deciding between the two. I think I have finally decided on the graco pack n play with bassinet. It is cheaper and can later be used as a playpen/crib when the baby is more than 15 lbs. Also, it folds up and is easy to use for travel, I am not sure the co-sleepers do that.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LNHTZK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 1, 2009', 'unixTime': 1243839600, 'question': 'Twins- do I really have to buy 4 car seats? Help! Do we really have to buy 4 - two for each car?', 'answer': 'Buy two sets of infant seats w/bases and then buy two extra bases. The seats detach to carry the infant so they can be used in both cars without having to buy four seats.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LNHTZK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2010', 'unixTime': 1276066800, 'question': 'Halo sleep sack = overheating. Anyone else? Did anyone else find that their baby would overheat when wearing a polyester Halo sleep sack?', 'answer': "Jules, I recently read your question regarding the HALO SleepSack wearable blanket. I am with HALO and I thought I might be able to provide a helpful perspective. The micro-fleece SleepSack has properties that help wick moisture from baby's skin. However, to ensure that baby does not overheat it's also important to take into account the temperature of the nursery and amount of additional clothing that the baby is wearing. In this case the micro-fleece SleepSack wearable blanket is intended for use at room temperature and has TOG value (a standard for measuring thermal resistance) of one. As you add additional clothing layers, the TOG value increases as well as the likelihood that baby will be too warm. I'd recommend making sure your nursery is at room temperature and that your little one is wearing a light coverall or bodysuit. If the room is quite warm, as may happen in the summer, you might consider a lighter cotton fabric SleepSack wearable blanket. I hope this helps. If you have additional questions please feel free to contact us directly at sleepsack@haloinnovations.com."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000LNHTZK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382425200, 'question': 'does it come with sheet', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No it does not. To my knowledge, none of the pack n plays come with the sheet. You have to purchase it seperately.'}
