{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000LNHTZK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2009', 'unixTime': 1234512000, 'question': 'Can a toddler use the Graco Pack n Play: Does anyone have experience (good/bad) using this with an 18-month of about 27lbs?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I've done it before, but be warned the baby can flip over the side if too tall..which is a scary sight to see - take my word on it. So far, both my older children have not slept well in the playpen, the flooring is hard and using blankets/extra padding is dangerous. All of mine were too tall to use the playpen by 18 months. Sorry to sound negative, these playpens are great but we have found them to be insufficient as sleep areas for baby or young toddlers and best used for play. I'd suggest a crib mattress on the floor in a babygated and babyproofed room, or one of those bean pod portable beds."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LNHTZK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'whose brand of mattress pad fits this pack n play', 'answer': "I didn't purchase a mattress pad but did purchase a Graco quilted playard sheet. It was made for the Pack 'n Play."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LNHTZK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393056000, 'question': 'what mattress pad fits this for more support?', 'answer': 'Kolcraft Cozy Soft portable crib mattress It was $24.99 on Amazon and my grand-daughter sleeps well on it she is now 12 months old'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP3VEG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2008', 'unixTime': 1206342000, 'question': 'GRACO TURBO BOOSTER SEAT: DOES ANY ONE KNOW HOW THIS WORKS IN THE MIDDLE OF THE BACK SEAT WHERE THERE IS NO SHOULDER HARNESS?', 'answer': "Modern booster seats *cannot* be used without a shoulder belt. It increases the range of motion of the child's body in an accident as well as the risk of ejection and 'seat belt syndrome'. The seat should either be installed in a vehicle position with a shoulder belt, the vehicle should be retrofitted with a center shoulder belt by the dealership, or an extended harnessing seat (such as the Britax Regent or Sunshine Kids Radian 80) should be used."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP3VEG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2010', 'unixTime': 1266998400, 'question': 'How do you keep a toddler from opening seat belt latches? Any ideas beside stapling him to the seat?', 'answer': "It's been at least a year since you posted this question, so I hope you've solved the problem by now. My parents had the same fight with me and my brother when we were young and solved it by slamming on the breaks when they saw our seat belts were off (obviously, they made sure the road conditions were safe for this!). I tumbled to the front of our van and my brother hit a cabinet. Then we got yelled at and (probably) spanked. We were unharmed, but very terrified by the experience and NEVER took our seatbelt off again. It's not a solution I can recommend, but it worked on me."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP3VEG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2007', 'unixTime': 1174546800, 'question': 'Cleaning this chair: Does the seat have a washable removable cover?', 'answer': 'Yes, the whole cover comes off & is machine washable.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP3VEG', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2009', 'unixTime': 1248073200, 'question': 'Graco Booster with high back fairy tale: is this seat acually safe if it does not strap to the vehicle?', 'answer': "I don't think there are any boosters that strap into the car. At 28 pounds though the child should still be in a car seat. The safest thing is a 5 point harness for as long as possible. I just bought this booster for my child who is about to turn 6 and just hit 50 pounds so to heavy for her car seat. I suggest another car seat that goes up to 50 pounds and has a harness the child can't open not this seat."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP2G6K', 'answerTime': 'Jul 16, 2009', 'unixTime': 1247727600, 'question': 'Pack n Play or Co Sleeper???', 'answer': 'I was also having a hard time deciding between the two. I think I have finally decided on the graco pack n play with bassinet. It is cheaper and can later be used as a playpen/crib when the baby is more than 15 lbs. Also, it folds up and is easy to use for travel, I am not sure the co-sleepers do that.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP2G6K', 'answerTime': 'Jun 1, 2009', 'unixTime': 1243839600, 'question': 'Twins- do I really have to buy 4 car seats? Help! Do we really have to buy 4 - two for each car?', 'answer': 'Buy two sets of infant seats w/bases and then buy two extra bases. The seats detach to carry the infant so they can be used in both cars without having to buy four seats.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP2G6K', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2010', 'unixTime': 1276066800, 'question': 'Halo sleep sack = overheating. Anyone else? Did anyone else find that their baby would overheat when wearing a polyester Halo sleep sack?', 'answer': "Jules, I recently read your question regarding the HALO SleepSack wearable blanket. I am with HALO and I thought I might be able to provide a helpful perspective. The micro-fleece SleepSack has properties that help wick moisture from baby's skin. However, to ensure that baby does not overheat it's also important to take into account the temperature of the nursery and amount of additional clothing that the baby is wearing. In this case the micro-fleece SleepSack wearable blanket is intended for use at room temperature and has TOG value (a standard for measuring thermal resistance) of one. As you add additional clothing layers, the TOG value increases as well as the likelihood that baby will be too warm. I'd recommend making sure your nursery is at room temperature and that your little one is wearing a light coverall or bodysuit. If the room is quite warm, as may happen in the summer, you might consider a lighter cotton fabric SleepSack wearable blanket. I hope this helps. If you have additional questions please feel free to contact us directly at sleepsack@haloinnovations.com."}
