{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP2G6K', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2007', 'unixTime': 1196755200, 'question': 'Suitable as a bassinet? Is it comfortable or safe enough?', 'answer': 'We have a similar pack n play from Graco with the bassinet and yes I think it would work fine. I put my little one down for naps in it. I use a sleep positioner wedge to keep her in place in it and to make it cozier. Ours came with a diaper changing area too which is so handy!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP2G6K', 'answerTime': 'Jul 25, 2008', 'unixTime': 1216969200, 'question': "Graco Pack 'n Play with Bassinet: Do regular bassinet sheets fit on these?", 'answer': "I don't think so. Its wider than most. I just used a folded flannel blanket or strategically placed diaper mats. Note that it has a weight capacity of 15 lbs."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000LP2G6K', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2009', 'unixTime': 1234512000, 'question': 'Can a toddler use the Graco Pack n Play: Does anyone have experience (good/bad) using this with an 18-month of about 27lbs?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I've done it before, but be warned the baby can flip over the side if too tall..which is a scary sight to see - take my word on it. So far, both my older children have not slept well in the playpen, the flooring is hard and using blankets/extra padding is dangerous. All of mine were too tall to use the playpen by 18 months. Sorry to sound negative, these playpens are great but we have found them to be insufficient as sleep areas for baby or young toddlers and best used for play. I'd suggest a crib mattress on the floor in a babygated and babyproofed room, or one of those bean pod portable beds."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LP2G6K', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'whose brand of mattress pad fits this pack n play', 'answer': "I didn't purchase a mattress pad but did purchase a Graco quilted playard sheet. It was made for the Pack 'n Play."}
