{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LXQVA4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406012400, 'question': 'What is the ideal age to start using it for the baby?', 'answer': "Totally depends on your baby! My son was 17 pounds at 3 months (98th %), so I'm sure he's a bit earlier than average. We is got this for him at 3 1/2 months and we started using it for short periods so he could get the standing up feeling and start learning the toys for cause and effect. Now, at 4 months, he loves to jump! We still have it on the setting that keeps him closest to the ground because he's average on height (25 inches now). His feet are almost flat, but the next setting is too high. In any case, we should be able to use this until he's walking, so many months of use. :)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LXQVA4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381647600, 'question': "What's the weight limitation on this?", 'answer': 'Well it says 25lbs...but my 6 month old son is about 22lbs now and it seems to be working just fine. We have it on the lowest setting for his tippy toes to touch the ground....I think it will be fine to use past the 25lbs limit....My husband thinks it should be ok up to about 35lbs.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LXQVA4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374130800, 'question': 'at what age could a baby be put in this?', 'answer': 'So we started putting the kiddo in it as soon as he could hold his head up on his own -- around 3.5 months. He was (and still is two months later) too short for it, so we have been placing various objects underneath so his feet hit something (couch pillows for a while, now a lap tray) rather than him dangling.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LXQVA4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389513600, 'question': 'how do you adjust height?', 'answer': 'Adjusting the height is very simple. There are 3 slots at the lower end of each strap. Numbered 1-3; 1 being for the shortest or lightest baby. The straps are held in place under the seat frame with a small bar that you lift to unsnap and turn to put the bar into the desired slot and turn back to snap into position. Should only take a couple minutes.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000LXQVA4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398582000, 'question': 'Does the jumper fold up for storage?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, unfortunately it doesn't. Not that difficult to disassemble though if necessary."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LXQVA4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387785600, 'question': 'When can you start putting your child in the jumperoo? How many months do you think you can get use out of it?', 'answer': "You should be able to put him in the jumperoo when they are able to support their head. My son could sit in a bumbo pretty well when I start using it so around 4 months. He couldn't jump at the beginning but enjoyed the toys. He started jumping around 5-6 months. He is 9.5 months, and we will use it on a daily basis. I would imagine he would enjoy it even after he walks. He really enjoys jumping."}
