{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000LY3W00', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2011', 'unixTime': 1315206000, 'question': 'jumperoo or bright stars around we go.. Hello,I am confused what to buy for my 5 mnth old son..whether a jumperoo or exersaucer or bright star around we go??', 'answer': 'Definitely the Bright Starts Around We Go!!! We have both the Jumperoo and Around We Go toys and after being able to run and move herself around on the Around We Go for long periods of time, my daughter only enjoyed the juperoo for a few minutes here and there and kept trying to walk in it. And, since being able to walk on her own, she still plays with the table on the Around We Go without the harness part. The Jumparoo ended up never getting used much.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000LY3W00', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2010', 'unixTime': 1291363200, 'question': "i can't get it to rotate: If I unbuckle it it will rotate but it will also come apart.... can anyone help me?????", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Mine works finally when I remove one of the little wheels that keep popping out. I suggest that you call Bright Start. They sent me a return label to return just the fabric seat, then they sent me a newel model which I have not put together yet, and was told that the newer model should be easier to rotate. I was told to keep everything else (the one that I initially received), so on the worst scenerio, I will end up with a set of toy that has no seat, but still usable when your baby turns toddler and play with it, and another one in the box which I hope works. They have good customer service.'}
