{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MAERLG', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2011', 'unixTime': 1311836400, 'question': 'Fit on a shopping cart??', 'answer': "It's not supposed to go on any part of the top of a shopping part, including over the basket. It sounds like you're talking about having the seat straddle the basket of the cart, which is just as dangerous. Sure, it *could* fall into the basket, a mere 8 inches. Or it could be knocked off completely. Carts are not designed to have items placed on top of them, they become top heavy. Please reference the American Academy of Pediatrics: http://aappolicy.aappublications.org/cgi/content/full/pediatrics;118/2/e545 If anything, put the car seat *in* the basket (or wear your child, have someone else come along, etc). I know its a pain, but so is using a car seat in the first place (on top of a million other child safety measures) and you wouldn't compromise a child's safety in the car just for mere convenience..."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MAERLG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 5, 2011', 'unixTime': 1320476400, 'question': 'is this a rear/forward facing carseat? meaning that she might fit in there even when she hits 12,14 months? Help?', 'answer': 'No. All infant car seats are rear-facing only. If you want a car seat you can switch to forward facing later, look at convertible car seats. They are designed to do this. Also the new recommendations from the American Pediatric Association, I believe, are to keep your child rear facing for 2 years, and the higher weight capacity of 30 lbs is designed to help you do that with this seat.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000MAERLG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361433600, 'question': 'Are there any Keyfit 30 systems manufactured in 2012? I ordered one and received it yesterday, and it was manufactured in 8/2011!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It's pretty much luck of the draw what your mfr date is. Mine was manufactured 3 months before I purchased. If you are not satisfied, contact the seller and request one with a more recent date."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MAERLG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 1, 2011', 'unixTime': 1298966400, 'question': 'Chicco Travel System Discovery and Adventure which is a newer model? My question is which model is newer Discovery or Adventure?', 'answer': "Discovery and Adventure are not models they are the color style. Chicco technically only makes one model of their travel system, which is called the Cortina. It is available with a KeyFit or KeyFit30 infant car seat, the difference being that the KeyFit is only recommended up to a 22lb baby, and the KeyFit30 will last until your baby is 30lbs. To answer your question a little better, I believe that Discovery is exclusive to the KeyFit and Adventure is exclusive to the KeyFit30. I personally would recommend the KeyFit30 it is slightly more expensive, but most convertible car seats that you would purchase as the next step for your baby have a minimum weight of 30-35lbs and you don't want your baby outgrowing his KeyFit carseat at 22lbs and be stuck without a seat or using a seat that doesn't fit him for such a period of time."}
