{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MAERLG', 'answerTime': 'Oct 12, 2012', 'unixTime': 1350025200, 'question': "Adjustable Handle? Does the handle on the stroller adjust, or is it high enough for a taller person (6'4) to push comfortably?", 'answer': 'The stroller handle adjusts up an down very easily. There are buttons on both sides that you push in and then move the handle. My husband is 6\' 2" and I am 5\' 2" so this was very important to us. We have this stroller and it is really easy for us to both use it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MAERLG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384588800, 'question': "I've used this car seat rear facing for a year and a half. Can I use it front facing as well or is it ONLY for rear facing?", 'answer': 'This seat is only to be used for rear facing. Studies show infants and toddlers should remain rear facing until at least age 2 or even up to three. Doing this will greatly reduce the risk of serious injury during accidents.'}
