{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MEB3GE', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384070400, 'question': "What does this device give you that an Iphone doesn't?", 'answer': 'We liked the ease of simply pushing a button to record these items. We tried using my iPhone, but when our hands were full, it was a pain to log into the phone, open the app, and record. Plus, we can leave the Itzbeen with our baby so when only one of us is home with her, it can stay updated. The night light on it has also been handy. We have loved this little thing, especially for tracking poos (we used the "*" for poo) as it is hard to remember because they do that less often. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000MEB3GE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425884400, 'question': 'Is it good for twins?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You could use it for twins if you were only timing two things each. It is great for babysitters or those who don't have (or want to use) a smartphone, iPad, or iPod. Once I started using the Total Baby app, I never touched this product again. You can track multiples, plus if you breast pump you can keep track of that as well, and it saves all of your information on the app."}
