{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MVQBG4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417680000, 'question': 'Is it easy to remove when taking a shower? Take out and put on the floor outside the tub?', 'answer': "Yes, you can easily remove it. It might drip water a bit if it's not dry."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MVQBG4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414825200, 'question': 'Does this collect mildew and get scummy? If so, is it easy to clean?', 'answer': "No mildew, and I had one for 4 years before I replaced it, it can get soap scum and collect dust sometimes but it's very easy to clean, I cleaned it right there in the shower and used q-tips to clean the narrow spaces; a product like windex also worked well."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MXJ25O', 'answerTime': 'Sep 26, 2008', 'unixTime': 1222412400, 'question': 'Graco Safeseat- do the straps adjust like the cheap Snugride? Does that also apply to the Safeseat?', 'answer': 'The safe seat does not adjust in the back, it adjust just like convertable does...by pulling the webbing between the babies leg at the end of the seat. Hope that helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MXJ25O', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2007', 'unixTime': 1171526400, 'question': 'Color? How do you go about choosing the fabric you would like?', 'answer': 'i\'m not sure exactly what you\'re asking, but maybe i can help. this pattern is called "ionic" - if you search amazon.com under "graco safeseat" you\'ll see more patterns, or you can go to gracobaby.com and browse the patterns there. i personally think this is one of the best patterns on the market right now, but if you\'re looking for something else, check other retailers. some patterns are specific to certain retailers (i.e. french roast is only available at babies\'r\'us). hope that helps...kelly'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MXJ25O', 'answerTime': 'Sep 25, 2007', 'unixTime': 1190703600, 'question': 'can you wash the material part of the seat? With what can you wash the inside of the seat when the material gets dirty?', 'answer': 'Yes. The padding on the Infant SafeSeat is removable for machine wash on the delicate cycle. Drip dry. The metal and plastic parts may be cleaned with mild soap and water and wiped dry with a cloth or towel. To clean the buckle, use a damp cloth or sponge. The harness straps may be spot cleaned. Never use bleach to clean this product.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MXJ25O', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2007', 'unixTime': 1198828800, 'question': 'Grocery carts? One reviewer mentioned the Safe seat did not fit onto a shopping cart like the older models--is this true?', 'answer': "Well this is the way I look at it. I have big babies (over 9lbs at birth) and my first two grew out of there other infant seats at 3-4 months old. Still being too little to sit in the cart on there own but to big for the infant seat. So to me any negatives that there might be of this seat are far outweighed by the fact that I don't have to worry about my soon to be new baby outgrowing the seat so fast."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000MZKTU4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2012', 'unixTime': 1354435200, 'question': 'Does this stool really weigh 49 lbs?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No, it doesn't weigh 49 pounds. I guess that's a typo-of some sort. It's more than 5 lbs, though. This is a great stool for all children, but especially for those with disabilities. The arms come up to child arm height. The arms are removable for when or if your child is more confident on the toilet. It's easily washable and has a nice wide, sturdy platform for boys to stand and urinate. The base has a U shape which fits up snug around the bottom of the toilet so it doesn't slide around like other stools. We found that my son (he has CP) is able to move it out and in, as opposed to moving it from side to side, but that is obviously an individual ability. Overall, this is the best thing we have found for a kid with special needs."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000MZKTU4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387785600, 'question': 'What are the exact dimension of the stool?', 'answer': 'the dimensions when put together are 22.5" L x 21" D x 25" H. Regarding the depth, the stool does wrap around the potty so it only protrudes about 7" past the potty seat.'}
