{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': 'Nov 21, 2011', 'unixTime': 1321862400, 'question': 'Can baby face forward? My son is used to facing out, is this an option with the Moby?', 'answer': 'Absolutely! My son uses a modified lotus hold where his legs dangle instead of being held up and in, so his arms and legs are free. He can happily hang out for hours like this. Once you learn the technique for wrapping, you can tailor your own style to suite baby and you without a problem.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': 'I have a large chest, would the Moby wrap work for my body?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes it would. I also have a large chest and it works great. It's very long so it is good for any body size. My baby loves it he tends to cozy up and fall asleep in it all the time. Just adjust it until you and your baby are comfortable."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2012', 'unixTime': 1351926000, 'question': 'Is the Moby Wrap easy to put on? Can I do it by myself? Does it come with instructions even a sleep deprived New Mom could follow?', 'answer': "The Moby wrap does come with instruction and a pucture how to guide. I also looked up videos on youtube it was helpful. Yes you can put it on yourself, my first couple time I put it on standing in from of a mirror and the more you do it the easier it will become. My daughter is 6 months old and I still love usign it with her. It is also good for the grocery store trps if you have 2 kids. My older one goes in the shopping cart and my 6 month old goes from her carseat to the moby (I wo uld put on the moby at home so when you get to the store you don't have to try to put it on in the parking lot."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 11, 2011', 'unixTime': 1299830400, 'question': 'Is it good for twins? Can you put two babies in the mob wrap?', 'answer': "Yes, the moby wrap comes with instructions on different ways to tie for different seating positions 1 or 2 of those include instructions for twins. If you go to their site or look on youtube, you also should be able to find instructions on how to use this with twins. I can't believe this made it to someones do not buy list. My daughter had reflux/colic and screamed constantly...within minutes of putting her in the moby she always calmed down and fell asleep."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': 'Aug 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409468400, 'question': 'Is it easy for bigger women to wear?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'My husband is 6 feet even, but with a 30-inch inseam he is all torso so needs length like he\'s 6\'6". He is also just over 300 pounds. I ordered an extra-long Moby by calling the number they list in the FAQs on their website. It\'s 6 meters instead of 5.5. He ties it in back, but has a ton of extra fabric when we tie it correctly and don\'t let the kid hang low, so she\'ll fit in for a good while to come (she\'s only 13 pounds right now). I\'m 5\'11" and 210. I bought a regular-sized Moby from Amazon before we went on vacation, and I have enough extra fabric to cross in back and tie in front with either of them. The Moby comes with a booklet showing different ties. I found the Kangaroo carry easiest to get my daughter in when I was first learning, but you put your baby in that and then wrap around her. I use the hug hold all the time now because I can put that on before I go out and just fasten my seatbelt over it, and slide her in when I get there. No wrapping in a parking lot.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379487600, 'question': 'will it fit on plus size mom', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It is long material that you wrap around yourself. My daughter is about a size 14 and it fit her but she has it wrapped around a lot! So depending upon what size you are (how plus), I would think it would fit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420790400, 'question': 'Hello! My daughter is 7 weeks old. Will I get much use out of this wrap? Is it too late to try this type of thing out? She wants to be held all day.', 'answer': 'You will get plenty of use with it. We decided to keep it for our second child and it has come in very handy as i do housework and or walk the dog. Keeps her close and warm and supported at all times.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2012', 'unixTime': 1334818800, 'question': 'Is this wrap easy to breastfeed in?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'yes, but it takes some learning. Ring slings are easier for nursing from birth. Woven wraps are great to nurse in and not as hot as a moby but can be challenging when they are itty bitty.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000N9H4SE', 'answerTime': '16 days ago', 'question': 'can moby wrap be used for 1 and half months kid?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "The newborn hug hold can be used for infants starting at 8 lbs. If your baby is below that weight you'd need to ask your pediatrician. Otherwise, yes, you can use it."}
