{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000NDY7TY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392019200, 'question': 'Is there still room on the sit-and-stand seat for a child if there are infant seats in both front spots? Looks like stroller seats have to be reclined', 'answer': "Hi! There is still room for a toddler or child when the infant seats are still in place. I had twin babies when my son was almost two. This was the only stroller I could find at the time (6 years ago), that would work for us. It is a dream to push when empty, but it is VERY hard to push and turn with babies on board. I quit using it when the babies were 12 months old. I hated this stroller, but didn't have much choice...."}
