{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000NV5VDW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397977200, 'question': 'Does this attach to an existing canopy to extend it?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "If I remember correctly, it has four strings that you use to tie it onto the buggy, like around the metal supports. Our buggy had an existing canopy, but it was very small & didn't shield her from sun, so we positioned it on top of the existing canopy and tied it down tightly so that it extended out as far as it could without falling off and onto my child's lap or the ground. I think what really made the difference in how well it stayed stuck to the existing canopy was how well we tied it and at what vantage points it was tied. There's no velcro on it, tho, so it won't just attach by itself, altho I'm sure you could buy some of that stick-on velcro for added staying power. We didn't, we only used the ties it comes with, and it worked fine for as long as we needed it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000NV5VDW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'Do you need an existing canopy on your stroller for this to work?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, otherwise I it would be too flimsy and won't hold."}
