{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OFNFDA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 14, 2009', 'unixTime': 1258185600, 'question': 'How many should I purchase to start? Can anyone help with some sound advice on a number?', 'answer': "P.S. Just a warning, in the beginning my daughter was too small for these diapers (6lbs 9oz) so we had to use disposables. That only lasted for about two weeks. After that it's been great. Buttonss"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OFNFDA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2011', 'unixTime': 1320912000, 'question': 'Anyone use cloth diapers who live in an apartment?', 'answer': "This is totally up to you. I use cloth, but they must be washed with a rinse, then a wash, then a rinse cycle and I usually do a load every 2nd day. Then I try to spend every 4th day doing a few loads of other laundry before the diapers. Are there enough machines that you won't be stuck without a washer when you need to do laundry?"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OFNFDA', 'answerTime': 'May 12, 2010', 'unixTime': 1273647600, 'question': "What do you wash your diapers in? I use the Fels Naptha-borax-washing soda combo for my clothes and I know they'll work with just prefolds but what about my BG all-in-ones?", 'answer': "I use Charlie's soap- powder on mine. It works great!"}
