{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OFT7O6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2011', 'unixTime': 1320912000, 'question': 'Anyone use cloth diapers who live in an apartment?', 'answer': "This is totally up to you. I use cloth, but they must be washed with a rinse, then a wash, then a rinse cycle and I usually do a load every 2nd day. Then I try to spend every 4th day doing a few loads of other laundry before the diapers. Are there enough machines that you won't be stuck without a washer when you need to do laundry?"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OFT7O6', 'answerTime': 'May 12, 2010', 'unixTime': 1273647600, 'question': "What do you wash your diapers in? I use the Fels Naptha-borax-washing soda combo for my clothes and I know they'll work with just prefolds but what about my BG all-in-ones?", 'answer': "I use Charlie's soap- powder on mine. It works great!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000OMSIN0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427180400, 'question': 'Will this gate work with drywall on one side and stair rail on the other side?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes this will work but make sure to use drywall anchors if there is no stud.'}
