{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OMSIN0', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': "Does this gate swing both ways or does it stop so it won't swing over stairs?", 'answer': "There is a plastic catch that theoretically is supposed to stop it from swinging over the stairs. However, it doesn't take a great deal of effort to push through. We've had many adults at our house unfamiliar with the gate, push it through and we rush to put it back in place. The gate has catch at the top and bottom. Once it is in place *correctly* at the top and bottom, it does feel sturdy. I like the gate, but it took a ton of time to put together."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OMSIN0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398063600, 'question': 'How tall is the gate? I have about 23 inches of wall to attach it to on one side.', 'answer': 'Our unit was, we just sold it at a garage sale, about 30 inches tall. Based on the method of installation 23 inches is not enough wall to work with for installation. The mounting hardware attaches at the top and bottom of the rail so you need an extra inch on the mounting surface beyond the rail height perhaps up to two inches above and below.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000OMSIN0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396422000, 'question': 'The banisters at the top of the stairs do not line up and one is a couple inches farther back. Will the mechanism be able to properly lock the gate?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. The gate should latch properly. I have the same siuation. The only issue we have is in opening the gate. The attached pin on the hinge side often pops out of the hole. It's an annoyance but not a big deal since it goes back in easily."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000OMSIN0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394780400, 'question': 'does it screw to metal', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think you'd have to purchase special screws."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OMSIN0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'My kids like to step on the open gate. Our other gates are pressure mount &amp; sit on the floor. Can anyone tell me if these will hold up to that abuse', 'answer': "No I would definitely NOT let your kids step on the gate. If it's only anchored into drywall, it will most likely pull out of the wall. Also, even though the gate is metal, the brackets are plastic. It's a tough gate but I wouldn't want my kid stepping or hanging on any gate, especially if it's at the top of the stairs. There isn't any gate I would recommend for that."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000OMSIN0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375599600, 'question': 'Does this gate come with all of the parts for assembly?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes! It was easy to install too. It's the only gate our son can't open and can't climb too."}
