{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OR3F1K', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'Help looking for harness to hold my extremely active 14 month old as I change his diaper tried everything to distract now looking for shoulder &amp; waist', 'answer': 'I have never done it but you could anchor the harness to the sides of the changing table if it is the rung type (you have to have something to slip it through and wrap around). The harness comes up pretty high. Your little one would still be able to wiggle and flail legs but it would probably keep him from flipping himself over. It would take a minute to get him all harnessed up each diaper changing but it may be worth it. My 17 month old is going through that same stage - freaking out during diaper changes.'}
