{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OS3AP0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398754800, 'question': 'On the BOB parts website it says that this works with Britax companion carseat- anyone tried it with the Britax Bsafe carseat?', 'answer': "I don't know about the Britax Bsafe... We used it with a Graco Snugride and it worked great. I remember thinking it was really expensive for what it really was, but after we had it, we would not have given it back. It worked great and felt really secure (but made the stroller a little top heavy on uneven terrain). Maybe you can compare the attachment points of the Graco and yours and decide. Also, have a look at the website www dot bobgear dot com. They will most likely list which adapter will fit your carseat. That's how we did it. Good luck."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384848000, 'question': 'does this kit on safety gates that are not Kidco brand?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It's just a kit that allows you to install a gate without damaging wood banisters...I used it with a Munchkin gate."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': 'May 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368946800, 'question': 'Will this work on metal banister/railing?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'All the installation kit is is a pair of plastic clamps that hold onto the railing. A wood bar attaches to the clamps with screws, and that piece of wood is how the fence attaches. As long as the metal railing is thick enough, there won\'t be a problem. And even if it\'s too thin, you could add a piece of rubber or padding to essentially make the railing thick enough to accept the minimum clamp allowance. It\'s an extremely simple design, and one you could easily makeshift with a 1"x2"x3\' pine board and two clamps from the hardware store.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406530800, 'question': 'How do I use the little plastic "shims"? The directions say these can be used to straighten out the top and bottom, but I don\'t see where to put them.', 'answer': "The shims snap onto the wooden board. After you install the brackets on the railing, hold the board against the brackets and see if it's straight. If not, snap one of the shims onto the board and try again. Slide the shim along the board so that it is even with the bracket, and sits between the board and the bracket. When you have it straight, install the board by screwing right through the board, shims and brackets (in that order)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385539200, 'question': "What are the dimensions of the plastic clamps that go around the banister? Our banister is thicker and want to know if it'll fit.", 'answer': 'The part that goes around the banister is able to be sized to your banister. It is two separate pieces so you can make it as tight or as loose as needed.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403766000, 'question': 'Given how bad the instructions are (see reviews), how DOES one install this correctly? For instance -- where do the small wood blocks go?', 'answer': 'Between the banister and the plastic piece only if needed'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': '26 days ago', 'question': 'We have a metal railing and the posts are 1" x 1" thick. Is that thick enough for this product to work?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it will. I did use a piece of the wood included which I cut to size to fill in a small gap. Behind the piece that secures it to the metal railing.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424764800, 'question': 'Could I put this around a hand railing? We are having difficulties finding a gate as we have a hand railing on one side of the stairs and post on othe', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I think you in theory could turn it sideways (if that's what you're thinking) and install in that way- or at an angle. Just make sure when you install your gate to the installation kit that you measure carefully and install level. As long as you fit it tight to the railing you should be good. Hope that helps!"}
