{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423900800, 'question': 'Will this kit work on a banister that is round on both top and the bottom (obviously being thinner at the top) ? Thanks in advance', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, you need an additional part that squares off the roundness of the banister.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000P007FI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421827200, 'question': 'How do you mount on a spindle that is skinny on top and bottom? How do you make the bottom fitting tighter like the "top" piece is?', 'answer': "Mine is skinnier at top, however if yours is skinny on both ends I'm sure you can tighten it equally.. Another possibility is to buy the round spare part to add to the bottom piece. I am very happy with mine, my dogs can take it off now"}
