{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000PRUAFI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412751600, 'question': 'Has anyone mounted this gate without the stick pads and if so, how well does it work?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm using mine as a little porch gate to contain my pooch; the gate is mounted to the brick sides of the opening without the pads and it's been fine. I think whether using it without the pads is going to vary, based on the texture of the surface it's mounted to. If you're concerned about protecting drywall, I think it would be counter-productive; you're going to damage the surface either way - it's pressure-mounted, so it's going to dig into it probably worse without the pads. Either way, you're going to need to do at least some minimal repair when you remove the gate."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000PRUAFI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420790400, 'question': 'I have a 36" door opening. Will It work. F so will I need to use both extensions?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it will fit. You will definitely use both extensions, but this will allow the gate to be centered and look much nicer imo.'}
