{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Q5KH3E', 'answerTime': 'Jun 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403506800, 'question': 'does it fit on the graco pack and play', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This is how the mobile attaches: If you look at the picture (lower left hand corner), there is a round disk that unscrews from the main arm of the mobile. You insert the screw between the slats of the crib, then screw back on the round disk (which is larger than the gap between slats). So unless the pack and play has an opening it wouldn't work. Most pack and plays I'm familiar with have the side netting attached all the way up to the top bar, so there would be no way this mobile could attach to it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Q5KH3E', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403161200, 'question': 'I cannot tell how it attaches. Could you attach it to the top of an infant bouncy seat?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I don't think you'll be able to attach it. The arm is designed to work with the bars of the baby's bed. It has two large flat parts separated by a screw, by tightening it with the bars in the middle you attach it to the bed."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Q5KH3E', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'It does not fit on my crib. Is there any kit to attach it to a wide crib?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I did not want to mark up my crib so I got a piece of wood a little taller than the crib, drilled a hold in it to attach this, and then used some of the pull away sticky tabs to secure the wood to the wall behind the crib. No marking up the crib, a perfect fit and very secure. Paint the wood to match the wall and you will never notice it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Q7G3VM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382684400, 'question': "The mirror at the end is super cloudy. Is there a plastic film over it? If there is, I can't find an edge to peel it off. Anyone else have this issue?", 'answer': "WOW! Wat a difference. Just grabbed mine to inspect it. It was cloudly! There isn't a place to peal it, but from a tad bit of wear, the stitches of the cloth border had sort of torn at that film stuff, so I was able to scratch at that and rip it off. Doesn't give the impression it was supposed to be removed, but it did come off and now it's nice and shiny!!! So thank you!!! Take a pair of scissors or a paper clip, and just kind of scratch along the edge until it tears open a bit and rip the thing!"}
