{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000RFC3BM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412060400, 'question': 'are they microwaveable?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "They're very thin - so even if you could I wouldn't advise it, they'd probably warp. Plus plastic leaches into food when it comes into contact with heat (remember, don't drink water from a plastic bottle that's been left in your car)... and even things that are BPA Free still have toxic chemicals... so I'd stick with using a glass or ceramic container. These are great for serving snacks in or storing small amounts of food in."}
