{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UCWXOY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424332800, 'question': 'Up to what age and weight my baby can use it? txs', 'answer': 'Age and weight won\'t matter since it lays on a solid surface like the floor or a bed, it\'s the size of your child. Assembled item dimensions with sides down equals L 52.5" x W 34.75" x D 1.25". and the sides are about 9 inches so with sides up I think it\'s about 34 inches long. This was a great for when we didn\'t want to drag a huge, heavy pack n play along for trips or even a day at grandmas house! It gave our babies a safe area to sleep. I hated just laying them on the floor in a room while at someones home, so we would use this often. Light/easy to pack alternative. I would suggest using from 0-12mo.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UCWXOY', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407222000, 'question': "This doesn't seem to have breatheable material on the sides. Are there concerns for older, mobile babies and SIDS, getting smooshed against the side?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It isn't breathable material, but it is also pretty stable. I don't think an older baby would get smooshed into the edges. However, I also don't think it would fit well for a mobile baby. Our son grew out of it in about 3 months. It was simply too narrow for him to sleep comfortably."}
