{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UGUF5O', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'How is the stage 2 nipple? Is it a pretty fast flow or is it still conservative (to mimic the breast)?', 'answer': 'Conservative! They still have to work at it to get the milk to come out. It mimics the breast still, but nothing like when we let down, it will allow the child to get more milk at their pace. I stayed with the advised 3+ months before introducing it since they seem to be better "suckers" and can handle a faster flow. If the child can\'t work the stage 1 nipple then they may still have problems with the stage 2.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UGUF5O', 'answerTime': 'Aug 8, 2009', 'unixTime': 1249714800, 'question': 'cost: Are these nipples really $49.99?', 'answer': 'no they are 8.99 for 2 stage 2 flow nipples.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UGUF5O', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412060400, 'question': 'Is this stage 2 nipple a variable speed?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It has a larger opening to allow more milk through, but it all depends on the child and how well they suck on the bottle. All of these bottles make the child "work" to get their food and is the closest simulation to breast feeding which worked great for a full time working mom who nursed before and after work. Had no problems going back and forth between bottle and breast.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398409200, 'question': 'So there is absolutely NO flame retardant? NO chemicals? Then how does it meet federal and state flammability standards?', 'answer': 'Naturepedic mattresses do meet all State and Federal flammability standards. The organic cotton used in Naturepedic mattresses is far less flammable than the polyurethane foam and other synthetic materials used in other mattresses. The organic cotton tends to smoulder, not burst into flames. The steel coils are not flammable. And this mattress does meet all safety requirements - without the use of toxic chemicals.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409814000, 'question': 'What were the dimensions of the crib sheets you bought Do the crib sheets fit the mattress well? Can you recommend some crib sheets for this mattress?', 'answer': 'I totally had trouble finding sheets to fit!! Since it\'s so much thicker than cheapo mattresses, it was a challenge. What I found worked GREAT were the Circo brand jersey knit sheets from Target. They are so stretchy (and soft!) and fit great. I also have one Pottery Barn sheet that was given to us that happens to work well, and a Dr. Seuss flannel sheet found on Amazon.com that was labeled "deep pockets." These all work well - Id recommend the Circo jersey knit or any that say they are deep pocket - these tend to be more expensive higher quality sheets. They will all say they fit "standard" crib mattresses, so the dimensions won\'t do much good - stretchier sheets fit much better than standard woven sheets. Good luck! It was worth the search in order to have the mattress!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': 'How can you tell the infant side apart from the toddler side? The instructions clearly say there is a difference and to flip at 8-12 months.', 'answer': "I wasn't aware there's a difference in the sides. They both look the same. We're planning on flipping the infant mattress every 6 or so months, at New Year's and the Fourth of July, as we do with our own mattresses."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': '3 days ago', 'question': 'is this mattress heavy?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Definitely heavier than a standard crib mattress but totally manageable. When I change the crib sheet I generally pull out one end and lift the whole thing on top of the crib to rest diagonally so I don't have to hold it up while also wrangling the sheet. This makes the weight not an issue for me."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414047600, 'question': 'Will this fit the Pottery Barn kendall crib?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Based on my own experience, cribs and crib mattresses come in a standard size and this one is no exception. I have the Pottery Barn Thomas crib and it fits perfectly. Unless the Kendall is some odd shape or extra long, it will definitely fit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412665200, 'question': 'Is this mattress 2 sided? with a newborn or toddler side? Or can either side be used for newborns?', 'answer': "It has a firmer and a less firm side, but, both are fine for an infant to use. I still use mine with my toddler now, two years later. It's a great mattress."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408777200, 'question': 'Which polyethylene grade is used in the mattress?', 'answer': 'Tested and Certified by Greenguard. The Classic surface is pure food-grade polyethylene, resembling a surface more like a traditional crib mattress but without any harmful chemicals. Made in USA.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407222000, 'question': 'Does this mattress really weigh 50 pounds?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No, that's a mistake in their labelling on Amazon. I have 2, they're about 20 pounds each."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402297200, 'question': 'Does this mattress need a separate waterproof cover or can I just use it with normal crib sheets?', 'answer': 'This has a waterproof cover on one side, but we used another waterproof cover on top of it to protect our investment (just in case). We have used it at times without the cover and we have not had any leaks go through, so you could probably do without the cover with no problem.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UN30Q8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388563200, 'question': "How do I know which side is the firm side?? I can't figure it out by just feeling it...", 'answer': "It's the same on both sides. Naturepedic makes another mattress that has a plush side and a water resistant side, but this one is the same on both...water resistant covering."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UPSVPG', 'answerTime': 'Jun 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403506800, 'question': 'Have you used this on an umbrella stroller? Any problem with the fit? I want to use this while traveling and am not lugging my big stroller. Thanks', 'answer': "I think it will be too wide but if you have a clip of some sort you could make it work. Your stroller has to have a canopy of some sort or it will not work! It would be right in the child's face."}
