{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UUBRYI', 'answerTime': 'Sep 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380006000, 'question': 'How big can the baby be to use this car seat?', 'answer': 'My daughter is petite, but at 14 months, she still easily fits in it. My niece was a bigger baby and was in hers for over a year as well. They say up to 30 pounds, which should last most for a year, if not more. Love mine!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UUBRYI', 'answerTime': '5 days ago', 'question': 'Does this base work for the Chicco KeyFit infant carseat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'John, which infant seat do you have?'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UUBRYI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424246400, 'question': 'I just purchased the keyfit car system for my daughter who is expecting in april. do i need a 2nd car seat for my car, or just the stand?', 'answer': "You only need the base (stand). I just leave the extra base installed in my car rather than transferring and installing my daughter-in-law's base all the time. The carseat clicks easily into the base."}
