{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UZFMH6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2012', 'unixTime': 1355817600, 'question': 'where can you buy ameda spare parts locally', 'answer': "I have not found any place locally that carries this... I can find medella parts locally but I haven't found any ameda parts locally. I know our local (small town pharmacy) carries some breast pump parts, and babies r us carries some breast part parts too so may be try there"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'May 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368514800, 'question': 'Can we attach 4 wheels to the co sleeper? (attaching 4 wheels to 4 leg extensions) All the images show it with 2.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I don't know if you CAN, but I don't think you SHOULD. The two wheels work fine to move it around, you just pick it up by the end without wheels. The wheels don't really lock, so I don't think it would be very safe to have four wheels."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363762800, 'question': 'Is it practical to move every morning to another room?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, I would say it is very practical. The part that anchors it to the bed can be removed at the co-sleeper by unsnapping two hooks very quickly. The bed itself is very light, probably no more than 10 pounds, so even a c-section recoveree can move it. It's also on wheels, so if you don't have carpet you can just wheel it around."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358668800, 'question': 'Question about sheet size for mini co-sleeper convertibles: What dimensions are the sheets that fit the mini co-sleepers?', 'answer': 'There is a sheet on amazon for this that says it is 19 x 33: http://www.amazon.com/Arms-Reach-Co-Sleeper-Bassinet-Natural/dp/B001O5GINS/ref=wl_it_dp_o_pC_nS_nC?ie=UTF8&colid=1147PB6NQDTPE&coliid=I2B4P10G67SHQO'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390550400, 'question': 'is it sturdy?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, but maybe not past about 25-35 lbs. Once the baby is rolling and moving more it may become less sturdy as well.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386921600, 'question': 'What is the purpose of the quilted coverlet-type thing? Does it stay on for sleeping or as a play pen?', 'answer': "It's really just to cover the plastic and metal frame. non-functional."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384416000, 'question': 'What are the inside dimensions of the sleeper (height, width, length)?', 'answer': 'I do not have the sleeper - it was a gift - however, both the recipients of the sleeper have used it until the infants were at least 3 months old and found it very useful.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384070400, 'question': 'Can anyone tell me about the play pen? is it spicous enough for babies to maneveur around?', 'answer': "The mini is big enough for a small child I wouldn't put a 1 yr old or older in it. It is however amazing for co-sleeping with out worrying about rolling over on your baby."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364972400, 'question': 'This co cleeper comes with a firm matteress and a matteress sheet - correct? Do I need anything else apart from this product for assembly?', 'answer': 'For assembly? No. It has everything you need for the initial build. I would recommend buying some other sheets, standard bassinet sheets will work even if you have to tuck in some loose parts, and a waterproof cover for those middle of the night "oopses", but in general, you have everything you need with the initial buy.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383202800, 'question': 'Does the bottom section have a zipper to allow for storing items underneath?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, it doesn't have zipper as it is ment to be convertible to pack and play. It probably would not be safe. But it is airy so you can definitely store in items you will need later on. It just is not for things you just want to out away for a day. Hope that helps. But I think there is a different model with the storage/zipper option. Btw we loved our co sleeper. Mary"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UZRRBU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379919600, 'question': 'is the mattress/ edge adjustable so that you can have it on an even level with your bed and attach it to your bed?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'to paraphrase the information which comes with the cot, it fits adult beds of 22 or 24 inches from floor to top of adult mattress. For adult beds 22 inches from floor to top mattress remove the 2 inch segment me check for adult matresses 26 inches to 30 inches a leg extension kit model number 9810 can be purchased separately. We had no issue with the fit, I am guessing most beds are 22 24 inches high. We used the 24 inch option and it was just brilliant.'}
