{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000V88HJM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': "Looking for nail clippers to use after birth so baby won't scratch her face. I hate the baby mittens. Would these work to use at birth?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I didn't use clippers, files, or anything on my daughter after butth. The problem with those is that their nails are connected to the skin and I mean right to the edge. The nurse advised us to wait until they started to peel and just peel them off, if they didn't come right off then they aren't ready. It works great! These would work best after the baby is a few month. They are amazing clippers! I highly recommend them, very sharp unlike dull grown up clippers, and are great even for adult nails. Good luck with you're baby and hope you have a wonderful birth!"}
