{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000V9IB0G', 'answerTime': 'Jun 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404025200, 'question': 'I want to cover the kids 12x12 bedroom carpet with these. Do you think is will work? Do I need to tack done plastic first? Does dye bleed?', 'answer': "I'd be perfect. We used it on carpet with our first child and now over wood flooring for our second. You don't need to put any underlayment. If spills happen, just lift up the foam and dry all areas quickly to avoid growing any mold. After 2 years, mine is still in perfect condition, none of the colors bled & it's easy to wipe down (for sanitation purposes if you have a baby who crawls/is teething). My only complaint is the smell when you first open the package-air it out somewhere dry and away from the kids for a day or two. Enjoy!"}
