{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000VVIHPS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406271600, 'question': 'How to set the Kids Sleep Classic?', 'answer': 'Press "set", the rightmost button. It will flash to set either a 24 hour or 12 hour clock. Use the up and down arrows to choose, then press set. Now it will have you select the current hour of the day. Use the up and down arrows to select the hour, then press set. Now you set the minutes the same way. Press set when you finish that. Next you select the hour of the time you want naptime to end, then press set. Next, select the minute of the hour for naptime to end, then press set. Next set the hour of morning wake-up, then press set. Next set the minute of morning wake up. Then leave the clock to flash until it shows the current time. If at any time you leave the clock to flash for too long before you are done, it will save your settings and then revert back to the current time display. To continue setting nap or morning wake up times, you start the directions at the very beginning. The slider on top has four settings: off, nightlight only, day/night light, and alarm. Off is... Off. The nightlight makes the whole face glow, which is great for the picture that is just one animal sleeping. The day/night light is to be use with the picture that is half day, half night. If you have set it correctly, once you switch it to day/night light, the bottom light (night) should be on while your child is sleeping, and the top light (day) should be on when it is wake up time. The alarm setting is the same as the day/night light except when it is wake up time, it has a VERY loud chirping bird alarm that caused my two-year-old to come tearing out of his room because "birds are in my room!!!" :)) There you go! It looks complicated typed out, but one you figure it out, it is quite simple :) Good luck!'}
