{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000WPBAVQ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': 'Good for dogs?', 'answer': "depends on location... if you have it configured as shown in the picture and it is outside you could stake it to the ground. I have mine indoors right now to keep my Australian shepherd out of the family room so he doesn't eat the Legos - one side is tucked behind a side table and the other aside the couch, with the gate at the pass through into that area... and that works great. but I did set it up octagonally and my dog dragged it all over the garage since it wasn't tied down to anything... it is very versatile - I think it has paid for itself in so many ways with both my kids and my pets"}
