{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000WUD83O', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395385200, 'question': "Must babies be able to hold their heads up completely for them to use this? Or will their head be somewhat supported if it's still a tad wobbly?", 'answer': "I would suggest your child be able to hold their head up on their own as the back support isn't built in such a way to hold up their head and neck. My nephew set in this when he was much younger and it was fine for him to look around at the items but they used a small pillow to add support."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000WUD83O', 'answerTime': 'Jan 11, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420963200, 'question': "Can I remove the red bar to disassemble the jumperoo for storage? I'm trying to do it, but no sucess. how do I do it?", 'answer': 'As far as I know, it cannot be removed. Nothing can be disasbled, at least for me nothing could. When I brought it over to my sisters & moms for babysitting, I had to put the entire thing aasembledin the back of my SUV. That is the only thing that I did not like about the jumperoo other wise I think its the best one by far. I think its for safety reasons.'}
