{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000XDYLEK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 4, 2010', 'unixTime': 1275634800, 'question': 'Can I use this at home instead of a bassinet for my newborn?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "no--I own this and it's a great travel crib, but because you have to bend over pretty far to pick up a little baby out of the crib, it would get tiring very fast. I highly recommend the arms reach mini co sleeper for a bassinet. I used it with my older child and my twins, until each was about 3-4 mos old, then graduated to crib. I LOVE this travel crib, but not for a regular crib/bassinet for newborn."}
{'answer': "I don't think so. You just need to make sure your fitted crib sheet is taut and there is no rumpling. On a side note we just returned from another trip with our two kids where this item was a lifesaver! It fits perfectly into our largest suitcase, folds up quickly and easily and was great for many places in Europe where they don't have pack and plays available. Our 16 month old has slept in it quite comfortably, and before that my 2 year old slept in it.", 'asin': 'B000XDYLEK', 'answerTime': '23 days ago', 'question': 'BabyBjorn for newborns? Is the mattress too soft? I was going to have my newborn sleep in this full time until we move. Is the mattress too soft?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
