{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000XDYLEK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404802800, 'question': 'Is it possible to push this over while standing inside? Woke up to my little guy (18mo 90%) trying to push it over and getting 2 feet of the ground.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I would say no. That never happened for us. I used this for my son a lot and have used it for my daughter as well. My son jumped out if his big crib just after 2 1/2. I don't recall when he was able to get out of the Bjorn but we never had a safety issue with it. It's the best!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000XDYLEK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392451200, 'question': 'My daughter is very tall. She is 2 1/2 and is approx 38in tall. Will she be too tall to lay down comfortably? Will her feet touch ends?', 'answer': 'My son is 34 inches tall and if he stretches his toes he has about 2-3 inches on either end. If he lays diagonally a there is bit more room. So depends how your daughter sleeps.'}
