{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000XHQTFA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 26, 2008', 'unixTime': 1222412400, 'question': 'Graco Safeseat- do the straps adjust like the cheap Snugride? Does that also apply to the Safeseat?', 'answer': 'The safe seat does not adjust in the back, it adjust just like convertable does...by pulling the webbing between the babies leg at the end of the seat. Hope that helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000XHQTFA', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2007', 'unixTime': 1171526400, 'question': 'Color? How do you go about choosing the fabric you would like?', 'answer': 'i\'m not sure exactly what you\'re asking, but maybe i can help. this pattern is called "ionic" - if you search amazon.com under "graco safeseat" you\'ll see more patterns, or you can go to gracobaby.com and browse the patterns there. i personally think this is one of the best patterns on the market right now, but if you\'re looking for something else, check other retailers. some patterns are specific to certain retailers (i.e. french roast is only available at babies\'r\'us). hope that helps...kelly'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000XHQTFA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 25, 2007', 'unixTime': 1190703600, 'question': 'can you wash the material part of the seat? With what can you wash the inside of the seat when the material gets dirty?', 'answer': 'Yes. The padding on the Infant SafeSeat is removable for machine wash on the delicate cycle. Drip dry. The metal and plastic parts may be cleaned with mild soap and water and wiped dry with a cloth or towel. To clean the buckle, use a damp cloth or sponge. The harness straps may be spot cleaned. Never use bleach to clean this product.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000XHQTFA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2007', 'unixTime': 1198828800, 'question': 'Grocery carts? One reviewer mentioned the Safe seat did not fit onto a shopping cart like the older models--is this true?', 'answer': "Well this is the way I look at it. I have big babies (over 9lbs at birth) and my first two grew out of there other infant seats at 3-4 months old. Still being too little to sit in the cart on there own but to big for the infant seat. So to me any negatives that there might be of this seat are far outweighed by the fact that I don't have to worry about my soon to be new baby outgrowing the seat so fast."}
