{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000XP96VQ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361260800, 'question': 'Has the seat length to canopy been fixed? The reviews that mention this are all over a year old.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not exactly sure what answer you're looking for. My 3 1/2 yr old fits under the canopy, however, my 6 yr old does not. He sits comfortly in the seat, but it too tall to use the shade as he's just shy of 48 inches."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000XP96VQ', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428303600, 'question': 'Is the seat comfortable for the child (meaning plenty of padding?)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'There is almost no padding, however we took it to Disney and my kids used it all day and never complained about being uncomfortable. It is roomy, because my 3 year old can switch positions.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000XP96VQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388390400, 'question': 'Can canopy be removed? I need a stroller for 60 lb/4 ft boy. Hes probably too tall to use with canopy.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The canopy folds almost flat against the handle bar; I am fairly confident you would be okay without removing it. To directly answer your question, after inspecting my stroller the canopy appears to come off by either a set of screws at the hinge point or a screw at the base of each hoop. Both methods would require removing a screw on each side of the handle bar to get all of the cloth off.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000XP96VQ', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372316400, 'question': 'Would it fit a child that is 44" tall? Would it be ridiculously big to drag on and off the bus at Disney World?', 'answer': "My 5yr old twins take turns riding in mine when my baby isn't in it. It isn't much harder to push. As for the Disney World question. If it were me I'd take it. It will probably be a little clunky but for me the benefits would outweigh the hassle. The fact that's the vizor shades so well and the search reclines completely. Plus the cup holders and extra compartments. All pluses for me at an amusement park."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000XP96VQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2012', 'unixTime': 1356768000, 'question': 'Is this stroller good for running long distances? Would I be better off buying the BOB Revolution? Thank you!', 'answer': "We have really loved using this stroller for running and it does really well. Haven't tried the BOB so can't say. But overall we have definitely enoyed it for walking, running, everything. One of the best things is that you can lock the front wheel for running or you can unlock it for walking. Lots of other joggers that we saw only have a locked front wheel. The only problem we've had with it is that it would pull to one side when locked. We figured out that the front wheel was not totally straight and contacted Joovy for a replacement. They were SUPER easy to work with and we got the new one in two days. Great customer service is always a big plus for products."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000XP96VQ', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427612400, 'question': 'What bug net will fit this?', 'answer': 'Hello Corey, Any bug net with dimensions 5.6 x 5.2 x 2.2 inches will fit with the Joovy Zoom 360 Swivel Wheel Jogging Stroller. Frequently bought bug net is of Jeep Mosquito and Bug Net. Please do contact us back for any further assistance.'}
