{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Y2GY40', 'answerTime': 'Feb 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392364800, 'question': 'What is the best way to clean inside the flexi straw part? I am using the cup for milk so I want to be sure to clean the straw properly.', 'answer': "I use the dishwasher... Those straws are a pain in the butt to get clean any other way. I can't even be sure they are all that clean after the dishwasher but I'd think that'd be the best solution. Good luck! PS-I use one of those top rack dishwasher container thingys that you put smaller stuff in (ie. Straws, bottle nipples, small bottle parts) for the straws."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Y89Y5U', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373439600, 'question': 'is this jacket good for a 11 month old', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "My kids have been boating for a long time and have always used Lil' Legends vests they are now 7 and 9 so I don't remember the sizes they used first. For purpose, quality and looks they can't be beat. They have a tag with size recommendations, please make sure you do the homework on which one will work best for you kid's age/size."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Y89Y5U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385366400, 'question': 'Does it have a harness loop on the back to put a tether to a jackline?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'From a grandfather sailor w/ 15 grandchildren: No! West Marine has a very excellent safe and proper. child\'s harness w/ a large reinforced "D" ring for attaching a proper tether. Preventing man overboard and keeping a kid afloat are best seen as separate concerns, especially w/ toddlers and non-swimmers. Lin'}
