{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000YZD0QM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2009', 'unixTime': 1234771200, 'question': 'Will this seat fit in a honda civic? Anyone know if it will fit?', 'answer': "This really would depend on how you have to have your front seats positioned. I know a mom who has this seat installed rear-facing in an older model 2 door honda civic and she has no issues with getting it installed or using it with her daughter. Best advice would be to hit up a babies r us or another store that allows you to take the seat out to the car and try it in the back seat where you want to place your child. Remember though it will likely fit nicer when properly installed by a tech then when you take it out to the car to try it. You will need a pool noodle (my recommendation) or a rolled towel to get a good Rear-facing install. Once you know if it would fit come on-line and order it for a better deal and nicer covers. I can't say enough positive things about this seat. I passed up buying a First Years (Compass) True Fit and Britax Marathon or Boulevard for this seat and I wouldn't trade it for any of the seats on the market today."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z3BT3Y', 'answerTime': 'Jan 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422172800, 'question': 'Does the top changing pad part come off? Just wondering about when they are done with diapers. Can it come off or is it attached?', 'answer': "It comes off. It just sits on top of the dresser & attaches with a few screws on the back. When you're done with diapers, it's easy to remove."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z3BT3Y', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389600000, 'question': 'i am confused by the changing pad explanation. what size changing pad can i put on top?', 'answer': "As far as I am aware, there's only one standard changing pad size. Approximately 32 x 16 inches."}
