{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z3DWHK', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': 'What is the measurement of the boxes it ship in?', 'answer': 'It\'s been about a year and a half since we bought this so I don\'t know exactly. Based on the dimensions shown in product details the length of box would be slightly more than the 53.9" and the width would be an inch or so more than the 35" height of the crib. The final dimension would equate to the depth (front to back). Since it is packed like a "flat" puzzle, I would guess the height of the packed box is about only the total of the thicknesses of all the pieces layed flat, maybe 12"-18". In a nutshell, roughly 55"L x 36"W x 15"H, not that large and easy to handle. It will fit thru any opening into a house easily. Hope this helps you more than it confuses you!'}
