{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000ZK3YBC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427094000, 'question': 'are the baby food trays any different than the breast milk trays?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes they are quite different. Food trays are usually made with silicone material and I found that when using those for my breastmilk the breast milk would stay behind on the walls or forms if you will. Basically the fat content of your breast milk :( also it's harder to remove the solid breast milk after it's frozen in general from the silicone/plastic forms. I've used the beaba, green sprouts, fresh baby, and so many others just because I wanted to store bigger sizes and the tried and true is what keeps me coming back to the Milkies trays. It's just easier to freeze and remove and so much more cost efficient. Not to mention it's medical grade!! Ultimately you get to keep your fat content from your breast milk and that's important for your baby. Hind milk is the fattiest and most nutritional part of breast milk for your baby. Other forms of storing breast milk and freezing take that important fat from baby. If you don't want to use Milkies trays I strongly suggest using broscillate glass bottles for freezer and the only bottle I am aware of that is made of this type of glass is life factory. I can't afford the price tags on that so I that's why I stick with Milkies milk trays :) its affordable and more importantly keeps all my breast milk nutrients and fat composition intact for my baby :)"}
