{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000ZK3YBC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397718000, 'question': "I'm concerned about using these at daycare. With my first child, they just thawed the bags that they needed for the day in the fridge and what wasn't used was used the next day. I'm not sure how they would thaw these sticks for a day's worth of milk at...", 'answer': "In fact, it's easier--each stick is frozen separately, so the daycare provider (I had a nanny but I'm sure a daycare used to handling breastmilk would work the same way) can just thaw what they need at one time for each feeding. This way you never need to worry about extra that won't be used for over 24 hrs and thus need to be thrown out."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000ZK3YBC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397718000, 'question': 'Has anyone using this product mass stored breastmilk? With my 1st child I used milk bags and I had months stored up. I was just wondering if there were any problems.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have. I pump several times a day and have since my 7-month old was born. We have TONS freezer bags filled with these milk sticks. I double bag them, one freezer bag inside of the other. They are quite easy to remove from the bag and do not stick together. It is very easy to snap the frozen sticks in half, also. I do not have any experience with milk bags but my husband and I are very happy with the trays and will use them for the next baby, too.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000ZKHVMU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417420800, 'question': 'Is this the exact same product as http://amzn.com/B001OIVDE4 ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "RinseWorks makes the Bum Genius sprayers as well as the Aquaus, so they are likely almost identical. There may be slight differences in, say, plastic vs metal parts, but I've seen it said on many reviews/forums that they are the same sprayer."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000ZKHVMU', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407308400, 'question': "What's the difference between this and a bidet sprayer?", 'answer': 'I own this sprayer and it is a far cry better than a bidet sprayer. The first "diaper sprayer" we purchased was really a bidet, and it didn\'t have the pressure that the bumGenius Diaper Sprayer has. The adjustable pressure on this product also makes a big difference when it comes to spraying off diapers.'}
