{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0010AN0JC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384329600, 'question': 'After having these for a while, do you kids still enjoy playing with them?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We've had them for almost a year now, not too long but awhile. My kids (2 &5) find some way to play with them a few times a week, not quite daily. They still get a lot of use and in many different ways. I highly recommend them. (They are very durable also. Still look and play like new!)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010AN0JC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423209600, 'question': 'Can you add pieces to this set? I would like to add a step to it; could it be combined with the Foamnasium soft play forms?', 'answer': 'The pieces do not attach you can place them in what ever order or use them individually. So adding other pieces would work just fine. However, a young child works best with only one or two because they do move when climbed on and can move apart with the crawling child falling through. The child however loves to pick them up and place them in different ways to engage in different play these are excellent for gross motor activity.'}
