{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010AN0JC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411369200, 'question': 'What are the sizes of the other pieces? I only see the ramp size listed.', 'answer': 'They are all proportional to the ramp. so the rectangle is the same width and the height of the tallest part of the ramp, the half circle is the same width, and the tallest part is as tall as the tallest part of the ramp, etcd.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010AN0JC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405839600, 'question': 'how do you keep these from sliding around? my 8 month old pushes them around as he is trying to climb on them. we have carpet and hardwood floors', 'answer': 'You could try some slip-not fabric under the pieces and even use double-sided tape to secure the fabric corners to the hardwood floor. Mary'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010BKO9A', 'answerTime': 'Aug 20, 2009', 'unixTime': 1250751600, 'question': 'Fit a Graco Carseat?? Can anyone tell me if you can sit a Graco carseat on it?', 'answer': 'I have this stroller and did use a graco carseat. It "sits" in there fine, we used the seat belt of the stroller and hooked it to where the seatbelt goes through the carseat. It did intrude on the other kids space, and it COULD fall out if hit very hard. It worked fine for us, though!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010BKO9A', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2011', 'unixTime': 1302591600, 'question': 'fit chicco keyfit 30 carseat? does this fit the chicco carseat?', 'answer': "I have a keyfit 30 chicco carseat and am planning on purchasing this stroller soon. We were able to try out the carseat with this stroller in the store. It does fit, but not perfectly. There is some little plastic snap that I think helps make the combi car seat fit. If you take this off (very easy to do) you have a little more room to wedge the chicco down in it. It's a little hard to wedge in there and maybe even harder with a newborn in it but it's good enough for me. Also, getting the right angle so the little one is not leaning too forward or backwards takes a little bit of playing with. Considering the fact that no other stroller besides the huge front/back double stroller that chicco sells fits the keyfit30, this stroller is a no brainer for me as we wont be buying another carseat. When my first was a newborn he didn't like sitting in the carseat at all and so I often just laid the seat all the way down in our stroller and let him lay in there. You could do the same with this stroller as well since it lays back pretty far. I compared the combi carseat with the chicco carseat and they are the only two with similar snap styles (on the sides) and the rounded bottom. The combi carseat is a bit narrower. Most of the time I will probably just put the baby in the stroller reclined, but if I have to or really want to put the infant carrier in their I know I can."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010BKO9A', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2011', 'unixTime': 1296201600, 'question': 'Carseat safe in stroller? Any suggestions????', 'answer': 'This is just my idea - but the lap straps are so long so can you buckle it in?'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010BKO9A', 'answerTime': 'Mar 28, 2011', 'unixTime': 1301295600, 'question': "storage really that small? I saw that some reviewers said their diaper bags won't fit in the storage baskets..they don't list any measurements though, exactly how small are these?", 'answer': 'Its not big enough to fit a diaper bag in them....you could fit a sweatshirt or something small but not a diaper bag. We have a diaper bag that has the stroller clips so its able to hang onto the handle and that is the reason this stroller works for us.'}
