{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010L98DI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414566000, 'question': 'Where do you put the adjustable locking ring? Direction on how to adjust it based on how much formula you are mixing would be helpful', 'answer': 'The locking ring (little blue figure-8 shaped plastic washer on the center stem) must be below the level of the formula you are mixing. So, if you are mixing 24 oz, you set it at, say, 20 oz. It is kind of a pain to move it, so I have left ours in a higher position, especially since we are mixing up a day\'s worth at a time. The ring prevents the mixing blade (in the photo, at the bottom) from coming above the level of formula and introducing too much air during the "cyclonic" mixing. I hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010L98DI', 'answerTime': 'May 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400310000, 'question': 'how does this mixer work? is it a hand mixer or motor?', 'answer': 'Hand mixer but it works great. My son had terrible reflux and was on thick formula. This worked great to keep it from being too clumpy.'}
