{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010L98DI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375772400, 'question': 'Can you sterilize this? What is the number (generally within a triangle) written at the bottom?', 'answer': "Product Description The formula mixing pitcher from Dr. Brown's eases formula preparation by allowing up to 4 bottles to be mixed and stored at one time. Unique features include a mixing blade that quickly dissolves formula with no clumping, and an adjustable stopper that prohibits the mixing blade from lifting above the surface of the liquid as to keep air introduction to a minimum. The compact size, locking lid, soft grip handle, and ribbed pitcher spout offer comfort and convenience when pouring. Disassembles without difficulty for easy cleaning. Dishwasher safe. BPA Free"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010PW47Q', 'answerTime': 'Sep 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379660400, 'question': 'Is the Ergo sold by amazon a fake? Not from third party sellers, but amazon directly?', 'answer': 'Mine was sold directly from Amazon and was a fake, verified by the manufacturer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010PW47Q', 'answerTime': 'Aug 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376118000, 'question': 'How often do you use the hip &amp; back carry position? Is it comfortable for baby and mom in that position?', 'answer': "I don't use the hip carry position that often because I feel like it's complicated to get into and my daughter didn't really like it. I use the back carry position the most because it is fairly easy to get into and it distributes my daughters weight better. I'm small and she weighs 25 lbs so it's easier for me to carry her that way. It seems comfortable to her-- she's fallen asleep in the back carry position before. I still use the front carry position sometimes too-- just depends on the mood I'm in. Let me know if you have any other questions-- I love this product."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010PW47Q', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412060400, 'question': "I've got a 23lb 10 month old - is it worth it to make this purchase?", 'answer': 'My daughter is 28 lbs (will be 2yrs old in December) and I still use my ergo all the time! I even used the back carry feature for my 5 yr old this summer! I love my ergo and say, yes totally worth the purchase vs other carriers.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010PW47Q', 'answerTime': 'Jul 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373698800, 'question': 'I just got an Ergobaby Camel color. Any of you have washed it before? I am wondering if it will be hard to clean it since is such a light color. Tks!', 'answer': 'I have washed mine in machine & even threw it in dryer on air dry for like 20 mins& it came out like new.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010PW47Q', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'how does the Ergo really fit with a 30-35 lb toddler?', 'answer': 'Yes, I still carry my 35lb, three year old on my back. She still loves it. I know she will be too heavy soon, but I will still carry her until she no longer wants to be on my back!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010PW47Q', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379919600, 'question': "How big is this for the parent? I'm a big girl 250 when I found out I was pregnant. Is this going to fit around my waist comfortably too?", 'answer': "There seems to be a lot of room to adjust the waist strap and would probably be okay. I've seen these at Babies R Us and Target but purchased mine from Amazon. You could look at the carrier in the store and try it on and then order from Amazon."}
