{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010WAXN6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394352000, 'question': 'how does it recline?', 'answer': 'That is the tricky part. You are supposed to press the bottoms on the side for it to recline. There are 3 levels. The one that I bought the plastic button keeps getting stuck. I have to use a butter knife to recline it. If you want it in an upright position it slides well. I think mine could just be a defect or the plastic needs some exercise. I should have bought mine from a store for an easy return. I hate mail order returns. So I just deal with it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0010WAXN6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396335600, 'question': 'I am looking for is a seat that reclines for a 4-month old to sit in front of the TV and feed him...thought this might work. Does anyone think it wil?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It has to be attached to a dining chair to work. It does not stand on its own on the floor. It does recline nicely, I would recommend it if you want to move a dining chair to the living room with the baby.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0010WAXN6', 'answerTime': 'Jul 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404284400, 'question': 'Does this chair recline enough for a newborn baby?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I said yes. Don't worry buy it excellent."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0010WAXN6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397113200, 'question': 'I am looking to use this for my 5 1/2 month old granddaughter..I would like to use it without the tray at the table. Has anyone done this.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I have done so. However, depending upon the height of the table, it won't push all the way under. The tray is really the safest thing for a child that young. I didn't start taking the tray off until my grandson was around 15 months old. The center bar and belts will hold her in good enough, just be careful."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0010WAXN6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395126000, 'question': "Where do you put this seat to recline it for a newborn? I'm confused because if it is strapped to the kitchen chair there would not be room to recline", 'answer': "That is correct. As long as is strapped to the kitchen chair it will not recline. You have to take it out, then press the 2 tabs on the bottom and pull towards you. It's a Lil difficult pressing the tabs in, but once you do you can move the chair to a reclining position"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0010WAXN6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390291200, 'question': 'Are there a bunch of crevices under the pad where food can get stuck?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I haven't had any problem. The pad is removable anyway. You can just lift it up some to clean under. I really love this chair as the child is not here all the time, so I don't need to have a high chair sitting around; just strap it onto a kitchen chair when needed."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0010WAXN6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389859200, 'question': 'Our chairs do not have slots in the back. There is a space between the bottom and the back rest, but no slots. Will this still work?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it should still work. Even if the back of the chair attached directly to the seat without a space it would still work. The straps wrap around the bottom of the chair and around the back.'}
