{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394607600, 'question': 'can i use batteries for pump?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, you can. The pump even comes with its own battery pack that you fill with 8 AA batteries. It's not as strong at the same level as when it's plugged into the wall socket but it does the job nicely at a slightly higher suction level. In addition, the batteries last for about 15 pumping sessions before you need to change them."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'I am wondering btw the metro bag and the backpack. Which would be easier to carry while wearing a pocketbook and carrying 2 other bags?', 'answer': 'You may like the backpack so you could close the bag. It may be difficult to handle so many other bags in addition to the pump metro bag that does not close and contents could easily fall out. Kathy Summers'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388131200, 'question': 'Can this pump be used as a single pump (one breast at a time) or do you have to pump both breasts every time you pump?', 'answer': 'Yes, it can be used as either a single or double pump.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395644400, 'question': 'Did anyone use their FSA to purchase this pump through amazon?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Just a heads up, check with your insurance, because the vast majority of plans are now required (under the new ACA law) to pay for a pump with zero deductible/co-pay etc. All most require is a "prescription" from your Dr (you can do this before or after birth)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392537600, 'question': "if I'm debating between the tote bag or the metro bag which would you recommend?", 'answer': "Metro-you can just take the components you need separately so you aren't always having to lug the big bag. Also good if the table or counter you're putting it on has limited space. The motor is the same though so if cost is the driving factor the tote will work."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419235200, 'question': 'Warranty: What does it cover and for how long? I want to buy now w/FSA funds but may not use it for a year - warranty may expire before I even try it?', 'answer': 'Not sure about the warrenty, but before you go and buy one check with your health insurance. I believe that now because of Obama care when you deliver a baby federal government gives you a breast pump at no cost. Kind of like Uncle Sam giving you a baby shower gift. We submitted our receipt to our insurance provider and we got refund from our healthcare provider when we had our son.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': 'Are there adaptors/plugs available for New Zealand or Australian voltage? If so, how do we purchase them?', 'answer': "You can buy them on this site as well. Here is one you can buy: http://www.amazon.com/Grounded-Universal-Adapter-Australia-Zealand/dp/B005JK6J06/ref=sr_1_3?ie=UTF8&qid=1418250373&sr=8-3&keywords=us+to+australia+adapter Just search for US to Australia/New Zealand adapter. I'm not sure if the pump is dual voltage. If the pump is only 110v-120v you'll need a transformer since I believe it's 240v in Australia."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Nov 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416556800, 'question': 'How loud is the motor on this pump? For example, is this whisper quiet, can you hear it through a closed door, etc.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It's not super quiet, but I don't think you can hear it through a closed door. I used it at work for a year in my closed office."}
