{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0011E5LXK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402556400, 'question': 'Can this pump be used with plastic bags as well as bottles?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E75RK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382252400, 'question': 'Backpack vs. Tote vs. Metro Bag? Which Medela PISA bag would be the best for my purposes?', 'answer': "I have both the tote and backpack. Backpack is best! I can put it on my back and pump with the battery attachment while making dinner or otherwise walking around. With the tote, you're stuck in one spot unless you're comfortable walking with it on one shoulder."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0011E75RK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': 'Can the electric motor be removed? I have the on the go tote and like that style bag better, but the pump needs to be replaced. This backpack is cheaper, so wondering if I could take the pump motor out and place it in the tote.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, the pump is attached with velcro around the frame'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E75RK', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379401200, 'question': 'It was ok with the space on the backpack?', 'answer': "When you use the cooler for the bottles that comes with it, there's not a whole lot of extra room but I thought it was fine. You can fit a box of pump and save bags, pump bra, burp cloth and some pacifiers, just to give you an idea."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0011E75RK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386662400, 'question': 'Does the cooler fit inside the bag?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The cooler shown next to the bag does fit in the top of the backpack. Everything shown fits back in comfortably. (It's not like trying to put all of the playpen accessories back in the travel bag.) I also have the optional car plug in the bag. I carry a small burp cloth, and a small tub of coconut oil in the front pocket.(I don't use lanolin.) Its not intended to be an overnight carryall, but it will hold everything you need for pumping to go back and forth to work."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E75RK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393920000, 'question': 'I am debating between buying backpack and Metro Bag. I am wondering which is easier to carry? I will be carrying a pocketbook, and 2 other bags.', 'answer': "I have the backpack and am able to keep extra bottles, wipes, the tubes/horns, and the small bag with the ice pack but that's it. Even though it holds a good amount of stuff I got annoyed lugging it, my purse, and my lunch box into work everyday and just started leaving it at work. Now I just have to bring the tote holding the milk in my lunchbox & I'm set. For comfort I would agree that a backpack would be better than a shoulder sling bag."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E75RK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388995200, 'question': 'Does this come with a bustier? If not, which do you use? Anyone familiar with Medela Easy Expression bustier?', 'answer': 'I have the Simple Wishes and the Easy Expression pumping bras. Simple Wishes is by far the superior product (more support, not as "flimsy", can wear it as a bra on days you will need to pump in inconvenient places like work or an airplane), but I used Easy Expression with my first child with no real issues. In fact Easy Expression is slightly easier to use in the middle of the night because there are two open holes and just one zip. With Simple Wishes, because it\'s adjustable, there\'s like a little flap to manipulate as you put it on. It\'s no big deal, but when every second of sleep counts... ;)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0011E75RK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423296000, 'question': 'what is included with purchase?', 'answer': 'Everything in the picture. The pump with backpack, the cooler with contoured icepack, 4 bottles with covers, and the tubes, breast shields,valves and membranes.'}
