{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0011ECP9S', 'answerTime': 'Aug 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377241200, 'question': 'I need a 9v adapter for my pump, however, my car lighter receptacle says 12v...will it work or mess up my pump? Will appreciate any feedback. Thanx!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Clarify: I use my 9v adapter with my 12 volt car receptacle. No issues.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0011ECP9S', 'answerTime': 'Oct 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382770800, 'question': 'is it as powerful as when plugged into the wall?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No. If you have the pump all the way on high with the vehicle charger, it's comparable to about mid-range when using the wall plug..it gets the job done though just takes longer. I've had better luck with the battery pack but that eats up batteries pretty quickly. It's not too bad if you have batteries that are rechargeable. I recommend having a vehicle and battery pack just in case. It's better to be prepared for any situation than being stuck with nothing."}
