{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0012J5GWK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2007', 'unixTime': 1198828800, 'question': 'Grocery carts? One reviewer mentioned the Safe seat did not fit onto a shopping cart like the older models--is this true?', 'answer': "Well this is the way I look at it. I have big babies (over 9lbs at birth) and my first two grew out of there other infant seats at 3-4 months old. Still being too little to sit in the cart on there own but to big for the infant seat. So to me any negatives that there might be of this seat are far outweighed by the fact that I don't have to worry about my soon to be new baby outgrowing the seat so fast."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0012KUDPE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392019200, 'question': 'Could you please tell me is it high quality?? has it any guarantee that it will not be damaged after 1 month. I want to use it for kids classroom ??', 'answer': "There's no guarantee, but it's very sturdy. I bought it when I had 6 month old twins... and they are now 5 and we still have it in the play area. There's no torn pieces, and the colors have held up well. We've had all kinds of toys and chairs/table on it over the years and it's still in good shape. It's easy to clean because you can sweep it, and wash off with a cloth. If a tile gets really bad, it's easy to remove from the set to go wash in the sink or bathtub."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0012KUDPE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391500800, 'question': 'Why is this recommended for children of 3yrs +? Why not younger children?', 'answer': "I am not sure why it is not recommended for children younger than 3+ yrs. I bought these for a play area in my house that is all tile and my daughter has been playing on them since she was a year old. She is now 2 1/2 yrs old and we have never had issues. The boarders of the mats are removable so maybe this is why, but even so, they are so big, I personally don't feel like they are a chocking hazard. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0012KUDPE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'do they contain formamide ingredient?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I believe all foam play mats contain formamide, but with different amount. Based on the actual testing, it was concluded that a child would need to mouth for 20 minutes, or ingest, at least 4.17 square metres of typical foam play mat every day over their entire life to approach a level of exposure to formamide which might raise health concerns.'}
