{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0012KUDPE', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': "How have the mats held up for any sharp objects? I want to use it for puppies playing on them so they don't slip and easy cleanup but they have claws.", 'answer': "We have one beagle who doesn't really play on them, but we haven't kept him off of them. He walks on them and lays on them often. The mats have a texture to the top anyway, so I think you wouldn't notice scratches too much. It would be easy to spot clean each mat when it got a mess on it too. I say it's worth a try."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0012KUDPE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424246400, 'question': 'how many would you recommend to cover a 3.5 x 4 floor?', 'answer': 'Each tiles measures 24 incehs x 24 inches (in other words 2 feet by 2 feet). Four tiles inter locked like a square will measure 4 feet x 4 feet. Thus, you would have to cut some of the tiles to get them to fit perfictly in a space that is 3.5 feet x 4 feet. Hope this is helpful!'}
