{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0012W02OE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2008', 'unixTime': 1220598000, 'question': 'Whats the difference between the Graco SnugRide and Graco SafeSeat infant car seats? Can anyone tell me the difference between the Graco SnugRide and the Graco SafeSeat infant car seats?', 'answer': 'The Safeseat fits a larger child and is a slightly larger heavier seat. The Snugride is up to 22lbs (Wt w/o base: 7.5lbs/ Weight with base: 12.7lbs/ Dimensions: 24.2"H x 17.5"W x 26.7"D) The Safeseat is up to 30lbs (Wt w/o base: 9.8lbs/ Weight with base: 17 lbs/ Dimensions: 15.6"H x 18.7"W x 30.7"D) Hope this helps, I was wondering the same thing myself actually!! Good Luck!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0012W02OE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 8, 2011', 'unixTime': 1307516400, 'question': 'Graco Snugride Platinum - adjusts at front or back? Can anyone tell me if the Graco Snugride Platinum harness straps adjust at the front of the car seat?', 'answer': 'Sorry to be so late to the discussion, but I own this carseat and I just want to be clear what you mean to by "adjust". If you are referring to pulling the straps tighter once the child is placed in the seat, then yes, the adjustment is made from the front of the seat. There is a strap located inbetween your child\'s thighs that you pull to tighten the straps, to loosen there is a little metal button hidden there that you push to release. If you are referring to raising the straps to a higher position for when the child is taller, than you must re-thread the straps through the back into the higher slots manually. I hope this makes sense!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0012W02OE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'The car seat and base are both included, right?', 'answer': 'Yes, both are included.'}
