{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0012YMWO0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390550400, 'question': 'Can it be rolled up without the pieces coming apart?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "no, not at all. it is too thick and stiff. I'm very happy with these mats so far. They are great for my son to play on instead of the hardwood floor. One great thing is that I can make it bigger or smaller depending on the space just by removing or adding tiles. As far as the end pieces coming off, any brand of mats will do this when children play on them. I solved this issue by placing some gorilla tape on the bottom side at the edge. I used Gorilla brand because it is much less likely to stain the floor with residue. Cheap duct tape will stain."}
