{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389686400, 'question': 'My crib has solid sides on the short ends and slats on the long sides. Will this bumper attach or does it need all four slatted sides?', 'answer': 'Mine is exactly like yours with solid end panels. I wove it through the slats only on the two long sides. Works well.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'Oct 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382770800, 'question': 'What are the dimensions? Length, width and height?', 'answer': 'It\'s probably 1 ft in height and the length varies because you wrap it around the crib bars. There\'s plenty of extra overlapped in his crib which is standard size. As for how thick it is...it\'s very thin. less than 1/4" Don\'t expect it to provide any padding really.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'Sep 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380351600, 'question': 'How thick is it?', 'answer': "As thin as the picture looks. You can se through it, it's a double layer of mesh and a thin satin lining on the top and bottom."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404370800, 'question': 'How "padded" is this liner? My baby moves a lot and bumps her head on the slates of the crib. I want to protect her head.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It is not padded at all, it's a thin piece of fabric. It looks good but wouldn't protect her head"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406962800, 'question': 'Will this work on a crib that has the ability to lower one side? ie: the front side lowers to reach baby easier then raises and locks in place.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It wouldn't be ideal because there are two panels and for the drop side to work, you would need to use one of the two panels on just the drop side. That means the remaining panel would need to stretch around the other three side of the crib. You could just use the two panels on the two long side of the crib and not wrap the short ends."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'May 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400482800, 'question': 'it is imported. Where has it been made?', 'answer': 'imported from China, it is Phthalate Free, Latex Free, Lead Free, BPA Free. We had to remove my 4 month old grand daughters bumper pad that came with her comforter due to the fact that she loves to get in the corner and fall asleep with her face against the bumper pad, when we removed it she decided that sticking her legs out of the crib slats would be cute. For safety we had to find something that would help keep her legs and arms in without having to add the traditional bumper pad back. This has been awesome-she can get in her little corner that she prefers and if her little face presses against it she can still breathe, yet it keeps her arms and legs in the crib where they belong :-)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404975600, 'question': "Why does the product say to stop using it when your baby can sit up? I don't want him to climb out so wondering if benefit is better than risk.", 'answer': 'I am really not sure why it says that to be honest. But, what I can tell you is that from about 4.5 years experience of using this (2 children later!) it has not been an issue after they were able to sit up. I would think that if they tried to stand on it, the material is soft enough that is would just mash down flat. Although, it is definitely sturdy enough not to look floppy or saggy per say! I have loved it and it is definitely worth the piece of mind and purchasing! As I stated in my review, it also keeps arms and legs in the crib which can be alarming when they wake up crying because a limb is stuck between the slats! Hope this helps! :)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 17, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421481600, 'question': 'Does it work for a round crib?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I would say it would. But only if the circumference is equal to the perimeter of a traditional crib.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0013FGWD0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422777600, 'question': 'Will the sides collapse all the way down? Trying to stop my 20 month old from climbing out. The decorative bumper we have now seems to be a step for h', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If your son stepped on it, it would collapse. My 8 month old tries to pull it down and it comes down a little, but if she was bigger and stepped on it I'm sure it would not be sturdy enough to give her a boost out of her crib! Hope that helped!"}
