{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0013HEF3W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390464000, 'question': 'How high does it boost the child?', 'answer': 'I just measure 5-6 inches from the seat of my dining room chair to the seat of the booster. Doesnt seem like much but it works perfectly. It depends on your chair also. We have woven straw seat that rests concave on the chairs frame so our booster seat is level. If you have a cushion that sits convex you may get an added inch or two.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0013HEF3W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388908800, 'question': 'Are the harness straps removeable?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The harness straps are NOT removable but situated in such a way that they can be easily tucked underneath the seat unobtrusively. Really a minor inconvenience in the big scheme of things as overall this is a fantastic seat! You could cut them off if it really bothered you but that would lower its resale value. My daughter doesnt use the harness anymore so we just tuck underneath into tye hollow area under the seat and nobody is the wiser.'}
