{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0015TM0M6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387094400, 'question': 'What are the parts made from (the exact specifics, if listed on package)? Also, is this better than NoseFrida and BabyComfyNose?', 'answer': "I do not have the package any more, but I have the product and it is the best thing I ever got. It can be taken apart and placed in the dishwasher or you can put it in the pot of previously boiled hot water to sterilize it. I use dish soap to wash it and put it in the dishwasher at the end of the day. It is plastic and hose is rubbery. It is small but very powerful just as everything else that is made in Japan. I had bought bigger aspirators or automatic ones, but they just do not work. In this one, you place white tip into the child's nostril and the end of hose into your mouth, and pull like you are sucking form a straw. It sounds yucky, but it all ends up in the little plastic cup, and the good thing is you can see how much is really stuck in your child's nose or baby's nose, and what color discharge is. As doctors will tell you anything green or yellow means infection. More often you clean, faster your child will recover and less the chance to develop an ear infection. Hope this helps."}
