{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0016KV8DG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407913200, 'question': 'Can this be used as a sanding potty all the time? I am looking for a toddler potty but I like that this can also fold and has liners.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think it depends on the age and wiggliness of the child, really. We started training our energetic child at 15 months and used the Baby Bjrn because it had a high back and was altogether more stable (she trained easily on it). We used that for a month and once she was fully trained (and didn't need a back to lean on, and knew how to sit still on the potty) we switched to using the Kalencom exclusively as her potty on the floor for another three weeks. Then we used it in the fold out mode and we just use it as the potty seat modifier. Now (5 months later) that's how we use it whenever she goes because her butt is too small for the regular potty. That's the long explanation to say, if you've got a wiggler, grab a bin of books only read on the potty or a discovery jar because this potty isn't going to feel as stable as a regular chair; however, it's a fantastic transitional chair and you won't regret your purchase. (The liners thing is just a nice perk, and a reusable liner is also available for day-to-day use.)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0016KV8DG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397545200, 'question': 'How many liners does this come with? Can you just rinse the liners and re-use or do they not hold up well?', 'answer': "It comes with 3 liners. You can't wash them; they are essentially fancy garbage bags like a plastic grocery bag with an absorbent strip."}
