{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0016KV8DG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407913200, 'question': 'The video to this product (under the green colour) shows a reusable liner as well as the disposable liners. Does this product come with it?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It does not come with the reusable liner, but I highly suggest investing in one (it\'s a reasonable price and will give you a lot of use). I even used it while traveling if she just needed to pee (using a cloth diaper to wipe it out when daughter was finished going, then throwing the diaper in a wet/dry bag until we got home). It can be found by searching "Kalencom Reusable Liner" on Amazon or following this link:'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0016KV8DG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407308400, 'question': "I'm having trouble unlocking the legs once in place (for stand up use, not as insert on toilet). Any tips on how to unlock easier?", 'answer': 'I had the same problem at the beginning, it does takes a little more strength than I expected but I just pull it out strong enough until it snaps off, I try it to contain the whole thing with my body (unless it has touched something nasty). Most of the time the legs snap out completely and I just pop them back in.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0016KV8DG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407913200, 'question': 'Is this solid pink (except for the gray grips)? Some have a pink seat with purple handles, but the one pictured here is a pink seat with pink handles.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Ours is a solid pink seat with purple sides (and gray grips). There is also a solid pink reusable liner available on Amazon http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0083WVGTG/ref=cm_cd_asin_lnk In my opinion, the pink and purple seat is more aesthetically pleasing (prettier shade of pink) than the all-pink version in the stock photo.'}
