{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0016L0MMS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363762800, 'question': 'Does this Potette Require bags to use!? Is it basically just a hole?', 'answer': "It depends on where you are going to use it. You could technically use your own plastic shopping bags, but I would double up in case there are tiny holes. The bags that you buy with it have an absorbent pad at the bottom and fit really well on the seat/chair. You don't need bags if you are using it as a ring on a standard toilet."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0016L0MMS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397718000, 'question': 'How is this toilet seat with boys? Is there a splash guard? I do you protect the urine from streaming outward?', 'answer': "It's ok. The splash guard is more of a curve up. It leaves a little to be desired in that area, but it's worth it for the travel ease."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0016L0MMS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380870000, 'question': "In the instructions it says that you should hear a click when you snap the legs up. I don't hear it and the potty collapses when she sits on it. Help?", 'answer': 'Also, I find it easiest too put the legs in the stand up position, put it on the floor, and then push straight down on the ring till you hear the clicks. You can also do the opposite, put potty ring on floor & push legs into ring while on the floor'}
