{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0016RVM4O', 'answerTime': 'Apr 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397458800, 'question': 'It says the top/bottom layers of this pad are 100% cotton but not what the center \'ultra thin waterproof barrier" is made from. Does anyone know?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You probably already found the answer to this question but I was just researching this myself and I believe it's a thin layer of food-grade polyethylene. According to the Naturepedic website, the waterproof cover for their crib mattresses is this food-grade polyethylene, so I'm pretty certain it's the same throughout all of their waterproof products."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0016RVM4O', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': "the description says the outer layers are organic cotton; what is the interior 'water barrier' layer made of?", 'answer': 'Hi. I\'m writing from Naturepedic. Your question is answered on our website. I\'m quoting it here for you. "DrySleep technology effectively blocks liquids from passing through the fabric while still allowing the material to "breathe." This is achieved by allowing a certain amount of water vapor (similar to humidity naturally found in the air) to pass through. This results in less "sweaty backs" and a drier, more comfortable sleep. Vinyl/PVC, latex, and rubber, on the other hand, are comparatively "sweaty" - they block all moisture from passing through, creating a more uncomfortable sleeping environment. Drysleep uses a specially formulated polyurethane waterproof barrier that is proven to not leach harmful chemicals. It is made from the same grade material as is required for food contact applications. It also meets the highest standards for medical device biocompatibility (USP Class VI). It does not contain any fire retardants or antimicrobial treatments and is free of vinyl/PVC, phthalates and latex. It also easily passes the GREENGUARD "Gold" certification standards for chemical emissions. With a Naturepedic organic mattress pad, you never have to worry about harmful chemicals or allergenic materials. "'}
