{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0018T1WUO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390982400, 'question': 'Both pre-pregnancy and now (37 weeks) I am a 34/36 B- should I buy the x-small or small? I am worried small will be too big.', 'answer': "While from a 44G perspective, my experience is that as long as it is smaller than the cup of your bra, big is fine. I had smaller ones and did not like the visible ring the edge of the pad left under clothes. If Amazon doesn't state the actual sizes, go to the company website, then cut a circle in a rag and try it. Go as large as you can to avoid ring around the nipple."}
