{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AH8JNC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397458800, 'question': "How do you turn it off so the timer doesn't go off all night long?", 'answer': 'You hold the black button and then push the color button it will display the word PLAY then push the color button through 30, 60, 90, then it will display OFF. Leave it there and it shuts off.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001AH8JNC', 'answerTime': 'Jun 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403938800, 'question': "Is it loud enough to wake them at night? He's fine during the day, its the night we can't break", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "For me, yes! I left it downstairs on a table and it even woke me up. I have to say it's fairly loud. My son didn't like to wear it so I would leave it on a table and we were able to hear it from multiple places in our home.."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AH8JNC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415174400, 'question': 'Is this watch actually effective?What happens when they no longer have the watch?Do they learn to go potty w/o it and not over-rely on it?Thank you.', 'answer': "I'm sure all kids are different, but it worked for my son. He wanted to wear it, but knew he couldn't wear it unless he tried to go on regular intervals. He just eventually transitioned out of it... And is completely potty trained. He just started going when he felt e needed to go"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AH8JNC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422518400, 'question': "How big is the main part of the watch? I'm trying to figure out if it would be too big for my 16mo old", 'answer': 'It works for my 20 month old, but it is very cheaply made!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AH8JNC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415606400, 'question': 'How do you change the batteries?', 'answer': "Not sure. Our son was potty trained before we ever had to try. I would start finding the small screws on the back if there is any and just start trying to take it apart. If all else fails, a new one isn't that pricy."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001AH8JNC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412233200, 'question': "Is there a way to turn the sound on? Currently the lights just go on and off. Not sure if it's defective or I'm missing somehing.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not that I am aware of. Sounds defective, my sons did that after about a month, it lit up but no sound. I opened it up to change out the batteries and it was rusted. Got a second one that only lasted a few weeks as well and broke when trying to replace the battery. It is a WONDERFUL AND USEFUL TOOL for helping remind littles to go potty, but it's not built well at all & doesn't last. Wish it did though bc it's an amazing idea, just can't pay 12 bucks for a new one every month."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AH8JNC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412233200, 'question': 'How do you turn it on? This is my 2nd watch and the blue button activates nothing?', 'answer': "It's been a while since we used it, but I think you have to hold the button down for several seconds to turn it on and off (longer than you think is necessary...I guess that keeps the kids from being able to turn it off themselves? )."}
