{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001AQLGO2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'Has anyone tried it with a Baby Jogger City Select set up with two seats? My son will be 20 months when the twins arrive.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, we did and it did not work for us (3 yr old in Junior rider, 2 yr old in BJ seat and newborn infant carseat with BJ adapter). I\'m 5"7 and was constantly running into it and had to walk on the side of the stroller, which was not very comfortable. My husband who is 5\'10 found he could walk behind it if he leaned forward a bit, but after awhile that would become uncomfortable too. We ended up buying the BJ glider board for our oldest, bc she usually wants to walk anyway, so when the glider board is not in use, we could fold it up and attach it to the frame. I found I could walk behind the stroller like I normally do. I think the Junior X rider is great in concept, but does not work for BJ City Select. If the City Select\'s handle telescoped a few more inches, then it would be perfect.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001AQLGO2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'does this fit the city select? thank you!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It does fit the City Select, but I found that it was hard for me to walk behind it (I'm 5'6 in height). We returned it and went with the BJ Glider Board instead, which works great for us."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001AV40Z4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428217200, 'question': 'Is the bottom non-skid?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No not exactly. The entire thing has the same surface covering. I would compare it to if you covered fabric with the plastic from a milk carton. It does slide around a little. You are supposed to bolt it to the dresser etc. We have used it 2 years no problems, and we have a pretty wily kiddo.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AV40Z4', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': 'Can this be screwed to a dresser or changing table? Many we looked at came with a piece to screw it on and the two sided one we have did not.', 'answer': 'it comes with snaps that can be screwed into the back of the dresser, so the changing pad can be snapped on and off.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001AV40Z4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'The Naturapedic covers are pricey. Can you recommend an alternative changing pad cover that fits this well?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I know this doesn't quite answer your question, but we've been using ours for 10+ months without a cover and we've been very happy. The surface is waterproof and very easy to wipe clean; ours has remained stain-free. A cover that's made of something like cotton will require laundering, etc."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001AV40Z4', 'answerTime': 'Sep 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380438000, 'question': 'Do these fit land of nod changer pad covers?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I don't know about land of nod, but I purchased a Summer Infant cover and it didn't fit great because this pad has raised sides on the long ends as well which makes the cover sort of suspend in air. However, I found that the pad is easier to wipe off itself than to have to wash a cover all the time and so I decided it didn't need a cover."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AV40Z4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381129200, 'question': 'Any benefit or drawback to getting the 4-sided vs the 2-sided?', 'answer': "Hmm.. I'm not sure. I liked it because it just felt like it would cradle him more. I like how it supports his head. This way we can put him down with his head on either side and he still has a little pillow cushion. Now that my son is getting older, he tries to crawl off the changing pad a lot and we have to distract him with toys. The curvature keeps the toys on the pad with him and also slows him down a tiny bit. I don't think there are any drawbacks I can think of, maybe a few very small benefits in my book."}
