{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AX1UQO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387440000, 'question': 'Please recommend a good battery charger to use with these batteries', 'answer': "I use the Tenergy Speedy Box - have had about 8 years - it holds all kinds of rechargeable batteries (4 at a time) from AAA to D. It's never failed. It's expensive, but in the end, I figure that I've saved a lot of money on batteries."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001AX1UQO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375167600, 'question': "Will these work the Energizer chargers? We have always used Energizer batteries for baby accessories/toys, but they don't seem to hold a charge very long, so we were considering a different product but don't want to buy a new charger.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hello, I can only say that I use a charger that is made only for mAh style batteries. I have not used the Energizer batteries but I think the Tenergy batteries are great, they seem to hold a charge for a long time and recharge very fast, been using these batteries for about a year now and love them.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AX1UQO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392969600, 'question': 'what is the difference between these and Low Self Discharge batteries?', 'answer': "The Low Self Discharge Batteries are listed as LSD NiMH. In my opinion these pictured here work fine for me since I change batteries on a couple of pest deterrents about every 1 to 2 months. LSD NiMH batteries will keep most of it's charge for a year or 2. If you are planning to keep batteries stored for a year or more I would suggest sticking with the standard Duracell's and Eveready's. They hold their charges way longer. Rechargeable batteries are for toys and devices that frequently need a battery change. Here is a link to a Wiki on the question that you asked. Hope this helps. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nickel%E2%80%93metal_hydride_battery"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001AX1UQO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412838000, 'question': 'Are the batteries charged "new, out of the box", or when they arrive do I have to charge them before using? Thanks!', 'answer': 'They are charged some, but no batteries stay in there charged state indefinitely. There is always some discharge, so you will be well advised to charge then upon receipt of them.'}
