{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001CAOYZ4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398322800, 'question': 'Will this liner protect a cloth diaper from meconium?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It should, but with any liner that you place in a cloth diaper, you run the risk of the liner moving/shifting inside the diaper and any solids getting onto the diaper itself. Honestly, I feel like these liners are a bit rough, even on my 17 month old, compared to others like OsoCozy and Gro-Via and would use another brand liner against a newborn's skin."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001CAOYZ4', 'answerTime': 'Aug 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407740400, 'question': 'What size would be recommended for an infant when using pocket cloth diapers? Small or Large?', 'answer': 'I always just suggest the large size. If they are too big, just fold them over. I use the large size for even my newborns (the smallest of which was 4 lbs when we took her home from the hospital-yea, she wore doll clothes, not even preemie clothes, for the first 3 months of her life). Yes, I folded the large liners over (a couple times), but I figured/still figure that just offered more poop catching potential. I have ordered the small size only once and just felt the larger size fit my needs better.'}
