{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001CB7I4W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410764400, 'question': "I just received this product and the package says 'water resistant' so now I'm wondering if it's actually waterproof.", 'answer': "When my boys have pee'd their beds, to me it seems to absorb the pee vs. if i were to just have a fitted sheet to pull it off and have slight puddling on their matteress... their still use their crib matteress which have that plasticy feel to them where pee doesn't soak into the mattress. I hope this makes sense for you! :) I also personally like them cause they give their flat matteresses some softness/fluffiness to them."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001CB7I4W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410332400, 'question': 'Is this mattress pad fit for newborns/infants or is it too soft?', 'answer': "If you or your pediatrician are nervous about SIDS, then yes, it's too soft for infants. Infants, also mostly don't notice so the simpler and firmer the better. Toddlers, like my granddaughter, however, do notice and like the extra fluff. Also, it's very absorbent and better able to contain the higher volume accidents. Washes very well, too."}
