{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001COIH3A', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2012', 'unixTime': 1330156800, 'question': 'Advent baby monitor: In all the reviews of tons of monitors - rarely is range discussed - Can I be out in the yard - How far away?', 'answer': "Depends on how far out in the yard you are. We regularly will be in the back yard with the monitor or outside in general with no issues... I would say about 100'- 125' if there are no real obstructions other than your house walls (stick home). Your result may vary depending on the type of wall, siding, etc on your house."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001COIH3A', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370761200, 'question': "For me,the Avent Basic Baby Monitor it's the best one, but recently something strange has happened ... I turn on the unit and after a few seconds goes on mute and I can no longer hear the sounds of my baby's room. When i push the sensitivity button its...", 'answer': 'Sounds like the sensitivity is set too low. Try increasing the sensitivity to pick up the sounds. Remember, if there are not loud enough sounds, the monitor does go into a \'\'mute" mode to save battery on the parent unit.'}
