{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001COPE86', 'answerTime': 'Jul 31, 2010', 'unixTime': 1280559600, 'question': 'has anyone tried using two avent dect monitors at the same time? has anyone tried using two avent dect monitors together?', 'answer': "We have two sets of the Philips DECT SCD590 monitors. The two sets of monitors work fine together in the same house, they don't interfere with each other and each baby unit only talks to the parent units it came with. We've labeled the parent units so we know which one is which. For those that need two parent units but want the newer model, you could just buy two and put both baby units in the same room to effectively have two parent units."}
