{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001CUPT76', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'Will it fit chicco liteway plus?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The Chicco Liteway Plus stroller looks a bit smaller than the stroller we have and does not have a front tray for the child, but it looks like it would work. The rain guard on top of the stroller and stroller handles is what holds up the plastic rain guard you are asking about. The rain guard you are asking about has an open section with snaps that allow the stroller handle to stay out where you can use them which would also help hold the plastic rain guard up away from the child. I can't promise that it would work, but based on the pictures of your stroller, I think it might. It is definitely worth purchasing and trying. If it didn't work, you could always gift it to another person with a stroller more like a Greco or Jeep. We live in the Pacific Northwest and deal with a large amount of rain in the fall, winter, and spring and we are very happy with the rain guard. I hope this answers your question and helps you make a decision. Like I said, we really like this and it works great. It even helps protect the items in the baggage area from getting wet, as long as you don't push it through a deep puddle, of course."}
