{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001CV13RA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416297600, 'question': 'Would this work well on a Baby Jogger City-Select double stroller?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001CV13RA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': 'Does this fit a joove caboose ultralight with the car seat adapter on?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't know if it would fit. You would have to look at your stroller, make some comparisons, and then try it. From looking at the pictures, however, I think it might. The way the rain guard works is through the use of the stroller's sun shade. You would definitely want the cover for the double stroller because the single would be to snug and would eventually rip. We have two covers, one for the single stroller and one for the double and like them both. The grandchildren can see what is happening, but remain dry when they go for walks with grandpa. The cover helps keep the wind off the kids in the autumn and winter, too, but it does not help keep them warm. You would definitely need to use coats and blankets to help keep the little people warm. I can't say you would like yours, but we like ours. It has worked for our 3 year old grandson every day walking to Head Start, even through the rainy Pacific Northwest winter."}
