{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001D1A4IS', 'answerTime': 'Nov 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416384000, 'question': 'WIll a 19 month still need the baby seat or be okay without the baby seat?', 'answer': 'I bought the baby seat back and tray for our chair and the 18 month old using it only used it for a couple of months. Admittedly he was big for 18 months, tall like his Dad, but after I saw what this bit of plastic was like I realized that it was a total waste of money. The baby was too big to fit in the small space between the back of the plastic support and the front tray, it is very narrow and very badly designed. I would say do not waste your money on this and just use a cushion support and pull the chair up to the kitchen or dinning room table.'}
