{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001D475FU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388476800, 'question': 'What height of microwave is required for this product?', 'answer': 'The steamer measures 7 inches from counter top to top of steamer. It fits perfectly in our. 8 3/4" tall microwave.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001D475FU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410850800, 'question': 'Do you have to hand wash the bottles and other components before sterilizing them?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi Lauren, Yes. We hand washed everything before sterilizing them. I am not sure if this is necessary, but we don't want to deal with bacteria build-up down the road. Annoying? Yes, but its for the good of our baby. Hope this help."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001D475FU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391587200, 'question': 'Is it better/easier to hand wash and then use this to sterilize or buy the dishwasher thingy only?', 'answer': "I suppose that depends on how many bottles you are planning on buying and how frequently you run your dishwasher. We cycle through 6-8 bottles, generally washing and sterilizing 3-5 at a time (plus, we wash and sterilize pump bottles). That results in this thing going through the microwave 2, 3, or 4 times a day. I can't begin to imagine running my dishwasher that frequently."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001D475FU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418284800, 'question': 'how many bottles will it hold?', 'answer': "Officially, it holds four bottles. However, it really depends on the size of bottle you use. I've managed to get five and sometimes six bottles fit in with sufficient space to get them properly sterilized. BUT they were not all 8oz bottles...if your baby is using the larger size, then four is really the max. We really loved this product and used it all the time!!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001D475FU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379228400, 'question': "My microwave is small it barely fits - do you need it to rotate to work? Or it's ok if it's just in the same position while microwaving", 'answer': "I don't really think this should matter much. The purpose of the sanitizer is to steam the bottles and components with the water that you put on the bottom. I don't think the sanitizer necessarily needs to rotate to heat the water to that point, so you should be fine."}
