{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001E6FY32', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': 'Does the chair tip over if the child moves around or tries to stand in the chair?', 'answer': "My grandson has turned around backwards, stood up,and leaned over edge and never even tipped the highchair. Not saying it cant happen, we've just not seen it. It's very sturdy."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001ECHXVC', 'answerTime': 'Jun 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371452400, 'question': 'What exactly is the learning tower, what benefit can be expected from this toy for the child?', 'answer': "It allows your child to safety stand at counter level for any number of activities. We like to make bread together (as well as various dinner items) and when we were using a step stool her movements constantly had me catching her from falling backwards, I could never have two hands to work on a project. She can climb into the tower without help and usually I have an activity set up for her on the counter every morning so she can work on it while I prepare breakfast or do dishes and she can feel like a part of the morning routine. She also likes to do water play in the sink so I just push the tower over and fill up the sink and she'll play in it for an hour sometimes! It really is great to have! Does this help at all?"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001ECHXVC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389427200, 'question': 'Can the outer buttressing feet be left off to prevent tripping etc? Can anyone give advantages of the Learning Tower over the Guidecraft model?', 'answer': "yes you do not need all the feet on so you can leave 4 of them off. I don't think this prevents tripping but cuts obstacles in half."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001ECHXVC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390032000, 'question': "What age would you say this appropriate for? My daughter is 15 months and her Montessori recommend it but I'm not sure if she's still too little.", 'answer': "My youngest has been getting in since he could stand on his own. 15 months is probably fine. If she's steady on her feet, she'll be fine."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001ECHXVC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418630400, 'question': 'Does the platform move easily? It looks as though putting a bit of weight on one side would make it come out of the grooves. Have you had this problem', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Not at all! We love it!'}
{'answer': "The platform height is adjustable. We currently have ours at the highest and it's approximately 19 inches off the ground. My son is about 33 inches tall and it's the perfect height for him to stand and play at the counter while we're in the kitchen. As my son grows, we will lower it to the two other notches as appropriate for his height.", 'asin': 'B001ECHXVC', 'answerTime': '25 days ago', 'question': 'how high is the platform?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001ECHXVC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429081200, 'question': 'Would a 43 pound 4 year old be too old for this? He usually just stands on a chair to help in the kitchen, but wants to feel more secure.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "This will definitely hold a four year old. My granddaughter is four and sometimes her 18 month old brother stands in there with her. So the weight should be fine. The height can also be adjusted on the tower so he should be able to use it until he's tall enough to help in the kitchen without the tower. Hope this helps."}
