{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001ENY02G', 'answerTime': 'Apr 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398841200, 'question': 'Does it come already fully assembled? Is it possible to take it apart when not in use and put it together again later?', 'answer': 'It does not come fully assembled but it is easy to put together. Yes you could disassemble it for storage when not in use. It just takes an L shaped hex wrench.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371625200, 'question': "What are the dimensions of the bed once it's inflated?", 'answer': "It's about the same length/width of a regular crib. It's probably 5-8 inches thick when inflated. The crib sheet I purchased from a local department store fits it perfectly. All I know for sure is that my granddaughter LOVED it. I'm so glad we invested in it! Now when she comes for a sleepover, I know she'll get a good night's rest . . . and so will we."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373958000, 'question': 'what age does this bed go up to? We have an almost 4 year old -- how long will she be able to use it?', 'answer': 'My granddaughter will be 4 in September and weighs about 36 pounds. She is still using the Shrunk bed and I expect will be able to do so for several more years before she would be too tall for it. The specs that came with mine indicate that it is good up to 150 pounds.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391414400, 'question': 'we are headed to Orlando soon. Would you bring this with you if traveling by plane or just use what the hotel provides in terms of a cot/roll away bed', 'answer': 'We have 3 kids, I bring inflatables for my 2 year old and my 3 year old, and have my 7 year old sleep on the day bed, pull out or 2nd bed. Sometimes I will ship them UPS ground a week ahead of time. about the same price as an extra bag fee and no hassle. I find most hotels only provide one rollaway, and some say "fire code" doesn\'t allow roll aways. Know before you go.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382425200, 'question': 'How young a child can use this bed?', 'answer': 'I bought this bed for my grand daughter who was 2.5 years old at the time. She had just gone into a "big girl bed" at home. The only spare bed I have in my home is queen size and we felt with the height of the bed off the floor and the inability to use rails, the The Shrunks bed would be the perfect solution. It proved an excellent choice. My other grand daughter who is 5 (she is small for her age) uses the bed when she sleeps over, too.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381042800, 'question': 'What is the voltage rating on the electric pump? Is it 110v only or can it handle 240v?', 'answer': "The voltage rating is 110v. I don't believe the pump can handle 240v. 240v may burn the pump up so I would not recommend that."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373266800, 'question': 'Dimentions', 'answer': 'The brown section where the child is actually laying is the same size as a toddler/crib mattress. The added white area around the "mattrres" is about 4 inches at the most all the way around. We use a regular crib fitted sheet when we traveled with it. The pump that comes with it inflates it in less than 30 seconds and it also has a deflate mode. We had it rolled up and back in its drawstring carry bag for transport and we threw it under our regular sized single stroller when we flew so it wouldn\'t take up space in our luggage when we flew. (It jus stayed under our stroller when we gate checked it). Here are the actual dimensions: Inflated size: 60 x 37 x 9 (inches), 152 x 94 x 23 (cm) The following link has other specs and a diagram with the dimensions. http://www.theshrunks.com/shop/indoor-products/travel-beds-and-security/indoor-toddler-travel-bed/?products_id=85001'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393488000, 'question': 'Curious if anyone has tried this on a tile floor. Wanting to try this for trip to Guatemala. Will the "cold" seep up through the mattress?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We'll we use ours up in the mountains it's on carpet but it's the mountains and my kids have no problem . I would maybe just put a extra blanket on the floor so it doesn't slide around plus it might help w the warmth. Hope this helps !"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385971200, 'question': 'How big is it when deflated? Will it fit easily into a medium size suitcase?', 'answer': 'The bag is deflated by using the air pump and reversing the nozzle location, so pretty much all the air can get sucked out. You may have to fold it and compress it some to get all the air out. It comes with a drawstring bag to carry the bed and the air pump. The pump has a cord, no batteries, btw. It would fit into a carry on size bag and still probably have room for a toiletry bag and a change of clothes, packed tightly.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EQ66WK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391760000, 'question': 'It looks like there are big ridges in the inflatable mattress is it comfortable?', 'answer': 'Oh yes, my 5 year old slept comfortably for a few days on this. The fabric, the brown part was soft and I also put a sheet on there, not needed, just for warmth..hope this helps'}
