{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001F50FFE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 12, 2011', 'unixTime': 1297497600, 'question': 'Which nipple does it come with?', 'answer': "Both the 4 oz and 8 oz evenflo glass bottles come with evenflo's slow flow nipples. Before my baby arrived, I bought the medium and fast flow nipples worried that I'd need them right away, but she's now 7 months and still using the slow flow. I'm not sure we'll ever switch. She can still power down 8 oz in 5 minutes with the slow-flow. Not sure if this is common for breastfed babies who also bottle-feed. We used the slow flow for formula as well as breast milk. The opening of the bottle seems to be the same as that of the medela bottles as it fits onto the Medela pump in style advanced that I have (but the glass bottles are so heavy that I prefer pumping into the plastic medela ones). Early on my baby showed a preference for the evenflo nipple over the medela, so we tossed the medela. Not sure what size it was or if all medela nipples are the same size but with different flow rates. One thing to keep in mind with using the evenflo nipples/bottles is that they work great as long as you don't have them screwed on too tight (the nipple will collapse and baby will suck and suck but get no milk) or too loose (leaks). It's their special air-vent system that requires some air to flow under the nipple base. If baby sucks and little bubbles flow into the milk shortly after that, then it's probably on just right."}
