{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001FBFIF0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375858800, 'question': 'The description says that these are bilingual. Are they available in Spanish and English?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The other customers were faster than me in responding, lol, so I guess you don't really need my answer, but the writer in me decied to give a bit of description to help you in your decsion. I often wish when buying things online we could see inside the item. So we have a much better idea what we're purchasing. So, I'll give you a description of what to expect, and snap a picture and try to upload it later. As others have stated, there is one set of cards (exactly as pictured). Inside, there is a Letter on the upper card and an animal on the bottom card. So for 'A' there is an Alligator. Beneath the alligator, it says Alligator with the 'A' underlined. Underneath Alligator is Caiman - spanish for Alligator. After 'Z' Zebra / Cebra starts a new section. The first section is outlined with green, the second section is blue and it is numbers. The theme is fish. So on the top you have the number '1' and the bottom card you have one fish. Beneath the fish is One and underneath One is Uno. Ten therefore has the number 10 on top, 10 fish, the numer Ten and then Diez. The final section is in yellow. It is colors and shapes. The top card has a red heart. Above the heart it says Red Rojo, and below the heart it says Heart Carazon. The bottom card has a blue square. Above the square it says Blue Azul. Beneath the square, it says Square Cuadro. All together you have the entire English alphabet with animal names in both English and Spanish. The numbers 1-10, with both the English and Spanish word. And 6 Colors and Shapes in both Englih and Spanish. I certainly hope this helps! OH! My toddler, a year later, still loves his! And it is holding up extremely well, especially since we tote it everywhere. I hooked a carabiner through one of the loops and attached it to my bag, so it's always on the go with us. The carabiner also helps keep it attached to other things: stroller, wagon, bibs... so he can't, quite as easily anyway, toss it. :)"}
