{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001FSL3NO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 8, 2009', 'unixTime': 1252393200, 'question': 'Double or single breast pump, which way should we go?', 'answer': "It's really up you what you like better. I bought a double breast pump thinking that at work every day, this would be faster. The one I bought had attachments to turn it into a hand pump in case of no electricity. I tried both ways and decided that I like the hand pump (single breast) better and I can use the other hand to continue working. The single pumps are usually cheaper but if this isn't an issue and getting it done faster is more appealing, then buy a double. This is the one I bought. Philips Avent ISIS iQ Duo Twin Electric Breast Pump, BPA Free - White"}
