{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001GQ2RYE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2009', 'unixTime': 1253602800, 'question': 'How wide is this? Can anyone tell me how wide the dining chair must be to accommodate this?', 'answer': 'Base that sits on dining chair is 15" side to side and 15" or 16" front to back. Arm rest/tray holders are 11" from the bottom of the base to the top of the tray holder. The tray holders stick out about an inch each wider than the base so the widest part of the chair is 18" side to side. I don\'t think you could use it with a dining chair with arms unless it is quite wide because you need clearance for the tray and the dining chair arms would get covered in food. I seem to have food splatters in a 5\'x5\' area! I have the seat as upright as it can go and it is about even with the back of the base. If you recline the seat the top part where the baby\'s head goes looks to be in line with the base but it is closer to my dining chair seat back. I hope this description makes some sense. I noticed that this year\'s model looks nicer than last year\'s and the vinyl looks easier to clean. I find this seat is soft and comfy but it has a lot of folds where food gets caught. Also, food falls down the slit where the crotch seat belt comes up so you need to clean under the padded cover. Although the padded cover says spot clean only I put it in the washing machine and it came out OK. I am considering buying a hard plastic booster with shoulder harness as it would be easier to clean. My boy doesn\'t sit in the highchair long enough for hard plastic to become uncomfortable. This chair attaches to my dining chair firmly and the harness keeps my boy secure. The tray comes off with one hand.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001GQ2RYE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2009', 'unixTime': 1235030400, 'question': 'FP space saver high chair and washability? Hi just wondered about the seat cover and machine washability?', 'answer': 'I have washed it on the hand wash cycle without problems, but I would not recommend this seat. There are to many places for food/stuff to get stuck in the arm rest when not using the tray and the cover is to hard to keep stuff out of the corners. I spent $16 on another seat at WalMart and I love it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001GQ2P78', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2010', 'unixTime': 1269673200, 'question': 'does this sound machine stay on? Does this automatically shut off or stay on?', 'answer': 'Yes! It will play continuously unless you select otherwise (it has a timer button).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001GQ2P78', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2011', 'unixTime': 1304578800, 'question': 'Is the night light optional? Is the night light always on when the machine is on, or is it optional?', 'answer': 'The "night light" feature can be turned off, but it still shines a lot of light out the little holes in the purple part, and all of the buttons are lit up all of the time. I found this really annoying. I taped black tape over the purple part, but still have to hide it behind books, etc., to hide the bright blue glow from all the buttons.'}
