{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001H0GF10', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388476800, 'question': "How stable is the third feature? I had one like this before and didn't like how unstable it seemed, so we didn't use it.", 'answer': 'Not sturdy at all :( It wanted to fall over at the slightest touch, and the middle piece that held the two halves together was very flimsy. We ended up taking it right back apart and putting it back as a saucer. Save the money and get a regular one.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001H0GF10', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379487600, 'question': 'Two questions: (1) Does the seat rotate so baby can move around to the toys behind her? (2) Is there actually a bounce in it? If so, where is it? (seat, or base??). Quick replies appreciate, I was hoping to decide in the next couple of days. Thanks!', 'answer': "1, yes, the seat fully rotates, and the child will use all of the toys around the base 2, it bounces a little bit; there are springs in those 4 legs so the infant can push with his/her feet and move ... however, if you are looking for a real bouncer (a few inches up and down, this is not the right product) Finally, I fully FULLY recommend this ExerSaucer over any other; mostly, it has 3 different settings - first, when the baby is very young (2+ months) laying on the back and playing with the toys - secondly, the 7+ months stage (what you see on the picture) and - thirdly, you can remove the base and have it stand standalone in a S shape once your baby is standing steadily. I got it as a gift and must say that we were using it from 2+ months all the way till 13+ months when my son already started to walk and stopped being interested in it ... that's a long stretch out of a single toy! Hope this helps!"}
