{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001JHSTS8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414220400, 'question': "I'm not breastfeeding anymore,those nipplete can help me anyways?", 'answer': "**As far as the niplettes slipping off, get a $1 tube of personal lubricant. You put it on the entire area, then put the niplette over it. It creates a seal that was strong enough for me to sleep in! Yes! I started using mine as soon as I found out I was pregnant. The longer/more often each session you use them, the faster/better the long term effect will be. I've had flat/inverted nipples my whole life, just never knew the terminology. After 6 children and only the last baby bf successfully for 6 months ONLY because I wore breast shells 24/7 before delivery and for 6 months after, I was determined to bf again... With a lot less trouble! These are great!"}
