{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001MS82HM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357632000, 'question': 'Could you please tell me how to clean and disinfect the breast pumps?Please tell me the best way?', 'answer': 'I have found the best way is to wash with dishwashing liquid, being careful to clean between all the little holes and spaces, then I place it in my steaming sterilizer for 15-20 mins. You can also pour hot water on the parts after washing and allow to soak for 15-20 mins. Be sure to put them out to dry before using it again since moisture could get sucked into the pump if the head is wet. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001MS82HM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381042800, 'question': "it's been 2 weeks since i've had this thing and one side already stopped working i'm a new mom and i need to pump i can't afford a new pump. help!", 'answer': "The company will send you another one but it took nearly a week for me to get my replacement. Then they wanted me to pay shipping and return my defective one (I did not return it). All together I had to buy THREE of these pumps and I have ONE that works...most of the time. If I were you I'd talk to your Dr. or the hospital where you had your baby and see if you can rent one. That way you know you're getting a good one and it shouldn't cost much. If I had it to do over, I'd either spring for the good/expensive pump or simply rent one from the hospital. This one is terrible, I'm extremely disappointed in the First Years product, customer service and company as a whole! Good luck to you!!!"}
