{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001N44BXE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370329200, 'question': 'I\'m getting a Pali Torino crib, and this mattress looks to be 5" shorter and less wide than the crib. Has size been a problem?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I bought a crib online, as well as this mattress which I really like a lot, and have had no problems at all with the length of the mattress. As long as your crib is "standard" size, this mattress should fit. It\'s a very snug fit, but I believe this is done on purpose for safety reasons. I highly recommend the mattress.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001N44BXE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370329200, 'question': "What makes it fire retardant? I'm looking for a chemical free mattress. The chemicals used do not necessarily have an odor.", 'answer': "Check out http://www.davincibaby.com/willow-natural-coconut-palm-crib-mattress and hover your mouse over the 'Meets Federal Flammability Standard CFR-1633'. They explain that the mattress does not contain any flame retardant materials, but use a thin layer of cotton-like material (possibly with Dupont chemicals) that do not contact the user and they use Kevlar thread to make the mattress, which is flame resistant. I did notice a slight odor when I removed it from the plastic wrapper, but aired it for several months before baby arrived and the slight smell was long gone. Good luck with your purchase- we have just flipped this one to the toddler side and I am still very happy with the purchase."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001N44BXE', 'answerTime': 'Aug 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407826800, 'question': 'What have you purchased as a replacement for this when your child moved to a twin/full size bed? I absolutely adore this mattress.', 'answer': "We personally did not like this mattress, but to answer your question. My granddaughter has gotten so very tall that she is now in what you would call a junior bed or a small twin bed and we use a Simmons Beauty Rest Med, Firm for her right now. Hope that helps, the important thing is to keep a bed guard up so they don't slip out of bed and as toddlers they seem to prefer a slightly softer bed than most adults can use , indulge them with a plush mattress for a while , it will change soon enough. Thanks for asking."}
