{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001N4TDI2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358582400, 'question': "Is Ergobaby and ERGObaby the same company, and what's the difference between teething pads and sucking pads?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not sure about the company name, but regarding the second half of your question, there isn't much difference between a teething pad and a sucking pad. Their purpose is to soak up the drool from your teething baby so that you don't have to wash the carrier every time you use it--you just wash the pads. Here's what happens--you put your baby into the carrier and he or she immediately starts sucking on the shoulder straps. Within ten minutes, both straps are soaked through. This prevents that from happening. You should get them if you get the carrier--get two sets. Keep in mind that you probably won't need to pull them out until your baby is around 4 months old. Then you'll use them until he or she is at least 20 months, I would think."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001N4TDI2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370242800, 'question': 'Can these be used as car seat strap covers too?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I haven't tried it but am sure they could."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001N4TDI2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372575600, 'question': 'Do these fit around the Beco Gemini straps?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, that's the carrier I have."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001N4TDI2', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380524400, 'question': 'Has anybody actually used these with there carseats? Do they fit or are they too small?', 'answer': 'They fit'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAATW0', 'answerTime': 'May 31, 2011', 'unixTime': 1306825200, 'question': 'Interference with WiFi network: Has anyone else been able to determine the specific frequency range (beyond just 2.4GHz) so it can be sidestepped?', 'answer': "Sadly, I think you (we) are screwed. I was having horrible speeds with Verizon FIOS for a few months (&lt;1Mbs), blaming Verizon and getting 3 new routers when I finally realized while I was on the phone with technical support that all my problems went away when I turned the BestView baby monitor off. I've tried all the channels with no luck. My wife and I just know to turn it off for a minute or two when we need to do some quick browsing. Very annoying..."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAATW0', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2010', 'unixTime': 1290499200, 'question': 'Additional cameras: Which additional camera can I use with this video monitor?', 'answer': 'Returning this product. I bought an extra camera only to find out I cant use them both at the same time (audio). So this is not a good monitor setup if you have multiple children. The extra cameras are only if you have 1 child and want to monitor him in different rooms.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAATW0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2012', 'unixTime': 1354608000, 'question': 'Replacement batteries: Anybody know what type of replacement batteries work with Summer Best View?', 'answer': 'I have a Summer Best View monitor that is about 3 years old. I replaced the batteries when they died with Duracell Rechargeable NiMH batteries. They came in a pack of 4 and I found them in stock at Best Buy. I still have to recharge them every day but they work fine. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAATW0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 19, 2010', 'unixTime': 1292745600, 'question': 'Extra cord/charger? Anyone know where to buy an extra charging cord for this monitor?', 'answer': 'I went to Radio Shack with the monitor and they sold me a cord that fit right.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAATW0', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2011', 'unixTime': 1306566000, 'question': 'Summer Infant Best View Handheld Color Video Monitor green static picture: Has anyone else ran into this issue?', 'answer': 'The exact same thing just happend to me! We have been using on and off for the past 4 months with no issue but not recently until we assembled the crib and moved our baby upstairs. Now suddenly we are getting the "green screen of death!" I\'ve try to shut off restart and also to re-pair the units but all i get is the fuzzy green picture. Any solutions welcomed. Thank you!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAATW0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2010', 'unixTime': 1280905200, 'question': "Can I Buy Two of These &amp; Use Each Monitor With The Other Monitor's Camera? If I wanted to buy two of these Video Monitors (each comes with a camera and monitor), can I use both monitors with both cameras?", 'answer': 'It doesn\'t work! Only one of the monitors will pick up both cameras. The other monitor keeps showing "Out of Range". Do not buy two sets with the intention of having two monitors for viewing because only one monitor will work! :( I know because I tried to do this.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAATW0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2011', 'unixTime': 1298275200, 'question': 'Multiple Cameras in the same room: Do, I need to buy an additional camera and monitor or do I need just an additional camera?', 'answer': 'Congratulations. I have 9 month old twin boys. I did the same thing: had them in the same crib at first. I used one camera then and when I separated them into their own cribs I ordered another camera on-line and used it with the same monitor. I have the Summer Infant Best View Handheld Color Video Monitor with 2.5" screen. You have to toggle between each camera to view each baby (I was bummed that you couldn\'t view them at the same time) but it works fine that way. Unless you have your cribs very close together, I would recommend two cameras so you can have them at a good enough distance to utilize the zoom feature. Otherwise, the view is too small and you can\'t check for their breathing (which I\'m sure every mother does in a paranoid moment!) I have the cameras mounted on the wall and they can reach them sometimes but they mostly leave them alone. If they detach the power cord, it will just fall to the floor. It isn\'t long enough for them to bring into the crib. I mention that because I recently received notification of a strangulation risk from the power cords on these monitors. I saw the photo dramatizations and the cameras were set up on a surface close to the baby\'s crib. Anyway, that\'s a few months away for you so you have time to think about changing the placement if you have to. The cameras and monitor work great still. I am very satisfied with them. Have fun!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAATW0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 24, 2011', 'unixTime': 1295856000, 'question': 'difference between "infant Best View" and "Slim and Secure"??? Anyone know the difference between the two Summer models (besides design)?', 'answer': "The Slim and Secure is a newer model. The handheld unit and the camera unit are quite a bit thinner than the Best View. I don't have it myself, so can only point you to the reviews on it for more info. Slim and Secure, see reviews. There's also a *Sleek* and Secure model. You may also want to visit the Summer Infant site."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQRI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380870000, 'question': 'Can these be washed in hot water and what size would an 18 lb 8 month old need?', 'answer': "Yes on hot water. I bought size mediums to go inside my BG 4.0 one size pocket diapers. They fit great on the medium and large rise setting. I use them under a one size microfiber BG insert for night. I rarely have leaks at night. Unless my daughter is a wiggle worm when I first put the diaper on. She's a tummy sleeper. My daughter is about 21-22lbs and almost 12 months. I've been using these for about 4-5 months now. Love them."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQRI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426748400, 'question': 'What size for Bumgenius 4.0? I am looking to use these as an overnight doubler in my Bumgenius 4.0 diapers.', 'answer': "We have Bumgenius Freetimes and have used the Large size for overnight doublers since our baby was 5 months old. She's now 13 months old and we still have had zero overnight leaks. We just fold over the ends and it will grow with the diaper as our daughter grows. it makes the diaper a bit bulky, but it's only for overnight and it lasts 13+ hours easily."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQRI', 'answerTime': 'Sep 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410332400, 'question': 'Do I need to wash these 5 or so times before use??', 'answer': 'I washed them once, and they worked fine but they do increase in absorbency after several washes.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQRI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': "What is the size of the medium and the large? Someone asked this questions, but the answer didn't say which size they were referring to.", 'answer': 'The mediums are 15 x 6 x 0.9 inches and the larges are 18 x 6 x 0.9 inches.'}
