{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQQO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380610800, 'question': 'Can these be washed with my microfiber inserts and pocket diapers, or do they require their own load?', 'answer': "I wash them in the same load as our diapers (organic cotton as well as microfiber) and fleece inserts. I've never had a problem with putting everything together."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQQO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'What size do you recommend for a 24lbs 22 month old who currently fits medium rise in BG 4.0 and Grovia hybrids?', 'answer': 'I would go with the medium. Once these are fully prepped they are really absorbent and can be used for many combinations in overnights or pockets. The length of the mediums worked all the way to potty training for me.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQQO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423123200, 'question': 'Are these better as a doubler or an insert?', 'answer': 'I would use something else in addition. They can cause irritation if placed right next to the skin. However they are incredible at absorbing large amounts. They work perfect in an overnight diaper in addition to a couple inserts!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001NAAQPK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392883200, 'question': 'Are they softer-more absorbent than other pre-folds? We have not had issues at all with our Bummis and Bumpkins...but I am curious about these.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Compared to all cotton, the are not soft. They're really rough if line dried."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001NAAQPK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371366000, 'question': 'Is small for three month?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'If you actually us it as a prefold instead of an insert, small should fit 0-3 on a small to average size baby. You could probably size up for an average to large baby.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQPK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392883200, 'question': 'Are these worth the cost? We are both Bummis and Bumpkins prefolds with Rumperooz covers-so bulky in front! What size for trifold in a cover?', 'answer': 'I think they are worth the cost. I have never used Bummis or Bumpkins but these are much trimmer than Econobum prefolds. As for size, it really depends on how big you little one is. We are still using the small on our 7 month old but the medium works as well. With our daughter, who potty trained at 23 months, we never used bigger than the medium.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001NAAQPK', 'answerTime': 'Sep 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411628400, 'question': 'Can these be used in a Flip Diaper Cover instead of Flip inserts? How do you make them sit inside a Cloth Diaper?', 'answer': "Yes. This is how we use them. I just do the newspaper fold and tuck them inside the covers. It works quite well, I hardly notice any shifting even though the Flip covers don't offer much fabric at the back."}
