{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001NJC5QY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385712000, 'question': 'Are the toys removable?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "you can pop everything out, but not to like play with on the floor - they're really just poppable to set it up or take it apart. the cups are removable, and my son loves to smash them on tables and the floor. the toys are flexible, though, so they're perfect for learning hand-eye coordination, reaching, and teething."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001NJC5QY', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387094400, 'question': 'is this made with PVC plastic', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not sure. I looked at the product info and it doesn't designate. We bought it for my grandson who is now six months old and we've had no problems getting him in and out of the seat. The tray revolves around when you hold the base secure. The front portion of the tray slides out so that you can put baby in and out easily. We've had no problems with this seat and my grandson enjoys sitting in it to play. Construction is even and secure and we've found it to be well worth the $33 I paid for it."}
