{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNK', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379401200, 'question': 'How wide is the base and the extensions?', 'answer': 'Hi, Ok so I measured everything to give you an idea of what all comes in box. Gate Without Any Extensions: 26.5in width 30in height Gate with Small Extension: 33.5in width 30in height Gate with Bigger(longer) Extension: 38.5in width 30in height Long Extension by itself: 13.5in width 30in height Short Extension by itself: 8.5in width 30in height Gate with both Extensions: 46in width and 30in height (This makes total sense now if you add the pressure screw length to this this will give you about 51-52in.) 4 Pressure Screws (all same size): 4.5 in length 4 Circle/Flower Pressure Screw Tightening Knobs (all same size): 1/2 in height 4 Circle Wall Cups (all the same) 1/2in height. There is a about 1in over gap on main gate on each side top and bottom for the extensions to overlay evenly when you put them on. This inch is included in width size above when I measured the pieces. First time commenting on here i would love to include pics but i do not know how to do so. Also they include 4 small screws to screw the 4 cups into the wall. You can use it without screwing them but seems more stable with doing so. Hope this helps. Let me know if you need more info.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNK', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399964400, 'question': 'how tall is this gate?', 'answer': 'The gate is 30 inches tall.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': 'Can you use the gate without the wall cups screwed to the wall?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, I use mine just pressure mounted - nothing screwed into the wall. It works fine, although if you bump it, it can move slightly, so it has to be adjusted when that happens. I've had one for a few years and bought a second one several months ago cuz I like it so much. I have them on either side of our kitchen to keep our little dogs contained when we leave the house. They work great. :-)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389772800, 'question': 'will the gate be able to adjust to 48 inches exactly and also does it have to be screwed into the wall', 'answer': "Yes, the gate will adjust to 48 inches and no, it doesn't screw into the wall. It has adjustable tension rubberized knobs on each end. Works well for me and my small dog."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': 'My pup is very small I am a little worried about the distance between the bars. she is about 4.5 pounds. I just wish I knew the size of the spaces.', 'answer': 'or easy reference, an upright coke/soda can just barely passes through the openings between bars.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374476400, 'question': 'Has anyone used this gate outdoors?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I have not but I can tell you that I would not recomend it. We use it inside. Personally, and from experience with other items made of similar material, that the plastic will sunn rott and the metal will rust. First thing that will go if you use it outside is the plastic and from there the gate is useless. If it is shaded and protected from the moisture it might last a while but not for a permanate fixture. Hope this helps'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': 'How wide are the slats? will they allow a cat to pass through but keep a small poodle out? Seems a little too tall for cats to jump over easily.', 'answer': 'No. It would have to be a very thin feline..or a kitten. Ours cannot.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNK', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414825200, 'question': 'distance between slats', 'answer': 'The distance between the slats is 3 inches.'}
