{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378882800, 'question': 'It says this is a pressure mounted gate, are screws needed at all to mount this gate?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "You don't *need* to screw it into the wall, but it comes with screws. I have 2 rather rambunctious cats that will pull on the gate if I'm on the other side of it for too long. Without it being mounted to the wall, they would, without a doubt, pull it down on a daily basis."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397631600, 'question': 'can a cat fit through the slots?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The widest gap is 2-3/4". A small cat could easily pass through. A larger cat would have to work at it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376809200, 'question': "I'm trying to figure out if this would be strong enough for my dog, who is 100 lbs and pretty strong, but doesn't jump. If not this, any suggestions?", 'answer': "If the dog doesn't jump on the gate it should work. Definitely mount to the door frame, it comes with the supplies. If you don't put the screws in the wall then anything that pushes up against it will knock it down."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418630400, 'question': 'Can this gate be mounted at the top of a stairway, where one side is a wall and the other is a wood banister?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't see why not. Mine is mounted in a hallway where the distance between the walls is wider than at floor level distance between the baseboard. Therefore, if your banister is the right height (at the top) it would work. Check the height of the solid most part of your banister to make sure it is the same height of the gate frame."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001OC5UNA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377673200, 'question': 'Does this gate stay open, or does it need to be propped open with something? Also, does it swing open either way or just in one direction?', 'answer': "It will stay open on its own. It only opens in one direction, it has a tab at the bottom of the gate but you can turn the gate so the door of it opens on the side you want.... Towards you or away from you. I turn mine so the tab at the bottom is on the side I don't want my dogs pushing open. I hope this helps :-) I wish I could send ya pics to help see it."}
