{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001QGIPS6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390204800, 'question': 'Can someone tell me how many trays come with this purchase? Also, how many trays do you recommend purchasing for a new or working mom? Thank you!', 'answer': "I have 2 trays, and looking at the price it must have come as a 2 pack...I know I wouldn't have spent $40 and ordered 2 individually. I am a retail store manager and work 40-50 hours a week and I did fine with the 2(and I had a serious over supply of milk so I was pumping and freezing A LOT!). Get yourself into a good rotation, remember to take them out of the trays the next morning and store them in a dated freezer bag. Do not put them in the dishwasher, my husband did once and one got a little warped."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001QGIPS6', 'answerTime': 'Jul 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404630000, 'question': 'How do you get the frozen milk out of the trays? I just froze my first batch and now I am battling to remove them.', 'answer': "Give it just a minute or two (not too long or they will defrost obviously) and then I just hold a hand on each side and try to twist the trays a little. I know it feels like there is no give but they will pop out. I've also run the back under warm water just for a second and then flipped it onto the lid and they slide right out! Good luck!"}
