{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001QIN6ME', 'answerTime': 'Dec 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386403200, 'question': 'How long does it stay warm after you unplug it ?', 'answer': "Not very long. Maybe an hour. Basically without being on it will return to room temperature or cooler because of the moisture. We do usually unplug when going out of town and try and leave empty. Sometimes my son just can't have the luxury of warm wipes. For example when we're on the go he gets a few spritzes of our homemade solution and dry wipes. For longer vacations we'll take a reusable wipes container, fill with wipes and our solution and use them cold. He doesn't complain too much. My son always appreciates coming home to his warm wipes. It's a good system! Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001QIN6ME', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400137200, 'question': 'are the wipes warm and damp? Or warm and dry?', 'answer': "Warm and damp if they start out damp. We use cloth wipes and we haven't had an issue with them drying out. If you don't have the antibacterial pad in the bottom, sometimes the last wipe will be dry. I just add a little bit of water to the warmer before adding my cloth, predampened wipes and I don't have any issues."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001QIN6ME', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389340800, 'question': 'what solution does it say to use?', 'answer': "My daughter uses Dr. Bonner's liquid lavender castile soap 2-3 capfuls to a quart of water. She has also adds a few drops of tea tree oil. I periodically remove the pad and thoroughly clean out the unit before I refill with clean cloths and solution. A great unit!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001QIN6ME', 'answerTime': 'Dec 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387008000, 'question': 'Can you use disposable wipes in this if needed?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I've wondered that too so I tried putting the whole package in the wipe container to see if maybe my pop-top lid disposible wipe package would help keep the wipes moist. I got nervous with that method because there was nothing btwn the warm plastic of the warmer and the packaging of the wipes. Typically they mention using a special wetted pad/sponge that's anti-bacterial, anti-mold, anti-mildew for your cloth wipes so they don't smell, so I stopped. It did feel like my wipes might dry out. I'd keep searching community boards for other expirences."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001QIN6ME', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418371200, 'question': "Can this be kept in a drawer (as long as there's a way to plug it in)? Does the exterior of the warmer get hot?", 'answer': 'Yes. The exterior is slightly warm on the bottom, but not enough to heat up whatever is underneath.'}
