{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001R2L6PS', 'answerTime': 'Jun 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402902000, 'question': 'how many wipes do you need for one baby?', 'answer': "It really depends on how often you intend to do laundry. If you're using cloth dipes and plan to wash your own (and daily), you'll need less. If you're using cloth diapers but with a service that comes once per week or if you're using disposable, you'll just have to decide what you're willing to wash them with or if you want to wash them alone AND how often you want to wash. I suggest at least 2 dozen to start. Also, if you know someone with a serger, have him/her serge around the edge -- they'll last a LOT longer if you do this. I love these wipes but they did start to fall apart quickly until my mom put them through her serger -- then they lasted wash after wash. Another tip -- don't ever use fabric softener or a dryer sheet with these or anything you want to be absorbent (like cloth dipes)...softeners leave a coating that, over time, builds up and will make the fabric less absorbent. Consider using a nice essential oil with your cloth wipes -- it makes the wipes smell so nice. Best of luck to you! :0)"}
