{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001SKKW0E', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': 'will it work for coax outlet?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It depends on the outlet. The back plate is shaped to fit around two standard outlets. If the coax connection fits in one of those two holes, it should be fine. The back plate is secured by replacing the center screw from a standard cover plate so the coax connection can't be dead center and needs to have that center screw. As far as routing the wire through the holes, it should fit - I've gotten thick gauge extension cords through the wire opening."}
