{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400137200, 'question': 'About how much milk can it collect before spilling out?', 'answer': 'I found it was two or three ounces before it got to the hole but I just kept an empty container (bottle or milk bag) handy and emptied it when it or close- was really a wonderful product and works really well- had no idea I was losing that much until I tried it!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385366400, 'question': 'IS it good to use at Night?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, do not use it at night for two reasons: It is not supposed to be worn for longer than the time it takes to nurse your baby (because after the milk collects in the milk-saver, it needs to be refridgerated). And also, the milk-saver has no top on it, so once the milk collects, if you were to bend over or lay down, all the milk would spill out.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404457200, 'question': 'Can I sterilize this in a microwave sterilizer. I have both a hard plastic sterilizing rack and the Medela bags, would it be safe in those?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Under the FAQ section of Milkies website, it says "Q: How should I clean my Milk-Saver? A: Be sure to thoroughly clean your Milk-Saver before first use. Rinse with hot soapy water, boil or run through your dishwasher on the top rack. Between uses simply rinse the Milk-Saver and air dry on a bottle rack or clean towel." I hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418025600, 'question': 'can you sleep with this product?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Ugh, no, don't do that. You'll waste all of your wonderful precious milk! The ocolette nursing cups are good for sleeping in."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383638400, 'question': 'Do they come in a pair? And would just one pair be enough? How many are recommended?', 'answer': "Only one device was sold on Amazon, but you can purchase a pair from the Milkies website. I've considered purchasing a second device since it does such a good job of collecting. However, I really only see using one at a time (while nursing on the other breast). If the milk saver was less bulky and were a closed unit to prevent spilling, then I would definitely order a second to wear while going about my day. But they are rather large and cannot be concealed under clothing. And I've forgotten twice and bent over, spilling all my collected milk. Therefore, it really should only be worn while actively nursing and should be removed when you remove the baby."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'Aug 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407394800, 'question': "Would these be something you can wear if you think you won't be able to pump for a few hours? Do they show under the shirt?", 'answer': "It's bulky. You can see it for sure. And movement is restricted since it's open top you can't bend over or it'll spill out the top. If I've felt my milk let down and didn't have my pump I've used it but it's definitely noticeable. And I recommend not using it as a substitute often from pumping. It's a great product. Worth every penny"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393920000, 'question': 'Any chance you can wear these while sleeping?', 'answer': "NO! the top is open, not only can you not sleep with them, but you can't bend over. It gives an all new meaning to crying over spilt milk, been there done that. I still highly recommend them though =D"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417420800, 'question': 'Would this be worth purchasing if I solely pump and do not breastfeed? (I produce quite a bit of milk throughout my day that is wasted on pads.)', 'answer': 'Yes! Omg yes! It catches so much milk! Instead of it getting wasted in s nursing pad!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001SMBRWO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384243200, 'question': 'wash', 'answer': 'The box says dishwasher safe. I have always just hand washed mine.'}
