{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001U7PV60', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388476800, 'question': 'Will this fit the 2012 Vista stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I am not sure. We have the 2011 stroller. I will warn you that I was informed in the stores that this would accommodate a 45 lb child, but the seat clearly states a limit of 35 lbs on the back. As a result, I have to put my baby in the rumble and my toddler in the big seat, which reclines. In short, I do not recommend this stroller for kids with a 2-3 year age gap. Perhaps this is a good idea for Irish twins, but it was not the best choice for my family. That said, we have probably put hundreds of miles on his stroller and rumble seat at the beach and in the malls, so we have made it work.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001U7PV60', 'answerTime': 'Mar 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394434800, 'question': 'I am expecting twins and would like to simply add the rumble seat to the stroller to use once the kiddos are 6 m old. (one kid in the regular chair one in the rumble seat) would that be comfortable for the twins? should i just bite the bullet and get a...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I doubt this would be comfortable for twins. I would not have wanted to put a 6 month old in the rumble seat. It has very little support and no ability to recline. It is not ideal for babies/toddlers who like to nap in the stroller. We purchased a city mini gt double and are happy with it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001U7PV60', 'answerTime': 'Apr 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396422000, 'question': 'Can the rumble seat face forward? If not, anyone find this a challenge with 2nd child having a view of the back of the other seat?', 'answer': "It only faces backwards. I never found it a problem as my toddler never sat in it for long periods of time. It's not a real double stroller-just a toddler seat for navigating parking lots etc."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001U7PV60', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385625600, 'question': 'Collapse', 'answer': "You need to remove the seat before closing the stroller. The seat itself does not fold up but it doesn't take up much room. It fits in the basket under the stroller (when stroller is open) and can be tucked into it when closed. I highly recommend it. My very tall 3.5 year old still fits comfortably when needed."}
