{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001VE00UO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384588800, 'question': "I've used this car seat rear facing for a year and a half. Can I use it front facing as well or is it ONLY for rear facing?", 'answer': 'This seat is only to be used for rear facing. Studies show infants and toddlers should remain rear facing until at least age 2 or even up to three. Doing this will greatly reduce the risk of serious injury during accidents.'}
