{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001WAJVZM', 'answerTime': 'Jun 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404111600, 'question': 'Does it protect your child from hiting the bottom of the faucet...it looks open at bottom', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. It has to be open at the bottom for the water to fill the bathtub. However, the whale comes down below the faucet about a half inch to an inch. That extra coverage means the metal of the faucet is covered. It has saved us from hitting the bottom twice.'}
