{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001XUIEFO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381820400, 'question': 'Has anybody used them outside? Would they be sturdy enough on a concrete patio?', 'answer': 'These mats are recommended for indoor uses. It is fine if you only use it temporary and put it away afterwards. Extended use outside may alter the color or quality due to the weather.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001XUIEFO', 'answerTime': 'May 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400569200, 'question': 'Have the mats been tested and shown to be free of any formamide emissions? (formamide emissions have been related to cancer and reproductive issues)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'A lot of customers were concern after France and Belgium issued a ban on EVA foam mats. However, these two countries have reversed the ban and reduced the restriction limit to &gt;200 mg/kg on how much formamide foam mats can contain instead. Keep in mind that no other countries have banned or set restrictions on formamide. http://newsletter.sgs.com/eNewsletterPro/uploadedimages/000006/sgs-safeguards-1291212-france-extends-temporary-ban-for-formamide-in-puzzle-mats-a4-en-12.pdf Australia conducted their own test on formamide in foam mats and have found no health risk, you can read the article in the following link: http://www.productsafety.gov.au/content/index.phtml/itemId/989496 All our mats have pass and exceed all US regulations. Our standard mats have not been specifically tested for formamide as we are not required nor any real tests show that it is a safety concern to children. According to our manufacturer in Taiwan, our standard mats meet the formamide limit set by France at &gt;100 mg/kg. In order to better serve our concerned customers, we have brought in formamide non-detectable mats. You can find the reports in the following link: http://www.ewonderworld.com/test%20report/ACT-Mats_FormamideNDTestReport.pdf You can order the Formamide Non-Detectable mats in the following link: http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B008YGT2GK Please note we do NOT plan on carrying these formamide ND mats in the future so supply is limited. It is too costly(to manufacture and for our customers as well), low demand, have not been proven to be a health risk to children nor is required by country other than France and Belgium. Let me know if you have any more questions regarding formamide or foam mats in general.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001XUIEFO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429167600, 'question': 'Does it include a storage container/bag?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No it doesn't"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001XUIEFO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429167600, 'question': 'Anyone know if the tiles get slippery when wet?', 'answer': "These tiles have a textured side and a smoother side. The smooth side might get slippery if a LOT of water (or beverage) were spilled but I've not found them to ever be slippery with a little milk or juice spilled. And because the tiles are foam and give a little when you walk on them they are less likely to present a hazard even with water on them."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001XUIEFO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412146800, 'question': 'Has the construction of this product changed? I dont understand how some state there is absolutely no ordor but others comment on the strong odor.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Great question. The constructions of this product has not changed. However, with any new shrink wrapped products there will a minor "new" smell that will fade with time. We recommend you allow them to air out for 1-3 days if odor is present.'}
