{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00260GN0I', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371020400, 'question': 'Is this product indeed non-skid? Numerous reviews say otherwise.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, it has a rubbery bottom which helps to secure it a bit. Of course it will move around somewhat but to secure it in place more it's best to attach it to the changing table in the back. That's how we have it. If you put a cover on it then it will no longer be non-skid b/c the cover goes over the sides of the non-skid bottom and that makes it slide around on wood furniture. but that's how it is for all changing pads. We've tried more than one pad and still use this one for over a year. for the price it's a good product."}
