{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0027UYT4O', 'answerTime': 'Aug 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377241200, 'question': 'How tight is the seal on the individual sections? Could I put yogurt in one section without the yogurt spilling into other sections? thanks', 'answer': 'There are seven sections to each container. There is not an individual seal for each section, only one large one that seals for the entire piece. From my experience, the one seal has been enough with the purees which is a similar consistency to yogurt. I have only used the tray for freezing purees and nothing has leaked, spilled or released after freezing even in the individual sections. If you plan on storing the tray in the refrigerator, you should not store the tray on its side or upside down. Hope this helped.'}
