{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ACEGDS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412319600, 'question': "Many of the reviews note that the drawers don't open very far (distance-wise). Anyone know how far they do open (in inches or as a percentage of total drawer depth)?", 'answer': 'So long as you install them correctly they open the full length of their depth (length of drawer going from front to back) and stop automatically once they hit the rollers. The drawers are about 1 foot wide and 1 foot long and about 6 to 7 inches deep and those are just rough estimates. If you align it correctly when its installed it will come all the way out about 1 foot which is the full length of the drawers.'}
