{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002AQIA3G', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387612800, 'question': 'Does the cover come off so it can be washed if needed?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Sorta, but not really. It is a VERY snug fitting cover so it is tough to pull off and put back on. I haven't actually done it with the sofa but with one of the little chairs. The cover was either glued or had fused to the foam in the crevices so I had to rip it free and ripped some small chunks out of the foam when I did it. I was able to get the cover back on but not snug in the corners/crevices like it started. I didn't machine wash either, only hand washed. My concern with the sofa is it would not snug back onto the foam where the sofa unfolds. All that being said, we've had good success with steam cleaning the covers while still on the furniture and spot cleaning with a scrub brush. We've had our little chair for six years and the sofa for three years and they are both holding up great. We LOVE them."}
