{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002C3S0QE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2009', 'unixTime': 1234771200, 'question': 'Will this seat fit in a honda civic? Anyone know if it will fit?', 'answer': "This really would depend on how you have to have your front seats positioned. I know a mom who has this seat installed rear-facing in an older model 2 door honda civic and she has no issues with getting it installed or using it with her daughter. Best advice would be to hit up a babies r us or another store that allows you to take the seat out to the car and try it in the back seat where you want to place your child. Remember though it will likely fit nicer when properly installed by a tech then when you take it out to the car to try it. You will need a pool noodle (my recommendation) or a rolled towel to get a good Rear-facing install. Once you know if it would fit come on-line and order it for a better deal and nicer covers. I can't say enough positive things about this seat. I passed up buying a First Years (Compass) True Fit and Britax Marathon or Boulevard for this seat and I wouldn't trade it for any of the seats on the market today."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002C4H0KU', 'answerTime': 'May 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401519600, 'question': 'How does the sizing work for this? Does it depend on the size of the baby or the size of the wearer?', 'answer': "It's based on the size of the wearer. The wrap is very adjustable and it's in the nature of it being woven that it will soften up/break in as you use it and therefore adjust as your kiddo weighs more. We love ours and wore it from the time our little one was about a month and still do now that she is 7 months. We got a large because my husband and I are both just under 6' and average size; and I wanted a long tale to allow for for privacy when breast feeding."}
