{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002CGRSXC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419753600, 'question': 'Could this gate be used outdoors? I am looking for a gate to mount between my garage and fence to block a path from my dog.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I think it could be mounted outdoors easily. That said, you might risk rust in a few places where the gate latches.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002CGRSXC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413442800, 'question': "How much space, width-wise, do you need to mount the gate on both sides? We bought a banister installation kit and it's only 1.5 inches wide.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'On one side (the side the whole gate mounts to) 1.5" would be enough. On the other side (the side for the latch/lock), you\'ll need about 2.5-3".'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002CRIQSW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2011', 'unixTime': 1308985200, 'question': 'how to convert to toddler bed? Can anyone help me with this?', 'answer': 'you take the front side off, put the mattress in the lowest setting, and use this product http://www.amazon.com/Kidco-Convertible-Crib-Bed-Rail/dp/B002ZDFVP4/ref=cm_cr_pr_product_top to make a short side to keep the toddler from rolling out. graco does not make or sell a conversion kit to make it a "toddler bed" that most people assume.'}
