{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002CYJU6C', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390723200, 'question': 'I have an antique cradle that is 18 by 35 1/8", does this mattress "give" at all? If the mattress was a hair too big, could I squeeze it in there?', 'answer': 'Yes it will give, should have no problem with it. We are satisfied with the purchase. Our cradle had a thin 1" mattress already, added this one on top to make a thicker padding. But this mattress by itself will work well. Good purchase for the price.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002CYJU6C', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385366400, 'question': 'Any chance it would fit in a 17" x 36" cradle?', 'answer': 'i dont think it would fit in a 17" x 36" cradle... It fits perfectly without any gap in my 18" x 36" cradle so it could be bigger to fit in a 17" x 36" cradle ...'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002CYJU6C', 'answerTime': 'Feb 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422777600, 'question': 'How is the firmness?', 'answer': "It is very firm. When I push on it it doesn't cause an impression. I imagine you are worrying that when a baby is lying on it either is to hard - which I don't think it is just firm - or to soft to worry about the baby and breathing. I don't see that as an issue, but that is my opinion. I do plan to use a mattress pad cover and then of course a decorative sheet. I hope this helps. I like this mattress."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002CYJU6C', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418803200, 'question': 'will this fit in the Eddie Bauer Wood Bassinet Cradle?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes it should as long as the bassinet is that same rectangular shape. This particular brand appears to be the same size as my daughter's cradle and it's a perfect fit."}
