{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413270000, 'question': 'How do you prep these inserts? Is there a special wash routine prior to using them for the first time?', 'answer': 'As with all natural fiber inserts, in order to get maximum absorbency, you will need to wash and dry a few times. You can use them after the first wash/dry cycle, but they become more absorbent after a few separate wash/dry cycles.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406444400, 'question': 'Could I use this inside a disposable diaper at night?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Technically u could but I would not recommend it. These are not quick absorbing. So you need like a cotton or a microfiber to go on top. If you use microfiber you need something on top of that because its not suppost to touch the babies skin. You would be better off just buying a diaper cover. You can reuse the cover and it's better than a disposable."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401692400, 'question': 'These are not straight hemp, they are a hemp and microfiber combo? So can I use just these in the diaper or I have to use it along with a microfiber?', 'answer': "They're hemp and cotton mix. Not microfiber. Yes I would suggest layering it with either a cotton insert/prefold or a microfiber insert only because hemp does not absorb quickly. Microfiber is like a towel and absorbs quick. Hemp takes a little more time to soak in, but it holds more. These are great I stuff mine with a insert for night time."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426748400, 'question': 'I see the dimensions (Large: 14.5" x 5.5" and Small: 12" x 5"), but is that new in package, or after washing and drying? I understand hemp shrinks.', 'answer': 'That\'s before washing. I have both sizes and they shrunk about 1" in length, .25" in width. Super absorbant even with the slight shrinking.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406012400, 'question': 'Do these have any kind of snap on them?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392105600, 'question': 'Can you use these on top of a prefold next to babies skin?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You can but it's not suggested, it is a slow absorber which means you would want something on top to wick away the moisture, we use charcoal bamboo on top, you could use a prefold as well"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413183600, 'question': 'Can these be used alone or they are doublers to be used under a Microfiber insert?', 'answer': 'Only as a doubler. They absorb very slowly, but hold A LOT! I use them under micro fleece in a pocket and also in the middle of a grovia insert. Love them!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426834800, 'question': 'Could these inserts be used by themselves in the Thirsties duo wrap cover?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'According to the manufacturer, these work best as stated below: Thirsties Hemp Insert for the very best in bulletproof protection against leaks. Made from 6 layers of remarkably soft hemp & cotton blend knit jersey, you will find that these are exactly what your baby needs to sleep comfortably through the night without leaks. The steady and stable absorption characteristics of hemp works best behind the fast absorbing power of the microfiber terry soaker of Thirsties Fab Fitteds and One Size Pocket Diaper. The manufacturer does not state that these can be used or not used with a Duo Wrap Cover, as long as there is no MICROFIBER to touch baby, these should be okay to use.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002FB7FLY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421740800, 'question': 'Are these machine washable? Do they work well with thirsties duo wrap?', 'answer': "Yes, they're machine washable. I don't have any of the duo wraps, but they work well with my Thirsties AIOs, as well as with all my other (various brands) covers."}
