{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002FKCOFM', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428217200, 'question': 'Will the mat colors bleed if used for wet blocking crochet projects?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'Hello, SueBee. I have no idea what "wet blocking crochet projects are" so I asked my wife....and she didn\'t know either. She\'s into quilting and not crochet. So, what I did was this; I took 2 of the darker colored "tiles" and brought them upstairs to the kitchen. There I wet a white paper towel and scrubbed them both (pink and purple) and absolutely NO color came off into the towel. Assuming that your crochet work doesn\'t involve solvents, heat or much friction, I would think that they would be absolutely safe for your projects. I hope this is helpful. All the best. Alan in MA'}
