{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002FKAMLA', 'answerTime': 'Feb 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391241600, 'question': 'How thick are the tiles?', 'answer': 'They are a full 1/2" thick. I used these as a play mat on our hardwood floors when I was babysitting my grandson every day from the time he was 4 months to 18 months and they provided plenty of padding. I also used them on my glass coffee table (2 layers of the tiles) so he could play with his cars and trucks on there. My daughter now has a row of them on her fireplace hearth where he plays. This summer I bought a second set of the tiles and used them both (in a single layer) as padding on our cement patio under the kiddie pool we got for him (the pool was big enough that his parents also sat in it with him) and they worked out great! My only complaint about this set is that it didn\'t come with the border pieces; not a big deal, but would have been nice.'}
