{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002G9UTVI', 'answerTime': 'Sep 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411887600, 'question': 'Would this fit with a Baby Jogger GT? Does one have to take it off to fold the stroller?', 'answer': "It should fit the GT but the only issue is the top of the bundle has a strap that you need to secure around the top of the seat, so in any of the strollers where the canopy cannot be disconnected from the headrest that will make it hard, but it will still work...but in a smaller child I would be concerned about the head part falling over the child's head and possibly suffocating it, in a larger/older child I would not have this worry. You should be able to fold the stroller with it on"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002G9UTVI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408604400, 'question': 'Does this fit the Baby Jogger Citi Mini? And can I use it for my 6 month old?', 'answer': "Yes it fits the Citi Mini (or is it City Mini?) but I don't know about the 6 month old. I'd say if you want to use it with an infant, you should probably roll the top like they have done in the picture. It's soft material so you can probably tuck in the extra material on the sides. But beware of overheating. It gets really hot in there. So open the zipper as soon as you get indoors and don't use it unless it is negative 10 or more Celsius (I don't know the Fahrenheit system)."}
