{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002G9UTUE', 'answerTime': 'Nov 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384502400, 'question': "My infant is almost 21 lbs, but he is only 9 months old. It looks like the infant size may be too small or not last long enough to justify buying it. Does the toddler size fit in a Chicco Keyfit 30 car seat? I'd like one that is compatible with both my...", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I would go with the toddler size. Worst case is it might hang over the end of the car seat-just be sure is does not mess with the locking mechanism when you use the base. The toddler size will fit on your bugaboo for YEARS to come.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002G9UTUE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383030000, 'question': 'size', 'answer': 'The size is 31.9 x 16.1 x 2 inches. Its pretty big and fits well in my sons stroller. The only problem is that the outer material is very stiff and its not so easy to manage because of that.'}
