{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002GD4H6M', 'answerTime': 'Jun 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371538800, 'question': 'How wide and deep is the attachment part? Meaning, how much overhang or table space is needed to attach it?', 'answer': 'The attachment part that goes under the table is 13 3/4" long from the seat to the farthest brace point. From the seat to the center bar it\'s 4 1/2" from the center bar to the far brace it\'s 8 1/2 inches. I have mine seated on our island bar where there is an 11" over hang and the seat is secure!! For the width, underneath it\'s 13 1/2" bar to bar. On top, with the tray, the width is more like 15 1/4". Hope that helps.'}
{'answer': 'Hi, I would say about 16-18" or so. It can attach to a table or bar without fully being pushed all the way in. It\'s very secure-my nine month old loves it & so do I!! Great for feeding & she loves sitting in there & playing while I cook! I would recommend this chair for sure!!', 'asin': 'B002GD4H6M', 'answerTime': '25 days ago', 'question': 'How much clearance is required for the brackets under the table? i.e. - what is the length of the arms from where the kid sits to where they end?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
