{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002GDF8GU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424937600, 'question': 'How many bottles are they?', 'answer': '5 total- 3 8 oz and 2 4oz with 2 extra level 2 nipple that fits any wide neck style bottle'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002GDF8GU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422172800, 'question': 'How old can the baby be to use these bottles? Is there a max age? Sorry...may be stupid question, but first time mom-to-be.', 'answer': "I wish I would have been smart enough to ask this! Our daughter is exclusively breastfed, and I never needed to use a bottle until she was about a month old. At that point, the smaller (4oz) bottles were more than big enough. But starting at about 3 months old, she needs between 4 and 5 oz to satisfy her. My biggest bit of advice would be to NOT overfill the small bottle. They will leak! I just assumed that if 5 oz would fit, it would be fine. No. I know that was a really long answer! I don't think babies ever need more than 8 oz of milk or formula at once, so they should not grow out of the 8 oz bottles. On a side note, we love these bottles! She never gets gassy from them, and she transitions from boob to bottle seamlessly! Congrats and good luck!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002GDF8GU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420790400, 'question': 'Made in USA or other country for bottle and nipple?', 'answer': 'Made in China'}
