{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ITDA9Y', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380524400, 'question': 'Can this be used with twins?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'You could probably put two small babies in. But for safety reasons, you would use this and another carrier. I know of a lot of moms that tandem BabyWear (wearing two babies at once) usually with a wrapped or soft structure on the back and wrapped/ soft structured/ ring sling on the front. Idk where you live but if youre near a meeting for beltway babywearers int they are great help. Check out this post about tandem wearing : http://somdbabywearers.weebly.com/1/post/2013/01/wearing-two.html , http://andbabiesmake10.wordpress.com/category/tandem-babywearing-2/ Happy babywearing!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ITDA9Y', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'How do you know what size to get? There is no sizing information available.', 'answer': 'Small is for people 5\'2" and below, medium for 5\'2"-5\'9", large for above 5\'9" and extra large is for people with a large frame.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ITDA9Y', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391760000, 'question': 'How long is the wrap? and does it take a long time to wrap?', 'answer': "I did a rough measure since I have wrapped mine and it is around 74 inches long. It took maybe 15 minutes to make the wrap a sling the first time. Once you sling it you don't need to keep doing it unless it comes out. I love using this wrap because it is very easy to adjust and does not take much time."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ITDA9Y', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425283200, 'question': 'Can baby be worn on my back with this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Maybe, but i doubt it would be as safe or comfortable as a soft structured carrier or a regular wrap for back carry, and you would defintitely need a helper to get lo on your back safely. The is a sling, not a full wrap. I only felt confortable wearing ds in front carry until he was about 15lbs, and as a hip carry for short periods until about 20 lbs. Having said all that, this carrier was ds's preferred carrier to nap in as a newborn. If you are looking for something to transition better to an older baby/ young toddler, but still help baby feel cradled, a full wrap would be a good choice (however, it's my understanding that they can take a while to get wrapping techniques down)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ITDA9Y', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422604800, 'question': 'What material is it made of?', 'answer': 'The material may vary depending on color chosen, but I think most are all cotton or cotton blend. The one I purchased (striped reobozo fabric) was all cotton.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ITDA9Y', 'answerTime': 'Oct 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413010800, 'question': 'Has anyone used this for heavier kids? I have a special needs son 30 lbs but 6 years old and need a way to have some outside support to help carry him', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Unless you are a regular weight lifter I wouldn't recommend it, and I am pretty sure he exceeds the weight limit, anyhow. I was no longer comfortable carrying my son for any length of time in a front carry after he was 15lbs; he's about 25 lbs and this *may* help a bit with a hip carry still. You should look for a toddler soft structured carrier (I think most are rated up to 40 lbs), or I think a Storchenwiege wrap could work. Either way, you'll have to shell out around $150-180 new for a carrier that will work for you. The structured carriers are very nice for back carries if you need to carry him for a longer period of time."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ITDA9Y', 'answerTime': 'Aug 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407740400, 'question': 'What is the maximum weight this can carry?', 'answer': "The Maya Wrap site says 35-40 lbs. I'm still using mine for my 3-year-old, who's just under 30 lbs, and she still comfortably fits."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ITDA9Y', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407135600, 'question': 'Could I wrap a newborn in this wrap? Is there a size minimum?', 'answer': '8lbs is the min weight.'}
