{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ITOC7S', 'answerTime': 'Jan 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390464000, 'question': "Will the alarm still work if the baby is in an automatic swing? Will the motion of the swing fool it into thinking the baby's breathing?", 'answer': 'I was told the swing would "fool" it and if you set it in the swing alone it will still blink as if it were on the baby. I have had it go off, however, while my daughter was in the swing. I think it had come loose, but the alarm definitely sounded and the swing was still in motion. I still used it everytime my daughter was in the swing.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ITOC7S', 'answerTime': 'Nov 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385712000, 'question': 'What voltage does this require? Or is it battery operated? My wife is having twins and we plan to put them side by side. Will it work independently?', 'answer': "A 3Volt Battery. It Attaches To The Diaper So You Would Need 2. It Comes With A battery. I Have Used One On My Son For All Naps And Bedtimes For The Last 7 Months And I Still Havent Had To ReplacetThe Battery. Look Up Snooza Battery On,Amazon They Aren't Expensive."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ITOC7S', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373439600, 'question': 'Does this work for a stomach sleeping baby?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, you just put it on the back of the diaper a little off to the side. I still use it on my 8 month old who sleeps mostly on his tummy.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ITOC7S', 'answerTime': 'Mar 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363503600, 'question': 'diaper changes and/or night feedings? Will it alarm? How does this work during diaper changes and/or night feedings?', 'answer': "For diaper changes, instead of turning it off I would clip it to my own shirt etc., that way I didn't forget to turn it back on when putting it back onto Baby, but it didn't alarm because it detected my own movement."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ITOC7S', 'answerTime': 'Mar 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363417200, 'question': 'Does anyone have experience with this product specifically when they brought their premature child home from the hospital? (27 weeker for us)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I love this product, it gives me peace of mind at night! Our baby was premature as well but not as premature as yours... Make sure when you clip on the Snuza that you fold over the diaper before clipping it on otherwise you will have false alarms!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ITOC7S', 'answerTime': 'Oct 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381734000, 'question': 'Can this monitor be used once the baby starts moving around in bed and rolling over to belly?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Absolutely. In fact my daughter would sleep on my wife's chest sometimes at night & if it came lose off her diaper while between them it would go off so it knew something was wrong. I've read parents with cosleeping twins used it just fine too."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ITOC7S', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385107200, 'question': "Does other sound in the room cause a false alarm? Because of close rooms and other house noise, we anticipate having a sound machine in the baby's room. I was just curious if this would interfere.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "As far as I know the snuza only alarms if there is an absence of movement. The sound machine should not interfere unless you of course you can't hear the alarm."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002ITOC7S', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427180400, 'question': "Does this work in the car? I'm interested in getting this for a very long cross-country trip with my baby in the back seat.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't believe it would. I'm sorry. Because it senses the baby's tummy movements I feel it would sense the vehicles movements of it is bumpy. Then again if you have a smooth riding vehicle I think it might work"}
