{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002MZZJXO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2012', 'unixTime': 1347433200, 'question': 'Unwanted wheel locking makes turning difficult: Has anyone else had this problem?', 'answer': 'Me too! Just had this problem...called and they were wonderful! Here is what they needed from me and voila...new wheel! :) Thank you for contacting Baby Jogger. I am sorry to hear about the issue you have experienced with the front wheel on your City Mini single stroller. In order to process a warranty claim for a replacement front wheel assembly, I will need the following information: Copy of your proof of purchase (original receipt, credit card statement, email confirmation, etc.) Serial Number and Manufacture Date (these are engraved in the vertical metal bar, above the back right wheel) US shipping address Phone number for shipping purposes Once I have received the above information, I will be able to begin processing your warranty claim. Please let me know if you have any questions or concerns. Thank you and have a great day! Just call 1800-241-1848'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002MZZJXO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 7, 2011', 'unixTime': 1307430000, 'question': 'Is it good in the dirt?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi Nathan. I have had a City Mini Double for over a year now and I absolutely love it. It really is as good as all the reviews say. The front wheels can be locked to handle some terrain better, but it really is not designed for off-roading. If you are just going on some flat dirt or even grass at the ballfield, you should have no real problem, but if you are a more outdoors family, I would recommend the Baby Jogger City Elite Double (must confess, I own this one too) instead or at least something with air filled tires. That's the one I use all winter in New England in the snow and to the zoo and stuff in the summer. The City Mini really is versatile, though. I've taken it on planes and to to Disney & Busch Gardens, etc. Just depends on your needs. The Elite is expensive, but can be found elsewhere online for significantly less. Good luck!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002MZZJXO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393228800, 'question': 'How to store on a garage wall', 'answer': "We use ours so much I haven't had to worry about storing/hanging it, but two large hooks screwed into your garage wall should do the trick."}
