{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002MZZJXO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1366959600, 'question': 'Good stroller for a large child? Is this a good stroller for a bigger child, or will he feel squished?', 'answer': 'McClaren. They make high quality strollers, and they are taller than most. My youngest is my tallest, and we bought a used McClaren that I adored!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002MZZJXO', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1301209200, 'question': "2011 City Mini Double Shoulder harness straps: Those of you who have the city mini, if you have older kids who don't like the shoulder harness how did you remove them?", 'answer': 'We took off the top hooks, un-threaded the whole strap, put the waist clip back on, re-threaded through the little sliding length adjuster. You will have some strap still dangling, because it is long, but it is working for us and way easier to load and unload our twins. They would hate being strapped down! This is on the 2009 version, but I think the straps are the same. Does this make any sense to you?'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002MZZJXO', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2011', 'unixTime': 1305529200, 'question': 'Difference between 2010 and 2011: Does anyone know what the difference is between the 2010 and 2011 model of the city mini double stroller?', 'answer': 'I called and asked customer service. They said 3 things: back support is increased, the sun visors come down separately and a little further down, and there is a feature that the child can sit upright a little more.'}
