{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ONUZMY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401606000, 'question': 'Is the mat cushioned enough to put it directly on the floor or should it be placed on carpet? My house is all wood floor.', 'answer': "It has been a while since I used it but it I remember it being quite cushioned. It does depend on the age of your child. If your baby's head is still wobbly, and their is a chance they could accidentally knock their head when rolling over etc, I think the wood floor directly underneath will be too hard. I also have wooden floors but lots of rugs too, and it was generally placed on top of a floor rug and not directly on a the wooden floor."}
