{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002OOWAB2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397631600, 'question': 'How padded is the bottom of this? Is it padded enough to allow for the baby to sleep comfortably for extended periods of time?', 'answer': "It's not super padded on the head but most of the bassinets I looked at weren't either. I used a yellow foam bath pad on the head area to add softness--the type you use to keep babies from slipping in the bath but I also didn't use this rocker until he was a couple of months old and had head control to move. If you're looking for something for a newborn, I'd recommend the FP Rock n' Play Snugglebunny. It's ideal for newborns and very soft. We used this Portable Rocker after he outgrew the snugglebunny since it's larger with a higher weight limit."}
