{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002Q0YA4O', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': "My son doesn't want to sit, he straddle the potty. Does anyone else have a straddler?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'My son did the same thing for 1 day. I figured he was trying to pee like Dad by kind of standing over it. I told him we sit on this potty and that it makes messes if he does that. Later we trained him to stand at the big one like Dad since he showed interest by standing at his potty. Maybe that is what your son is trying to do? He might want to be a stander.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002Q0YA4O', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371711600, 'question': 'good for a 9 month old, ECer?', 'answer': "yes! my boy is just over 8 months and big for his age and though we've been using it for awhile it's perfect now. he sits on it independently and his feet touch the ground. we love it."}
