{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QEAJ9K', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': 'Does this adapter work on the Britax B Safe car seat?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'This is a basic strap that will work with nearly any infant seat to secure it to a stroller. It is two separate pieces that loop onto a stroller (1 on each side bar) then it goes over the top of the stroller and clips it into place.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QEAJ9K', 'answerTime': '19 days ago', 'question': 'Will these adapter straps secure my britax b-safe car seat to a valco snap duo?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No please contact the stroller manufacturer to determine if they offer an adapter that passes regulatory requirements with the car seat.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QEAJ9K', 'answerTime': 'Oct 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414134000, 'question': 'Can I use this with Maxi Cosi Mico?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'This strap will work with any car seat that has a seat belt spot on the too of the car seat. Its basically two straps that look onto your stroller and clip over the top if the seat. They are awesome!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QEAJ9K', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'I have a Chicco KeyFit 30 infant seat and a Graco Snap N GO stroller frame. Would this strap work well to secure the infant seat in the frame?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Probably? It's just a set of straps with a buckle in the middle. It's never going to be as secure as using the separate pieces as they were intended. However, if there is a place to hook the straps onto the Graco Snap n Go, you could probably cobble it together that way. It would obviously be safest to either just get a Graco seat that fits the Snap n Go or the Key-Fit caddy."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QEAJ9K', 'answerTime': 'Jan 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390464000, 'question': "I have a Chicco Cortina Together double stroller and I'm getting a Britax Chaperone car seat. Would this adapter work for that?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It would likely work ok. It's just a set of straps you loop around the stroller frame to snap around the carseat. You'd be better off with the Keyfit for that stroller though, if you're buying a new one anyway. The straps will kind of be a pain and with the keyfit, your carseat will snap right in an be a lot more stable."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389254400, 'question': 'Anyone know if this will work with the older (pre-2008) chair?', 'answer': "It definitely does! Our chair is a hand me down from the early 2000's and it works great."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387612800, 'question': 'Is this tray compatible with the Baby Set?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes we used it with our baby set. Make sure to only use water and mild soap to clean this tray and nOT any type of household cleaner spray. It ruins the plastic.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391328000, 'question': 'Does anyone know how this tray compares to the one Stokke is now making themselves?', 'answer': "Caveat: I haven't actually used Stokke's tray, but I can give you a few differences just from looking. 1) PlayTray is smooth all over, it quickly wipes down (even on the bottom side). 2) Playtray is a little bit wider, as it fits over the side of the chairs. 3) Playtray is the only option for older Stokke chairs. 4) Playtray does not need the infant attachment to work. However, I wouldn't put an infant under 6 months (ie, NOT sitting capable) without an additional restraint of some sort for support. Around 9 months, my kids were quite comfortable and capable of sitting in it without the support; but at that point they were likely to climb out if not restrained. (Around 12 months, we put the Playtray away and have the child sit directly at the table, although there is no reason it can't be used longer if you want.)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'Dec 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418630400, 'question': 'Do you need to have the baby seat for this play tray to fit on the chair?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, you don't"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'Jan 11, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420963200, 'question': "work with the latest tripp trapp model? i just got it and it can't be right", 'answer': "My grandchildren have aways used it. Again today! The youngest, aged 23 months, won't sit in his Tripp Trapp without the tray. His older brother, aged 3, sits in a Tripp Trapp without the tray. The older grandkids used it till they were 6 and 7 years old. The best buys ever. I have two!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417593600, 'question': 'Does anyone know if an older (pre-2008) play tray works with a newer chair and baby set?', 'answer': "I just checked the bottom of my chair and it was made in 07, I have the baby seat on mine and we use the tray with no problem. The tray doesn't line up with the baby seat perfectly there is a space of about an inch in the front (that tapers down on the sides) that food sometimes gets dropped down and she almost got her finger stuck in the smaller space but we stopped her before it did. Overall she is more interested in the food on the tray or the food being dropped off the tray. So yes it fits but it isn't lined up perfectly. We love our tray she hangs out eating off the tray while we make dinner or do dishes and we loose the tray for meals."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'Oct 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413874800, 'question': 'Can you use this tray with the Stokke Handysitt?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'With stokke babysit kit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'May 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401174000, 'question': 'Does anyone know the difference between this tray and the $50 one?', 'answer': "Yes! You have to have the infant seat to use the $50 dollar one, so as soon as the baby outgrows the baby seat, you are trayless! It's a bummer that there are so few options, because we have this tray and it peeled pretty quickly after we got it. But, love the stokke seat!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399964400, 'question': 'If you only use soap and water (and not a household cleaner spray), does the plastic on the tray still peel off over time?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "We've had our white tray for over a year and we only use soap and water. The plastic has scratches and is a bit rough where my son scrapes the silverware. We have no flaking of the plastic though. We were worried about it based on reviews, but I'm completely happy with how it's performed. It's far better than the stokke tray. We've used it 3 times per day every day and the wear is minimal and barely visible."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QRVH1Q', 'answerTime': 'Jul 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375254000, 'question': 'Do you have to use this with the baby set or can you just use it with the tripp trapp chair?', 'answer': 'U can just use it with the chair. My baby is 18 mo now and just uses it with chair'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QYW8LW', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404802800, 'question': 'Does this product really take 1-2 months to ship as stated? My daughter will almost be done teething by then!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If ordered from Amazon, it will ship immediately. Be careful who you order from. Anything shipping from Hong Kong or China is a knock off and may not be safe for your baby.'}
