{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QYW8LW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': 'How do I used it for my 4 month old? Is it okay for him to chew it like a teether?', 'answer': "Yes, it's totally a teether. It's a rubbery silicone teether. My twin girls love theirs. Feels good to chew on and easy for baby to hold."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QZ64T8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379833200, 'question': 'Can these be used with diaper rash cream (zinc oxide or aquaphor) to keep it off of the cloth diapers?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes and No. If these liners stay in place then they would do an excellent job shielding the cloth diaper from the rash cream. However many times they will move, wrinkle depending on how active your baby is and then it may not offer that kind of protection. I have two recommendations for you - Buy a microfleece cloth by the yard from any hobby store (Joanne, Hobby Lobby etc.) and cut them to the size that suits you best. They work the same way and you won't burn your pocket. Also Grandma El's diaper cream has worked very well for us."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QZ64T8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383552000, 'question': 'What are the dimensions?', 'answer': 'I just measured mine at 4.5" by 10.5", plenty big enough for all my diapers. They are about 6 months old, washed and dried every other day. I have noticed no shrinkage and only minimal pilling. Though they are almost paper thin, they work fabulously at keeping wetness away from the baby\'s skin. I highly recommend these.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QZ64T8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394866800, 'question': 'made from polyester?? I guess the process is fleecing and the material can vary? Does the package say polyester?', 'answer': 'The package insert states: "Fleece Liners-- Made from 100% recycled polyester....made in Canada from Repreve yarn with 100% recycled content." I hope this information is helpful.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QZ64T8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422259200, 'question': "These are two-sided: one side is fuzzy, and the other is smooth. Which side should go towards the baby's skin?", 'answer': 'The fuzzy side goes face up.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002QZ64T8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422172800, 'question': 'Can these be used for cloth pad liners?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "They are really not wide enough to use as liners. I use bumpkins liners that I buy from amazon. I've tried a few different kinds and they are the softest and actually have a little bit of stretch to them. I bought these fleece liners to use under his disposable liners for when using diaper ointment. After buying these I found them to be overpriced for just being thin fleece and there is no sewing or edging to them. I then bought some thin fleece from Walmart and cut several out myself. And could make them the size I wanted. I got a LOT MORE for my money and no sewing! They hold up great as I have washed them at least 50 times by now and they do not fray! Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002QZ64T8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389340800, 'question': 'What is the washing/care instructions? Any recommendations please because there are no details on the packaging.', 'answer': "I washed mine with my diapers in Seventh Generation liquid detergent. It doesn't leave a residue and is sensitive to baby's skin."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002R0DVL6', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399964400, 'question': 'do you have to have the insert for a newborn? It seems to be an add on rather than included', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It is an add on but to put a baby under 3 months old in the carrier you'll need it. Their legs are too small to straddle you. With the insert you tuck their legs up on top of the insert pillow."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002R0DVL6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392364800, 'question': 'My daughter is about 35inches and weighs 19.5 pounds. Would she fit comfortably in one of these?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'd say yes. Our baby is more than 22 lbs and still rides comfortably in the Ergo (don't recall how long he is) - you may find that as your daughter gets heavier, *you* are more comfortable with her on your back instead of in front (and the side-carry option is nice to switch things out, though I never do that for long periods of time). We still use the Ergo in all three holds with our little guy. :)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002R0DVL6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428822000, 'question': 'I\'m 4\'11" will this work with my height?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi A220. You may find the Ergo a little large. There are quite a few adjustment options. The height of the connection between the shoulder straps can be adjusted (up and down the middle upper back). I found that I wished this would actually slide down lower. In terms of strap length - you could definitely tighten all around to suit your smaller frame. FYI I am 5\'7" and around 145lbs. I would still recommend. I have read from other reviews of plenty of women 5\'0" wearing them. Even after a long walk, I can feel tired carrying my little one. I think it\'s just the nature of carriers. Still far less if I had carried her for same distance &#128512;'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002R0DVL6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411023600, 'question': 'Is this authentic?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Authentic Ergo, you mean? Yes. It's an actual Ergo product...."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002R0DVL6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395471600, 'question': 'Is the Ergo Infant Insert included or do you have to buy that separately?', 'answer': 'Must buy it seperately.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002R0DVL6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'My husband is 6 ft tall and 300 lbs. He wears a 3x tall, very muscular build. Does this carrier fit ok on larger people?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The carrier fits a person up to 6ft 5. The waist belt fits up to a 43inch waist. Hope this helps.'}
