{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002S52XHI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385452800, 'question': "This ad doesn't show a size, how do I know it will fit?", 'answer': 'I was a medium size 4/6 125 lbs pre pregnancy, so i ordered a M. It was tight, but as it should be. It was not uncomfortable at all. Felt good. Held together, vs my jiggly self. I had a vaginal delivery, so im unsure how it would work w a c-sec insicion. I recommend this product.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002S52XHI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401606000, 'question': 'Are there sizes? there is no option for me to choose a size on amazon', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'There are sizes, S, M, L, XL. It may help if you visit the Wink website. If you are still pregnant, you may want to wait 2-3 weeks before your due date to order. I went from a size L to a S really quickly too. . . like within 4 weeks.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002S52XHI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394866800, 'question': 'Since this just has the little hooks in the crotch area, how is it with the postpartum bleeding? and wearing pads??', 'answer': "I wore regular cotton briefs (with a pad) so I wouldn't have to wash it as often and to keep everything clean. It worked great. It's really easy to hook/unhook and the extra pressure from the garment helps hold the large pads stay in place instead of wadding up or moving around."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002S52XHI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398582000, 'question': "I am 8 1/2 months pregnant and I've gained a LOT of weight, should I get it for the size I am now or a middle zone between what I used to be?", 'answer': "I gained 45 pounds so I was 165 when I delivered. I bought the medium at first. It didn't fit for the first week or so but then I squeezed into it and within a month or so I bought the small and wore that until it got big. Hope that helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002S52XHI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409122800, 'question': 'How does it work for petite people?', 'answer': "I'm really short waisted, it came up to my bra line - I liked that though because everything was smooth instead of having a line where the undergarment ended and my bra started. I also wore underwear beneath it to reduce the amount of washing needed."}
