{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002SG7JSU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405407600, 'question': 'will this ruin the furniture once we take if off?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "After a couple months, my toddlers ripped these off of my coffee table. What now remains is the adhesive (still very securely stuck to the table) and bits of the foam (still stuck to the adhesive). I've tried to pick at it and it absolutely won't budge. I guess I'll have to try some kind of gunk-remover, but I'm afraid it will damage my table. I wouldn't recommend these for wood furniture."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002SG7JSU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374908400, 'question': "Safety 1st sells foam corner bumper guards, Does your product look like Satey's?", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No. The corner for my product has a intact corner, just softer. Safety first corners are rounded, and do not come to a point.'}
