{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002SNAK6G', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2011', 'unixTime': 1302678000, 'question': 'Reviews state both: Can anyone tell me real answer of whether or not this will work on my dining room table that has a small lip and center post with four floor extended table ends please?', 'answer': 'It will depend on the width of your table lip. We have two of these for our twin girls and really love them. Our table has a 3.5" lip and the chairs fit fine. The curved bar along the bottom adjusts up and down to tighten and loosen the chair. I would say it has about a 4" clearance when it\'s adjusted as far down as possible. If your lip is wider than that it might not fit. As far as pedestal table, I don\'t think it\'s that it would never work on one but it would depend on the sturdiness of the table. I\'d stand at the edge of the table and push down putting a fair amount of weight on it and see if the table seems to tip at all. Typically pedestal tables in restaurants are where it\'s a problem.'}
