{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002T1HH0E', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397631600, 'question': 'What does the 3 in 1 convertible crib mean if the side does not drop?? as compared to the other Jenny Lind cribs? Fixed sided crib?', 'answer': 'This is a fixed side crib, meaning you cannot let the side down to get the baby out. It is stationary. The 3 in 1 refers to the 3 different ways this can be used as a bed: crib (with 3 mattress height settings)/ toddler bed (like a daybed) with no rail/ or toddler bed with rail (must purchase "conversation kit" separately).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002T1HH0E', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379314800, 'question': 'My bed skirt is not fitting the crib correctly because of the metal hardware holding the base - is anyone else having this issue?', 'answer': "Yes, it's very frustrating!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002T1HH0E', 'answerTime': 'Jul 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406358000, 'question': 'Do I need to buy a bumper with this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Consumer Product Safety Commission recommends that no crib have pillows, quilts, comforters, stuffed toys, cushions or bumpers to reduce the risks of sudden infant death syndrome.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002T1HH0E', 'answerTime': 'May 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401174000, 'question': 'What size mattress do you need for this crib?', 'answer': 'Any standard crib mattress will fit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002T1HH0E', 'answerTime': 'May 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401346800, 'question': "Can you remove both long sides of the crib and just have the two ends on? I haven't seen any photos where it is used like that.", 'answer': 'Yes, you could remove both sides but it would be very wobbly because the side pieces are what keeps it stable. I have used it with just one side taken off as a toddler bed and that works great. Basically the metal frame that the mattress sits on has little metal "arms" on each corner that screw into the legs on the short sides of the bed. These arms can pivot where they are connected to the metal frame so there is some give and the side rail is what keeps the bed square and you need at least one of them on for it to be stable.'}
