{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002T1HH1I', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361260800, 'question': 'What is the height at the top of the mattress at the highest setting? Then, how many inches to the top of the crib railing?', 'answer': 'I actually didn\'t use the casters (they\'re ugly!), so that takes a few inches off of the total height (floor to mattress top). But it\'s 18" from the BASE of the setting, where the mattress would rest, to the lowest railing. With a 7" mattress, the top of the mattress to the lowest railing is 11 inches.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002T5Q01C', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395730800, 'question': 'I am learning about cloth diapers. So what do i need for a single cloth diaper? A cloth diaper, an absorbent insert and then these Liner?', 'answer': "This is a big question in a simple question disguise... The simple answer is these liners are really 'poop' catchers. They are a thin layer that lets the pee pass through, but holds the poo so you can drop it in the toilet. Long answer: If you are exclusively breastfeeding you can wash the poop in your machine (breast milk breaks down so easily) Then, when starting solids you'll need one of these because the poo will get firmer. You'll need one on every diaper because you'll never know when baby will poo. As far a cloth diapering goes, we talk about them in terms of covers (leak proof outer layer, also includes pockets diapers), cloth (pre-folds, hemp, soakers, etc) and then liners. You will always need some form of each of these when diapering (unless using all-in-ones and then only add the liner)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002T5Q01C', 'answerTime': 'Sep 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380006000, 'question': 'Would these help with absorbencey/leaks? Instead of having to double-up on the cloth inserts?', 'answer': 'No. They are simply meant to keep diaper a bit more clean from #2. And also it makes it easy to simply pick up the flushable liner from diaper and toss in toilet. It is not meant to absorb in any way, they are really thin! Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002T5Q01C', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380783600, 'question': 'Can you use these inserts with most of the cloth diaper brands?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I use them with Sun Baby, BumGenius, Alva, Kawaii. Pocket diapers are what I mostly use, and the liners work with all of those.'}
