{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TLRDRQ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2010', 'unixTime': 1265184000, 'question': "Expired 2002 Britax Roundabout: I feel like if anything was to ever happen to our child in a crash, I couldnt live with myself for using the old seat, but is it really as dangerous as my first time mother's imagination is making it seem?", 'answer': 'The other answer is 100% correct! The plastic becomes brittle over time, meaning it will break much easier in an accident. This is especially true because carseats are in extremly hot and cold conditions in the car. A carseat specialist told us that carseats in drier climates should expire after only 4 years. Hope this helps!'}
