{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002TNBIEI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382425200, 'question': 'Does anyone have experience with using this as a travel pool for a 1 year old? We are going on a cruise and want our lo to be able to use it poolside.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We love it, but it's really a little tub that fits into a regular sized tub, not so much a baby pool. That might be perfect for what you want for traveling, but wanted to make sure you knew it was relatively small. Not a bad idea, though to use it the way you are planning. It is pretty well made and sturdy for an inflatable tub, though there is no real cushion on the bottom (you may not need that anyway)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002TUTP0A', 'answerTime': 'Oct 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380610800, 'question': 'is this okay for a 10 month old baby', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No. It is too small and a bit shaky. I highly recommend a Phil & Teds travel crib. A bit more expensive but I was able to use the Phil & teds until my baby was 3. Years old. Got my money's worth out of it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TUTP0A', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381129200, 'question': 'Do this come with a fitted sheet? If not where can I purchase them?', 'answer': "No, I don't think mine did. I just bought the sheets from Babies 'R Us. They sell them separately there. You don't have to buy Graco brand. I'm pretty sure I bought mine from their line (BRU), Koala Baby. Just make sure it's for the smaller-sized pack 'n play/bassinet."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002TUTP0A', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370761200, 'question': 'Can the bassinet bumper be removed? Bumpers are a suffocation risk.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The bumper in the top bassinet portion cannot be removed as far as I know. But keep this in mind.. The baby cannot roll over until s/he is 3 months old.. And.. You if you look a bit closer you will see there is a mesh area where the babies head will be.. I used this product for our daughter (now 3yrs old) and I highly recommend it. Another perk is its on wheels and can be easily moved from room to room.. Good luck! Enjoy your precious bundle. :)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TUTP0A', 'answerTime': 'Jun 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370070000, 'question': "How big of a baby would be comfortable sleeping in this? We're looking for a bed for the RV but don't want our baby to grow out of it too fast.", 'answer': 'Girl = up to 5 months. Boy = 3 or 4 months.'}
