{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TUTPQO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383724800, 'question': "I noticed on some play yards that the mat doesn't snap in to stay in place. How does this mat stay in place? Thanks for the info.", 'answer': 'This mat has snaps on a fabric tag that is part of the mat. The tags (as I call them) go through the side of the base in four locations. You snap the tags under the base. It is a little difficult to do but with some pushing and pulling I was able to snap all four snaps. I had a 2 year old and 1 yr old in there and the mat stayed in place and did not unsnap. They loved playing in it. I hope this helps'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TUTPQO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386057600, 'question': 'Is it suitable for crawlers...or would I need something larger?', 'answer': "Definitely! I bought this one since I am watching my nephew, but had one almost identical for my daughter. My daughter was rolling over at 7 days old, so I had to find something with soft sides since she kept hitting the wood railing on her crib and waking up all night long. She ended up sleeping in it until she was 2 yrs. old. When she started to try to climb out of it I stopped using it obviously. I never thought I would use it as long as I did but she loved it and we ended up taking her crib down. Unusual use I know, but it shows it's definitely safe for a crawler!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TUTPQO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358236800, 'question': "What is the weight limit/capacity.Age isn't really helping.Not all children weigh the same at same age.", 'answer': "It is recommended for use up to 30lbs. At 22 lbs and 11 months, it is really sturdy for my baby and she is pulling up on it too. I only use it for a few minutes at a time when I'm cooking dinner, etc. and I think we still will probably use it for this purpose for the next year or so."}
