{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002TUTQMM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422345600, 'question': 'Can you use on a padded chair?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, we are using on dining room chairs ... Some are upholstered and some are wooden with pads. I do recommend you putting down a towel or cloth to protect the chair from food spills. Our grandson is 21 mo old so we do not buckle it to the chair when someone is nearby. Was perfect for our needs.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002TUTQMM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409641200, 'question': 'Can this be used with an upholstered seat cushion', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Ours is used on a 1950s dinette chair with the vinyl cushioned seat. It can be used on an upholstered seat but I would not recommend it unless your seat cushion already need to be redone. The booster compresses the foam and flattens it over time. If you remove it between uses you should be fine but who really does this multiple times a day with a toddler in the house?! I hope this helps. If not let me know how I can better help you.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TUTQMM', 'answerTime': 'Aug 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408345200, 'question': "The description says it can't be used on a padded chair. Our kitchen chairs have light padding built in - why wouldn't this seat work?", 'answer': "Heather, I think the description refers to the tie-on type seat cushions, which would cause this booster to slip; but if the cushion is built into your seat this booster should work just fine. It has an adjustable strap for around the chair as well as one for under the chair. It's straps down very tight. I would highly recommend this booster seat."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002TZA536', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373439600, 'question': 'Are there any universal stroller frames that this seat "snaps" into (i.e. more than just being held on by the strap on the stroller)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We purchased the Safety 1st stroller made for the car seat. Snap in and out, very easy. Therefore we never shopped for anything else. This was 1 1/2 ago, so not sure if there is a universal stroller.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TZA536', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383724800, 'question': 'How much does the seat weight with out the base?', 'answer': "don't know about the actual numbers. I was surprised, however, how light it was as compared to what I had anticipated given its size and all. And given that I am small woman probably it really is."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002TZA536', 'answerTime': 'Oct 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381734000, 'question': 'Can the shade rotate from back to front?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Not sure what you mean by rotating it. But it is movable - you can "fold it" so the seat is open so to say, or "extend it" all the way to the front, up to the handle (I found the shade to be quite generous). Hope it helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TZA536', 'answerTime': 'Sep 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379660400, 'question': "I can't find this answer anywhere. What double strollers will be compatible with this carseat?", 'answer': "We just went through this. I hated all the safety 1st strollers that this seat latches into. We used the clic system and the stroller still annoys me to no end. We ended up with the Chicco cortina together double stroller after spending a few hours at babies r us going through all the double strollers with our car seat. We found that if you recline the back seat a click or two that this car seat will fit snuggly rear facing inside. It won't click into place despite the similar attachment system it uses with its bases but it definitely won't pop out. It works nicely with the strollers sun shade and the seats sun shade, makes a great little cocoon. The only con is that the front seat had to site upright and cannot recline with the seat in back. I love the stiller in itself too. The back fully reclines to a bassinet and it handles very well with a kid in front and the seat in back. I highly recommend it"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TZA536', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1369724400, 'question': 'What jogging strollers can this car seat be used with?', 'answer': "it's being a while but from when I looked at this car seat (and bought one) it could only fit Safety 1st stroller specifically made for this car seat. The car seat fits larger children and has a lot more leg-room than a typical car seat, still is very light and provides great protection but you do pay the price price-- it's not compatible with typical stroller..."}
