{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002U0AD3C', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358582400, 'question': "Is Ergobaby and ERGObaby the same company, and what's the difference between teething pads and sucking pads?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not sure about the company name, but regarding the second half of your question, there isn't much difference between a teething pad and a sucking pad. Their purpose is to soak up the drool from your teething baby so that you don't have to wash the carrier every time you use it--you just wash the pads. Here's what happens--you put your baby into the carrier and he or she immediately starts sucking on the shoulder straps. Within ten minutes, both straps are soaked through. This prevents that from happening. You should get them if you get the carrier--get two sets. Keep in mind that you probably won't need to pull them out until your baby is around 4 months old. Then you'll use them until he or she is at least 20 months, I would think."}
