{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002UN4G0U', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374303600, 'question': 'what is the child weight limit?', 'answer': 'This carrier is for DOLLS, not for living babies. It fits 15-18 inch dolls only and although it is designed very similarly to the mommy size one for a real baby it is not authorized or safe for living babies, it is only designed for toys. As for the weight limit of the child WEARING the doll carrier, we have one and my daughter began using at at her 3rd birthday and still wears her dolls in this carrier and has just turned 6. If waist measurement is an issue, I would say that it is pretty expandable and that given its straps and buckles a pretty hefty child could still wear this to carry their doll. The Ergo Baby carriers for baby that a mom would wear usually cost $100 or more. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002UN4G0U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415001600, 'question': 'Will this securely carry an AG bitty baby or AG girl?', 'answer': 'It should. My daughter has an Our Generation doll (Target brand 18" doll) that she mostly carries in it. Fits her smaller dolls as well. It really is like the adult Ergo if you have one. The only difference is that there is an extra fabric on the inside that you can put the doll in so that when your child takes the carrier off, the doll does not fall out. I actually really like that feature. It is not quite as comfortable with the harder dolls, but with a little adjustment, my daughter doesn\'t mind and she is VERY picky about how things feel and I don\'t think this would be any different with a different carrier.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UN4G0U', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': 'Does the Galaxy Gray (darker gray) have a chest strap?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
