{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UP391K', 'answerTime': 'Oct 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381906800, 'question': 'Can this seat be used in vehicles that only have lap belts?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'Are you talking about a sports car with no latch system? A 70\'s classic car? Either way, no. You MUST have a latch and be able to tie over the seat back because this chair is a SOFT back. It collapses without your car\'s seat back to hold it in place...and also for the latch belt to go over and tether safely. That is key!! I think the pictures online give the impression that it sits upright without being installed like a "typical" seat and it does NOT. Hope that helps you!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UP391K', 'answerTime': 'Oct 24, 2012', 'unixTime': 1351062000, 'question': 'Is the base width really 17 inches? Trying to fit 3 across in a 52 inch space, so each seat needs to be 17.25 inches or smaller.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Just measured mine. The widest part is actually the arms. If you squish the padding on the arms I got 16 3/4". The seat part is closer to 14" but you need to have the car seat belt buckle come up between them so you can get the belt buckled. Also check where your top latches are located. You will need 3 of them, roughly centered for each seat.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002UP391K', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379314800, 'question': 'comfort', 'answer': 'My Daughter says it\'s very comfortable. It\'s so comfortable she wants to sleep on it. She\'s 6 years old. 3\'9" height , 39lbs weight. Fits her great.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UP391K', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2012', 'unixTime': 1355817600, 'question': 'Can a cup holder be attached to this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I haven't tried it and don't know how it would be possible. Unless you could slide something underneath the seat (so the weight of the child and seat would hold it in place), I don't know how it would work."}
