{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002UP1WS2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372057200, 'question': 'Are children able to buckle/unbuckle the harness themselves?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'They can do it as well as any other car seat (the unbuckling is easier for the 6 year old than the 3 year olds, since his hands are bigger and more coordinated). We have 4 car seats, 2 of which are the safety first, and the kids are able to buckle/unbuckle themselves about equally in either (we have a rule that each kid gets in the car and does their buckles, but only a grown-up is allowed to un-do them).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002USE0Q0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397026800, 'question': "What's the size of these blanket?", 'answer': 'They are 44"x44" I think. The square shape is great. They are thinner than the boutique ones (which are 47" square I believe). They do get just as soft and my son, nephew, and niece are addicted to them - as are some others I know. It is slightly transparent so he can put it over his head like a ghost and isn\'t as apt to run into things. And when they mash the blanket over their face when sleeping it is comforting to know they won\'t suffocate - this is true of the boutique ones as well.'}
