{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002V92XAS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380265200, 'question': 'Does it work with Depends?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Sallie, yes roll them up into a ball and drop them in. I wear XL and can get 14 diapers into one bag so I know when I finish a bag of diapers it is also time to change my bag in the pal. I know they say they can hold up to 25 diapers which I am sure they can depending on the size of the diapers. They are based on children sized diapers I'm sure. But by rolling the depends into a tight ball you can get a full pack inside. I have IC/Incontenence so I go through a diaper bag in 2 days-3 days, on bad days sometimes 1 bag a day. I love the locking/sealing/odor fighting mechanism that this diaper pal has so it does lock in the odor. On a good week I did go 4 days without having any smelly odors in restroom. I love it. I replaced it with another brand and will stick to this one again if I ever have to replace the pal again. I just reordered the 30 count bags as I am so pleased with them. They are also easy to take along with you in your travel diaper bag and no on knows you have been carrying diapers around with you if you have accidents where you can't leave diapers (like restaurants). I just go home and place the bag in the pal and use that as my next bag and sit it in the bottom of th4 pal until I'm ready to lock into the 4 slots. My own tip of the day making incontinence easier to live with."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002V92XAS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404457200, 'question': 'How do you refill the baking soda in the cartridge or is there a replacement for the cartridge?', 'answer': 'You can twist it off and just refill it with baking powder and snap it back on.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002V92XAS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380265200, 'question': "Has any1else had problem of pail making loud noise every time u close lid?Sounds like it's breaking,but it isn't.Very odd.Appreciate any&amp;all feedback!", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "`Michele, that loud sound is the diaper pal twisting the bag/vacuum sealing the diaper into the bag as well as turning the odor eating cartridge. Both of these dual actions help to seal in the odor until you open the pal again. When you open the lid it releases the pressure around the bag so another diaper can go into it. I think this was an ingenious way to seal in the smell so it traps it inside of the pal. The odor eater isn't strong enough without this recirculation. By doing both those poopy smells are locked in. I am using it for myself being an adult so my bag goes out every 2 days to 3 days. I love the pal and know from the use of other systems this is the best one because loud sound means the pal is sealing in and masking the odors. Most importantly, for me, it also means the air quality is more sanitary by not breathing in the odors. That is why we don't throw them into the trash can to begin with? Please, be assured that this is a good sound."}
