{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002VA2UFA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': "I'm looking for a diaper system that would be good for traveling or summer camping. Would this system work?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I would definitely go with flats. At least two dozen. Look up "origami fold" on YouTube. I use the same diapers with the origami fold for my five month old and my three year old who is still not potty trained. Close them with a Snappi and cover them with Dappi brand nylon cover. The nylon covers are easy to hand wash, and dry incredibly quickly. I\'ve had to rinse one off at a rest stop, and lay it out in the trunk to dry, and it was dry the next time we stopped on the road (usually in about 1-2 hours).'}
