{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002VLW9XM', 'answerTime': 'Jul 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405062000, 'question': "We don't have a dryer. How important is it to dry these diapers in the dryer to fluff them up in the beginning?", 'answer': "It's not. You can boil them first, and then put them onto the line/rack to dry. They will dry quickly, too. Just as a reminder, if you rinse with a bit of vinegar, the diaper will be less stiff when dried because it helps get the soap out."}
