{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002VLW9XM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424764800, 'question': 'Hi, I am new to using Flats. How do I prep the flats for the first time? And how do I wash and dry them subsequently?', 'answer': 'The unbleached kind need to either get boiled for a bit, like 15-20 minutes or you can wash them in hot water a few cycles, though this uses a lot more water and is not as efficient as boiling. You wash then, same as any other cotton diaper: cold rinse, hot wash with plain soap, then two rinses. I typically do the last rinse on cold just to save energy. Flats dry on the line in no time and the sun bleaches stains and kills germs.'}
