{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002VLW9XM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417680000, 'question': 'Do these have serged edges or folded over seams?', 'answer': "Our's are folded over seams where cut from the bolt, and then a selvaged edge - not sergered - on the side of the fabric. This means that it is the edge of the woven fabric where cutting and sewing isn't required due to the weave."}
