{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2G9S', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400137200, 'question': 'At what height would you say a child is too tall for this stroller. I have a 4yr old that\'s about 40" tall? Do you think he\'d be comfortable?', 'answer': 'I dont think so. There is a 50 lbs weight limit but nothing that mentions height. I would think at 40" tall, your 4 year olds legs wouldnt be comfortable and it would be possible their little feet might drag on the ground. My son is less than 30" tall and his feet already touch the plastic foot rest.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2G9S', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410850800, 'question': 'How do you clean the fabric?', 'answer': "We usually use Clorox or Lysol wipes to clean the fabric and plastic/rubber parts, or baby wipes if we're out when LO makes a mess. I wouldn't use bleach solution since it would probably bleach the fabric."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WB2G9S', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408690800, 'question': 'can a 4 month baby use this stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I wouldn't recommend this stroller for a baby that can't sit up on its own. It's a very very light stroller, in terms of support. It doesn't have big incline/recline options and the baby's head may tip forward. But it's up to your own discretion, depending on the baby's development."}
