{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2GAM', 'answerTime': 'Aug 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376031600, 'question': 'What is the minimum age/ or minimum weight of an infant for this stroller?', 'answer': 'I put my granddaughter in it who is 25 inches long, 4 months old and 13 pounds. She slumps to one side. I would think it works better for a 6 month old who has more neck control. It does not lie flat so baby will always be upright or semi-upright. After using it for two weeks, she has already gained more control and a rolled blanket is keeping her more upright. She has no trouble falling asleep in it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2GAM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388995200, 'question': 'Could it fit a 3 year old child? or is it basically for smaller kids? (she does not exceed the weight limit)', 'answer': "It's too hard to determine. Depends on the build of your child. Eg a person 6' tall weighing 180 lbs is slender whereas a person 5' tall weighing 180 is obese. Our 2 yr old granddaughter is petite so she'll fit into it for a long time. If your child is on the chunky side, it's not going to fit as long."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2GAM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2012', 'unixTime': 1348729200, 'question': 'What is the best rain cover for the Ignite Stroller? One question: what is a good rain cover to buy for this stroller?', 'answer': "found this review for the Comfy Baby Deluxe Weatherproof Rain Cover with Retractable Sun Shade and Large Easy-Access Window 5.0 out of 5 stars Perfect Fit for my First Years Ignite Stroller!, May 7, 2010 By Candy Coated - See all my reviews Amazon Verified Purchase(What's this?) This review is from: Comfy Baby Deluxe Weatherproof Rain Cover with Retractable Sun Shade and Large Easy-Access Window (Baby Product) It is a perfect fit for my new The First Years Ignite Stroller! The picture of the item here on Amazon does not do justice to the product. The plastic portion in front which opens up via a zipper is very clear, thick and stiff. The zipper area opens quite large so you can tend to your child without removing the entire cover. There are ventilation holes on both side of the cover. The sun shade is another great thing this product offers that other similar stroller covers don't provide. Also, it's nicely folded in a way that it fits flat at the bottom of my stroller basket. It stays there and I pull it out when I need it. This is a great purchase!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2GAM', 'answerTime': 'Apr 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364886000, 'question': 'What are the dimensions when folded? Wondering if it can fit in a large suitcase?', 'answer': 'About 43" long, 8-1/2" high and 8-1/4 wide when folded and lying on floor. I think it would have to be a very large suitcase.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WB2GAM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380524400, 'question': 'Does this stroller recline far enough for comfortable sleeping for a 27 lb two yr old?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It does lean pretty far back. Without an actual measurement I would say 120 degrees or more. My baby girl sleeps well in this stroller.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2GAM', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397545200, 'question': 'Is this light enough for me to carry on and off a bus or subway? For NYC travel. Thanks!', 'answer': 'Absolutely. This stroller does not weigh much. It can easily be picked up with one hand, preferably folded. I will say, though, that it is not exactly a one-hand-close type of stroller.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2G98', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403766000, 'question': 'Does the fabric of the seat breathe well? Will this be too hot to use outdoors in a humid summer?', 'answer': 'honestly, ive never thought about the breathability if the fabric, but we use it all the time in the heat and my kid never turns into a total sweatbag. hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2G98', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400137200, 'question': 'At what height would you say a child is too tall for this stroller. I have a 4yr old that\'s about 40" tall? Do you think he\'d be comfortable?', 'answer': 'I dont think so. There is a 50 lbs weight limit but nothing that mentions height. I would think at 40" tall, your 4 year olds legs wouldnt be comfortable and it would be possible their little feet might drag on the ground. My son is less than 30" tall and his feet already touch the plastic foot rest.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WB2G98', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410850800, 'question': 'How do you clean the fabric?', 'answer': "We usually use Clorox or Lysol wipes to clean the fabric and plastic/rubber parts, or baby wipes if we're out when LO makes a mess. I wouldn't use bleach solution since it would probably bleach the fabric."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WB2G98', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408690800, 'question': 'can a 4 month baby use this stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I wouldn't recommend this stroller for a baby that can't sit up on its own. It's a very very light stroller, in terms of support. It doesn't have big incline/recline options and the baby's head may tip forward. But it's up to your own discretion, depending on the baby's development."}
