{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WDAW5Q', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388995200, 'question': 'does it have flame rerdardant', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I cut the tags off of mine so can't go off that. I looked on their website and it had this which mentions the infant support pillow however at bottom it says all boppy products meet some standards. This lounger is not to be used for sleep so might not have what you are lookin for. From Boppy Website: We take great care in the quality of our products. The fabric and filling in the Boppy Feeding and Infant Support pillow (and slipcovers for those pillows) meet all flammability standards without the addition of flame retardant chemicals. All bedding items containing filling material must meet certain flammability standards to be sold in the U.S. The State of California has the strictest standards and so all Boppy pillows are manufactured to meet the flammability requirements of the California Bureau of Home Furnishings."}
