{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WDAW5Q', 'answerTime': 'Mar 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394434800, 'question': 'I have a couple questions--first, can you use this for tummy time for baby? And second, what is the earliest baby can sit in the pillow? Thank you!', 'answer': 'We used it as soon as we got home from the hospital and are still using it 3 mo later. Although not as often. And yes you can use for tummy time, but we just prefer the floor. This has become my go to baby gift!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WDAW5Q', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419840000, 'question': 'How does this compare to the regular Boppy? Pros and Cons of both? Is baby supported enough in this to be able to take a bottle while sitting in it?', 'answer': "I use both, for different purposes. The regular boppy is great for feeding, but I wouldn't lay the baby on it because they slip down and aren't supported right. With the lounger, their butt lays in the crook and their feet and heads are supported in a comfy position (esp. if your baby has any spit up/acid reflux issues!). I think it's about a 30 angle so it could take a bottle, but if your baby can hold their own bottles, they might be too big for the lounger! The regular boppy is great for helping YOU hold your baby comfortably, whereas the the lounger is great at holding your baby comfortably FOR you! I hope this helps. Ask any follow up questions if needed!"}
