{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WGI5SE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403161200, 'question': 'Can anyone compare to the LifeFactory glass bottles? Advantages/Disadvantages of each?', 'answer': "We bought one of both to try and ended up settling on buying more of the Pura Kikki. While not an exhaustive review my quick summary would be (noting that our preference ended up being Pura Kiki): Pura Kiki: +Lighter than LifeFactory (important for if/when the baby is holding or when you are travelling) +More robust then LifeFactory (important for if/when baby starts throwing/dropping the bottles and travelling) +Can use the nipples/tops interchangeably on the small Pura Kiki and the large Pura Kiki bottles. +Can convert to sippy cup and also food container (for example we keep Gerber Puffs in one of our PK's when travelling) +Can fit other brand's nipples e.g. we ended up using MAM nipples -Cannot sanitize in the Microwave -When using the flat cap tops to mix formula we have sometimes (and only sometimes) noticed a slight leakage from where the flat silicone top didn't properly seal. -Not quite as easy to see how much water/liquid is in the Pura Kiki. Need to have a reasonable light source and look in through the top at the interior markings. Usually not an issue, however if your kitchen doesn't have good ambient light then means you need to switch on the lights etc. Or if travelling etc. LifeFactory: +As it is glass it is easier to sanitize when travelling or at home by using the Microwave +Easy to see how much liquid is in the bottle -Heavier As for price, it varies and depends on the full lifetime of the bottle. We bought Pura Kiki and would do so again if we went back in time."}
