{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WLGV08', 'answerTime': 'Dec 19, 2012', 'unixTime': 1355904000, 'question': "what's the difference between the snuza go and the snuza halo?", 'answer': "The snuza halo will vibrate after 15 seconds have passed without movement/breathing and will alarm at 20 seconds. The snuza go only alarms, no vibration. I would prefer to be alarmed anytime there is no movement/breathing for any length of time, that's why we have the snuza go :). Also, the lower price was greatly appreciated!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WLGV08', 'answerTime': 'Aug 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377846000, 'question': 'Do you clip this to the diaper and then snap their onesie over it? That seems like it might be bulky.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, you clip it to the diaper. I don't put my Baby in a onesie to sleep, just a gown or zip up sleeper, so it's not bad. Even when he was a newborn and swaddled though it was fine. The only problem is when they get to be a few months old and move around more it can come off and the alarm will go off. That's just starting to happen at our house. If you have too many layers over I when that happens it could be a bit bothersome. I still think it would be worth it though."}
