{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WLGV08', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395903600, 'question': 'Could this be used with a belly sleeper? My son must sleep on his stomach because of a medical condition', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "As long as they have on an elastic waistband or onesie, I don't think it's a problem. My daughter is 1-1/2 now and still wears it at night. As long as you put the diaper on tight enough, it stays put. I rarely took hers off during the first year...and she was walking at 9 months and super active. I've even heard some people that have put it on the side or back of the diaper."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WLGV08', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428303600, 'question': "It lists this product, the Snuza Go! as discontinued by manufacturer, however I don't see any information confirming that on the manufacturer's site.", 'answer': 'As far as I know there are 3 versions of this product. The model in this listing which is older and uses a difficult to find battery. I ordered recently from this listing and received that model with the hard to find battery. The Levana Oma which is a newer version but is also being discontinued according to the manufacturer. And finally the latest version also by Snuza that uses a more common battery easier to replace.'}
