{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WLGV08', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393920000, 'question': 'Up to what age is this product recommended? first 6months, first year?', 'answer': "I used it for my middle son (wasn't around when my oldest was a baby) until he was a year and a half old. SIDS risk tends to decrease at 6 months of age. And significantly decreases at one year. So you can stop using it anytime you really want and feel comfortable with. My son had sleep apnea so I used it longer than most."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WLGV08', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383462000, 'question': 'Can I adjust the volume?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Not that I know of. It was loud enough for me to hear over the monitor with no problem.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WN20GK', 'answerTime': 'Sep 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379228400, 'question': 'Did anyone else have problems re-snapping the cover after installing this seat rear-facing? The rebound bar prevents you from accessing the snaps...', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, until I realized you don't have to unsnap the cover to install it :) You can work the belt (or LATCH) through where it needs to go without unsnapping the cover. There are slits in the cover near where the belt path is. Hope that helps :)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WN20GK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393574400, 'question': 'Can this seat be used for an infant, Im due to give birth and im wondering if I can bring her home from the hospital in this carseat or will it be too big and I will have to start out with an infan carrier?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "My baby was born at 10lb 8oz, quite a bit bigger than a typical newborn, and was a homebirth - we didn't take him anywhere for 2 weeks. When I put him in his seat for the first time, I was *really* uncomfortable with how far apart the shoulder straps are. They slip off his shoulders unless I have the chest clip higher than typically suggested - basically as far up as I can go. This is despite the infant insert padding. I've never been a fan of needing a separate car seat for a newborn, but honestly I'm not sure this seat is the best choice because of the width between the shoulder straps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WN20GK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381993200, 'question': 'Will it fit properly it an A4?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I must admit, the seat is quite big. My car is a nissan tiida and it takes up almost 1/2 of the back seat. The front passenger seat 'chucks' the baby seat in place so the passenger seat cannot move once the carseat is set. Yes it will fit, but u have to compromise on availabilty of space in ur car for the baby's safety."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WN20GK', 'answerTime': 'Aug 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377241200, 'question': 'Anyone who has purchased the two tone gray and black seat please tell me if it is as light gray as the product picture? The customer picture is significantly darker, not sure which is more accurate', 'answer': "It is actually a very dark charcoal gray with a small white pinstriping. Quite good looking. The seat is wide and well cushioned. My daughter's only complaint was that her toddler son did not sit up as straight in it as in his other car seat."}
