{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WN20GA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389340800, 'question': 'Descriptions states this is "Forward facing". Is it also for rear facing? Maybe I missed this somewhere, but I want to confirm. :)', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Absolutely rear facing and so comfortable for it. We used RF until 3. My 5 yo is still in his and comfortable.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WN20GA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'is this a good carseat for flying with?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "i've never flown with it, but it is pretty heavy to carry around an airport. its easy to install with a belt, so that wouldn't be an issue, but the weight would be too much for me."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002WN20GA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388649600, 'question': 'Will this seat install in my 1997 Astro Van? It is not set up for the latch system, I will on only have the shoulder/lap belt to use.?', 'answer': "I am not particularly familiar with the van, but I can tell you it works great with the shoulder/lap belt. That's what I use in our van, even though it is latch system-capable, because that is what I am the most comfortable installing. Works great."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002WN20GA', 'answerTime': 'Oct 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383116400, 'question': 'I am having a difficult time tightening the harness each time since that rebound bar is in the way. Does anyone else have this problem?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "With the convertible seat, I didn't find it necessary to loosen the straps every time I took the baby out. Try getting the babe out without loosening it and see of you really need to loosen them every time which will make it easier in the long run."}
