{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002ZSP72G', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Are the wheels a nice rubber or cheap plastic? What is the weight limit? Also do you end up kicking it a lot?', 'answer': "The board and wheels are very high quality. It was one of the best investments we made and avoided having to buy double stroller and double jogger. The board latched up and out of the way when you don't have a child standing on it (so you can leave it attached all the time). I can't remember the weight limit listed on the description but remember that we used it past the top number. I have very long legs and remember being mindful of the board but didn't kick it much. If you have a stroller with extendable arms that would be great but probably not necessary."}
