{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00318CLTQ', 'answerTime': 'Jul 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406185200, 'question': 'Why would someone get this one over their metal cup?', 'answer': 'I have both kinds of cups and I have found that the plastic base which is glued onto the metal cup comes off alot. Although Foogo is really good about warranties (every time this has happened, I send it back to them and they send me a brand new one, no charge), its really annoying because it causes the liquid to leak. Also, the metal cups are much heavier than the plastic (if you plan to carry in your purse/diaper bag, etc)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00318CLTG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388044800, 'question': 'Does this have a valve? How hard is it to suck vis-a-vis other straw cups like nuby?', 'answer': "There is a soft rubbery valve insert that goes into the inside of the lid and the straw is inserted into it. It is fairly easy to clean, and the kids have no problem drinking from it. The straw is very hard plastic and is therefore not collapsible, and it is cut at an angle to allow it to rest flush with the bottom of the cup and access the entire contents. We love these cups- just make sure they aren't shaken if the lid isn't closed as they will sprinkle liquid all around if so."}
