{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00318CMBS', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372143600, 'question': "What's the advantage of a bassinet vs the car seat for one w/an infant and a toddler? Seems like car seat would function longer for the infant? Thoughts?", 'answer': "I have twin daughters and we purchase every option with this stroller. If I could go back I probably would not have purchased the bassinets. Most of the time we used the car seats and when we did use the bassinets it was very warm for the girls, a breeze can not get to them. I stopped using the bassinets at 3 months. I will say I did appreciate having them when I was in a very crowded place, people didn't ask to see or touch my babies. I also noticed they would sleep longer with bassinet, maybe comfort, less noise and darkness. You also can not swap between stroller seat and bassinet very easy. The bassinet uses the stroller seat frame, it is a 10 minute process to change them out. I hope this helps."}
