{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0031ARQLC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428994800, 'question': 'Does anyone know if the wood is FSC certified or what the finishes are made of?', 'answer': "Thank you for your inquiry. The wood is New Zealand Pine. The wood stain is a water based stain, that has no VOC's (Volatile Organic Compounds). Also, the FSC Wood is the Forest Stewardship Council. It pertains to wood that is endangered. As an example of an endangered wood would be Mahogany. All woods that are used in all Orbelle Products, are wood that has been grown for furniture, or other complaint products. If you have any additional questions, please do not hesitate to let us know."}
