{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0031E1GEG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422950400, 'question': 'Would this be good for a 7 month old learning to use a cup?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It wasn't for my kid. I had much more success with The First Years Take & Toss straw sippy cups. Since they're made of a a plastic that you can squeeze, you can squeeze the liquid up to the top of the straw so that my kids could get the idea of the straw. Then you squeeze a little bit less each time so they have to suck a little more. Both of my kids were drinking through a straw within 24 hours using this method."}
