{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0031E1GEG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393488000, 'question': 'Is it microwave safe?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't put any plastic in the microwave for my daughter so I have not put the cup in there. The cup may be microwave safe but definitely NOT the lid with the straw. The straw bottom is plastic covered steel. Here is what I found on their website: Can you place hot liquids, carbonated beverages or juices with pulp inside the BOT cup? Hot liquids, carbonated beverages, and juices with pulp are NOT recommended You can place lukewarm beverages inside the cup, but anything warm will create a pressure so be prepared that there might be some liquid that will flow up through the straw. Zo-Li also said they don't recommend heating any plastics in the microwave."}
