{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0033RIE28', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': 'Can the swing be used for newborns?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I think a newborn would be fine in this swing as long as you put the swing speed on low. The weight in the swing is what determines how fast the swing will go on any set speed. Being a lighter weight baby with a newborn thus it will go much slower. It's such a great size as you're not always tripping over the legs or base and is very portable to move from room to room. It can even be set on a table, counter or coffee table as long as they are stable and with adult supervision. If you have pets and you don't want the baby down on the floor by them you have the option of moving this swing up on something as long as you don't leave them unsupervised. I bought this swing for my now 3-1/2 month old grandson and have used it before that. I don't advise using it as a bed for a baby, but they certainly can take a nap in it as long as you are there. It's universal for either a boy or a girl and a great little swing with the Fisher-Price name behind it."}
