{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0035ER8JE', 'answerTime': 'Jul 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405234800, 'question': 'What size mattress does this take? Is it a mini crib?', 'answer': 'Yes, this portable (folding) crib is smaller than standard size. Ours has been perfect for our two new grand babies, but once they are over 1 1/2 years it may be too small for either of them. The crib has caster wheels that can lock in place, or wheel freely. The crib was easy to put together, came with a very thin pad for a mattress, so we ordered another mattress offered with the crib. The mattress board is adjustable in a high or low position. I measured the inside of the crib to be 38" long x 24" wide. The internet offers pads and fitted sheets in this size as well.'}
