{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0035ER8K8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424851200, 'question': 'My baby hates the PNP mattress for sleeping overnight. Is this easy to fold and put in the back of an SUV for trip? Or is it too bulky w/the mattress?', 'answer': 'The crib is easy to fold up, but only the crib sides fold in for storage (i.e. it gets thinner not shorter). In other words, the length of the crib stays the same, the legs do not fold. It is nothing like a pack in play that folds into a small rectangle. That being said, if you had a really big SUV this could potentially fit in the back (you may have to fold down the seats). The mattress that comes with this crib is very thin and comparable to a pack and play mattress. However, I purchased a thicker pad/mattress and my daughter seemed to like it fine. I would think that purchasing a thicker pad that would fit into your pack and play may be the best idea if you are looking to travel a lot. Hope this helps!'}
