{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0035ER8K8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405234800, 'question': 'What size mattress does this take? Is it a mini crib?', 'answer': 'Yes, this portable (folding) crib is smaller than standard size. Ours has been perfect for our two new grand babies, but once they are over 1 1/2 years it may be too small for either of them. The crib has caster wheels that can lock in place, or wheel freely. The crib was easy to put together, came with a very thin pad for a mattress, so we ordered another mattress offered with the crib. The mattress board is adjustable in a high or low position. I measured the inside of the crib to be 38" long x 24" wide. The internet offers pads and fitted sheets in this size as well.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0035ER8GC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379919600, 'question': "What are the 2 mattress position heights? I'm trying to match the height close to the height of my bed to use the crib as an attached side sleeper.", 'answer': 'My crib has 3 possible heights for the mattress. The mattress support sits at approximately 14", 19" or 24" from the ground with wheels on 13", 18" or 23" without the wheels. These measurements do not include the thickness of the mattress. It is difficult to measure because the bracket that supports the mattress brings the mattress about 3" lower than the holes that it screws in to. I hope this helps. From the bottom of the leg (no wheel) to the bottom border is 12"'}
