{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0035LLG2W', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388044800, 'question': 'How long does it take to warm up 4 oz of milk?', 'answer': 'Are you heating formula or breastmilk? Also, depends on if it is cold or not. For breastmilk out of the fridge I have my warmer set at 3:25, it comes out perfect every time. I think with formula you will have to warm it longer, but not sure. You would have to play around with it. To make sure it heats consistently every time, make sure you clean it every few weeks and your warmer will work great. Also, there is a list on the back of the warmer for a guide on how long milk/food take to heat.'}
