{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0035RQF54', 'answerTime': 'Sep 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410159600, 'question': 'would this work on a condo. we are fixing to sign a 1 year lease and I need to know if this would work, we cant do any modifications and our 3 year old grandson gets around any childproof locks.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This will definitely work! You attach to the door by pressure, not screws or anything permanent. It has a clamp at the end with what appears to be silicone (very good anyway) padding to protect the door surface, and it comes with a little allen wrench that is used to tighten the clamp. We removed them when we moved out of our house and you never would have known anything was ever there. That's why even though they're a bit pricey I like them."}
