{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0035RQF54', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422259200, 'question': 'I have double front doors (only one is used regularly) - will this device: a) work on double doors? b) be strong enough for 8 year old "runner"?', 'answer': 'This device can be defeated by a 18 month old. That was my experience. It might work if the fit is perfect - whatever that is. But a good stiff pull will open my basement door secured with this. I think it is time for simple solution of a cord tied to eyelets on the door and frame with a simple shoe bow knot that can be untied from either side with a simple pull with the door opened an inch or two.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0035RQF54', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418025600, 'question': 'Will this work on a front door that opens outward?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It should work fine. It's all tension and spring based. You would, however, have the latch showing on the exterior part of your door. If that happens to bother you. But I do like these door latches. They require no screws or permanent damage to the doors. They function easily. Can be set to an unlock position which is nice if the kiddies are away for awhile or if you're in and out of a door with the latch on it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0035RQF54', 'answerTime': 'Aug 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409382000, 'question': 'Can you disengage it from either side of the door?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, very easily. When its engaged in door slightly open position, there is about 1-4 inches of play, so kids can't open and can't crush fingers. An adult can reach up, tap the device so that it swings on hinge and disengages. Then when the adult swings the door in what would be a closing motion, the unit re-engages. You can disengage easily with one hand, allowing you to carry something in the other."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0035RQF54', 'answerTime': 'Aug 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409036400, 'question': 'Would this work on a front door?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It depends on your baby's age. For any door really."}
