{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00389VFH2', 'answerTime': 'Oct 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413183600, 'question': 'can you use plastic grocery bags in it instead of the refills?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You can, I guess, but the results will probably not be very good. The idea behind the bag isn't just that it's designed to fit the container. It's also built to hold the diapers (way more than a grocery bag) and it helps control the smell. Grocery bags are not nearly as strong as these, and they are more porous, meaning they are far more likely to rip, leak, or both. You're better off taking your old grocery bags back to the grocery store as most will recycle them. Look for the recycling bin, usually right near the entrance of the store."}
