{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0038OM4PO', 'answerTime': 'May 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400396400, 'question': 'How is this gate adjustable from 29.5" to 40.5"? Are the metal wings on either side of the wood frame removable? Thanks for any help!', 'answer': "Yes, they are removable. Also, the tension bolts adjust, which helps if the opening is slightly uneven or the gate doesn't latch properly. We are very happy with the gate and have used it in various openings."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0038OM4PO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416038400, 'question': 'Does the gate door open 180 degrees so it can be kept fully open if desired?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, but the gate is spring loaded so it will not remain open. It would need to be propped open with something, otherwise it just closes and latches by itself.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0038OM4PO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428649200, 'question': 'What is the opening mechanism? do you have to pull up on the door top open?', 'answer': "There is a little lever that you have to push to the side and then lift the gate up. This gate is very nice looking and works well. Because we didn't have to use the side panels the gate occasionally gets out of alignment, but is easily readjusted back. Everyone who see the gate compliments on what a nice looking gate it is."}
