{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003AJHDQW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376982000, 'question': 'How long did size 1 work?', 'answer': "My size 1 OsoCozies fit until around 15 pounds, I think...but now I use them to stuff my baby's pocket diapers and they are still working great. You can tri-fold them into either pocket diapers or waterproof diaper covers and they can last a lot longer that way. Love em!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003AJHDQW', 'answerTime': 'Sep 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409641200, 'question': 'Should I boil them for 30 minutes and cold wash before use? What should I do before use? What kind of detergent do you recommend?Thanks', 'answer': "You should definitely prep these before use. Because they are unbleached, they retain a little bit more natural oil. You can boil them to prep them or wash them a few times (you don't need to dry between washings), and the absorbency will improve with more washing. You can use a detergent specific to cloth diapers, or any detergent that is free of dyes/scents. We use Country Save."}
