{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003AJXY60', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': 'Read reviews still super confused. What all do I need to buy with this to start being able to use?', 'answer': 'This is just the waterproof shell that goes on the outside of the diaper. You will need the absorbent insides. You have several options here: 1- you can use an old school flat diaper which you fold and pin around your baby. If you use those, you will need "flats" and something to pin them with, either pins or snappis. 2- you can use what is called a fitted diaper. Those are less intimidating than flats. They look similar to the outer shell but are soft and absorbent. They sometimes have snaps on them to close them and sometimes not. If they are snapless, you may want a pin or a snappi. 3- you can use prefolds which are really similar to flats but are already sewn into a partially folded shape. You may want a snappi or pin for these too. 4- you can simply lay something absorbent into this shell without pinning or snapping it around your baby. You can use a folded up flat or prefold for this or a cloth diaper insert (NOT the microfiber kind because those cannot go next to baby\'s skin, but you could use hemp, cotton, or bamboo). In this case you would not need pins or snappis. I don\'t like this as much because it doesn\'t contain poop as well and so poop can get on the cover which means you have to use a new cover. If the cover doesn\'t get poop on it, you can reuse it. Hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003AJXY60', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392451200, 'question': "I purchased this cover and some thirsties duo inserts. They don't seem to go together. Does the duo insert just lay in the cover? No way to secure it", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It just lies inside the cover. The cover can be used over prefolds or with Flip inserts. I use it with Nickis prefold in large and it's very good. My LO is 7.5 months and it just fits her well. She's 18lbs. I think the duo inserts can be used for them."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003AJXY60', 'answerTime': 'Jun 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402383600, 'question': 'How many of these will I need to get me started. For example, how many will I need to get through 1 day with a newborn? Thank you !', 'answer': "I followed my friend's advice. She had twins and used these. start with 6, you will have more than enough. You don't always need to put them to wash every day, if the poop has not touched the wrap, you can reuse it. However, we did not use it for our newborn, she was too small, 6.3lbs. We started with 6, we are still using them and our daughter is now 6 moths old. They are great."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003AJXY60', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'Is this product machine washable?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes! It's very durable too. I let mine hang dry and they look brand new after 9 months."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003AJXY60', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382511600, 'question': 'How does this diaper work? Is it like Econobum or Flip, where you put a folded prefold/insert flat in, or diaper in a prefold and cover?', 'answer': "It's just like the Econobum or Flip covers - you can use either a prefold or an insert inside of it. We found that the Thirsties covers were really great for when our baby was very small, because they have extra coverage around the leg holes. But, he's already grown out of them (by 7 months)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003AJXY60', 'answerTime': 'May 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399878000, 'question': 'How many covers are needed if you want to do laundry every other day?', 'answer': 'Bare minimum of 5, but newborn poo is explosive, runny, and frequent, so it is very possible that you could need more. If the elastic or gussets get wet, or if poop gets into the seams, they need to be washed, otherwise they can be wiped and reused.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003AJXY60', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388563200, 'question': "We're TTC #2 and I'm seriously considering cloth diapering this time around. Any known leakage issues or latex bands with this set?", 'answer': "I don't know about the latex but we have had virtually no leakage issues with this wrap when we fold our prefold cloth insert properly. It took us awhile to figure out what worked for our baby, I watched a video on YouTube on how to fold the prefold different ways to minimize leaks and immediately saw improvement when coupled with this wrap. We also used the snappis for awhile while we were getting the hang of cloth diapering, this also seemed to help stop leaks."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003AJXY60', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419753600, 'question': 'Has anyone tried these with a newborn?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, I have used these with a newborn. The prefolds I used were large enough for a 1+ year old, so the diaper as a whole was quite large. But the wrap worked as expected.'}
