{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003CL8ICQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2011', 'unixTime': 1325318400, 'question': 'difference in product: What is the difference between Ameda Carry all and Ameda ultra lite?', 'answer': 'Hi, The Ultra is not "ultra lite" -- it\'s Ultra as in "loaded with features". Read my analysis of it here: http://www.a-natural-birth.com/2011/12/31/ameda-purely-yours-ultra-review/ Basically, it comes with the various size flanges you would need, as well as all accessories. The Carry-All is a plain tote bag, while this tote bag is larger and has compartments and is more useful, IMO. I would prefer the Ultra over the Carry-All, as I have personally seen the need for different sized flanges, even on the same woman as time and pumping necessitate. Hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003CL8ICQ', 'answerTime': 'Nov 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385452800, 'question': 'Does this kit come with the AC adapter?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It comes with a plug, yes. A normal AC plug/adapter. IF you mean for the car, then no, it doesn't. I actually bought an adapter that has a plug for the cigarette lighter in the car. You can plug in any normal 2 or 3 prong cord to it and it works great. This pump is an amazing pump too, if that helps with your decision. Their customer service is great too. I once called them two months after my warranty expired and they still helped me and sent me a free replacement part."}
