{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003DIMKRM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382511600, 'question': 'Would it keep my babys bottles warm?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes but I wouldnt count on it for more than an hour. It doesnt keep baby bottles cold without the ice pack I have for it. I bought my own. You are better off for warm ones to warm how ever many bottles worth and put into a good glass lined thermos. Then bring empty bottles and fill as needed.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003DIMKRM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390204800, 'question': 'Does this fit 8 oz Medela bottles and the Medela ice pack?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I think it will, worst case scenario would be that you might only be able to put bottles on one side. I use a similar icepack that is made to put cans on each side but I have fat 10 oz bottles so I put 3 on one side and I lay a spring water bottle one across the top of everything for me before I close it. Lets face it though, you aren't gonna pack more than three bottles in this as the ice pack itself will only last so long. So if you had 6 in there, by the time you got to number 4, they won't be kept cold enough. Nice pack though. I have abused mine terribly and it saved me many times. I put 3 diapers (my baby is size 6) and a small personal size wipes in the top. Bah bahs in the bottom and its a lot easier to carry this than a cooler for sure. You can just sling it over the back of baby carriage where you push."}
