{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003ES4SBM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412924400, 'question': 'Is there a latch to keep this booster secure on the seat? Would you reccomend this seat? This exact model is not on the consumer reports for safety.', 'answer': "There are Latch hooks on this seat, but they are not for securing the seat in case of accident...they are on fixed length 6'' tethers that are meant only for keeping the seat from flying around the car when the seat is not occupied. The seat is designed to be held securely by the vehicles seat belt restraint system! Yes, I highly recommend this seat, we are completely satisfied with the safety of the seat. You have to be sure to use the shoulder restrain properly and that means fully extending the belt completely out and letting it reel itself back to engage the lock sprocket! Remember to read your vehicles manual for the proper use of your restraint system."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003ES4SBM', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401778800, 'question': "i can't find info on minimum child's weight and height?", 'answer': 'The front of the Instruction manual says age 3 or over, 30-100 pounds, 38-57 inches. There are car seat safety guidelines on different websites (highway patrol,consumer reports, etc) and car seats are still believed to be safer. We waited to switch over until our son was 40 pounds, over 40 inches and almost 4 years old. We are pleased with the booster and it is easy to use.'}
