{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003G2YUU0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373698800, 'question': 'Anyone hear loud thumping or ticks while its going?', 'answer': "No, not at all. I've been using our mobile every night for about 6 months and no complaints."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003G2YUU0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386662400, 'question': 'What kind of music or sounds does it play?', 'answer': "This isn't specific but: There are settings for different types of noises, including lullaby type, nature sounds, etc. Why don't I have details off the top of my head? Because it isn't annoying. In fact, the renditions of classical type music get stuck in my head, in a good way, and I am NOT a classical music person at all. You won't be irritated by this, but you will have options if your child has a preference. The more you hit the bird that makes the music play, the more you advance to different songs. My 11-month-old smacks it till he gets to the specific one he wants, then sits down and enjoys. It's that good. Way better than the music on on chair he has, which is high-pitched and whiny."}
