{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003GC4SX4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372834800, 'question': "Does the back stay up when there is a rear-facing, convertible car seat in place? I don't want my two year old to mark up the seat with his shoes.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I've strapped in rear facing car seats for my grandchildren. The seat-back portion of the mat stays in place for me. There is a tab on the mat that tucks into the fold of the seat and helps keep the back in place. In addition the car seats put pressure on the seat-back portion to keep it in place. It's also stiff enough that it does not flop towards the car seat. I hope this helps you."}
