{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003GQ0LQ8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371884400, 'question': 'does this meet the requirements for airplane travel', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "It does not, I fear. As the prior responder notes, bubblebum is designed to boost kids so that the shoulder strap sits at the right level across their chest. With airplanes, there is no such strap. However, there is a perfect, albeit somewhat pricey solution called CARES. It's a strap in harness system you can use for kids who weigh between 20 and 44 lbs. You can learn more at www.kidsflysafe.com."}
