{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003GQ0LQ8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1360742400, 'question': "I bought two bubble bums in November 2012 and the air in one of them won't stay in. I can hear it escaping but I can't feel the air come out anywhere", 'answer': 'Hello Jeanne, I had the same issue. Apparently there was a bad batch shipped out. Please contact fintankelly@bubblebum.us and let her know the issue. They have EXCELLENT customer service and will resolve the issue. In my case they replaced both my seats immediately at no cost to me! Once you get the replacements, you will love this product! Kelly did tell me that the seat was tested deflated also and meets safety standards without air provided you use the belt hooks on both sides of the seat to keep the belt snug across your child.'}
