{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003GQ0LQ8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361433600, 'question': 'is it safe to use for occasional use on travel with a toddler who is 2.5 years old and weighs 35lbs??/', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The weight is a minimum of 40 lbs. What I would personally be more concerned about is the tot being fidgety and getting OUT of the belt. I started mine when my daughter was 3.5, and we had to constantly be on top of her about sitting back, keeping her feet down, not stretching the seatbelt out. I would personally wait, and make sure that the child is old enough to sit still with out being told every ten minutes, otherwise you would be having to sit directly next to him/her. The size is great for us, we have it smooshed in between a baby seat and a booster in the back seat of a PRIUS, but it might be unstable for such a little one with nothing on one or both sides.'}
