{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003H3GL3M', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407135600, 'question': 'with If there is hot water/formula in the bottle does the outside get hot as well?', 'answer': "I have both bottles the thermal and not thermal. The thermal ones don't get hot or cold on the outside they're amazing at keeping milk cold. You can feel the temperature of the liquid on the bottles that aren't thermal - I love it because I couldn't tell with the plastic ones I used what the actual temperature of the milk was, so I always had to test it. With these bottles, you can tell right away so if it's too hot, you'll know, it's a great safety feature actually. I also like that the non thermal bottles heat up so quickly, much faster than glass or plastic bottles. I just run mine under hot tap water for about 30s. Hope this helps!"}
