{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003HEX4Q8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371106800, 'question': 'Is there a list of what car seats this stroller is or is not compatible with?', 'answer': "It fits most carriers. Keep in mind that carriers do not click or lock into this universal base; carriers rest on two support bars and are secured with a red strap that runs through the base of the carrier, much like a car seatbelt would run through the bottom of the carrier. I've had a Jeep Liberty stroller for 8 years for two kids and I love it because it's light, portable, sturdy, has a great bin on the bottom for storage, folds with one hand, and the wheels move exceptionally well. I bought the Jeep stroller base when I had a baby last year because I knew it would have similar qualities and it does. I used it for about five months until my very big baby outgrew his carrier. Short story long: I liked it a lot, but it is important to know that carriers don't lock in place on this stroller base."}
