{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003HIXOF0', 'answerTime': 'Jun 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403074800, 'question': 'What is the height from the ground to where the changing pad would lay? (Was curious as to how high I would actually have to lift baby)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'In the front corners, from the bottom to the top is 37 inches (its a few inches higher in the back corners). The top 5 inches of the dresser is open on the top for the baby to be changed in (we put a thick pad in, which fits great). There is a small cut-out in the front, as you can see in the pictures. But basically you need to be able to lift the baby about 36 to 37 inches to get into the changing area. I\'m 5\' 8" in height, and the baby changing height is just perfect for me (high enough so I don\'t need to bend over the change the baby, low enough so it\'s not awkward to change the baby).'}
