{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003ITAUTG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375686000, 'question': "How does the Recaro Proride compare with Britax with respect to Britax's Integrated steel bars? Does this seat have something similar?", 'answer': "recaro proride is better than britax. it's way stable and sturdier feeling than britax. i have no problem with recaro proride convertible. but if you want something that would be user later after your lil. one is more than 2 yo then go with britax frontier 85 because after 2 yo your lo will want a cup holder and snack slot. trust me on this part. i have 3 recaro proride, 1 recaro prosport, 2 britax boulevard, 1 britax marathon, and lastly britax frontier 85. i buy them as my lo grows."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003ITAUTG', 'answerTime': 'Jun 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404025200, 'question': 'When you pull the strap to tighten the chest straps, is it very easy? I want it to be easy to pull and for the chest straps to be very snug.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, very easy compared to other car seats. I can get it snug and my husband easily gets it uncomfortably tight.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003ITAUTG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386230400, 'question': "Is the padding on seat intended for all ages' use or should it be removed for older kid?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The padding is for all ages. I actually lost the bottom seat cushion on a flight and called Recaro to ask the same question. The cushioning provides protection against specific types of common injuries that occur during collisions, such as pelvic injuries, in the case of the bottom seat cushion. So long story short, it stays in all the time.'}
