{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003KEMMNG', 'answerTime': '14 days ago', 'question': 'will this work in a 5th wheel camper bunk bed? It would be for a 19 month old on the lower bunk', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes, but as I stated in my review, I don't like how these are in two foot pieces. I would rather buy the long one piece stay put bumpers and cut it shorter. The two pieces apart are more likely to not catch my child as well if the really pushed against them. The longer one seems to also stick to mattress better."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003KEMMNG', 'answerTime': 'Sep 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409727600, 'question': 'Do you think these can this be used to prevent an elderly person who weighs 175 lbs from rolling out of bed? He hates the confinment a bed rail gives.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Possibly. As soon as my daughter hit that 30lb mark she could easily roll over them if she wanted to get out of bed, it served more as a deterrent than anything. We no longer use them. It would really depend on how much this person moved in their sleep. It could possibly work if you got 2 sets, one to line each side of the bed as long as they are not physically trying to get up and over them.'}
