{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003KFCV6S', 'answerTime': 'Sep 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411974000, 'question': 'I\'m confused as to how many 24\' bumpers are included in this product. Are there TWO 24" bumpers or FOUR?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You get FOUR pieces that are each 24". I started with all four on my daughter\'s bed (two on each side) - so they ran nearly the length of the bed. She really only needed one on each side, so when my second daughter moved to a big girl bed, I took two from the first bed and put on either side of the second bed. This works out great for us; my girls are now 5 and 3, and we still use them.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003KFCV6S', 'answerTime': 'Jan 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422172800, 'question': 'Would they be high enough for elderly adult?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes I think so. I think they are a great aid in keeping people from rolling off the bed.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003KFCV6S', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': 'Can I make the bed and it look "normal" with a comforter as if there are no pads under it?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I wouldn\'t guarantee that the bumpers will be totally inconspicuous, but there are some bedding options that will certainly help. The thicker your comforter, the more "normal" the bed will look. Especially if you were to add a down comforter - that would help; the extra fluff and bulk would fill in the middle, and the weight could help "pull" down the sides and keep the middle taut and smooth. After awhile though, you get used to the bumpers, and I don\'t even think about them anymore. I would much rather deal with two small humps than those side rails/gates or pushing the bed up against a wall. Hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003KFCV6S', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428649200, 'question': 'Is this a good SAFE replacement for a bed rail, or is this more for traveling etc.?', 'answer': "I believe it's safe for every night use. We kept our son in a crib until he was almost 4 years old for safety reasons, he was a crazy active sleeper. It's been about a year, he's almost 5 & has not fallen out of bed, yet. I do check on him before I go to bed & often move him back up to his pillows because he finds his way to the only unsafe spot without bumpers, the foot of the bed. We had a typical bed rail on our 3 year old daughter's bed & I ended up switching that out with these foam bumpers because they were working well with our boy, changing sheets are SO much easier, & they look better than the clunky bed rail."}
