{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003LNU8PK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390291200, 'question': 'Will this work on a stokke tripp Trapp chair?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I am sorry I can't given a definite answer, but from what I can see in the pictures of the stokke tripp trapp chair, there seems to be only one slit (point) of insertion for the bottom piece (again I could be wrong about this). The boon flair does not strap all the way around as it seems that some of the stokke do (from what I can gauge from pictures, not from experience). In sum you would need slots for insertion (slits in chair) in 5 places for the boon flair to work (1 at bottom, 2 on sides, and 2 at top). The only thing that keeps this harness from coming out is the doubling of the strap at the end, with fold at end (wide enough to pass through slit but with enough of an obstacle to keep it from coming out). It has worked well for me without problem. I hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003LNU8PK', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375599600, 'question': 'How does this attach?', 'answer': "This is hard to explain - the straps are folded on themselves at the end and sewn in place (like a loop?), it goes thru the slots in your chair then the strap (that's sewn and folded) opens and catches, preventing it from pulling back thru. I hope this helps."}
