{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003MZCSJG', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': 'Is this item waterproof (can I wipe if off easily)? Or is it fabric that I have to wash after every feeding?', 'answer': "It is a tough fabric (like a canvas) on the back and it's laminated with vinyl on the front. The trim is like a polyester or nylon fabric. They are extremely waterproof and can hold up to about 8oz. of fluid in the pocket. I generally wipe them down with a washcloth after each feeding (if really messy I rinse in them in the sink (if the trim gets messy) and hang them to dry before the next meal. I usually toss them in the wash with towels once a week (dry on low/med heat and usually remove it before the rest of the load)."}
