{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003N3AHKE', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': 'Is this item waterproof (can I wipe if off easily)? Or is it fabric that I have to wash after every feeding?', 'answer': "It is a tough fabric (like a canvas) on the back and it's laminated with vinyl on the front. The trim is like a polyester or nylon fabric. They are extremely waterproof and can hold up to about 8oz. of fluid in the pocket. I generally wipe them down with a washcloth after each feeding (if really messy I rinse in them in the sink (if the trim gets messy) and hang them to dry before the next meal. I usually toss them in the wash with towels once a week (dry on low/med heat and usually remove it before the rest of the load)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N3AHKE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382770800, 'question': 'Are these made with BPA?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Website dexbaby.com says bpa free. Check it out. On the tag, "content: poyeurethane" hope that helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003N3AHKE', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': 'Is there a snap at the neck or is it Velcro?', 'answer': 'There are two snaps (for sizing purposes). Hope that helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407222000, 'question': 'Does anyone sell replacement parts for the clear plastic top/straw that fits into the screw on lid? Mine have held up great, except for this part.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I too have looked and looked, and finally found them on www.buybabydirect.com for $3.49 for a pack of 2. 2pk Replacement Flex Straw with Extender Straw SKU: X9904FSCS500 Manufacturer: Nby'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': 'is there a cover for the straw', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "There is no cover for the straw but they really don't leak as long as you have the parts all together correctly. These are the best as far as no leaks, but they seem pretty hard to suck to me, but my kids (ages 1,2, and 3) don't seem to have an issue with it. I've tried a lot of cups and these are my favorite."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381474800, 'question': 'How many different parts are there to clean? Are disassembling and cleaning difficult? Thanks.', 'answer': "There's 4 parts total. The cup, the screw ring, the rubber center part of the top and the straw you see are one piece that also acts as a seal between the lid and the cup, and a hard lower straw. These cups have been fantastic and they're not difficult to clean. We just pinch the straw to run water through the seal. We give our toddler milk and water in these all the time and the only time they leak is when pressure gets built up inside them."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426402800, 'question': 'Neither me nor my wife can suck anything through this straw...are we doing something wrong?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes: I think you have to bite down to free the passage of air/fluid.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418371200, 'question': 'None of these products have an age range, what is that??????', 'answer': 'These particular cups start at 12 months but my son started using them at about 9 months'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414911600, 'question': 'does it spill when upside down.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No it doesnt. Now if it gets hot the pressure builds up and some will come out the straw but thats it'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412578800, 'question': 'Does the little one have to bite the straw to get the liquid? My little guy is having trouble....', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "When the child puts the straw in their mouth, they automatically put enough pressure on the straw to release the liquid. They don't have to bite hard like some of the other cups."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405839600, 'question': 'does anyone know if they sell a replacement hard inner straw?', 'answer': "I do not know if they offer additional straws. However I have used straws from some of the fast food restaurant's that have large diameter straws that will work; just cut to length. try the straw from the arches."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404802800, 'question': 'Are these BPA free?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Allegedly, but they had a strange smell and they don't stand up. Poorly designed. I threw mine out."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N49ML8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388563200, 'question': 'Is there a way to adapt the cup/lid/valve/straw in order to make the straw less difficult to suck from and more like a regular straw?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'If you really want to make these bottles work, you could use a thin exact type knife and score out the valve on the inside of the straw, coming in from the top. Cutting out the two pieces that are about 1/2" from the top would remove the restriction from inside. As you wash these bottles though, the rubber becomes softer and you\'ll get more flow anyway. However, if your kiddo is at the point where he\'s needing more volume out of the straw, you may want to look for a bottle that has a hard straw. Now that mine is a little older, we use cups with lids and a hard straw that has a rubber ring around it to keep it sealed. Nuby soft tops aren\'t known to be long lasting bottles after all. Good luck!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N64Z7W', 'answerTime': 'Mar 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394521200, 'question': 'Will this fit a Graco fast action stroller with the infant car seat attached?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Depends on how much space it takes up. Could possibly be adjusted to fit with an infant seat, may not cover the same way but enough to do the job.'}
