{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N64Z7W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390291200, 'question': 'Has anyone tried using two of these in a Baby Jogger City Select 2-seat configuration?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I haven\'t, no... But if you\'re talking about the "narrow stacked" buggy (not the old-school "wide" models), I do expect that it might work. The shape of this cover isn\'t glove-fit... it\'s more like a 3D apron: relatively loose and adaptable. With a little tinkering, I\'ll bet you can make it work. (Adequately covering the rear-seated baby\'s legs will be your main problem, I think.)'}
