{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003N9M6YI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424419200, 'question': 'What does "3 months +/ BPA FREE" mean?', 'answer': '3months+ means it is suitable for babies over 3 months & BPA "stands for bisphenol A. BPA is an industrial chemical that has been used to make certain plastics and resins since the 1960s. BPA is found in polycarbonate plastics and epoxy resins. Polycarbonate plastics are often used in containers that store food and beverages, such as water bottles. They may also be used in other consumer goods."'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003N9M6YI', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411455600, 'question': 'can I put this in the freezer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't leave them in there over night. But I'll put them in for 20mins for my daughter. They seem fine though. Had them for a few months and they still have no cracks"}
