{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OBYTSG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377327600, 'question': 'can you use a bassinet sheet in it?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I personally did not use a bassinet sheet. I tucked a blanket around the pad. This bassinet has a pad that is detachable. You would definitely be able to place a sheet on it if it was the correct size. I truly love this bassinet. We use it all the time.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTJA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 1, 2012', 'unixTime': 1343804400, 'question': 'Travel bag for Britax B Ready: Does anyone know of a travel bag that will fit the b ready?', 'answer': 'Hello I was looking for the same thing and found a review of the JL Childress Standard and Dual Stroller Travel Bag. http://www.amazon.com/Childress-Standard-Stroller-Travel-Black/dp/B000262HMQ/ref=cm_cr_pr_product_top If you go to Customer reviews the newest review said that the B-ready stroller fits in the bag. I hope this could help.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTJA', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391587200, 'question': "I just got this stroller and am testing it. I'm struggling with the recline function. I got it to recline, but can't get it up anymore?", 'answer': 'That sounds like a problem. I would suggest contacting Britax.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTJA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2012', 'unixTime': 1331535600, 'question': 'Infant in toddler seat? Just curious-- has anyone used the "toddler seat" in a fully reclined position for an infant under 6 months?', 'answer': "Personally, I wouldn't put a newborn in the fully reclined toddler seat. It doesn't seem very safe and comfortable when they are so little. I have used the bassinet for my baby from 0 - 7 months and now (she is 8 months) I am using the toddler seat. I think Britax also says that the toddler seat is not for children under 6 months."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTJA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1366268400, 'question': "The front wheels appear to be stuck on swivel. It will be a pain for me to return so I'm thinking about just keeping it. Why do I need it locked?", 'answer': 'You really only need them locked if you are on rough terrain. Like sand, or heavy mud (although not sure you would ever be in mud!) I have had mine for 2 years and have never locked the front wheels. Actually more annoying pushing a stroller with the front wheels locked- so hard to turn!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTJA', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393228800, 'question': 'What is the width of the stroller when folded at its widest point (from one end of the rear wheel to the other)', 'answer': 'I\'m not sure if having the second seat attached makes a difference but, I just measured 24" wheel to wheel, 18" from back to front and 39"tall (while folded). I hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTJA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 10, 2011', 'unixTime': 1315638000, 'question': 'Using this stroller with other Britax Car Seats: Is this stroller compatible with the Britax Boulevard car seat?', 'answer': "No it's not. The boulevard is a convertible that stays in your car. B ready is compatable with the britax chaperone or b safe seats . You can use it with other brand seats with an adapter bar."}
