{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423468800, 'question': 'Do you have to buy the adapter also? or just the second seat?', 'answer': 'I have the Britax B-Ready stroller and all I had to but was this second seat. I later decided I also wanted the lower infant car seat adapter but it was not necessary. My two year old fits comfortably in this lower seat when I have the infant seat on the top and/or when I have the bassinet. The infant car seat adapter is to put the infant on the bottom whenever I want my two year old on the top. I hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': 'Sep 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378105200, 'question': 'Hi, could you tell me the dimensions of the shipping box? Thanks!', 'answer': "It came in the original packaging from Britax and wasn't big at all :) I don't know the exact dimensions as we recycled the box awhile ago but it was smaller than I expected, maybe 6-10 inches, 2 ft by 2 ft?"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': '6 days ago', 'question': 'Can this be used with the B- Agile stroller as well?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No it is not comparable with the B-agile stroller'}
{'answer': "I used either the bassinet or the car seat on top for my newborn and my two year old in the bottom. It worked better since my newborn needed more attention than my two year old. I didn't buy the bottom car seat adaptor because I knew I wouldn't use it.", 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': '7 days ago', 'question': "I have this second seat, but I'm wondering what the best configuration is for newborn and toddler (2.5)? Should I also get the adapter to put car seat low?", 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': '10 days ago', 'question': 'Is there a use for the main seat that comes with the stroller originally?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes the main seat has a weight capacity of 55lbs and can be used from 6 months. The second seat can be used from birth and has a weight capacity of 35lbs.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422259200, 'question': 'is that a good stroller for a 2 1/2 year old and a 6 months old?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Absolutely! My boys are 19 months apart and we've used this stroller from the beginning. There is an adapter you can buy to click an infant carrier into the stroller. We used it until our youngest outgrew his infant carrier car seat and then switched to the second seat. Of all the purchases we've made along the way, this stroller is by far my favorite! I can't even imagine using a bulky side by side stroller. How do you get through doors with those things?! Well worth the cost in my opinion!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421913600, 'question': "Can a child sit in the bottom seat without another child in the top? I want to make sure it won't tip over i the weight distribution changes.", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No the second seat is only to be used when there is a child in the primary position.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420790400, 'question': 'what is the size of the b-ready stroller folded with the second seat attached? Many double strollers will not fit in my trunk...', 'answer': 'The folded dimensions are 26.5w x 16h x 30d. This stroller allows you to easily remove the wheels by pushing the center button so that it becomes more compact for storage in your car.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OBYTO0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420704000, 'question': 'Would the second seat connect to the b-agile stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No it only fits the b-ready stroller'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OGVAGA', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404198000, 'question': 'I have a B-Ready stroller. I am going to buy the second/lower seat. Do I also need to buy this adapter? Or is this only for attaching non-Britax seats? Thnx', 'answer': 'This attachment is used for the baby car seat... we knew that our older child was not going to like sitting on the bottom so we decided to buy this and use it for the car seat of our new baby which is the britax chaperone. The car seat came with the attachment pieces that mount to both the be ready stroller and this device. If you are going to have your older child sitting on the bottom then you just need the second seat. We are going to wait till our baby is bigger and get the skate board attachment for our older child and then the baby can use the regular seat on stroller. Look into it and if u can go to store to seethe different options installed and see if your child will like the low ridding. Hope this helps. Good luck and congrats!!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OGVAGA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385107200, 'question': 'chicco', 'answer': 'Yes that piece fits on the bottom of stroller where the lower seat would go. You would also need the universal adapter to go with that, which snaps into that piece to use with chicco car seat. So, u need both adapters if you want to use car seat on the lower part of stroller. If not you would just need the universal adapter which snaps into the top so u car use chicco car seat. Hope that helps!'}
