{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJ4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1298793600, 'question': "Anyone used the Britax Roundabout with a newborn? I'm wondering if anyone has used this (or any other convertible) car seat from day one?", 'answer': 'I was also thinking of doing the same. I will be a first time mom in July and the infant seat seems a bit of a waste of money and also a big carbon footprint considering all the safety advocates say not to use a used car seat. I was doing some research and a site called Consumer Search mentioned that Britax sells "...a foam positioning insert..." for smaller infants.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJ4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1303887600, 'question': 'Does anyone have Britax Roundabout 50 in your Honda Civic?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We have the Roundabout 50 and I have fit it in smaller passenger cars -Mazda 3 and mid-size cars - Altima and Camry (these were rentals). I find that if it is installed rear-facing in the center seat the car seat is narrow enough that it should fit in between the space of the front seats (such that driver and front passenger can still move their seats far back without interfering with the car seat). The seat is easier to install with the latch though (center seat usually only has seatbelt option). Because of that I have normally installed the car seat in the outer position directly behind the front passenger seat. The car seat is very long and the front passenger seat must be pushed pretty far forward to accommodate this - leaving little room for a passenger, even a petite one and definitely a tall or large person would not fit in the passenger seat. Since these were temporary rentals it was no big deal, but it may be a problem for everyday use, especially if you can't get the seat installed correctly/securely in the center position."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJ4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 30, 2011', 'unixTime': 1319958000, 'question': 'can the straps be removed to wash? Any help would be appreciated. also how easy is the latch system to install in vehicle?', 'answer': 'Never submerge straps in water. It will say so in the manual. Doing so weakens the fibers and they can over-stretch in an accident. Spot clean with a damp cloth.'}
