{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJ4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2011', 'unixTime': 1309503600, 'question': 'moving car seat: How easy is it to move this seat between two cars?', 'answer': "I don't do it that often but find it rather easy. However I do have the latch system and it fits easily in my impala. I can move it to my mother in laws jeep but cant fit the jeeps latch system, think I'm doing something wrong. I can confidently install it forward facing in the jeep and thats what I do. All in all, takes about 10 min and I don't do it often."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJ4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2011', 'unixTime': 1301036400, 'question': 'Britax Roundabout 55 for plane: Has anyone used this seat in an airplane?', 'answer': 'I can tell you from experiance using this seat on an international flight it is great. I flew from Germany to Texas without a car seat. I had this one ordered and sent to my destination, as my daughter was about to out grow her infant car seat. On the flight back to Germany my husband buckled this seat into the normal plan seat, and within mins my daughter was asleep and slept the entire 10 hour plane ride, lucky we had a night time flight. We also had a rental car while in the states and it fit perfectly. I did not install this car seat my husband did, but he said it was easy both in the car and on the plane.'}
