{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIPI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2011', 'unixTime': 1318834800, 'question': 'Why is there an Onyx I and Onyx II (or old and new)? Anyone know what that means?', 'answer': 'I called Britax to ask the same question. They said they are exactly the same seat, but they are using a new manufacturer to make some of their parts. The parts are the same, the seat is the same, and one seat is not older than another (she said they could have been manufactured just days apart even). She said it is confusing that it is listed here as an older model and a newer model, but that is not the case and there have been no changes to the seat, so there\'s no reason not to order the "older model". Hope this helps. I just bought the Onyx.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIPI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394780400, 'question': 'my kid is using this model 70-CS. I am thinking of buying another advocate to put in another car. Is the latest variant G4? what is the difference ?', 'answer': 'The basic difference is the infant position pad, and the belly pad. The shell is the same, the harness is the same, and the installation is the same.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIPI', 'answerTime': 'Jul 30, 2011', 'unixTime': 1312009200, 'question': 'Advocate 70 vs Frontier 85 for short toddler', 'answer': "I have both...I have a 6 year old, a 3 year old and a 6 month old. I purchased the newer frontiers for my oldest children and an advocate for my youngest because he's heavy and I knew he would outgrow his infant carrier a lot sooner than expected. I noticed that my 3 year old was struggling to sleep in her frontier on a 12 hour car ride so we pulled over and gave her the advocate and placed my then 4 month old back into his infant carrier and base (luckily it was still in the back of my van) and she passed out within minutes. I find the smaller children still aren't ready to nap in the frontier without looking completely uncomfortable and leaning forward constantly...I've seen purchased another advocate for my son since his sister took his. Hope that helps."}
