{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIPI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2011', 'unixTime': 1321603200, 'question': 'Anyone use it instead of an infant car seat? Has anyone done this and what has your experience been?', 'answer': 'I used Britax convertibles with both of my kids from birth just because infant seats are not safe! They were fine and my children were not big(my daughter was 6lbs 11oz and my son came home 4lbs 12oz-he was 3lbs7oz at birth). We have the new advocate for the upcoming baby ;-) The advocate even has an "infant insert" that can be purchased to improve the fit. Yes, they look small in the seat, but it does not affect the safety of the seat-at all. Think about this, a piece of plastic that goes through constant stress of in and out of the car(we have a materials engineer in the family and he was very adamant about it not being safe-too much stress on plastic). The studies about this have been buried time and time again, but there is some evidence if you search the net. Unfortunately, we were hit by a drunk driver when my daughter was only 4 mos, she was just fine in her Britax seat! When my son was 9 mos, our Corolla was sideswiped by a semi-truck, both kids were fine(they slept through it), my son in his convertible, my daughter in her Britax booster. We drive A LOT(40k miles a year) and I have never felt uncomfortable with the convertibles from birth and after our second accident we were told by the investigating officer that the Britax saved my son major injuries! I think you will be just fine going with the convertible from day one, we were and ours were "tested."'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIM6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 11, 2011', 'unixTime': 1307775600, 'question': 'Do new Britax carseats (August 2010 models) fit on airplanes? Has anyone tried installing any of the new Britax carseats (Marathon 70, Boulevard 70, or Boulevard 70 CS) on an airplane, rear-facing or front-facing?', 'answer': "Actually, only some airlines have that policy. Though I have found if you ask nicely and explain that you need a little time to put the carseat in and don't want to block the other passengers, some staff will let you even if it isn't their policy. However, some folks take it as a personal affront, which I don't really understand."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIM6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2012', 'unixTime': 1330329600, 'question': 'will this fit rear-facing in a 2002 vw jetta? anyone know?', 'answer': "Did you ever find out if it fits? I'm looking at getting it for my 09 Jetta."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIM6', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2011', 'unixTime': 1317625200, 'question': 'How is the Britax Blvd 70 for newborns?', 'answer': "The new Blvd has an infant insert you can purchase through Britax that makes it an acceptable fit for larger newborns but the average to smaller newborns still won't fit even with the insert. Their top harness slots are just too high for most newborns since the slots need to be at or below for rear facing. The Scenera, True Fit, MyRide65, Triumph65, Cocorro and a couple others fit newborns well."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIM6', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2011', 'unixTime': 1313478000, 'question': 'Will Britax Boulevard fit in a Mini Cooper?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Front facing or rear facing? What year is the car seat?'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIM6', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2011', 'unixTime': 1313478000, 'question': 'Fitting carseats into our car for 20 hour drive. What carseat(s) would be best in order to fit the three youngest in one row of seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm sure you've already taken your trip, but here's what I think, in case it helps someone else. I assume you'll have the 2 year old rearfacing, especially since you're traveling at what I assume will be highway speeds. I would put them on one side of the back row in a Britax Boulevard or Advocate. It depends how big your 6 year old is, but probably something like a Graco Nautilus on the other side of the back seat. The 8 year old can be in a low back booster in the middle of the back seat and you should be able to access both side seats still. The 12 and 14 year old don't need boosters anymore and can go in the captains chairs, but could also switch out with the 8 year old. Hope this helps someone."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIM6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1317106800, 'question': 'Infant seat vs convertible seat: Would appreciate any feedback on if this is a good choice for 0-6 months or not.', 'answer': 'I agree completely. I had the bulky travel system with my first child and decided to skip that and just get Britax straight away. We are getting a lightweight stroller for when baby gets bigger but I plan on mostly carrying them with me with the help of a moby. The infant carriers are overrated and unnecessary.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2011', 'unixTime': 1300777200, 'question': 'Does Britax Marathon fits in your Honda Civic? Does anyone has Marathon in your Civic?', 'answer': "This is a little late but I just saw your post. Yes this will fit in a civic, I'm actually going to purchase one today for ours. www.car-seat.org is a great place to search the forums to see others' experiences with seats (and you can usually find pictures too)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1303887600, 'question': 'Is Cowmooflage cover too hot for the South?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Crimson, Allison and Cow are velvety. Blueprint and Onix are smooth, almost satiny. Waverly is smooth, but a little more "rough. Jet Set is very rough, so I absolutely hated touching it in the store. I was considering Crimson, but thought of our hot GA summers and will now get Blueprint or Onix. By the way, even though Babies\'R\'Us does not have seats in all of the fabrics, they have swatches so you can touch them and judge for yourself. :) Buy-Buy Baby has seats in most of the fabrics.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2011', 'unixTime': 1300172400, 'question': 'Harness adjustment on Britax Marathon 70 Convertible Car Seat: Can anyone tell me how the harness straps are re-adjusted for this carseat.', 'answer': 'Hi Carrie, I measured the backseat of my outback. It measures approx 50 inches across. I hope this helps with determining if the marathon will be too big for your forester. The marathon fits great in my outback. I\'m 5\'4" and my hubby is average height and we don\'t have a problem with not being able to sit comfortably in the front. Good luck!'}
