{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 29, 2011', 'unixTime': 1311922800, 'question': 'Reclining Rear facing: Does anyone know if this seat reclines well in the rear facing position?', 'answer': 'You can use pool noodles to increase the incline to closer to 45 degrees. I would contact a local car seat safety inspector to help you with this.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIJY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 7, 2011', 'unixTime': 1315378800, 'question': '2009 Honda Civic Si fit? Does this fit in a Honda Civic Si?', 'answer': "We currently have the Britax Marathon 70 in a 2008 Honda Civic LX Sedan. We previously had the same car seat* in a 2004 Civic LX Coupe. It fit just fine in both, even with the front seat adjusted all the way back. The difference in the trim/option packages (LX vs. Si) won't affect whether the car seat fits at all. And the body did not change from 2008 to 2009, so that shouldn't affect anything either. I'm very confident it will fit. It wasn't all that easy getting our daughter in and out of the coupe (2 doors), but that's going to be the case with any car seat. After doing that for awhile, the sedan (4 doors) is a pleasure. By the way, we were rear-ended pretty hard (we were stopped waiting to make a left-hand turn) with this our daughter in this car seat in the 2004 Civic. The trunk was crumpled too close to the back seat for my comfort. And yet my daughter was completely protected. I'm 100% sold on the Civic/Marathon combination. *ETA: Not the exact same car seat. We replaced it with the same model and disposed of the seat that was in the accident."}
