{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIL2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1303887600, 'question': 'Is Cowmooflage cover too hot for the South?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Crimson, Allison and Cow are velvety. Blueprint and Onix are smooth, almost satiny. Waverly is smooth, but a little more "rough. Jet Set is very rough, so I absolutely hated touching it in the store. I was considering Crimson, but thought of our hot GA summers and will now get Blueprint or Onix. By the way, even though Babies\'R\'Us does not have seats in all of the fabrics, they have swatches so you can touch them and judge for yourself. :) Buy-Buy Baby has seats in most of the fabrics.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIL2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2011', 'unixTime': 1300172400, 'question': 'Harness adjustment on Britax Marathon 70 Convertible Car Seat: Can anyone tell me how the harness straps are re-adjusted for this carseat.', 'answer': 'Hi Carrie, I measured the backseat of my outback. It measures approx 50 inches across. I hope this helps with determining if the marathon will be too big for your forester. The marathon fits great in my outback. I\'m 5\'4" and my hubby is average height and we don\'t have a problem with not being able to sit comfortably in the front. Good luck!'}
