{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIMQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2011', 'unixTime': 1317625200, 'question': 'How is the Britax Blvd 70 for newborns?', 'answer': "The new Blvd has an infant insert you can purchase through Britax that makes it an acceptable fit for larger newborns but the average to smaller newborns still won't fit even with the insert. Their top harness slots are just too high for most newborns since the slots need to be at or below for rear facing. The Scenera, True Fit, MyRide65, Triumph65, Cocorro and a couple others fit newborns well."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIMQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2011', 'unixTime': 1313478000, 'question': 'Will Britax Boulevard fit in a Mini Cooper?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Front facing or rear facing? What year is the car seat?'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIMQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2011', 'unixTime': 1313478000, 'question': 'Fitting carseats into our car for 20 hour drive. What carseat(s) would be best in order to fit the three youngest in one row of seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm sure you've already taken your trip, but here's what I think, in case it helps someone else. I assume you'll have the 2 year old rearfacing, especially since you're traveling at what I assume will be highway speeds. I would put them on one side of the back row in a Britax Boulevard or Advocate. It depends how big your 6 year old is, but probably something like a Graco Nautilus on the other side of the back seat. The 8 year old can be in a low back booster in the middle of the back seat and you should be able to access both side seats still. The 12 and 14 year old don't need boosters anymore and can go in the captains chairs, but could also switch out with the 8 year old. Hope this helps someone."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIMQ', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1317106800, 'question': 'Infant seat vs convertible seat: Would appreciate any feedback on if this is a good choice for 0-6 months or not.', 'answer': 'I agree completely. I had the bulky travel system with my first child and decided to skip that and just get Britax straight away. We are getting a lightweight stroller for when baby gets bigger but I plan on mostly carrying them with me with the help of a moby. The infant carriers are overrated and unnecessary.'}
