{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIMG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2011', 'unixTime': 1313478000, 'question': 'Fitting carseats into our car for 20 hour drive. What carseat(s) would be best in order to fit the three youngest in one row of seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm sure you've already taken your trip, but here's what I think, in case it helps someone else. I assume you'll have the 2 year old rearfacing, especially since you're traveling at what I assume will be highway speeds. I would put them on one side of the back row in a Britax Boulevard or Advocate. It depends how big your 6 year old is, but probably something like a Graco Nautilus on the other side of the back seat. The 8 year old can be in a low back booster in the middle of the back seat and you should be able to access both side seats still. The 12 and 14 year old don't need boosters anymore and can go in the captains chairs, but could also switch out with the 8 year old. Hope this helps someone."}
