{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIQ2', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2011', 'unixTime': 1318834800, 'question': 'Why is there an Onyx I and Onyx II (or old and new)? Anyone know what that means?', 'answer': 'I called Britax to ask the same question. They said they are exactly the same seat, but they are using a new manufacturer to make some of their parts. The parts are the same, the seat is the same, and one seat is not older than another (she said they could have been manufactured just days apart even). She said it is confusing that it is listed here as an older model and a newer model, but that is not the case and there have been no changes to the seat, so there\'s no reason not to order the "older model". Hope this helps. I just bought the Onyx.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIQ2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394780400, 'question': 'my kid is using this model 70-CS. I am thinking of buying another advocate to put in another car. Is the latest variant G4? what is the difference ?', 'answer': 'The basic difference is the infant position pad, and the belly pad. The shell is the same, the harness is the same, and the installation is the same.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIQ2', 'answerTime': 'Jul 30, 2011', 'unixTime': 1312009200, 'question': 'Advocate 70 vs Frontier 85 for short toddler', 'answer': "I have both...I have a 6 year old, a 3 year old and a 6 month old. I purchased the newer frontiers for my oldest children and an advocate for my youngest because he's heavy and I knew he would outgrow his infant carrier a lot sooner than expected. I noticed that my 3 year old was struggling to sleep in her frontier on a 12 hour car ride so we pulled over and gave her the advocate and placed my then 4 month old back into his infant carrier and base (luckily it was still in the back of my van) and she passed out within minutes. I find the smaller children still aren't ready to nap in the frontier without looking completely uncomfortable and leaning forward constantly...I've seen purchased another advocate for my son since his sister took his. Hope that helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIQ2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': 'will this fit rear facing in a 2014 ford focus', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I am sorry. I am unsure. We never used it as a rear facing seat and we have a honda accord so I am not sure if it would fit in a focus.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIQ2', 'answerTime': 'Nov 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383638400, 'question': 'Any one knows the size of the box that was used to ship this car seat?', 'answer': "Don't remember the exact size but very large because of the size of the car seat. No assembly required. So, the box is at minimum the height, width and depth of the car seat."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIQ2', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375772400, 'question': 'subaru', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIQ2', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2012', 'unixTime': 1348383600, 'question': "Click &amp; Safe Snug Harness doesn't seem to work... Is this car seat broken?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it is broken.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIQ2', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2011', 'unixTime': 1321603200, 'question': 'Anyone use it instead of an infant car seat? Has anyone done this and what has your experience been?', 'answer': 'I used Britax convertibles with both of my kids from birth just because infant seats are not safe! They were fine and my children were not big(my daughter was 6lbs 11oz and my son came home 4lbs 12oz-he was 3lbs7oz at birth). We have the new advocate for the upcoming baby ;-) The advocate even has an "infant insert" that can be purchased to improve the fit. Yes, they look small in the seat, but it does not affect the safety of the seat-at all. Think about this, a piece of plastic that goes through constant stress of in and out of the car(we have a materials engineer in the family and he was very adamant about it not being safe-too much stress on plastic). The studies about this have been buried time and time again, but there is some evidence if you search the net. Unfortunately, we were hit by a drunk driver when my daughter was only 4 mos, she was just fine in her Britax seat! When my son was 9 mos, our Corolla was sideswiped by a semi-truck, both kids were fine(they slept through it), my son in his convertible, my daughter in her Britax booster. We drive A LOT(40k miles a year) and I have never felt uncomfortable with the convertibles from birth and after our second accident we were told by the investigating officer that the Britax saved my son major injuries! I think you will be just fine going with the convertible from day one, we were and ours were "tested."'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWILW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 11, 2011', 'unixTime': 1307775600, 'question': 'Do new Britax carseats (August 2010 models) fit on airplanes? Has anyone tried installing any of the new Britax carseats (Marathon 70, Boulevard 70, or Boulevard 70 CS) on an airplane, rear-facing or front-facing?', 'answer': "Actually, only some airlines have that policy. Though I have found if you ask nicely and explain that you need a little time to put the carseat in and don't want to block the other passengers, some staff will let you even if it isn't their policy. However, some folks take it as a personal affront, which I don't really understand."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWILW', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2012', 'unixTime': 1330329600, 'question': 'will this fit rear-facing in a 2002 vw jetta? anyone know?', 'answer': "Did you ever find out if it fits? I'm looking at getting it for my 09 Jetta."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWILW', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2011', 'unixTime': 1317625200, 'question': 'How is the Britax Blvd 70 for newborns?', 'answer': "The new Blvd has an infant insert you can purchase through Britax that makes it an acceptable fit for larger newborns but the average to smaller newborns still won't fit even with the insert. Their top harness slots are just too high for most newborns since the slots need to be at or below for rear facing. The Scenera, True Fit, MyRide65, Triumph65, Cocorro and a couple others fit newborns well."}
