{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIKS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2011', 'unixTime': 1300777200, 'question': 'Does Britax Marathon fits in your Honda Civic? Does anyone has Marathon in your Civic?', 'answer': "This is a little late but I just saw your post. Yes this will fit in a civic, I'm actually going to purchase one today for ours. www.car-seat.org is a great place to search the forums to see others' experiences with seats (and you can usually find pictures too)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIKS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2011', 'unixTime': 1303887600, 'question': 'Is Cowmooflage cover too hot for the South?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Crimson, Allison and Cow are velvety. Blueprint and Onix are smooth, almost satiny. Waverly is smooth, but a little more "rough. Jet Set is very rough, so I absolutely hated touching it in the store. I was considering Crimson, but thought of our hot GA summers and will now get Blueprint or Onix. By the way, even though Babies\'R\'Us does not have seats in all of the fabrics, they have swatches so you can touch them and judge for yourself. :) Buy-Buy Baby has seats in most of the fabrics.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIKS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2011', 'unixTime': 1300172400, 'question': 'Harness adjustment on Britax Marathon 70 Convertible Car Seat: Can anyone tell me how the harness straps are re-adjusted for this carseat.', 'answer': 'Hi Carrie, I measured the backseat of my outback. It measures approx 50 inches across. I hope this helps with determining if the marathon will be too big for your forester. The marathon fits great in my outback. I\'m 5\'4" and my hubby is average height and we don\'t have a problem with not being able to sit comfortably in the front. Good luck!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003OUWIKS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357027200, 'question': 'Is it small', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No, it\'s quite large. We have a Mazda 3 and we have to push the seat all the way to the front. But it "is designed for children rear facing from 5 to 40 pounds and forward facing up to 70 pounds." It really covers baby and toddler years.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIKS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 29, 2011', 'unixTime': 1311922800, 'question': 'Reclining Rear facing: Does anyone know if this seat reclines well in the rear facing position?', 'answer': 'You can use pool noodles to increase the incline to closer to 45 degrees. I would contact a local car seat safety inspector to help you with this.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003OUWIKS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 7, 2011', 'unixTime': 1315378800, 'question': '2009 Honda Civic Si fit? Does this fit in a Honda Civic Si?', 'answer': "We currently have the Britax Marathon 70 in a 2008 Honda Civic LX Sedan. We previously had the same car seat* in a 2004 Civic LX Coupe. It fit just fine in both, even with the front seat adjusted all the way back. The difference in the trim/option packages (LX vs. Si) won't affect whether the car seat fits at all. And the body did not change from 2008 to 2009, so that shouldn't affect anything either. I'm very confident it will fit. It wasn't all that easy getting our daughter in and out of the coupe (2 doors), but that's going to be the case with any car seat. After doing that for awhile, the sedan (4 doors) is a pleasure. By the way, we were rear-ended pretty hard (we were stopped waiting to make a left-hand turn) with this our daughter in this car seat in the 2004 Civic. The trunk was crumpled too close to the back seat for my comfort. And yet my daughter was completely protected. I'm 100% sold on the Civic/Marathon combination. *ETA: Not the exact same car seat. We replaced it with the same model and disposed of the seat that was in the accident."}
