{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003SWZVG0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395212400, 'question': 'We have had this thing for a couple of years now, how does it dispense soap???', 'answer': 'Hi John, Sassy has several models of these soft rubber bottle scrubbers and the picture of yours shows it is not the one I own. Basically they all fill with soap from the end of the handle. The fill spot in the handle will either pop out like a stopper or screw off like a bottle cap. If you look at the center bottom of the scrubber you will see a hole where the soap will be dispensed during use via an unseen membrane that activates when pressed the scrubber end against the bottom of the bottle or jar you are cleaning. If the membrane inside the hole goes bad or you do not tighten the handle fill plug correctly the soap will just run out of the bottom and be lost. I always hold a finger gently against the bottom hole when filling to assure soap doesn\'t flow through for lack of a vacuum. If you have put soap in the handle and it is not flowing then the hole at the bottom may be "clogged" so try using toothpich with point cut off to clear it--be gentle and do not push so hard inside as to puncture that membrane just beyond the hole. If you have had your brush two years that membrane in the bottom may be a "crispy critter" by now and may not work correctly but give it a try anyway and see. Hope this helps.--- Dixie'}
