{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003TJAGB2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402556400, 'question': 'Do these work with the standard size AVENT pumps? I tried to order other valves on here but all i got was the ones for the comfort pumps.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Unfortunately these will not work on the Avent ISIS IQ (classic and not new "comfort") breast pump. The Avent plastic trumpet has a hole that the Avent duck bill valve presses into, the valve having a collar that protrudes into the hole. The Ameda valves appear to fit over a collar as they have nothing that protrudes from them that would fit up into the hole on the AVENT trumpet piece. I was bummed these didn\'t work, the AVENT ones are very hard to find now. You can get them direct from Philips but the price is outrageous and they are sold each valve. Sad.'}
