{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003TPNV1S', 'answerTime': 'Oct 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381215600, 'question': "what is the height of the mattress when it's set up? We have a low platform bed so I'm not sure if this is too high.", 'answer': 'You can\'t tell from the picture but the legs are adjustable - when at the lowest point the baby would be about 19 inches from the floor and if fully extended about 8 inches higher. The legs have 4 sections they can extend - with about 2 inches between each section. The product description on Amazon says you have to buy the leg extension kit separately. That has to be wrong because this model has caster wheels so I don\'t see how the extension kit would work with this. The Arms Reach website says this, "**For bed heights starting at 24", measured from the floor to the top of the adult mattress." Although their website doesn\'t mention that it is adjustable which is strange. But trust me unless they changed it within the past 8 months I have mine extended all the way because my bed is high.'}
