{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003TRZIGW', 'answerTime': 'Nov 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416470400, 'question': 'How much do the seats recline? Enough to put tiny babies in them? We had premature twins.', 'answer': "the seats don't necessarily recline. There is a clasp behind the seats (similar to a seat belt) where when you unclasp, the canvas seats give and drop down an extra 2 inches or so. I purchased the stroller when the twins were 8 months and it's perfect for every day use, and they are big enough so that their head hits the top of the seat that gives and it gives enough for them to nap - the clasp part is closer to the top - if twins are newborns and tiny - they may not be tall enough to hit the area that gives. you may need to wait a few months. Hope this helps."}
