{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003VNKLIY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'If setting it up like the picture shown with the fire place, is there another way to mount it besides it being permanent?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "When you mount it, you attach it to the walls with screws so you can always take it down and reuse it. You can also take the gate down but leave the wall mount in the wall if you want to temporarily take the gate down but put it back up later (like if you want to light a fire etc). Just a side note: the screws they supply are useless so you'll need to get longer ones if you are looking to use the wall mount."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VNKLIY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389945600, 'question': 'We are looking for something like this for a church nursery. If 2 were bought would there be enough room for about 10 children and toys?', 'answer': 'It probably depends on the numbers of toys. I suggest thinking of it in terms of your space. I did the math, if you made a square with it, you would have 7.7 ft sides and 58 square feet - pretty big - but probably not for 10 kids. That is like putting 10 kids in a dorm room. Still, put some tape on the floor in the shape you want to find out for yourself. Segments are roughly 23 long - you would have 16.'}
