{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003VNKLIY', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': 'will it handle chilren shaking the fence', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We have ours stretched out as a fence with half of it straight and half zig-zagged, crossing a room, anchored to two walls. Our 19-mo-old son REALLY likes to grab it in the middle with both fists and shove it back and forth. A lot. With his whole bodyweight. It slides back and forth across the Berber carpet, because the plastic-toothed joints aren't industrial quality and do have some give to them in the middle of the fence no matter how you tighten them, when it's stretched out like this. However, having him treat it like that for a few months, now, doesn't seem to have worn or bent anything yet (I just keep having to reposition and tighten the fence every few days)..."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003VNKLIY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390377600, 'question': 'Has anyone used this for a medium size dog?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I\'ve been using this for our Doberman puppy who is currently 5 months old, weighing 42 lbs. I\'ve currently opened it up and used it to corner off part of my office with a whelping pad on the floor to protect the carpet. She can actually jump it, though if I keep the "no-no" bottle nearby, she tends to stay in her playpen better. I think even a small dog could eventually figure out how to jump it, though. Overall, I\'m still very happy with this purchase. I just can\'t use it to pen her up when I leave the room.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VNKLIY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413529200, 'question': 'easy to open', 'answer': 'Yes & there is a sliding lock on the latch to make it childproof'}
