{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VNKLI4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392192000, 'question': 'What is the height, from the floor to the top rail of gate, after the gate has been installed?', 'answer': '30.5 inches from floor to top of gate. BUT, it depends on how you attach it to wall. My husband did it almost flush with floor. There is a middle knob that twists and provides support. This can be twisted to provide more middle support and can touch or not touch the floor. We keep it off the floor but still providing support on transitions because it scratches as you open it. We could just add some felt, but never did.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VNKLI4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386489600, 'question': 'How does it attach to the wall? I need to attach to wall and banister?', 'answer': "Three bolts into the wall, wrap around latches to the banister. We decided to use heavy duty zip ties instead, because the plastic didn't seem super secure."}
