{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VNKLI4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427180400, 'question': 'Can this be mounted between two 1" metal banisters (no wall)? if not, what can?', 'answer': "It's hard to say. You might be able to make it work with the material provided. The problem is u have 2 sets of rubber brackets and Velcro for the 4x4 square part of the post and 2 round kits for the round part of wooden banister. They also is a complete kit to wall mount it which could be used around the metal banister. I think u might be able to do it with using some of the pieces in the mounting kit the more I think about it. I like it!!!! I suggest checking the Amazon return policy on it prior to purchasing. We bought 2. 1 from Amazon and the first one from wal Mary because if it didn't work we could just take it back to wal mart. Of all the ones I looked at, this one seemed to me to be the nicest and cleanest to mount. Hope that helps. You could make it work I think. But again make sure you can return it if it doesn't Good luck"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VNKLI4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424505600, 'question': 'I have a huge banister (6" x 6"). Do you think it will fit around? Or, if not, is it possible to rig it with extra velcro? Thanks!', 'answer': 'It will not fit all the way around, no. If the Bannister is perfectly round shaped you could probably find a way to attach it using Velcro/zip ties/whatever. Then it comes to personal preference and your ability/willingness to diy a product that you paid money for to do a specific job.'}
