{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VNKLIE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425369600, 'question': 'How easy is this to install/unintall? We only need it when the grandbaby comes to visit.', 'answer': "If you have a banister on both sides or handy stud in the wall it will be fairly easy. If you don't have anything solid to mount the gate to on the wall side it will not be easy as the weight of the gate will eventually break any drywall mounting methods loose after awhile. I rated this fate low due to the clumsy closing method which requires two hands and some fiddling to close. If you only need to open it occasionally you will probably be happy with the gate."}
