{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003XT43MG', 'answerTime': 'Sep 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411542000, 'question': 'Anyone been using the Toddler side for a while and has it held up well? Still recommend this mattress?', 'answer': 'I would recommend this mattress. We got this for our \\7 month old who was having trouble sleeping in her crib. We noticed that she fell asleep on our bed very quickly, but not in her crib. We figured that the mattress we had was not comfortable for her. It is an older mattress. We purchased this mattress for ability to have something more comfortable now and into the future. I did notice a slight difference in the two sides. We put the infant side up for our little one. She fell asleep the first night no problem. It seemed to make a big difference.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XT43MG', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409900400, 'question': 'I am looking for a mattress that does not contain harmful ingredients for the baby to breathe. I find myself very confused! Is this choice best?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'This is the best option I could find. No PVC, lead, etc. Some mattresses say "soy" but if you investigate, they only contain soy, like 1% of the total mattress. I\'m so glad we got this mattress. It was worth the extra money (Mother in law bought it as a shower gift) to have something safe next to my baby\'s nose/mouth for over 12 hours a day. It also has square corners, so no/less risk of him/her stepping into a hole in the corner of the crib created by round corner mattresses. It really has a feel of quality to it vs. other mattresses I\'ve worked with and seen at the store.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XT43MG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415865600, 'question': 'Does the mattress fits AFG Nadia crib 3 in 1 ?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'this mattress is a standard size, regular size crib mattress. I think the dimensions are 27" x 52". If the crib you are speaking of is a normal size crib and it states that it takes a full size, regular crib mattress, it should fit.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003XT43MG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393488000, 'question': 'Does this mattress fit well with the Westwood Waverly Cottage Crib?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have the Westwood Stratton Convertible Crib. This mattress fits very snugly in it. I do feel like I have to "squeeze" the mattress in just a little bit, but it fits well and you won\'t find any gap (except just a little at the corners, after all, who makes exactly square corner mattress!) between the mattress and the crib, which is a good thing.'}
