{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003YVHXAW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'We have old wiring with only 2 pronged plugs. We use adapters for 3 pronged plugs. These protrude quite a bit from the wall. Will thesefit under this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'There are about 2" of clearance inside the unit to give you an idea. I think it will depend on how stiff the cord you\'re plugging into the adapter is. For example, a typical lamp cord is pretty flexible and I would guess will fit fine with a typical adapter. However, a stiff, straight plug like those found in a lot of surge protectors definitely will not fit with an adapter.'}
