{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041EDZBW', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': "Could you get this off in an emergency if you didn't have a key or other slim item to push the button through the grates?", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'NO! I use mine guard when I am driving with my one child which is only short trips---school and back. It does not fit my 2012 Camry, but does my 2000 Ford SUV. When we go on longer trips, it is with other people who can help make sure that my child does not undo the seat belt. It was great with teaching my child when to undo the seat belt and when no too. I am not ready to go cold turkey yet, but think we will not need it soon.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041EDZBW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'Is the guard breakable? My son has had a number of buckle guards and he just snaps them and breaks them off.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I'm sure it could break, is made of plastic, but we have had no issues so far and have used it daily for about 2 mos. now."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041EDZBW', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424851200, 'question': 'Does this fit the 2014 Nissan Sentra ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "it fits any standard buckle clasp. if your child still can or will wiggle out from being seatbelted, this won't help. if they'll stay buckled though, it will keep them from being able to unbuckle"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041EDZBW', 'answerTime': 'Nov 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416038400, 'question': 'Does this product work with a Toyota Sienna van?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not positive, but feel it should work on any seat belt with the release button on top next to the slot. We have a Santa Fe and does work on his transportation vans. Thinking they may be Dodge Caravans, definitely on Fords & Mercedes. Sorry I couldn't have been of more help."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041EDZBW', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410937200, 'question': 'Has anyone used this successfully in a 2011 Honda Odyssey?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't think the make of the vehicle matters for this buckle. I purchased it for a client who drives a older model Nissan Altima. I've also seen other clients use the same buckle in Dodge Vans, Ford wangons, and Nissan Rogues."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0041EDZBW', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404543600, 'question': 'Does this stay on even when the seat belt is unbuckled? Or do you have to take it on/off each time your child is in/out of the car?', 'answer': "It's held in place by the seat belt - so yes, it would come off each time you unbuckle the seat belt. We used it to keep my grandson from unbuckling his car seat (5 point harness type)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041EDZBW', 'answerTime': 'Dec 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387872000, 'question': 'We have a 2010 Lexus GX 460 SUV, will this fit properly on our seat belts? I need one to keep our 72# lab safely buckled.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I drive a Honda, so I couldn\'t say for sure. As shown in the photo, it is slightly larger than the buckle. So if seat belts aren\'t all a standard size, it would accommodate a larger one than mine. Good luck. (works with my four year old. So unless you have one of those "My lab is smarter than your honor student" dogs, it should work for you!)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041F2CFQ', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406530800, 'question': 'Is there a weight limit on the joey toddler seat? All I can find is "for children of all ages".', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The seat says max weight in Joey seat is 44lbs. Hope that helps! We have loved it for our three kids ages, 3,2 and 10 months.'}
