{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041FI7BY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401778800, 'question': 'would a fisher price tub fit in this stand?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The only tub I found that fits it calls "the first years" wasn\'t easy to find one. Also I had to wrap both sides because the bath slides over it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041IYOFY', 'answerTime': 'May 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1369897200, 'question': 'Does this support forward facing?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "It does not. It does hip, back, and facing the chest. I will tell you that I got a ton of guff for facing my son forward. Everyone told me it wasn't good for his hips, it would over stimulate him, etc. and so on. This irritated me because he loved facing out. I worried he would hate this carrier. Well he loves this thing to bits and it has been a lifesaver! I'll tell you exactly why, for one he falls asleep in this thing almost every time which is awesome, it's crazy easy to nurse in it and no one even knows you're doing it, and the biggest reason is how incredibly comfortable this is. I've hiked several miles and honestly it doesn't even feel like I'm carrying him. The Beco Gemini carrier does allow you to face your baby forward but it doesn't have the hood or the handy pocket. Those I know that have the Beco hardly ever use it for forward facing but at least there's the option. All that being said I am completely in love with the Ergo baby. Just make sure you get it from a certified supplier. I got a fake the first time. Read my review on here for the names of the certified suppliers. Good luck!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0041IYOFY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373439600, 'question': 'Up to what height child does this work well for?', 'answer': 'it\'s more is based in the eight, according to the manufacturer the range is between 7*-45 lb. My baby girl is actually 1\'11" and works great.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0041IYOFY', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': 'How many grams of EVA foam does this "ERGObaby Organic Baby Carrier" contain? Is it made with any other non-organic components?', 'answer': 'The snaps are metal but they are not organic metal. That technology has yet to be created. In Terminator 2 even the T100 was made of organic organism over metal endoskeleton.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041JVBXG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359360000, 'question': 'Will this fit into my trunk easily? I have a 4 door sedan.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It will probably take about half your trunk but I am pretty sure it will fit unless you have a really tiny trunk. My guess is you could slide it in wheels first and it will go in and out easily. I drive a minivan and stand it up in the back in the folded position. It has made our life sooo much easier. Our almost two year old loves it! I can take it into a store and he will take a nap in it. We will NEVER go back to one of the tiny strollers.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0041JVBXG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 19, 2012', 'unixTime': 1353312000, 'question': 'does the seat allow the baby to sit straight upright?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes! About 70 degrees'}
