{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00423A60U', 'answerTime': 'Jul 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374822000, 'question': "Does the elephant attach to the crib? In the description it doesn't say the elephant does, but the frog description says it attaches to the side.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'We got the butterfly. It just sets on the dresser or travels if one of the twins carries it. These are really very cute and are very calming to children. They put off a soft light which gently illuminates the room then turns off after a period of time. My granddaughters are 2 years old now and still love to go to sleep with their butterfly on. It is bedtime routine to turn it on as they are being dressed for bed and they dance to the music. It settles them right away when they are in their cribs - even at nap time.'}
