{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0042D69XS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397113200, 'question': 'Do I need to buy a bouncer, a sleeper and a swing? or if i bought one of those will replace the other? if so, wich?', 'answer': 'I have a bouncer, bassinet and a swing and we use all of them on a daily basis. Its not recommended for the baby to sleep in the seat or the swing. The bouncer seat was a god send because it was the only thing that calmed my colicky baby. I took off the toy bar and did big bounces to calm him down and even put him to sleep. The toy bar is great for entertaining for 10 minutes while you shower or wash dishes. I would recommend the bouncer over a swing, but the swing does pacify for a longer time than the bouncer.'}
