{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0042D69WO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2012', 'unixTime': 1354435200, 'question': 'What are song titles of the eight lullabies?', 'answer': '"Beautiful Dreamer", "Twinkle, Twinkle Little Star", "Pachabel\'s Canon", "Hush Little Baby", "Jesu Man of Joys Desiring", "London Bridge is Falling Down"...these are the song titles I am sure about, there is also one Mozart sonata but I can\'t remember what number it is (I only know this because I trained classical piano for 12 years), and the eighth song is driving me crazy because I know what it is I just can\'t think of the name, which means you\'ll probably recognize it too...lol...it\'s a little reminiscent of "Somewhere Out There" from American Tale but not quite it...the sound quality reminds me of a synthesizer and all the songs are uniquely arranged with a little classical deviation...it\'s very nice not hearing the regular toy box tinny versions over and over...in fact, it takes a moment to recognize the songs because of the arrangements... You will be very happy if you choose to purchase this swing. Hope this helps :0)'}
