{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0042D69V0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388217600, 'question': 'how should the feet be, while they are using it? using only the toes or using the complete foot?', 'answer': 'As a pediatric physical therapist, I would say make sure there whole foot touches the floor. Think about when you jump. Do you just jump off your toes or do you use your whole foot? If just toes are touching, this could cause toe walking which could lead achilles tendon tightening.'}
