{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0042RU2SW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425970800, 'question': 'How does this compare to the other Skip Hop Activity Gyms? Why would you choose one above the other? Thx', 'answer': 'a great play gym -- 4 month old has been using it at various levels for a month now (at this point, grabbing toys and rolling over). Soft and cute, attention keeping for baby. I bought this for my daughter as a gift (baby\'s mother). For Grandma\'s house I have the Fisher Price with lights and music (baby likes nature sounds). Both are great -- one "no-tech", the other mildly stimulating with sounds and soft lights. Really just depends on what you like... I thought the Skip Hop was little pricey, but baby does love it and it is well-made (toys on this are super-cute, and soft. Mostly hard plastic on the Fisher Price one). Hope this helps!'}
