{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0043YVL7U', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390982400, 'question': 'Can you use a car seat with this stroller and/or does it take an adapter?', 'answer': "Yes almost all car seats will fit in this. It comes with straps in little pockets on the sides that you use to buckle the car seat to the stroller. Then you just tuck the straps back in when you're not using it! Works great."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'Is the Jovvy Ergo trail worthy and airport useful?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Not a great choice for either I would say... its not an offroad stroller, and its simply too large to be reasonable at a busy airport. I wont lie, this sucker is heavy and long. I would take measurements of your vehicle before you buy because it wont fit in some. That said for things like zoo days or parks with sidewalks, we absolutely love it. Our 4 year has some physical limitations and the back seat allows her easy in and out and lets her feel like a big kid without being strapped into a traditional mobility stroller. I completely endorse it, but you need to be aware this is probably not an every day kind of stroller.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378710000, 'question': 'Trying to decide between this and greyco ready to grow sit&amp; stand does any one have a comparison? Is a britax b safe carseat compatible with either?', 'answer': 'I have a britax carseat and it fits on the joovy. I love this double stroller but know nothing about the greyco. This one worked best for me because my son who is about to turn 3 is very tall for his age and he has plenty of room in the front seat.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398841200, 'question': 'Trying to decide between ergo caboose &amp; caboose too ultralight stroller. I have a chicco keyfit22 carseat. Which one will be a better choice?', 'answer': 'When we demoed these at a shop the ultralight is longer and when folded would be difficult to fit in the car due to the length. The ergo is much heavier, but it feels sturdier and is a bit easier to control. It also folds down to a more reasonable size to fit in the car.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426834800, 'question': 'Can I convert this stroller into a single stroller, if I would like? Not always I have my two son with me.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No. It's always a sit/stand stroller. The second seat in the back is just a little bench seat so it's kind of like 1.5 stroller since it's doesn't have a full second seat. There are videos by different moms on YouTube that show how this stroller is configured."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385539200, 'question': 'I will have a newborn and tall (40") 3.5 yr old...Will the front seat fit a taller child? Most of the ones I have looked at will not...', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The front seat is great for tall children! My 45 inches tall 5 year old still fits.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Aug 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407567600, 'question': 'can i add a seat in the back if my 2nd child wants to sit?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You can but the cushion costs extra and beware, the buckles snap and break easily with open and close of the stroller.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429081200, 'question': 'Is it possible to by a replacement shade for the part of the stroller where the toddler stands?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hello, Please call Joovy's Customer Care Center at (877) 456 5049 to check for availability on this part. Thanks!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426834800, 'question': 'Super confused on joovy ergo and contours double stroller? I am targeting for compact stroller between. Which one requires less space opened?Compact.', 'answer': "I'm unsure as I've only owned the Joovy Ergo Tandem stroller, not the Contours. But in looking at the dimensions, it seems like the Contours might be just a little smaller. The other thing is that the Joovy Ergo does not stand on its own when folded. I'm not sure if that matters to you. I think there's a relatively new stroller out there called the Kinderwagon Hop Tandem Stroller. They are supposed to be much smaller and lighter, but not sure what you'd give up for the smaller size. Overall, i really liked the Joovy. Just keep in mind that all tandems are big and heavy, no matter what they say. Maybe except for the Kinderwagon, but I've never used it. Finally, Joovy's customer service is fantastic. You can always speak to a person, not a machine, and they've sent me spare parts for free when I was the one who lost them. They're a really great company. I wish I could buy more stuff from them, but my kids are now too old!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426834800, 'question': 'super confused on ergo and contours double stroller? I am targeting for compact stroller between. Which one requires less space en opened? Compact.', 'answer': "I would not consider this strollers compact in it's opened or closed form. It's quite large."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0043YVTPY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422172800, 'question': 'what infant car seats are compatible with the ergo joovy?', 'answer': "A lot of different ones. I have Graco and it fits just fine. How it works is the infant car seat sits on a strap, then there's a buckle that keeps it secured. I really like this brand... We are actually upgrading to their triple stroller."}
