{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7I1O', 'answerTime': 'Nov 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383984000, 'question': 'How does the wood hold hold up after many time of cleaning?', 'answer': "I've had the high chair for over a year and a half and it still looks great. I got the lighter maple-ish colored chair. The wood for the foot rest has some wear streaks in it, but not in a tacky ugly way. My son liked to naw on the top back of the chair when he was teething, so there are some teeth lines in it, but the color didn't change and the stain did not chip off, which was great! He likes to climb the back and front and it hasn't tipped over or wobbled yet. He also likes to wave through the holes in the back and peak toys through them. Lots of good entertainment from this chair. It has definitely stood up to the abuse of an active toddler and I am very happy with the purchase even after a year and a half."}
