{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7G8E', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'The description says "made in USA" but Amazon lists the country of origin as Taiwan. Which is it for real??', 'answer': 'My highchair says it is from New York. So that is all I know. Except that it is a WONDERFUL piece of furniture and I Highly recommend it. Just be sure you look on line for the instructions as to installing the seat insert.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044R7G8E', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423036800, 'question': 'Is there a 5-point restraint with the infant insert?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Ours just has a 3 point restraint with the infant seat, but it's never been an issue. If it helps, the tray sits low (compared to the other chair we have) and she'd have a hard time getting her legs out even if the restraint were to fail. We don't leave her unattended or put the chair close to things she can pull or push on for leverage."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044R7G8E', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': 'Is the chair foldable?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No. It does not fold, but it is light and easy to move. My family moves between two homes and we take this chair with us. It's lasted through two kids and am going on the third! It's held up well and still looks about new!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044R7G8E', 'answerTime': 'Apr 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398236400, 'question': 'Thinking of buying one off Craigslist, it has the wood tray but not the plastic tray topper, can you purchase the plastic tray separately? Thanks!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you can't find the plastic part, you can use the wooden part without the plastic. It is more difficult to remove, but you will need to remove it to get your child in and out safely anyway. We quit using the plastic part as soon as our child became interested in removing it herself, because it snaps on very tightly to keep food out, and can pinch little fingers. The chair is designed to push under your table and can also be used without the tray, which you will not be using for the life of the chair but only for about 2 years. The original chair comes with parts that go on the sides to replace the brackets that hold the tray in. If you are buying used, be sure that you are getting these parts as well."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7G8E', 'answerTime': 'Aug 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376809200, 'question': 'Does the chair with the infant insert also come with the toddler cushion or do you buy something else for that?', 'answer': "It doesn't come with the toddler cushion, but I've found they don't need it. I have 2 chairs - got one for my 8 month old and 2.5 year old. It's been great."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7G8E', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373007600, 'question': 'Do you take the tray on and off for convenience? Can you just slide the kid in with the tray in place?', 'answer': "If you have the insert (which you need unless your kid is really big or 2+) then yeah you have to take it off. It's very easy, even if you have a baby in one hand. We love it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389859200, 'question': 'Can you take the bar off between the legs and still use the tray?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you can.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Jun 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372489200, 'question': 'Do you need to have the infant insert to use this with a 6 month old?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Not if they already can sit up relatively well. But it is kind of a slouchy chair, even for older and bigger kids. We sometimes stuffed a folded up blanket down behind my son's back to help with that."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379401200, 'question': 'What is the maximum seat height? We need a chair high enough to scoot up to the kitchen island.', 'answer': 'We have seat on highest position for 2 yr old and it is perfect for a regular height table. Dont think it would work for counter height'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383289200, 'question': 'Is it appropriate for a growing 6 yr old? Will the tray adjust to for use with a growing 6 yr old?', 'answer': "yes it would work for a 6 year old ... I personally think it could work for an 11 or 12 year old or older to be honest... I do believe this is the last chair I will ever buy for my child.. She is 5 now and we haven't even adjusted it once yet... There are a bunch of grooves to adjust the seat to so if your child is 6 I think you are VERY safe.. (I asked my son, he is 7+, to try it and he was very comfortable in it..)...Good luck..."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416643200, 'question': 'Could a toddler climb up and sit themselves in this chair?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'May 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399100400, 'question': 'Anybody know if you can buy replacement straps?', 'answer': "I had a problem with the straps and emailed Keekaroo directly (http://www.keekaroo.com/). The chair was new so they sent me straps free of charge right away. I would think if your chair isn't under warranty (which is 5 years) you could buy the straps from them."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Apr 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398063600, 'question': 'Can you remove the padding on the chair to wash it?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes you can. The padding velcro's to the chair and is easily removed. I haven't tried putting it in the washing machine, but I have hand washed it in the sink and then dried it in the dryer on low. It's also pretty easy to wipe/scrub while still on the chair after meals and dries in an hour or so."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Apr 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397977200, 'question': 'How many inches from the floor to the tray? thanks!', 'answer': "I wish I could give you a good answer but we have not used a tray. The chair is used by my 3 year old G'Son by sliding it directly up to the table. Works very good! Very good product ."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388476800, 'question': 'What is the max height/weight that one can use the tray with their child. Looking for my 3.5 year old who is 36 inches and 29 pounds', 'answer': "I don't see a 3 year old using this high chair with the tray."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044R7I00', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385193600, 'question': "does this high chair fold easily for storage....grandma's useage", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No, this chair doesn't fold up at all. One needs tools to put it together and take it apart and it has a pretty large profile. It wouldn't be my choice if one wanted to store it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00451ACV2', 'answerTime': 'Sep 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379746800, 'question': 'Can you remove the top changer? Or is it one piece?', 'answer': 'It is one piece and secured with screws. You cannot detach and put back the top changer if that is what you are asking. So if you are looking to use the top changer as a separate unit, that will not be possible with this design. However, if you are looking to make this just a flat top chest-of-drawers like furniture, then the 4-side flanks of the top changer can be taken out by making appropriate alterations to Assembly Steps 8 and 12 (in the assembly manual) and you will need to procure 4 separate screws to secure the side boards to the top one.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00451ACV2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372489200, 'question': 'assembly instructions', 'answer': 'The assembly wasnt difficult, however, after we assembled it it was very flemsie and we had to buy brackets to sturdy it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00451ACV2', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'What size changing pad works with it? Can I use a standard size changing pad or is it smaller?', 'answer': 'We ordered the Summer infant contoured changing pad. Dimension 32.5 x 16.5 x 4 inches'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00451ACV2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423296000, 'question': 'What is the height/depth of the shelf?', 'answer': '35.5 x 19.5 x 39.2 inches This is really a good changing table. My son loves it. But the drawer is too small.'}
