{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395471600, 'question': 'Are there any fire retardants used in this chair?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The seat liner states that it meets all flammability requirements for California Bureau of Home Furnishings Technical Bulletins 117. And "Care should be exercised near open flame or with burning cigarettes".'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'May 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400828400, 'question': 'Is there a smaller permanent tray under the large removable tray?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'There is a removable tray, almost the same size as the permanent slide out tray. It is the removable tray that fits in the dishwasher. Once the removable tray is removed you can attach the toy to the permanent tray. It works very nicely!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Sep 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411542000, 'question': 'Hi! I just wanted to know what color is the dishwasher safe removable tray? Thanks!', 'answer': "It's a cream beige color"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Jul 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404284400, 'question': 'Do the wheels have breaks?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, they do, all 4 wheels have independent brakes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428303600, 'question': 'Hi! I just wanna know the mesures W x L X D of the product, not the product box the mesures of the high chair. Thanks in advance.', 'answer': 'look under: "Product Information" "Technical Details" and you will find that it says "44 x 34 x 23 inches". I don\'t know anyone who would have listed the measurements of the box. The high chair comes in pieces...'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410505200, 'question': 'My baby is 6 months old and he is a little chunky, for how long will the baby be comfortable in this chair? Any help from moms with chubby babies?', 'answer': "I am going to buy this one, I had an older version of a Fisher Price highchair and I put my kids in it until they didn't want to sit in it, about 18 months-2 years. My twins were/are skinny but my singleton was a Chuuuuunky Monkey. You are safe with this. (and for the record I will only buy Fisher Price highchairs, the crotch notch that is actually attached to the chair makes a world of difference and you don't have to use the buckles later on and they won't slide out)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Nov 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383811200, 'question': 'for what age is it made?', 'answer': "My granddaughter has been in it since about 6 months and she's 1 now. Her brother had the same chair and he sat in it until age 3. He still fit in the chair but he felt like he was a big boy and wanted to sit at the table in a chair like the rest of the family."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'Could you tell me the cover is made of cloth or nylon?', 'answer': 'cloth : ( that is the only downside to this highchair!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388563200, 'question': "Hi, what's the difference between your Rainforest Healthy Care High Chair and Precious Planet Sky Blue High Chair?", 'answer': "We started out with the Precious Planet chair and returned it. It isn't made anywhere near as well as the Rainforest. There was hardly any adjustment in the straps that you secure the baby with therefore if your child was small they were just kinda flopping around. Also, the back of the Precious Planet chair, and this may have just been our chair, kept on slipping out of adjustment. If your child decided to lean back in the chair it would slip out of gear and go into an almost laying down position. The Precious Planet was very cute but the con's far outweighed the pro's"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045JKUU2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426230000, 'question': 'The rainforest high chair has a seatbelt like a carset for infant I want to use it for my 4 month old baby please reply.Thanks,', 'answer': 'I\'m not sure what you mean by a "seatbelt like a carset" other than I\'m taking it to mean it has the shoulder and leg fasteners? I don\'t actually use the shoulder parts as my son likes to reach forward and for a high chair I never thought it was necessary.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045K616S', 'answerTime': 'Aug 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376031600, 'question': 'What makes the DRIA cover different from other nursing covers?', 'answer': "This is the only cover I use! It's light and airy and versatile. You can use it as cover, poncho or stroller cover. I keep it with me at all times and use it to cover my car seat as well. Other covers don't breathe as well as the dria does and my little one is much more comfortable under it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045K616S', 'answerTime': 'Oct 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381388400, 'question': 'what are the measurements?', 'answer': 'It is stretchy material so I may not have it spot on, but about 50" x 42". :)'}
