{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045VA3SO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389600000, 'question': 'Will this work for a preemie baby (4-5 lbs) or 7lb infant in the Britax Marathon carseat?', 'answer': 'I would imagine that it would work in any carseat. I have a graco model. My son was born early and was 6lbs 9 ounces. My friend had the same item and her daughter weighed less than that. The reason why I loved this item so much was due to the support it gave my son. It kept not only his neck and head in a comfortable position, it also supported his body as well. The head portion velcrows to the body portion as well, so you can use the pieces seperately, and it makes it easy to assemble in the carseat. As my son grew larger I used just the head portion until he had good neck control which was around 3 months. I feel for the price I got good use out of the item...'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0045VA3SO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392019200, 'question': 'Could this be used in a baby bath tub as a nice support pillow for infants that can be machine or air dried?', 'answer': "Hmmm, I think it would probably kinda float and would take a long time to dry either way. It's like a fiber fill so there'd be air pockets (floating) yet it's dense (long drying time)."}
