{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416211200, 'question': "How do you charge this? My daughter is looking for a night light that can't be unplugged for our 2 year old granddaughter.", 'answer': "It works like a cordless phone. There is a base which you place the nightlight on all day, and you simply remove it when you'd like to use it. It is cord free, battery free (in the traditional AA, AAA sense). My daughter has it on a shelf right next to the bed. It really does illuminate the room in a glow. She has also slept with it in the bed, it is completely cool to the touch. You can choose to set it to a short timer or have it light all night long, as well as choose one color or have it color change through its rainbow of choices. They really are adorable."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413788400, 'question': 'Can you leave this charging and on all night, or do you have to remove it from the charging station to turn it on as a night light?', 'answer': "I leave it on and on the charger all night, every night. It's lasted 2.5 years so far."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419667200, 'question': 'My son wants something he can read with at night without waking his sibling on the lower bunk with the big light. Is this bright enough to read by?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I would say it's absolutely bright enough, but there is no way to direct the light to the page. Being an all-over glow it may cause a problem trying to read with it as I imagine if it was close to him it would shine into his eyes at the same time as on the page, but if it was farther away it may cause eye strain."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 28, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427526000, 'question': 'Is there an easy way to turn it on, in the middle of the night, for diapering and feeding?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We have the bear and it turns on from the bottom or base of the bear. Not really a simple thing in the middle of the night until you get used to working with it by touch'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 11, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428735600, 'question': 'How long is the battery time if leaving it on?', 'answer': 'Hello Chloe. The KinderGlo will typically last between 8 and 12 hours depending upon several factors. Color mode and battery condition (how well charged the lamp is and the age of the lamp) both affect the use time. Color cycling mode uses slightly more power than a constant color mode, so the light will last for slightly less time on this setting. We hope this is helpful!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428044400, 'question': "Is there a way to reset the night light? The Dino stopped working last night. No red light when charging doesn't turn on.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you see no light at all it could be a problem with the base, not the Dino part. We had a problem with the base prong once. I emailed the Kinderglo company and they trouble- shooted with me to try to determine if it was something easily fixable. When it wasn't they asked me for my information and sent me a new base. In my case the metal prong was bend a bit and it simply wouldn't line up correctly to form a connection."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424332800, 'question': "I'm looking for a red night light. Do you have to cycle through the different color settings every time you turn it on?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423296000, 'question': "Blue light is bad to use because it stunts melatonin. Is there an option of yellow light? Can't imagine red wd be soothing.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hello Ninjabetic, and thanks for your question. At this time, a solid yellow setting is not available for the KinderGlo. The four light settings are solid green, solid blue, solid red, and continuous color changing. While some of the colors in the cycle are brighter than others, in general all of the light settings are soft enough to sleep by. As far as concerns about impeding melatonin levels, the science behind this shows that lights with a brightness of under 5 lux have no effect on the body's production of melatonin. Because we use soft LED lights which are then filtered through a translucent plastic body, the brightness of the KinderGlo never reaches 1 lux. The lights are bright enough to see by, but soft enough to sleep by."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415433600, 'question': "Does the red charging light turn green when charging is complete? We've had ours charging for 12hrs and it's still red.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not sure. I just charge it and is lasts forever. Don't pay attention to light. Will try and see"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0047N15KU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415174400, 'question': 'My question is in regards to batteries - are they included? What battery type does it take?', 'answer': "The unit is sealed, so I can't really say."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379574000, 'question': 'My 7 year-old is 51 inches tall. Will this Britax Parkway high-backed booster seat will accommodate a child who is that tall?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi. My 5 year old is not quite that big yet, but the back extends quite high. The height of the back extended is about 28 inches from the top of the car seat to the top of the back. Also, the back can be removed and seat used as a booster. In fact, the booster is also highly rated.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Oct 19, 2012', 'unixTime': 1350630000, 'question': "Several reviewers complained about the seat belt guide piece - sounds like if the child leans forward &amp; the belt pulls out, it doesn't always retract? Anyone else having this issue?", 'answer': "I didn't have a problem with the belt pulling out. I had an issue with the entire seat back coming forward when I braked. I only used it for one trip down the road and after I saw that happen, I took it out and returned it. Interestingly, the clerk at the store where it was purchased was not surprised that we weren't happy with it and said he sees a lot of them returned. Hope that helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Aug 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408863600, 'question': "I have a Volvo XC90 . When I installed the Parkway, the forward slope of the headrest wouldn't allow the seat to lean back properly for install?", 'answer': "I don't know the year of your Volvo XC90 but I was just looking at pictures of a 2015. It looks like the headrest is adjustable to go back to a more straight up and more flat position. It also looks like the headrest was removable. Take a look at the headrest on yours to see if any of this works for yours. Hope that this helps!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388822400, 'question': "Instructions say insert the seat back cylinder then lift to a point where it does not fall flat. Mine won't sit up on it's own. Is it defective?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It took me a few tries to get mine to click/lock into place. If it really won't then it could be defective. Mine fell flat like that too until I was able to connect them properly."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376895600, 'question': "I'm a Canadian customer. Does this have the National Safety Mark (NSM) on it? It is required in Canada.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it does ... the number is a rating score for reliability. This seat scroed an overall 8.7 out of 10. We love this seat!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370242800, 'question': 'Does this seat meet the Canadian safety standards? Can it be used in Canada?', 'answer': 'I am not sure about the Canadian laws, you may want to check Britax website or contact their customer support for verification.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362384000, 'question': 'Can anyone recommend a travel bag that will work with this seat? Thank you!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The Britax Car Seat Travel Bag fits all Britax models.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362297600, 'question': "I currently have a chevy traverse and am looking at getting a suburban. Does anyone have these kinds of cars where the booster seat didn't work?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Hi Tia. I am an automotive consultant and as far as I am aware, this seat should work fine with either of the vehicles you mentioned. I know of two that are used in midsize sedans (Camry, CTS) and another that is in a Toyota Venza and they all work with no problem at all. This seat does have the LATCH connections at the base, but they are used solely to keep the seat in place when a child is NOT sitting in it. When a child is in it, the seatbelt keeps both the child and booster seat in place. I have this seat personally in my own car and it has been working well for the past couple of months. I hope this helps and feel free to contact www.autoacademics.net if you have any other questions. Chris, Automotive Advisor and Consultant'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358755200, 'question': 'Does the back come off so this can be a backless booster?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It does - it arrives with the back off in the box and instructions on how to attach/detach it (very easy).'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0047O3Y26', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358755200, 'question': 'Can you remove the cover to clean it?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. It has little elastic loops that attach to little hooks on the seat part and on the back part. The back is completely removable as well. Super easy to get in and out of the car. Very light weight. Hands down the best booster seat.'}
