{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00483GAJU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424678400, 'question': 'How well would these work with pocket diapers such as "Sunbaby?"', 'answer': "I've never used pocket diapers (we've used prefolds and the Flip diaper system), but I think these would work with any type of cloth diaper. These just sit on top of whatever surface touches your baby's bottom. They don't move around as long as the diaper is snug. They're a little wider than my Flip inserts, so I like to fold them to size (my husband doesn't bother and they work fine either way) so that the liner doesn't hang out of the leg holes. Depending on the width of your sunbaby diapers, this may or may not be a problem for you."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00483GAJU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424678400, 'question': 'Are these liners absorbent? If so, how do the compare to a cloth insert or a disposable diaper?', 'answer': 'They are not absorbent. They are used to protect cloth from diaper creams or make it easier to clean poo off the cloth.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00483GAJU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393401600, 'question': 'Will these liners protect my cloth diapers from a zinc oxide-based diaper cream?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I wouldn't guarantee 100% protection, but I had very, very little of my zinc oxide (or my un-petroleum) creams get through onto my diapers. If you are worried about it for warranty issues on certain diapers, then definitely do as the other comment states and grab some light flannel liners or boosters. If, however you are worried about it for absorption issues personally, then I can just state that I have not had any issues from the minute amounts of creams that may occasionally go through. Hope that helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00483GAJU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424937600, 'question': "Has anyone had problems flushing these? Our plumbing is from the 1960s. From the warnings on the package, not clear if they're flushable.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We don't have problems flushing them, although I only use them occasionally."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00483GAJU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424678400, 'question': 'Are these liners absorbent? If so, how do the compare to a cloth insert or a disposable diaper?', 'answer': "They are not meant to be absorbent. They are paper-thin. The urine goes right through it. They are intended to catch the bowel movement so it's easier to dump it out of the cloth diaper."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00483GAJU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418025600, 'question': 'Which are softer, these or bumkins?', 'answer': "My son has never complained about these nor has his skin appeared irritated. He is 23 months now and we have only ever used Grovia Bioliners so I can't comment on any others. When I started buying them they were the best value of all the liners and we stuck with them."}
