{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00488TF38', 'answerTime': 'Jan 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390032000, 'question': 'how long do they last?', 'answer': "The bead itself is the Baltic Amber. It isn't a bead that's coated in Baltic amber. The amber will do what it's supposed to for as long as you wear it or your child wears it. You way worry about it eventually breaking, but you wont have to worry about beads going everywhere since their knotted between each one. You can easily re-string the beads when/if this happens. My son wore his for a year 24/7 before it finally broke. So, I hope that answers your question. :)"}
