{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0048BP5RU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371020400, 'question': 'Can two Gia Nursing Pillows be overlapped for tandem nursing of twins?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I'm not sure that they overlap really well. I tried it (without the babies LOL) and it might put the babies up a bit too high. Though I'm sure with a bit of trial and error she could probably get it to work. These are the best nursing pillows I've ever had. Even if she doesn't use them for tandem nursing, she could probably find a use for them. I put one behind my back and use the other to nurse my 2 year old. At night I even sleep with one of them as my pillow. It doesn't hurt my neck like regular pillows do. I don't think you can go wrong with these pillows but that's just my opinion. Good luck with the twin grands :)"}
