{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0049YS46K', 'answerTime': 'Nov 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384243200, 'question': 'Can these bottles be warmed in a warmer? Is there a recommended warmer for them?', 'answer': "Because they are dishwasher safe (and we've been using/ dish washing ours for almost 2 years now!), I think it's safe to say that you can use them in any bottle warmer that's no hotter than a dishwasher. Now, dishwashers get pretty dang hot, so I doubt there's any bottle warmer that comes even close to that hot. I wouldn't worry if I were you ;) and we LOVE our Life Factory glass bottles. Good luck! :)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0049YS46K', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Do these bottles have a measurement that you can read so that you can fill a 9oz only 4oz to avoid having to buy the smaller size?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. The measurements are there. But I find the smaller ones are easier to handle. And since they will last for years. You can find other uses for them e.g. In lunch boxes. Another thing to consider is that breastfed babies generally don't drink more than 4 oz at a time. So if you are exclusively using breast milk the 9 oz bottles would actually be less useful to you than the 4oz bottles. It all depends on how you plan on using them. Honestly if you're looking for things to save money on you won't need mittens to keep the baby from scratching. Buy footed sleepers because booties and socks don't stay on & three swaddling blankets is plenty if you do laundry once a day. And skip the stroller base for the car seat/carrier and buy your long term stroller with an adaptor. That said. All babies are different. You inevitably will spend money on things that are never used. Congratulations. And. The life factory teething rings are great."}
