{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004A15YSS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411369200, 'question': 'the only thing i need to do is remove a "wall" to convert this into a toddler bed? it seems the bed would need all 4 walls. Graco= unhelpful', 'answer': "Actually, a toddler bed (as it is known) has three walls to allow the toddler to get out of, or into, the bed on their own. I plan to convert my granddaughter's bed when she's old enough, although I am not altogether satisfied with the manufacturer's suggestion to just remove the front side because it would leave the edge of the mattress and spring exposed. I plan to fabricate a length of PVC lumber (that white stuff), because it's soft and there are no splinters to worry about, to fit over the front just to cover where the edges of the mattress and spring are exposed (so they won't slide around, or where she might get caught), but allow her to easily roll out of the bed over the panel I install. But it won't be for a while, yet."}
