{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004A910UG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398495600, 'question': 'Can you use the original seat as a second seat and use adaptors to install a baby capsule/car seat as the alternate seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'the seats are identical and can be used in any position (Secondary or primary). the car seat adapter can also be used in any position (primary or secondary - top or bottom). to use car seat, make sure you have the car seat adapter. without the car seat adapter you cannot attach the car seat. I put my todler in the seat near the front wheel and new born in the car seat adapter on top. I think that is what you are trying to do as well... oh and you need brackets to attach the seat on the bottom. those bracket are either sold in a package with a second seat or you can buy them individually. I bought it with a second seat, since my new born will eventually grow out of the car seat.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004A910UG', 'answerTime': 'May 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367564400, 'question': 'Can I put my 1 month old who is 10 lbs in this stroller without a car seat? We have a car seat, but no adapter.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think the instructions said not to use the seats until the baby is like 6 months old. However, because it reclines into an almost flat position I feel you can use it on a younger child. 1 month & 10 lbs. is probably a little small... But once they are like 4 months old it's probably okay as long as the straps can be adjusted tight enough to safely hold the baby in the stroller. For a 1 month old I'd recommend using the bassinet add on or buy the car seat adapter to use that on your stroller until your baby is a bit bigger. I hope this helps!"}
