{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004A9ZF3Y', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372316400, 'question': 'After you pop the food out, do you thaw it in the microwave? How to you heat the frozen food?', 'answer': "I feed my daughter the puree for lunch so typically every morning I take out whatever cubes I want to give her that day, and leave them in a covered bowl on the counter. They thaw completely in 60-90 minutes. When I'm in a hurry I put them in the microwave on medium power for 45 seconds, then check on them and heat for additional time on medium power as needed."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004A9ZF3Y', 'answerTime': 'Nov 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384243200, 'question': 'Breast milk storage usage?', 'answer': "Yes!!!! I used these for freezing over 600 oz of breastmilk. I didn't store BM in them long term. Once the milk was frozen, I popped the cubes out and stored either in a vacuum sealed bag (highly recommend this for long term), or a zippy freezer bag. Then they were placed in a deep freeze and some stored for up to 5 months. I never had any problem with milk quality. The vacuum sealed bags make the cubes stick together a bit as they are pressed onto one another, especially when stored for a few months, but a quick smack on a counter top broke them up well."}
