{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004AHKUHM', 'answerTime': 'May 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400742000, 'question': "Can the monitor in the baby's room be plugged in or does it have to run on batteries?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The monitor in the baby's room can be plugged in. It does not need batteries to work. In fact both units have AC adapters. Either can be plugged in or use batteries. I always leave the baby monitor (microphone) unit plugged in under my baby's crib. The parent unit (speaker) is plugged in when next to my bed at night, but I use the batteries when I am awake and carrying it with me."}
