{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004AHKUHW', 'answerTime': 'Dec 22, 2012', 'unixTime': 1356163200, 'question': 'Does adding a 2nd Graco set for a different room cause interference with each other?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I wanted to let you know that we bought the double set. It has two receivers and two bases so that you can with one receiver monitor two different rooms. We had one receiver downstairs in our den and the other in our bedroom. The monitors were placed in the infant room and toddler room. The way the dual monitor functions is by operating on two frequencies and it will switch back and forth and show different color lights so that you know which room is being monitored. You can turn one off completely too or only listen to it for 15 seconds before switching to the other one for say, 2 minutes in length. If you were thinking of purchasing a new one, you might want to just go ahead and purchase the dual one and sell the single one used.'}
