{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004AKWVUS', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416124800, 'question': 'Do the figurines stand up on their own or do they topple over?', 'answer': 'The figures can stand on their own yet they topple pretty easily because they are light weight. Pretty much anything made of fabric will fall over if brushed lightly, or if the table it is on is bumped. This nativity set is meant to be played with rather than used as a display and little ones don\'t seem to mind if a figure happens to fall over. The figure is either "sleeping" or it gets picked up and reset. And it really takes nothing to "moosh" the stuffing inside and work it around to create a more stable base for a figure to stand. Enjoy the set!'}
