{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004B6FJNC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421740800, 'question': 'How fast is the shipping to the USA (NY)? //TO THE SELLER:Do you always have them in stock? ( planning to buy it in March)', 'answer': 'We are shipping all our items within 24 hours on business day via FedEx or UPS from Illinois. As usual it gets to NY in about 3 days. We could be short on some colors for limited time, but yes, we are trying to have most popular models/color in stock all the time.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004B762AK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363676400, 'question': "Is it possible to purchase a second monitor to hook up to one camera? I'd like to have one monitor upstairs and one downstairs, for the nursery camera", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No it is not. You can hook up more than one camera but not more than one monitor. However, it's portable, light weight and easy to move around. The internal battery lasts several hours once it is fully charged on the base. Every time I put the baby down, I grab it from my bedroom and either hang it on my pants waistband or just bring it with me wherever I go in the house. I do not find it cumbersome."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004B762AK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428822000, 'question': 'My monitor is saying no signal. Cords are in correctly but still no picture it just stopped working any suggestions on how to fix it?', 'answer': 'Hey, I had the same issue and was able to resolve following the instructions in that site: http://www.summerinfant.com/consumer-care/faqs/my-video-monitor-is-saying-no-signal-no-camera-out The steps are (in case the page is off-line): The Monitor and Camera are synched at the factory for privacy reasons. If the Monitor and Camera are not synching with each other for any reason, please sync them as described below. 1. Move the Monitor and camera right next to each other so they are only inches apart and make sure both are plugged in. 2. Turn both the Camera and Monitor on. 3. To add camera, press the add camera button from the touch menu. Press the up and down arrows to navigate to the "add camera" option press the check mark icon to select and enter the "add cam" menu. Navigate the left or right button to select the camera to be synched. Press the check mark icon and the camera image should start blinking. 4. Press and hold the code button on the back of the camera head to synch (may take up to 20 seconds). 5. Once synched, a picture from the newly added camera should appear on the monitor screen. 6. If this is unsuccessful, you should repeat steps above making sure the Camera and Monitor are close enough to each other for synching.'}
