{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004BSFC50', 'answerTime': 'Jul 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373698800, 'question': 'Can anyone give feedback on how easy it is to actually stack the rings? Is the center post soft so that it bends a lot, or sturdier inside?', 'answer': "It's super easy to stack and restack these rings, and it's an added bonus that they are soft and squishy. My little girl loves is toy, and I never have to worry about injury from hard plastic."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004BSFC50', 'answerTime': 'Dec 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386921600, 'question': 'What age is this toy best for?', 'answer': "I bought this for my granddaughter when she was 6 months old because it is safe, soft, and colorful. The rings are different sizes so the smaller rings were easier to grasp and chew on at that age. At 10 months she was trying to put the rings on (sometimes sucessrully). At 13 months she loves putting the rings on and off and throwing them around. She doesn't always put them on in the right order, but they can go on in any order the baby likes. She will reach for this toy in her toy box as it is easy to grasp by the top. Very pleased with this purchase."}
