{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004C053C4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429081200, 'question': "What's difference between 6 months and 6 M+? Does 6 months have two holes?", 'answer': "Hi Cathy - I've summarized all 4 types of flows that we have for you: Slow Flow (0-3 months) - 1 hole. Truly slow flow, ideal for newborns up to 3 months. All our 5oz bottles comes with this flow. Medium Flow (3-6 months) - 2 hole. A bit faster for your growing little one. All our 8oz bottles come with this flow. Fast Flow (6+ months) - 3 hole. Suitable for your babies 6 months and up. Variable Flow (6+ months) - Y-cut. This allows your baby to control to flow rate, and its good for thicker fluids."}
