{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': 'Does this gate work well with baseboards? The doorway has a 33" opening at the bottom but a 36" opening at the top.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'There are 4 individual adjustment bolts, one at each corner of the gate. Each bolt has 3"-4" of travel or \'play\', so you should be able to use it with an opening of varying width.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398409200, 'question': 'how is wide', 'answer': "The gate that opens in either direction is 22 inches wide. I'm assuming that's what you wanted to know. The width of the whole unit is adjustable."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382079600, 'question': 'Can this be pressure mounted only, meaning not drilling the cups it comes with into the wall?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes...no problem with it staying in place and it is secure.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381820400, 'question': 'Is there a bar at the bottom that could be tripped over?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'yes'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398582000, 'question': 'Will this work in a hallway opening that is 30" wide at the bottom (due to baseboards) and 31" wide at the top?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, we had the same issue at bottom of stairs. And at the top where we attached it to newel posts. There are bolts that allow for adjustment. The ends of the adjustment caps sit in a cup that is screwed into wall, baseboard etc.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394866800, 'question': "How wide is this gate? I have a 41'' opening at bottom of the stairs", 'answer': 'Details say for up to 40.5 inches, but extensions can be added. I do like the gate. Opens easily both ways and closes easily with the latch.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405666800, 'question': 'Could this gate be used outside?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, I can't see it being for outside use. The wooden parts aren't treated. We use it at the bottom of our stairs to the second floor so our grandchild can't climb up unattended."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359792000, 'question': 'Where can you get the 5-1/2-inch and 11-inch extensions to allow this to fit a larger opening?', 'answer': 'On their website....it is the only place I could find extensions. http://store.munchkin.com/product/11"-standard-extension---dark-silver'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YHS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382079600, 'question': 'Also, when you first open the box, does the gate look like its worped...the lock does not meet the gate? thanks', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, I think a lot of people have this observation. It is designed this way. It lines up as you tighten the bolts on either side.'}
