{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YZU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428476400, 'question': "I wish this came in black. Am I missing it? I only see the extra tall one in black, but that won't fit my banister.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Amazon has a wood and steel munchkin gate that is not extra tall. Do a search for a Munchkin Wood and Steel Designer Gate.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YZU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403074800, 'question': 'Can this be used by pressure mounting and if so, can a toddler knock it over?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'We have it pressure mounted at the bottom of the stairs. Neither the 3 or 5 year old can dislodge it, even when they (against orders!) Swing on it. I think I could if I tried really hard, but it would take a series of strong kicks.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CL9YZU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402815600, 'question': 'How wide is the part you walk thru?', 'answer': "I don't have a tape measure, but it is easier to get thru because it is a shorter gate. I'm guessing about 30 inches."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CL9YZU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402729200, 'question': 'What no-drill mounting kit do you suggest for either a square post that is 1-1/4" wide or 6" wide at the bottom of a staircase?', 'answer': 'I suggest another gate. My son figured this gate out (all 3 steps) within a week. At 2 1/2 we now only keep it up to block the dog out. My son can do all 3 steps very fast.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CL9YZU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402988400, 'question': 'Is the paint on the gate low or zero VOC (Volatile Organic Chemicals)?', 'answer': "What does this matter, VOC's are only released when the paint dries, there are no Volatile Organic Compounds left when the paint is dry. Hence the name Volatile. If the paint is applied in a facility (which it is) there is no VOC's released into the atmosphere as the fumes (vapors) are captured in the paint booth vent system."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CL9YEQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377586800, 'question': 'How much clearance is there between the wall and the gate at the bottom? I want to see if it will fit with the baseboard trim.', 'answer': "The hinge, on the one side, gives a good inch or inch and a half of clearance. The locking side is adjustable so that wouldn't be in the way of the baseboard trim."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YEQ', 'answerTime': 'May 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367823600, 'question': 'Does this expand to 40 inches as the box in the product description indicates?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes--these gates expand nicely. We've had ours up for about 7-8 months now, and continue to be quite pleased with their look and function."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CL9YEQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375340400, 'question': 'Is anyone else having the gate fly right past the connection point if you swing it closed too quickly?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yeah, from time to time. You get used to how much force you need to close it and not swing past the connection point pretty quickly, I would say.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412665200, 'question': 'Any tips for getting my gate to slide onto the wall mount? The video makes it look so easy but mine stops at about one inch down.', 'answer': 'Here\'s the deal. You purchased an attractive, but poorly manufactured gate. So did I and welcome to the club. It only gets worse from here, so if you\'re smart you shod return it and purchase something else. If you are dumb and stubborn like me, by all means keep it and suffer the consequences. The reason your gate doesn\'t slide down is most lily because it\'s getting hung on the screw heads. The holes need to be countersunk deeper than they are to accomosh this. A countersink bit is too wide to fit into the trough to accomplish this, so you or your mignon will need to do this using a 1/4" (ish) drill bit and further counter sink the hole creatively. The good news is that the rail is aluminum, which is very soft and makes this doable. After this is done, you should be able to slide the gate in with relative ease. Then you\'ll be home free for a few months until it needs a mystery adjustment. Good luck!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402556400, 'question': 'Can anyone measure out for me what the width of open space there is between the aluminum slats? I have a cat that needs restriction. Thanks!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Gap is 1 7/8"'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384761600, 'question': 'Has anybody mounted this gate to a banister? Was it effective? We have a double-banister.', 'answer': 'It would need to be 100% flat surfaced. If there is a wall on one side you need a beam behind the wall. The gate doesnt hold up with regular dry wall anchors well.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422086400, 'question': 'Is locking the gate loud or is it pretty quiet?', 'answer': "Both. If you just push it swiftly it can be a bit too loud for sleeping babies in a nursery. But we have learned how to shut the door quietly when the twins are sleeping quietly and we don't want to wake them. It shouldn't keep u from buying it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394866800, 'question': "I watched the video and don't see how the gate closes securely is there a lock or safety catch", 'answer': 'Yes it is very secure. You must press a button at the top of the gate at the same time press up on a button on the underside. Its easy to use and secure. My son is able to unlatch most child safety locks as well as his car seat breast latch but has been unable to unlock this gate.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379314800, 'question': 'We have a clear opening of 42 inches. Is this gate wide enough? I thought I read somewhere it only fits up to 40 inches.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I just measured my opening and it measured 36 inches. I used every extension the gate comes with so i would have to agree that i do not believe the gate would fit anything over 40 inches...'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427007600, 'question': 'Is the gate itself 30.5 inches in height, or is that the installed height?', 'answer': 'I am seriously surprised that people are still willing to shell out their hard earned cash for trash like this gate. How many bad reviews do you need to not buy it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426230000, 'question': 'When you remove the gate from the mounting strips, how far do they stick out on either side (how much is the width of the door opening reduced)?', 'answer': 'little more than a 1/4"'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425884400, 'question': 'Love this gate...BUT i just measured my stair openings and one is 43 and the other is 44. I see the max is 40...is there anyway to make it wider?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'If you attach a wood strip to the wall on each side of the gate, you will make a great anchor for the gate and it can narrow the opening. John'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBWY6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422259200, 'question': 'Does this need to be mounted on a wall on both sides? how would you attach to a stair banister/rail/post?', 'answer': 'Yes, it requires a guide piece mounted on both sides. I think it could be mounted to some railings but depends on the design. It is the best baby gate! I highly recommend it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'May 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367823600, 'question': 'How far apart is the widest openings between slats?', 'answer': 'The spacing between the bars is 2 and 1/4 inches (2.25 inches).'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Nov 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384243200, 'question': 'Is the mounting hardware on either side (top and bottom) thicker than 1 1/2"?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't remember the actual length of hardware or thickness of brackets, but I absolutely do not recomment using the mounting hardware (i.e. screws and anchors) that come with this gate. Gate should be mounted directly into a stud and you will need longer screws than what comes with the gate to accomplish this. The screws that come with this gate are WAY too short to effectively reach into a wall stud once it goes through the mounting bracket and drywall."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389772800, 'question': 'We have a 70 lb dog that will try to get to the other side of this gate (to go down stairs) with all his force. Will this gate hold up to such force?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'd be a little concerned about that. My concern would probably be the plastic mounts... either the mounts themselves not holding up or just the job you do securing them to the wall. The gate itself will take the force of a 70 lb dog in my opinion."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Oct 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382598000, 'question': "Some reviews are saying it falls right out of the wall. Does it really need to be installed into a stud? That's not an option where I need it.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It's a pretty heavy gate. I have it installed into a stud. In one case I even nailed a 2x4 to the stud in the wall and then attached the gate to that. I wouldn't attach it directly to drywall (no stud), I can easily see it coming out of the wall."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Apr 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398150000, 'question': 'can a 3 year old open this easily?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Our 2-1/2 year old can "usually" get the gates open, so probably a three year old can without much trouble.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391414400, 'question': 'Could older children open this easily? I have a 7, 6 and 3 yr old that have their bedrooms in the basement but we have another baby on the way and wan', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I dont know about easily, but my 6 yr old has no problem. Also, my almost 3 yrs old figured out how to open it today. It takes a fair amount of strength to lift and open.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'I have a 42" opening at the top of my stairs. Will this gate fit there? I haven\'t seen how wide it is, just the height?!', 'answer': 'Yes, it says in the description: "fits 33 to 56 inches"'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389686400, 'question': 'What is the maximum spacing between the bars, please?', 'answer': 'Between the bars I can fit 3 fingers so I would say 4 fingers for the average woman. I have high base boards so I was concerned about that but it proved to not be a concern. The main thing on this product is to make sure the swing supports are mounted on a stud, this will prevent having to remount after a few days opening and closing.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Jul 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406703600, 'question': "Can this gate be installed in an angle? I have stairs with a handrail on one side and a wall on another and I don't want to cut the handrail.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'As long as the locking brackets are perpendicular to the to the hinge side. You will have to fabricate a way to mount the brackets on an angle.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBX0Y', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': 'Would it be ok to attach the weight-bearing hinged side to our solid bannister but have the other side plastic catches attached to drywall with anchors?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'As long as you use the heavy duty wall anchors you should be ok. A better option would be a good piece of wood like a 1x4 about 40" anchored to the drywall. The locking mechanism is pretty stout and a good bump might pull the drywall anchors out.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX8G', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403852400, 'question': 'What is the distance between the bars? I want to use it at the bottom of my stairs for my dog.', 'answer': 'Just under 3 inches. My 3 lb chihuahua can get past it but my 5 lb chihuahua cannot.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX8G', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378969200, 'question': 'So this gate goes down to fit a 25 inch door opening? My door opening is 27in and if it does not go down to 25 then i cant use it', 'answer': 'Yes it does with A few inches to spare. You will love this. My kitchen doors are smaller than normal as well and we had to get this one.'}
{'answer': 'Call customer service 18003442229', 'asin': 'B004CLBX8G', 'answerTime': '25 days ago', 'question': 'Where can you purchase replacement hinges for the baby gate? I looked on the munchkin website and I did a search for hinges and replacement parts.', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX8G', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397113200, 'question': 'does this gate have the ability to stay open or is it an automatically closing gate?', 'answer': "It can stay open. It doesn't self close."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX8G', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396335600, 'question': 'Are pressure-mount hardware included with this gate or is it only to be used with permanent/screw mounts?', 'answer': 'Only permanent screws (preferably upgraded over what comes with the package). The unique design of these gates does away with any permanent cross bar that has to be stepped over. That is a plus. The down side is that there is no way to put a tension bar across the opening or it would defeat the design.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX8G', 'answerTime': 'Jan 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388908800, 'question': 'squeaky hinges', 'answer': 'Hinges are quiet, even the last ones I had never made a sound. Realized though when my last one broke. I could have just ordered a new wall mount. Not the entire system. The gate itself seems indestructible.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX8G', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': 'How wide is it?', 'answer': '40 inches. Although they are designed if you bought 2 you can connect them together and go 60 inches and up to 80 inches. I have not done that though. I only use mine on my kitchen doors and stairway. Still love them.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CLBX2M', 'answerTime': 'Nov 5, 2012', 'unixTime': 1352102400, 'question': 'is this a pressure gate? no nailing to the wall', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This is a pressure gate. There are rubber stopper things on each side of the gate and you use a small tool (included) to tighten it on each end. They are EXTREMELY sturdy. I have three of them - and one is at the top of my stairway so it is used multiple times every day and has never moved or loosened. Couldn't get a better gate. They are pretty attractive too. P.S. I'm not sure why other people are answering this question. I think you are mistaken. They do NOT nail or screw or mount into the walls. Perhaps you are looking at the wrong gate."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CLBX2M', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403852400, 'question': 'Will this gate stay open or does it automatically close? I would like to leave it open when not in use.', 'answer': 'Yes, it stays open. There is no closer on the gate...just a really nice latch.'}
