{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004CQGD7W', 'answerTime': 'May 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401001200, 'question': 'What brand of dishes work best with this product?', 'answer': "I found that the Playtex bowls and plates without dividers worked best. They come with all sorts of designs for all children's tastes and we got months and months of use out of them. Hope that helps. http://www.amazon.com/Playtex-Mealtime-Plate-pack-Colors/dp/B007PF0JNQ/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1401069007&sr=8-1&keywords=playtex+plates"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004CQGD7W', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': 'Has anyone tried this with the oxo tot plate?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have not used the Oxo plates, so all I can say is, if there is no embossing or indentations on the base of the plate, it should work well. We have always used the Playtex plates and bowls and found that they work perfectly with the Lil Diner. If the sucker has to go over any type of embossing or indentation, it won't work. Hope that helps."}
