{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004DC9TAI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424160000, 'question': 'when the canopy on the stroller is collapsed, it hits my 8 month old child in the head. Anyone else have this problem? Is there a way to fix this?', 'answer': 'I just bought this for my 3 Year Old. When canopy is pulled back it was slightly hitting her head. Another mom told me to pull in the straps near clear window back. It then pulls clear up in canopy and allows for more head space. So i pull this back first then close canopy 100%. I found this solved 80% of my problem'}
