{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004DC9TD0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421654400, 'question': 'Is this a good jogging/running stroller or is their ironman better equipped for this?', 'answer': "Absolutely. I've trained for a marathon and done various other distance runs with this. I really like the front swivel tire because its easier for me to turn and maneuver the stroller. My runs take me all over, sidewalks, trails, parks, etc. However my running partner has the Ironman and prefers the locked front wheel. Its a preference thing. Mine does have the ability to have a locked front wheel but that drives me bananas! I would NEVER recommend this stroller to a non runner! Its very costly if your not going to run with it, but for me it's worth every penny since I've done ALOT of running."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004DC9TD0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2012', 'unixTime': 1329724800, 'question': 'twins: Does the Duallie stroller have the capability to hold two car seats for twins?', 'answer': "With the old one you could only use one car seat at a time, and I have not seen a double car seat bar for the new (just tray/tray and car seat/tray) You can put a baby directly in the Bob, it lays flat enough and then just get a J J Cole body support (it's better than the snuzzler IMO but about the same price) We did this with my youngest at 4-5 weeks. If you really want the ease of popping in and out with a bucket, even if Bob offered such an add on, with their prices you wouldn't pay much more for a new double snap n go, less for used, and it would be so much easier to travel with. I have 3yo twins, i got my doubl snap n go for 10 bucks on craigslist and it was a great purchase."}
