{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004DC9TAS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382770800, 'question': 'Can this be used for a newborn / infant?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Hi Kelly! The owners manual doesn't recommend running with an infant until 8 months of age. We waited until our child could sit up by herself at 6 months before just using the stroller by itself. I'm not sure of your situation but, the best set-up would be a Bob Stroller with a Britax adaptor and Britax car seat for the first 6 months. After that you would just use the stroller by itself. The stroller is awesome, we used it for walking around stores when she was a newborn in her car seat and now we run with her in the stroller. It's definitely worth the money, especially of you plan on having another kid. Hope that helps! If you have any more questions feel free to ask! Travis"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004DC9TAS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374217200, 'question': "I'm wondering if I should get a compact stroller in addition to this one? is this stroller to big to go into stores? Small stores like at the mall?", 'answer': "It's not to bad for malls. But I would get a compact one for small shoppes or going to the DR. It's pretty bulky for some situations. I like the stroller though for parks and walks."}
