{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004DC9TAS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388995200, 'question': 'What size are the inner tubes?', 'answer': 'Tires: Pneumatic tires. Rear 16" x 1.75", Front 12.5" x 1.75".'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004DC9TAS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363158000, 'question': 'First week, the back left tire popped - is there a warranty? Should not have to buy new tubes so soon.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Best I know, tubes aren't covered. Be sure to check pressures, and know that pressures increase with temp. As a matter of practice, we keep a small pump and spare tubes in a small pouch in our strollers. Started with our Phil and Teds as that thing is notorious for being finiky on pressure and slipping beads/popping tubes. When you change the tube, feel around the inside of the tire AND wheel to make sure there are no rough/sharp spots. If there are rough or sharp spots on the wheel, then I'd contact BOB."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004DC9TAS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380697200, 'question': 'How does this work for an older/taller child? Like a 4~5 year old. I cannot find specs on the seat itself.', 'answer': "My 4.5 year old is 44 inches tall and when the canopy is open he is pretty much right to the top. When it's closed it is all bunched up behind his head which is kinda annoying but if they're not bothered by it no big deal. If I were to do it all over I would get the baby jogger summit x3 since the head room is much better."}
