{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004DIQTD2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370934000, 'question': 'when does this car seat model expire?', 'answer': 'Answer from their site to a costumer with the same question: . We do have a 5-year expiration recommendation for all of our car seats and bases. Most car seat experts do recommend that you not use a car seat or base that is more than 5 years old from the manufacture date (located on a white sticker on the bottom of your car seat). The theory is that as plastic ages it becomes brittle, so it may not perform correctly in a serious crash. The harnesses and other components also wear, and the car seat may no longer meet current standards. - See more at: http://blog.pegperegousa.com/2011-collection/2011-primo-viaggio-sip-3030-faqs/#sthash.1NTih6G7.dpuf'}
