{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004EWG4ZA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': 'Is there Vinyl covering? Is it VOC safe? Anyone know..thanks in advance', 'answer': 'The most outer layer of the mattress is vinyl. You should check out this page (see below what they say about this specific mattress) and you can follow their suggestions on better options https://www.facebook.com/note.php?note_id=10150355883242799 As an example, top-selling Sealy Baby Firm Crib Mattress uses a vinyl cover, coated with proprietary antibacterial STAPH-GARD. Despite stating on their website that their product "does not contain any harmful chemicals" and "does not contain toxic fire retardants," they refused to provide information about how they meet flammability standards or clarify what chemicals make up STAPH-GARD. Vinyl manufacturing requires use of toxic chemicals, and chemicals must be added to vinyl to make it flexible.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004EWG4ZA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391155200, 'question': "Just because it say's it is waterproof, wouldn't you still want to use a zippered allergen mattress protector, knowing this is for a first baby?", 'answer': 'Yes it is truly waterproof but I always use a mattress protector in addition. I think it is more pleasant for the baby to lay on a mattress with a protector and a sheet. Also it is easy to whip off the protector if there is an accident, wipe off the mattress and put on the spare...I would use a mattress protector even if it was a second or third baby :)'}
