{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FI2P88', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391500800, 'question': 'Can a person use a regular magnet to unlock, or does it need to be the Safety First "key" magnet?', 'answer': "I haven't found a magnet strong enough to open the locks, so I wish the Safety First keys weren't so ridiculously overpriced."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004FI2P88', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418889600, 'question': "Could these be installed for drawers? Especially drawers that are not very high, so there's no clearance for a drill or short screwdriver.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you can take the drawer out and have enough clearance to set the latch inside the frame, you could put the locking mechanism in the drawer and reinstall it. If you can't remove the drawer, these unfortunately might not be the solution you're looking for."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004FI2P88', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428303600, 'question': 'Would these locks secure cabinet doors closed with enough force to hold snug against weatherstrip, creating a strong seal?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It's a solid latch. Can't think of why it would not hold against weather strip. Make sure weather strip is already on when using the screw template or test how snug you want it by pressing"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FI2P88', 'answerTime': 'Dec 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419321600, 'question': 'what is the pounds of force these hold?', 'answer': 'Complete estimation... 10-15lbs (if mounted properly)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FI2P88', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409900400, 'question': 'How big are the locks themselves? Trying to gauge whether they will fit on the wooden part of our glass cabinet doors.', 'answer': "An approximation since I'm not at home right now, the lock is about 1.75 inches tall and 1 inch wide and sticks into the cabinet a little over an inch in depth. The catch is very small, not even an inch wide, the depth is about 1/4 of an inch."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004FI2P88', 'answerTime': 'May 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400050800, 'question': 'Does this come with a template for installation?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It does come with an installation template that is only helpful to make the first set of holes on the cabinet base. The template is quite inaccurate for predicting the placement for the holes on the cabinet door. On the first one I made 3 sets of holes in the door before I figured out that the template was not working. Turns out that the placement of the part on the door is less exact than I expected and eyeballing it works fine.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004FI2P88', 'answerTime': 'Apr 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396940400, 'question': 'Has anyone tried using the product on small sliding doors? For example, the doors on a wooden TV stand, thanks in advance.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Won\'t work unless you build out a "L" type of piece in the back and attach the item there. Still may be an issue. You can use a standard Key lock for that from the hardware store that has a turning radius with a locking mechanism.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FI2P88', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391068800, 'question': 'Will the magnet work through nearly 2 inches of wood? Through the drawer front and the face as well?', 'answer': 'Yes, the magnet is strong! I have not had any problems with the locks.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FKPZBA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389772800, 'question': 'Do you have to wash the cover every time you change? Or is it only the prefolds that have to be washed every time?', 'answer': 'You have to wash the prefolds every time. You can get several diaper changes out of a cover, until you get a major poo. The rule of thumb is 3 or 4 prefolds for every cover. PS The econobum prefolds are my favorite so far. The cover is so-so.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FKPZBA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362470400, 'question': 'How to wash them ?', 'answer': 'Very simple routine: rinse in plain cold water and spin to prewash, wash in hot normal cycle with 1 tablespoon Tide powder per 12-15 diapers, extra rinse.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FKPZBA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': 'Why do I need snappies with these, as some people have suggested in the reviews?', 'answer': 'To be honest, I thought the same thing and bought some myself, but never used them. I think you use them on the insert and then put the cover on? Never tried it that way. I do use the snappies on the other cloth diapers we have from our second child.'}
