{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FOWDKC', 'answerTime': 'May 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399014000, 'question': 'How would you rate the absorbancy compared to imagine or green mountain diaper prefolds?', 'answer': "I would say green mountain are slightly more absorbent. They are great but like with any prefold you'll have to change more often than a stay dry insert or disposable. I would go up to the ones with the red edge. It says they are the same size but they are actually a little bigger and much more absorbent."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004FOWDKC', 'answerTime': 'May 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400396400, 'question': 'Does the 4x8x4 vs the 4x6x4 refer to the number of layers of cloth?', 'answer': 'Yes, the sides are 4 layers, the middle section is 6 or 8 layers respectively. Thus, if you do a trifold you get a total of 14 or 16 layers of absorbent fabric.'}
