{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004FOWDKC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410159600, 'question': 'Do these fit in newborn diaper covers?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "The short answer is Yes, but I like my Traditional Fit diapers much better. The are easier to get on because they are longer, especially when my son is wiggling around (I use Thirsties wraps and Snappis to hold the diaper in place). And they didn't leak as soon. I stopped using my Better Fit diapers months ago, but my Traditional still work great. I have a few pocket diapers and the Better Fit worked better for those, but I would recommend the Traditional size if you are primarily going to use wraps."}
