{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004GP45XS', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391760000, 'question': 'Is it BPA free?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't know that it is BPA-free. I don't recall the packaging or the listing stating one way or another (I made this purchase almost a year ago). However, it is melamine, and melamine contains formaldehyde, which is something to be aware of. I never heat or microwave these dishes (several health authorities recommend heating foods in safe containers, such as glass, and then transferring your food to the dish if you need to). I do use them in the dishwasher and they come out fine. If you are concerned about chemicals, etc. contaminating your foods, then I would look into this on the World Health Organization (WHO) website as they have done extensive research and studies in these areas. Good luck!"}
