{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004HFQLOI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397458800, 'question': 'Just poured the lukewarm milk/dry milk/yogurt into the jars and turned it on. But why do I have so much mix leftover? 2.5 cups leftover go to waste??', 'answer': "i agree that the jar is not very accurate by the measurement. but i never had 2.5 cups of leftover! that's a bit too much... i usually put in 6oz yogurt (1 of those store bought, or one jar from last batch), then add 18 oz of milk. that'd do. once you do a few batches, you'll have a pretty good idea of how much you need to put in there. Or you can always use the cups that come with it to measure. that'd never go wrong. on a different note, if you ever have extra leftover mixture, just drink it. :) I like it that way anyways. sometimes if i made the yogurt too sour, i just add some milk, and do a yogurt drink. you can use that for smoothy as well. don't waste it~ :)"}
