{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004HKIIGC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424073600, 'question': 'Is this sippy cup with a straw or just a straw like top? And is it actually non spill?', 'answer': 'It\'s a "straw" connected to the lid but it\'s hard plastic, not soft. It\'s pretty good for non-spill. I don\'t think you\'ll find a completely non-spill cup ever! haha. But this comes pretty close. It will drip liquid if you turn it upside down and shake it though.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004HKIIGC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420704000, 'question': 'Is it safe to warm up milk in it? The teachers use a crockpot at daycare to warm up the milk, will this be okay?', 'answer': 'My experience has been that this cup leaks. I would especially say that it would leak through the spout upon temperature change. I put cold milk in the cup, it warms up on the counter and flows out like lava from a volcano. Same goes when it would cool back down. So although I think it would be safe to warm in the crockpot, it may flow out the top.'}
