{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004HKIIFS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 17, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426575600, 'question': 'Does the child have to suck to get liquid or does it pour out? How easy is cleaning?', 'answer': "Child has to suck to get it out, but not super hard like some sippy cups we've had. However, after having ours for about six months, the no spill valve has broken and it pours out. I could just replace it with another valve, but I probably won't bother since I don't let him walk around the house with it to spill it anyway. We only use ours for water because I'm not fond of things that need a bottle brush to reach inside, I never feel like it gets it clean enough anyway. I suppose you could put it in the dishwasher however, which would be easy enough. Overall, I like this sippy cup a lot and would recommend it as one of the better, if not the best sippy cup we've ever used."}
