{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004HO587A', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396681200, 'question': 'Does anyone know how this stroller compares to the City Versa (also reversible) besides the price?', 'answer': 'I seriously considered the BJCV and can tell you the following: 1. The BJCV is is more compact -- both in use and when folded. We use our Kolcraft only for "around the neighborhood" because it can\'t fit in the back of our small car. If we had bought the City Versa, it would have fit (I tried it out.) 2. The City Versa also folds more easily and has a much bigger shade and an adjustable handle. 3. The City Versa does NOT have an included parent tray or belly bar and you have to buy the car seat adaptor separately. However, the car seat adaptors for the Baby Jogger strollers are of higher quality and more secure. 4. I THINK that the BJCV seat is roomier, with more of a leg rest, etc. Overall, if I had the money, I\'d buy the BJCV. For just a stroller that is used around the neighborhood (or if you have a huge vehicle and space doesn\'t matter), this Kolcraft stroller works pretty well.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004HO587A', 'answerTime': 'Jun 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370502000, 'question': 'Does it work with the Safety 1st infant car seats?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Per the kolcraft website, its compatible with safety 1st designer 22, onboard 35 and onboard 35 air. Honestly though, you can use this stroller with the recline feature for a newborn. We did.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004HO587A', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383724800, 'question': 'Is the handlebar adjustable? I\'m not quite 5\'2" so I don\'t know that a handlebar that works at 5\'10"+ would work well.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It is not adjustable, but I'm 5'3 and find it quite comfortable. My husband is 6'3 and it is easier for him to push than other ones."}
