{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004HWXCJS', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377068400, 'question': 'Is the pump built into the bag, or can it be used separately without carrying the bag?', 'answer': 'It is fastened to the inside of the bag with Velcro strips so I can be removed if needed. I found the bag very handy though, the flap in front unzips and folds down and kind of acted as a tray to hold everything and protect furniture/counter surfaces, and wipes clean easily. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004HWXCJS', 'answerTime': 'May 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400655600, 'question': 'can you use any kind of bottles for this cause im wanting to use glass bottles thanks', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have used the Evenflow Classic glass bottles with this pump and they fit perfectly! I avoid plastic whenever possible, even when it's BPA free. You don't have to worry about any toxins leaching from glass bottles, and they still look brand new after over a year of daily use."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004HWXCJS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381734000, 'question': "Is there enough space in teh bag to not need to also carry a purse? For example I'd want to put keys, wallet, smartphone, and maybe ipad mini.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I used to bring it up to school and put my lunch in it. There's a lot of room on the side and top of the bag. I also could fit my phone, hand purse, and kindle in it with ease."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004HWXCJS', 'answerTime': 'May 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399100400, 'question': 'How big of a pain is cleanup and maintenance? I am concerned about the parts being high maintenance and afraid they will grow mold easily.', 'answer': "It's much easier than the cleanup for my Ameda. There are less little parts to deal with and I think easier to clean. The only thing I don't like is that it's not a closed system so it is possible for milk to get in the tubes. That shouldn't really happen but I do get condensation so will probably flush with rubbing alcohol and water every month and replace the tubing every few months (not expensive)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004HWXCJS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358323200, 'question': "Does it come with some bottles? The product description doesn't say anything about it, but it looks like there are 4 in the picture...", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, mine came with 4 bottles with caps but only one nipple (Which, we didn't like the nipple anyhow, we've had much more success with feeding with the Medela Calma nipple). Also comes with a freezer pack and case to put the 4 bottles in."}
