{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004I0YZTA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395212400, 'question': 'Is it small enough for a 14 month old who is almost 30" tall and weighs 24 lbs? Does the leash attach to the bottom or top of the backpack?', 'answer': "Critsmama, We love this little buddy. It's small enough for your little one and he or she will have a couple of years use of it. We travel alot and it comes in handy at airports and just walking around. The leash attachment is located on the bottom of the buddy, and its removable, similar to a leash. Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004I0YZTA', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391587200, 'question': 'Is it large enough for a 3 year old', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "YES! For you, I just tried it on my almost 5-year-old girl who wears size 6 and 7 clothes....she stout, not fat. There's still room for more growth! Actually, I had it for my petite son around age 2 and it was pretty roomy on him. I loved this thing while I needed it...the reason I got it is because my boy jumped out of the van one day in a busy parking lot and took off like a track star sprinting! For a couple of months while he was learning, I am sure it saved his life!"}
