{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004I16DOY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382598000, 'question': 'Will these fit the Tommie tippie closer to nature 9 oz bottles??', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yep! I use them almost every day with the 9oz bottles.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004I16DOY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427439600, 'question': 'Do you have to use an ice pack if using it for breastmilk?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Hi Glenda, There is no mention on the package or their website the need for an icepack so I'm assuming no. I haven't used it with an icepack. I put a small (50mL) glass Pigeon bottle containing water in the fridge for a few hours and when it was cool enough, I placed it inside the insulator bag and made sure it wasn't opened for an hour. After 1 hour, I checked on the bottle and it was still cold. 3 hours from when I first took out the bottle from the fridge, it was cool but not as cold as when I first put it in the insulator. What I am using is the medela cooler - I find it very handy. The cooler that it comes with is made in such a way that it contours the bottles which makes them stay in place during travel and separates the bottles from one another which is perfect for glass bottles. The only negative to it is that it takes up more space than the Tomme Tippee Insulated Bottle but as far as I'm concerned, if the breast milk is cold for as long as I need it, it can take as much space as it wants. Hope this reply reached you in time."}
