{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004IPBH50', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386489600, 'question': 'Do you need a separate waterproof mattress pad for this mattress? Do you need a separate waterproof mattress pad for this mattress?', 'answer': "The mattress is covered with a white plastic cover. Technically, it is waterproof, but I wouldn't want to have to wipe it down and dry it off every time there's an accident. We use the waterproof naturepedic pads so you can quickly replace the sheet and pad. You wouldn't need two pads though - the waterproof pad alone is fine. Also, I had a couple of the portacrib waterproof pads (flat, not fitted) that I used when the full crib pad was being washed. I just put it in the center and never had a problem with either child wetting around the edges of the crib. It's possible of course but probably worth the gamble if you want to save some money and avoid buying extra pads."}
