{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IPLFNO', 'answerTime': 'Mar 17, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426575600, 'question': 'Have you noticed any sagging after a few months of use?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Short answer: Yes. However, I don\'t actually own the mattress you\'re asking about. Long answer: First of all, I have to say that although I did order this mattress, the one they actually sent me was the seamless version with coils, not the lightweight that I wanted. By the time I received it, I had waited a really long time, because the first shipment never arrived and Amazon re-ordered for me. By the time I got it I really didn\'t care that it was a different type. I didn\'t want to send it back and wait for the right one, and it was actually priced higher than the one I paid for. It was the same brand with most of the same qualities, and it wasn\'t really that heavy. So I can only answer about the coils version, not the lightweight version. Now that I\'m writing this, I wonder if I had originally decided on the lightweight because the reviews mentioned less sagging? I don\'t remember. So mine is the "Naturepedic No Compromise Organic Cotton Ultra 252 Seamless Dual Firmness Crib Mattress" I wasn\'t looking for sagging until I saw your question, so I just checked. My daughter is 6 months and weighs about 16-17 lbs. She has been using the mattress for 2 months. She is a consistent back sleeper and doesn\'t move much during the night. There is definitely an indentation in the middle of the bed in the spot where she sleeps. I still have it on the "firm" infant side and have never turned it over. The indentation is noticeable, but I wouldn\'t say it is dangerous or uncomfortable for her. I may try rotating the mattress now that she\'s old enough and see if turning it over helps. I guess it\'s designed to leave it on one side for several months for an infant and a couple of years for a toddler, but it doesn\'t make sense to me to never rotate it. Now that I can see it I\'ll have to see how much it bugs me and whether I feel like making a warranty claim...'}
