{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IYFMCK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401778800, 'question': 'Is this suitable for a 1 year old (29"+ long)? Looking for something smaller than a pack n play for international travel.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Too small for a one tear old. My grandson is one, 31 in tall and he could never sleep in this bed.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004IYFMCK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Would you recommend this instead of a pack and play? Or did you use this in addition to a pack and play?', 'answer': "I used my nest with my daughter until she was 9 months old and now I'm using it with my son and he is 6.5 months. We use it instead o a pack and play. It's fantastic since it is his suitcase as well. We used it for a few big airplane trips with my daughter and are using it for my sons luggage and and crib for an upcoming disneyworld trip this month. You would still need to purchase a pack and play when they are older (9months plus) but it's awesome when thy are small. It's also great for day trips ,camping , beach trips ...."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004IYFMCK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429167600, 'question': "How would I clean up spit up or diaper leaks? The matress is cotton/polyester, fitted sheet is 100% cotton. I can't find any waterproof protectors.", 'answer': 'I just always laid a blanket under her. It was never a problem. I think you can just wash the mattress'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IYFMCK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427439600, 'question': 'Could this be used with a rocking moses basket base?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think that would honestly depend how far off the ground it was. The sides of the bed on the Phil and Ted are stiff but not stiff enough if your baby can one sit up on his/her own and rock the moses basket over. If the baby is under 7 months and its low to the ground it would be ok but I would be sure that it fits tightly into the moses basket. Check measurements because i wouldn't want it to tip my little one over."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IYFMCK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423900800, 'question': 'Would this fit on two empty seats of an airplane?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The Nest Travel Bed manufactured by Phil & Teds is 30" x 15" x 13" when open. When stored, it measures 31" x 17" x 5". To find the exact seat dimensions of your particular airline and type of jet that you\'ll be flying (usually you can see the jet classification on your ticket information) you can search that on a helpful website www.seatguru.com. Depending on whether the flight is domestic or international it seems that the average economy class seats range in widths from 17"-20". This would be even more for business/first class seating. That being said, with the seat dimensions of two adjacent seats, the 30" length of the Nest (when up and being used) should be able to fit in even the smallest width of two airlines seats combined (34").'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IYFMCK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421395200, 'question': 'Do you think this would work as a bassinet substitution from birth until the baby is too big?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you really can't have a bassinet this would work for the baby up till 5 to 6 months. Once the can push themselves up this will not work anymore."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IYFMCK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418803200, 'question': 'Hi, I am going to be moving a few months after my baby is born. Is this a suitable bassinett for the first three months (meaning, to sleep at night)?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "We have used it for 2 babies... one until 3 months, the other until around 2 months. Our first baby didn't move much, our second is quite the wiggler and she seemed to out grow it a bit faster. We loved this and have given it great reviews. You can pack a ton inside of the luggage side. Great for travel or just using at home! Congrats on the new baby!"}
