{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004IYNG8C', 'answerTime': 'Nov 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415088000, 'question': 'Has anyone used this travel bag for a Baby Jogger City Select without having to remove the wheels? Otherwise, what travel bags would you recommend?', 'answer': "I have only used this travel bag for the uppababy vista, and I was SO disappointed with it. It looks amazing, and definitely protects your gear, but that's about the only good thing I can say about it. Taking off the wheels and packing it up was such a pain and took forever. It took 3 people taking it apart again and again until we packed it up correctly. It is not very intuitively made. The stress of rushing to pack it up and get on the plane was not worth it. Unfortunately, I will not be using it again."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IYNG8C', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410678000, 'question': 'Does stokke xplory fits in this bag?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It's designed for the UBV so even if it does it is unlikely to fit well. I doubt that you'll get the insurance protection either. So would advise against it, even if technically it does fit. Why not just buy the one specifically designed for the explory? Even if it's more expensive, choosing the UBV one is likely a false economy."}
