{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004IYNG8C', 'answerTime': 'Sep 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378191600, 'question': 'what is the dimension of the packaging? as i need to send it overseas, thanks!', 'answer': "It rolls up to about the width of the stroller, and maybe a 6 inch diameter. I don't recall how it was shipped to us from UppaBaby, but you could re-package to the dimensions listed above. If you are shipping with the stroller in it, it is just slightly larger than the stroller folded up without a seat or rear (large) wheels on it. The seat and wheels nest inside the frame when folded. It is a bit of a jigsaw puzzle to fit it in the first time!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IYNG8C', 'answerTime': 'Aug 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376982000, 'question': 'Does the bag hold the toddler seat as well as the base?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It holds the rumble seat as well, but it is tight so be careful with the zipper. My friend was able to fit her rumble seat and her family's winter coats, but she's used hers many times so it's stretched out."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004IYNG8C', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405839600, 'question': 'does this fit a Baby Jogger City Select with the two seats?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We took the gamble and bought this bag reading reviews on other websites that it could handle the City Select with two seats. After about 20 minutes of figuring out the puzzle, yes, I could fit the whole stroller (w/two seats)in the bag. However, I think it will only work one way and it\'s not quick. First, you have to disassemble every thing, that is, all four wheels have to come off, the front posts that hold the front seat, the canopies from the seats, and the aluminum extrusion that forms the foot rests for each seat. Perfectly fold the stroller body together and sit it flat in the bag. Then place the front wheels and posts at the bottom of the bag. With the foot rests off the seats, they fold up fairly flat, stack them on each other atop the stroller (Note: place the head of the seat towards the bottom of the bag and tilt the foot rest towards the back of the bag. Lastly, stack the 12" wheels at the top of the bag, stacking them within each other and angling them against the seats, (when stacking them, alternate the axles, one up and one down). I was able to get the two canopies in placing them atop everything, but it then got pretty tight. When we travel in a couple weeks, I think we\'ll place the canopies in another piece of luggage.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004IZWQYQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377154800, 'question': 'Does anyone know if this toy is compatable with the Fisher Price Look a Rounds or FP Roll a Rounds?', 'answer': 'I am not familiar with those. But if they are like the old peek-a-balls, I would say no. The holes on this toy are smaller than those balls were. But the toy does come with three similar balls with beads in them. My son has learned how to use the toy and LOVES it, he is now 11 months. He has learned to put the balls in the slots and take apart and put together the layers.'}
