{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004L2JX06', 'answerTime': 'Aug 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376550000, 'question': 'Creaking &amp; squeaking noises - did any of you have it &amp; fix it?', 'answer': 'The creaking and squeaking came just before the chair self destructed. Try tightening all allen head screw/bolts. Be careful, this is a poor quality product, the arms are held in with small wood dowels and poor quality glue which will dry out. Also, the bottom back, where the long back rest slates fit in cracked all the way across. We did try to secure the arms by drilling pilot holes and the using drywall screws but it was a short lived fix. If it is new we recommend returning this item. As you can tell we are extremely disappointed with this product.'}
