{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004P7EC7Q', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393920000, 'question': 'Is there any padding to help protect in plane cargo or just a bag? This 1 seems to have good reviews - how is this different than 1 made 4 cityselect', 'answer': 'There is a very skinny padding mostly it is a tuff bag that will not let the bagage claims machine tear up the stroller. If you run the stroller in the machine without the bag it has the chance of getting snagged on something of any grease or dirt that is on these machines would end up on your stroller. It does have seprating pockets on the inside to help keep the dirty wheels away from the stroller fabric. Unless you plan on jumping out of the plane with the stroller bag you would not need extra padding. I have used this bag on three trips and it is a life saver.'}
