{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004PBH7A6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395730800, 'question': 'How does this product compare to the Belly Bandit? Has anyone tried both?', 'answer': "Hi! I have tried both. I like the belliefit for right after delivery. I thought it sucked everything in really well. My only caution would be If you had an episiotomy. I used the Belly bandit after I had shrunk some in size. That one is nice because you can make it smaller as you shrink but I don't think it is as comfortable. Hope that helps!!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004PBH7A6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385884800, 'question': 'Does anyone know how this product compares with the squeem waist cincher?', 'answer': 'Hi Kathy, Squeem is the best body shaping product out there, but if you had or planning on a C-section, definitely get the Girdle Belt first. It will support you incision better! After about three weeks wearing Girdle I purchased squeem. Hope it helps. Good luck. P.S. Be careful choosing a size, visit http://www.bellefit.com/choosing-and-sizing.php to help you with sizing.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004PW4186', 'answerTime': 'Oct 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412751600, 'question': 'on average, how many 4 oz bottles do we need? and when do babies outgrow them to the 8 oz ones?', 'answer': "The answer to that depends on multiple factors but I will give u my situation. I started with 4 and found I was always playing catch up with sterilizing them in time so I finally bought 4 more. For me this worked becUse at one point my daughter was drinking from the bottle all day and only bf at night(so that's about 4 bottles/day at that time) after she turned around 4 minths(can vary by baby) she started to drink more but not at the same time just more often. My friends have told me that breastfed babies mostly drink upto about 4-5oz Max at a time so you never really end up needing bigger bottles. She is now 7 months and we are using the same bottles. If ur baby will consume formula either entirely or supplemented with Breast milk he or she will drink more at a time and u will probably need bigger bottles around the 3-4 month time frame so maybe just purchase 4 of the 4 oz for now. Hope that helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004PW4186', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402642800, 'question': 'Has anyone tried these using a bottle warmer? Does the silicone sleeve start to stretch and does the bottle take longer to warm? Thanks!', 'answer': "The sleeve stays put. Haven't had a problem with that. It does take longer to warm but worth it! Who wants those nasty chemicals that come with plastic bottles leaching into your baby's milk. Also I've used them for my daughter and then for my son, with no issues."}
