{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Q3LBTG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426921200, 'question': "What are these (2) red rings that came with my machine? They don't seem to fit anywhere that I can see and I don't see anything in the instructions.", 'answer': "They go in the center thing that the blade goes onto. too bad you purchased this product. It doesn't grind things well. Be careful that there are not bits of food. Plastic container breaks too easily and the company will not let you buy a new one. They will send you a new one only if you write to them and include pictures of the broken part. So the machine becomes useless if they container breaks."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Q3LBTG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423036800, 'question': 'what is the power rating of this products? 500W ?400W? or 300W?', 'answer': "The bottom says processor 150W, Steamer 500W. I wouldn't buy this item. The container plastic is very thin. It is hard to unlock so when you put pressure, the handle breaks. Mine now has so many cracks in the container that liquid spills out all over . Sometimes the food gets under the blade and then you end up with bigger pieces of food. I only use it to grind food for my dog. We found it is easier to buy organic baby food. I tried to buy a new container. My daughter-in-law was able to get a new one from the comapny for free for me because it broke in less than a year but she had to send the old one and alot of trouble.On their website they show one for $25.00 but you cannot buy it. I called the company and they said they don't sell them because it is a liability because if someone hands theirs down to another person and don't wash it well, their could be bacteria. I told them then if they sold new containers, people wouldn't have to keep the old one that may have bacteria and that would be LESS of a liability for the company. I think they don't want peopld handing down their machines so that people will buy a new one. Also, they said, even though it was more than a year, they would give me a replacement but I would have to send them pictures and find the receipt because how do they know that I really bought one. Really, first I don't have a digital camera and I don't have a receipt within almost 2yrs. I just want to buy one. I don't want a Free one. Again, they want you to buy a new machine not just replace the container. Their policy for not selling a new container is stupid!! So since my daughter-in-law doesn't even use her machine anymore, she's going to give me her container. Now she has a new machine that is worthless without the container and if my container breaks again, mine will be worthless also. Do NoT BUY ThIS baby food grinder."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Q3LBTG', 'answerTime': 'Jul 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404716400, 'question': "I'm using baby brezza for the first time, it flashes all the lights then nothing else works?", 'answer': "It would do that for me as well when there wasn't enough water in the reservoir or if the canister and top weren't totally locked onto the base. I also remember reading reviews where some of them had glitches that caused the lights to flash and it wouldn't turn on. I would contact the manufacturer!"}
