{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004QOY0SY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416902400, 'question': 'What are the dimensions of the quilt?', 'answer': "This a pretty little set, the quilt is a complete square and the weight of the fabric is really only suitable for spring or summer, it has no real warmth but would be nice over a fleece or fuzzy blanket for a little one. As for the exact measurements of the quilt, kit is about 40-45 inches by 4045 inches give or take , it is just about the right size for a crib . I may be off by a couple inches because it is not here with me , it is with my granddaughter . but as i said it is a square quit and not rectangle. Although this quilt was bought for spring weather when our baby girl very little , i know she still likes it because of the colors and pattern. she won't let her mother put it away because she likes the colors. Hope this helped and much happiness you, the family and your wonderful baby."}
