{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004QXZD68', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378710000, 'question': 'Can anyone recommend the Mountain Buggy (plus) +one for running 3+ miles 3 days per week? Mostly on roads and sidewalks but occasionally through a little grass. Do the kids complain in the seats? Do the tires/shocks seem to do ok? does the carrycot or...', 'answer': "I LOVE my Mountain Buggy, it is great in grass and all terrain. My complaints on it would be that when you are going off a curb or a tilt you have to be careful because it is 3 wheeled and easily can go from 3 - 2 if not careful. Also when the second child is still in the cocoon I found that the head was lower than her feet and therefor not super comfy for her, she was long also so her head was right at the back of the first seat. Now that they are both older 2.5 and 9 months I really like it and the child in the back doesn't ever complain. For 30 min running in the stroller I think it would be a great stroller. I always have people come and ask me about mine because it is the same size as a single and not bulky at all! Worth every penny."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004QXZD68', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425110400, 'question': 'Anyone with bigger than average kids use this and are they comfortable? The kids in all the pics seem to have knees pushed into their armpits.', 'answer': "I have a very tall 3 year old in both seats his knees were very close to his chest. In the backseat his feet didn't but barely fit into the foot area. We went with a phil and Ted (that's also what we had previously but wanted to try something different) but sticking with the phil and Ted was the best choice. Although I do love their original models the new ones aren't bad just a little smaller"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004QXZD68', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'We currently have 2 newborn carseats (Chicco Keyfit and one other). Will these snap right in, or do I need a carseat adaptor?', 'answer': 'We had a Graco car seat and it would only snap in to the car seat adapter (separate accessory). We have a 3 year old and now a 1 year old. When the 1 year old was still an infant, we found It much easier to take her out of the car seat and put her in the bassinet behind the toddler seat and have her older brother in the seat. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004QXZD68', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389081600, 'question': "Do you know which model this is? Looking at the Evolution Swift All-Terrain or Evolution Terrain elsewhere for comparison but not sure it's the same?", 'answer': 'This is the plus one, it looks like the same framework, but different attachments. The pluse one can seat 2 seats. Evolution is a single seat.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004QXZD68', 'answerTime': 'Nov 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384502400, 'question': 'What car seats and adaptors work with this model of Mountain Buggy One? Does Maxi Cosi work?', 'answer': "I believe maxi cosi is compatible, but you can use only the car seat with the adapter-- removing the seat fabric-- which makes it a very expensive one child stroller. Better to get a snap n go if that's how you'll use it. It is not very good for baby's back to be in the bucket seat position for long periods of time; personally, the lie-flat newborn cocoon was part of what sold me on this stroller."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004QXZD68', 'answerTime': 'Feb 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392192000, 'question': "We live in Connecticut where it's extremely hot in summer, anyone live in a hot climate that used this? I worry about my newborn getting too hot", 'answer': "We live in Atlanta and we used the carrycot until the end of June when our daughter outgrew it. We unzipped it all the way and she just wore a onesie. She was completely shaded so it wasn't too bad. If it was so hot it would be unsafe I just wouldn't take her out. Hope this helps"}
