{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004R221ZE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370502000, 'question': 'can you use these with bum genius?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes! I have BumGenius Elementals all in ones, but I lay these on top for extra absorbency without too much extra thickness. Works great. Length is good to go all the way from front to back. Even up higher in the front for boys. Doesn't bunch up and they are soft. Gets my 15 month old through a long nights sleep with no leaks."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004R221ZE', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': 'I am new at this. Do they velcro or snap? I am planning to use them for outdoor play, do I need liners?', 'answer': "They don't do either. If you have a cloth diaper (Velcro, snap, or even a diy diaper) these fit right inside and absorb more from your baby. These would be a good outdoors if you're planning on being outside for an extended amount of time. I wouldn't use liners just because of how big they are and how well they absorb. It's up to you though if you want to play it extra safe. A lot of people use both."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004R221ZE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394352000, 'question': "What is the difference between the small and large? I'm registering for a newborn, but would rather not buy new, larger ones in just a couple months.", 'answer': "Hello, the difference in size really isn't that much..being that it's a new born your going to have more protection and peace of mind if you go with the large. Allow room for shrinkage as they do shrink. I would say getting a large you would get some good use out of them. They are very durable and for a newborn I would say there wouldn't be a problem doubling one of them up as they are very absorbent. So if your little one is within 6 to 8 lbs I would say you will be safe as you can double one up. Then later on as he or she gets older they will benefit even better as the coverage will be great on the wetness. I go for large all the time...and they work great. Don't be afraid to double one up. It might be a little bulky but it's still comfy as they are terry clothe. Hope this helps."}
