{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004T6G550', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370415600, 'question': 'Do we need to Adjust temperature?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No..just keep in mind that if you are used to taking the temperature by mouth, the temporal artery will read slightly higher as the normal range. The normal oral temperature range is 97 to 99. The normal temporal artery temperature range is 97.4 to 100.1, so a reading above 100.1 would mean a fever is present.'}
