{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004TYOJNW', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'Can this work with the City Versa seat as well? On the Baby Jogger website, it lists the HyChair as an accessory but never references the Versa.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes I believe it will work with your city select versa seat. As per the FAQ: What is the HyChair and is it safe to use? The HyChair accessory is used to convert a City Select or City Versa seat into a high chair. We designed the HyChair with safety as a top priority. It features 2 auto-lock mechanisms, soft, textured grips to prevent sliding on table surfaces and adjustment knobs which provide a secure fit to table tops ranging from .75 inches to 2.75 inches thick. Additionally we have ensured that the HyChair complies with ASTM F1235-08, the Standard Consumer Safety Specification for Portable Hook-on Chairs. We do not recommend using the HyChair on pedestal tables, glass tabletops, over tablecloths or placemats, or with children under 6 months of age. While the HyChair does comply with all safety standards, it is important to always keep an eye on your child while they are seated in this accessory. It is also the responsibility of the consumer to ensure the accessory is installed correctly and to use good judgment to prevent any potentially hazardous situation.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004TYOJNW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407394800, 'question': 'Does it work well on tables with aprons (like the one in the photo)?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I don't see a photo. I have used it on 3 different tables. 2 of them had a lip underneath. It just depends where it is and if you can lift the seat frame past/over it. I love it and am super glad I bought it. It's not my everyday high chair, but is perfect for camping or visiting friends where you'll have the stroller out anyway."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004TYOJNW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398150000, 'question': 'How far does the seat recline when attached to the table? Do your children seem to get food all over the seat? What age would this fit up too?', 'answer': "You can put the seat in any of the 4 recline positions when attached to the table. I typically put a towel down on the seat when she eats but she doesn't get any more on it than she does with her normal high chair. As far as age, I'm not sure. My daughter is 15 months now and I would still be fine using it. Probably just depends on height and weight. We have loves it for vacations and traveling though!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004TYOJNW', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': 'Does this work as a second seat to the city select?? What attachments are needed', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'Hi. No, it does not work as a second seat to the city select. It can only be mounted to tables. You will need the the seat adapters for the city select in order to utilize a second seat. You can use your city select seat with the HyChair.'}
