{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004VG6FBC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 17, 2011', 'unixTime': 1321516800, 'question': 'Using on Skype or MSN: Does the audio not come through the usb when using it with Skype or MSN?', 'answer': 'Correct, you can\'t hear them and they can\'t hear you. When I first bought this camera I assumed since it "worked with Skype" and since the cameras have built in speakers and microphones, that there would be support for 2-way audio, or at least 1-way audio. Unfortunately there is neither. I guess on the plus side if you set Skype to auto-answer like I decided to do, you can\'t have grandparents and such calling in to the camera and waking up your baby or overhearing a private conversation going on in the room.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004VG6FBC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386403200, 'question': 'it says you can watch on your TV screen, but can you watch it on a laptop or ipad?', 'answer': 'It does have a USB port, and I was able to see it on my laptop once, but the parent unit has to be connected to the laptop, plus the driver is very unreliable. After the one time it actually worked, I could never get it to show up again.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004VG6FBC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 4, 2011', 'unixTime': 1309762800, 'question': 'security: Does anyone know how secure this monitor is?', 'answer': 'The manual says: - Virtually eliminates interference using a secure and private signal and the video unit/camera need to be paired. Pairing Camera: Power on and turn the switch to ON. The power LED for the camera and receiver should be ON. Press the [MENU ] button on the receiver. Select Pairing menu by pressing [A] or [M] key. Press the [ ] button to go into the Pairing menu. Select a channel by pressing the [+] or [-] key. A message will be displayed on the receiver screen. The receiver will count down from 30~0 sec you must press the pairing button on the camera during this time to successfully pair the camera. Press the [ ] button on the back of the camera. If not, the receiver will return to the view screen, and no pairing will take place. Once the camera has been paired, it will be immediately viewable on the receiver monitor.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004VG6FBC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 15, 2011', 'unixTime': 1316070000, 'question': 'Alternatives? Anyone have other good alternatives?', 'answer': "I'm not sure if PTZ is all that practical. I guess it might be cool to have, but I can't imagine much use for it for my baby. I just need a monitor with a good picture and sound quality. Simple design and as you said, big screen. To be honest, I know a lot of people have a lot to say about the SEW-3030 and it's not perfect, but I really like mine. read through the reviews again. The issues with this monitors are with its lesser important features. Just don't use them and you'll still have a very solid monitor."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004VG6FBC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1360742400, 'question': 'does anyone know the range on this one?', 'answer': "I don't have exact range but I was worried about it before I purchase it reading the descriptions. I live in a two story house and I have my camera up in my girls room and I can take the video receiver anywhere in the house and it works. I don't have a huge house about 1600 square feet but did not have problems downstairs and through walls. I see other people had problems with this so it probably depends how thick your walls are..."}
