{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004WI2XU6', 'answerTime': 'May 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367823600, 'question': 'How does it compare to the Contours Options LT Tandem Stroller?', 'answer': "It's a little large then the Contours Options LT Tandem Stroller. The basket is a lot bigger & each child has their own cup holder & it has the parent tray with 2 additional cup holders. On the Optima Aluminum the child seats are even with each other in height. Where on the Options LT the back is higher than the front. So if facing face to face one child is higher than the other. Both are well made & easy to steer. Also there is a little more room between both seats on Optima Aluminum then the Options LT. I hope this helps! Our major things we were looking for where for the seats to recline all the way back & we wanted a double that was front to back not side by side. We found it with this stroller! Good luck!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004WI2XU6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397026800, 'question': 'I am looking to buy one that is about 4 yrs old, does anyone know if this is compatible with the infant adapters i would buy here on Amazon?', 'answer': "The contours optima has a infant car seat holder that accepts just about any car seat because it is just two bars that the car seat sits on. The car seat does not lock into place, it just rests on the two bars. There is a seat belt that goes over the car seat to keep it in place. This way it is totally universal to all infant car seats. Most of the time I don't use the seat belt because the car seat stays in place by itself pretty well. We love ours. Works great. No complaints."}
