{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004WP8QIM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382684400, 'question': 'Do they have a waterproof layer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes, they do. They have a thick layer of cotton fleece and a layer of PUL lining underneath. So, you won't have it seep through to your panties. FYI: I have a small amount of flow, so these are thicker than I thought. That could be good or bad depending on your own personal needs. I bought some from a work at home mom on eBay called goodmamabear that don't have the PUL and I personally like the thinner ones better. Hope that helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004WP8QIM', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': 'how long are the pantyliners vs the regular vs supers?', 'answer': "The liners are 4.5 inches, and the regular pads are 6.2 inches. Not sure if they have any super pads. The liners are shorter and work well on light days, but the regular are good for normal days, or changing frequently on heavy days. I use it as a back up to the Luna cup. I really like that these are soft and not bulky. They don't bunch up or shift ( unless I wear super loose fitting undies, then they may shift just a little, but deffinately less than anything else I've tried. They also fold up real nice, so u can carry them discreetly, or fold them in so you can keep all the icky stuff inside until you can soak them. I soak them in cold water and a drop of pure Castile soap for a day, then wash with the laundry, and they always come out real clean. For super days, I have found that I like the Domino pads the best ( normally just the first day or two), then I prefer the Charlie Banana pads the rest of the time."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004WP8QIM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380524400, 'question': 'What material???', 'answer': "Well, the inside is a nice super soft cotton, and I'm not entirely sure what the outside is made of, perhaps a polyester ? It's slighty slick material. The great thing is that it cleans very nice. I normally soak them for a day in cold water and a few drops of Dr. Bronner's castile soap. I keep it in a small tupperware container descretly stowed in the bathroom. Then I rise them out and throw them in the wash. They come clean every time. Hope this helps."}
