{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Y426XM', 'answerTime': 'Jun 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402038000, 'question': 'how to fold to make it like a bag?', 'answer': "The instructions aren't very clear on this but you have to take the storage pouch on the back of the cover and flip it inside out. You should see a blue strap that's meant to be the strap for the tote ( it's underneath a little flap so you may not see it at first). You can then roll up the the cover from the bottom and stuff it inside the storage pouch, but I prefer to take a little more time to fold it because it makes it look like the picture. Here's how I do it: Step 1: I do the inside-out thing with the pouch then lay the cover flat and turn it so the back is facing me. The two wings on the side should already be folded in. Step 2: I fold both sides toward the middle over the wings so the two sides are touching but not overlapping (this will later make a rectangle as opposed to a square, which I find to be more bulky). Step 3: I fold it up in thirds from the bottom so that I'm left with a rectangle with both of the leg holes facing up. Step 4: I push the rectangle into the pouch (note that the front of the cover rolls in on itself to form the front of the tote), making sure that it's as flat as possible and all four corners are pushed completely out. This whole process takes me around a minute when I really try to get it perfect but, like I said, it works just as well if you spend ten seconds just rolling the whole thing into the storage pouch :-)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004Y426XM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386057600, 'question': 'Is this item machine washable?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes & it holds up great. I'd gotten a few for baby showers & hand me downs but I found this one on my own & it's THEE best! It also works great as a highchair cover which was another selling point for me. Some of the others were more padded, but don't work we'll as high chair covers because of the padding."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004Y426XM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387353600, 'question': 'does this cover have any padding?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, but that's not a con in my book. Makes it SO much easier to get on a cart while holding my daughter. I tried a whole bunch of padded ones, from light padded to sanitarium cell worthy, but found I preferred this one. Granted, if your child is not able to sit up straight yet, padding may be needed. Though I think a child should have mastered sitting up before being put in the cart. The non-fabric material is also so easy to wipe down in between washings."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004Y426XM', 'answerTime': 'Aug 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408086000, 'question': "Does this cover fit well on a highchair? I just want to make sure it doesn't ride up and collapse inside the chair when a toddler moves around.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It is a little big for a high chair, so it is bunched up. I haven't had any trouble with it riding up or collapsing though."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Y426XM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387267200, 'question': '8 month', 'answer': 'My daughter was around 8 months when I put her in the shopping cart for the first time. As soon as they can sit up on their own then they can use it. My daughter always liked sitting in the cart with it, looking at the sights and people. Even now at over a year she still loves it. Hope this helps!'}
