{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004Y99M52', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393574400, 'question': "I recently bought this car seat and I feel like the Belts are not long enough, isn't this case? With my son's coat on I don't find enough belt for him", 'answer': "Bulky winter coats should not be used in any car seat. In an accident the fluffiness of the coat compress causing the straps of the seat to be very loose which would result in the harness not keeping your child restrained. In a car seat you should use a light weight fleece sweater/jacket that is more than enough to keep your child warm in the car. You could put the jacket on backwards after you've secured the child in the seat for extra warmth or keep a blanket in the car."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004Y99M52', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388217600, 'question': 'Is it easy to remove from base? Considering buying this seat and an extra base for our two cars rather than buying two separate car seats.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I bought it for that reason too but honestly... No. It's not like an infant base and if you have a small child you have to think about where to put them while you are trying to switch it between cars. It's not light. We have found it easier to have two separate carseats for our vehicles. I still love this seat, though, so it's in my car (which is used daily)."}
