{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0050GD2AY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379055600, 'question': 'Having problem leveling the base. watched video, Pressed the button - not able to slide the base up/down. defective? Need to unlock something first?', 'answer': "There is nothing that you have to unlock first. I found that if I installed the carseat (facing the correct direction) with either the shoulderbelt or by attaching it to the bars in the crease of the seat with the attachments on the base, it leveled itself. It should be pretty easy, so if you are having additional issues leveling it, it may be defective. [While it is super easy to install now after doing it a few times, I was ready to throw it accross the room initially, so I get the frustration. Everything is actually pretty user friendly so don't overthink it too much. Hope that helps.]"}
