{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005123EHI', 'answerTime': 'Jul 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404630000, 'question': "It was stated in a review that static cling products don't lessen the heat in a car,only the glare of the sun(?).This doesn't make sense to me. Help!", 'answer': "I guess that could be true as all the windows probably won't be covered. BUT...it definitely lessens the heat on myself after I put them up. I have even put one on top of another at times when I wanted more shade. They are so versatile, awesome and cheap! You can put them up quickly and take them down quickly (which I often do when we change direction and sun is in a different place or if blocking view for driver). I also often fold one in half and stick it on part of my passenger side window when I don't need the whole window covered. TIP: I found when I put them on the dash in the sun to warm up for awhile before putting them up, they cling better. Hope that helps!"}
