{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005194OJ8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393228800, 'question': 'Can you put an infant car seat in this stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The quad is a great stroller, HEAVY TO LIFT, but very functional and compact for the size. However, I have a Britax Chaperone carrier and it would not fit in the stroller, but a smaller car seat may fit, depending on the orientation that you are hoping for. You would probably have a better chance of it fitting, if it was placed in the backrow sideways vs in one seat facing front / back. I don't think their would be enough clearance facing forward in one seat, it would have to go sideways, BUT I could be wrong. I didn't use my car seat, I just took out my newborn and secured her in the back seat with blankets and the seat buckle, it worked perfectly."}
