{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0052QYLUM', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1365145200, 'question': "Having issues with interference and my router/wifi. I've tried changing channels in my router settings, but still same thing. Any suggestions?", 'answer': 'We too were unable to utilize our Wi-Fi when the monitor was on, and we dealt with it for many months. But I found a solution, by accident, but it worked: I saw that my neighbor wi-fi signal and mine were all overlapping on channel 6, so I logged into my wi-fi router by typing the IP address for it in my web-browser (this is how you probably initially set it up some time ago) and change the CHANNEL from "Automatic" to a specific channel...in my scenario i changed it to channel 1. After I did that we get no interference from the monitor and can use wi-fi and monitor seamlessly. Hope this helps. Also, we have a Verizon FIOS router (n) technology.'}
