{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0053TSFV4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382943600, 'question': 'Are these plates microwaveable and dishwasher safe?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "They are not microwavable safe according to the packaging, but I know my husband has inadvertently heated food up once or twice for 20-30 seconds, so I know they don't melt instantly! They are dishwasher safe, though the manufacturer recommends doing so no more than 10 times. I have not seen any degradation, however, after having put them in the dishwasher about two dozen times over the last two years. I do make sure to hand wash most often, though."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0053Y2B6E', 'answerTime': 'Jul 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404457200, 'question': 'Do you spray cloth diapers off before you drop them in the pail? Is mold ever an issue?', 'answer': 'We do not spray off pee diapers, but once we introduce solid food we spray off poop diapers. If you are exclusively breast feeding (i.e. no solid food at all) you do not need to spray. As long as you are washing regularly (ever 2-3 days max) you should not have a mold issue. We never have. I hope that helps.'}
