{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0054WHTRG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'How does this pack up? Is it portable?', 'answer': 'It is portable. If you mean just on a daily basis for quick pick-ups, it folds up with everything intact. There are snaps on the two corners so you just fold and snap to acquire a half size shape. So just picture it half the size it is with the arches on the outside. I do that at the end of each day. On the weekends, I unsnap the arches and fold them up just as they were packaged using the original plastic straps and then fold the mat into a smaller size to put in the closet. My granddaughter is now 10 months old and I still use it. She still loves to lie on the smooth, silky, colorful fabric and look at the pretty colors and animal imprints. The little monkey that used to dangle from the arches is one of her favorite little guys. I did not expect to get this much use out of the mat. I had expected to box it up for long term storage when I decided it was time for the arches to come down but there are still things about the mat she likes. I babysit three full days a week and put this item at the top of my list of favorites. The designer got it right.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0054WHTRG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375686000, 'question': 'Can you attach additional toys to it?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The hanging toys are removable and there is one extra "toy hanger", but it doesn\'t have holes up and down each arch like some of the previous Tiny Love Activity Gyms. I really like this one, but my mother in law has the older version and I actually prefer the way that one is set up. The toys hang better for the baby\'s vision and grasp.'}
