{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0055LV4HC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404198000, 'question': 'Will this gate be able to accommodate a top mounting width that is a little different than the bottom mounting width?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Maybe if they\'re not more than .5" different. It only lock latches on the top so that would need to be the narrower width. The bottom doesn\'t latch, it just slides into a metal bracket, so it could still close and latch on top if the bottom is a little wider. If the width was too different, the top might still latch, but a child could push on the bottom and get an arm/leg/head through so you might have to modify the bottom bracket by using a piece of filler wood between the bracket and the wall.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0055LV4HC', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403852400, 'question': 'Are you able to use this if one of the mounting sides is a bannister?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "if it's a wood bannister you can drill right into it...only 4 screws per side....if metal railing...we strap a piece of wood to it and then mount gate into wood"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0055LV4HC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357804800, 'question': 'Does anyone know the difference between this and the Evenflo Top of Stairs Gate Plus?', 'answer': 'Seems to be same. I got two of this one and we love it.'}
