{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0055PJUL0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397458800, 'question': 'I have a Trek FX 7.2 will this work?', 'answer': 'I have a Trek Multitrack 730 (which is like the great great grandfather of your 7.2) and had no problems mounting/using the Tyke Toter with it. We just took the training wheels off his own bike this spring, but my son loved riding on the Toter with me when he was younger.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0055PJUL0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': 'Does the bike seat have to be in an elevated position to fit this underneath it? My bike seat is at the lowest setting for me feet to touch ground.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'That\'s the ideal set up but it was uncomfotablre for a petite like me. I have a 20" bike and I mount the tyke toter in the lowest possible, touching the bike\'s body so I can have the seat to its lowest position with my feet at least slightly on the ground. It also gives me the comfort that my child\'s more steady in front of me than in that elevated position.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0055PJUL0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'I have a Schwinn Men\'s 700c OR2 28" Hybrid Bike, front suspension travel. Will this work with it? TIA', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I THINK so... I looked at the pic of your bike on google and it should work...it works on my hybrid! It attaches to the seat post, so the front suspension shouldn't have anything to do with it. The only thing that matters is you don't want to be leaning TOO far forward like on a racing or road bike, because then you are banging into kiddo. You have to sit a bit more upright. With a hybrid you should be able to adjust your handlebar height or some other dimension to make it work out for you. We love ours and have been using it for just about 2 years."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0055R6AYS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378882800, 'question': 'Does this fit the Maclaren volo stroller?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I have an uppababy gluxe and this bag is great, we have flown with is several times and the stroller is in great shape. I have not used a volo, but the dimensions are as follows: Folded Volo: 10 x 14 x 41 \x03Folded uppababy gluxe: 12 x 16 x 42.5 So I think it would fit great with a little wiggle room. Hope that helps!'}
