{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0057EEC3A', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397718000, 'question': 'What does it mean with "Orthodontic"? Is this to correct an existing problem? or to promote natural development of a baby\'s teeth?', 'answer': "Neither, actually! While pacifiers certainly have their benefits, they have been linked with dental issues in later life (underbite, overbite). Orthodontic pacifiers are created with a rounded top and a flat bottom. This is thought to minimize pacifier-induced dental problems because the shape more closely conforms with the infant's mouth."}
