{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0057VZBB0', 'answerTime': 'May 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368255600, 'question': 'Does the car seat snap into the stroller?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, it fits perfectly. We love this stroller and have not had any problems with it. I've had 3 other carseats and strollers with my older kids and this one is by far my favorite. It is very pretty too."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0057VZDHC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'See mixed reviews on the padding. Some say its too thin and others say its comfy. Also being that there is no comfort grip on the handle, does that make it more difficult to hold and or carry?', 'answer': "It's not any easier or harder to carry than a few others I've used. The annoying truth for me was that every car seat this style is something I didn't want to carry around very far because it's heavy and I just gave birth. By the time my pelvic floor was strong enough to carry heavy awkward things, baby was big and old enough to rarely make it a feasible idea. I carry the car seat when he is sleeping, and only to load it in a stroller or grocery cart. And this particular model doesn't even clip onto the grocery cart like most do. I would generally call the padding thin. The head support padding is useless. The shape of it pulled the straps to make it ill fitting on my baby. The nurse/lactation consultant helping me install my car seat advised that I take it out because it was restricting the proper fit of the belt and to just use a rolled up burp rag. While this seat is ok, I find a lot of things annoying and would go with another model next time."}
