{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0058HTIMG', 'answerTime': 'Jul 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405926000, 'question': 'Does it really only weigh 8lbs or is that a typo? OTher carseats are 21 lbs.', 'answer': 'It really does weigh just 8 lbs. That is the seat itself not including the base which you never carry around it just stays in your car. My daughter is pregnant with her 1st baby and we were car seat shopping, it was confusing. A lady with three kids and one on the way asked my daughter if this was her first baby, she answered yes and the lady said "follow me" and she led us to this car seat. She said "this is the easiest lightest best car seat around." We bought it then and there and then bought an extra base to so my daughter coukld have a base in her cvar and one in her husband\'s so they don\'t have to move the base each time they are in a different car. My daughter\'s baby will be here any day now but she said the car seat and bases are installed and easy to do. We\'re more than happy with it!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0058HTIMG', 'answerTime': 'May 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401174000, 'question': 'Does this work with the city select stroller? Not the mini but the bigger version?', 'answer': 'I have the City Jogger "Elite" and I got the infant car seat adapter bar. It never "clicked" for me on the adapter so I never felt too comfortable using it so I only used it once or twice with the strap that was on the adapter. With that said, I read and looked at YouTube videos and it seemed to work for them, but not for me. However, I loved the car seat especially with the snap and go stroller. I felt it was more convenient to use the strap and go stroller anyway.However, I come from a tall family and my little one is tall so in some ways I wish I would have gotten a car seat that went up to 35 inches because my girl grew out of it by 8 months. So many opinions and things to think about but it will all come together! Good luck!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0058HTIMG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 24, 2012', 'unixTime': 1327392000, 'question': 'Is this the Chicco Keyfit 30 Magic?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This is not the Magic. The Magic only comes in the "Rattania" color... which is basically brown. My husband and I just received the "Graphica." It is black and grey. The fabric seems nice, but the shade is the same size as the regular Keyfit 30. The big selling point on the Magic is the extended shade. I have not seen the Magic on Amazon... only at BRU. It is rather new though so maybe it will be on here soon. Hope that helps.'}
