{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005A7VI9A', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1369724400, 'question': 'What is PLA filling?. Is it polyester', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'PLA stands for polylactic acid. It is a "polyester" in the chemistry-sense of the term, but it is not *the* polyester (which is PET). PLA is plant-based (corn starch, sugar cane, e.g.) It is compostable. I went for the PLA filling because if needed you can run the pillow through a washing machine, not that you should do it very often.'}
