{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005ASKQ42', 'answerTime': 'Jun 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404025200, 'question': 'Is the whole sleeper washable?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not certain. There was a vinyl mattress that I would wash with vinegar and water spray, along w extra sheets I would launder regularly. We traveled with them and used the co-sleepers for probably a little under a year and in that time they didn't really get dirty. I imagine any soiling could be wiped off w a simple detergent, water, and towel combo (The ole fashioned, elbow grease, spot treatment). In short, I think throwing it in a washing machine might be weird and very loud bc of the metal and plastic leg parts (which fold up easily) but hand washing/spot washing is probably best. I hope that helps!"}
