{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005AUYEHA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411369200, 'question': 'How well does the waist/hip strap transfer the weight? Any 6-foot or larger men have an opinion on how well the weight transfer works to your hips?', 'answer': 'It does a decent job, but in order to be comfortable for any length of time you definitely need to spend some time adjusting all the straps. I\'m about 6\'2" and sometimes wish it would sit an inch or two lower on the hips, but once its all adjusted have carried my boys for long walks (2 or 3 hours) in comfort (well as comfortable as you can be with an extra 15 or 20 lbs hanging off your chest).'}
