{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005AUYEHA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408863600, 'question': 'Our baby is short (2nd percentile, 24") but almost 7mo. We want her facing out, but our current carrier seems too tall. Will this work better for her?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'My daughter is 5mth old, and is ~24in tall. She\'s able to face front. The "bib" rests just under her chin. She\'ll be more comfortable at 25inches, but it\'s totally doable. For what it\'s worth, This is Fantastic. I\'m a big dude, and can wear this just fine.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005AUYEHA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407481200, 'question': 'Does this model have a pocket or place for phone/keys like the original ergo?', 'answer': "No, unfortunately it does not. It has great back support for mom but doesn't appear super comfy for baby. I just bought an ergo... my baby is more comfy in the ergo but for stability, line running through an airport, I like the bjorn he's very secure and it saves my back. For his comfort, I use the ergo."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005AUYEHA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406962800, 'question': 'Can u sit with the baby facing out in this carrier? Is it a good choice for long air travel?', 'answer': "Baby can face out in this carrier once he can support his own head. They recommend you have them face in until then. Not sure about air travel; I know that anytime I want my son to be still and quiet, he's going to be squirmy and fussy. Presumably even more so on an airplane surrounded by irritable passengers, ha ha. Good luck!"}
