{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005BEKUIW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407135600, 'question': 'Does this diaper come with any inserts or do they need to be purchased separate?', 'answer': 'The inserts need to be purchased separate. They have different sizes, I had the smalls and then used doublers and then went into the larger inserts, skipping the medium size all together. The shells last a long time, so are worth the cost. We only cloth diaper with best bottom and have had the ones we have for 17 months and they still look new. Hope this helped answer your question.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005BEKUIW', 'answerTime': 'Nov 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385798400, 'question': 'Can you use Flip inserts or other snap-in inserts, or Best Bottom brand only?', 'answer': "I've never used flips but I use prefolds and other inserts in them and it works perfectly. These happen to be one of my favorite diapers and we have a large collection of all different kinds of cloths."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005BEKUIW', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421913600, 'question': "I am a first time mom due in April. I'd like to go for these, how many shells and how many and what kind of inserts would you recommend for my stash?", 'answer': "I would recommend trying different kinds of diapers until you find what works best for your baby. But I will admit, this is one of my favorites!! I much prefer the snaps to the Velcro, because they are softer and more flexible. I use these covers with bamboo and charcoal bamboo inserts. I wash every other day. I think at least 20 covers and 40 inserts is a pretty good number to get started, but I'm sure you will have so much fun finding different diapers, styles and prints you will get many more!!"}
