{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005EGYLMS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404370800, 'question': 'Is this sturdy enough for my 4 year old to color in his coloring books on top of?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It is sturdy enough, but the sides don't stand straight up. The way my daughter's carseat is built/positioned...or maybe how I connected it, the crayons would slide down into her seat easily. I think it was a good purchase."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389772800, 'question': 'Is anyone concerned about child being cold since he or she stays low to the floor?', 'answer': "I would assume if room was a proper temperature, shouldn't be a problem. Also, mattress buffers. Of course, if in a basement or cold room, could be an issue, I guess."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424937600, 'question': 'Does anyone know the height limit? My son is very tall(34 inches) for his age and I want to get ample use out of the product. Thanks.', 'answer': 'We bought this as a crib for our grandson, who stays with us at least two days a week. He is now 18 months old and is more than 100% of his age group for height... and he still sleeps in this Babyjorn travel crib.. we love it... very easy to pack up and take on vacations, as well as using it every week for sleep overs and daily naps...'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423209600, 'question': "How is this different from Baby Bjorn's Travel Light Crib, currently sold for $199 on Amazon? I can't find this model on Baby Bjorn's own website.", 'answer': "The difference is that the 190$ one is all net. This one from the base before the net so your baby's face doesn't inhale the dust from the floor since his face will be close to the floor."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403161200, 'question': 'Does the mattress fit inside the travel bag?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': 'Can this be used as a playard also?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It could be used in a pinch as a playyard while on vacation, but I don't think it would satisfy that need regularly. Not only is it small, but the mattress just sort of hangs in the fabric at the bottom, meaning that the sides go up a bit and I think it would not be that sturdy a surface for a little one to move around on."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': 'We are expecting twins. Can this function for two? Have any moms of twins used this?', 'answer': "I don't think two babies oldef than 3 months can fit in there."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395644400, 'question': 'Does anyone know if this can be carried on a plane vs. having to check it in? It looks a little big as a carry on but not sure.', 'answer': "I didn't inquire about carrying it on. We just checked it through since we were on Southwest. It's a square, and it's longer/wider than the depth of most overhead bins, for sure. Though, it's definitely not bulky. Streamlined and weighs something around 11 lbs."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395385200, 'question': 'How steady is this? It looks like it would be fairly easy to tip over even for a 1-2 year old.', 'answer': "It's pretty steady. The legs spread outward, which makes for a steady base. We love our travel crib! It's light and easy to travel with."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384761600, 'question': "I have a question about the silver color. In some pictures I've seen it almost looks like a frosty, pale blue. Is it, or is it more grey?", 'answer': 'It is really silver, no blue/icy effect'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF3J2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403420400, 'question': 'Up to what age can it be used?', 'answer': "It would all depend on how tall and heavy your child is and how likely they are to make serious attempts to climb out. Our son is a tall 2.5 and we still use it when we travel. While he is starting to fill it out with how tall he is, because it is so deep, he doesn't even think about trying to get his leg over the side or anything. Also, he is quite happy and relaxed sleeping in it so he doesn't really care to get out. I really debated buying this because of the price and the fact that we already had the typical pack n play, but I must say it has made extensive travel for us much more pleasant. When baby brother doesn't sleep well, no one sleeps well!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383462000, 'question': 'Is this a good substitute for a bedside bassinet when the baby first comes home?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "My wife and I would say no (but you could get differing responses). It's not a good substitute for a bassinet because a bassinet is meant to mimic closeness to mom/parent and at the same height as their bed. The Travel Crib is great as a substitute for a real crib and it packs up quite nicely. I am currently responding to you on vacation with my wife and 5.5 month LO in Playa Del Carmen Mexico and she is sleeping soundly in it right now!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392796800, 'question': 'do regular porta crib sheets fit babybjorn travel crib light 2, silver?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I used Regular Crib sheets and they fit fine.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382166000, 'question': "Does anybody use this also as a Playard? We would like to use it for this purpose too, I'm wondering if it's not too small?", 'answer': 'I think it depends on the baby - we used it for travel but my son also like to play in it. Though I thought it was a little small he seemed not to mind.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385625600, 'question': 'Which is best - BabyBjorn or Lotus travel crib for a very tall and heavy baby?', 'answer': "We own the Lotus travel crib and really like it. Since you know about the Lotus crib, then you are already aware of its advantages in terms of portability and ease of use. The way the Lotus crib is designed, it is definitely suitable for babies regardless of length and weight. It did take our baby a little bit of time to get used to this crib (which based on reviews doesn't seem to be the norm?). The added benefit is that Guava Family is a small US-based company and offers fantastic customer support."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'May 8, 2012', 'unixTime': 1336460400, 'question': 'Safety Concern? Would this have the same safety concern as the PeaPod?', 'answer': 'The fabric is light enough to be able to breathe through it. We own it and I tested the breathability myself.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395471600, 'question': 'Can this be used as a play yard like the pack n play?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Maybe for a young baby. The sides are soft. They stay up, but aren't as firm as a pack n play and it is smaller than a pack n play. (is a great travel crib)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416470400, 'question': 'May I know the difference between Light and Light 2?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Baby Bjorn no longer makes this version. The new one has mesh all the way down, which seems safer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404370800, 'question': 'Used for airplane travel: Does it fit inside a large suitcase or did you have to check it as a separate piece of luggage (at extra cost)?', 'answer': "I can fit it into a large hard suitcase that I have, but it is the only one that it fits inside of. I would check the dimensions of the crib against those of your suitcases, mainly because it has to be rectangular, it can't be sort of rounded at the top. Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374994800, 'question': 'how sturdy is it? can an angry toddler knock it over?', 'answer': "Anything is possible, but I think it would depend on the size/strength of your toddler. The base sits on the floor and is much wider than the top. Even if baby tried to run the length of the cot in an attempt to flip it, 1) I think the padded mattress would slow him/her down and 2) because the top is smaller, I don't think baby could get up to a speed that could cause the cot to tip. However, if the cot was close enough to a solid object (ex: nightstand) and baby was tall/strong enough, either the cot or object could move. There is a height max on this cot. I sold our pack-n-play and bought this new for our third kid and haven't regretted it. We have been traveling all summer and it is infinitely better than standard pack-n-plays."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EWF4BY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372921200, 'question': 'good for twins? up to what age/weight? thanks in advance for taking the time out to answer!!!', 'answer': "It is not as big as a pack n' play, but I think it would work for twins if they are not too big. My son is almost 2 and he can still fit in it, although probably not for too much longer."}
