{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005IA84M8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'What kind of security must be used with this system and/or the wifi so that others outside or elsewhere cannot also be "monitoring" the baby?', 'answer': 'As far as I know, the only video monitors that can\'t be hacked into have to have a "video encryption" guarantee on them. This does not. Audio or video monitors run on local frequencies and if someone in the neighborhood has your model, they might accidentally be able to tap into the sound or image of your monitor. Honestly, I\'m excellent about only turning it on when the baby naps. Otherwise it is off, so I decrease my chances of leaving an open opportunity of viewing where the baby sleeps. People who are forgetful and leave the monitor on all the time are the only ones who need to be more vigilant. Having said that, I\'ve used this device religiously for 16 months and have never picked up the image or sound of some other baby\'s nursery. So I\'m guessing that since I haven\'t picked up someone\'s frequency, then nobody\'s picked up mine because it would glitch both ways otherwise. Hope that helps.'}
