{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005IT8PMI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'can the actual pillow be washed? the description just mentions the outer case.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No, it should not be washed as the wool is supposed to be moisture resistant, so if forced to take in moisture by putting it in the wash the wool will lump up and shrink. I had to wash my son's pillows after he got sick when simply washing the pillow case was not sufficient. The wool took forever to dry, when it did, it was rolled up into balls. It can be reshaped but you must use a steel comb to comb it threw, which is very time consuming and takes alot of effort. Better off buying a new one, make your own pillow case to put over it for double protection."}
