{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005IWM6DY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402902000, 'question': 'Does this come in separate parts so it fits a travel case? Is it easy to assemble?', 'answer': "The part with the toys hanging from it removes (I remove it sometimes when I give my daughter a bath I place on towel on the seat and lay her there for minute while I set up her bath). It snaps into brackets on the sides. The cushion/seat comes completely off so it can be washed and believe me if your baby has a blowout you'll need to wash it and it comes clean great. The frame will fold flat so you could travel with it. It's simple to put together you just need to screw the feet onto the bottom. I remember it being pretty easy. I did it myself. It's worth the money. If you have a multilevel house I'd get two of them. I wish we had another one."}
