{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005JDOYF0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387785600, 'question': "Does this stroller fold and unfold with one hand? Also, does it stand up on its own after it's folded?. Lastly, is the basket underneath sturdy?", 'answer': "Yes, this stroller easily folds and unfolds with one hand. It does NOT stand on its own once it is folded. The basket underneath is very sturdy considering it's a fold-n-go stroller. I use it to carry my large diaperbag which weighs around 15 lbs."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005JDOYF0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385971200, 'question': "Can you take a walk outside with it? I know it's great for malls &amp; travelling but can you walk around the block with it until baby fits a reg stroller", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Absolutely. It's very sturdy."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005JDOYF0', 'answerTime': 'May 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400914800, 'question': 'Do you use it for longer walks? Would it be sufficient for somebody who intends on taking long walks with the baby?', 'answer': "It strolls and maneuvers very easily. However, the wheels are hard so if the surface you are walking on is rough there will be air of vibration and I don't think the wheels would last long on a rough surface. Mine has had heavy use and has lasted through 1 baby and is now being used for a second baby so it is durable. I use a Bob stroller for our numerous long walks because the tires are like bicycle tires."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005JDOYF0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425884400, 'question': 'Since there is no sun shade, what do you do to block out sun? Any recommended products that fit well over car seat?', 'answer': "You snap your keyfit 30 into this caddy and the keyfit 30 provides the sunshade -- and it is barely a sunshade indeed. We used a lightweight blanket draped over the keyfit 30 to help get the sun out of my baby's eyes, but, yes, this is a limitation of this system."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005JDOYF0', 'answerTime': 'Oct 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412492400, 'question': 'Is this a good urban stroller? Anybody able to compare it to the City Mini GT?', 'answer': "It is very light weight, easy to fold and open up, the large basket at the bottom is very useful. The price is reasonable compared to other strollers, and it works seamlessly with the Chicco keyfit 30 carseat. We live in the middle of a city with a long set of stairs going up to our home. I can't imagine having to carry a stroller heavier than this. It's also easy to steer."}
