{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005KWL0OI', 'answerTime': 'May 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367478000, 'question': 'What are the foods that can be put in this?', 'answer': "You can put almost anything that will fit, but just be sure it's age appropriate for your baby. Here are some of the foods I have put in here for my baby: Breast milk mini ice-cubes (great for teething) Frozen yogurt cubes (also great for teething) Frozen and fresh fruit (bananas, apples, pears, peaches, mango, etc.) Vegetables (peas, potatoes, avacado, tomatoes, etc.) I have not introduced meat to baby yet, but if you're at that stage you could dice up meat and put it in the feeder as well. Hope that's helpful. :)"}
