{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQRCIU', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376377200, 'question': 'How does this compare size wise to the Britax Marathon? Our 6 year old daughter is finally getting too big for her Britax seat. Hers is the older model obviously that sits higher up then the newer models. I am just looking for size comparisons as we...', 'answer': 'I ordered this seat just as my best friend ordered the Britax Marathon. My son is just under 70 lbs. and 4\'1" at 5, so we\'re constantly running into challenges with sizing. I think that this seat allows for more room and growth as the sides adjust out to accommodate his broad shoulders and the headrest moves up enough to wear I could sit in it comfortably (I\'m 5\'4"). I like the narrower base that the Diono has versus the Marathon because we drive a Scion XD with a fairly small backseat. With my booster, I can still fit an infant carrier (no base), and another *narrow* booster for when I\'ve got extra kiddos. It\'s a tight fit, but it does work. However, the Marathon seems to take up the majority of my bestie\'s backseat and while it is a decent sized seat, I don\'t think it allows for the adjustments that the Diono does. I hope that helps. :)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MQRCIU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1357113600, 'question': 'Does the cover remove all the way so it is machine washable?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. We have removed ours. It is simple to remove and replace. You should use gentle cycle if you use the machine and air dry.'}
