{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQRCIU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373439600, 'question': 'Fit three across? Will this fit as the third one across with the other two?', 'answer': 'I just called Diono and they said NO, that 51" across is the limit and the Monterey is wider...you probably already figured this out by now, but you need the GTX or the RXT to fit three across :)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MQRCIU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373526000, 'question': 'Will it fit 3 across a midsize car seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We have a Mercedes R350, more of a cross over. We opted to not get the center seat but a console instead. There is ample room for a third to fit with room to spare. Our sister cared for our kids for several days while we were away. She has a Mini-Coop, certainly a compact car. Three would fit across her back seat. They are only slightly wider than those cheap booster you can pick-up anywhere. We have 2 of these as well for back-ups. In the Mini Coop with 3 across, I don't think you would be able to use all of the built-in cup holders but you might be able to use one cup holder on each seat if positioned correctly. Hope this helps as they are comfortable and safe seats. The ability to fold them flat when removed makes them great to change between vehicles and for travel."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MQRAMI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390377600, 'question': 'Will this seat fit in a Honda Fit?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I wouldn't see why not. I have an electric Focus and the seat back lost some room due to the battery. I have the passenger side seat up a little bit and my 99% tall daughter (37 inches) fits fine, but doe kick the back of the seat. This seat 'fits' much better than the Britax, etc convertibles because the base is more the size of the seat."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQRAMI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1366441200, 'question': 'How many inches is it in rear facing mode?', 'answer': '31 inches in its longest point. It is 15.5 wide at the top and fits in between the front seats when my husband drives and has the drivers seat back further than I do. We drive a Subaru outback. Hope this helps...we love it so far!'}
