{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQR96U', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395644400, 'question': "How long can your kids last in this before they are too tall? I heard that it doesn't work well for a booster?", 'answer': "The seat is outgrown as a booster at the same time as the harness. That's why it doesn't make a great booster. If you harness to the max, the child's shoulders will already be almost to the headwings so they won't fit any longer to use it as a booster. The R120 will last a little longer as a booster since it doesn't have the wings, but not by much."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQR96U', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427180400, 'question': 'Hi! My 1 yr old cries in the car, as did my older son in the same car seat. Wondering if the crying would stop or ease up in a new one. Any expierence', 'answer': "The car seat is padded with memory foam. That being said I have seen parents struggle with car seats no matter what the brand. My advice is to make sure that your child is properly fitted for the seat and that you observe whether or not your child's reaction is one of discomfort or discontent."}
