{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQR794', 'answerTime': 'Dec 14, 2012', 'unixTime': 1355472000, 'question': 'Diono Radian - does it fit well in the backseat of a car? Anyone with experience here?', 'answer': 'Matrix has fairly decent room, but you should be leaving 1" clearance to the back of the seat in the rear-facing position so you will definitely have it somewhat forward. If your passenger seat usually has a 6\'+ person in it they may not be particularly comfortable. Still, worth it to keep the seat rear-facing until 2. US is way behind changing their rear-facing recommendations.'}
