{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQRAXM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393574400, 'question': 'Has anyone traveled (via air) with this? Do those backpack straps (pictured in their ads) come with it? How comfy is it to BP thru an airport?', 'answer': "I have traveled with the carseat and alone with a 2-3 yr old, both internationally and domestically. Now, I'm a pretty strong woman, but it's not very joyful carrying this over your back along with carry on bag, stroller, kid, backpack, and or whatever you choose to bring with you. It does not come with the back straps, they have to be purchased separately (I purchased on amazon) and they have about a 6 inch long padding strip (which is very minimally padded). My daughter is 3 now and I have no plans to travel anytime soon, but if I do I'll be checking in the seat, not bringing it on the plane. Now, the seat itself is incredible, it's fits on any airline seat, its comfortable, safe, amazing quality. Although I can't really give a great experience traveling with this seat, I do have to say it is and was a lot easier than when I used to have to travel with a regular carseat. It is also alot easier if you are traveling with an adult companion (I've always traveled alone with toddler with this seat), and can find a way to add a little extra padding to the strap, then you will be golden! Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQRAXM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393488000, 'question': 'how is the seat fabric? we have a britax, and my son sweats so much when in it.', 'answer': "Our son sweat a lot in his Britax B-Safe infant seat, but we have had this seat for about 9 months and haven't noticed any issues."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQRAXM', 'answerTime': 'May 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400569200, 'question': 'which car seat is better, the radian ext or the britax?', 'answer': 'I have both. I *LOVE* both. I say if you need room, go with Radian, If you have the room and your child has outgrown the 45lb weight limit or nearing it to RF in the Radian, go with Britax (Frontier 90) Both HIGHLY HIGHLY rated for safety and overall so either one is great. Radian over Frontier: - Child is less than 3-4yrs old. - Child is below 45 RF weight limit (of the radian, Frontier doesn\'t RF) - If you need more room - If you plan on flying Frontier over Radian: - Child is over 3-4yrs old. - Child is at or near the 45 RF weight limit (of the radian, Frontier doesn\'t RF) - If your child is on the "bigger" side'}
