{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQR9J2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393228800, 'question': 'How does the RXT compare to a RECARE ProRide? and is there any other material besides nylon?', 'answer': 'The ProRide provides very little legroom for the child rear facing, and does not last as long rear facing by a significant amount. The Proride is also difficult to get the child in because of the shape of the shell. The Radian lasts an average sized child until around 4 rear facing, and the ProRide would not provide that. There are other materials and colors if you click around the Amazon Radian page or the Diono page.... and each Radian model has different fabrics.'}
