{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005MQR9J2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393401600, 'question': 'Is it easy to change reclining positions when forward position? where is located the reclining adjuster and how many reclining positions there are??', 'answer': 'There are only two positions and must be adjusted prior to your child sitting. It is basically a wedge that pops up the front part of seat (near childs knees) that gives the seat its recline. It doesn\'t really lay the child back but more so elevates their legs from a flat position. Its a bar mechanism you pull into place located underneath the base of chair. Gives approx. 1 1/2" difference.'}
