{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005OFLFGO', 'answerTime': '29 days ago', 'question': "Has anyone had a hard time getting their back wheels to stay in place? We bought two of these and can't get the wheels in right.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "We bought three of these, one for each grandchild. The wheels were tough to get in but after watching the video my husband got them in and we haven't had any trouble with them staying in place. Don't be afraid to really use some strength on them. Make sure you have them in the correct position, it almost seemed to me that you are putting them in backwards. Once they click into place they are locked in and stay. Good Luck and I hope you get this mastered. The grandkids as well as the adults have had hours if fun riding these."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005OFLFGO', 'answerTime': 'May 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399014000, 'question': 'Are these wheels hard plastic or are they roller blade wheels? thanks!', 'answer': "They aren't exactly roller blade material but a very durable hard plastic, high quality. We've had these for two years now, using them inside and outside on the street, still in perfect condition."}
