{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005OIBG88', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391500800, 'question': 'It "features 3 level adjustable mattress height support," but it doesn\'t give specs on the height of each level. Do you know how tall each level is?', 'answer': "There are 4 levels on ours. There are 4 holes for the mattress spring frame to hang from. At it's lowest level, the hole is 11 inches from the floor, but since the frame hangs down from that attachment, with a 5 inch mattress, the top of the mattress is 13 inches from the floor. The holes are in 3 inch intervals, so going up, the next hole is 14 inches from the floor and the top of the mattress would be 16 inches from the floor. Third hole, 17/19 and the fourth hole, 20/22. So the highest mattress height (with a 5 inch mattress) would be 22 inches. This crib grows with the child. Hope this helps."}
