{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005SP2LWW', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400137200, 'question': "I see spandex is used. Is this similar to a Moby Wrap? I'm looking for something for older babies/toddlers (30+lbs). Is this it?", 'answer': "This is similar to a Moby in that it's a stretchy, knit fabric; IMO, the Boba's fabric is significantly thicker and more substantial than the Moby. User instructions say it can be used for older toddlers, but from experience, stretchy type carriers don't feel as supportive once they get that big. I used this carrier mostly when my baby was very young. I'd recommend a structured carrier (Ergo, Boba 3G, Beco Soleil, Kinderpack, etc.) or a woven wrap -- besides offering more support for the weight, you can wear on your back which is much more comfortable as the child gets heavier. Hope to help!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005SP2LWW', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420704000, 'question': 'I am using this wrap with a 6 pound newborn. It seems like it stretches out quickly and she ends up sitting pretty low. Is that as expected?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Anne- The fabric has 5% spandex in it so that it will mold to you and your little ones body. Please make sure that you are tying the wrap tight against your body. We have instructional videos on our website and on Youtube. If you need further assistance please let me know and I would be more than happy to chat with you over the phone. (888)567-9727. Thanks, Jenna Benson'}
