{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005SPCXKC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373439600, 'question': 'What are the height and width measurements for the panel that goes against the back of the child?', 'answer': "At the smallest width, the section that would hold your baby's tush is approx. 11.5 inches wide. The widest sections which would if wearing front carry-style are at chest/bust height and are 15-16 inches wide. It's almost light bulb shaped when laid flat. The height is approx. 15 inches from the very top (not including head cover) to where the belt seam begins. I have used mine with my baby since she was just a hair shy of 3 months and aprrox 12 lbs."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005SPFFPW', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379833200, 'question': 'Boba or Beco, which is better? Trying to decide and they both look similar. Thanks!', 'answer': "I bought both the Beco and the Boba. I personally preferred the Beco Gemini so I kept it and I returned the Boba. The Beco Gemini was softer material, more comfortable and I loved that I could crisscross the straps in the back. I didn't like that the Boba straps go right underneath the armpit area, it wasn't comfortable for me and the straps cannot crisscross in the back."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005SPFFPW', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358755200, 'question': 'what is it about the boba that makes it more comfortable than the ergo?', 'answer': "The Boba sits higher on the waist than the Ergo. Of the two, I prefer the Performance Ergo. It's more durable and better for hot weather. The Boba is canvas and doesn't hold up too well after a washing. Hope that helps."}
