{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005SPFFPW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': "Boba or Onya Cruiser? How useful are the pockets on the Boba 3G and what is the width of the seat and length of panel on this carrier? I'll be travelling with my 2yo+ toddler and hope to carry our passports/boarding passes and some cash for easy access...", 'answer': "My son is only 11 months and we have the Dusk, so I can't talk about the black fabric issue. The back carry is simple especially since your 2yo will probably be able to help you by leaning forward when you need her too. However I don't think that the pockets are big enough to fit your passport. The bottom pockets fit my iPhone 5 and that is about it. The larger pocket, can be used to store the hood or something else. You might be able to fit the passport there, but you would have to have the hood dangle out. I did see a mom use the Boba 3g for her daughter who looked to be about 2. Her arms were over the top of the straps, so if you are expecting to have her whole back in the carrier I don't think that is realistic. I loved our Boba. It made security a breeze, some of the airports didn't mind if I kept my son in it and let me go through security as is. Other checkpoints made me take him out. I used a front carry for that because I find it easier, and my son is easily distracted and not always able to lean where I want him. I'd Recommend it, but be aware that the pockets are small ish. There is a purse holder strap so you could put the documents in there and then clip it on and not worry about it."}
