{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005SPZG5Q', 'answerTime': 'Apr 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397977200, 'question': 'So, do you think this would work as a drink (beer bottle) holder on a pony carriage going down a bump road?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It would definitely hold a beer bottle. If the bottle is very tall it you may want to drink some of it so that the holder isn't close to being top heavy, other wise it will tip over and empty your bottle for you. I've only had that happen with a very tall coffee cup. If you tighten the green knob it should hold very well. I've never had it come loose on me during hour long walks. The bumpy road may pose a problem that i haven't encountered. Depends on how bumpy. As long as the beer is shlossing out of the bottle on the bumps then this should still be ok. I'd check it very often until you are sure it is holding tight for an entire outing. I would definitely buy more of these if I had places to put/use them!"}
