{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005U6ZFG8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'is there an insert for newborns that can be attached to this carrier ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It does not require an insert like some other carriers. (Ergo) the waist band folds up and snaps to make the body of the carrier shorter to accommodate a newborn. I believe that is a feature that has changed on the newest model recently released.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005U6ZFG8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384761600, 'question': 'I know the capacity is 45 pounds, but has anyone used it for larger toddlers? Ours is tall, and 36 pounds, and was uncomfortable in the Ergo. Is this really different?', 'answer': "I carry my son in mine pretty often, but not for long amounts of time. Probably no more than 20 minutes. He is 30lbs, so not quite as big as your child. I think the Boba distributes the weight really well. I don't feel any pain when I carry him. It feels more like a weight pulling me back, like a turtle with a shell, but not to the point where it is painful. Idk where you are from, but there are baby wearing groups near me that hold meetings so that you can try out different carriers. I found a group on Facebook. That may be a way to try before you buy."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005U6ZFG8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384588800, 'question': 'What is the carrying capacity? How many pounds can it hold...', 'answer': '45 lbs. My son is 26 pounds, and is 18 months. There is still plenty of room. It is also very comfortable to carry, and evenly distributes the weight so it is not on your shoulders'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005U6ZFG8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384675200, 'question': 'is this the only the baby carrier or can I carry toddlers in it too?', 'answer': 'I\'m still using it with my 2 year old who is 30 lb and 36 inches and we still have room left to grow in it. One note though is that my husband is very tall (6\'5") and wide so with the fabric stretching to fit on him and the the toddler in it there isn\'t any extra room when he wears her. But for me at 5\'4" we\'ve got plenty of room.'}
