{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005UV0UDG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367218800, 'question': 'What kind of playyard mattress and mattress sheet should I buy with this product ?! Please help!!', 'answer': "The floor piece of the playpen is padded, so it can be used as a bed without buying another piece. We have a crib for every night use, but use a playpen when we're on vacation, etc. Unless you're planning on using it as a primary, every night bed/crib, I wouldn't worry about spending the extra money on something that you aren't going to use as often and would be difficult to store. I would recommend the sheet, though, as the fabric/lining doesn't seem overly comfortable. Graco sells fitted sheets specifically for their playpens, but the sizing seems to be standard among brands of playpens and sheets."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005UV0UDG', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370415600, 'question': 'Does the changer attach to the bassinet or to the playard itself, i.e. can I use it as a playard with a changer (without the bassinet)?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'it attached directly to the play area frame. if you look at the picture you can kind of see it. the bassinet is a removable mat with a hanging net that has rods that run underneath it. if you enlarge the picture you can see plastic gray clips on both ends one is a solid piece the other looks "broken". those are the pieces that attach to the play area which they are a pain in the butt to clip on/off. once the netting is clipped on with the rods the mat rests on top of it. so long winded yes you can use the play area with the changer, because the bassinet is also the mat for the play area. hope this answers the question.'}
