{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005UV0UUE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382684400, 'question': 'does this product come with a mattress? its a co-sleeper correct? thank you', 'answer': "It isn't a co-sleeper. It is a standard packnplay playpen but the floor raises up to be a bassinet or elevated portable crib. The floor is padded. Then on top of this sits a cozy bassinet sleeper with lots of good comfy padding and fleecelike material on it. The changing table on the other side is great. We use ours in our living room. It comes in quite handy. It even has shelving when the floor is raised up. Perfect to store all types of necessities. I highly recommend this pack n play. It can be used for a long time. It even has music and vibration for soothing your baby."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005UV0UUE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381474800, 'question': 'Can the napper come out and be used separately on a different surface or can it only be used in the pack n play?', 'answer': 'I just recvd this item as a gift a love it. I would say that the napper cannot be used on different surfaces. It does not have any kind of "stand" per se (or legs) to hold it up. Also, you cannot carry an infant in it. The handle in the picture is merely for decoration and snaps off and on very easily. I still like the product tho bc, from previous experience with my other two girls, some newborns sleep better propped up a bit. The napper is the perfect angle for this. It is roomy enough for her to use for several months if not longer. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005UV0UUE', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386230400, 'question': "When the Changing table isn't in use, does it flip over and hang on the side? Or is it always sitting inside the bassinet area like that?", 'answer': "No, this model doesn't hang over the side, it does however lift out easily when you press the two pins on the ends."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005UV0UUE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395903600, 'question': 'Can you leave in the changing table when you take out the napper and use it as a bassinet?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You can. Just keep in mind though that only half of the bassinet is then exposed. If your baby is able to roll over, he may roll under the changing station. It is recommended in the instructions to not use the changing table in this manner. Also, it is worth noting that the napper is rather difficult to take on and off, but the changing station is simple. You could remove it until you need it and just click it back into place.'}
