{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005V09R26', 'answerTime': 'Oct 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381042800, 'question': 'what size bulbs?', 'answer': "The light bulbs came with the chandelier. They were in individual little boxes. I believe they are 120V 25watt. It is a plug-in chandelier but has the pieces to be hard wired. If you use it as a swag/plug-in light, there is not a toggle type switch to turn it off and on. You have to plug it in and unplug it when you are done. It's a pain. The only solution would be to have a toggle switch put on/re-wired, I suppose, or leave it plugged in all the time if there is a light switch that is hooked up to the outlet it is plugged into to turn it off and on. That is the only real downfall. It is a very nice, pretty chandelier. All put together right out of the box. I do love it. Mine is in my bathroom. Hope this helps!"}
