{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005VM62QS', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361692800, 'question': 'I will have an 18 month old and a newborn in July. Is there a back seat for this that has a buckle or is it just the little plastic seat?', 'answer': "I bought this for my 2 1/2 year old daughter and newborn son. While I think it's a great stroller, I think my daughter would have appreciated an actual seat. She still likes to take the occasional nap, and when we're on the go, there's no way she can nap on the bench. The seatbelt is ok for the bench, not the best, but it works. When you have an infant carseat though, it actually sticks out past the back of the seat and hangs slightly over the bench, which means it does get uncomfortable for the child sitting on the bench. An 18 month old would be too small to stand at that point, especially since the handles are too high for younger children to hold on to, so they would have to sit and be a bit uncomfortable. I think it would work perfectly for slightly older kids but not for younger ones, and especially in your case when they'll only be a year and a half apart."}
