{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005VM63X0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359532800, 'question': 'Has anyone traveled with this stroller on an airplane? We are taking a trip to Disney and are thinking of taking our stroller.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Agreed. We literally got back from California tonight. My kids are 16 months and 3 and a half years old. Very few cars could accommodate a stroller this big is the only downfall, we rent mini vans, by the time you get it and your luggage in, you'll be happy you did. I have a toyota Highlander so it's no biggy for us around home. For anyone who doesn't know though, you don't actually take the stroller onto the plane, once you are about to board the plane from the airwalk you drop the stroller there and it gets checked, then you pick it up in the same place after the flight.. Most air lines check strollers and car seats for free fyi as well. Your wording sounded like you planned on taking it onto the plane, so I thought I would clarify that."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005VM63X0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397113200, 'question': "What are the folded dimensions of this stroller? With everything assembled? Just trying to figure out if it'll fit in the back of my minivan.", 'answer': "I have smaller sized mini van (Mazda MPV). It is difficult to fit the stroller in the back with all of the seats up, but if you remove the front snack tray and both sun shades it will fit with no problem. It is a bit thick, so if you have a long minivan it would be easier. I do not, so it still fits with some work!! It's a bit of a pain, but I do like the stroller. I will try to fold it and measure at home for specifics."}
