{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005WH3RV0', 'answerTime': 'Oct 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412578800, 'question': 'Would an average 5 or 6 yr old fit in this seat still forward facing? isit be comfortable at that age?', 'answer': 'My son is only 2+, so I can\'t speak from experience, but with top slots of 17", it is comparable to most other convertible seats, and should easily accommodate an average 5 or 6 year old comfortably. We expect to be able to keep our son rear facing until 4+ years old, and you would still have two headrest positions available once it goes from rear facing to forward facing. That said, I would not buy this seat if you only plan to use it forward facing. For the price, you are better off getting a Britax Frontier (20.5" top slots) or a Britax Pioneer (19.5" top slots) - both will safely and comfortably keep a child forward facing until they are absolutely mature enough to sit in a booster properly 100% of the time. In case you find it helpful, here is a link to a very thorough review of Peg Perego convertible: http://csftl.org/peg-perego-primo-viaggio-5-70-convertible-car-seat-review-and-giveaway/'}
