{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005WH3R9M', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392883200, 'question': 'peg vs clek foonf? any thoughts?!', 'answer': "From what I've read, I'm going with the Peg over the Clek Foonf. One reason is because it seems to be one of the lighter seats, although Amazon says 11 pounds and the Peg website says 21. I believe the Clek is like 25 or 30, maybe more. The Clek has a great wheeled travel bag, which might change my mind if we did a lot of air travel. But we mostly travel in the car, so the simple Peg travel bag will work. And the Clek Foonf can be difficult to clean if you have a major spill (or motion sickness issue). I'm a clean freak so it needs to be fairly easy. We have the Peg infant seat which is basically the same seat in a smaller version and I had no issues removing everything to clean it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005WH3R9M', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372834800, 'question': "What is the Height Limit for Rear Facing? I don't care about weight limits my baby is tall &amp; I want him rear facing until age .", 'answer': "I'm not sure of exact inches. However, their website says the childs head must be one inch below the top of the seat. I've had my 4.5 year old rear facing in it. She is 3 and 1/2 feet. Hope that helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005WH3R9M', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426230000, 'question': "Is it possible to recline this car seat in the FF position? How is the baby's head in the FF position? Does it fall forward when the they fall asleep?", 'answer': 'It doesn\'t recline in FF mode but the seat is designed into a slight reclined position. My 4 year old sat FF in this seat in a long flight and he had no problem sleeping, no head slump. Just a friendly reminder that a "baby" should not be FF until at least 2 years old. This is a fantastic seat I am very happy with it, it\'s very nice. My 10 month old rides in it very comfortably RF and falls asleep as soon as he gets in it and he screamed in his infant seat. :) Hope that helps.'}
