{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005XJ2VGY', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388476800, 'question': 'Do the wheels lock into place?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, but since the wheels are made of plastic or rubber, the chair can still be pushed around by my 15 month old. We have tile, but I'm sure the same thing will happen on carpet. Not a deal breaker. The chair does not move at all when the baby is in it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005XJ2VGY', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368601200, 'question': 'can this be used at a dining room table when baby gets older?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Just now, I went to look at my chair to see if it fits under my dining room table right now, and it does. The eating tray can even remain on the chair, but it sits above the table top. You can also make adjustments in height on this chair, but so far, my grandson hasn't needed any. But, it is nice to know that you have a lot of flexibility when using this chair as children grow and change. For me personally, I feel as though I made a very wise choice when I bought this chair. It has been a joy to use, and has caused me no problems whatsoever. However, you must remember that this is just my experience and my opinion. I can't guarantee that things will be exactly the same for you."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005XJ2VGY', 'answerTime': 'May 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1369465200, 'question': 'Is the "snack tray" (underneath the main sliding big tray) removable? Or do I have to slip my child\'s legs under it when placing her in? Thanks', 'answer': 'No, it is not removable. I was worried that it might be difficult to get my boy into the seat (he is 6months old at 19pounds) but on the contrary now I am glad that the snack tray is fixed so that it keeps him in place while I buckle him up.'}
