{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0062NJ4ZG', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'Is the food processor good for making fine purees for young babies(5 mon)? Seems that unless you have lots of food, the blender is not a good option.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Absolutely! We started using our Sage Spoonfuls set when our son turned 6 months (he's now 17.5 months) and we're still using it beyond his food needs. The blender has the option of attaching to the bowl or used as a wand. And, because of that, you can make various batch sizes. You would absolutely love this set. We only have our one son for now and the blender/processor worked excellent for one pure up to multiple purees. We have done it all and am so glad we have this set. One thing I did was purchase a inexpensive coffee grinder to grind my oatmeal/barley/rice/etc cereals. That made the cereal more fine powder and easier for my son to eat. That was the only hiccup I found with Sage. It just didn't get the cereal to the consistency I wanted. But that's like a $5-10 purchase on the side (since we don't drink coffee). The recipe book alone is so worth this set and is so simple to follow. My son has tried everything in the book and there's even some yummy combinations that we didn't necessarily think would go together. And now our son has a good palette. We still pure quite a bit of food so I can add to my other recipes (to include our son still has a favorite breakfast of non-pured oatmeal with quinoa and pured carrots). Oooo...and the processor is great for soups and sauces. You will not be disappointed with this set."}
