{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00636X2KK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387353600, 'question': 'What is the distance between the bottom of the trunk and the lowest branch and can this distance be customized?', 'answer': 'The distance between the bottom of the trunk and the lowest branch is 36 inches. The tree is shipped in several pieces that you then line up together to put on the wall. The distance between the bottom of the trunk and lowest branch could be customized if you wanted to cut off the lowest branch. As you can tell from the photo, it is a smaller branch. The next one is about 10 inches up from that. You could also cut inches off from each trunk piece, but realize that the width of your trunk on the two corresponding pieces may differ after you cut them shorter.'}
