{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0065LTW52', 'answerTime': 'Oct 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381302000, 'question': "Can you use Medela or other brand storage bags / supplies with this Dr. Brown's pump?", 'answer': 'The comment about customer service... they are extremely helpful and happy to replace parts for free. The silicone part wears out which is what causes loss of suction. The time that they wear out ia usually about a month but again, they replace it for free and will even send you extra so you have back up. Milk can get on the cloth piece if you WAY overflow your bottle. Ive been using this pump 5-6 times a day for 7months and never had the milk get on that part unless i turn the whole piece upside down then om done pumping. It is ok for it to get wet, in fact you are suppose to rinse it. It has to be completely dry before you can use it which drying with a towel usually works.'}
