{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0067GKHVS', 'answerTime': 'Jun 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401865200, 'question': "I use wipes for art clean up and I don't use them every day. Does this container prevent the wipes from drying out better than regular pop up boxes?", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "I think so. There appears to be an air tight seal around the top of the lid. I have one upstairs and one downstairs, and only use them intermittently at this point (1-2x a week?) and I have never had a dry wipe come out. Even when I used them both multiple times every day (newborn...) I never had an issue with dry wipes. I disagree with the other answer - if you're using the wipes frequently then you're constantly taking the top (potentially driest) wipe out. The only way these would dry out is if you leave the top open when not in use. Also it's virtually impossible to close the lid on a wipe - they come out nice and clean without pulling other ones out. I always had that issue with the plastic wipe containers - part of a wipe sticks out and I can't close the lid all the way, which leads to drying out wipes..."}
