{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00687S3ZI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': 'my opening is 63 " how many extensions would I need?', 'answer': 'First, we really like this gate. A well built and funtional product, better than most if not the best. However, this wide of an opening will be difficult. This gate works by pinching between the jambs of the opening creating a large pressure and compresssive force in the gate, enough to flex the gate substantially (way it is designed). With the wide opening the gate may become unstable. You could give it a go with three 10.5" extensions (10.5 x 3 + [28"-32"]) = 59.5"-63.5" opening.'}
