{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0068IGSHM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422950400, 'question': 'Is this FAA approved and allowed in aircrafts for use?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "I'm not sure what you're asking. But if you're wondering if the strap (the car-seat pictured is not included) can be used on a plane, I would say no. Your child must be in your lap or in a seat of their own (possibly in a car-seat, depending on the airline) and your luggage must be tucked under your seat or in an overhead bin, so there would not be a way to keep them attached while flying."}
