{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006IKTYL2', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388476800, 'question': 'What is the width between the arms, specifically the part of the arms towards the front of the chair.', 'answer': 'Hi Sara I\'m going to do a few measurements for you since the arms are angled and the padding is removable. 1. At the very front of the chair (farthest from the back rest), at the top of the arms (farthest from the seat) the width between the wooden structural arms is 26" 2. The removable pads start about an inch from the front of those wooden structural arms. At the top of the arms (farthest from the seat). The width between the padded arms is about 24" 3. The width narrows at the back of the chair and at the bottom of the arms. The width between the padded arms at the back of the chair is about 23" at both the top and bottom of the arms. At the front of the chair, the width at the bottom of the padded arms is 22"'}
