{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006JTNXDW', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392105600, 'question': 'Is it consistent or it changes the temperature every time? Can you fully trust it?', 'answer': "It is consistent +/- 0.3 degrees.... There are variables of the user technique and subject. For example, I've had patients take off a hat and it reads at least a degree or two higher than it will only 30 seconds later. Also, distance from skin is a factor. You must consider too that body temperature, while remaining within a narrow homeostatic range, does vary itself from moment to moment. What I will say is that this meter INVARIABLY detects elevated temperatures and fever."}
