{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006JV4HNK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406012400, 'question': 'Would it be safe to hook on to a glass table of 10 mm, less than half an inch thick?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The default 100% safe answer is NO that is not safe. Though the table can most likely handle the torque and weight of your kiddo in the seat, it changes the physics just a bit when you snug the handles down on the glass like a vice. Supposing you install it on glass, you then have compression pressure on the glass in addition to the weight and torque of kiddo in the seat. Our kid would sometimes bounce around in the seat a little bit and bang on the table which in your case would cause a lot more stress on the glass (which doesn't give any clues that it is about to break), so I'd suggest not putting this seat on a glass table. I *might* reconsider if the glass were 25mm+ thick and if it were a smaller table, but when talking about the safety of my kid, I'd just avoid the situation 100% especially when you consider what could go wrong..."}
