{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006JV4HC6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392796800, 'question': 'We have a flat, no "skirt" bar top. Do clamps get super tight to secure the seat from the child pushing off under wall preventing sliding of bcwards?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, we have a similar table with just a flat wood surface that would be perpendicular and the lower clamp would grab onto the underside of the table. It clamps on very tightly when applied and the baby would not be able to slide the seat backwards. The clamps are also made out of a rubbery substance that grips very tightly. We have also used this seat an many restaurants, including tables with table cloths, and it grips strong enough to keep the baby from pushing backwards. Its an awesome chair!'}
