{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006JV4HC6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422604800, 'question': 'Does the chair fit securely,or do you feel like it shifts,slides out at times, or could be pulled off by another child? I have a wooden table.Thanks!', 'answer': "it fits very securely. The parts that go on the under side of the table are fit on on a long screws with rubber at the top (where it actually meets the table). You screw the rubber parts up until it is as tight as you want it. So how tight it fits, depends on how tightly you screw the rubber parts up to the bottom of the table. They do not come loose either. In fact, if you screw them too tight, it gets a little difficult to undo them. I have used it on my glass table at home (though I stopped as I wasn't sure about the integrity of the glass table top and my 25 lb 14 month old. I have used it at my office a few times, attaching it to my wooden desk. My desk is a shiny, slick finished wood lamanate."}
