{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006JV4HFI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407222000, 'question': 'We bought this about 4 months ago from amazon, but the stitching is coming loose on one side. Is there a warranty from the manufacturer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Not too sure, but usually any product that you buy through amazon will have a warranty, especially one for this amount'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006JV4HFI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402297200, 'question': 'What is the ideal age for this chair? Would it be worth the investment if my twins are 1?', 'answer': "I started using this chair when my son was about 8 months old -- basically once he had good head control. He couldn't even sit up independently but he could sit in this chair just fine. He is now 13 months and 20 pounds and we still LOVE this chair! We plan to use it through the recommended weight of 37 pounds, which is about what our almost 5yo son weighs! I will add that we leave it attached to our counter and do not travel with it to restaurants, etc., as it is a bit of a pain, especially considering you'll never really know if it will fit on the different styles of tables when dining out. Overall it's a WONDERFUL chair and we love how little space it takes up while allowing our son to dine at the table WITH the family! Hope that helps! :)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006JV4HFI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401951600, 'question': 'can you use this on a round table?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006JV4HFI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'Does this one work with the fast dining tray?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "According to the review I saw, and the item description, yes it does. I don't have the tray, just the chair (which we love). I honestly didn't know there was a tray. But it sounds like the reviewer is still using another mat to catch food that falls in the gap between the table and chair. I have the may she mentions (tiny diner) and it is more of a hassle than anything."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006JV4HFI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391500800, 'question': 'The main table I am planning on using this hook on high chair has a 2-inch lip and a 4-inch skirt. Do you think this will fit on this table???', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If the skirt is close to the lip of table, there won\'t be enough room for the chair to slide into the table. My chair advances inward about 4-5". Hope this helps you.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006JV4HCQ', 'answerTime': 'Jul 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406444400, 'question': 'What is the recommended age to use with children? Meaning what is the youngest and oldest based on typical averages?', 'answer': "it really depends on your child's ability to sit up. my daughter was five months old and was able to sit up with assistance. we put padding (blankets) around her when she sat in this chair so that she didnt have a lot of room to move and we made sure she was always supervised. as far as the oldest age, that depends on the child's weight. I believe it holds up to about 35 lbs."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006JV4HCQ', 'answerTime': 'Jun 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401606000, 'question': 'How far do the clamps go into the table? We have a leaf and are concerned that the gap between the edge of the table and the clamps is not big enough', 'answer': 'Upper arm rests ~5" into the top of the table. The lower arms rest ~2.75" inside the table.'}
