{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006MVHCN4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396162800, 'question': 'Is it really 32.5" long? Some reviews say it is actually longer. Trying to fit a smaller BabyLetto change table and am concerned with length.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It is 32.5" long and just the perfect size from newborn until whenever you wanna use it. My baby is 26inches at 4mos right now and he still has a lot of room. He wiggles and able to roll now, so this size is perfect. We use this on top of my baby\'s dresser which is waist high. I feel this is safer than a changing table, which he will outgrow really fast too. I would suggest not using a changing table, you won\'t really need it. As far as the quality of this product, it is the best. I even use it when he starts to be fussy and crying, this pad is so comfortable that he calms down when he lays on it. I\'m planning on getting the same brand of mattress for his crib when he gets a bit older.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006MVHCN4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382252400, 'question': 'Oeuf recommends to "use with a waterproof cover" but all I see on Amazon are waterproof pads. Any suggestions?', 'answer': "As I have the oeuf dresser I didn't want to buy any other pad, it works ok. If it gets wet I just clean it with a sponge w/water and soap and put it to the sun or just in the window for an hour and its done. If the size is right you can try a waterproof one instead, I don't think you can go wrong with either."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006MVHCN4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388908800, 'question': 'Do you need a cover for this changing pad or can you use it as is?', 'answer': "You don't need a cover, but I would recommend one."}
