{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006NWMNR2', 'answerTime': 'May 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400742000, 'question': 'Does the anti rebound bar "work" if the seat is rear facing in the middle? I have an SUV w a low box btwn the driver and passenger front seats. Thanks', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "As long as the seat is rear facing it will work. It prevents the carseat from rebounding into the seat. It doesn't affect the recline or positioning of the carseat. For a secure fit, we reclined our rear seat while installing, then brought the rear seat back upright to really wedge it into place. We have a Subaru Forester and the rear seats have two positions, although the difference is marginal. And for clarity, the anti-rebound bar shouldn't be used if the seat is forward facing."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006NWMNR2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394607600, 'question': 'Has clek changed the "annoying" harness release lever "hole"?? Is there any improvements/differences between the 2013 and 2014 models? ty!', 'answer': "I don't know if it has changed. contact customer service at www.clek.com or call them on their phone"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006NWMNR2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394607600, 'question': 'A lot of reviewers complained of fwd facing "head slump" Can this be avoided by reclining the seat? Isn\'t that how other car seats work? ty!', 'answer': "Hi! The seat does have an adjustable recline. However, it may not provide enough recline depending on your car's seat cushion angle. When my foonf is in a car with really flat seats, I make it more reclined by boosting the front of the seat up with a piece of a styrofoam pool noodle. The Foonf manual includes the range of angles that are acceptable for both forward and rear facing. I check the angle with my iPhone app just to be sure. This is how we avoid head slump. But in some vehicles it is not a problem whatsoever."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006NWMNQ8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392883200, 'question': 'Would this be comfortable for a 9 month old baby? also, how does it fit rear facing in a lexus RX350? Thanks!', 'answer': 'I think most 9 month olds are still able to fit in a rear-facing infant carseat. I would probably stick with the infant carseat until your kiddo needs to change to a convertible. Our Foonf fits in our small ford focus so I assume it would fit in the lexus SUV. The retailer Buy Buy Baby will let you install a Foonf in your car if you want to try it out first.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006NWMNQ8', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'Any input on cleanability of major incidents that cannot just be wiped off (think gastro, vomit galore)?', 'answer': 'I have been able to successfully and easy clean off weeks old dried grape juice. Vacuum and wet cloth worked well.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006NWMNQ8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394607600, 'question': 'A lot of reviewers complained of fwd facing "head slump" Can this be avoided by reclining the seat? Isn\'t that how other car seats work? ty!', 'answer': "I just recline it. Sturdiest car seat ever! My kid loves it because it's higher than his old seat and he can see more."}
