{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006NWMNPO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374217200, 'question': 'is this carseat difficult to rethread and install? would it take up a lot of room in a lexus RX350? Thanks', 'answer': "It depends, are you installing it rear facing or forward facing? Rear facing: It does sit up pretty high on the base, so depending on where you have it in the back seat and how tall you are, it could block your view looking out the back windows. Other than that you shouldn't have a problem fitting it in there. To install rear facing you have to take the seat cushion off, thread the seat belt through, close the lock-offs, and put the seat cushion back on. It's not necessarily HARD, once you get used to it...but it's not super quick, and it's not the easiest to understand for a grandparent or babysitter/nanny who doesn't use the car seat every day. Forward facing: pretty easy install, especially if you can use the rigid latch but you have to check the latch limits for your vehicle first. Clek has apparently approved the use of the rigid latch AND seat belt at the same time on this seat, so you can call them about that too. The REACT technology doesn't do much good if it's not installed with latch (for forward facing)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006NWMNPO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374044400, 'question': 'I want to know if anyone has installed this seat in a 2001 Isuzu Rodeo and where did you place it? Thanks', 'answer': 'Great car seat. Child must be 1 yr old. I installed it in a 2012 Kia Sorrento in the middle seat in the back of the car. Very stable no movement what so ever. Using the stabilizer bar also.Car seat is no larger than most on the market for this level of quality. I have a orbit toddler car seat which is larger. the plus of the clek is the stabilization bar to stop it rotating in an accident and the fact that it has reclining features.'}
