{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006PB2B6O', 'answerTime': 'Aug 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408950000, 'question': "Is there a 'stroller' system that I can convert this car seat into a 'sit and stroll' like thing that I can pull through the airport etc.? Thanks!", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'We purchased a converter strap called the "traveling toddler" from Amazon. I think it was under $20, which allowed us to strap this car seat directly to our rolling luggage. We were very happy with the way that it worked. And it even fit down the aisle of our Southwest Airlines flight. Although it was a very tight fit. Definitely practice hooking and unhooking the strap at home without a child in the car seat before you travel or it will be a nightmare in the security line. But after everything is adjusted and you practice 1 or 2 times it\'s very easy and quick to attach and detach.'}
