{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006PB2H40', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389340800, 'question': "How wide of an entry way does this cover? I'm looking for a gate for a 64 in wide entry - would this work?", 'answer': 'I went on to a number of other web sites when I was considering this purchase because Amazon did not really mention the opening maximum that it would cover. Walmart says it fits up to 60 inches, and that was what I used as a gauge. My largest opening is 55 inches. Think about this: there is a bar at the top and one at the bottom and they unscrew sort of to fill the opening and they are like tension rods. With a 64 inch opening it may not even make it across the opening or won\'t have enough tension to work. You could "build up" the opening with a block(s) or maybe even a tennis ball at the top and bottom, on each side if it is a child or larger pet. That might not keep my 2 year old grandson confined but would work for a young child who isn\'t climbing. It is too tall for my grandson to climb but he shakes the heck out of it. You could examine it at Walmart or maybe Toys R Us and see what I mean. I don\'t have an opening that large in my tiny house or I would try out my theory.'}
