{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006QH43WW', 'answerTime': 'Oct 24, 2012', 'unixTime': 1351062000, 'question': 'Is the baby jogger warranty valid in Australia if bought on amazon?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Hi, baby joggers bought from Amazon are not covered by Bj in Australia. But Amazon have a amazing customer service and cover there products for 12 months. My 2 month old GT had a brake problem I did the online chat with a lady called Rochelle at Amazon she ordered a new pram replacement and advised me on returning the pram. They even pay for the returns. Baby jogger in Australia told me to if it had been bought here they would send the brake system out and I had to fit it all myself! All in all the warranty is far better along with the price from Amazon 10/10 service I'm very happy."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006QH43WW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398754800, 'question': 'Whats the difference between birth and one size?', 'answer': 'I\'m not sure why there\'s even two sizes listed for this stroller. I think they both mean the same thing. The stroller can be used with a car seat with an adapter (I guess this is the "birth" size) and then, of course, older. My daughter is 2.5 years old, #33, and about 38.5 inches tall and still fits in it comfortably, and we\'ve been using it since she was about 4 months old, I think.'}
