{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006QH43IQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386230400, 'question': "The instructions say this stroller isn't for running/jogging, but does anyone run/jog with this stroller and how has it held up?", 'answer': "It's lightweight and maneuvers easily, but I don't think I'd use it as a jogger. The three wheel design works for other joggers bc they are bigger, in this one I think the compact nature wouldn't be an asset for stability. I also have the City Elite and that one I'd use as a jogger, I currently use that to power walk with my dogs. It's much sturdier. All that said, if you still opt for this stroller, get the GT model with real wheels. We use this for travel and as a car stroller, and in just that I am not happy with the plasticy wheels. If you ran w it you'd definitely need real wheels! Hope that helps :)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006QH440S', 'answerTime': 'Nov 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384502400, 'question': 'Can you add a car seat adapter to one side?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, I believe you can. Certain carseats require different adapters. Check out their website to see which kind you'd need. I know that they do have an adapter for a Chicco carseat because thats what we had....I just opted to not buy the bar and put my baby at the fully reclined position with a snuzzler as well at around 3 weeks and it worked great. Wouldn't recommend that though if you are going to use it for jogging and what not."}
