{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006QH43XG', 'answerTime': 'Aug 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406962800, 'question': 'What is the difference between one size and birth and up?', 'answer': "I am guessing what you are referring to, but here goes...the City Select can adapt to a car seat. This stroller is better in my opinion for a baby and toddler combo. You can use a car seat adapter. However, you can't close the stroller with the adapter, I believe. The beauty of this stroller is it is the easiest to close by far, so we didn't want to complicate things. We did use it with a newborn because the seat does recline all the way."}
