{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006QH458Y', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': 'Can you put two infant car seats, or are the infant prams better?', 'answer': "You cannot put two carseat adapters as there is insufficient room. The side-by-side strollers are designed to fit through a standard doorway, and it would not if there were two carseats. We ended up buying a Snap n Go tandem stroller for our twins' infant carseat phase. I hate that stroller with a passion as it is hard to control, awkward, and I question how someone with a normal sized car can get it in their trunk. However, it does do its job. I LOVE the Mini GT, and prefer to take the twins out of their carseats and into this stroller if we are going somewhere for more then 30 minutes at a time since they can recline all the way (flat), it has better shock absorption, and I can push and steer with one hand (probably one finger!). It is a beast, though-- very heavy. But after lugging 20+ pound twins around at the same time, I've gotten quite strong. :)"}
