{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006QH43FE', 'answerTime': 'Jul 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405926000, 'question': 'Why is this so much cheaper than the newest version, Baby Jogger City Mini GT Single Stroller $349.99?', 'answer': "The GT is a different model, not just a newer version of this stroller. The GT has all-terrain wheels and an adjustable handle (maybe other differences, but those are the biggest). I think this one is easier to push one-handed, personally, and this still pushes across grass just fine (though I don't need it to do so often). Regarding the adjustable handlebar of the GT: I am 5'1 and my husband 5'10, and neither of us have a problem with the non-adjustable handlebar of this version. The GT just wasn't worth the extra money for us."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006QH43FE', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2012', 'unixTime': 1356940800, 'question': 'Can you use this stroller from birth or does the baby have to be a certain weight/length?', 'answer': "I think from birth is fine. Our little guy is now 13 pounds, 22 inches, and fits really well. When he was born he was early at 5 pounds and change; he didn't fit well at that time, but sometime in between everything worked out, probably all depends on length. Even when he was was tiny we put him in once for a short walk and just reclined the back so that there wasn't as much effect of gravity. The next time we tried it after that he was around 8-9 pounds and was fine. Hope that helps some."}
