{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006QH43GI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398236400, 'question': "Can anyone compare the City Mini to Peg Perego Si? The canopy on the Si is best I've ever seen, and the fold is similar to an umbrella/sits upright.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I had a Peg Prego Vela before I bought the City Mini. The front wheel got stuck all the time and I hated it. I sold it after a few months and bought the City mini. I wish I had just gotten it in the first place. I love it, love the fold, love the weight, love how easily it pushes and turns. It reclines well and I love the canopy, it's huge! I also like that when you recline the seat, there is a mesh part to allow air to flow through the stroller. I would go City Mini, hands down, even though I am not familiar with that Peg Perego model."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006QH43GI', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406012400, 'question': 'I have the baby trend flex loc car seat, can i use with this stroller"?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "You'll have to search for the specific accessories. They have some for particular brands (graco, chicco, etc), and then also a universal adapter. I never used it with a infant carrier, but they list the compatible seats in the details for the respective accessories."}
