{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006T6CJYO', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376636400, 'question': "Is there a gap between the tray and the child for food to fall into their laps? I've read the peg perego pappa best has this problema, and I was wondering if the siesta has it too.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "yes there is a gap but it will depend on the build/weight of the child, as how much that will be a problem for you. My baby is petite, I use bibs with a pocket and that helps catch most of the food that goes flying. Anyway, I gave this chair a 4 star for our situation, at the time, baby wasn't sitting up and I wanted safety, that narrowed the choices down greatly! Now 4 months later baby sits up and I have way more confidence, I still wouldn't buy the fisher price e-z chairs or others but I'm now dreaming of the boon - because she is petite and the tray is smaller and it would fit in my sink/dishwasher, but I also love that its all plastic and I can hose it down more easily. but sigh, I just don't know if I can justify spending that kind a money again! I would defiantly buy it on Amazon get your kid in there and if its not a fit you can send it back. Oh and I wished I had owned this chair from when she was born because it would have been nice to put her in there in the lower positions while mommy was cooking/ cleaning . So now at 4months use i would give it a 4 for not sitting up babies and 3 stars if baby is sitting up and yes it is the safest no doubt . good luck"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006T6CKG6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390291200, 'question': 'Is it easy to clean?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think so. Easier than a wood one- I like the vinyl seat- easily wipes clean and I find removing a fabric cover and throwing in the washer much harder. Chair still gets it's fair share of food in crevices , but I find my baby is comfortable and that I am able to keep the chair clean."}
