{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006T6CKG6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386057600, 'question': 'Can the straps be adjusted to prevent a smaller baby from slouching to one side?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'From what I can gather from the person whom I gave it to is that the straps can be adjusted and the back can go down far enough but their heads may shift from side to side if really young. It is a really good chair for a large age range of kids.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1360396800, 'question': 'What is included in this set??!', 'answer': 'One nipple, one 4oz bottle (the same type as the ones that come with the pump) and a cap for both the nipple and the bottle.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'What is the difference between the Calma and the Wide Base Nipple? Have you found one or the other to be preferrable?', 'answer': 'The calma nipple is designed to make the baby express the milk out like the breast. The breast nipple, when being nursed on, is stretched long like the calma'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'Has anyone tried using the Calma nipple to transition a preemie from bottle to breast? If so, how did it go?', 'answer': "Well our baby girl was not a preemie but we did try it when she was 1 month old to help her between bottle n breast transitions when she needed to be fed breast milk from bottle. I would not recommend it for a preemie our any small baby. It was to big for our 8 lb baby girl nearly choking her because of the length of the nipple. Being it wasn't cheap and I do like the concept we kept it to try again later and she is just now able to comfortably use it at 6 months and over 14 lbs..."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391673600, 'question': 'where is the medela calma bottle made?', 'answer': 'bottle is made in Canada, nipple is made in Switzerland, packaged in USA'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420444800, 'question': 'Is it compatible with the "pump in style advanced" pump ? Can you pump directly into the bottle ?', 'answer': 'Yes- the pump in style & free style pumps are compatible with any of the medela bottles.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': 'Is it possible to sanitize it in avent microwave steam sterilizer instead of boiling or using medela bag?', 'answer': "I've used all of those options interchangeably so I would assume yes. The dr browns bags are easiest for me but I have also used the aveng system"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385280000, 'question': 'Can you use the regular bottles with the calma nipples? Or do you have to use the calma bottle and nipple together?', 'answer': 'You will not b able to use with other bottles. I absolutely love the calma. Well worth the money.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418284800, 'question': 'I bought the 8 oz bottle and the cap that goes on the nipple does not close. It seems to be loose. Is it normal or is it damaged?', 'answer': "The clear plastic cap over the nipple should fit tightly enough that you need to apply a little force to remove it. There is the yellow cap that goes on what would be the bottle end to keep it clean and sanitary on mine I never felt that yellow cap stayed on as well as it should. Unfortunately I only have one of these (didn't work for my baby) so I would say if the clear plastic cap is falling off it is likely damaged."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415260800, 'question': 'Does this bottle include the Medela CALMA Breastmilk Feeding Nipple?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, bottle and nipple. The nipple was a little long for our 2 month old. He ended up getting use to a cheap nipple and bottle while we waited on his mouth to grow longer. I really wanted him to use it because it is most like a nipple and fits the pumping system...but baby rules and no go.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T899QI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387699200, 'question': 'can formula be used with this bottle set or just breastmilk?', 'answer': 'You can def. use it for formula but they get tired faster because they have to work at sucking, I recommend the regular medium flow nipples for formula.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'Does this need a collar, or does it just screw in directly to the bottle.', 'answer': 'It goes directly on'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397631600, 'question': 'Why is it leaking?', 'answer': "1. It may not be assembled correctly. 2. It isn't screwed down enough. 3. Check the yellow base for cracks. I find it is brittle. Also are you interpreting the milk that has let down into the nipple as leaking? My husband made that mistake."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394006400, 'question': 'Has anyone tried using the Calma nipple to transition a preemie from bottle to breast? If so, how did it go?', 'answer': "We didn't use it for a preemie, but did use it for a tongue tied baby to transition from bottle to breast. It REALLY helped. Before my daughter would just try to clamp on with her gums, this bottle taught her to suck properly."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'Does this fit the bottles that come with the Medela Breastmilk Storage Solution set?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not entirely sure what that is, but it does fit on all the Medela bottles we have, including the very small 2 oz ones."}
{'answer': "I can't say it helped my little one to learn to latch, it just helped with her confusion between breast and standard bottle nipple. We started using it week 3 and has helped a lot. I could tell almost immediately that there was more consistency for her. I really like the calma. I like how she can control the flow so much better too. It helps with her gassiness and burping. Hope this helps! Good luck!", 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': '16 days ago', 'question': 'For those who felt calma helped baby to learn to latch, how soon did you notice a difference? And how many weeks was baby?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': 'Jan 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422086400, 'question': "How long can you use these for (age of child)? I don't see any stages?", 'answer': "From 0months on....the nipple doesn't have stages like other nipples. It's suppose to mirror a breast. The babies sucking motion determines how much milk comes out. As they get older their sucking mussels get stronger and stronger. It's a great nipple; pricy but well worth it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': 'Nov 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415347200, 'question': 'How often do you have to take apart and wash/sterilize?', 'answer': 'Take apart at every wash-after each use. Sterilize, same frequency as any other nipple. We did daily at first...But as our child got older we sterilized less frequently.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415001600, 'question': 'Does this fit into the regular medela bottles or does medela have specific bottles for these nipples?', 'answer': 'They fit the regular ones :-)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006T89X9Q', 'answerTime': 'Oct 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414566000, 'question': 'is this nipple difficult to clean?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, it has 3 separate pieces so it gets a little annoying. But I do think it works really well at slow-drip versus other bottle nipples making it closer to a breast feeding experience.'}
