{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006TJP8A8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405234800, 'question': 'Would this work with a city versa? Also would it keep mosquitoes out?', 'answer': "I'm not sure about the city versa part. I've got an older bob jogger and it works really well on it, but I would not say it would keep out mosquitoes, there are clear gaps at least on this stroller on the side. If you're stroller is smaller it would probably wrap around better and then possibly it could keep out mosquitoes. All in all though we love this thing, we keep it attached 24/7 and use it a lot."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006TJP8A8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401692400, 'question': 'Do you have to take the shade off to get your baby out or is there a zipper that allows you to get him easily?', 'answer': "There is a zipper. However, the elastic fits so well over my jogger that I don't even snap it down so I can just lift it up easily and take it off."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006TJP8A8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': 'It will not work with travel system strollers right (since there is a tray before the baby and that tray would stop the sunshade from fitting there)?', 'answer': 'I am not familiar with that stroller. I have a Graci jogger and it has a tray. It works great with it. It has elastic around the entire shade so it fits easily on to it and hangs in.'}
