{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006UJLHMK', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399964400, 'question': 'Can anyone comment on how this product compares to the Shrunks blow up travel bed?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'This tavel bed is well worth the money!!! I purchased then when my little one was 20 months and he has used for a year. He loves this bed, he runs to jump into it, and sleeps well. Because of the enclosure around the bed, I think he just feels so cozy and secure. We have traveled with this bed on a plane, on as train, ferry and in the car. It is a bit bulky but can be squashed to fit where it needs to go, and it bounces back. It easily washes as the foam comes out of the cover. The zipper enclosure is easy to use. Everything about this bed is excellent and I would highly recommend it!!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006UJLHMK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397545200, 'question': 'Does it fit a toddler with 38 inches long &amp; 32 pounds? What are the dimensions of the sleep portion only (exclude bumpers)?', 'answer': '43.5" long x 23" wide are the interior dimensions between the bumpers. There is plenty of sleeping space for a toddler and would fit yours fine. My 4 year old can still fit in it just fine but we have passed it on to my son who is 36" tall and he has more than enough room. I have had this product for a couple of years now and would still give it 5 stars. I think it\'s better than other toddler sleep solutions I\'ve found. I\'ve looked at the sleep pods, the Shrunks blow up bed, and other options. The BumpZZZ is very cozy with the bumpers and has plenty of padding to be comfortable sleeping on the floor and it\'s easily transportable with no fuss..no need to blow up, etc. We just fold ours in half and secure the Velcro tabs and that is it! When the kids are done with this, it will probably go to the dog. Love it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006UJLHMK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Is this safe for a newborn to sleep in (3 months old)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'For a 3 month old I would use a travel co-sleeper. The Leacho BumpZZZ is made for a toddler.'}
