{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006UMUB92', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401778800, 'question': 'A lot of the reviews say to purchase your own (longer) screws. If I want to buy them in advance, what size screws will I need and how many?', 'answer': 'I would suggest 3/4" to 1" drywall nails. If you\'re using the regular mount you\'ll need 8 screws. If using the stair banister kit, you\'ll only need 4.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006UMUB92', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401260400, 'question': "does it swing open in only one direction or come with that option so that it won't swing out over the stairs?", 'answer': 'Gate swing both ways. Small, included stops can be installed on the latch. The stops are supposed to keep the gate from swing one way. I would not depend on them. The latch itself does seem to hold pretty good. A kid big enough to defeat the latch should have already learned to safely use stairs. Works well for us so far.'}
