{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006VIJOPW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395385200, 'question': "Does anyone know how to warm up this bottle straightly from refrigerator without breaking it or destorying breast milk's nutrient?", 'answer': "We warm the bottles up in a hot water bath. Just set the bottle in a bowl and pour just boiled water into the bowl to gently warm the bottle. Swirl the milk around so it heats evenly and check temp. Takes 15-30 seconds depending on how much we're hearing up. No concerns with breaking--these are very durable bottles."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006VIJOPW', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'Are there interchangeable travel caps for these bottles? Which brands?', 'answer': "If you mean you want to use flat travel caps rather than the nipple and cover, then you are all set. The bottles come with flat caps that you insert under the nipple ring for travel or mixing. I've found that with the glass bottles, just the flat cap and nipple ring hold a tight seal. However, with the plastic bottles (we have the classic heat resistant plastic as well as glass), there is an additional piece that nests on top of the flat cap to hold the a tight seal. Or you can insert the vent unit with the flat cap and nipple ring. Either way, you shouldn't need to buy any additional products."}
