{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006WHG6XU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413270000, 'question': 'I see that the gate self closes and locks behind you but in the video you still have to push the lever down to lock as well. Is this true?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We have the gate at the top of our stairs. It closes automatically and "locks". To open again you\'ll need to lift the whole door up and swing it open. Think of the lever like a deadbolt on your door. It closes and locks by itself but if you want to really seal it then you\'ll need to manually flip the "deadbolt" down.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006WHG6XU', 'answerTime': 'May 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1369292400, 'question': 'I\'d like to verify that this gate is 26" high. I\'ve seen what I thought was the same gate on other sites and it\'s 29.5", which is more standard.', 'answer': 'Jillian the top of the arch is 29.5 in. The gate overall is 28.5. We have to of these and feel they are the best gates. Magnetic and stay open feature at no gimmick. If you use the "cups" that screw to the wall with the mounting hardware it makes them rock solid. Josh'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006WHG6XU', 'answerTime': 'Aug 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407567600, 'question': 'Hi is that "lock" at the bottom of the gate on both sides so that i can have it as an added security protection? or is it just located on one side?', 'answer': "It's on both sides. It allows you to control the swing of the gate in only one direction. I think you will find that you don't need it as extra protection though because the locking handle makes sure the gate isn't going anywhere."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006WHG6XU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404630000, 'question': 'Could a 4 year old open the gate? We want him to be able to open it, though having it close so our 10 month old gets blocked if need be.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I can't say for sure if a 4-year old can open it. I can tell you that my almost 3-year old cannot, and that it is hard for me to open. In fact, it is the hardest gate to open of the 3 we have. It is also quite noisy."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006WHG6XU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421308800, 'question': 'how wide an opening will this accommodate? The top of where i need gate is 40inches, the bottom is 43inches. Also, how wide is the walk thru?', 'answer': "That is a tough one to answer, with a three inch difference in opening. I have the 5 inch extension on an opening that is 37.5 inches. I believe it would extend out to 40 inches but for sure not to 43. And I don't know if you could squeeze two extensions to fit the 40 inch opening."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006WHG6XU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415606400, 'question': "After installing, I can't open the gate. Anyone else have this issue or is it a bad installation?", 'answer': 'You might have it too tight dont adjust too much after the indicator turns green. Then to open you must pull the lever and lift the gate. But the indicator must be green for it to work properly.'}
