{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006Z2BZBU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389600000, 'question': 'I have a Graco model 9651VL ... Assuming this will fit well ... ?', 'answer': 'I have a different model, a model in which the sides of the play yard bow outward, making it so the middle of the playpen is wider than the top or the bottom. The reviews I have seen where they were complaining about the fit were models like mine, so I assume it will fit your playpen very nicely. I also recommend disregarding the comment about how hard it is. Baby mattresses HAVE to be very firm, or else it increases the risk of SIDS. They are supposed to be a lot harder than a mattress you would buy for a real bed. This mattress is about the same if not softer than the one that a baby sleeps on in the hospital. It is also WAY softer than the "padded" mat provided with the play yard. My daughter is now 5 months and the only way we could get her to sleep in her play pen was after we put this mattress in.'}
