{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006Z2BZQK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423296000, 'question': 'How is the flat plane that the mattress rests on attached to the sides of the crib? Is this sturdy enough for a toddler to jump and flop in?', 'answer': "The mattress rests on a relatively thick wood slab which is bolted tightly to the crib with four nice, solid metal fasteners that you ought to tighten with a wrench. I'd trust the crib to hold my baby's weight until he's about 18-24 months old or 25 lbs, whichever comes first. Though it holds up when my toddler daughter (2.5 yrs, 35 lbs) climbs inside, I would never let her jump in it. It's very sturdy when all the screws are tightened well, but it's still too lightweight to withstand the kind of thrashing a larger toddler can give it!"}
