{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006ZISTTA', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371106800, 'question': 'is the tray easy off, easy on', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Hi Brenda, it was our first high chair and my wife and I were very satisfied with the product. The tray is very easy to get on and off with one hand. The tray also has a removable tray liner making the clean up simple. Removal of the cloth liner on the seat is also easy for cleaning. It is also easy to raise and lower the seat and the legs can fold up like a step ladder would making storage easy. I highly recommend it to you. If you have any other questions, please feel free to ask. -Kevin'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006ZISTTA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378191600, 'question': 'Is this a model upgrade from 3 point to 5 point harness? Does it recline enough for an infant? Is the non removable snack tray a pain, can you fit chair at dining room table with that snack tray still attached? I need to buy 2 chairs and want them to...', 'answer': "These chairs do have a 5 point harness. I have been using these chairs for my twins since they were 4 months old, they are now 6 months old. We love these chairs they recline enough to feed them baby food or bottles. The chairs seem to be comfortable they do not mind sitting in the chairs while we eat dinner or clean up the kitchen. I would rather not have the non removable snack tray but it's not too big of a pain. We ordered a Graco chair before we found these and sent it back because it seemed like the babies would outgrow the seat too soon. This chair is nice and big with room to grow. Yes the chair will fit and the dining room table because the height is adjustable. I recommend these chairs because they work well and won't break the bank when you buy two of them. They don't seem very sturdy when you put them together that's the only thing I don't like. We haven't had any trouble with them though. Good luck! Who knew high chair shopping could be so hard! The great thing is you can always send them back if you decide they aren't what you want."}
