{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006ZIST04', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377154800, 'question': "How long is the expiration date on these car seats....will it last until she's out of the booster if she's 1 now?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "For Safety 1st years the average is 6-8 years from the date of manufacture. I don't remember the window of time for this one specifically, but it will def get her through the years you would want a good carseat and solid booster! Most kids want the smaller less obvious boosters when they get close to reaching the age that they ALMOST don't need one anymore. And it can be used as five point harness seat for a LONG time. My son is almost 4 and still has LOTS of weight and height to go before he meets the recommended requirements for the booster option! I love the Alpha seats, all three of my kids have them :)"}
