{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006ZISSGO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411974000, 'question': 'I can install this car seat only with belt buckles?', 'answer': "Laura, you can NEVER install any car seat using both the seat belt and latch system. You must use one or the other. Both are equally safe as long as you get a proper installation. We have had seats that just don't install well in our car using latch, but we can get a great secure install with the seat belt. Install with each and see which one gets the best recline for your kid and make sure there is an inch or less of movement at the belt path."}
