{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006ZVV0R0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409295600, 'question': 'Can anyone comment on the fit of this pillow in the Britax B-Safe infant carseat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Our carseat safety inspector advised against using this, even though we have a Britax carseat, stating that it was too bulky and not sized to fit properly. It would be similar to buckling in a child wearing a thick winter coat because it prevents the straps from being tightened sufficiently. She recommended rolling up receiving blankets and using those for support if needed.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006ZVV0R0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385971200, 'question': 'Would you use this and the foam infant positioning insert for a newborn with the convertible Advocate 70-G3?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I triple checked with Britax and two car seat safety groups (the car seat lady and one that does the most safety checks.) While pillows are not normally recommended as they are an afterproduct, Britax has tested this pillow with the car seats in their safety tests, so it\'s not an afterproduct and is safe to use with any Britax seat. It states it on the packaging too and I would recommend keeping that with you if you go to any car seat fit checks and to the hospital because everyone kept giving me trouble (the hospital made me remove it during their tests and refused to bend from their "no pillows" position), which is why I triple checked. My seat was the Pavillion (same as the Advocate but without the side-passenger pillows) and we used the infant positioning insert and this pillow to give a nice, safe, snug fit for my newborn (7lbs 11oz 20inches.) It worked very well.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006ZVV0R0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393142400, 'question': 'Has anybody used this in the BOB stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "yep, we have. worked really well to enable us to utilize the stroller before our baby could support himself well. (We weren't using it for jogging at this point - we waited until he was older.) It enabled us to ditch the car seat adapter much more quickly than we would have otherwise been able to do. It also helped him nap exceptionally well, which is a great plus!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006ZVV0R0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363676400, 'question': 'Will this work on a convertible car seat for a one year old?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I am using it for my newborn...now almost 3 mo. I originally used it in the convert able car seat, since we did not have an infant seat. He is nearly 16 lbs now, and it us getting a but snug. Also, I was thinking of altering my original post to add that the top and bottom should be able to be adjustable , since you can take them apart with Velcro. However, if you do try to separate the top from the bottom and extend the length, the harsh part of the Velcro goes against the baby's back."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006ZVV0R0', 'answerTime': 'Sep 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410159600, 'question': 'i am wondering if it could be fit in the Advocate G4 Convertible Car seat? thanks.', 'answer': "Yes, I have that seat along with the B-safe. I'd recommend it for any child under 11 lbs or so that can't support their head or doesn't fit snugly in the seat."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B006ZVV0R0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392969600, 'question': 'would this work for the city jogger mini stroller, and britax pavilion carseat if my baby weighs about 17 pounds?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. I've doublechecked with safety groups and it's appropriate to use with the britax car seats, as they were made and tested with them. As far as the mini-stroller, it worked in ours much longer than I wanted to use it in the car seat. We have a pavillion and by about 17lbs the cushioning in the seat was enough to not need this and it made her more uncomfortable by that point (we used it from birth, so she did like it when she was 7lbs.) The stroller, I used it longer because it kept her a bit warmer along the sides and let her rest her head a bit more. She's a year old now and took it out this week."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B006ZVV0R0', 'answerTime': 'Jun 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403420400, 'question': 'Have you tried the reversible "moisture wicking" side? Is it appropriate for warm summer weather (the plush side looks hot)?', 'answer': "Yes, the plush looks hot but it doesn't seem too hot. My baby is very sensitive to heat and sweats easily, and when I use this product, I don't see him uncomfortable hot. I haven't tried the moisture wicking side."}
