{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0072AN3KA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385539200, 'question': 'Do any Chaperone owners find the shoulder straps really short? My son is 5 months and 27" tall and I can barely buckle the straps between his legs.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No we don't have problems with the length. Do you have the manual? The straps hook behind the seat into a metal locking clip. But, there are 2 different slots on the straps to hook them into the clip. One is supposed to be used when the baby is under 11 pounds. The other is for babies over 11 pounds. When you switch the locking clip at 11 pounds, the straps get longer. I would check to make sure your straps are in the right setting. But I would advise looking at the manual because placing the locking clip in he wrong place could be dangerous. I hope that helps!"}
