{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375340400, 'question': 'From the BG freetime reviews I understand flaps cause problem cleaning up solid poop. Does having a diaper sprayer help? Is there a good alternative AIO to bumgenius freetime flaps?', 'answer': "I personally haven't had issues cleaning up solid poop with the Freetime diapers. In fact, they are my go to overnight diaper because they can take the challenge with no leaks. Diaper sprays are most helpful AFTER baby has started eating solid foods but while just drinking milk/formula it's not necessary. The best way to deal with the flaps is to place them the same way every time. For example: the front flap (the one that is sewn near the belly button) I place down first. Then I place the rear flap (the one sewn at the buttocks) over it. This gives a solid surface which is easy for wiping. If you place the flaps the other way it makes cleaning poop off hard because its on both flaps instead of just one. Free times are definitely worth the try. Don't let a few inexperienced folks scare you away from them. There isn't a problem when the flaps are properly placed."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377759600, 'question': 'Is the "Mirror" color too feminine for a baby boy?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I have that color for my little guy. I put him in every color except pink. He has red, orange, green, blue, white, yellow. It doesn't matter :) Teaches them about colors!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Oct 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414479600, 'question': 'How can you line dry the covers and tumble dry the inserts? I thought the inserts were sewn into the covers?', 'answer': "You can't. You have to line dry the whole thing. The inserts do not come out of the freetimes. The 4.0 has the sperate inserts and honestly they hold more baby crap! So I'd suggest getting the 4.0s!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411196400, 'question': 'We are not sure if this can be used as a day time diaper, can we use it for 12 hours in the day?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No diaper can be used that long. A diaper needs changed every few hours, no matter what kind of diaper it is ( aside from over night when child is sleeeping ).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403247600, 'question': 'how long can you reuse one of them. Say I buy 7 can I reuse those seven and save money on buying disposable diapers? and How long would this system?', 'answer': 'we have about 20 diapers that we have been using for 2 years. we plan on using them for baby #2. will last you through potty training if you take care of them.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': 'What are the approximate folded dimensions of this diaper?', 'answer': 'It has many. From a baby over 10 pounds to over 20 pounds. I felt they were too bulky for my baby. None of his pants or onesies fit him when he wore them.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Dec 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386921600, 'question': 'I have heard that cloth diapers can sometimes be very bulky and change the way a lot of clothes fit. Are there any complaints with the BG freetime?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "They are thicker than disposable diapers and little leggings or tighter pants can become snug. Being a grandmother who used cloth diapers years ago, I don't see that as a problem"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Oct 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382079600, 'question': 'How often can you machine dry these without sacrificing quality? We have no space to air dry in our apartment.', 'answer': "We have been macine-drying these (on low) for 5 months and have not seen any quality loss. We only put them outside to remove stains. They dry fast, as long as the dryer isn't too full!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRG1W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376895600, 'question': 'New mom. Tried these and planning to get a stack. Anybody who is using it for a long time, are there any leakage issues? How u wash n dry? Thanks', 'answer': "Been using these for over 3 months (since birth). No leaks - only time it has it's because I didn't get the leg fit right and laid her on her side. That's been fixed since we found the perfect setting. I wash about 10 diapers at a time, plus about 20 washcloths we use as wipes, and the wetbag we use. All on a cold wash/rinse. Once every month or so a hot wash/cold rinse. They work very well if you hang them in the sun - stains bleach out and dry quickly. These also dry very quickly in the dryer."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRENC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397113200, 'question': "I'm new to cloth diapers - so do you just wash these after they are soiled? How many pairs do you need realistically?", 'answer': 'You wash them, there are a couple different methods but they usually involve a cold rinse and/or soak before washing with free& clear detergent on hot/cold. An extra rinse cycle on cold may be necessary (sometimes 2 extra rinse cycles to really get the amonia smell out if you cant line dry). Line drying in the sun is best but they can be tumble dried on low. How many you need depends on how often you want to do laundry! I do laundry every 2 (sometimes 3) days, and have almost 30 diapers, which is more than enough.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRENC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373180400, 'question': 'Aplix vs snaps - which ones are better?', 'answer': "It's more about personal preference. I like snaps better, they last longer. I know a lot of men (dads) that seem to prefer Aplix."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0072FRENC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389081600, 'question': 'Im new to cloth diapering. Sorry for my ignorance. Is there a replacement insert that you need to buy with this diaper shell, Im confused.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No insert is needed. An all in one diaper has a sewn in inset. I love these diapers because I don't have to fuss with inserts."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRENC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397026800, 'question': 'Since this is an all-in-one diaper, does it take longer to dry these than the Bum Genius 4.0 pocket-style diapers? How much longer?', 'answer': "I haven't found that - I'll do my best to describe... it is an all-in-one but the inside has 2 flaps, one attached at back & one at front, they overlap (see the 2nd pic). So while it's AIO, it's not bulky cloth, the layers make it as quick to dry. I also have a Grovia AIO & a few pocket diapers - the Grovia defintely takes a little longer! Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0072FRENC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416124800, 'question': 'I bought a few of these from the BRU and now i see that they want you to was each diaper 6 times separately and then prewash. Is that necessary?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Nope. You should do 1 wash altogether to rinse them. If they were a natural fiber a lot of people would suggest the 6 washes but that's not fully necessary either. Natural fibers get more absorbent as you wash them so just doing the 1 wash and then using them is OK."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRENC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411196400, 'question': 'Hi, I&Acirc;&acute;dm using cloth diapers for the first time and I&Acirc;&acute;d like to know if any of you regularly tumble dry your diapers?', 'answer': 'Yes, we tumble dry our freetimes on rainy days along with cotton prefolds we use as doublers. I only machine dry on low heat setting. High heat can ruin the waterproof fabric and elastic. In the winter, I hang then overnight in the laundry room, and they are usually dry in the morning. Bumgenius does not recommend machine drying at all though.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0072FRENC', 'answerTime': 'May 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399014000, 'question': 'Are these diapers really able to fit on a 8 lb baby?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "They're supposed to, but I found the fit to be awkward and not ideal. They did fit nicer once my daughter was over 10 or 11 lbs. that's when I really used them."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0072FRENC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398754800, 'question': 'How many cloth diapers come in a package? Or am I paying 19.95 for 1 AIO?', 'answer': 'Yes, one diaper. These are pretty expensive and work pretty good. I highly recommend the "Diaper Safari One Size Pocket Diaper". It has worked the best out of all the different diapers I bought and is a better value. They only come with one stuffer (high quality) so sometimes I double stuff with a bum genius stuffer or a homemade stuffer...especially for nighttime. I bought a pack of white washcloths, folded them in half, and sewed the sides. Super cheap stuffers. You don\'t even have to sew them, I guess.'}
