{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0073DNYSW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408518000, 'question': "The manufacture say US version doesn't get 180 degrees flat. It only get 169 degrees. Is this still ok to use as bedside bassinet ?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It does get all the way flat - or darn close to it from what I can see... Pediatricians recommend newborns sleep on a slight incline anyway as they're often a bit congested after birth so the flat that it's not totally flat makes it even more ideal for a bassinet. We loved this item and our baby slept in it next to us until she was 10 weeks old."}
