{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0076A7R8U', 'answerTime': 'Oct 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381215600, 'question': 'Can you use this stroller for the airport? Would they let you go to the gate or do you have to check it in?', 'answer': "I recently used this stroller in the Chicago O'Hare Intl. Airport. Since its so big you have to get it checked in as luggage not carry on, but they will let u take it until u are about to board the plane then they take it to cargo, but if u have multiple stops they will bring it to you at every stop at no extra cost. I would double check with your airline when you're checking in, but that was my experience. Also this is the best brand of stroller I've ever owned!"}
