{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0077P3UP8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397113200, 'question': 'If i need to purchase a bassinet bumper for this what would be the recommended size needed?', 'answer': "You shouldn't use a bumper - they are a suffocation hazard for your baby. This goes both for the bassinet and for a full size crib, whenever you are ready to switch your baby over."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0077P3UP8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': 'Where do you find sheets for this bassinet?', 'answer': 'These actually take cradle sheets, not bassinet sheets. You can find cradle-sized sheets all over, but I bought mine at Babies R Us.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0077P3UP8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403679600, 'question': 'I bought the naturepedic 18x36x2 mattress after reading all the reviews. Its not fitting in the bassinet at all. help!?!?!', 'answer': 'That is the same thing I bought: the naturpedic crib mattress with the dimensions 18 x 36 x 1.5". It was a snug fit to get it in the cradle and had to be smooched down. But once the baby was on it, it flattened out pretty well, with some bowing at the edges. In spite of the imperfect fit, it was lightyears better than the thin, crappy "mattress" that came with the bassinet.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0077P3UP8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388995200, 'question': 'how does it turn into a toy box?', 'answer': "The legs come off, so it's just the little 'cage' part :). We didn't end up doing that - my 3 year old was too rough with it (the baby was fine :)) and we had a friend that needed it anyway so we passed it on. hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0077P3UP8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364454000, 'question': 'It says the bassinet is solid wood, but what about the flat base the mattress sits on? Is that MDF/particleboard?', 'answer': "Yes, I believe it is particle board, however, it seems very sturdy. I'm not due for a few weeks so we haven't used the bassinet yet but we were really happy with the quality and look. FYI, it is definitely larger than I expected. Make sure to check measurements to see if it is what you are expecting."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0077P3UP8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402556400, 'question': 'Are the bassinet sides solid wood, plywood or MDF? I see that the base is MDF.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'All the same material.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0077P3UP8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'What size mattress fits in this bassinet?', 'answer': "It's 17x36. It comes with a small mattress pad. Finding sheets is another story. I've had to purchase changing pad sheets or cradle sheets."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0077P3UP8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403247600, 'question': 'Can I use this as a co sleeper next to my bed? Would one of the sides come off so its an easy access for me when I want to feed my baby over night?', 'answer': "The side does not come off, but I found that it is the proper height to scoot right up next to our bed anyway. My boy's sleeping surface was level with me and it was easy to look over and make sure he was doing fine, and reach in to soothe him during the night."}
