{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Aug 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377586800, 'question': "What happens if you have molding on the groud where you want to install this product? I can't go over the molding, not enough height!", 'answer': 'Purchase a set of Dreambaby Retractable Gate Spacers (was 9.99 from baby haven through Amazon). Use the longer curved unit for the top of the gate installation. At bottom, Lascal Gate Body will lay flush against existing molding, and top of gate unit will attach to wall through the spacer. The Lascal gate has two installation clips included, one for top, one for bottom. Screw bottom clip into existing baseboard molding. The top clip will fit between the Lascal Gate Body and the spacer unit. You will have to drill out the plastic holes on the gate spacer by just a hair to allow for proper alignment of the upper gate clip and the spacer holes. Pay attention to layout of proper clip height from top to bottom. Start with bottom clip positioned on or near floor height-test install with clips pushed into receivers on Lascal Gate Body and mark hole positions from the side with a pencil. If wall is sheetrock behind the spacer, use toggle bolts (ITW Brands "Toggle Lock 100lbs" work best, buy at Home Depot or online and follow installation instructions carefully. If wall is solid (wood stud) just screw in with screws that will reach through clip, spacer (3/4"), and sheetrock (usually 1/2"), and still bite into the stud at least 1/2". If wall is concrete block hire a handyman. Pay attention to install instructions from Lascal as well. This method will take 30 min to 1 hr depending on your comfort with this sort of thing. If not comfortable, get a handyman but provide these materials for a proper job. The toggle bolts I mentioned will hold up well if installed correctly following their special instructions.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390118400, 'question': "How flexible is the mesh once pulled out? We have 2 cats and I'm wondering if the mesh is flexible enough for them to squeeze underneath.", 'answer': 'The material is pliable so that it can be retracted, but it does not stretch. Once locked, the material will not move. You just need to ensure that you install the gate at floor level. If you install it above a 3-inch baseboard, pets may be able to squeeze under it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407222000, 'question': 'can you connect another panel to one of the edges of the first panel and form a corner?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'You would not be able to connect the panels directly to each other. You would need a post that each panel could connect to in order to form a corner'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396681200, 'question': 'we have a banister at the top of the stairs with 1.5" (maybe a tad smaller) posts that this will have to mount to...at a slight angle. Will it work?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'From a dimension perspective it should work. Having said that, I would NOT put this gate at the top of a staircase. The fabric that slides across is very easy for baby/toddler to push and get under. It is more of a deterrent, not a full proof safety gate, especially for a staircase. We love the gate to shut off a section of rooms on the ground floor.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'Can you mount this gate at the bottom of a stairway that has a curve to it? Wall on either side at the bottom to mount to.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Without seeing exactly I cannot be sure, however, as long as there is a clear line between the two sides where the gate will be mounted it should work fine. If the curve of the step passes through the line then the gate cannot be closed as it should depending on how far it extends. This is a wonderful gate because it provides excellent safety when needed and retracts when not needed.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405234800, 'question': 'Can this gate be used outdoors?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I doubt it. The internal mechanism is spring loaded and probably not water proof. The rest of the parts are plastic or fabric, but I think if the internals got rusted the gate would fail to operate.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'Does the mesh go all the way to the floor? Can small dogs slither underneath?', 'answer': 'The mesh goes very close but yes, a small and determined dog could sneak under.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390204800, 'question': 'Does it make noise when opening or closing?', 'answer': "It doesn't make that much noise unless you don't turn the dial enough and pull after it winds down. There is a dial that you turn to be able to extend it and it is kind of like a timer and clocks back until it gets to lock mode. This gate worked great for us, but if you install above the baseboards and they are really high your kiddo or pets will discover how to crawl under it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388217600, 'question': 'what is the maximum length that the gate will cover? my area is 8 ft..', 'answer': 'It only covers up to 4 1/2ft'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007D1NTN4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385539200, 'question': 'Is the mesh easy to clean or does it stain easily?', 'answer': 'It does get a bit soiled, not terribly but we currently have it installed at the top of our stairs to keep the kiddos up and the dogs downstairs as a second bonus. Worse than the mesh, though, I would note that the white plastic handle (which you essentially have to use to get the bar latched across) gets finger marks on it but does clean up with a little effort. The ribbons (top and bottom) that give the mesh its strength have started to wear and have thread-like feathering that makes it look worn but we literally open and close dozens of times daily.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395385200, 'question': 'can this be used on a trundle bed that has no boxspring?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. My daughter's bed is a platform bed with no boxspring tucked right into the corner of her room. There are straps that go from the rail and they run between the mattress and platform. The straps end with a round metal disc that then rests perpendicular against the other side of the mattress to hold it in place. Works great. We've never had a problem."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378969200, 'question': 'Would this rail work with a 5 inch foam mattress?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I don\'t think so. I have a firm 10" mattress and a little lip in my bed that holds it pretty tightly. I fear the foam Will be too soft to hold it in place'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386403200, 'question': 'would this work with a mattress on the floor?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'In theory it will work. The bed rail comes with two metal bars along the bottom so if you have wood floors it might scratch the floors. However, if you use it on carpet it should be fine.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385366400, 'question': 'Is this product BPA, phthalate, PVC and lead-free?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "I believe it is as I have purchased an organic bed and I don't think I would've purchased something to attach to it that was not safe, however, I would suggest to the check with the retailer as I no longer have the box."}
