{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409641200, 'question': 'Would this work with a platform bed that has a lip on it?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. My son has a pottery barn bed and it has a lip and this bed rail fit fine. No problems'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': 'Aug 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408950000, 'question': 'Would this work for a top bunk in a college dorm with a metal spring frame?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You would need a board under neath for the bars'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': '24 days ago', 'question': 'Can this be used when bed sits inside frame and not on boxspring? My daughter hs a trundle bed where the mattress sits inside the frame.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't think that this would work in your situation. I tried to install this on a bed without a box spring- the mattress sat on the wooden slats. The rail part (which is what you see in the picture) is a round metal tube perhaps 3/8 inch diameter- so there would have to be a gap between the bed and the frame. The other issue I ran into was the round piece at the end of the strap to hold the rail flush against the bed (the straps run under the bed and are meant to wedge between the box spring and mattress). Since I was trying to install it with a mattress on a flat surface the circle was unable to lay flush against the bed and would slip free. Both issues meant that I was unable to secure the bed rail to our child's bed and I ended up having to return it. I went with the little bumpers that slip under the sheets and that has worked wonderful for us. Since you are using this on a trundle bed I would expect you to run into similar issues."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424592000, 'question': 'would this fit on a crib with one side taken off? Plan to ease into the transition while we wait for his bed to get here.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, I expect that it will. My daughter used this on a conversation crib instead of purchasing the extra conversion piece to convert her child's crib to a toddler bed."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007D1NKK6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419667200, 'question': 'How do I install this on a twin bed with a box spring?', 'answer': 'I brought the straps to the other side across the box spring, the put the mattress on top of the straps and secured it with the round metal disk that will rests against the mattress to hold the bed rail in place.'}
