{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007E2E706', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397026800, 'question': 'Does this help remove deodorant build up on clothes?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Rlr removed all sorts of build up from our clothes! Soap build up, mineral build up even deodorant build up on my husbands workout shirts :)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007E2E706', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425715200, 'question': 'Is it supposed to sud? Or the crazy suds I got when using it alone (no detergent at all) is only from the clothes and sud buildups in my washer?', 'answer': 'No, rlr does not sud. What you are seeing is what was built up in the fibers.s and your washer.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007E2E706', 'answerTime': 'Aug 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407394800, 'question': 'Does this work to get rid of dingy marks on sheets? I have pale blue sheets with body-shaped dingy spots! Ewww!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I don't use this for my regular laundry much, just cloth diapers. I use it to remove detergent and ammonia build up and it works like a dream. It does a great job on my white towels but was not able to get old dingy marks that get left behind the hand towels. Honestly, your best bet would be to fill a squirt bottle with half lemon juice half white vinegar 9% if you can get it, and spray the spots all over saturating them and set them in direct sunlight all day maybe even 2 days. Then was again with detergent and oxyclean. if you have hard water and you don't treat it, be sure to add calgon or just 1/4 C regular salt. That should get out the sweat stains. This works on pit stains in undershirts as well."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007E2E706', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394352000, 'question': 'Hi. Has anyone tried this to remove the stench of chemicals/fab softener from hand me downs? I am curious about trying it on dark colors as well.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I haven't, but it has not caused any issues when cleaning dark diapers."}
