{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007E8RSGA', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413961200, 'question': 'I am having the hardest time deciding between the Onya Outback or the Boba (3g or 4g)...help! We have a Mei Tai wrap (which we love but are outgrowing). In need of a great carrier for my 9 mo. old. for hiking and travel. Any advice welcome. Thanks.', 'answer': 'I have not used those other packs, but I can say I love the Onya. I wear my 3.5 year old daughter at Disney Land in this one and it is great. I am able to fit snacks in the zipper compartments, travel size sun screen, chap stick, and hand sanitizer. I have hiked with it as well and it was lovely.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007E8RSGA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415088000, 'question': 'Can this be used with an infant? Can the baby sit facing in AND out?', 'answer': "They do have an infant insert that you can buy to go with it. I carried my son in it with the insert right from the get-go. The baby only faces inwards to your chest, not out. At that age they don't need to be bombarded by all the stimuli coming at them by facing out. Snuggling in to your chest is the safest and most comforting spot for them to be. It will also ensure they are in a better position for hip development and takes the pressure off their crotch."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007E8RSGA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395212400, 'question': "Does this carrier work well for short ladies? I am 5'1.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I wouldn\'t see why not. I am 5\'5" and have no problems wearing it. The shoulder straps are adjustable so you can just cinch it up nice and tight if you need to. There is a chest strap you can use too if you are doing a back carry. I find that helps the shoulder straps from sliding off the shoulders. For front carry I always crossed the straps across the back and it fit awesome that way. I guess depending on how big your baby/child is as well will help fill it out more or not. If it is for an small baby they do have an infant insert that works really well. I can wear it with my 33lb 3 year old on the back but also used it for my newborn on the front. Both very comfortably. Depending where you are located it might be helpful to see if you can try it on first. There are tons of retailers in the U.S. and Canada that carry the Onya (just check their website for a listing). Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007E8RSGA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427353200, 'question': 'How does it work in summer?', 'answer': 'it is the only one I have used through summer... it was fine (I live in Phoenix) but was a bit warm after extended wearing. If/when we do summer outdoor outings I do the stroller until baby needs to nurse or something then I put him in my Onya Outback. overall it is a great carrier'}
