{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007F337NM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379314800, 'question': 'Is it FAA approved?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'According to Babycenter.com it is FAA approved provided your child is still in the 5 point harness. Once s/he is in a booster, the seat is not. Fair warning though, it is a heavy beast of a seat. Dragging it through the airport would be tough. It is very sturdy, and the weight comes from the safe heavy duty construction. The nautilus is also FAA approved (provided kiddo is still in harness) and is lighter.'}
