{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007F8SEIK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406012400, 'question': 'What fire retardant chemicals are used in this mattress?', 'answer': 'i emailed them because i was also curious - quick response from their team "Thanks for being interested in our products. L.A. Baby is committed to providing a safe and comfortable sleeping environment for everyone\'s little ones! In order to provide a non toxic and more chemical free fire barrier, as a fire barrier is required by law, we use the mineral compound boric acid. This compound is bonded to cotton in the comfort layers below the outer cover of the mattress, which in addition to having been proven safe over many centuries of use, is also an essential nutrient. Babies obtain this essential nutrient, and in the case of a nursing infant, from mom\'s diet of citrus intake of various fruits and juices. Because of the way our mattresses are made and the outer covering is constructed, they do not allow the release of boric acid into the air in a manner that anybody sleeping on it could absorb it though their lungs or skin."'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007F8SEIK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392969600, 'question': 'What is it made of? Did it smell of chemicals when you received it?', 'answer': 'It is made of a dense foam (no coils) - it only states the cotton cover is organic, so would assume the foam is not. However, it did not have any chemical odors when I unwrapped it. The foam is a much more dense, (seemingly) higher quality than what came with the portable crib I purchased - firm, not a lot of give, but still soft feeling. Plus the organic cover seems to be of high quality. My grandson sleeps soundly on it. Note that the mattress cover is not waterproof. I purchased an organic cotton waterproof mattress cover to go over it and then covered all with an organic cotton portable crib sheet.'}
