{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007FRJQ5G', 'answerTime': 'May 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401087600, 'question': 'Does anyone know when you can switch from the infant to toddler side.....my son is almost a year old....is it time to switch to toddler?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi Dorian, Technically, a 'toddler' is approximately two-years old, and most likely walking. Their little bones are getting stronger, and are exercised more once they start alking and eventually running. About that time you may want to consider 'turning' the matress to the more orthepedic-friendly side for toddlers and smaller children as their 'comfort-needs' are now differnet than when they were infants. Ultimately it is up to you, but the 'toddler-side' is more chushy, ans supportive of a larger little one . . . ."}
