{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007HKOL92', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393747200, 'question': 'How many do i need for the first year of my baby??? Which one do i use for milk feeding? Not sure if it depends on the liquid density or baby age.', 'answer': "How many do you need in the 1st year? I a actually have 5 bottles so I get a bottle that already has the nipple and then 2 packages of 2. 1 hole is great for the 1st few months, then when your baby is eating more, go to 2 holes and then after a few months go to 3 holes. Don't worry about following the timeline set by Avent. If the milk is thicker more holes is better but just know that your baby may not be ready for more holes if they spill a lot. Also if they get suction blisters on their lips, that's a clear sign to up the holes on the nipples. I hope that helps. Good luck!"}
