{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007I0K4S8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405580400, 'question': 'what is the difference between this mattress and their "stage 2" mattress that is $30 more? Which is the better purchase?', 'answer': 'The 2-stage mattress actually has two different firmnesses. One side of the mattress is the "infant" side which is more firm, and the opposite side is the "toddler" side which is less firm. The idea is that a firmer side is more appropriate for an infant, which I think is more relevant to parents who chose the stomach-sleep method with their babies. This is strictly my speculation, but I think a firmer infant side is meant to ease parental concerns about SIDS. Again, just my speculation. I sincerely doubt the less expensive version is any less safe or is of lesser quality, so it\'s really a matter of your comfort. This is the language from the product website: "The 2-Stage Lullaby Earth crib mattress features a firm, flat surface on the infant side (as recommended by pediatricians and the Consumer Product Safety Commission), and a softer sleep surface on the other side for growing toddlers. Strong edge and side support adds structural stability and makes the Lullaby Earth mattress an excellent choice for toddler beds." Hope this answers your question.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007I0K4S8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412665200, 'question': 'What percentage of food grade polyethylene foam is used vs. polyester? And which part exactly is the polyester used for?', 'answer': "It's about half food-grade polyethylene and half polyester. The mattress meets all flammability requirements without needing any flame barriers or other flame retardant chemicals. It's also completely waterproof without needing vinyl or perfluorinated compounds. It's hygienic in that anything wipes right off, and without staining. It is firm (the way the Consumer Products Safety Commission wants it). It's also firm at the edges (for jumping toddlers) with a snug fit. It is free of known allergenic materials like latex. It does not contain any polyurethane foam or so-called soy-foam (which is polyurethane foam). It comes with a limited lifetime warranty and is durable and well-built, even though the whole mattress weighs only about seven pounds (which makes it real easy to bend over the edge of the crib and pick up the mattress and change the sheet). Healthy Child Healthy World recommends this mattress. And Lullaby Earth has won a ton of awards."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007I0K4S8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390204800, 'question': 'Do we need a waterproof mattress pad or is it enough that the mattress itself is waterproof?', 'answer': "The mattress pad is easier to take off and clean than cleaning the mattress itself. So while the mattress can certainly handle messes it's going to be a lot easier for you guys to clean up by pulling a pad and putting in a clean one."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007I0K4S8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420185600, 'question': 'Is this an innerspring for foam mattress?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'This mattress is neither. When people talk about a "foam" mattress, they generally mean polyurethane foam or soy foam (which is basically polyurethane foam) or memory foam (which is also basically polyurethane foam). Then, when they talk about an "innerspring" they\'re, of course, talking about steel springs. Steel innersprings don\'t have the chemical issues that come with polyurethane foam, but they are heavier mattresses and many people need something more lightweight so that it\'s easier to lift and change the sheets, etc. Lullaby Earth solved this dilemma by using food-grade polyethylene (not polyurethane) to make the support core. Food-grade polyethylene meets the FDA standards for food contact. It\'s favored by all the environmental groups. This design provides a safer baby mattress and still is lightweight and easy to lift. As well, this design doesn\'t have the high flammability of polyurethane foam, and no chemical flame barriers or chemical flame retardants are necessary in order to meet the government flammability standards. As a side point, Lullaby Earth is also free of other materials commonly used in baby mattresses, like vinyl, phthalates, antimony, perfluorinated chemicals, pesticides, GMOs, etc. "'}
