{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007NG5UEU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390291200, 'question': 'I have this product and my parent units will not link with the baby unit anymore. What can I do?', 'answer': 'The exact same thing happened to me! I contacted the manufacturer and they were happy to replace the entire unit. You will need your Amazon order number and the date purchased.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007NG5UEU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389772800, 'question': 'The reviews look great other than the units not linking at or around the 6 month mark per the reviews. Normally I do not pay much attention to negative reviews when there are so many positive reviews, but almost all of the negative reviews are of the...', 'answer': 'i have had these since early may of 2013. i use them everyday in a 2700 sqft home in a high wireless communication area and we have only had this occur once due to a lightning storm and they reset on thier own. these have been a fantastic purchase for us and our baby. from my perspective, this is a non issue.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007NG5UEU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386144000, 'question': "If I buy two of these (2 baby units/4 parent units) will they all work together? One baby unit in each child's room, parent units spread around home.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "They won't sync together where the parent unit hears both children in one unit. But we own two sets. I have one in each child room and then a parent unit for each child on the kitchen counter. They do not interfere with each other at all."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007NG5UF4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389081600, 'question': 'Why did you buy this product instead of a video baby monitor? Is it just price, or something else? Trying to decide for myself!', 'answer': "We take it with us to my moms,etc. So I just thought it would be easier for her to use. In addition I felt I might have a want to just watch the video monitor and felt like I could just as well have him sleeping next to me then because I'd get about as much done ;) I also have 2 older boys and this is like what we had for them, so it's what I know and am completely comfortable with. Plus the range is great, as I could take it outside without having to have it plugged in."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007NG5UF4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415433600, 'question': 'Is anyone using two (2) of these units successfully without problems? We often have two grandchildren staying and would like to buy a second unit.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I disagree that two units work properly together. I bought a second set of these same monitors to use with our second baby and they repeatedly interact with each other and lose the link to the base. I called VTech and was told that they run on the same frequency, so this will likely continue to be a problem. I would not recommend using two at the same time.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007NG5UF4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391846400, 'question': 'Is the distance range really close to 1,000 feet? I want to use this as a barn monitor for baby goats, and our barn is quite a ways from the house.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We found it to not pick up a signal when we were nowhere near 1000 feet away from our house; more like only about 200' away. Big disappointment. It wouldn't pick up the signal from our house when I was just across the street in our neighbor's house, and you lose reception even faster if you have a more solid wall like plaster or brick instead of drywall. We live in a city so not sure if there were other interfering signals from home wireless networks or radio."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007NG5UF4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390118400, 'question': 'Does the baby unit have a rechargeable battery too, or just the parent unit?', 'answer': 'Just the Parent Unit. The Baby unit needs to be plugged in.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007NG5UF4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364108400, 'question': "How long will the parent unit's battery lasts when it is fully charged?", 'answer': 'Depends how long you have been using it. When we first bought it it lasted 8-9 hrs. After about two months of use (not usually longer than a few hours unplugged) it has dropped to around 5 hours.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007NG5UF4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397199600, 'question': 'I am going to use this with my 90 year old mom. Is there a button for her to turn on to talk to me?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Place the baby unit in mom's room. Make sure the baby unit and parent unit are linked then adjust the volume and you can hear any time mom speaks. If you want mom to have the parent unit then show mom that on the left side of the parent unit there is a button she must push when she wants to communicate with you to the baby unit. If mom is alert enough and able to hold unit and push side button at the same time it will work great. However, I would be inclined to give mom the baby unit and you control the parent unit. We love ours, in fact we've purchased two since one quit working after 3 years. Good luck"}
