{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007PLZUUC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': "How do you get it open quickly if there's an emergency?", 'answer': "There's a small button. When you push that the rectangular white plastic part can easily be slid off, leaving just the thin metal mounting plate. The window should then open. It should be mounted so that the metal plate doesn't block the window. That was not a problem on 2 different types of windows with 2 different mountings for me."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007PLZUUC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397458800, 'question': 'I have double hung vinyl windows . Does this device work in this type of window?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I have double hung windows as well and this device should fit into yours. It actually fits into the track on which the windows slide up and down essentially blocking my son from being able to life the bottom window too high. Unless your track is too thin or too wide then I suppose they won't fit but I suppose that there is some standardization in the industry."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007PLZUUC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389600000, 'question': 'How to install it. Do you have to screw anything in or do you just put it in place?', 'answer': 'There is a small but sturdy metal bracket that is secured with 2 screws. Incredibly easy to install and very secure. I installed mine a bit different from the supplied instructions as I have double hung windows. That means both the bottom sash and the top sash move up and down. I had to mortice out a groove in the bottom sash to accept the metal bracket. That way each sash can move freely when the lock was removed for greater circulation.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007PLZUUC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'Will these work for screen windows? Thanks', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'What do you mean by "screen windows"?'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007PLZUUC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426230000, 'question': 'Does the bracket itself protrude much? I am worried about being able to completely open my windows when the stopper is removed from the bracket.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The metal bracket that attaches to the jamb sticks out about 3/8", maybe less. I have wood double hung windows so I actually carved out a groove so the bracket sits flush with the face of the window. Now I can open both sashes all the way if I want to. It still looks very professional and clean.'}
