{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007TD9JC6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401692400, 'question': 'Can someone tell me how easy it is to install on an airplane? want to make sure it is very easy to do. thanks', 'answer': 'The easiest way is to put the chair face forward and pass the airline safety belt through the slots on the back of the chair. The chair is quite light and compact. I was traveling overseas alone with my one-year old, and was able to carry both the baby and the chair (and a diaper bag, and a backpack and a stroller) I still keep this chair for future flights.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007TD9JC6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402124400, 'question': 'is this faa approved with sticker, that says faa approved?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, it says, in red print, that the seat is certified for used in motor vehicles and aircraft. Also, the owner's manual also says it is certified for aircraft use; however, it specifies that it is for use of forward facing aircraft seats where the lap belt can be fully tightened and to check with your airline for their regulations. It also says that the seat can be installed in the aircraft seat the same way it's installed in a vehicle, so I assume that means forward or rear facing. Again, I suggest checking, since if your need rear facing that takes up significantly more front to back space."}
