{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007TY12JS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': 'can you recommend a cotton sheet to use with this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I first looked at this: http://www.amazon.com/SnuggleWool-Lambs-Wool-Crib-28x52/dp/B000H4C6QU/ref=pd_sim_sbs_hg_10?ie=UTF8&refRID=1BYXW7SZ4R4STXAG9323 but decided against it because of the polyester backing. In the end I used an oversized 100% cotton thick plush beach towel over the plastic encasement to cut down on the crinkle and give a little comfort. I laid an organic wool piddle pad over top like this one: http://www.greenmountaindiapers.com/wool-mattress-pads.html Then I put an Ikea 100% cotton fitted crib sheet over top. It has worked out well, very little crinkling, comfy and breathable. Good luck! :)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007TY12JS', 'answerTime': 'Nov 7, 2012', 'unixTime': 1352275200, 'question': 'what material and how thick is this cover made of?', 'answer': 'I just posted a review that should help, I no longer have the paper that came with the mattress, but I believe you can get the material from their website, it is a non-toxic plastic. and is very thick for a clear plastic sheet. I really cannot think of something comparable, thicker than a heavy duty freezer ziplock I believe, but not as thick as say an office chair mat. I was not disappointed with the money I spend on this purchase. Quite the contrary, I was extremely pleased with it. and still wonder why there is no law requiring hospitals to provide these and training on their installation and use to every new parent.'}
