{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007VBYVXI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413874800, 'question': 'Are these stitched over aroudn the sides or are they flat? I have specific type of blanket I am trying to find that I can not find in stores anywhere!', 'answer': "These are diapers, and have several layers in the center. They are not FLAT diapers that you have to fold to make the padding, but are pre-folded diapers. These wouldn't work for you to use for a blanket as they're thick with several layers in the center, and thin on the edges where you pin them together around legs. Then they are serged/finished edges, keeping the edges of the diaper nice and flat so the gauze won't fray when it gets washed. Hope this helps."}
