{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007WF2PGS', 'answerTime': 'Jun 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402470000, 'question': "I have twins in the same room, can I move the camera to check on the other child with the hand held unit? Or do I need two camera's for one room?", 'answer': "That would depend where you put the camera and how big the room is. The monitor has the ability to rotate the camera either direction, so if the camera is in the middle and each child is on the side, I'm thinking you could. The rotation might be 90 degrees. I liked the option because my son moved around a lot in his crib and I could rotate the camera from the monitor to view him when he scooted to the other end of the crib."}
