{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007WF2PGS', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424764800, 'question': 'Will this camera interfere with my wireless network?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, there is a possibility of wireless interference. The monitor broadcasts on 2.4 GHz and some routers run on the same frequency (we have a Qwest Q1000 and it does get interference). Check to see what you wireless router uses to see if there is a conflict.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007WF2PGS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425283200, 'question': 'How sensitive is the camera rotation? Is it easy to use? We have another monitor and each tap to the side jumps the view halfway across the room...', 'answer': "The camera is not super sensitive at all when panning around the room. When you want to pan the camera you actually hold down the left/right or up-and-down buttons. We purchased this monitor for our first son who is now three years old and we still use it for him and I just bought another one for our new son who is three months old. Now and then the Parent monitor tells you that it's out of range and the screen goes black but only for a few seconds. I'm thinking that's because ours is a little older but it still works great."}
