{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007X64EKG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386748800, 'question': 'Hows the harness system? Is it really hard or cumbersome to adjust? Thanks', 'answer': "I wouldn't say it's hard to adjust, but it isn't made to adjust on a daily basis. It is a little tricky to figure out at first but not impossible. And you set in once and leave it until your little one gets bigger. It's easier to do small fine tuning like to adjust for small growth or a big jacket. But readjusting to go from a small infant to an older toddler takes some work. The arm strap is one strap that goes from behind on shoulder down to behind the hip then comes back out behind the other hip back up to the other shoulder. Like a big U attached behind the bottom. So if you pull the right arm strap forward, the left gets pulled back. It's all one belt. So to adjust you have to get this lengthened then the clips where you want them. Then the crotch strap is its own adjustment. I wouldn't say it's hard but maybe a little confusing the first time. But all the other benefits of the stroller are well worth it. I love it for my 2 boys. I hope my explanation is understandable."}
