{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0080D59XM', 'answerTime': 'Jul 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405494000, 'question': "Anyone know how snugabunny swing compares to discover'n Grow Swing? Looking for one that can be used for baby sitting upright.", 'answer': "I actually used both swings with my daughter (first one motor ran out- our overuse, not the product). For an infant, I would go with the Snuggabunny. I had the Discover and Grow first, and my daughter just slumped over in it. I actually had to use blankets to keep her somewhat upright- not great. We made due, but after I got the Snugabunny I wished I had started with that. She used the Snuggabunny until about 9-ish months, and it was a great swing. The Snuggabunny does adjust to sit upright as well. It just won't be as roomy as the Discover N Grow. I recommend the Snuggabunny, unless it's for an older baby and it isn't for napping- just playing. Hope that helps."}
