{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0080D5982', 'answerTime': 'Jul 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374822000, 'question': "What's minimum ht &amp; wt to use this? My son is 5 month, 16lb 26inches. He can hold his head up, but cannot sit up yet.Would he be wobbly sitting inside", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not sure what the minimum is but my daughter started using this at around four months and at the time she couldn't sit up either. The seat in this chair was deep enough to provide her with support to play comfortably."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0080D5982', 'answerTime': 'Jun 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401606000, 'question': 'How does it compare to the Baby Einstein model?', 'answer': "I didn't purchase the baby Einstein model because there was a recall on it when we were shopping around. I can however compare this to the fisher price rainforest jumperoo since we bought both. This discover and grow model is not as stable as the rainforest jumperoo. It tends to shake and wobble and the hard plastic hanging toys on this one hit my daughter in the head as she grew into it. The rainforest model has nice soft plush hanging toys and you can adjust the height. We bought my daughter the rainforest jumperoo when she was about 4 months old. She's 11 months old now and still loves it. I'd highly recommend that one over any of the other models. Doesn't exactly answer your question but I hope this was helpful."}
