{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00834D7DC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380092400, 'question': "Will this fit rear-facing in a 2004 and/or 2009 Honda Civic? I have been perusing other answers but I'd appreciate any additional feedback...", 'answer': "I can't say for sure. We used the Britax B-Safe infant seat for our son until he was old enough for this seat in a forward facing position. But if I had to guess, it will fit, but anyone in the front seat in front of it will be sitting up very straight. I still recommend this seat tho. I love it and our son seems real comfortable in it, and safe. I don't think it's any bigger than any other convertible seat that would be rear facing."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00834D7DC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394006400, 'question': 'Rear-Facing, how EASY is it to get children in and out of this car seat? Not baby-sized children, but long-legged, 36" tall toddlers? TIA!', 'answer': "As long as the seat is at the right incline, it's just fine. My son is almost 2 and 98th percentile for height and he has no problem with it whatsoever."}
