{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D7DC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394006400, 'question': 'Does this car seat has isofix device?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I believe ISOFIX is the latching system used in Europe. For more information, see the Britax UK website at http://www.britax.co.uk/car-seats/isofix .'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D7CS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379314800, 'question': 'BuyBuy baby calls it the 70-G3 XE....is it the same thing? They are charging $299!!!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It seems to me that it just comes with a few extra items: *XE model has a 7-year warranty. *It includes a cup holder and storage pouch which attach to the sides of the seat to store drinks, snacks and more'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00834D7CS', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393574400, 'question': "Has anyone taken this carseat on an airplane? How was it? And did people on the side fit well? I have a flight at the end of Jan and I'm curious.", 'answer': "We took it to NYC from California on a Jet blue airplane. We put it next to the window and it fit fine. It is a bit big but not so much that it blocks the middle seating area. We had the whole row, so it wasn't a problem for space. She was comfortable and I recommend this car seat 100%. The flight attendant actually let us board first so that we could install it properly. If you ask, I'm sure they will allow it. It is a bit heavy as well so keep that in mind when you are trying to tote this and your bags around the airport."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D7CS', 'answerTime': 'Dec 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419062400, 'question': 'Will this fit in my 2 door BMW? God daughter is 4 1/2 years old. I would only use occasionally.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It probably would be ok if you can get the front seat up far enough. It is a great seat, but base is fairly large.'}
