{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D7CS', 'answerTime': 'Oct 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381474800, 'question': 'I am interested in buying this item for my baby, instead of buying a regular carseat and in a few months buying a bigger one. Is this safe for a baby', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It comes with inserts for a newborn and says on the manufacturer info. that it is for a newborn to up to a toddler. The lbs is listed on it, says 5-70lbs. The straps are a little on the heavy side (there is rubber on them) but it states that it can indeed be used for a newborn.... I used a lock in type at first and then bought this once my daughter hit 20 lbs...but it was more pricey to do that. It comes down to what is most affordable for you and what your preferences are. Maybe reach out to the manufacturer if you want more clarity. Hope this helps:)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386921600, 'question': 'Does anyone have this car seat installed in a Prius?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yep, we have it rear facing behind the passenger seat. Works great!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359532800, 'question': 'Can it be used safely for a newborn / early infant?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We purchased this to be used from birth for our baby. Our daughter went home at 6 pounds 10 ounces and it worked fine. It looked huge for her, but it is designed for babies as small as 5 pounds. However, you will want to purchase the Britax Infant Positioning Insert so that your baby fits safely until s/he reaches at least 11 pounds. She is 6 weeks old now and we are very happy with this purchase. You just have to be willing to go places without the "convenience" of an infant carrier (we have been using a ring sling, which I think is actually more convenient).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': "I know there is a 70lb weight capacity, but what about height? I looked on the Britax website and couldn't find anything in regards to ht. Thanks!", 'answer': "Forward facing only with children who's height is 49in Or less"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Aug 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377846000, 'question': 'Can this seat be used on airplane?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We used this seat on several plane flights with no issue.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1360483200, 'question': 'Would it fit in a 2010 Ford Focus?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi - with these seats, it's really more about if you can fit them backwards-facing (recommended for at least a year, and luge saving until 4) without the passenger seat having to be so far forward that no one can sit there. I would contact your local dealership, or just drive your Focus anywhere that sells these seats - they will let you install it before buying. And, of you plan in having more than one child, make sure to try to fit two. I cannot say enough good things about this seat - I have three of these seats (my boys are 2.5 and 11 months)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'When the straps are tightened, do both sides tighten at the same time and rate?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1358150400, 'question': 'Do you use this with a base? As in, do I buy an extra base for our other car, or just move the whole thing back and forth?', 'answer': "I just move the whole thing back and forth. It takes me about 5 minutes using the LATCH system that both our cars have. This includes utilizing the 3rd attachment point from the rear of the seat to the front passenger seat mounts that's included with this seat. If you only used the LATCH attachment points it would take less than 5 minutes."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': 'seatbelt', 'answer': 'The car seat can be anchored by either using the seat belt in the car or the anchors provided on the seat. The actual seat belt in the seat is a 5 point harness that is quite easy to buckle and unbuckle. It has adjustable straps and the buckle can also be adjusted as your child grows.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393747200, 'question': 'is it 3-in-1? Following positions: rear-facing, forward-facing with harness, then booster', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It is 3 in 1 but it does not come with the booster. You will not be disappointed with the product!!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00834D5SO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372057200, 'question': 'installing using seat belts?', 'answer': 'Yes, it is very easy. It has clips for both forward and rear facing.'}
