{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008389Y80', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390204800, 'question': 'How tall is the stroller? Up to the handle? We are tall people and are sick of hunching over to push a stroller.', 'answer': 'From where your hands take the handle, it is 40.5 inches, so just over 3 ft to the ground. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008389Y80', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': 'Is this stroller compatable with Safety1st infant car seat?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I believe it will work with most infant car seat. I had a Britax and it fit fine. But I do NOT recommend using it with the car seat on the back portion because it makes it back heavy if you don't have a child strapped in the front at all times. It fell back with my baby in the car seat when someone bumped into it after I took my daughter out so she could walk around. Thank God I had him strapped in and locked into the stroller or he would have been seriously hurt."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008389Y80', 'answerTime': 'Mar 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395990000, 'question': 'For the Chicco infant seat, is an adapter needed in order to make it fit? If so, what am I looking for?', 'answer': "Nope. You just have to move the snack tray to the back, fold it down, then sit the seat there. The baby's feet will be under the handles. There's a strap that holds it in place. I just went to look at it at another store to make sure before I bought it. I'm not sure if you can use the seat in the front seat."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008389Y80', 'answerTime': 'Oct 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381042800, 'question': 'Is this stroller compatible with Chicco infant seats?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it is. We use it with our Chicco infant seat.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008389Y80', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378969200, 'question': 'Can you put the infant car seat in the back to allow the toddler to sit in the front?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes! The car seat can go in the front or back position. We usually have the car seat in the back (closest to us) and my preschooler sits in the front. We have been really happy with this purchase and strongly recommend it!'}
