{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085CBA90', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426834800, 'question': 'I think I need a small(21mm) Medela shield does this set have one that size?', 'answer': "Don't agree with the YES answer. It's a bit more complicated, but I tried to answer this in a video that shows both the Pumpin Pal next to the Medela:"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085CBA90', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412319600, 'question': 'What size of Medela flange do these fit in to? The 24mm flange or the 27mm? I want to order the one with best fit.', 'answer': 'They fit directly into the valve of the Medela pump, not into the flange. You take the Medela flange out & use these instead. I highly recommend them. My son is a preemie with a small mouth. He was not able to latch very well. Due to that, I became very raw & nursing was painful. I was already pumping with the pumping pal shields. I took a couple of days from nursing & strictly pimped with these flanges. It helped me heal up so I could return to nursing my son. I still use these flanges every day. They are very helpful.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085CBA90', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402297200, 'question': 'What is the correct fit? Should there be space all around the nipple or not?', 'answer': 'Same as with regular flanges. I use the smallest size I can without any skin rubbing against the edges during pumping.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085CBA90', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403852400, 'question': 'What are the actual sizes of the flanges?', 'answer': "There isn't a great answer to this question, because they are tapered to fit a variety of sizes. I believe they roughly correspond to Medela sizes Medium (24mm), Large (27mm) and XL (30mm). They all taper down to fit into a standard 24mm opening. However, I found standard 24mm flanges to be too big for me (even the Medela 21mm flanges were too big), but the smallest Pumpin' Pals flange fits just fine. I believe that the vast majority of women will be accommodated by one of the three included sizes in the kit."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0085CBA90', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397026800, 'question': 'Does this work with Ameda Purely Yours pump?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, I have used them with my Ameda Purely Yours. I have also used them with a Medela Pump in Style and both worked well with the Pumpin Pals attachments.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085CBA90', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421222400, 'question': 'Hi, do these work with the Spectra S2? I saw someone say that you can use Medela parts with the Spectra- can someone explain how?', 'answer': "I am the product designer for Pumpin' Pal. There are some moms that have a Spectra pump and the Pumpin' Pals fit well but there seems to be inconsistency from the Spectra manufacturing of the pump because there are other some moms that received Spectra flanges with their pump that don't accommodate the Pumpin' Pals. Since we can't assure that any mom has the ones that work we are saying that we don't fit Spectra:-("}
