{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0088CNKAY', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418803200, 'question': 'What type of materials is this made out of? and does it have flame retardants in the material or added to the product? Safety certifications?', 'answer': 'Sorry it took me so long to respond. To be honest I can\'t remember and I\'ve lost the original paperwork, probably because it\'s been about two years since purchase. However if I were to judge simply by touch and sight I would say the materials were a synthetic blend. The mattress cover, cotton. Flame retardant? Not likely, especially since everything can go through the washing machine. Most items I\'ve encountered that are "flame retardant" are NOT machine washable. Safety certifications? None that I remember, though I was very thorough in reading the warnings. They were fairly simple. Do NOT use once child begins to roll over. Do NOT use if child exceeds certain weight. (The certain weight I cannot remember. I had a smaller baby so reaching the weight limits were not a concern for us.) The Arm\'s Reach came with very simple instructions as well as a detailed do\'s and do not\'s that kept my little one safe, as well as a friends little one safe. Now we\'re getting ready to use it for our second, and I would not pause a moment to loan or gift it to another expecting mom.'}
