{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008BGNT4O', 'answerTime': 'Feb 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423382400, 'question': "Will this walker improve my baby's self-esteem? I'm really concerned about my 8 month olds shyness.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "If your little one is having problems with walking this product will certainly help by building up his/her leg muscles which will eventually help baby's self-esteem. As far as shyness goes, it depends how often he has interaction with family members, babies of the same age or could just be a part of baby's character. Give it time, your little one is only 8 months old but he/she should enjoy this product. I know the baby who was lucky enough to receive this product did and his legs didn't quite reach the floor but that's where some interaction came into play. I walked baby around in it. Lots of little laughs!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008BGNT4O', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390896000, 'question': 'can this walker be put into a stationary position during meal times?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Sort of - we would put our daughter in it on a fluffy blanket to keep her in one spot. For meals, the bigger problem was that she liked to bounce and hitting a moving target with a spoonful of prunes was disastrous. We loved this for many reasons but meals are best in a high chair.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008BGNT4O', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386748800, 'question': 'How tall can a baby be to be comfortable in this walker?', 'answer': 'My 9 month old is around 30" and uses it on its tallest setting (almost a standing position). It\'s great for feeding and easy to travel with for feedings. He used it early to work on sitting up, just used a towel to help prop him up (around 5-6 months) I would buy this again. I imagine we have a couple more inches and he will have grown out of it.'}
