{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008C02AYO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380265200, 'question': 'Is the size (height) able to be manipulated up and down? In other words if my son is shorter now can we move the seat down so he can reach the floor?', 'answer': 'It\'s like a harness so the child is not actually sitting in it. However, it "catches" the baby if s/he is getting tired and does not want to stand anymore. I hope this helps. Our nephew is a very early walker (first steps at 9 month!) so we bought this walker to boost his confidence, even though his legs were already very strong. He started zipping around in just a few minutes. In a few weeks, he was walking completely on his own, w/out a walker. However, he still likes the walker because it\'s like "driving" a car -- complete with looking over his shoulder while holding the wheel with one hand; just like Daddy! :)'}
