{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008C2YKWC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417593600, 'question': "I wasn't fond of the sheet choices on Amazon and am trying to buy custom sheets on Etsy. What size sheet fits this sleeper?", 'answer': "You can just use king size pillow cases. That's what I use and works just as good if not better."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008C2YKWC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417680000, 'question': 'is this JPMA certified?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Looking through the little brochure that came with the co sleeper, I only see a note inside that reads, "Member of JPMA. Products meet all applicable ASTM standards." I\'m not sure if that applies to this specific co sleeper, but it seems at least the COMPANY is a member of JPMA. I also came across an article on thenightlight.kinja.com where the reviewer stated: "I also reached out to Arm\'s Reach and learned that all of their products meet the safety standards put forth in ASTM F2906 (as well as ASTM F2194, the international standards for free-standing bassinets.)" Now I personally can\'t verify this, but the article DOES give an extensive description of the process and other info of selecting co sleepers.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008C2YKWC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391846400, 'question': 'are the wheels removable in the event you have to add the height extensions to the bottom?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "We just tried and the plastic caster wheels can be pulled off the bottom of the legs by hand (no tools needed). As we recall from setup, the legs are retractable providing height adjustment--we weren't aware of any available height extensions for use with this model, and think that the extensions sold for other co-sleeper models may not be compatible--probably best to check with the manufacturer on this."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008C2YKWC', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401951600, 'question': 'What is the size of the box this co-sleeper is shipped in? Is it smaller or the same size as the assembled bassinet?', 'answer': "It's smaller. Flat."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008C2YKWC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': 'how old or how much did your baby weigh before they outgrew this bed?', 'answer': 'My baby is 3 months and just outgrew it but she is pretty large for her age, 25+ inches and like 15+ pounds. I know of other babies that used it for a lot longer. Even though I only used it for 3 months I feel it was definitely worth it especially if you are breastfeeding!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008C2YKWC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405926000, 'question': 'I want to buy this, but I want to by a nicer mattress for it. Would a 37.5x25.5x3 mattress fit? If not, what brand and where can I buy it? Thanks!', 'answer': 'I looked into doing the same thing but it is not suggested because of the weight restrictions and the added height it would create. Because one side lowers to be used for access during the night increasing the mattress height leaves room for injury.'}
