{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008CMQTZI', 'answerTime': '10 days ago', 'question': 'Will a super active baby able to push the fence and move the whole thing around on hard wood floor?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "If it's closed off, like in the form of a square, all ends are attached, no. If you have it open and using it just as a freestanding barrier, yes."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008DDPL32', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377068400, 'question': 'What is the size of the pad? Will a bassinet mattress fit in it?', 'answer': "No, a bassinet mattress won't fit in it. For safety, I wouldn't recommend using anything else other than the pad that comes with it. My grandson is 5 months old now and still sleeps through the night in it. I haven't measured the pad but I think the size is on the web site"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008DDPL32', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380265200, 'question': "How long can I expect my baby to use this for? He's 4 mo &amp; moves around a lot in his crib and I constantly have to get up to flip him over.", 'answer': "my grandson just turned 6 mo. and started sleeping in a portable crib 2 weeks ago, I think that when a child can pull himself in to a sitting position that it isn't safe to leave them alone in it as they could wake up and pull up to the sides and tumble over the side onto the floor, my grandson could no longer stretch out comfortably in it but he still likes to get in it for a supervised nap ."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008DDPL32', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375599600, 'question': 'Considering this in place of a "normal" bassinet - good idea? How flat is it? Worried about baby getting used to the incline. Thanks!', 'answer': "I think this is better than a regular bassinet because it is portable and easy to travel with. This really doesn't have a incline, she lays flat, it is deep which is good and bad. Good because when your child pulls up it is still deep enough, and bad if it is next to your bed will have to get up to get the baby. I hope this helps"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008DDPL32', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374562800, 'question': 'can you use regular bassinet sheets or are there some you can purchase that will fit this?', 'answer': "The link below is to a sheet that fits pretty well. It's not perfect because the sheet is for a rectangular bassinet but this bassinet pad is a little rounded. I think it works great. I use a waterproof pad between the bassinet pad and the sheet. My little guy goes a lot and we have had a lot of leaks trying to find a diaper that works. The bassinet pad is washable, which is nice. Carters Easy Fit Jersey Bassinet Fitted Sheet - http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B001CWJEXE/ref=oh_details_o05_s00_i00?ie=UTF8&psc=1"}
