{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008DDPL32', 'answerTime': 'Feb 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424678400, 'question': "Is the pad comfortable on it's own or do I need to buy an additional pad. Does the pad come with a sheet? If not, do they sell sheets that fit? Thanks", 'answer': "The pad is pretty soft... at first. Its pretty thin, and quickly flattens out and becomes hard if you have baby sleeping on it every night. Due to the odd shape, there aren't really any mattresses you can buy, and last I checked, Fisher Price didn't sell replacement pads. There is no sheet, and I haven't seen any in this size or shape. Eventually, I cut a small slit in the bottom of the pad and inserted a blanket to pad it. Also, the pad is not machine washable. If baby pees through or spits up on the pad, you have to hand wash and air dry. And then hope in dries before nap time. Because, no replacements."}
