{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008E8KMJ4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 12, 2012', 'unixTime': 1352707200, 'question': 'What fabric is on the other side of the bumper?', 'answer': "The fabric is the dark fabric with circles. There is about 3 inches of lime green fabric that borders the edges around the circle fabric. I purchased 2 sets of this bedding for my twins and absolutely love them. The only thing I don't like about this set is that all of the labels say not to wash, dry or iron the set. Obviously, this is not practical with babies and all the spit up and goobers they launch. I wash my bedding sets normally but, dry each of them separately. I air dry the curtains, bedskirts and bumpers and steamed out the wrinkles. I dry the sheets the same as any normal sheets. I hope this is helpful to you."}
