{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008FX73PY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398754800, 'question': "How much room is left for changing? Looks like edges are so thick there wouldn't be room for more than a small infant, but 29 inch size is a hard find", 'answer': "We wanted to use the chest of drawers my dad made for me when I was a baby for our daughter. Because her room is small we decided to convert the top into her changing table but it would only accommodate a 29 inch pad. We bought this pad and have been very happy with it. We wanted something with 4 contoured sides rather than two, so this fit the bill. She is 7 and 1/2 months now and we still use this changing table everyday. Granted she's on the smaller size lengthwise but she still fits well in it. As she's gotten bigger her feet start to creep over the one side but it still works well. We are very happy with this product and how it works with our nursery."}
