{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390291200, 'question': 'Will I go to Hell if I just make my own Squatty Potty with scrap lumber?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hell or Heaven are more long term issues; however and in the short term, if you use scrap lumber-make it is not crappy lumber though and well sanded-then you'll save some money which you can use to buy food rich in fiber, that in turn will help you live a healthier life, that in turn will keep you from going to the doctor with hemorrhoids issues. Overall, the money that you'll save in doctors, medicines and insurance can be donated to your favorite charity, which in turn will probably put you closer to Heaven. Another added benefit of making your own Squatty Potty is that it will be stronger than the plastic model and, when standing on it, you'll definitely be closer to Heaven and farther away from Hell by either 7 or 9 inches. One more thing, don't do like in the picture, when you go potty make sure you drop your pants, otherwise it could turn messy. In conclusion, you'll probably will not go to Hell and the benefits are many."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Aug 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377846000, 'question': '9" vs. 7"', 'answer': 'It depends on the height of your toilet bowl from the floor. 15 inches or less buy the 7 inch. Above 15 inches, buy the 9 inch. Mine was exactly 15 inches, purchased the 7 inch and perfect.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387612800, 'question': "Don't you think that simply investing in a lower toilet would alleviate the need for a product like this? Serious question.", 'answer': 'No. There is no toilet that sits low enough. Any stool of similar height will work. The advantage of the squatty potty is that it fits well up against the toilet and out of the way when not in use.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375772400, 'question': 'My toilet is 15". I\'am 5\'5" tall. What size should I get? The 7" or 9"?', 'answer': 'My toilet is 16" and I\'m about your height. I tried the 9" but went with the 7" one instead. It works very well. Good luck with yours! Joan'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386230400, 'question': 'wouldnt just a regular stool work the same? Does this work for kids? My 7 y/o has potty issues and hemorrhoids already and this sounds like it might', 'answer': "The wrap around shape of the Squatty Potty positions your feet on the sides of the toilet, which allows your business to fall where it should. It is perfect for those of us with hemorrhoids or other gravity issues. The weight of your body shifts onto your feet and off of those delicate tissues. Stronger muscles then hold your body weight, allowing you to relax and go. I still think it's much more fun than the conventional way. A sound piece of advice came my way recently from my favorite old timer- Drink a cup of water first thing every morning. It really helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2012', 'unixTime': 1356508800, 'question': 'how do i know wheither to get the 7" or 9"?', 'answer': "I bought the 7 inch because I have an older toilet and it's shorter than the newer ones. Measure the height to get an idea of which size would work best."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418112000, 'question': 'Will this work for a plus size person? my husband has very thick thighs and I want to make sure it works before purchase.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I realty think it would work fine. I sit down then slide the squatty potty in position under my feet. It's a squat position without the weight on your legs."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Nov 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415952000, 'question': 'Do you like this item?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391155200, 'question': 'Do you leave it there all the time or only bring it out when you have to use it? I have a small bathroom and wish this could fold up when not in use.', 'answer': 'It is contoured to fit around the toilet bowl base. So it can stay in place and not take up much room.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008G9B11E', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404543600, 'question': 'Why should I buy this? I could lean forward and achieve the same angle recommended by the web site.', 'answer': "It's not the angle of the torso that is important . It's the lifting of the knees above the torso that makes a difference."}
