{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397631600, 'question': 'Is it possible to sit while wearing the carrier?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I do all the time when I wear mine. It isn't the most comfortable thing to do but it is possible."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397718000, 'question': 'My baby is due July 1st. Will she be hot in the carrier?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We live in Kentucky and i cant put our daughter in the baby carrier when its hot outside. We both get so warm from being so close together that its due to the weather absolutely not comfortable. But i think you have this problem with every baby carrier during the summer.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395298800, 'question': 'Can you nurse baby in this wrap?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, I know people who do consistently and I have a few times, but it isn't what I would consider ideal. It's a bit awkward."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397718000, 'question': 'Can you face the baby forward in the carrier?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, this baby carrier is not made for forward facing!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': 'Does having large breasts impede in the use of this carrier, since the baby can not be forward facing?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "I would not think so. I used this carrier and I have a fairly large chest, especially when I was breastfeeding. The carrier has straps that are adjustable to make it comfortable for you and the baby no matter your size, breasts or otherwise. I tried a couple carriers and the ergo was the best one that I found. I even carried my baby in it when he was 3 months on an uphill hike in the mountains for multiple miles. And I was not even remotely in shape. So it was very comfortable for me and the baby and worked very well. I would say this is the carrier you'd need with a larger chest because it really is designed to be ergonomic and it's way easier on the back."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402556400, 'question': 'Will this fit a petite Momma like myself? I\'m 5"2, and we have a preemie who is now at 8 lbs., 2 months old. Thanks so much for replying.....', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it will work for you. Actually it will help you how ever you choose to use it. You can carry on the front or back or even on your hip if you like. Whatever is most comfortable for you.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385884800, 'question': 'How is this different from "ERGObaby Performance Baby Carrier"? The only difference I see is it comes with the infant insert. ?', 'answer': 'As far as we could tell that is the only difference. Our daughter and son-in-law use it and they love it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422518400, 'question': 'How big does baby need to be to be used without insert?', 'answer': 'I think it was over 8 pounds? Should have good head control tho'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008GVGKPY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422518400, 'question': 'What is the age limit for this carrier? Or weight limit?', 'answer': 'Weight limit is 40 lbs. Which means I could carry my four year old if I wanted to - but I would not - I am still carrying my one year old in it and have a new baby coming anytime who will be carried in it. Sorry I do not have a secure answer on the age limit. I think that it really would depend on your child and how long you both feel comfortable wearing and being worn in it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Oct 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413097200, 'question': 'Can you use on the counter, or in a sink or tub only?', 'answer': 'You could use it on a counter to give sponge/wipe-down baths. It has a nice rubber ring completely covering the base that touches the tub/counter. However, the water will seep straight through the holes and will get water everywhere. It is great in that it air dries quickly which is good for preventing mold. I absolutely love this bath support and if your sink is big enough, it will fit nicely for an easy bath. I would recommend this to anyone! love love loved it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Nov 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414911600, 'question': 'Will this fit in the stokke flexi bath? http://www.amazon.com/dp/B00K0K6F4A?t...', 'answer': "I just use it in the regular bathtub, so this is just a guess, but I doubt it, as it is slightly wider/longer at the base. I'd stick with the infant support that goes with the stokke if you need one."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420531200, 'question': 'Can this be used for a newborn or should it be used once the baby is bigger?', 'answer': 'My granddaughter has usd this everyday sense her baby was born 3 months ago. She loves it'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420531200, 'question': 'How many months could you use this for? Did it last until the baby could sit in the tub?', 'answer': 'You can continue to use this until your baby can sit up on their own without support. My son is 9 months (wearing size 12 months clothes) and still needs a little help when sitting on his own. I still use this bath support but watch him closely if he tries to roll over. This bath support is my most favorite purchase!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Oct 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412838000, 'question': 'Does this float? The previous infant bath seat I had constantly starts floating around in the water and it drives me batty.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It floats a bit until you push it down. Then it pretty much stays put'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406876400, 'question': 'Will this tub fit in an infant tub? I have one from my first baby, but the support I had was kind of worn out and I wanted to put a new infant support', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Most likely no. It's fairly large. and it has a large flat base to make it stable in the tub. But you'd have to measure to be sure as I don't know how big your infant tub is."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395903600, 'question': 'Do you have any advice for transitioning from using this bath to just being in the tub?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I used this for my soon until he was almost 7 months and sitting up on his own very well. We didn't have to transition out of it before then because he never tried to sit up or roll off of the Angelcare Support. When he was ready, we moved him to a blow up ducky bath from Target. He loves it. He sits up well in it because its small and the sides help support him and I just stay right there to make sure he doesn't accidently fall. Easy transition. If I put him in the regular tub, I get in with him just to make sure he doesn't fall over."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'Could you use this in a sink or only the tub?', 'answer': 'You need a size large sink for it to fit. I bought a baby tub on a stand that I put it in and I thought it was an amazing product. It helped keep my wet, slippy and wiggling baby safe!:)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Sep 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378278000, 'question': 'please What is the size of the shipping box? Hi, I need to know the dimensions of the shipping box.', 'answer': "Just add a few inches to the length and width of the support and it should give you an idea of the size of the shipping box. The support is wrapped in a plastic bag and only required a box to fit it. That's the best I can do."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008H3PFM0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391760000, 'question': 'Is there a way to tell how far to fill up the bathtub with this support?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes; there is a line on the front which shows the max fill line. It only has a maximum fill line, but you can sort of see it in the picture; it is right be the Angelcare logo. It fills the bath up enough that the baby is sitting in a little bit of water, and there is plenty around to use for washing.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Oct 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383116400, 'question': 'When you use 2 infant car seats with the adaptors, do you still have the option to face the seats in different directions? Twins on the way...', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes! You can turn them in either direction. The stroller comes with 1 car seat adaptor so you will need to order a second one. My kids are 2 year old and a 5 month old and we love this stroller it's perfect!!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Dec 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388131200, 'question': 'Looking for a stroller that will fit newborn twins, which means two car seats. Will this stroller fit double car seats?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, but it only comes with one universal car seat adapter, so you will need to purchase one additional. It also comes with two regular stroller seats, so when they are older you are all set! I love mine for my infant and toddler. super easy to change the seats. Pushes great!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379487600, 'question': 'If you have the car seat adapter on it, does it fold up with it, or do you have to take it off every time you fold the stroller up? Thanks :)', 'answer': "You flip up the sides of the car seat adapter(s) -leaving them attached- and then the whole stroller will fold up. We use ours with two adapters because we had twins. It's a great stroller- very easy to use and manouver and not too terribly heavy."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376377200, 'question': 'good for infant?', 'answer': 'Yes it has a bar that you can use in place of the seat that allows you to snap the infant seat onto.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'box contains two chairs shown in the picture?', 'answer': 'Yes, you get both seats with the stroller.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403852400, 'question': 'Can you tell me what mosquito netting works best with this?', 'answer': "Sorry, I didn't buy a netting for mine."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388563200, 'question': 'Can both the two seats full recline?I have twins baby ,so I want know whether my babies can sleep comfortable at the same time without carseat.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The seats have three positions. The lowest position reclines quite a lot, but its not flat like a bed. My twins slept well in the pram from birth, no problems. We still use the pram now and I'm still enjoying it very much. My twins are now 16 months! All the best, hope this helps"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363158000, 'question': 'Can we use this pram for our newborn without a car seat? What age is it recommended for when not using the car seat?', 'answer': 'Yes i put my newborn in the seat all the time. I recline the seat all the way back.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T65W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379314800, 'question': 'How stable are seats once in place? Do they jiggle or vibrate while strolling? How well does this fold flat? Is it awkward to push? Would u buy again?', 'answer': "The seats are secure. They do rock a little forward and back once snapped in, but it would be a bumpy and uncomfortable ride for the kids if they didn't since the tires are not inflated. It folds flat easily and fits well in the back of a van or wagon. It handles well, just don't expect the turning radius of a single stroller. Would definitely buy this again. We looked at numerous tandem strollers and you will not find a better one without spending $700+."}
