{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008H3T5SA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378710000, 'question': 'Can this be fitted with two infant car seat adapters? We are having twins, so this is a must for us!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Love Love Love this stroller!! I use with infant and toddler but can be used for two infant carseats. You will just need to purchase another adaptor. Hope this helps!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T5SA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396767600, 'question': 'As it is can you use this for twins without buying anything additionally', 'answer': 'I would say for 5 month olds. The only con I see in this car is that the front seat does not layd (?) as much as the back one, if both kids are facing front. Sometimes I use the car for my old boys (2 and 4 years old), sometimes the 2 yo with the baby (6 months). But it is very easy to change the seats (I do it even when my 2 yo is seated and start kicking the front seat. i simply put him facing me).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T5SA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398322800, 'question': 'Anyone ever own the City Select double stroller as well? How does this compare? Much cheaper, but is it at a cost of quality and functionality?', 'answer': "I have owned this stroller for a year now and my first choice was the City Select, but the price was prohibitive. I liked it at first and I still do, but I am now wishing I would have spent more money initially and gotten either the City Select Double or the City Mini Double. I bought this after my second daughter was born. She is now 14 months and my oldest is 3. The 3 year old is 32# and 37 inches tall (63rd percentile), and she looks a little squished in the seat. It does push really well and I liked that it came with both seats and the infant seat adapter, but I don't know how much longer my oldest will be comfortable. Also, it is kind of awkward to move once it is collapsed. I think the Baby Jogger City models fold up better. For these reasons, I am now considering buying the City Mini double. Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T5SA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407826800, 'question': "Do the seats pop in and out easily? I've heard the stroller is hard to fold with the seats in?", 'answer': "Seats pop out very easily. I always fold mine with the seats in, both facing front (that's how we usually use the stroller these days) and as long as both seats are up and the belly bars don't get stuck when I fold it because I'm not paying attention, it is fine."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T5SA', 'answerTime': 'Jun 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403938800, 'question': 'I have a 2007 chevy tahoe, does anyone know if this is storage compatible with this same type of vehicle or not?', 'answer': "I have an older Tahoe and I can put the stroller in on it's side and it fits across the back. It's long but not terribly bulky."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008H3T5SA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407826800, 'question': 'Issues with steering and the wheels popping off? Read some reviews to that effect.', 'answer': "The only time the wheels have popped off have been if I am lifting it out of the van and one gets caught on something. And even then it's only been the front wheel (and only one) and it's my fault, really. So I haven't had that issue. I also haven't had issues with the steering. If it were a car, I'd rate it as I would a Buick or a high end Ford, not a Lincoln or Cadillac, but I have been through all kinds of terrain with it and never had a problem."}
