{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008KCR7VK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383030000, 'question': 'Some stores sell this as the "car seat base" without adding the work "kit." Is it the same item? (I believe it has the same item number.)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I am not sure what the "kit" is but this base comes with everything you need to use it in a vehicle minus the car seat. We had the car seat and base for one vehicle and I needed a base for my car. I purchased this and it is the exact same as the base that came with the car seat. Hope this answered your question. Thanks'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008KCR7VK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386316800, 'question': 'Sorry what is the function of this base? I seems like a baby car seat', 'answer': "The base is separate from the seat. The seat can lock into the base, but it can also lock into a Britax stroller. A seat comes with one base. The base has a quick release handle for easy unlocking and removal of the seat. My wife and I bought a second, separate base so that we could lock one down in the back seats of both her car and my SUV. This allowed us to quickly unlock and lift out the seat (which has a stowable carry handle) and transport our son, rather than having to unstrap him or strap him every time we exited or entered a vehicle. Note that the base can lock to a seat by either of two methods: via the seat belts; or via hooks and latches, if your vehicle has anchor brackets. (If your vehicle is so equipped, your vehicle owner's manual will have a section on this; more than likely, you will have baby seat symbols marked near your anchor points.)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008KCR7VK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425542400, 'question': 'does this base work with the newer Britax B-Safe 35 model car seat?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, you would need the base named Britax B-Safe 35 base.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008KCR7VK', 'answerTime': 'Sep 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411542000, 'question': "Can this car seat base be used for a larger car seat? We need to upsize our car seat soon, as our baby is 30 lbs. It'd be nice to use the same base.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think this product only works with the B-Safe infant car seat. The next size up car seats are convertible, meaning that your child will sit in them rear-facing until they reach a certain weight then you'll turn the seat around so they sit front-facing. This base would not work with such a seat because it's too high in the front. Ironically I had the same question yesterday because I'm ready for an upgrade and I just did some research on convertible car seats this morning. I like the Britax brand and I think I'm going to go with the Britax Boulevard G4 for my next car seat."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008KCR7VK', 'answerTime': 'Aug 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407567600, 'question': 'do they have expiration dates just like the car seat?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'They have a serial number & manufacturer date on them. Amazon sent us one with a manufacturer date of a year old from the time of purchase.'}
