{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008NJLDKG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'Is this breathable and sturdy enough to carry a toddler (25 lb one-year-old) on my back to hike?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Depends how long you're going to hike...It's pretty breathe able but the straps aren't padded, also since baby is right next to your body it'll be hotter than a frame carrier. So they aren't as comfortable as other carriers for long times, because of no padding. That being said I have worn my 20lb 12 month old for some extended periods, usually on my front if she nurses and falls asleep. I really like my boba air, it comes in handy in lots of random situations. For long hikes we usually mostly use a frame backpack and stuff the boba air in a pocket if the backpack in case she gets fussy or wants to nurse."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008NJLDKG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 11, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426057200, 'question': 'Is it good for a newborn? Will the baby be comfortable?', 'answer': "No. I recently called the Boba company since I love this carrier with my 2 year old, but wanted to give it as a baby shower gift. This isn't recommended for a new born. I would recommend the Boba wrap for those first weeks and months. It is extremely comfortable and the baby's weight melts into your body. Then buy the Boba Air as the next step. I love the Boba Air (and the wrap while it could carry the babies weight) and looking back those would be the only two carriers I would buy instead of wasting my money on others. I hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008NJLDKG', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401778800, 'question': 'Can this carrier be used in the water, like in the pool or at the beach?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It's a nylon (parachute) type material so if you are just standing in a pool or whatever, it wouldn't be bad if it got a little wet. No pads, so it would dry quick, but I don't think it's necessarily made for it, so too much chlorine could be a problem if prolonged use in a pool."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008NJLDKG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1430377200, 'question': 'can we have the 21 lb 18 month old in front outward facing position', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Boba specs the front carry for 15-30 lbs. They do not recommend front-facing, because that position forces the baby's legs to hang down and strain her hips and arch her back. I never carried my daughter front facing because she hated it...maybe that is why. Anyway, I'd say the design of the carrier follows Boba's thinking on the matter."}
