{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008OHWNOC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427958000, 'question': 'Do you think this would work on a convertible backpack/roller type of luggage??', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Honestly, I don't think so!! Unless the convertible back pack is as rigid as a true carry on roll on luggage!! U also got to keep in mind that the back portion of the ride-on-carry on sits against the front of the travel luggage!! It may not sit right or it may be extremely uncomfortable for ur child!! This is just my opinion!!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008OHWNOC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426662000, 'question': 'How do the straps work for attaching to the luggage? Looks like just one strap? would it not slide down/off with the weight of your child?', 'answer': "There's a strap that goes around the body of the luggage (and through the side handle) and a strap that goes on too over the pop up handle of the luggage. I just used this on a trip with my 35 lb 4 year old and he loved it as much as I did. The only problem I encountered was the clasp on the top strap breaking on the firsl leg of our travels. It would have been devastating if I wasn't good at figuring out how to fix stuff. I would suggest they use metal clasps instead of plastic. Even if a child is well below the weight allowance, all the bumping and shaking that the seat takes puts extra strain on it. That said, I LOVE THIS SEAT! And i probably sold about 8 of them with all the people that stopped and took photos of it and asked questions. A great purchase!"}
