{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008OJ7C6Y', 'answerTime': 'Jul 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373958000, 'question': 'What is the difference between the Snuza hero and Snuza halo baby monitor?', 'answer': "Hi, The Hero is the newest model. I am not certain that much, if anything has changed in features, except possibly this. I believe one of the features is that if the monitor has to vibrate to stimulate the baby more than twice within a short period of time the alarm will go off even if the baby is breathing. I did a good bit of research before buying the monitor and I couldn't find that feature with the halo. It may be the same, but I couldn't find the feature listed in its description. We have been using the monitor for two months now and love it. We did have one false alarm after changing the brand of diapers we were using. The diapers became looser as they got wetter through the night. What I discovered though due to that heart stopping incident is that the alarm worked even though the baby was swinging. (early on we needed to swing her at times to get her to sleep) Since the monitor is a motion detector I did not think it would work properly while the child was in motion, but it did."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008OJ7C6Y', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388995200, 'question': 'Is this product reliable and comfortable for tummy sleepers? My baby is six months old and has started rolling onto her tummy and face planting....', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Shannon, I use this every nap and every night. It depends on how much you baby moves around at night as they get older, and how securely you slide it on to the front of their diaper (you need to fold the top front of the diaper under a half an inch or so to provide a secure place with enough material to keep the Snuza in place). The Snuza is perfect, it probably comes off once every month if the baby is rolling all over in which case you hear it, pick it up from the crib mattress and slide it back on the diaper. Tummy sleeping is perfectly fine, and my baby has never noticed it's on, and you can hear it if it ever goes off. Bottom line: Get this, it's the most important purchase I've ever made as it saved my baby's life when he stopped breathing one night at about four months...scariest night ever, but after picking him back up and rocking him the stimulation started him breathing again. Sometimes babies forget to breathe when they are asleep because of the immaturity of their brain stem, and I would never put my child down for a nap or at night without this on. Never. Two of my friends had babies die of SIDS. I wonder how different their lives would be if they had bought this and used it. Blessings to you..."}
