{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008TA9X74', 'answerTime': 'Aug 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377846000, 'question': 'Will this work with Dr. Browns glass bottles 4 oz and 8oz?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It sure does! When our little one was born, we knew we were going to use glass exclusively and bought the Born Free bottles, bottle warmer and sterilizer. Well, the bottles weren't so good for gas, so we switched to Dr. Brown's glass bottles and bought the Dr. Brown's sterilizer too, but we kept the Born Free bottle warmer. It worked great and was one less thing we had to replace! I will warn though that the Dr. Brown's bottles aren't as wide as Born Free, so when heating you have to be mindful of the hot steam rising up around the bottle if you try to remove the bottle before the time is up. We never used the back portion for frozen breastmilk or formula. Hope this helps!"}
