{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008UKKXRC', 'answerTime': 'May 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401519600, 'question': 'I want to light a 5 meter (16.4 ft) strip of 5050 RGB lights for a few hours per charge. What mAh rating will suffice?', 'answer': 'The math looks like this - Plan 60 ma per 5050 LED, Multiply that by the number of LEDs, the result is what you would need to power the strip for an hour, Multiply that by the number of hours you need and that will tell you your power requirement. This would be the LEDs burning at full white. if the flash or change colors the time they will last goes up. As they come in 30, 60 & 144 per meter I cannot guess the number of LEDs you have.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008UKKXRC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387353600, 'question': 'The specs say 6.5 x 6 x 1.1 inches. In the pics it looks more oblong. Are those the correct dimensions of the brick itself?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'As measured my me, my Model 12450 is 4-7/8" X 2-3/4" X 1-3/16" for the body of the housing itself. on the 4-7/8" side, add an additional 3/8" for the on/off rocker-switch that sticks out a bit. Picture looks proportional to my unit.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008UKKXRC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405580400, 'question': 'Could you measure the battery for me and give me the LxHxW', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The length of the battery is 4 7/8". The thickness or height of the battery is 1". The width of the battery is 2 3/4".'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008UKKXRC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'Hooking this battery up to a 400w inverter. When I turn on the inverter with no load, the low voltage alarm sounds, the inverter turns off . Thoughts?', 'answer': "This doesn't produce enough current for that. Just not enough power. You'll need something larger."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008UKKXRC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424160000, 'question': 'I\'m looking at charging a lav mic transmitter w/ the requirements: "13-15v dc nominal 500 ma" will this 12.6v do, or do I need something stronger?', 'answer': 'Depends on what the lowest voltage your device can function at. The battery pack voltage is lower than what you specify. It actually puts out about 12.2v when fully charged but will drop to around 10.5 to 11v as it discharges. It is not a true 12v battery pack by design.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008UKKXRC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428908400, 'question': 'Will this fry a device that needs 12V 0.6A?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Absolutely not. As long as the device is 12volts it will only draw power from the battery as needed. In other words you can hook one of said devices to the battery or many.. the only thing that will change is battery life. I love mine.. and I use it to power anything from 12v cameras to 12v led's to 12v lcd monitors. From 0.2A all the way to 4.5A"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008UKKXRC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 31, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427785200, 'question': 'What size is the DC output jack?', 'answer': "It's the same size as the plug that goes into your PC. It's a standard size."}
