{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008VQLPY0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394866800, 'question': 'does this have rubber or plastic wheels?', 'answer': 'Rubber around the plastic wheels and they are good quality. So far we found no issue with it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008VQLPY0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404370800, 'question': 'Does it fit the Britax B-Agil stroller?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it does. I have the Britax B-Agile stroller and purchased the Dream On Me Tag Along Stroller (skate) and it fit perfectly. As Jane responded, it attaches to any stroller that has a bar going across the back wheels.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008VQLPY0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404284400, 'question': 'Does this fit a Graco Quattro Tour Deluxe stroller and if so is it hard to steer the stroller with a toddler standing in front of you?', 'answer': "I think it's pretty universal. It is a bit harder to stear the stroller when using the board, but you get use to it. I love mine, use it all the time. It's very easy to put on & take off."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008VQLPY0', 'answerTime': 'Sep 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378882800, 'question': 'Can this be used with the City Mini GT single?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Believe it can be used with any stroller that has a straight bar at the back of the stroller to attached the dream on me tag-a-along board. The board can be adjusted vertical and horizontal.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008VQLPY0', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'Will this work on a standard umbrella type stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It attaches using two open latches, and although they are adjustable width-wise you need them to attach at the same height. If your umbrella stroller has a horizontal bar across the back, you should be fine. If it has only an X brace, it may not work. We have an old Maclaren umbrella stroller (10 yrs old) that has an X brace but also a bar, and it works fine. The bar is thin and flat, not round (which would be ideal), but it still works. The other consideration is how tall your umbrella stroller is -- the cheap, free-with-purchase types are shorter and I think pushing it with the board attached would be very uncomfortable, as you would have to bend over too far.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008VQLPY0', 'answerTime': 'Sep 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410418800, 'question': 'will it fit a chicco liteway stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It fits any stroller that has a bar between the wheels. If there isn't a bar there is no where to attach it"}
