{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008VWEDJI', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': 'how many exterior pockets does this bag have?', 'answer': "It has 3 exterior pockets. Two at each side which are very deep, eac can hold two standard Dr. brown'ss bottles and the back pocket holds the changing pad. I also keep any soiled clothes there as well. The two zipped pockets in the picture are I guess mummy pockets. The top one is deep and I keep hand sanitizer, tissues, lipgloss etc. the bottom zipped section has card slots for credit cards etc...I keep my phone there tho and my keys. Hope this helps"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008VWJHUS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429340400, 'question': 'Can you use regular grocery bags instead of liners?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'You can use a regular grocery bag and half a paper towel at the bottom to reduce splatter. It wont be pretty but it should work.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008VWJHUS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396767600, 'question': 'The description says it "has no liners", but the people in the reviews indicate that it came with liners or bags. Does it require liners or not?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It comes with 10 liners, which are helpful when you are away from a sink. In a house you can just wash and wipe it clean, just like regular potty. After the Graco baggies ran out, I just ordered the refill of Pottette baggies (30 pack available on Amazon) - it works perfectly, so no worries about compatibility.'}
