{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008VWJHUS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426834800, 'question': "How big is the hole in this potty? I have a toddler that is off the charts in height so the little potties won't work.", 'answer': 'It is small, much smaller then normal potty chair openings. I would guess no more then 8 inches. It is not tall either. I was worried about this at first but honestly, my 3 year old has no problems using it when another potty is not available. We love it as it is great to take on hikes or in the car or any other area that we need an emergency potty chair. It is small enough we can pack it in our suitcases as well.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008VWJHUS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409641200, 'question': 'Can this be used as a seat on top of a toilet or is it only stand alone?', 'answer': "It's a stand alone only. It's a great travel potty for toddlers though. I take it everywhere. It fits in a small bag. I tried using the toddler seat on top of the full size toilet and it was just to big and intimidating for the my toddlers. We just took the Graco twisting travel potty to the fair and worked like a dream."}
