{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008X7CKJG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362902400, 'question': "I'm trying to figure out if my kids will fit in these seats. The options lt seats are too small, my 23 mth old didn't fit &amp; he isn't a big kid.", 'answer': "my big boy - 17 kgs and 27 months old fits. Granted he is too tall to sleep in it (head is just taller than pram back rest) but he doesn't sleep in prams anyway. And he either bends his knees to place feet on foot rest, or he just dangles and swings them - which is fine because they are miles away from the ground and dont bang the pram :) Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008X7CKJG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2012', 'unixTime': 1355212800, 'question': "I have a 2007 Toyota Camry and I've already bought one double stroller that didn't fit into my trunk, is there anyway of knowing if this one would?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It measures 40inc tall (wheels to handle) and 26in across the base. This pram collapses front to back - so there fore does not fold 'in half'. You will need to have the 40 in clearance to get it in the boot. Other than that, its the same width as a single pram and about as bulky as a single. Awesome pram :)"}
