{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008YL94PY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406271600, 'question': 'Has anyone found this cotton carrier to overheat? I am torn between the cotton (softer I assume) and the mesh one (cooler).', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It is mainly body heat that warms you up, but I have both this one and the mesh one, and the zip down panel does make a difference. I'd say which to get depends on where you live... it has to be pretty hot (like, over 85*, for me at least) before the mesh helps much... and the cotton is softer and generally more comfortable (though not by a large margin). So if its hot a lot where you live, go mesh. If heat isn't an all-the-time issue, go cotton"}
