{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008YLCUOG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390982400, 'question': 'I heard you can use this carrier with the straps criss-crossed in the back - is this true and if so how do you put it on (by yourself)?', 'answer': "I've never tried to wear it that way, but theoretically I guess you could. The only reason I can think of for wanting to though is because it can sometimes be hard to snap the two straps together behind your back by yourself. Although, crossing the straps would give less room for the baby because it would have to pull the sides together across the front a little bit. I wouldn't recommend it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008YLCUOG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386662400, 'question': 'Will this really work for my two-year-old? She weighs around 25 pounds.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi, I bought this baby carrier when my daughter is 1 month old. Now she is 10 month and 4 week old. She is 20 pound. I am still using my carrier but I am not comfortable as previous. The carrier has one snap-fastener both side of down part of carrier. It should be stay more stable to keep bottom part of it wide, but when baby is gaining weight and moving her leg more stronger then snap fastener easily opens. That time my back getting ache quickly. This carrier is not good and strong for big baby. I hope this review is helpful.'}
