{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00917LK16', 'answerTime': 'May 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368514800, 'question': 'What is the difference between this car seat, Chicco KeyFit 30 MAGIC Infant and the Chicco KeyFit 30 Infant?', 'answer': "The major difference is in the canopy. The magic model has a fantastic canopy that almost completely covers the baby. It has a zip feature that opens up to a mesh material to allow air to circulate. It also has a different infant insert than the other chicco models. Another thing worth noting is that when the inserts are removed there is no ribbing on the seat fabric. Many review on the regular chicco model complain about this ribbing digging into a baby's head and causing a mark. Personally, I chose chicco because of its high safety ratings and ease of use which you will get with either model, but the magic had more of the features I was looking for. We've been using the magic for 5.5 months now and love it! I'd highly recommend it, especially along with the chicco caddy stroller frame!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00917LK16', 'answerTime': 'Feb 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423382400, 'question': 'Which shade covers more: Zip or Magic model?', 'answer': 'The Magic model has much more shade coverage, which is one of the main reasons we purchased our Key fit 30 Magic.'}
