{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0091E31KM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392537600, 'question': 'If the power goes out, will it switch to battery automatically?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. In fact, we routinely keep batteries in ours because if the power goes out and then comes back on, it goes to the default sound, the heartbeat, which we find rather creepy.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0091E31KM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381388400, 'question': 'Some of these machines have about a 3-second loop; the sound recycles every few seconds. How about this one?', 'answer': "Yes, there is a short loop that plays. It still works just fine for us (for ocean, or rain, it works great. the forest has a bird chirping a bit too regularly for my taste.) But if you are sensitive to it, this could drive you nuts. We've bought these for years (we use them every night and they eventually break down). I prefer them to some of the other similarly priced or cheaper models because of the quality of the sounds."}
