{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00952P7PC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': 'What does the cup look like without the lid? Child is just about ready for a regular cup and would like to use to transition from sippy to regular.', 'answer': 'These are not good for that. The entire cup edge has screw-top threads and little "lock" tabs that stick out on each side. The First Years Take & Toss Spill-Proof Sippy Cups are like regular cups when you take the lid off.'}
