{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYBPC', 'answerTime': 'May 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399014000, 'question': 'My son is 27 1/4 inch tall but he only weights 15 lbs. would the small size fit him?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Your son is longer than my daughter (25 inches) but weighs the same. I think the length would force you to move to the next size quickly. I would probably go with the next size.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYBPC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423555200, 'question': 'My son is about 25 inches long and a little over 14 pounds. What size should I get?', 'answer': 'Large'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYBPC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421136000, 'question': 'My daughter is just shy of 14lbs and only 24in tall. I am debating about the size because she is going to be 7 months old, but she is little.', 'answer': "My little guy is 7.5 months old and we had him in the Large about three months ago. It was big but it was still effective and he didn't mind sleeping in it! It wasn't a magical experience as he still is up every two hours to nurse (no fault of the sleep suit of course!) but it REALLY did help with the amount of jerking movements that would wake him up. He is 18lbs and 28 inches and the large still fits his body but his arms and legs have grown out of the length of the sleeves (poor boy goes to bed in high waters but we are still using the sleep suit ;)!!!! So if you want a snug fit go with the smaller size! Hope my babble helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYBPC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418284800, 'question': 'Is this magic suit the microfleece option?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The outside is fleece and the inside is soft cotton material. It's pretty thick so I typically pit baby in a short or long sleeve onesie and socks."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYBPC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414566000, 'question': 'My son is 20.1 lbs 6 month old. We are having a horrible time at bedtime. Because of his size, is it even worth investing in one?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes get the bigger size. My 18 pound baby was a little small for the big one so your 20 pound baby will be great in it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYBPC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410418800, 'question': 'My baby is 15 lbs. Should I get the medium or large sleepsuit? Will it be ok to be a little big at first?', 'answer': "The medium should fit well for awhile yet. It's ok for it to be a little loose, but not so loose that it moves up over the baby's chin and mouth."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYBPC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362985200, 'question': 'Is this suit not a SIDS risk with over bundling? It looks like a snow suit, very thick and heavy.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It is indeed thick which is what helps keep them feeling snug similar to the swaddling effect. I've found that dressing my daughter in just a short-sleeve onesie and no socks and keeping the temp of the room btwn 69-70 degrees all winter has worked well and she doesn't get overheated. Heat escapes through the hand and feet openings, plus her neck is still exposed for ventilation. In fact, on very cold nights I added socks while she slept when her feet seemed too cold and was grateful she was cozy in the suit. We started her in the suit at 4 months old - she's now 6 months and has slept comfortably in it every single night!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYBPC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394006400, 'question': 'Concerning the position of the arms &amp; legs for development: Is it stiff? Can the baby still get his legs in the froggy position? Can he bend his arms?', 'answer': "The suit is not stiff, but it is padded so that the baby isn't disturbed by their 'startle reflex'. I think the padding also helps make laying flat more comfortable as it gives some cushion to the back. My son did not move his legs in to the 'frog' position, but he was able to kick. He could not lift his legs enough to grab his feet though. He was able to move his arms and touch his face, but I know others who have told me their babies were not able to touch their face. I showed the suit to 2 very well known Pediatricians in the Phila area and they both saw no reason why a baby should not wear the suit - they did not feel it could harm development. They did just make sure that we would not use it once our son was able to roll on his own."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415952000, 'question': 'is this garment treated with flame retardants? is it made of fabrics that have been treated with flame retardants?', 'answer': 'Oops...I just asked this myself. Have you found an answer?'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1430118000, 'question': "Is this too hot to start using in spring? We have AC, but I'm worried about overheating", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't think so. Regardless of the time of year I keep my thermostat between 70&72 with the fan running low. I also have blackout panels so even on warmer days the nursery remains the same temperature."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385280000, 'question': 'Is it too early to try this if my baby is only ten weeks old? (He is 12 pounds so he meets the weight guideline but is not long.)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No, it isn't too early. My son is around 12 pounds at 16 weeks but is short and I just cuff the legs to make them shorter."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390723200, 'question': 'Why should I pay $40-$70 for this item? Why not just use a sleeper?', 'answer': "The Magic Sleepsuit is uniquely different from a sleeper since it is made of three layers of fabric, which provide babies with a cozy, secure feeling and help muffle their reflexive startle movements to aid in their sleep. The Magic Sleepsuit was designed by a mother of four who is also a pediatric physical therapist. It is designed to be introduced as babies are transitioning from the swaddle, and should be used for back sleeping in the crib. In addition to transitioning from the swaddle, many customers have used the Magic Sleepsuit to help successfully transition from a smaller sleep space (e.g. Rock N Play, bassinet). Please feel free to visit our website (www.magicsleepsuit.com) and Facebook page (www.facebook.com/MagicSleepsuit) for more product information and testimonials from customers. The Magic Sleepsuit is also talked about on many parenting sites, and blogs to give you more information on other parents' experiences with the Magic Sleepsuit. The price of the Magic Sleepsuit is $39.95 for one and $69.95 for any combination of two Magic Sleepsuits. Please feel free to contact us directly with any further questions - info@magicsleepsuit.com, 1-877-458-0130. Thank you! Baby Merlin Company"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': '25 days ago', 'question': 'My 3 month old likes to cross her legs while she sleeps. Would she be able to cross them with this product? Thank you.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I doubt it. At 3 months, or any months, the suit is pretty "marshmallow puffy" so it restricts movement. It\'s a transition from swaddling, and keep babies warm.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424246400, 'question': "I have to feed my son a few times during the night. Do I take him out of this when I'm bottle feeding? Im afraid if I do, he will wake up.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You don't have to take him out. I nurse my son to sleep every night in the suit."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415952000, 'question': 'Does anyone know if these are treated with flame retardants?', 'answer': 'No'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412060400, 'question': 'Do you put baby in the suit and then breastfeed? Or, feed first, then suit up?', 'answer': 'Breasfeed first.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391155200, 'question': "We have a little guy - he just turned 5 months and is 14lbs... he's long though - should I get the 3-6 month one or the 6-9 month?", 'answer': 'My son is 16lbs and 25" long (4.5 months) and he\'s in the 3-6 size. It still has plenty of room for him to grow another inch or so. I put him in long sleeved sleepers, so it doesn\'t matter if his legs or arms stick out a little bit...'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY7RY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384070400, 'question': "How should the Merlin Sleep Suit fit? Should it be somewhat roomy. My 4 month old is 14 lbs and I'm afraid the 3-6 mon is too small.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Our baby is close to 13lbs and I feel like she has a few more months in it- it is very roomy on her. I think you would still get a lot of use out of it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Jan 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390550400, 'question': 'How is the sizing? My 4.5 mo is tall (27") on the thinner side (about 14lbs). Currently he\'s in 6mo clothing. Would the 6-9 size be too big?', 'answer': 'My son was the same when we bought ours and we found 6-9 to be a good fit. He is almost 6 months now and he still fits but it is more like capris and the neck line goes low.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Jul 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405494000, 'question': 'My daughter is almost 5 months old &amp; is 18 lbs. If she can roll easily, will she be able to roll in sleep suit??', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I would assume that she could roll in the sleepsuit. It is slightly weighted and makes it harder to move/roll but if she's rolling easily I would think she could roll in the suit."}
{'answer': "It's like a very think cotton filling. It's just heavy enough that it helps with their reflex so when they jerk, it won't wake them up. It worked wonders for my son.", 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': '1 day ago', 'question': 'I am baffled, what is it made of or how does it work, is it filled with something that makes the suit heavy or stiff?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': 'Are the sizes true to the months?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Fit is extremely important to the safety and effectiveness of the Magic Sleepsuit. If the suit is too large it will not be able to keep your baby cozy and muffle the startle reflex as it is intended to do. Since every baby is shaped differently, our sizing guidelines are a suggestion based on the average 3-6 and 6-9 month old. When in doubt, choose the size closest to the clothing size that your baby is wearing. Please give us a call and we will be more than happy to answer any additional sizing questions at 877-458-0130.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425456000, 'question': 'Is it safe &amp; effective for a 6- month old who loves to roll to sleep on his stomach?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "My 8 month old just started to roll and sleep on her belly. I can't keep her off it! I use the snooza every night and we have never had any issues."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423814400, 'question': "My 4 month old is huge - 28 inches and 21 pounds. I'm afraid this might be too small, any ideas?", 'answer': "I think it should fit him at his current size, although it might not fit him for very much longer. My 7 month old was about that size last month when he stopped wearing it (not because it didn't fit anymore, just because we thought it was time). The makers of the suit made the crotch really low to allow for taller/longer torso babies, so his arms and legs might stick out more than they would for other babies, but it won't be uncomfortable for him. My little one is pretty chunky, and we never had an issue with tightness around belly or anything. Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': 'How difficult is it to get baby to learn to sleep without the suit once they are used to sleeping in the crib with it?', 'answer': 'I put my baby in the zipadee zip next and is currently still in it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Oct 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413788400, 'question': 'Can the baby still suck their fingers to self-soothe?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It depends on how long the LO's arms are and how strong they are to reach their mouths. My LO could easily teach his mouth, but not at first."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Jun 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402038000, 'question': 'The material looks hot. Is it too heavy to use in the summer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Not at all! We live in south Florida , so and always hot here We put him in a onesie and then the suit and he has never sweat. He had been wearing it every night for 2 months now'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YY99K', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'What size to get? My babe is small - 6 months but 15 lbs and 25 inches....', 'answer': '6-9 month'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376722800, 'question': "How old does the baby have to be to use Merlin's magic sleep suit?", 'answer': 'The suit recommends about 3 months old, which happened to be right about when we found out about it. You probably can try sooner but it really may not be too much help when lo still needs to eat during the night.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428649200, 'question': "What is the optimal sizing? Is it supposed to be so tight that they can't get their hands to their mouth?", 'answer': 'Optimal would be a snug fit. Suit is not intended top completely limit movement or access to hands, but to muffle movement and provide as safe secure feeling.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427353200, 'question': 'What material is better for the spring and summer months?', 'answer': "It really depends on the temp of the baby's room more than the season. If the baby's room is on the warmer side in the winter or summer months, then the cotton exterior may be best. If the room is cool, then fleece exterior may be best. Also depends on how your baby regulates their temp. If they run warmer, then cotton may be best. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426662000, 'question': 'Can you use this when baby is 8 months and flipping over?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This suit is only for back sleeping, the company says it is not safe once the baby can roll over in it. However, just because a baby can roll over out of the suit, it doesn't mean they can roll over while in it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423987200, 'question': 'Can you breastfeed with it on?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419753600, 'question': 'it comes in micro fleece or cotton. What is the difference? which is better?', 'answer': "We got the micro fleece instead of the cotton because we like the fleece material better on jackets we own. i believe the inside material is the same, so it's just a matter of preference as to which exterior material you prefer."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414825200, 'question': 'How do these fit? big or small or true to size?', 'answer': 'True to size'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411282800, 'question': 'My daughter just started rolling over at night swaddled which wakes her. Will this help her not roll over at night?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes my son can not roll over in this it's pretty weighted. Its wonderful!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Aug 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408863600, 'question': "Is this appropriate for the summer months (i.e., when it's hot)? I like the concept but fleece seems like it would make my baby too warm w/o the AC.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We have our a/c set to 72 and she sleeps in it with a tshirt onesie on. I think it'd be too hot without a/c, depending on where you live."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYAW6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402902000, 'question': "Anyone have any experience using this during teething? Everyone keeps telling me his sleep patterns won't last! I'm loving my 9 hrs every night!", 'answer': "We had a couple nights where he didn't sleep through because his teeth hurt, but once we handled that and got his pain under control he slept great. It's designed to help with the jerking awake not the other factors that may come into play."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0095YYAGC', 'answerTime': 'May 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399878000, 'question': 'Does anyone have experience transitioning out of the sleepsuit once your child has outgrown it? Was it difficult?', 'answer': 'I have not personally experienced this. However, my good friend transitioned her son at 6 months. She tried cold turkey and he screamed for hours. So she put him in the suit with just leg in and arms out for a few nights zipped up. Then a few nights just legs in not zipped and then a few nights laying him on top. Then took it away. During the whole time she gave him a blanket to hold on to. He now sleeps with his blanket and no sleep suit just fine.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0095YYAGC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380351600, 'question': "I'm looking for a warmer swaddle for our baby to wear in the winter months. Would this be a good choice for a warm, winter swaddle?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It's pretty warm without being too hot. She slept in it all summer with a onesie on. As it's gotten cooler out, we actually dress our little girl in normal PJ's with feet. She doesn't get overheated. She typically sleeps 10 hours at night now and takes a two hour nap during the day. We have two suits now... one for home and one for daycare. It's the best $40 we've spent so far on baby stuff! Definitely worth a shot!"}
