{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00978OWVE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380783600, 'question': 'can a 3 month old use this? will it fit in his mouth?', 'answer': "Absolutely. They're kind of like knobby terry wash cloths, and they have so many edges that it's easy for them to get some part of it in their mouths. The grapes are maybe three inches across the top of the bunch, but any baby could chew on a stem, leaf, or corner, if nothing else. I didn't give them to my son until he started cutting teeth at four months, but there would be no harm in letting a three month old chew/suck on them. They're not a choking hazard, and they're fun when frozen. I just wring them out before I freeze them so they don't get everything wet as they melt. These are my son's favorite teething toys."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00978OWVE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402383600, 'question': 'when they start to thaw will they drip with water?', 'answer': 'Yes. Honestly- using a frozen washcloth is about the same thing.'}
