{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0097F3YES', 'answerTime': 'Jun 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403938800, 'question': 'can I use these with my IPOD or computer?', 'answer': 'Yes you can use it with both'}
{'answer': 'Once you receive the Belly Buds a code is included to sign up for voiceshare for free. A link is emailed to anyone you choose. This link allows the receiver to record a clip to be played for the baby. The website will then allow you to download the sound clip onto a device. The Belly Buds will hook up to your device and play the sound through them, just like done when head phones are hooked up to a device. Once I signed up and realized how it actually worked I decided not to utilize voiceshare. My significant other recommended that I/family/friends record a voice memo on the iPhone instead, and share through text/email. Then you can connect the belly buds up directly to the iPhone and play. I even play classical music through youtube on my iPhone.', 'asin': 'B0097F3YES', 'answerTime': '26 days ago', 'question': 'I see that you can give access to distant family members to record audio for the baby. How does the audio sync to the Bellybuds? WiFi?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0097F3YES', 'answerTime': 'Aug 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407049200, 'question': 'What is the different between the deluxe &amp; original version? Does the cheaper version have the audio splitter ?', 'answer': 'In addition to including everything that comes with the Original (Bellybuds, 2 pair of adhesives and VoiceShare access), the Deluxe includes an audio splitter, storage pouch and a music album download.'}
