{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009HPGA5I', 'answerTime': '13 days ago', 'question': 'Is one-handed steering possible with the double helix?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Only if the terrain is flat and straight. In my opinion it's tough to steer with one hand due to the weight and size of the stroller. I find it's tough with a double Bob as well, so I don't think it's the stroller, but more so the fact that you're pushing two children."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009HPGA5I', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395385200, 'question': 'Is it hard to walk behind the helix with a long stride? It looks like the handle is right above the 2nd seat.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'With one seat not at all. We have not used the second seat yet, but I can tell you that the handle extends outwards about 1 ft. With the extension we do not see it being a problem either. My wife walks with it all the time with no problems. Good luck!'}
