{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009IVKY7Q', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379919600, 'question': 'Has anyone tried the Nourish with Style refill pouches with this filling station?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have not but can give you a little insight on the product. The top piece that you push the food through actually screws onto the pouches. I don't know if it has the same screwing pattern as these pouches. If your baby goes through a lot of squeezies, it would definitely be worth a shot!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009IVKY7Q', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': 'Will this work with pudding thick purreed food? Or only with thinner liquids?', 'answer': "You squeeze the food into the same size hole that the baby eats out of. So I can't see why pudding thick wouldn't fit. I have only put homemade baby purees inside pouches."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009IVKY7Q', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424764800, 'question': "How long will i use this system for as I think we only give babies purees between 4-6months &amp; i've read you can't put lumpy mixtures in the bags?", 'answer': 'If there are any chunks it will not go in through the cylinder into the pouch. My baby is 8 months old and I still feed her purees. I mix her fruit with cereal in the morning. Even if I only use it for 4-6 months, I feel it is totally worth it for the fresh food. I plan on using it past age 1 for fruit on the go. Just like those applesauce pouches you buy.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009IVKY7Q', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420531200, 'question': "Can you pour puree into the bags while it's still hot from cooking?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I usually do! Then I just wait a little bit before I stick it in the freezer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009IVKY7Q', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361779200, 'question': 'Does it seal them? Or do you have to still keep them in the refridgerator or freezer?', 'answer': 'You have to freeze them or use them within 2 days if you refrigerate them.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009IVYNGO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422691200, 'question': 'Why are there 3 sizes? I thought all cribs were standard.', 'answer': "It's not sizes. It is just what is included. Crib 3 includes 3 items-skirt, sheet, bumper. Crib 2 only includes 2 items. Look at the feature details."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009IVYNGO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401606000, 'question': 'How deep are the sheets? Will they fit a 6 inch deep crib mattress?', 'answer': 'Yes the sheets will fit a 6 inch deep mattress. My only complaint about the set is that the sheets are not soft. I am surprised at how rough they are, especially being made for a baby. I am hoping after more washes it will soften up some.'}
