{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009S1DWOS', 'answerTime': 'Feb 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392624000, 'question': 'Is the latch system a metal snap in or is it straps?', 'answer': 'The LATCH system is the way it straps in to your car. Your car will have metal loops in the back part of the seat. The car seat has straps with a metal clip at the end. You snap the clip to the loops and then tighten the straps so it fits snuggly. I hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009S1DWOS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398409200, 'question': 'Is this too upright? i.e. If this child falls asleep, will they have the same problem with some other Dionos where their head will be slumped down?', 'answer': "It is pretty upright, but my 3 year old doesn't have a problem falling asleep in it. he just turns his head to the side and put a blanket between his shoulder and head. I will say it is more upright than say a britax or something, but those don't go up as high in weight as this."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009S1DWOS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420790400, 'question': 'How does this car seat compare to the Radian RXT? I have heard that the wings on the RXT can be problematic so I was drawn to this model.', 'answer': "The only real difference between the Radian RXT and R120 are the headwings. I actually have 2 RXT's and 2 R120's... I originally got the RXT's because that seemed the better option but like you, I've heard that the headwings can limit the full height ability of the booster mode (I have short kids but they are also skinny so it's possible this will eventually be an issue for me)...after hearing that I decided to just go with the R120's... they are a bit cheaper and if they give me a bit longer of a booster seat life, great!"}
