{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009UPUFCY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373958000, 'question': 'Would this work with a arms reach co-sleeper?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'In short, yes. This is like a "Travel" vibrator. It works best when it\'s under a mattress. It does have a handle (with on/off switch) that you can pop out from under the mattress if you happen to have a crib with slots on the side. If you don\'t then all you\'d have to do is place it far enough from the baby\'s feet, so as to not disturb her when you lift the mattress slightly to turn it on/off. I\'ve even used it with the stroller and the carseat. You just have to figure out the best place where it\'ll fit, not fall and still deliver vibrations significant enough to make your baby zzzzzzzzz. Like is said in my review, it does work as it\'s marketed, but, I\'d suggest buying a bunch of AA batteries or several rechargeable ones as this is an battery gobbler.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009UPUFCY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374735600, 'question': "Does the unit create a problematic bump in the mattress or is it not an issue? I know a few reviewers mentioned this, but I'd like to see some other opinions as well. Thank you!", 'answer': "Honestly, I don't have the unit under the mattress. I actually have it setting on the mattress in one of the corners of the crib and have the handle sticking outside the slats of the crib, so at any time I can sneak up and turn the unit on without baby knowing. Having the unit on top of the mattress creates a better vibration and the hum of the vibrator on the mattress is a plus to help baby sleep longer and better."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009UPUFCY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372057200, 'question': 'What are the measurements?', 'answer': 'The item is sort of irregularly shaped due to the soft and baby safe cover; however, from the end of the handle to the end of the circle vibrating area is 10.75" and the circle vibrating area is 7" in diameter or across. It is shaped like a 7" frying pan.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009UPUFCY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390550400, 'question': 'How long do the batteries last?', 'answer': "I'd say ours last about 3 weeks, considering it stays on for a half hour at a time and we usually put it on 2-3 times a night it's not too bad but we will probably invest in rechargeable batteries for it. It is a lifesaver though!!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009UPUFCY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413529200, 'question': 'Has anyone tried this on an older baby (around 1 year old) that wakes frequently?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I quit using around 6 months bc I got tired of replacing the batteries near daily.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009UPUFCY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410505200, 'question': 'We just bought this and use it 3-4 times per day have changed out the batteries every two days so far. Any recommendations to make it last longer?', 'answer': 'Wean your child from needing it all the time. Put him/her to bed without the paddle and allow him/her to self-soothe. Only use the paddle when crying is past a certain number of minutes and/or if crying starts after sleeping has started. Also, it helps to turn off the paddle after your baby has fallen asleep. For us, we only use the paddle when our baby wakes in the middle of the night. We change out batteries about every 5 weeks.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009UPUFCY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410246000, 'question': 'Will this somehow work on a pack and play?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': '.only if your use it the way I do, under neath the sheet by the feet. Or inside a pillow case w the pillow. I\'m thinking the pack n play is a thin plywood on the bottom , so it might make a rattling noise.also you can try to do some research on camomile tea and cat nip. If it\'s that your child or baby over 6 month is having issues staying asleep or teething. Both works great with my 7 month old twins.walmart has a tea by traditional medicinal called "nighty night" (purple box) My daughter hasn\'t been crabby or whiny due to her teething'}
