{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009VARM42', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427612400, 'question': 'Can this jog on sidewalks and work from infant to toddler? Is there a need for a bulky jogger/travel system (like Graco) too? I only want 1 stroller.', 'answer': "I've jogged with it but it's not designed as a 'real' jogging stroller. We do have a jogging stroller and the regular graco stroller that we got as a travel system w the car seat snd I'll tell you that both of those are in the basement except this mini. We love it. It's lightweight and so easy to operate. We took it to Mexico when our little one turned 1. We didn't have to check it in, again, because it's so light it's considered a lightweight stroller but it's also sturdy and much better quality that most 'umbrella' strollers. We love it and we have no complaints. Oh and it is very much easy to transition from infant to toddler."}
