{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009X4C796', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394352000, 'question': 'Is there a stroller that I can lock the car seat into?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No, this seat is bulky and heavy. It is meant to stay in the car. You are thinking of an infant car seat (like the chicco keyfit 30). The infant seat is useful for the baby\'s first 6-12 months or so (because you can snap it in and out of the car and into a stroller). After the infant is around 6-12 months, you\'ll switch to a convertible car seat like this one. If you don\'t want to buy two separate seats, you can skip the infant seat (this convertible seat accommodates infants and toddlers--but you need to buy the version with "tiny fit"--it\'s a separate Amazon listing and cost about fifty dollars more) but you lose the option of toting the baby around in his seat. Good luck!'}
