{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009X4C796', 'answerTime': '22 days ago', 'question': 'can i ues the isofix connected this maxi cosi pria 70', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Hello Nelson! Thanks for your interest in the Pria70! The LATCH feature that connects car seats to vehicles with ISOfix works in the same way that the ISOfix feature would. The only difference is that the actual connectors for car seats with the ISOfix feature are rigid, meaning you don't have to tighten any belt. There are some US vehicles that label their Lower Anchor positions as ISOfix (Toyota Solara is one of them) and in instances such as this, you will always just need to check the vehicle manual. That is where you will be able to determine whether or not the vehicle is compatible with LATCH and whether they allow a LATCH installation with ISOfix. If you cannot tell, you can always call your local dealership to get clarification. If you are not located in the US, this car seat will not be designed/approved for use outside of that region so you while the seat may be compatible with other model vehicles and ISOfix, we have to strongly suggest that the car seat must comply with local standards and regulations. This car seat, if purchased on the US Amazon site will not comply with European, Canadian, or Australian regulations/standards. If you should have any further questions, we are more than happy to help you any way we can. We can be reached at 1-800-951-4113 or consumer@maxicosi-us.com."}
