{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A0FGPFO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381647600, 'question': "I don't understand the 4 (2x) directions. Can't I just fill it to 8. Perhaps I fill it to 4 and heat it two times.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Fill to the 4 twice. The measurements are not incremental so it is not the same as filling to the 8. I tested this by pouring the amounts into tubes and found out that at the 4 it is 6mL (2x would be 12 mL then) and the 8 is 10 mL.'}
