{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A0H1BEC', 'answerTime': 'May 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400655600, 'question': 'Is it worth the extra money over the standard Travelmate?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "To my understanding, the standart travelmate only has 2 wheels vs the deluxe has 4 wheels. For me, I like the stability of the 4 wheels and I wanted something to make it easier on myself since I was traveling alone with my baby girl. My daughter's Chicco Nextfit was pretty heavy and I wheeled her around while strapped in so I liked that it was safe for her and that I could easily handle it with luggage. Plus, it had brakes which I found useful numerous times. I also liked the deluxe b/c the car seat never once touched the ground which was important to me since I like to keep my vehicles clean."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A0H1BEC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394780400, 'question': 'Has anyone ever used this with a Diono Radian?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes.....I've used it with the Diono Radian. We traveled overseas this past winter. It was very helpful.....everyone loved it. Closing it was easy. The only challenge I would say is that it took time and patience to set up the car seat with the straps. Not bc it was a diono, just making sure straps were in the correct place. It fit well, my son who was 18 months at the time is very tall but still had proper leg space."}
