{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A0H1BEC', 'answerTime': 'Aug 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408950000, 'question': 'Has anyone used this with the Britax Boulevard 70?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I have - it worked great! Traveling through the airport was SO much easier than the last time I traveled, without the Go-Go Babyz Travelmate Deluxe. Be prepared for a handcheck at security, as the car seat and carrier won't fit through the x-ray machines (the car seat doesn't fit through on its own either, even without the carrier). You'll have to detach the car seat from the carrier when you're boarding the plane, because they won't fit down the aisle. I used the car seat on the airplane, and tucked the carrier under the seat while flying. When traveling through the airport, it works just like a stroller. I buckled in my 3-year-old and off we went! He enjoyed riding in it as much as I enjoyed the stress-free travel. I highly recommend it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A0H1BEC', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407308400, 'question': 'Do I need to order an adapter to fit my Chicco Key Fit? On the go go baby website it reads that I do but it can only be purchased directly from them.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I guess you can attach your Chicco Key Fit on the Travelmate using the default straps provided. The adapter makes it easier to attach the Chicco to the Travelmate (just clips the Chicco on the Travelmate and go) instead of having to deal with the straps. I have a Recarro car seat for which no adapter exists and using the straps is really easy with it, fyi. If I were you, I'd try the Travelmate without the adapter and if you feel like it's too much of an hassle to use the straps, try the adapter. Hope this helps."}
