{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A0ID90A', 'answerTime': 'Jan 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422000000, 'question': 'How does this seat compare to the baby born, as far as stability, seat height/width, back rest height and ease of use?', 'answer': 'I have both the Baby Bjorn and this one. The Baby bjorn is made of sturdier plastic and has more of the base touching the floor. It\'s a little more narrow than the Summer but the back is slightly taller. The Summer potty seat seems plenty stable and is wider across the "seat" (the part their tush would be sitting on). My daughter is really tall and big for her age (37 lbs, 42" tall, size of an average 4-5 year old). I would say she fits on the Summer seat better and her knees are at a right angle when she\'s sitting. On the Baby Bjorn, we had to put something under the potty seat to raise it up because her feet were falling asleep. I bought the Summer as a back-up seat but it\'s just as good and much cheaper!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A0ID90A', 'answerTime': 'Sep 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378191600, 'question': 'Are there any issues with discoloration of white color overtime?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'If you soak it in bleach ever couple weeks, discoloration comes off.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A0ID90A', 'answerTime': 'Aug 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377759600, 'question': 'Does the whole section where I see the line in the picture come out for disposing into toilet? Is it easy to dump without making mess?', 'answer': "Yup the whole sections pops out and my clumsy 20 month old cna take it empty it in the potty and put it back after momma washes it :). Liquids pour out super easy from the back if that makes sense. Solids yo ukinda have to shake em out a bit if they are stuck to the bottom but they find their way out! I usually wipe with a baby wipe then rinse in the bath tup with a spritz of soap for solids or just quick water rinse for pee. There is a sort of built in channel so you can empty from the back of the potty (once that section is pulled out) , it's hard to explain but when you come to empty it it makes sense! I've bought 2 of these and while light weight they are still pretty sturdy and haven't been damaged here yet. The white one gets a little dusty sometimes but a wipe wipes it off well. and my son doen't usually pee out, the pee guard seems decently high but he can get on/ off easy. We've bought 2 (they were on sale under 10$) to have one in the car for traveling and one in the house."}
