{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A0ID6YO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389168000, 'question': 'What is the range? How far can the camera be from the monitor and still get a quality picture?', 'answer': "It's actually a pretty decent image for a basic video monitor. We have it on the opposite end of the house and it works perfectly--have also had it in the basement with a clear image (it is black and white though). Depending on how our baby is laying, I can see her breathing and you can easily tell when their eyes are open."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A0ID6YO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411714800, 'question': 'what kind of warranty does it have ?', 'answer': 'I don\'t recall without looking for the paperwork. My original monitor like this from when my son was an infant with seizures (12 yrs ago) was much better than the newer ones. The one I bought last year, I had to have replaced 2 times (within the first 3 wks) because of issues with it. A buzzing coming from the adapter plug and no picture after only using it 12 hrs. Just a flat line across the screen. The 2nd one - the volume wasn\'t loud enough and the picture wasn\'t clear at all. Plus there\'s no handle like the old one to easily carry it from room to room. There\'s no on/off dial like the last one that also controlled volume. The first one you could easily dial the volume and/or turn it right off. With this new one, you have to hold a button in until all the lights light up to turn it on. The volume is a different button to push. Also, when you unplug it and move it to a different room - the old one would turn on as soon as you plugged it back in. This one you have to push the button and wait for the lights to all light up. Oddly, when you wait for the lights to light up. To turn on - they have to change to red. When turning off - green. Common sense you would think to turn it "on" to make it "go" the lights would turn "green". Which means should be "red" for "stop" and "off". Just a few quirky things that bother me about the newer model. Sometimes if something works well, don\'t tweak it, right?'}
