{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUH72', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395558000, 'question': 'What is the difference between the boulevard and marathon from britax', 'answer': 'The Boulevard had a set of "head wings" which are simply a thick second layer of EPS foam layer of designed to provide additional protection to head in the event of a collision. They are specifically designed to provide the extra protection in the event of a side impact collision. SIC account for less than % of all collisions but they account for more fatalities than frontal, frontal offset & rear impact collisions. When the shoulder harness hight is adjusted, the head wings automatically adjust to correspond in height so that the head wings are always centered around the child\'s head. The headwings are the only difference between the Boulevard & the Marathon. They have an identical shell and are identical in all other respects. We were fortunate in that we were never involved in a collision. But the head wings on the Boulevard are nice when a child is napping. On the other hand, if your child wants to be looking out the window the head wings could potentially obstruct their view. Neither of my children ever complained about the head wings though.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUH72', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390377600, 'question': 'Does this carseat come with the base as well or do you need to purchase that separately?', 'answer': "It's all one piece."}
