{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUGXC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379142000, 'question': 'Does anyone use this for an older child? I read that the short height of the seat might limit its longevity as the child gets taller.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It depends. If it is rear facing the shoulder height is between 9-16" and up to 40 lbs. If it is forward facing then the shoulder height should be between 12-16" and up to 70 lbs. So older than 2 is when you can turn the child around to a forward position, however this car seat works best in a mini van or SUV so the child can stretch his/her legs out. But you can adjust the head rest on the car seat and the backseat of the vehicle to allow for the extra height. If your child is too tall for this particular seat, you might want to go up to a booster seat. They do make a booster seat with a harness that is for taller children. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUGXC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378796400, 'question': 'Can you fit 2 of these seats in the back of an SUV?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I only have one in the center but yes I would definitely think you could fit two, especially in an SUV.'}
