{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUGYQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387180800, 'question': 'Has anyone installed this in a smaller auto? I have a 4 door jeep wrangler so am a bit limited on space in the back seat.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'My husband works for Enterprise Rent-a-Car and we have installed this in everything from a compact car to a suburban. In a jeep wrangler, I-the one sitting in front of the car seat-had plenty of room with my son rear-facing. You should be able to go to babies r us and try one out even if you buy from amazon :)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUGYQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380610800, 'question': 'Has anyone used this car seat for a new born, 6 lbs or so in weight? Thank you!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have never used this particular car seat for a 6lb baby because the starting weight is 5lbs. We used the Chaperone for our new born. This Advocate would be a pain with a new born baby due to the seat is not designed to be taken out of the car like the Chaperone. This seat is designed to be used with the next level up from a new born. I would not recommend this seat for a 6lb. baby. You will end up buying another carrier if you do. The Chaperone has multiple purposes, a car seat, or it can be put in the stroller to be used as a stroller seat.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUGYQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382079600, 'question': "Is it normal for cracking to appear on the HUGS chest pad? I've only had mine a couple of months, but there are already 3 small cracks on the rubber!", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Don't know if it is normal. Ours cracked during a cleaning. We e-mailed Britax and asked for the hugs pads that they put on the 2nd generation. They are not as padded but made of a tougher rubber. They never e-mailed me back but they sent them free of charge right away. We had them in about a week. Make sure you provide them all of the serial/model info from the seat."}
