{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDPS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373266800, 'question': 'I just bought this car seat, I plan to use it rear facing in a 2012 Honda CRV. Is the top tether easy to use rear facing?, I find the instructions a bit confusing, I have not started to install yet, just reading the manual first. Any comments?', 'answer': "I haven't used the top tether rear-facing basically because the anchor is behind the seat, meaning the tether would end up over the seat itself making it hard to put the child into the seat. If the anchor is on the floor than that would make it easier to use but I don't think your car has that."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDPS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409554800, 'question': 'When do you usually remove infant body pillow?', 'answer': 'We removed ours when my grandson turned 14 months old. Probably left it in there longer than necessary but just kept it for comfort.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDPS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395558000, 'question': 'What is the difference between the boulevard and marathon from britax', 'answer': 'The Boulevard had a set of "head wings" which are simply a thick second layer of EPS foam layer of designed to provide additional protection to head in the event of a collision. They are specifically designed to provide the extra protection in the event of a side impact collision. SIC account for less than % of all collisions but they account for more fatalities than frontal, frontal offset & rear impact collisions. When the shoulder harness hight is adjusted, the head wings automatically adjust to correspond in height so that the head wings are always centered around the child\'s head. The headwings are the only difference between the Boulevard & the Marathon. They have an identical shell and are identical in all other respects. We were fortunate in that we were never involved in a collision. But the head wings on the Boulevard are nice when a child is napping. On the other hand, if your child wants to be looking out the window the head wings could potentially obstruct their view. Neither of my children ever complained about the head wings though.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDPS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390377600, 'question': 'Does this carseat come with the base as well or do you need to purchase that separately?', 'answer': "It's all one piece."}
