{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUFBA', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412665200, 'question': 'what is the different 70-G3 and G4?', 'answer': 'Hi, they have updated the carseat. First, the G4 seats include an infant positioning pillow which must be used up to 22 pounds and then removed while in the 3G you removed it once the child could sit unsupported. Second, the harness covers where redesigned and third, they removed the "70" out of the name due to less weight capacity. It now supports 65pounds while the 3G 70... Hope this helps. Whether you decide to buy the 3G or the 4G you won\'t regret it. Britax, of what I researched is one of the best carseats. I am very pleased with my purchase and for my second child I will not hesitate on buying Pavilion once again. Good Luck...'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUFBA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418025600, 'question': 'Is this seat easy to install? We are traveling abroad and want to bring a car seat with us. Will be using in taxis, so quick installation is a must.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No, this takes a bit of time. It took my husband and I about 15 minutes together to install it. If you are very familiar with it and practice a lot, maybe it could be quicker.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUFBA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408345200, 'question': "What is the material like in this car seat? Does it seem like it would breathe ok,looking for something that wouldn't make him hot or sweaty.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The insert and head support is a soft material with a texture like felt or velour. The material of the seat is a little stiffer. It is an extremely comfortable seat, our son loves it and he is a very hot baby and it has never made him sweaty. The material wipes up well also for spot cleaning. Hope this helps :)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUFBA', 'answerTime': 'Jul 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406617200, 'question': 'If we need you send it from USA to China, how much the shipping cost?', 'answer': "Good morning Unfortunately Bambi Bambi doesn't do international shipping. We can ship it to any Freight Forwarder that you pick that can do the international transportation for you but that would be under your own cost."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUFBA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396076400, 'question': 'Is this good for use inside the air craft ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It is certified for aircraft use - I have not taken mine on the airplane. The carseat is large and difficult to carry thru an airport, I am also not sure if it will fit in the airplane seat well - so I chose to check the carseat and take my baby as a lap child. It is a FABULOUS carseat for everything else though - we love both of ours!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUFBA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389254400, 'question': 'Some car seats have a max height, I was wondering if this car seat did as well?', 'answer': 'According to the Britax website, the safe maximum height is 49". The seated shoulder height for rear-facing is 9" - 16.75" and for forward-facing is 12" - 16.75". This information was obtained from http://www.britaxusa.com/car-seats/pavilion.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUFBA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389254400, 'question': "What's the package size and I want to take it ti out of USA by airplain?", 'answer': "It comes in an appropriate size box, I didn't measure it.. We've traveled several times with this carseat with no issues. You can buy a bag for convertible car seats on Amazon as well which makes it even easier. They check it at security (TSA) and we've never had an issue. We love this seat"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUFBA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387612800, 'question': 'can use this for new born baby?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It's rated as low as 5 lbs., but the seat does disconnect from the base; therefore, it cannot act as a carrier."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDOY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382425200, 'question': 'How many recline positions does it have in rear facing? and also, can it be reclined when baby is already in seat?', 'answer': "There are 2 reclining positions. The recommended position depends on the seat it sits on. I think it's a 45 or 35degree angle. No it can't be reclined when the baby is in the seat. It has to be set when the carseat is installed. I purchased this carseat for my 8month old. I would purchase this seat again. Britax is better quality and has more metal protection than any other carseats I have found."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDOY', 'answerTime': 'Sep 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380178800, 'question': "Do the foam panels for the side impact protection block a child's side view? They seem bulky.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'They are bulky. My daughter tries to lean forward and look around them at her sister from time to time. Generally she is happy to sit back and look out the window or talk to her reflection in the mirror.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDOY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370156400, 'question': "Has anyone used the Britax Pavilion 70-G3 for a newborn? I don't see a carry bar like the infant carries so I'm interested to know how you carried the car seat from the car to your house, grocery store etc. Thank you in advance.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I didn't get it for my daughter until she was over a year old, but you don't carry these around. You take the baby out of this and carry him/her (or wear in a sling, etc) instead of carrying the baby in the car seat."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDOY', 'answerTime': 'Oct 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381820400, 'question': 'LATCH system?', 'answer': 'Yes. you can use both the latch system and/or seatbelt to secure the seat...the latch system is actually super easy to use for both rear facing and forward facing positions....look up on Youtube for their instruction videos using latch system instead of reading the manual ...'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDOY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362470400, 'question': 'Will this car seat fit in a VW Beetle 2012?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I wouldn't bet on it. Sorry I grabbed an 2013 Acura ILX from work the other day and had to pull the seat up to get it in there. The car seat is a monster - not saying the ILX is big but guessing a larger back seat than a Bug. Agree with everyone below saying stop by a major chain and give it a shot. If it does fit I found getting the little one in there a bit of a challenge without occasionally and *softly bumping them into the door molding and roof. I was interested in getting an ILX till I realized it just doesn't work if you have a baby. *** EDIT **** My seat was installed rear facing - forward facing would be been much more doable. PS the seat is AWESOME! Don't listen to any of the reviews saying the straps at too small. They just didn't spend 30seconds studying how they work to release more slack."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDOY', 'answerTime': 'Aug 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376290800, 'question': 'airplane', 'answer': "Yes it's airplane approved has the sticker for it"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A2HUDOY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372143600, 'question': 'I feel like I must be doing something wrong. My 8 month old twins cry every time I put them in/take them out. I have to dig the straps from behind their backs and pull them over their shoulders each time. Should I be loosening the straps each they get...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The straps seem too short on this seat to get infants in and out easily. I have heard other reviewers mention that you can call Britax and get longer straps, which I have been meaning to do, because it is a pain to dig them out from behind my daughter.'}
