{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A3XNUQA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409036400, 'question': 'Do I need to buy a container for defrosting and heating up baby food? If so, which one?', 'answer': "If you make the food and then freeze it, yes, you will need a separate container. This only has a pitcher that you can steam and directly blend in same unit. I use an ice cube tray to freeze, then put it in a Ziploc bag with the date once it's frozen. When I thaw the food, I put it in a plastic container in the fridge each day. I just use a small Tupperware container. This BEABA is really nice and easy to use and clean!"}
