{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A47J6YU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': 'Is high chair counter height - 25" tall and is there a weight limit listed?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't know what the exact specs are, but we feed my son in the chair while we sit at the dinner table. It is a little bit low, but not bad. Also, my son weighs 30 lbs. now and there are no problems with him and the chair. I don't have what the exact specs are but maybe that is of help to you."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A47J6YU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402642800, 'question': 'my only concern is tipping...thoughts on the sturdiness of the product? My daughter is 8 months and hyper so I dont know if it could tip over?', 'answer': "My almost two year old has been using this chair for almost a year. She and her cousin who is three weeks younger than her like to (try) to rock back and forth in them, just slamming their heads back really which can cause the chair to scoot back. For whatever reason this has become a fun game for them that they egg each other on with but neither one of them have ever tipped over. If they get too carried away I simply put my foot down inbetween one of the legs as an extra anchor. Just like with any highchair adult supervision is required but I'd be more concerned with them climbing out of it (someone might forget to buckle the waste belt ;-) ) than tipping it over. It's really been one of the greatest baby product investments we have made!"}
