{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A5AWV48', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407913200, 'question': 'What is the universal accessory mounting bracket mentioned in the description? Where is it located on the stroller?', 'answer': 'It is a part of the stroller where you can easily attach accessories like the car seat adaptor or the child tray. Accessories are sold separately and they can be easily mounted with a simple click into the mounting bracket.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': 'Jun 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371970800, 'question': 'I am interested in purchasing this jogging stroller and have a Chicco KeyFit carseat. It does appear to be compatible but I have read on the adapter that the "new range" strollers that have the zip-away fabric are not compatible with the universal...', 'answer': "I'm not sure. I did not have that specific carseat. I didn't use the Terrain with a carseat actually, but I know that there are moms that have used the adapter. Can you call customer support and ask Mountain Buggy directly before your order."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389081600, 'question': 'Why is it stated Max weight rec: 77 Pounds when on their official website is: Maximum load 25kg / 55lb', 'answer': 'I actually had the same question and called Mountain Buggy. They told me it was because the previous testing on the pre-2013 models was done at 77lbs where new testing is only done at 55lbs so that is where it is safety tested at. But they did say that the seat would hold up to 77lbs without a problem, but due to they change in safety tests it can only be listed at 55lbs. You may want to call just to make sure nothing has changed. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385625600, 'question': "What's the difference between the 2013 version and prior version? Thanks.", 'answer': 'I asked Mountain Buggy, this is what they wrote back- "Thanks for reaching out to us concerning our Terrain model buggy. Below is a list of upgraded features, outside of these everything will remain the same. - zip off fabric - tail free safety harness - swivel bumper bar - automatic frame lock"'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392883200, 'question': 'Is this stroller suitable for infants the way it is? or do I need to use the car seat/carrycot', 'answer': 'We bought this stroller because it is suitable for newborns from day 1. The stroller bed reclines to 180 degrees so your baby can lay flat. You should not jog with your baby until he or she has adequate neck support; roughly 6 months old.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': '20 days ago', 'question': 'Do you sell the carrycot compatible with the Terrain stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We had to buy that separate. Also, if you can buy a car seat and car seat attachment separate as well.'}
{'answer': '2014 the newest model. Thanks!', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': '21 days ago', 'question': "Which year's model is this stroller?", 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403766000, 'question': 'Can the folded stroller fit into the trunk of a regular compact car? I have a Toyota Corolla.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have a Lexus and it fits fine. Another one of my clients has a Prius and it fits too. I'm not positive though, because I don't know how big your trunk is. I'd say it would most likely fit."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': 'Jun 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403506800, 'question': 'Has anyone ever taken this to the beach and pushed it ON (in?) the sand?? Curious how well i works in sand. Thanks.', 'answer': "It will work as well as a bike through sand... so you can imagine it being a pain...we've never done it and probably won't, but if we did, you would probably need to let some air out of the tires for better traction."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396162800, 'question': 'does the front wheel have any wobble/shake when running (running, not jogging)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I've never experienced wheel shake when running, with wheel unlocked or locked. Very well made stroller, we love it!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A61DCBM', 'answerTime': 'Mar 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395990000, 'question': 'Has anyone used this with an infant car seat? What car seat did you use?', 'answer': 'Yes...Peg perego sip 30/30. It works great with the car seat adaptor and very easy to use.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382425200, 'question': 'Do you attach the hose to a sink or a shower?', 'answer': 'It actually attaches to the water line on your toilet. The packaging has the instructions. Our toilet has a flexi hose so it was easy to add the sprayer in line.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396335600, 'question': 'How long is the sprayer hose line?', 'answer': '4 feet long'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396335600, 'question': "does it leak like the reviews i've read on the other brands?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have no idea why other reviewers said it leaked. It will have some water that remains in the hose even after you turn it "off," but my solution to that is to hold the spray handle down until the water stops before hanging it back up. I\'ve not had any problems with mine and I use mine constantly :-).'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': 'Feb 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423209600, 'question': 'Do you have to turn the water supply off after using every tiem?( some of the manufacturers recommend this)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't know that you have to, but we generally try to. Otherwise, the trigger might get inadvertently pressed and you're going to have water all over your bathroom."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': 'Aug 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409209200, 'question': 'Does this have various pressure settings like the BumGenius sprayer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'the product says "allows for adjustable water flow Spray wand with adjustable lever" Is this wrong?'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'Has anyone else had problems with the toilet tank filling up extremely slowly and very low sprayer pressure after you install this?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No I have not. Make sure your main water valve is open wide enough. You had to close it completely during the install.'}
{'answer': "I think it would be too strong! Much stronger than that in a kitchen sink! Use a spray bottle if you'd like to use water.", 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': '3 days ago', 'question': "I don't use cloth diapers, but can you use this to clean baby's butt? or is it too strong?", 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
