{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420531200, 'question': 'after attaching the hose to my toilet, I cannot get my toilet water to stop running. Is there a way to stop this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Is the toilet leaking? I needed plumbers tape to make it a water tight fit on my toilet. The water does not constantly run.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A65YN8E', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416124800, 'question': "My hi-rise apt bldg has commercial-like toilets (without tank + std. residential plumbing) - how do I connect? Can I connect to sink H2O just 2' away?", 'answer': 'From my husband: If your sink line is easily accessible, you should be able to install it to the wall pipe and attach the flexible hose from the sink to the top. The on/off switch for the sprayer will be on the line attached to the wall, so if it is in a cabinet or vanity it may be difficult to get to each time. The bumkins website has instructions on how to install to the toilet. It would be the same, just to the sink line instead. Hope this helps!'}
