{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A67C564', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393488000, 'question': 'Is this Happenstance the newest version of the Onside Air Convertible car seat? Looking for one recently manufactured, not already 2 yrs old. Thx.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I just looked on the Safety 1st website and this looks like it is a current model. The actual seller would be the one to contact about when it was manufactured, however. If you are worried you can always buy directly from Safety 1st. It is currently listed there for a few dollars more (probably plus shipping costs, as well). Or you could find a store to buy from.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A67C564', 'answerTime': 'Jul 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406185200, 'question': 'Hi, can you use this product on the plane? Is it FAA approved?', 'answer': "We ONLY use this carseat for air travel. It is FAA approved for forward facing, narrow enough to fit with the armrests down, and lightweight for carrying through the airport. There is a carseat backpack available which it fits into nicely. It is very easy to install in an airplane seat. BUT, it is a major pain-in-the-neck to install in the car once you get to your destination. It doesn't seem as stable in a car as some of the more expensive brands, and you can't adjust straps with your kid in it. For that reason, it pretty much collects dust for us when we're not traveling."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A67C564', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': 'I need to install this rear facing in a 2012 Kia Sorento. How hard will it be to install in its bucket seats?', 'answer': 'I have a 2006 Pontiac Torrent with a decent slope not much of a bucket but the only struggle I had was to ensure the rear facing strap was taught - but once we got that taken care of it was fine. Took all of 20min - approx 10min of that was trying to get a good place for the rear facing strap. My mom has a 2008 Toyota Avalon which has bucket seats and I find that the same seat fits well :o)'}
