{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A6XKNAS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395471600, 'question': 'Hello to all the mommies out there. I want to buy the Beaba but was wondering if the two mixers is needed? Also if it mixes good.? Thx', 'answer': "I have the Pro2X and have owned it for about 4 months. I really like having the two canisters, since I tend to make food and then freeze it. I like being able to steam two foods at once. Makes the whole process go that much faster. One thing, you can't blend/mix on both sides, just on one, so you steam the food then blend one after another on the primary side. The blending works well. I have been able to get the smooth consistency needed for babyfood, so no complaints there. My opinion is if you want/need to save time, the second cansiter in the Pro2X is definitely worth the money. I estimate it saves you 20 minutes of overall time per two foods you are planning to cook, since you are steaming both foods at once. If you don't care as much about saving the time then it's not as worth it. BTW - my opinion is the larger canister in the PRO is definitely worth it over the std so you can make food and then freeze the rest and don't have to be making food all the time."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A6XKNAS', 'answerTime': 'Nov 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383375600, 'question': 'Has anyone had issue with the steamer producing brown burnt smelling water? I saw some people with the single unit had the problem. Review to follow.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Nope. Unit still working beautifully :).'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A6XKNAS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405580400, 'question': 'Has anyone noticed how dirty the water reservoir gets after using it? I was curious and checked with a flash-light after 1 month of use (it is so hidden that it was hard to do..) There was dark brown stuff all-over the walls of the water reservoir! I...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I am considering the Beaba, but what you've written sounds like there may be mold in the reservoir. Ugh."}
