{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A74ERVC', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': "Has anyone tried this and the keekaroo version? I'm torn between the two, not sure which is better. Thanks!", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't know the Keekaroo version, but had the Boon station and sent it back right away. The pad had a nasty chemical smell and was not soft at all. I like the idea of the Boon changing station, but after baby arrived, I really don't see how I would have used it for long (baby would have outgrown it within about 4-5 months and has become way too mobile for something like this)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00A74ERVC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395558000, 'question': 'Are the sides high enough to keep the baby from rolling?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, and you don't want them to be. Safety comes from having your hand on the baby at all times when you are changing. There is a single, connected strap for securing the device to a changing table. This is the best purchase I have made, why? Babies pee a lot on the changing table and you don't need a load of laundry each time that happens. You want to wipe and go."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A77OKNE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427698800, 'question': 'How long does bassinet feature work? Until what weight or height?', 'answer': "I'm not sure, I'd have to look up my stroller instructions, but my baby is 4 months old and weighs about 16-17lbs (I think or more) and he still uses the bassinet. His feet aren't too close to the edge. Even if I lift the bassinet to stroller position now his feet dont get cramned too much at the end. I like this because if it is windy or raining it doesn't get him all wet. The hood of the stroller would be nicer if it was a little bigger or had a middle position. There isn't any shocksystem, but it's a stroller and I'm not jogging or going over bumpy terrain with it. I love the stroller. But I can't see some people not."}
