{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00A7DATQ0', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403679600, 'question': 'I have the city mini GT. I see this product says "uses mounting bracket".Do I need to use the mounting bracket? or can I just snap this adapter and go', 'answer': "The mounting bracket it refers to is one of the two spaces you can plug in stuff on each side. The top set is typically used by the sun shade. The bottom set is for a belly bar or tray, but when the baby is young and not sitting directly in the stroller yet, it can be used by this set of car seat adapters, no extra pieces needed. Once you plug these in to each side of the stroller, you can just snap the Britax car seat right in. It's nicer than some of the other infant car seat adapters out there that use a metal bar across the seat of the stroller because it doesn't get in the way when you try to fold and store the stroller!"}
