{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AC5S5XW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401778800, 'question': "I have a best view choice color monitor.When you plug in the new camera, does the monitor just pick it up? I've never seen a feature for a 2nd camera?", 'answer': 'Yes it does. Make sure camera and monitor are powered on. Tap the monitor power button (top left button) once and a new screen will come up. When that screen comes up you will see a camera at the bottom. Using the arrow buttons and arrow once to the right to highlight the camera. More options then come up. Arrow up to the plus sign to add the new camera. Once it is added if you select the # sign you can specify the room you want the monitor to view. If you select the rotating cameras the monitor will scan all the cameras you have added. It will do so every 8 seconds. The screen will say scan on the too right corner of the screen when you are in scan mode. Hope this helps! You will love this feature.'}
