{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AFV5E1O', 'answerTime': 'Dec 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387872000, 'question': "How can you make sure you don't get a girls blanket when you have a boy? I did not see any option to specify during the process of checking out.", 'answer': 'This seems to be a generic barcode and generic listing. As a seller of this blanket, I sell the boys blue blanket. If you are looking for one of the others try to find the name and search specifically for that one. Try searching for "little taggies polka dots," "little taggies confetti," etc.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AGJFNCA', 'answerTime': 'Oct 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381561200, 'question': "Our Murano's rearview mirror has the garage door opener button attached to the bottom. Will that still be accessible with this product?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It would depend on where the button is on your mirror. If the button is on the face of your mirror, then no. It will be covered by the new mirror. If is across the top, back or bottom, it would depend on the location. There are two, i'll call them little arms, on the top and bottom each that hook over your existing mirror that could potentially cover the button. You could attach the Pikibu slightly to one side or the other to go around this issue. Depending on the size of your existing mirror, you may not be able to SEE the button, you may have to feel for it until muscle memory just automatically goes to the button. I wouldn't think that would be a huge deal since half the time pushing buttons like that is done without looking anyway."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AGJFNCA', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385193600, 'question': 'Does this cover your actual rearview mirror? That seems unsafe to block a mirror you need for driving (even if you do have side mirrors)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It clips on over your existing mirror but it doesn't prevent you from seeing behind you. it actually gives a great view of the kids while still letting you see traffic at the same time. Things behind the vehicle do seem slightly smaller because of the way the mirror is made. I found this to be a good trade off so I can see my little one without having to compromise on checking traffic."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AGJFNCA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395385200, 'question': "Is this mirror made of glass like your mirror already on your car? Or is it plastic. Mainly I'm asking is it very clear or a little distorted?", 'answer': 'Glass. Quality is great. I bought other 2 mirrors that I returned due to the distorsion. Only thing it gets a little used as image is smaller to be able to see the full back. As per my review takes only 1 day to get used to.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AGJFNCA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'How does this work for seeing kids in rear-facing carseats? Particularly those behind the driver?', 'answer': "I didn't have it yet when my son was rear facing and he was on the passenger side but this would allow you to see him/her as long as you have a mirror also on the rear seat. That's the only way you can see the little one but with a standard rearview mirror you can't see behind the driver's seat. With this mirror, the way it is curved, you should be able to. I would recommend getting (if you done already have one) a rear mirror that can tilt and adjust do you can make the angles just right. Good luck!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AGJFNCA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386144000, 'question': "Can I see children in seats other than directly behind the diver's seat, like on the passenger side?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, I bought to be able to see my two children in the back and I can. It takes a bit (about a day) to get used to the view while driving but then it is great.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AGJFNCA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': 'How does this work for night driving? Usually I can use a lever to tilt the mirror to dim the headlights behind me.', 'answer': "I find that it's not really an issue. Since the mirror is convex, it makes everything a lot smaller, including the high-beams of the jerk behind you. So it's not as bright and annoying."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AGJFNCA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427180400, 'question': "When installed, the mirror weighs down the rear view mirror so it won't stay in place. Anyone experience this issue and have a fix?", 'answer': 'Never. Mine works perfectly. I bought it 2 months ago. I would check the rear mirror and make sure there is no a loose screw or something before installing the Pikibu-baby car mirror.'}
