{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AHPZY6S', 'answerTime': 'Jun 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371970800, 'question': 'can someone please tell me how much it actually weight? It says 15 lbs on the description, but some video review I saw said it was about 20 lbs. Thx', 'answer': 'I am not sure on the exact weight, but I would say it was closer to the 15 lbs. from personal experience with it. I am a petite woman and I have no problems with the weight of this stroller. I hope this helps :)'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHPZY6S', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368428400, 'question': 'Reviews on the regular Liteway complain about the crotch buckle being tight and not adjustable. Is it the same on this model?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The crotch strap on the harness is not adjustable. I didn't find it to be tight on my 18 month old, but I could see it being a potential problem as she gets bigger."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHQ021Y', 'answerTime': 'May 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401174000, 'question': "Is there any settings that allows to view baby's face (baby facing rear) while I push stroller forward?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Baby can be rear-facing if placed in a compatible car seat. We used the Chicco Nextfit carseat and it clicks to lock into place inside this stroller, facing the adult who is pushing the stroller. You just have to expose two little holes by moving some of the padding in the stroller and you're all set to place the carseat in it. I love that no additional equipment was needed. Now that he sits up well, we don't use the carseat anymore and he just sits in the stroller like normal."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AHQ021Y', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393920000, 'question': 'how many positions does the seat recline before flat? Are there just 2 positions (upright and flat)?', 'answer': 'You pull a lever and place it where you want.'}
