{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AHVR7ZI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395212400, 'question': 'Can anyone inform me how thick the padding is? Also, is it considered three-pint harness? Thank you.', 'answer': "The padding does not seem very thick on the seat bottom and seat back but my 4 year old finds it very comfortable and falls asleep in it. This is NOT a 3 point harness as it does not have it's own harness. The seat belt in your car is used to secure the child. The latch system simply attaches the booster to your car's seat and keeps it from sliding or shifting out of place."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHVR7ZI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': "Is the seat still functional without using the latch system? We have a vehicle that doesn't have the required hooks for the latch.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it is. It is just as functional as a regular high booster seat. But the extra money on it is for the latch system. I would save the money and just buy one that does not have the latch system.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHVR94W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378105200, 'question': 'do you have to use the latch system with this booster?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You don't have to use the latch, it's just convenient for keeping it in place and not having to buckle the seat belt into it every time it's not occupied by a child. It's a nice booster with convenient cup holders. The only feature I would've liked is arm rests that fold up and down to make buckling more convenient."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHVR94W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'does this seat include a belt positioner?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes it does have a strap that hooks to the rear of the seat and the connects to the cars seatbelt and can be used to hold the seatbelt in the position you want'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHVR94W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359360000, 'question': 'Can you use the Affix in a car that does not have LATCH?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You can but you're better off saving money and getting a booster w/o latch. Graco makes the turbobooster which is very safe, veyr comfortable, and a great seat for almost half this price. Nearly the same seat (plus still has pull out cupholders etc) but w/o latch. I find the latch preferable but if you have a vehicle that doesn't use it and don't plan on upgrading any time soon you're better off saving the money."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHVR94W', 'answerTime': 'Dec 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388131200, 'question': 'I have a small coupe, does it fit ok on those seats?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I can tell you it fits fine in the back seat of a 4dr Ford Fusion. It is easy enough to install and remove so if you can get to the child seat anchors in back seat I would think it would do well. We are pleased with it for our then 7 now 8 year old grand daughter. Convinced her it isn\'t a "baby seat" and explained the value of the shoulder harness not cutting across her neck. Sits her up higher and she can see out well. Hope this is of some help.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHVR94W', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385366400, 'question': 'Are the cup and side holders detachable, making the seat even narrower? Thank you.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No, Tracy, the cup is built within the frame of the seat, so the width is not altered. The arms can be removed, though this wouldn't affect the width as they are directly over the seat. There is a lower slide-out cup-like drawer which is flush with the outer edge of the seat when closed. It really could be left closed all the time if space is an issue. One drawback: Once installed, the seat is very secure. In fact, we have not been able to remove it from the back seat configuration of our Prius. This may be easier in other car models. Bette K."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AHVR94W', 'answerTime': 'Feb 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392710400, 'question': 'What material is the latch? Is it metal similar to a latch on a convertible car seat or heavy duty nylon or fabric?', 'answer': 'It is made metal.'}
