{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHVR3G6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401692400, 'question': 'Are head supports OPTIONAL? I have read that the head support "pillow" is removable, but that doesn\'t necessarily mean you can remove it and still safely use the car seat without it. I\'m leaning toward the LX model for it\'s other features, but if this...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yep! You can remove the pillow and safely use the seat once your child gets a little older. We have this car seat and now that our daughter is seventh months old and has much better head control we have removed the infant inserts from the seat. For more information on this seat you can look at the manual online http://download.gracobaby.com/ProductInstructionManuals/PD261464A.pdf Page 18 has the information about the infant insert. We really like this seat - it is easy to adjust and is light/easy to carry. However, one thing I'd like to warn you about is that the click connect sometimes does not fit adapters made for the Graco classic connect seats. For example, we have a BOB stroller and the Graco car seat adapter works only with the classic connect and not with the click connect. So if you have existing gear that you plan to use the car seat with, you may want to get the classic connect model. Good luck!"}
