{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AHVR4KG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383811200, 'question': 'I\'m debating between a BOB Revolution SE and this stroller. Does anyone know if this is a good stroller for toddlers (do they still fit)? Also, how is the handlebar height? I\'m 5\'9" and my husband is 6\'4". Thanks!', 'answer': "Heidi! This stroller is indeed a great and comfortable fit for toddlers - when I purchased it my 2 1/2 yr. old daughter fit great and was very comfortable. The handlebar height would b good for you because you are taller - it is set to a pretty high level. However, choosing this Graco over a B.O.B. I would say, all depends upon how much you plan on using it for actually jogging.. If I wasn't going to run a lot with my daughter I would've definitely kept this stroller because it is very durable and comfortable. If you read my review on it, though, it definitely was not nice to use on a run! It was too heavy and loud and has no shock support, so unless you are running on a smooth, straight road every single day it isn't what you want! I read a lot of reviews that said they chose a B.O.B over this Graco simply because it was lighter... I ended up exchanging my Graco for a Schwinn Turismo and I have to say, I couldn't be happier and more pleased with my decision! Hope this information helps!!!"}
