{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AHVR5U0', 'answerTime': 'Jun 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402815600, 'question': 'Has anyone found a pad and sheets for the bassinet on the stand? Babys r us makes a bassinet pad that is 31L by 18W. will it work?', 'answer': 'A foam pad is included, and the liner is machine washable. However, my personal recommendation is to choose another style. My son did not sleep well in the bassinet; even after adding various bedding material. The storage pockets under the changing table could be better. If I have another child, I will get the style that has the rocking chair and the storage pockets hanging down the side. My primary use for the bassinet is a storage area/changing station.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AHVR5U0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398409200, 'question': "I wanted to know how I would set up the Mattress pad when the baby is about a 8-12 months? The only option I see is setting up all the way down? I would like to set it up in the middle not all the way down. Most graco's have that option. Since this one...", 'answer': 'From what I can tell, it looks like unfortunately the upper level is connected to the diaper and bassinet holder. The only options I can see to hold it in the higher level and use for a napper would be to cut away the sections on the top, or to try and find an upper level at a thrift or second hand store.'}
