{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHVR4JW', 'answerTime': 'Nov 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416816000, 'question': "I'll be running 3-10 miles, 3-4x/week. I'll be using a '07 Toyota Yaris to transport it. Does it work well on a gravel trail?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I changed out the tires with these: Kenda MX K50 BMX Bicycle Tires - 12.5 x 2.25 for the front, and 2 Kenda Comp III Style Wire Bead Bicycle Tires, Blackwall, 16-Inch x 2.125-Inch for the back. I also added Slime Smart Tube bicycle tubes, because the terrain I take the stroller is prone to sand burrs and puncture vines. This is one of the complaints I had about the stroller, the tubes and tires were not made to handle small punctures. These tires will have better grip on the ground whether it is wet or dry. Good luck!'}
