{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AI4BTYY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384329600, 'question': 'When using two cameras, do you get split screen video and audio from both at the same time, or audio only by cycling between the two cameras?', 'answer': 'There is no split-screen. You have to flip from one feed to the next for both audio and video--one view/audio feed at a time. However, there is a "scan" function that automatically rotates among the camera feeds very frequently, changing which camera it\'s on every few seconds, so while you can\'t see two rooms simultaneously, you can get views/audio of them in quick succession of each other. It seems frequent enough for you to feel like you have your eyes and ears on two places at once. Hope that helps!'}
