{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AJSIQEU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421049600, 'question': 'How do you adjust the seat belt?', 'answer': "When you say seat belt, I'm assuming you're referring to the harness straps that secure the child in the seat. On the back of the carseat, you will find two black levers with straps secured through them. Hold down the two levers with one hand and then pull the harness straps on the front of the seat to loosen the belt. To tighten the belt, just pull the strap hanging from the back of the black levers. If you're looking to adjust the height of the shoulder straps, you're going to have to rethread the strap through a higher or lower slot. Go to 3:13 in this video to see: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d9pi6x90lLU"}
