{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AJSIS9S', 'answerTime': 'Aug 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376031600, 'question': 'Our daughter\'s very tall. She just turned 6 mos old &amp; is 28" &amp; 18lbs. In NJ she has to stay rear facing 6 more mos. Will this seat be roomy enough?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "My daughter is very tall also, 100% for her age group. At 18 months and 35inches, she is at the next to the top shoulder strap. The manufacturer recommends turning it forward facing when they reach the top strap holder. I just asked our pediatrician at our 18 month check up what we should do when she reaches that point as I am sure it will be soon, and before she is 2 which is the law in CA. His response was to turn her around when she reaches the top strap even if it is before age 2 as she will then be big enough. That being said we bought this carseat for traveling. It is the smallest and lightest carseat we could find. She seems very comfortable in it. The bottom strap to attach it via car latches does not adjust on both sides which makes getting a perfectly tight fit impossible. It has good safety ratings but in comparison to the Britax carseat we use for every day, it really doesn't seem as safe or tighly secured in the car. Hope this helps."}
