{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AJSJFYU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403161200, 'question': 'The banister at the top of my stairs is metal...would it still work there or does it need to be screwed in on both sides?', 'answer': 'We did not screw it on even though we have a wood bannister. Bought a wooden plank that is about 1.5 inch thick and used industrial plastic ties to secure it to the bannister. The little metal clamps that come with the gate are screwed onto that. Plank and ties came from Home Depot.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AJSJFYU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374476400, 'question': 'what size opening does this gate fit?', 'answer': 'I had the same question- not a good description from Amazon. I found this info on Walmart\'s website: Evenflo Top of the Stairs Extra-Tall Gate: *Safe for use at top of stairs *One-hand-release Evenflo extra-tall gate is convenient for high traffic areas *The swing control feature is removable so the Evenflo extra-tall gate will not swing out over stairs *The four-point hardware mounting is easy to install and is easily removed *32" tall and can be installed up to 3 inches above a floor for 35" of protection *Evenflo extra-tall gate expands from 30" to 48" wide to fit a variety of openings'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AJSJFYU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420444800, 'question': 'what is the difference between wood and hardware mounted one? The photo and descriptions look rather similar. And the price is a bit different.', 'answer': "Not exactly sure. But the Hardware mounted one, i own two of and had one at my old house too. The gate is made of wood, and then there are metal hinges and locking mechanism that are attached to the wood gate, and Both pieces mount to the wall/railing with metal hardware. The gate can be quickly removed without uninstalling the hardware from the wall, and it just slides right back in. If the wood mounted one have wood mounts, i would say its not as sturdy/rugged, but i can't say for sure since i haven't seen it."}
