{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AJSJE6O', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410937200, 'question': 'Can baby bounce around in this like a baby bouncer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes. There are springs in the brown stumps. Makes a lot of noise and sounds like baby's at a casino but it does bounce. Not a ton but better than the baby Einstein oceans exersaucer which has no bounce. Son prefers this one to baby Einstein."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AJSJE6O', 'answerTime': 'Jan 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422000000, 'question': 'Am i the only person who feels like its an OVERLOAD? Why arent there caps to fill in holes of toys removed?', 'answer': "It has several toys. There aren't any caps to block the holes if you remove any of the toys. I do not see any harm if you leave holes open. You can buy a different exerciser with less toys, but you can't add more toys when babies grows up. You have made a good choice to get this one with more toys. I am very happy with this as it keeps my baby pretty busy."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AJSJE6O', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378364400, 'question': 'How old was your baby when he/she begin to use this?', 'answer': 'About 4 or 5 months'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AJSJE6O', 'answerTime': 'Aug 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377327600, 'question': 'The colors shown in the photo are mostly blue and green. But when I looked at the photos it was multi colored. What color is the product?', 'answer': "It's been awhile since I have seen the pictures so I will describe the product as it came to me. The base is solid green and the toy tray is too, just a lighter green. The legs are brown.. The toys themselves are really colorful: green alligator/crocodile in blue water with a small green turtle and several green lily pads (his center section is divided in three parts with buttons underneath that do shapes, colors, and numbers--123, yellow-blue-red, and circle-square-triangle ; a blue chameleon that lights up with blue, red, yellow, and all three; two brown monkeys on a white half-loop; a purple dragonfly with blue wings on a green stem; a blue and white parrot on a brown & green tree branch; two hanging butterflies with crinkly blue wings, one yellow and one purple (also the green tree leaves on the larger half loop are crinkly); and three birds, one red and blue and yellow macaw with a yellow drum, one white cockatoo with a purple spin-y instrument, and one blue parrot with a yellow horn (he squeaks but it is really hard to push his head down); the globe is mostly yellow with a blue and green Earth map-it has three musical animal faces, a brown monkey, a red bird, and a yellow cat. They all light up when pushed for music: the monkey green, the bird red, and cat yellow. I didn't use the playmat that came with it, but I remember it being a mostly blue background with repeating small jungle-themed pictures--birds and monkeys and the like."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AJSJE6O', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395903600, 'question': 'does it have pvc? what kind of plastic is it made from?', 'answer': "If you are thinking the hardness of schedule 40 PVC pipe as in the type your would buy from a home depot then no it is not that unforgiving. It is durable enough to withstand a rambunctious baby. It has a matte texture so it is smooth enough and not catchy on delicate skin like a gloss surface would so baby can slam, skim, skid his/her hands on the table top and not get any skimmed hands or elbows (if you know what I mean). It has not broken on me or shown any of those white stress lines you would find in bending plastic. Otherwise, it is the best I can describe it as the instructions do not specify why type of plastic (or its components/percentages) it is made from. If you know what one of those plastic cars or wagons for little children that they go in and drive. It feels like that - think of it more like that only in thicker layers. - enough layers that it will now bow under decent pressure. I hope that gives a better idea. For what it's worth, I would not hesitate buying it again over the metal rod/bungee types. He loves this thing and loves it even more now he is better at sitting and standing. I retracted the stabilizing legs so the saucer can wobble now and he goes crazy for it!!"}
