{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ALOT5AG', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410678000, 'question': 'What do they mean it adjusts over crown molding? Did you have to mount it into the molding? Would it work in spaces that 108"?', 'answer': "You do not need to screw attachment into molding/trim. The piece that you screw into the wall can slide up and down along the pole to clear trim/molding so you don't damage it. For example, I have trim that extends about 3 inches from the floor so the lower attachment piece was slid up a little to clear the trim so the gate would mount flat without damage to any trim boards."}
