{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AQ693RO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405926000, 'question': 'Is this the same changing pad that comes with the matching diaper bag?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I had to look up the bag online to see the similarities because I do not own it. Now, from what I\'ve seen, the shapes of both changing pads are the same -- oblong or oval. As far as the size and texture, I am not certain. I only went as far as looking at pictures. To get a better idea, go on YouTube and type in "JJ Cole Changing Clutch, Mixed Leaf." This video is a little over 2 minutes long and the lady is explaining all the little details. There is also a 29 second video on YouTube which gets to the point and just shows you everything without all the blabber: "JJ Cole Changing Clutch - Compact for on-the-go changing," typed as is. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AQ693RO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401951600, 'question': 'Is the clutch machine washable? How can you wash it?', 'answer': 'I wipe it down with clean wipes. It is plastic and a canvas material. Easy to clean.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AQ693RO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404025200, 'question': 'Does it include wipe case or just a pocket to hold it and we have to buy the case separately?', 'answer': 'There is no wipe case, but there is a wipe holder that a pack of wipes will slip into, with an opening that the wipes will come out of without having to take the pack of wipes out of the clutch. So you use regular flip top wipes with it, not a wipes case that you need to take out to use.'}
