{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AQE6Z6I', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389600000, 'question': 'I need something to fit a 64 inch width. Will the pressure mounters expand enough (2 inches on each side of gate) to fill the 64 inch gap?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I don\'t think it will although I have not tried it. My guess is that the 60" wide that the gate is supposed to fill includes the 2 inches on each side to press the whole thing together enough for the gate to close. That said, you can always see if you can get an additional extension piece from Summer (if they offer it an support it as a viable solution). Also you can also consider putting a couple of 2x4\'s on either side of it, but that will likely mean nailing the wood into the walls to prevent the gate from falling down.'}
