{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ASI748A', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408604400, 'question': "I'm a first time mom and need stroller advice! I have a Toyota Corolla and I'm looking for a light weight easy to man", 'answer': 'The jogger stroller is a little bit bulky. The 3 wheels do easily disconnect (with the push of a button) and easily re-connect (just push / snap into place), which makes more compact and easier to transport. I\'m think the stroller would fit into the corolla trunk if you pop the wheels off. With that said, I would NOT consider this a "light weight easy to manage stroller". What we did is purchase this set (jogger stroller and carseat) and we also purchased the "frame stroller" -&gt; Graco SnugRider Elite Stroller & Car Seat Carrier (http://www.amazon.com/Graco-SnugRider-Elite-Stroller-Carrier/dp/B008OIPZW8/ref=sr_1_1?s=baby-products&ie=UTF8&qid=1408646069&sr=1-1&keywords=graco+frame+stroller). We are glad we did - get the best of both worlds. - The "frame stroller" is super light weight and compact - we keep this in my wife\'s car trunk all the time and use it whenever we are around town (I.e. grocery shopping, dining, etc). - We use the jogger stroller when going on walks from home, or when we want something more heavy duty (I.e. going to an amusement park, going to the beach, or just about anything that is a longer all-day adventure). Now that our daughter is getting a little bit older / bigger (15 months) she really enjoys sitting in the jogger stroller without the carseat (prefers it greatly over sitting in the carseat). Hope that helps...'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ASI748A', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385884800, 'question': 'does this come with the car seat base?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, the base comes with the stroller and car seat. It's a set."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ASI748A', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397718000, 'question': 'At what weight/age do I move the baby from the upper seat (car seat) to the stroller seat?', 'answer': 'Once baby can sit up well you can think about making the switch. Babies vary so much in size and it is really more of a developmental issue. You could of course "prop" your baby, but if things start shifting, while you are jogging, you won\'t have a happy baby anymore. As a car-seat, the limitations are: 32" or 35 pounds, which ever comes first. But this is for crash safety, which shouldn\'t be a problem for stroller use, as long as your baby is comfortable. Hope this helps you sort it out. ENJOY your baby!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ASI748A', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419840000, 'question': 'The stroller colors vary in price. Are they the same or different?', 'answer': "Yes it's the same stroller different collors"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ASI748A', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408604400, 'question': "I tried this out in the store and I loved how light weight it was but since it's a jogging stroller, is it good for everyday use as a primary strolle", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It is not good as primary stroller. Specially if you live in the city, it is too heavy and bulky. It barely fits in toyota Camry trunk. Front wheel came of in 3 months, called them and have been waiting for replacement over 45 days. So I purchased lightweight one and boy what a difference. Going up and down stairs is so easy. Shopping became easy too. Although, i miss it when i got into the parks or hiking. Next, car seat attached is low quality and became too small in just 2-3 months.'}
