{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AV53YJ8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379401200, 'question': 'What grade stainless steel is this? Is this lined with plastic? Does it contain aluminum? Thank you for your help', 'answer': "Pura bottles are entirely stainless (no aluminum) classified as: food-grade, #304, or 18/8 (all different classifications/lables for the same material). There is no liner and no plastic. The spout and/or nipple and caps are made of silicone and the cap ring is also stainless steel. You can read more on the manufacturer's website: purastainless.com. These bottles are wonderful--they hold up very well to wear and tear (although the color coating may eventually scratch, but NOT peel). The bottle is compatible with both the sippy cup spouts and regular bottle nipples, which really eases the trasition from bottle to cup. They will, naturally, conduct heat or cold, so if your little one has sensitive fingers and likes his/her milk warmed or cooled, I'd reccomend the silicone sleeves that are available."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AV53YJ8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374303600, 'question': 'does this bottle come with the travel cover?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it should come with a silicone cap. For the record, both my nieces love these cups (and they were HARD to wean off the bottle!), although I recommend a sleeve, as they can get chilly for little fingers.'}
