{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AW0MZF6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389427200, 'question': 'How easy is this to move from room to room? Does it have wheels?', 'answer': "This is a little difficult for you to move from room to room ONLY if you don't know how to properly collapse it. In the bottom center of the playard is a pull cord and you can collapse it by pushing down on the parts of the frame. You can find videos instructing you on how to collapse (and even take it apart to wash it) online."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AW0MZF6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394694000, 'question': 'Does the main basinet sag in the middle or is there enough support? Looks sunken in the middle on the picture...', 'answer': 'No it is not sunken at all. The whole playard is very sturdy with no sagging anywhere. The changing pad is exceptionally strong with no slanting and plenty deep enough that the baby does not need strapping in. Highly recommend.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AW0MZF6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393747200, 'question': 'What brand sheets has anyone purchased to use on this play yard that fits well?', 'answer': 'I use an American Baby Company organic playard sheet and it fits perfectly. Any sheet sized for a standard playard should fit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AW0MZF6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398322800, 'question': 'Would it be a good idea to buy a crib mattress for this? If so, what type/brand?', 'answer': 'I think it\'s a good idea to buy a playard mattress for ANY playard if you intend to use it for naps, sleeping. Those planks in playard mattresses can still be felt, even though they are padded. The same is true with this model. I bought a Dream On Me 3" Foam playard mattress and it fits perfectly.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AW0MZF6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420358400, 'question': 'Can I use a sheet saver or lap pad or some other waterproof layer in the bassinet, and what do you recommend?', 'answer': "Yes I used Graco pack 'n play changing pad cover, 2 pack, cream. They fit both the bassinet and changer and are under $10 on Amazon and ship Prime!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AW0MZF6', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404370800, 'question': 'Does the changing area fold over the storage compartments if you want to use the bottom playyard but still want access to the changing table?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, the changing area folds over the side storage slots to give easy access to the crib part. It is easy to snap the two "legs" off of the side bars, allowing you to swivel the entire changing table over to the side.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AW0MZF6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398322800, 'question': 'Did anyone know what playard mattresses fit safely in this playard?. Is it standard playard mattress size?', 'answer': 'I bought a "Dream On Me 3" Foam Playard Mattress" and it fits just fine. It measures 39" x 27" and the bottom of the playard itself measures about 41" x 27.5". There is a little wiggle room between the sides and the foam mattress, but it is very slight. I kept the included mattress platform on the bottom and put the foam mattress on top layered with a cushiony mattress pad cover (like American Baby Organic Cotton Quilted one). The foam mattress is not as soft as I would have liked, so the quilted mattress pad really helps. Combined, they make a perfect sleeping area. Top that with a soft flannel fitted sheet and I want to crawl in there!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AW0MZF6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416988800, 'question': 'Does this have seams in between the board in the bottom? Is each individual board separated somehow or do they overlap? Or is it just one big piece?', 'answer': 'It is one piece that folds up. You can see and feel the seams where it folds though.'}
