{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AY96SSK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402556400, 'question': 'Hi, will this liner fit the diono rxt car seat? Is it machine washable? Thanks', 'answer': "I don't know about the car seat, but we have only hand washed it. We use a wool wash (Eucalan Lanolin Enriched Delicate Wash, purchased on Amazon). And then we just hang it out to dry. It will look really matted when its wet, but will dry nicely and be just as soft and fluffy as when new. We really have only ever washed if when our kid's thrown up or something serious. Due to the lanolin in wool, it is naturally antimicrobial, antibacterial, antifungal. When urine or breast milk comes in contact with wool - even saturating it - wool is self-cleaning due to lanolin's anti-fungal and antibacterial properties. Rather than washing with regular detergent and rinsing, wool should be soaked or washed in a lanolin wash and not rinsed. This is important to know, because rinsing the lanolin from the wool will take away many of the benefits. The lanolin is the natural wax that needs to remain in the wool in order to help make it so amazing! Hope this is helpful. And we have washed ours every 6mos or so, outside of the situations I mentioned above :)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AY96SSK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391673600, 'question': 'Will this liner fit a BOB Revolution SE jogging stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not really. You need to be able to remove and reinstall the straps in order to make this fit well and I don't think that's possible on any Revulotion jogging stroller. I sometimes use this for my BOB Revolution SE jogging stroller but it's not a perfect fit. Works great on most non-jogging strollers though."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AY96SSK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390723200, 'question': "Does this fit an infant car seat? I'm getting the graco click connect and would rather use this than a synthetic insert.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I used this liner in a Chicco KeyFit when my LO was 5-8 months old last winter. There was still plenty of room for the straps to fit comfortably around her. This year, she is 21 lbs and it is too snug if I put her, with a thin puffer jacket (patagonia puffer or gap thinsulate puffer) and the liner, so I've been putting the liner over her for warmth. and I also used it in the spring in her stroller when it was too warm for a full bunting, but still chilly. They say you can use it when it's hot out, but it was 90 degrees here and she was sweating like crazy when I had the liner in her stroller! I loved this liner so much I got the full bunting for her stroller (I walk in the city a lot) and it's amazing. I think going the natural route is a lot more flexible (and perhaps healthier) than the synthetic. I'd recommend it."}
