{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B07STBO', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1367910000, 'question': 'Could someone post a picture of it folded up? Is there any way to put the infant seat in the rear seat or is it clipping to the tray in front?', 'answer': "Well... TECHNICALLY, you shouldn't put the infant seat in the back. I have a Chicco KeyFit30 though, and my husband forgot to bring the infant adapter to the zoo recently. It actually fit quite nicely (sideways) in the rear while my toddler rode up front. I wouldn't recommend that as a regular configuration though, as there is no safety strap like there is in front."}
