{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2N6K', 'answerTime': 'Apr 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398236400, 'question': "Microfleece is so hot, isn't it? Do you children get overheated in this sleepsack? The lightweight doesn't look warm enough, but is the fleece too hot", 'answer': "Well I live in Seattle, so the temp hasn't gotten too high here- 60s- but we haven't had any problems with overheating. I probably wouldn't use it during the summertime unless you have air conditioning going- I keep their rooms between 68-70 and they're fine. I just put him in light cotton pjs-(carters 2piece pjs) and socks. I have noticed that the polyester type 2piece pjs seem to keep him on the warmer side, so intend not to put socks with those or only use those on colder nights. As it gets warmer I'll use it with just at shirt or onesie underneath. But once summer hits, I either switch to the thin cotton sleep sack or just put them to bed in their pjs. So it probably depends how hot it is where you live and how warm you keep your house but my son doesn't get overheated if his room is kept between that 65-70 mark. Hope that's helpful :)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B1M2N6K', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418284800, 'question': 'Does this product have flame retardants in it? Thank you', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Halo site says no'}
