{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2N6K', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423123200, 'question': 'My son is 23 lbs &amp; 32 in. What size should I get him? I know what Halo recommends, but based on reviews I think I want to get him a smaller one.', 'answer': "I would think a medium. My daughter is about 18 lbs and it's HUGE on her. I think a medium is the smallest it comes. We bought a large 1st and couldn't return b/c we washed it... I think I could fit in it!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B1M2N6K', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408604400, 'question': 'Does the feet sticking out offset the warmth of the fleece? Worried that his feet will be ice and the rest hot.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "I put socks on his feet and he seems comfortable. He's slept in this for about 7 months now (prior to that we used the regular sleep sack). When I check on him, he doesn't seem overly hot and his feet are never cold. I would just make sure they're not thin socks."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2N6K', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': "I'm considering this product for my 18 month old to see if it will keep her from climbing out of the crib. Does anyone know if this would work?", 'answer': "It's not meant to keep your child from climbing just to keep them warm."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2N6K', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': "I'm considering this product for my 18 month old to see if it will keep her from climbing out of the crib. Does anyone know if this would work?", 'answer': "That is a nice little side benefit. It doesn't make it impossible, so a determined kid (especially a tall one) could probably still get out, but it certainly makes it more of a challenge. They simply can't freely throw their legs up like they can without one (though, the kind without feet holes are even more effective.) Our 26 month old hasn't gotten out yet and I would attribute that, at least in part, to the fact that she still sleeps in one. She will likely get a toddler bed before ever climbing out of her crib (she still sleeps well in it, so we haven't felt compelled to transition her yet.)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2TUK', 'answerTime': 'May 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400482800, 'question': 'what is the length? My son is very long', 'answer': "I'd look at the size chart on Halo's website (http://www.halosleep.com/size-chart/). If your son is in one of the larger baby sizes, I'd recommend the Early Walker version of the sleepsack. Not only is it a bit longer than the regular sleepsack, but the foot holes allow for even more length... just put socks on the baby if you use the holes, otherwise the feet may get cold being outside the sack."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2TUK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': 'How many of these would you buy for a baby?', 'answer': 'We liked having two (in each size), so that you always have a clean one.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2TUK', 'answerTime': 'Nov 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417334400, 'question': 'Hi, wonder what should I wear for the baby when using this. Just a long sleeve romper will do or romper with long pants and footsie? Thanks!', 'answer': 'I typically just put a onesie with long sleeves on the baby for the colder months. For the warmer months I will just put the sleep sack on by itself so the baby does not over heat.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2TUK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403334000, 'question': 'What season is the product for? For what indoor and outdoor temperature?', 'answer': "I was surprised at how much I love this sleep sack! We live in California, so the temperature can start at 85 in the evening and drop to 65 by midnight, and, personally, I've found this sleep sack was able to span those temps no problem. It's both lightweight and substantial. Cozy and breathable. We always use the sleep sack and just switch out the clothes underneath to accommodate the weather - I'll just add some warm socks if the temp gets colder or put her in just a t-shirt if it's hot. In the winter, we used the fleece version so I would call this a 3-season sleeper."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B1M2TUA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398841200, 'question': 'I have a rapidly growing 15 month old who is 24 pounds and 28 inches. He wears 18 month clothes. Any size recommendations?', 'answer': 'The large would be your best fit for a while (it still fits my 32" son) but the XL won\'t be too huge if you want to use it for even longer. My son can\'t walk in it too easily but it\'s not for walking, it\'s for sleeping!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B1M2TUA', 'answerTime': 'May 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400914800, 'question': 'Is this sleepsack good for summer?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes! We use it constantly with our little guy. During the day for naps (sometimes he'll sleep with just a onesie or tee shirt and diaper underneath) and with short sleeve/ short pj sets at night. In really hot weather I'm anticipating we may just put him in the diaper and the sleep sack:) We love our sleep sacks!!"}
