{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B507D7C', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1420012800, 'question': 'It is hard to decide which to buy - Performance Sport and Performance Booster. The price is very different. We are currently using ProRide - love it', 'answer': 'I have the Performance Sport and love it. I believe the difference is that the Performance Sport has a 5 point harness to secure the child starting at 20 pounds and can go up to 65 pounds. Once they reach that weight limit you use the vehicle seat belt to secure them in the seat. The Performance Booster does not have a 5 point harness. The child must be 30 lbs to start using this seat and is only secured by the vehicle seat belt. So, it would depend on the age/size of your child and whether or not you want them protected by a 5 point harness if he/she is still under 65 pounds. If they are already past that weight limit I guess the seats would work the same.'}
