{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B507DN6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392105600, 'question': 'I already have a convertible car seat and am trying to figure out if this is the Recaro seat I need or just the booster. How does "booster mode" work?', 'answer': "It depends on what kind of harness you want. I wanted my 4year old in a 5 point harness for as long as possible, so went with a seat that converts form a 5 point harness to a booster with seatbelt. The harness mode is good to 90lbs ( can't remember height limit) once over 90lbs you can remove the harness and use the seatbelt mode (there are guides to hold the seatbelt at the correct position). I am very happy with the seat, it is very well made and my son loves it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B507DN6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398063600, 'question': 'Are kids comfortable if they fall asleep while riding in this seat? I see it can recline some. Does that help?', 'answer': 'hi Anne - this is one "feature" of the seat that completely blows me away. In our old Graco seat, our son\'s poor head would nod back and forth when he\'d sleep. hit the breaks and his head would just bob forward, often waking him up. In these Recaro seats, they did something with the design / angle that this NEVER happens. I have no clue why but my wife and I talk about this all the time. It just works'}
