{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B507EQW', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': 'Would this seat be appropriate for a 6 month old who weighs 20 lbs (carseat minimum), developmentally-speaking? He is quite young to be so heavy.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This doesn't have a rear-facing mode. State regulations (I live in CA) require infants to be in rear facing seats for at least the 1st year. The American Academy of Pediatrics has a similar guideline. It has to do with head & neck muscle development, if I recall correctly. I would urge you to check your state regs, the AAP guidelines, and your pediatrician yourself to be sure. Going by those guidelines I don't think this is the right seat for such a young baby. One of my twins was about 20lbs at 6 months old and we kept him rear-facing for the first year. He was long, too, so his feet stuck out over the edge of the rear-facing seat for the last month or two before his 1st birthday. Right after he turned 1, however, we put him in this seat and he loves it."}
