{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B7M7CLA', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'My front bucket seats (2003 Jeep Liberty) do not have removable headrests. Will these kick-mats still work (just looping around the narrower top)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The headrest doesn't have to be removable. The loop at the top of the kick-mat actually is adjustable. I never had to remove my headrest to install the kick-mat. You just have to have a headrest to loop it around."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B7M7CLA', 'answerTime': 'Sep 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380438000, 'question': 'I love these kick mats but I have a 2005 Honda Pilot EXL &amp; the top part fully extended will not fit around the headrest of the front seats. Ideas?', 'answer': "Yes you need to remover the headrest first. In the '05 you need to press where the seat meets the bottom of the headreast and on one of the posts near the top of the seat should be a button like the rest of the headrests in the car. You feel in the fabric and press that and that should release the headrest. Make sure to press hard enough once you find it. The front headrests should be able to be removed in the same manner like the 2nd and 3rd row headrests."}
