{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B7ULJQQ', 'answerTime': 'Mar 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394092800, 'question': 'Does anyone use regular trashbags with this product? If so, which and how?', 'answer': 'I use a regular trash bag. I think it does just as well as the refills. I like the idea of using an old snap ring. Right now I just use a rubber band around the round part inside that spins. It works well. Just remove the rubber band, tie the bag, shove it down through the hole and pop the bag out the door. Clean and smell free. I also use baby powder in the thing in the top instead of baking soda. I love the smell of baby powder.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B7ULJQQ', 'answerTime': 'May 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399014000, 'question': 'Is this the type of pail that "twists" after each addition?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. When I was first researching this product I was confused as to how adding a twist into the bag after every addition could really be efficient use of space, but it un-twists when you lift the lid and re-twists when you close it. The twist really helps to keep the smell in. We've been using ours for 1.5 years now. My husband and I also really like that you can refill the arm and hammer container at the top with regular baking soda and not with some special money making device from the company."}
