{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B7ULJQQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387267200, 'question': "Do you have to push or smoosh the diaper in to get it to go in, or does it drop in easily? I'm worried about pushing a full/messy diaper in.", 'answer': 'Usually diapers fit through the hole nicely. I always wrap them tightly though so I can fit more diapers in the pail. The one thing that gets kind of messy is if you want to put wipes on their own in the diaper pail.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B7ULJQQ', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372662000, 'question': 'Can this pail be used for bagged dog waste in an area that has ony weekly trash pick-up?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, I think it would. If the dog poop is already in a bag it should work just fine. It would not work if you use a scoop to pick it up, because you have to push it down through the hole. Even if you have a big dog, I think the hole is big enough for dog poop, considering how big some of the diapers are that I put in mine. I'm not sure if it will hold a whole week's worth of dog poop, but it might. Now that I think about it, I probably change my pail out about once a week, with about 3 diapers per day in it. The only thing to watch for is that after a few days it sometimes stinks when the lid is opened and you push another diaper inside. For me though, the smell goes away after you close it. But all in all, I would definitely give this a try for that purpose, I think it will work."}
