{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B7ZMORE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394694000, 'question': 'Is this compatible with Graco snugride classic connect car seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It should be. That's one of the main reasons I bought it because it's suppose to be compatible with most car seats. It seemed like all the other strollers I looked at made you either buy a adaptor for the car seat to fit or their brand car seat."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B7ZMORE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389081600, 'question': 'will a chicco keyfit 30 lock into this stroller or does it just rest in it?', 'answer': "It rests in it nice and snugg. two red straps goes over the chicco and clicks together. If you look at your chicco you'll see two little hooks on either side. The red strap goes through those hooks. Added note..this is a good stroller but came with no instructions and missing two screws. The lady at jeep was helpful and sent the screws pretty fast and directed me to the online manual. The tires were flat and too hard to pump with bike pump so went to gas station to pump. One tire has a bubble in it but doesnt wobble. The big plus to this stroller it locks front wheel or swivels and is lite. The cover fits nicely over chicco. Cons no manual missing parts plastic clear ski light on cover with no zipper to close up ipod is very cheap I use it to hold my phone. Still happy after looking at ones in dept stores though and it feels sturdy the mag wheels are a plus making it liteweight. One more thing that no one online mentions is that they say don't jog with an infant"}
