{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B9ZHLRU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416816000, 'question': 'What is the chunkiest type of food that you think will work in this? 1-Oatmeal? 2-star pasta? 3-smoothie fruit? 4-small diced soft veggies?', 'answer': 'Oatmeal, no problem. Star pasta(like Campbell\'s chicken and stars soup) sure. The are that it must fit through is about the size of a McDonalds milkshake straw, so if your fruit or veg is relatively soft and could fit through that sized opening, then it should be able to come through this ok. I wouldn\'t want the chunks to be solid enough to pose a choking hazard though--even an adult could get an unwelcome surprise sucking a green pea through a short straw right? So I would go with at least a "mashed" consistency, not a "chopped" texture if you get my meaning.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B9ZHLRU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403852400, 'question': 'Can you unscrew the top so you can fill it in with like a spoon or a funnel? In other words, can I use it without the squeeze station?', 'answer': 'Yes, it comes with a screw top for filling and cleaning. I use a spoon to fill it which is a little messy but a funnel would work great. This also fills at the top. Some of the filling station ones fill on the bottom and can unfortunately open for a total mess. This is very convenient and I have had no mishaps.'}
