{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B9ZRZFS', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406530800, 'question': "I'm so confused. Do I need a rocker, a bouncer and a swing or does this rocker replace the 3?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "this particular item is for a newborn up till your child is 3. It rocks but also it can be used as a chair. My daughter didnt like the swing we had, it was a Graco swing. And we had a jumperoo for her, which she did like..but that is more for exercise and activity. This is good if your doing things around the house and you can strap your child in while he or she is drinking a bottle. Or if your in the bathroom and you want to keep an eye on your child you can bring this in the bathroom with you and strap your child in. Really there is not much you nessacarily NEED...its more of what will your child like and what will fit your lifestyle in your household. Your child can also sleep in this, there is a strap in the back that unclicks and it the back falls down a bit so your child is laying. I like this chair personally and my daughter likes it. Shes now 18 months. To answer your question this doesn't replace say a swing. but again its about what you want your child to have and think what he or she would like."}
