{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BAAX39E', 'answerTime': 'Oct 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414738800, 'question': 'How is the splash guard for boys? It needs to be tall and not let pee up and over.', 'answer': "I found it to be great-good size, not intrusive so it's not uncomfortable, never had an issue with it going up and over the splash guard with my boy."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BAAX39E', 'answerTime': 'Aug 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408604400, 'question': 'What type of plastic is the material made from? Recycling code? I am concerned with PVC, Lead, Phlatates, Cadmium, etc.', 'answer': 'Not entirely sure of contents. Made in China. There is the recycling symbol on the bottom with a &gt; PP &lt; and a clock-like symbol with the hand pointing to the 12. Hope that helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BAAX39E', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402642800, 'question': 'Will this fit a round Toto seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I use it on an oval seat and it has a great fit. It is supposed to be adjustable to fit other sizes but I haven't tried that. It is sturdy and the little handles are great so the little one can feel secure"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BAAX39E', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'Is the splash guard smooth or does it have lip or edge? I have read about boys getting injured by splashguards if they get up too quickly.', 'answer': 'The top of the splash guard is smooth. The only part that had a lip it the part the touches toilet seat. We have girls and love this seat. Only draw back is it has to be removed for adult use (which is just lifting off, not difficult at all) and you can not close the toilet with it on.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BAAX39E', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395903600, 'question': 'is the shield tall enough for boys--does it fall off very easily?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "The shield is attached to the seat it's one piece. and yes its tall enough for boys. It is actually better for boys than girls. But my grand daughter gets up there and uses it just fine. It is super stable and durable she isn't scared at all. Its a good product."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BAAX39E', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': "How quickly does the seat attach? I'm looking for a portable seat to take out and about with us, as our 18 mo old now signs when he has to go!", 'answer': "It just snaps right on depending on what width you have the two stabilizing prongs set on. It's easy."}
