{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BATQJE6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402038000, 'question': 'Can I use a liner with these to easily remove poo? Also, what do I need to do to condition these/break them in?', 'answer': "Poo hasn't been difficult to remove at all and I don't use a liner. Neither does my daughter with hers. All I did to break them in was to run them through a sanitary cycle on my washer. If you don't have that cycle on yours then I believe the directions say to wash 5 times. I dry them on a low setting on my dryer too. My daughter's diapers are the kinds with the inserts, but I like these better There are two flaps that lay down in the diaper that are attached so you don't have to fool with removing and sticking the insert back in"}
