{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BBKLMUA', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429426800, 'question': 'I do have the Summer infant baby touch boost monitor. Will this camera work if my current model is # 28810? the headline states #28810A', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, I believe it will because the 28810A is the current model being sold on Summer Infant\'s website. And the manual they post with the 28810A is the 28810 manual. http://www.summerinfant.com/monitoring/video/babytouchboost Manual: http://www.summerinfant.com/getattachment/e91cd766-6c0f-4f7d-8090-5d33a2e9fcb4/28810-Baby-Touch-Boost-IB.pdf.aspx?ext=.pdf I think they added the "A" as a dating method for when the unit was purchased. The baby touch boost model has been around since late 2012. Then they had a battery issue with some of them. I imagine they updated the model number after this battery issue was resolved so they could differentiate between the two. The technology is the same. You can always call Summer Infant Customer Service to confirm this info. Their number 1-800-268-6237.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BBKLMUA', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402642800, 'question': "In the title of the ad says it's for model 28840, but in the description of the ad says model 28810. It Works with both models?", 'answer': "I'm not 100% on the model numbers and I don't still have my packaging. It looks like maybe they have a typo in the description. Make sure that the camera that you already have is the Summer Infant Baby Touch BOOST. If it's the earlier version (just the Summer Infant Baby Touch Video Monitor) it won't work. I made that mistake when I first bought this. Then I tried to find an extra camera for the earlier version and couldn't and just ended up buying the new system as well. I made sure to buy the BOOST version and this camera works with that so you can look up that model number to confirm that it is what you have."}
