{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BDCNT0W', 'answerTime': 'Dec 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386403200, 'question': 'Does the adapter need to be removed before folding the stroller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You do not need to remove the adapter. However, the stroller does not fold as flat if you do not remove it. We found that we would have to remove it sometimes when going through airport security screeners, but that was about it. We would also generally remove it when going on long road trips in a packed car (to get extra space). One thing we also learned is that you can make the stroller a lot lighter by removing the existing seat (so you would just have a frame, the adapter, and your car seat). It is very easy to remove the seat and put it back on when you are done with the adapter and your child is in the main seat.'}
