{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEJP3VC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'would this work for a trip to London with an 11 month old in December? does it fold easily for gate chcek?', 'answer': "I've never been to London so I can't answer the first question, but I have traveled with this stroller several times. It folds up fairly easily and also comes with a nice travel bag. I just put it in the bag for gate check. The bag rolls up to be about the size of a loaf of bread once you take the stroller out of it and easily fits underneath. It rains a lot in London, right? We also purchased the rain cover which has come in handy a few times. The seat reclines to almost horizontal. A few times we've been traveling and needed to let him take a nap and it worked out fine. EDIT: Sorry, we bought the travel bag separately. It's $50, but we travel enough to make it worth while. The stroller is durable enough but the way luggage gets thrown around I wouldn't check it without some protective cover."}
