{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2TI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414825200, 'question': 'Has anyone had an experience with this seat in an accident? How did the seat hold up?', 'answer': 'My husband, six-year old, and myself were rear-ended last night (13 hours ago) by a guy driving a 2013 Porsche Cayenne (1999 Camry for us). My husband and I both needed to be examined at the hospital and have whiplash injuries. My son was completely unscathed, scared for a moment but not hurt in any way. The fire department first responders took one look at Felix\'s seat, checked that it was installed correctly, and high-fived Felix, telling me that they rarely see any injuries in big kids in those kinds of seats. Felix is 6.5 years old, 45" tall. 45 lbs of muscle. He is not sore at all today either, but holy crap, I am sore. The fire captain advised me that even though the seat visually looks fine that the seatbelts have been strained and the foam is probably somewhat compressed so we should replace it. I am here to buy another one today. Worth EVERY penny for Felix to be completely unhurt and the guy who hit us or his insurance will have to pay for it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2TI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413270000, 'question': 'What is the manufacture date on your carseat if you bought it in August-September 2014? I want to know if Amazon is shipping "fresh" carseats. Thanks', 'answer': 'Why are you looking for a "fresh" one? I am looking for the model revised to address the IIHS "Check Fit" issue. Britax Customer Service told me that the seat was revised on July 17, 2014.'}
