{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2TI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419062400, 'question': 'will this fit in 2 doors mini cooper?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not sure if the Mini is a 4 or 5 seater car. If a 5 seater, then the car seat should fit in the middle back seat. We have it in a 4Runner rear middle seat, fits well but is tight for passengers sitting next to it. It won't fit in our 4 seater Volvo C30."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2TI', 'answerTime': 'May 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401001200, 'question': 'My son is about to turn two, and is not small at just under 30 lbs. We still have him in the infant carrier seat (but he is about to be too big), and we were thinking about skipping the convertible seats altogether and moving straight to this. Does...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I know that it seems that most people do not keep their children rear facing until at least 40 pounds, but in actuality extended rear facing is much, much, much safer for your child. Other countries keep children rear facing until age four and have much lower rates of child mortality in car crashes. Should you be interested in extended rear facing, I would check out the Diano Radian and the Clek Foonf. If your child is not tall, the Britax Advocate is another great choice. If you are set on turning your son around, I will say that we have this seat and absolutely love it. We use it for our almost 6 year old daughter and she is very comfortable in it. The seat installs like a dream and is very solid. It's heavy though, so I wouldn't choose it if you need to move it a lot. Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2L6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395644400, 'question': 'Does anyone find that harness is hard to tighten? I am looking into getting a booster car seat and want one that is easy to tighten.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Out of the five car seats I have owned, this is the easiest to tighten. I would say it is easy to tighten.'}
