{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2L6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417248000, 'question': 'Tall children and the harness - any height restrictions for harness use?', 'answer': "Yes for harness mode 30-58 in tall. Seated shoulder height is 12.5-20.5 inches. Booster is 45-62 in with seated shoulder height 15-23in. Top of ears shouldn't be higher than top of head restraint."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2L6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383724800, 'question': 'hi there, may be a silly question. my nephew is 25lb but he is only 1year old. Is it possible to use the seat or it has to be a 2yr+ child?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No I d9nt helieve this would be safe for a 1 year old. And im not positive but I dont think he meets the weight requirement. My 3 year old daughter is 36 pounds and was just over the weight minimum. I dont think your nephew would meet the minimum height either. I highly recommend Britax Boulevard. That held my daughter until she was 33 pounds but had plenty of room for the straps to expand if she was heavier. She was getting to tall for it at 39 1/2 inches tall. My 8 month old is in the Boulevard now. He is 19 pounds and 28 inches tall. Fits him great. It can be put in the rear facing position for longer providing added safety. This one cant rear face.'}
