{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2L6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411023600, 'question': 'Can a child sleep comfortably in this seat? It seems too "upright to me" and I am afraid the head will be wobbling all the time.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "As long as the seat size is a good fit for your child it should be no problem. My son sleeps fine with his head resting on the side panels and his head does not wobble about. Again, just ensure that the seat is adjust properly for the child's size. If it's too upright, you can adjust it so that it props the child at a slight incline. hope this helps. We love this seat although during the first few days of use I thought about returning because it didn't feel as sturdy as the Frontier...but it feels perfect now."}
