{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1W6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370674800, 'question': 'Can a 13 month old use this car seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Mary, I am a certified Child Passenger Safety technician, and Safe Kids and the American Academy of Pediatrics recommend having your child in a rear facing car seat for two years at minimum, preferably to the height/weight limits of the convertible car seat. As this forward facing only car seat is intended for older children, Britax specifies that the child must be at least 2 years old and I believe 25 lbs to use this particular seat. I would recommend looking for a convertible car seat for your 13 month old. Hope that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1W6', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404198000, 'question': 'Is the center strap long enough for boys to be comfortable in the seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "My nine year old grandson uses one of these and loves it. His momma wants to keep him in a five point harness as long as she can because she feels they are safer than a booster. I have a 7 year old grandson who also uses one. I hear no complaints from either. Britax sells a special part that is used instead of the normal buckle between the legs. It is used when kids grow out of the harness and into the booster. It hooks onto the cars waist seat belt to keep children from submarining (sliding out the bottom under the waist seat belt. It is called the Britax SecureGuard Clip. (http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B004U5NVX4/ref=s9_simh_gw_p75_d0_i1?pf_rd_m=ATVPDKIKX0DER&pf_rd_s=center-2&pf_rd_r=13E3RXPY91QXN71XQYS5&pf_rd_t=101&pf_rd_p=1688200382&pf_rd_i=507846) My 9 year old grandson isn't looking forward to moving out of his Frontier 90 because he says it is so comfortable."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1W6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389686400, 'question': 'I just bought this. Does anyone know how to loosen the harness? I pressed the lever and tried to pull the harness but no move at all. solution?', 'answer': 'Buckle the chest piece then press the lever and pull on the chest piece. Both straps have to be pulled at the same time.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1W6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398150000, 'question': "my child still gets carsick even at 3 years, how do I wash the cover as I can't just wipe it clean, the smell would linger horribly!!", 'answer': "Take it off, all the covers can be removed, all BRITAX materials are to be used in laundry machine and dryer, I've washed the carrier and baby carrier, it did not loose any color, yes I've got to take them off from the Frontier 90, cause my 2 year old girl drinks too many liquids and the diaper got to it's limit so the seat also has a smell."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1W6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389772800, 'question': 'Britax Frontier 90 &#x441;an be set in the middle (center) of the rear seats? Or only the sides? For children of any Strength (weight) that chair?', 'answer': 'It could be placed in the center with a seat belt, as most vehicles do not have a center latch system (and you won\'t want to use latch anyhow when you see how easy and secure the seat straps in with the "click tight" technology.). However, this car seat is huge and I can\'t imagine you would be able to get a person on each side of it unless you drive a crazy huge vehicle. We drive an Odessey. We probably couldn\'t buckle it in the center if either the second or third row and still have room for the other passengers to be able to buckle, as the center seats are considerably smaller than a standard side seat.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1W6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390636800, 'question': 'What is the difference between the Frontier 90 and the Pioneer 90?', 'answer': 'The most important (I would argue) difference is the height maximums. The Frontier 90\'s highest harness position is 20.5" whereas the Pioneer 70\'s highest position is 18.5", on par with a lot of other combination seats out there. A lot of the time kids outgrow seats by height before weight - few kids would be able to use this seat harnessed all the way to 90 lbs or the Pioneer to 70 lbs. The Frontier, as the tallest combination seat on the market, is great for really tall kids but may be overkill for kids of more average or short stature. Great comparison: http://carseatblog.com/22545/review-of-the-britax-pioneer-70-a-pioneering-new-seat/'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1W6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390204800, 'question': 'Frontier 90 vs Pinnacle 90 ...which is WIDER, especially across the top OUTER dimensions? Looks like the Pinnacle is MUCH wider? Which do you like more?', 'answer': 'The pinnacle is wider.'}
