{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVSSWG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': "I bought this for my 8 mth old, but though he was sucking, he didn't seem to get any liquid out. Do you need the orange bit on the inside?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'That little cap you mean? That is for added leak protection when transporting the cup. You take it out to drink. When the spouts are new they take a little "breaking in" first. Pinch it a few times and also let some of the air out every so often. Hope that helps!'}
