{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2NY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397718000, 'question': 'Are the straps hard to tighten?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The straps are very easy to tighten if the seat is not installed. However, after you fasten the seat in the vehicle and the mechanism that snaps down to clamp to the vehicle's seatbelt is in place, then the straps are a little difficult to move. It is easy to make a small adjustment, but for a large adjustment in the strap length it is more difficult. So all that you need to do if you need to make a large adjustment in the strap length is to release the mechanism that clamps to the vehicle seatbelt and then make your adjustment and then put it back and put your child back in the seat to make the final adjustment. This may take 1 or 2 tries when you first install the seat but it is not a big deal. And this seat is so easy to install with the new mechanism that clamps down on the seatbelt that overall it will still save you time and effort to install over a conventional seat, even if you have to unclamp it from the vehicle seatbelt once or twice to make a strap length adjustment."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF2NY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390723200, 'question': 'Does the 5 point harness have a very long belt? Worried my son will quickly outgrow it. Can seatbelt be used instead of harness if that happens?', 'answer': 'Yes, the harness belt is long, however there is an age/weight limit on the use of the harness. After that limit is exceeded the car seat is used as a booster seat, utilizing the seat belt instead of the harness.'}
