{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1XU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392969600, 'question': "Has your child ever complained that the seat wasn't comfortable? My friend's daughter complains her butt hurts after a while. They have the older one.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "No, she hasn't complained. We took a long trip over this past weekend (5 hours each way) and she seemed comfortable the whole time."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1XU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392796800, 'question': 'is this seat better than all the rest?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "That is obviously a matter of personal opinion. However, this car seat is rated very well for safety and the majority seem to be very pleased with it. It is a heavier seat and I wouldn't recommend it being used for a seat that needs to be moved a lot. That's probably the only negative that I could come up with. I have 3 kids, have used many car seats, and this is by far, my absolute favorite."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1XU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382943600, 'question': 'How many years from the date of manufacture is the expiration date?', 'answer': 'Update: It is 9 years for Frontier 90. Found it in the user manual on the britax site. On page 2 it says: "To prevent injury due to deterioration or hidden damage, discontinue use of this child seat when it is older than nine years or has been in a moderate or severe crash. See Serial Number and Manufactured Date Label located on the child seat shell." http://www.britaxusa.com/uploads/products/user-guides/122.pdf I couldn\'t find information on expiration for Frontier 90, but managed to find out that older version called Frontier had expiration date set to 9 years from date of manufacture. http://www.britaxusa.com/car-seats/frontier'}
