{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1XU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403852400, 'question': "Can this seat be buckled into a middle seat using just a lap belt?I'll be using the harness but want to know if the lap belt will secure the base well", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes you can use a lap belt to install the seat using the 5pt harness. Lap belts only just aren't allowed when using it as a booster. :)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1XU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381734000, 'question': "I have this carseat and I'm wondering if other parents/grandparents have the problem of the child being able to reach over and unclasp the seatbelt?", 'answer': 'When I was deciding on a car seat, I purchased (and returned) 4 other seats, and this particular problem (being able to reach the seat-belt release) is a deficiency of all the seats I tried that have booster or shoulder belt convertibility. While my son did release it once, I came "unglued" and seem to have sufficiently scared him from ever touching the buckle again. Additionally, I found that if I have the harness tightened appropriately (making sure he only has 2 fingers of space) he can\'t reach it. The biggest deciding factor for me was that my son was unable to fully free himself once strapped in properly (he was able to loosen the straps on the other brands and unbuckle and then he was out!) The Frontier 90\'s harness strap release button is to far in for his fingers to reach it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BEVF1XU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394607600, 'question': "I have a hard time tightening my child's harness when she's seated. I pulled in all angles &amp; it's still really difficult. Is anyone else experiencing this?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I do find it more difficult than our other Britax. I always have to readjust the shoulder straps and make sure the chest piece is in correct position for it to tighten correctly. Pulling straight out is the only way it will work though. Good luck!'}
