{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYAO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384329600, 'question': 'What is the mattress made of? Is it non-toxic?', 'answer': "It's garbage. It reeks horribly... I believe it's got a polyurethane wrapping, which is responsible for the majority of the off-gassing. Big, giant notice stating that it meets CA flammability requirements, AKA it's chock full of flame retardant chemicals. Not at all non-toxic."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYAO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378623600, 'question': 'How much weight can it hold? Baby up to 20 pounds? 30 pounds? 40 pounds?', 'answer': "For co sleeper and bassinet modes the instructions say up to about 5 months or until baby can push himself up on hands and feet. Doesn't really give a weight limit per se but I would guess about 20lbs is the most you'd want to go."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYAO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391068800, 'question': 'Does this fold up like a pack n play?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. It folds up like a pack n play. It can be used as a crib, co-sleeper, play-yard, or pack n play. The front side slides up and down and locks in to place. We are really happy with it, except for the mattress. It says it comes with a mattress, but it is basically just the pad that would be used in a pack n play. You can get a decent mini mattress for it on amazon for about $30. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYAO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391155200, 'question': 'Anyone get the mattress un-stinked, or cover mattress w/ something to block smell? I want to love this thing but worry about the smell/gases. Thanks!', 'answer': "I hung mine up in a room with open window - it's still hanging there because we are not using it yet. If you are more worried about the gases, then perhaps it would be worth investing in organic mattress? I may do the same, just waiting to see if my kid actually ends up sleeping in this thing."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYAO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402470000, 'question': 'The measurements say 34 x 11 x 10 inches. Which portion is the height? My bed is 23" tall, so will the mattress of the cosleeper align w/ my mattress?', 'answer': 'Dear Lana & Peter K, the dimensions listed are apparently those of the shipping box. The height of the baby in the co-sleeper is at 20 inches. The height of our mattress is 26 inches and it worked just fine. Yours should line up even better. By the way, we found the co-sleeper a very helpful product.'}
