{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYAO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416816000, 'question': 'If you are laying in bed, can you slide the baby in and out to nurse? Or do you have to pick them up? Defeats the purpose if you have to sit up out of', 'answer': 'You do have to lift the baby from the co-sleeper but you don\'t have to fully sit up to do it. The mattress is a tad lower than the bed mattress. There is a bar/ cosleeper "wall" that keeps the baby from rolling into the crack between the mattresses. You cannot slide the baby necessarily... you can put the baby in your hands and slide onto bed but I wouldn\'t want to bump the head/back on the bar. It\'s really not hard.'}
