{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYDG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385712000, 'question': 'is the mattress of the co-sleeper at the same level as our mattress when it is connected? Or is the co-sleeper mattress offset from adult mattress height?', 'answer': 'We love our co sleeper. We used a mini with our daughter and the regular size one with our newborn twins. The mattress is at the same level as our mattress. We have a regular bed frame and it works perfectly for night feedings in terms if easily reaching our babies.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYCC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379919600, 'question': 'What is the weigh limit on this? The convertible aspect is nice, but how long would it last for a growing baby?', 'answer': 'The Co-Sleeper and bassinet modes are only for an infant up to approximately 5 months in age or when the child begins to push up on hands and knees, whichever occurs first. Move your child to another sleeping product when this stage is reached. The play-yard is for a child who cannot climb out and is less than 35" in height. If your bed is greater than 24" tall, a leg extension kit can be purchased at an additional cost. source--https://www.armsreach.com/shop/co-sleeper_bassinets/mini-arc-convertible'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYCC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384761600, 'question': 'Can this be attached to the bed?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes! There are straps that buckle to the sides of the CoSleeper. The straps go between te mattress and bedspring and are attached to a plate that allows the straps to be tightened so the CoSleeper is secure.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYCC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414306800, 'question': 'Is the top edge of the drop down side flush with the mattress ,so you can slide baby in and out? Or is there a lip you have to lift baby over?', 'answer': 'There is a lip u will have to lift the baby over. It is convenient and can be rolled to any part of ur home and fits in any corner. Glad we bought it!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYCC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384761600, 'question': 'Does this product include a mattress or a comfortable sleeping pad?', 'answer': "Yes, it includes a mattress pad with a fitted sheet. It's a bit hard though. I use another blanket on top of it, and tuck it under for added padding and comfort. This way, I also can change out the blanket if it gets dirty rather than buying more fitted sheets from Arms Reach, since I don't think its worth it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BFBUYCC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381474800, 'question': 'When the liner is removed, is there mesh siding so baby is visible? What is the point of the liner?', 'answer': 'For the play yard mode, yes. But while in co-sleeper/bassinet form, no. The purpose is partly aesthetics to cover the frame and padding at the top. Its nice though, because from inside, baby may be kept warmer and cozier since the liner extends down, not exposing her so much to light or cool air from the three sides. Its also washable so you can keep things clean'}
