{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BLBLR1I', 'answerTime': 'Sep 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378796400, 'question': "Where is the adapter that lets you dual pump. I got mine in from Amazon today and couldn't find the adapter anywhere in the box. Does it come with it", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'There is no adapter, there are 2 places to plug the tubes into- you simply remove the "clear plastic top" off of the bottom hole on the bottom of the machine. If you want to dual pump just plug each tube into the holes on the front of the machine- when you only want to pump one- just replace the "clear plastic top" back. Also note, this clear plastic will not fall off it is attached to the machine. I think the instructions in the box are out dated. I hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BLBLR1I', 'answerTime': 'Oct 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412146800, 'question': 'Does the milk go through the tubing like in the medela?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No it does not. It has a backflow filter that creates a barrier between the tubing and flanges. Since it is a closed system, you don't have to replace your tubing.. Unless you misplace them. But milk does get into the filter, so make sure you clean them. The filters are easily opened and closed, perfect for an easy cleaning. I recommend using babyganics foaming dish and bottle soap to clean the pump flanges, valves, bottles, and filters. It gets the residue off and rinses clean. I also use a skinny nipple cleaner (I buy the cheap babies r us brand skinny nipple cleaners) to get any gunk out of the part that connects the filter and breast pump (if you purchase it you'll see what I'm talking about). I also recommend boiling your parts or using a steam sterilizer bag to kill off any bacteria every other day or weekly. Also, if you ever lose your valves or rip them, and need to replace them ASAP the Medela valves and membranes are compatible with the spectra S1, S2, M1, and 9 breast pump flanges. If you decide to purchase this breastpump, first check with your insurance if you are eligible to receive a free breastpump covered by your insurance. Call and ask to see if your insurance company's DME supplier for breast pumps is Edgepark medical. Edgepark carries the S2 model and the 9+ model. I'm sorry if this is lengthy, just wanting to make this as clear as possible to understand."}
