{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BM9MJNE', 'answerTime': 'Dec 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388131200, 'question': 'I was going to buy a breast pump until I realized that I can get one for free through my insurance. Is this pump as good as the Medela Pump in Style Advanced? Is the tote kind of ugly?', 'answer': "Good evening I would like to start by saying we sell hundreds of Madella pumps a year and to be honest with you they are basically all the exact same motor. The only difference usually is the style of the bag. Typically the insurance companies will give you the not a stylish brown lunchbox style tote or the one listed above with the cooler. The ones the people are typically purchasing now are the metro bag which is more stylish and looks like a large diaper bag and serve the dual purpose of diaper bag as well as pump but does not look like a pokey hospital style pump What's also convenient about the metro bag is that the pump is in its own little lunch bag style size told that is removable and you can use it for portable pumping in your home your vehicle or wherever you choose to pump without having to carry large awkward tote looks like a big beach cooler. If you have any additional questions please feel free to contact us if you're looking for a stylish pump we have many in stock somewhere listed and some are not yet listed. Thank you very much the baby Depot"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BM9MJNE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382252400, 'question': 'What kind of car adaptor do I need to get for this pump?', 'answer': 'I have this pump. Per the user manual you need to purchase the 9V medela car adapter. The 12V is only for pumps purchased earlier than 2008.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BM9MJNE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411282800, 'question': 'Is this a closed system? Can I buy this used without risk of bacteria from previous user transferring to my milk?', 'answer': 'As Ashley said, this is a single user pump and should not be transferred.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BM9MJNE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393401600, 'question': 'What accessories would you recommend to buy with this or are non necessary?', 'answer': 'I would buy extra membranes. They are very thin and can break easily. Plus you probably need to replace them every few months. I have found if my production starts going down and I change the membranes, it goes back up. I would also get a good hands free pumping bra. Mine did not come with a nipple for the bottles, so you would need that to feed a baby, and you would need extra bottles for the baby. http://www.amazon.com/Medela-Spare-Membranes-Breatpumps-Pack/dp/B0001CTZ8K/ref=sr_1_2?ie=UTF8&qid=1393430032&sr=8-2&keywords=medela+membranes'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BM9MJNE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389081600, 'question': 'Does this use the same tubes and breast shields as the Symphony and Lactina?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes and no. The symphony and lactina require an adapter on the end of the tubing, whereas this does not. If you rent a symphony or lactina, all that you need to do is cut that end off the tubing, and it is good to use on this pump. The breast shields are the same.'}
