{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BR0OMG0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393488000, 'question': 'Are the Graco Nautilus car seats being sold today (Feb 27, 2014) on Amazon come with the new (non-recalled) buckles?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'My guess is that it is unlikely as it would be based upon production date. The good news is that the problem only occurs after a child has spilled food and drink on the buckle. If you plan to order, I would go ahead and visit the Graco site. All you have to do is enter the style carseat you have and they will mail a replacement out right away.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BR0OMG0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393228800, 'question': 'Is it under recall?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The buckle, and only the buckle, is under recall. According to the Graco recall notice: "As part of our continuous product testing and improvement process, Graco identified that food and dried liquids that can make some harness buckles progressively more difficult to open over time or become stuck in the latched position. Therefore, we have decided to conduct a voluntary recall on the harness buckles used on all toddler convertible car seats and harnessed booster seats. Graco would like to stress this does not in any way affect the performance of the car seat or the effectiveness of the buckle to restrain the child. And a car seat is always the safest way to transport your child." If you go to the manufacturer website there is a link to read the notice and see pictures of the buckles to determine if you have one of the new or the old (recalled) buckles. If you happen to get an old buckle, there is a link to order a replacement. That being said, we have a seat with that buckle we bought in 2009. We keep it clean, and have never had a problem. Our daughter has never had a problem opening it herself. We actually prefer the old design and might stick with it anyway. A link to the recall announcement with more info: http://www.pages02.net/newellrubbermaid/harness-buckles'}
