{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BUO4664', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393574400, 'question': 'Is this product part of the recall on FP rock n play sleepers?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The only recall I'm familiar with is because of possible mold growth under the padded seat. It's not like the sleeper collapsed or something dangerous. There's a thin material covering the hard plastic contoured support piece. If your kid messes in the rocker, you throw the washable pad in the laundry and CLEAN UP the rest if it soaked through! My son spit-up like nobody's business, and I never had a problem with this item. I cleaned it with baby-safe disinfectants etc. and let it air dry while the pad was in the laundry! You could always place a disposable or washable waterproof mat between the plastic piece and the padded seat."}
