{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BWIPD42', 'answerTime': 'Dec 16, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387180800, 'question': "Has anyone used this for the 1st time with a toddler? I'm worried my 2-yr old will be afraid to sleep in this since she's never been in one before.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We used for the first time with a fifteen month old. She was happy to crawl inside. We left the side overs open so she could see out and provided comfy bedding inside. Also a hint...leave zipper open enough to slip a hand in to adjust blankets on sleeping child without waking them with sound of opening zipper'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPD42', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': 'How did you get your child used to sleeping in it before actually using it or did you not have any issues and he/she slept as usual in it?', 'answer': 'We just took a chance and had our 13 month old sleep in it for the first time on a vacation. Luckily it worked out. I would suggest starting with nap time to get your kiddo used to it just to be on the safe side, especially if your dealing with a fairly young child.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BWIPD42', 'answerTime': 'Apr 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397458800, 'question': 'I have twins. Could they share this for awhile?[', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Absolutely perfect for two. My grandsons, 4 & 2 share all the time. They are both pretty wiggly but there is really no problem. It has been a safe & comfy & familiar, fun place for them to sleep while camping or visiting. We love it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPD42', 'answerTime': 'May 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399878000, 'question': 'Is the weight/size worth carrying around South East Asia for 19month old (and possibly 6yr old brother?) Would they both fit for a nap?', 'answer': 'Two kids of any age most definitely would not fit in comfortably. I have doubts that a 6yr old would fit in alone.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPD42', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403766000, 'question': 'Can this also be used on the beach or outdoors for playing/napping?', 'answer': "Yes, it's perfect for that. Easy to clean and folds down quickly."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPD42', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392537600, 'question': 'How do you clean it if a child wets inside?', 'answer': 'The fabric is the same as any tent fabric. I have thankfully not had to clean it yet, but I would recommend spot cleaning with a mild soap and water.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'age limits?', 'answer': 'I would think any age limit up to small children. I bought this for my 2 year old granddaughter, when my kids were visiting from the UK. My 6 year old grandson was able to comfortably climb in, because he thought it was fun. The bed was perfect for containing my granddaughter and her sleep toys for her naps and nighttime.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'I have a tall 2.5 year old...will she fit comfortably in here? Going on a trip in a month and she still sleeps in a crib. Need something small for plane travel.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "My daughter used this until she was almost 5 and she is tall as well...granted her head rubbed the top of the tent by then when she sat up :) We still have it because she still likes to lay in it sometimes. It's so easy to fold and basically pops open on it's own when you pull it out. The only downside is that it's not very cushioned on the bottom so for Disney we put the tent on a folded blanket to pad the bottom. Hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422259200, 'question': 'Does this lay flat on the ground?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It lays as flat as the floor it's on. If you pop it up inside, it's perfectly flat. If you pop it up outside (which I don't think is recommended) it conforms to the curves and bumps of the ground."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'Nov 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416816000, 'question': "Would a 2 yr old be able to unzip it from the inside. I'm trying to keep him safe at night. (He climbs out of everything and over the babygate.)", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes! It has a double zipper so it can be opened and closed from both the inside and outside.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407308400, 'question': 'What kind of sheet do you use with this?', 'answer': "We don't use a sheet, we just wipe it down with a baby wipe every now and then"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'Is this the peapod plus? It does not list it as plus in the description and it is priced similarly to the plus models? Please advise. Thank you.', 'answer': "That's a very good question! I bought the kiwi one for my grandsons (age 1 and 2) and seems plenty big enough. The Amazon website says this s 28 x 46 x 18 ... same as it said on every other color I checked. But on the blue one, the Amazon site says that size, but what appears to me to be the same one is listed on an outside website as 34 x 52 x 25. I don't have it with me to measure, so not really sure if there are still two sizes or not ... may want to check with the manufacturer to be sure. I thought the difference between the two was that one was for infants, but I don't understand the price differences on the colors on Amazon."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'May 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400914800, 'question': 'Are the dimensions of the Peapod Plus the same as the Peapod? If not, what are the dimensions?', 'answer': 'The peapod plus is larger than the regular. Our special needs 6 year old was comfortable sleeping in it during our vacation. Open Dimensions: 52.5&#8243;L x 34&#8243;W x 25&#8243;H Storage Bag Dimensions: 19&#8243;L x 3.5&#8243;W x 19&#8243;H'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': 'After the voluntary recall did pea pod remanufacture the products or did they simply leave the same product on marketplace and issue kits to everyone', 'answer': 'My understanding is that the pad/mattress thing used to be inside the tent. It is now fastened to the bottom, outside of the tent.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'Oct 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381820400, 'question': 'Is there a way to attach a mobile or any hanging toy to the "ceiling" of the Peapod? If so, does anyone have any recs for such mobiles/toys?', 'answer': "There isn't anything provided for attaching such. The material is thin and may get ripped if you did so. But it's possible with a safety pin or like. My 1 yr old lives it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BWIPC6G', 'answerTime': 'Aug 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377586800, 'question': 'what is the difference in the peapod and the peapod plus?', 'answer': 'There are several differences. The Plus has: Two zipper panels for easy access (instead of just 1) Inner mesh zipper panel keeps bugs out Adjustable window screens The bag dimensions are different. The plus is: Bag dimensions: 3.5"W x 19"H x 19"L Unfolded dimensions: 34"W x 25"H x 52.5"L And is for ages: 1 to 5 years old The Peapod is: Bag dimensions: 3"W x 16.5"H x 16.5"L Unfolded dimensions: 28"W x 18"H x 46"L and is for ages: 1 to 3 years old'}
