{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C0XNITU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415865600, 'question': 'Can you set the display to show the clock only, without a sun or moon?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C0XNITU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383030000, 'question': 'Does the awake setting have a blue light or a yellow light? When does the awake light turn off?', 'answer': 'The awake light is yellow (or you can place the sleeping disc on the clock and it will look blue). You can go into sleep mode at anytime by hitting the "GS" button or go to sleep button. This will start a 10 minute timer and the sun will slowly set. You can also go into immediate sleep mode and bypass this with the top switch. My daughter loves the sun setting feature and in the morning she watches the moon setting 10 minutes before the wake up time we set. In fact the only slight negative I would say is that she has figured out how to put it on the alarm mode (she just turned 3) because she likes to be woken up by the birds chirping (you pick the sound). This is not always ideal if you want your child to wake up naturally or sleep in! But we love this clock and highly recommend!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C0XNITU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386144000, 'question': 'How do you turn alarm and/or melody sound off?', 'answer': 'The alarm only comes on if you move the switch above the digital clock all the way to the right. If you just want the picture to change with no sound, you put the switch in the middle.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C0XNITU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416470400, 'question': 'Please help! I have the same question as some others, the button is moved to the center "on" position, yet the clock is always blue with the moon ?', 'answer': "When you turn it 'on' by moving the button to center it turns to the moon/sleep mode. The sun comes up at your set wakeup time. If you are trying to do the 10 minute countdown with the sun going down, move the button to center position, then push and hold the blue button on the larger part of the clock (2nd from the top). Hold until the sun pops up for the countdown. The other button will play music."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C0XNITU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389945600, 'question': 'Just received clock. Set to current time &amp; set wakeup times. However, the display keeps showing the sleeping bunny &amp; LCD display shows moon. Why??', 'answer': 'If its the first time it will show the moon until the wake up time, then it will switch to the sun.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C0XNITU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1430118000, 'question': "What is the difference between this newer $50 model and the older $40 one? We have the old one for my son's room and love it, but now we need a 2nd.", 'answer': 'I am not to sure I have the one pictured and the thing I love the most about this clock is the timer. We set it for 10 minutes and I lay with the kids and rub their backs until the timer goes off , which is a very pretty sound. The kids don\'t fight with me they know it\'s time for mommy to leave the room. We also set it for 730 am and they know when the "Choo Choo" train goes off its time to get up. My 5 yr old uses the day and night as a way to tell the time as my 7 yr old uses the actual clock to tell the time. So this clock really works for my age groups. I hope this helps.'}
