{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392105600, 'question': 'Can you tell me what the seated height is, from seat to the top harness postion, and from seat to top , please?', 'answer': "17 in from top harness to seat--15 inches from lower harness to seat--27 inches from top of chair to seat--and 29 inches from the top of batmans head to seat. the seat itself is 10 inches wide at the back. it's been a great seat for us-- hope this helps"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404630000, 'question': 'Can this car seat sit rear facing in the back seat?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This car seat is designed as a forward facing booster seat only.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Jul 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406185200, 'question': 'Is this seat easy enough for a 3 year old to buckle themselves into the harness?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Well I'm sure a 3 yr old could possibly buckle themselves in, but I highly recommend an adult doing it for the safety of the child to make sure they are properly secured. Personally I would never let my 3 1/2 yr old grandson do this for himself, 3yr olds cannot possibly understand the importance of this. Wow I can't even believe someone asked this question, I'm a little concerned for the 3 yr old being allowed to do his own seat buckle."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378710000, 'question': 'How many pounds does it hold?', 'answer': 'This car seat accommodate kids 22 to 65 lbs, booster seat fits 30 to 100 lbs.'}
