{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428390000, 'question': 'Will this seat suit my child until a car seat is no longer required?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'My grandson will be 5 soon and loves it!! It sits lower than a regular seat, more like a booster seat. Should work until child is old enough or large enough to not be in safety seat'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427612400, 'question': 'Does it recline?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'Unfortunately, the seat does not recline'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426230000, 'question': 'The bottom latch is very hard to open on our seat, even for an adult, does anyone else have this problem?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, it is VERY hard to open. Sometimes I spend minutes trying to unlatch it and almost panic that I can't get my son out. The size of the latch is much smaller than Britax I have had. The other thing is that the straps are too short. My son, who is just 6, cannot wear his winter jacket as he doesn't fit, and he is a skinny kid. Other than the Batman coolness of it, I would not recommend buying this."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425884400, 'question': 'will this car seat fit in smaller cars such as the Chevy Cruse?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Oh yes! We have a jeep grand Cherokee that we bought it for but we also had a mustang. It fit perfectly and they have NO room in the back seat. Also just some added info, this is our second one. We were in a really bad car accident in the mustang. The other car T boned us right were my son and I were, I walked away with a lot of problems and all my little guy got was a scratch on his ear. It by far is the safest carseat we have ever owned. You eony be sorry :) good luck!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2JKUAC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425283200, 'question': "How big can a child be and still wear the harness? I have a special needs 5 1/2 year old and she needs to be harnessed in. She's pretty tall.", 'answer': 'They said up to 100 lbs.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3II', 'answerTime': 'Nov 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385280000, 'question': 'Can I use this as a co-sleeper for a newborn next to my bed? First time mom here.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes! I use it next to my bed every night with my baby. This is a wonderful bed!! I have been using this since my baby was two months old and my only regret is that I didn't get it sooner! She refused to sleep on her own and I had to hold her. That led to many sleepless nights! The first night in this bed we saw a difference. I am also a first time mom. I'm glad I found this bed!!!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3II', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392019200, 'question': 'Is the color in these pictures accurate? Everywhere else I look its bright pink', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The color in the first picture is accurate! Definitely not bright pink. I use this for my son and it doesn't look girly at all."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3II', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': "Why would this cause a baby's head to be flat more so than a normal crib?", 'answer': "As others said, maybe because it limits baby's ability to move freely. I noticed our little one has his head tilted down when he sleeps so its different position than a crib but it worked wonders for his acid reflux and he can sleep up 9 hrs in it. I think the important thing is to not overuse all the devices with baby on their backs like car seats, swings etc etc and that they get enough tummy time to avoid flat head."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3II', 'answerTime': 'Mar 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395126000, 'question': "How tall is this sleeper when it's set up?", 'answer': "23 inches and it's great to have"}
