{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3II', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421049600, 'question': "How stable is the Rock n' Play? I worry that our cats might tip it over. (Obviously would supervise to the best of our ability, but... still...)", 'answer': 'It only rocks back and forth not side to side so it is very stable our big dog bumps it every once in awhile and it hardly moves'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3FG', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401260400, 'question': 'If you have the baby sleep in this at night next to the bed, do you use the restraint or just set the baby in like you would in a bassinet?', 'answer': "I usually use the restraint. Whether it is necessary or not, I don't know, but it gives me peace of mind."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3FG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390636800, 'question': 'Does this rock only with a push from mom, or does is have automated rocking action?', 'answer': 'It only rocks when pushed... But it does have the vibration feature which is soothing for our babies. I place the Rock n" Play by me, and rock with my hand, or it\'s easily rocked with my foot.'}
