{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3FG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 12, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423728000, 'question': 'I have very tall 2 month old. Baby loves it, but now feel legs are way too crunched up at the bottom. How many inches is too tall for nightly sleep?', 'answer': "I'm not sure, but our pediatrician told us not to let our baby sleep in it much past 2-3 months. She said she had seen patients that flipped and rocked out of it. Our baby loved it too, but at about 3 months, we transitioned to the pack and play for about a month or so, then the crib."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3FG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421222400, 'question': 'How long was your baby when she/he outgrew this? Our 3-month boy is below the weight limit but is almost 25 inches. Thanks!', 'answer': 'My son still uses it but he is failure to thrive so is still pretty small for 18 months. 18 lbs. And he is 25 inches long and still fits comfortable Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3FG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391328000, 'question': 'Is anyone continuing to have mold or find water in the sleeper as mentioned in the 2013 recall? Is this product in any way improved since the recall?', 'answer': "I've never had a problem with mold. At first I was making sure to wash the cover weekly but even now I don't and no problems. I also usually have my baby on a blanket over the cover not sure if that makes a difference and I also put a receiving blanket behind where her head lays so its not too hard. I love this sleeper and so doesn't my baby. I wish I had this since the day we brought her home from the hospital! I forgot to mention I got this when she was around a month old and she is now 4 1/2 months old."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3FG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391155200, 'question': "Does this have a hard plastic lining in the seat or is it all fabric? I'm concerned about baby getting a flat spot on the back of the head.", 'answer': 'Yes, it does have a hard plastic lining. Some people say their babies developed a flat spot but my daughter never did and she slept in this until 4 months due to reflux. I used a head support sometimes that had a hole cut out to help prevent a flat spot. Believe its by boppy brand.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3FG', 'answerTime': 'May 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1430463600, 'question': 'Are there any flame retardants in this product?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Being that item for sleep and that there are regulations in place requiring flame retardants in sleepwear and other items I'm going to assume there very well may be but your best bet is to contact fisher price"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C2KW3FG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427094000, 'question': 'Is this a good option for travel (instead of a pack n play)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I would highly recommend this for travel. Unless you need something to let the little one play in, I would pick this over the pack n play. My little one sleeps better in the rocker than she ever did in the pack n play and you don't have to worry about the assembly either."}
