{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C7JW2R6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392883200, 'question': 'Do you have to change the shell every time you change a insert?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. You should change the shell when you change the insert. This is a pocket diaper. The insert goes in a pocket, and that touches the baby\'s skin. This "pocket" also gets wet or poo on it, so it should be changed. There are 2 inserts per diaper. I have found one is great for daytime and 2 gets me through the night! If you want a diaper that you reuse the shell, I would recommend either the flip system or econobum. Both are great. I have noticed that I almost always have to change the shell as well. EBF poo, rarely misses the leg gussets on diapers, or so is my experience. I would not recommend best bottom. I have used the newborn alva pockets with a g-diaper insert layed on top of the pocket. I can then take the insert out and reuse the shell. I have been able to get a couple of diaper changes out of one that way, but this is not what is intended, and I would not use the included microfiber insert for this purpose.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C7JW2R6', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': 'Anybody used these successfully on a newborn?', 'answer': 'My newborn was a little early. He was only 5 lbs. That being said we put him in them about 1 month in. He may have been about 7 lbs'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C7JW2R6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411455600, 'question': 'How many do you need? I just started with the 6 and feel I have to wash them every other day', 'answer': "If you cd full time, and want to wash no more than every other day, I would recommend starting with 18 on hand. I like 20-24 better, it gives more room for washing-that way you don't have to wait until the last diaper change of the night before washing. A baby should/needs to be changed at least every 2 hours during the day in any diaper-but especially with cd. This may vary with older children. If you have too many diapers it may encourage you to put off washing them to a third or fourth day which will allow for bacteria to grow and a lot of smell to build up in the diapers."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C7JW2R6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416470400, 'question': 'how do i change my baby with these diapers? How does the process go?', 'answer': 'The diapers come we with inserts that you just remove and wash...u can Google tutorials of detergent to use as well as care instructions'}
