{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00C7JW3GQ', 'answerTime': 'Nov 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385020800, 'question': 'Are these good for newborns on up?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, I used disposables for the first couple of weeks, because I couldn't figure out how to size the diaper correctly. Then I found a video on YouTube that showed how to do it, and they worked well for my daughter after that. She was about 9 lbs at that point."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C7JW3GQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409209200, 'question': "Are these standard sizes or a new born can grow in? I am going to deliver my first baby in 2 weeks and don't know if these are the right size to buy.", 'answer': 'These do snap down in width AND in length, so, yes, they will fit a newborn. It will look a bit "overwhelming" on the newborn for a week or two...just because babies are so tiny when they are born. but, you should have a good fit if the baby is average newborn weight. if the baby is 8 pounds or so, you are good :) 5 pounds...gonna be awful big :/'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00C7JW3GQ', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': 'can you use the gro-via or any other brand of disposable liners with these?', 'answer': "I don't use disposable liners so I can't answer your question easily. What I can say is that these are just like any other pocket diapers. So if you can use the liners you wish to use with pocket diapers (say bumgenius, blueberry, hero, etc) then you can use those liners with these diapers."}
