{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CCA025O', 'answerTime': 'Nov 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385452800, 'question': 'I am a Grandmother buying a monitor for first time. I read reviews &amp; several of the mothers bought extra equipment. What extra equipment do I need to buy?', 'answer': 'I like this monitor, however I had problems with the first one I ordered. I ordered a new one and at times the screen will display broken images. Almost like the Monitor has damage. Not sure how else to describe it to you. I have to turn it off and turn it back on to get it to work properly. As for the extra equipment, we never purchased anything other than what came with the monitor. Good luck! and Congratulations!!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CCA025O', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385971200, 'question': 'Can you put the monitor on "sleep" mode while on the charger? So I can still hear sound but not have the video on all night until baby makes a sound?', 'answer': 'Yes, the middle button on the top of the monitor turns the picture on or off while on the charger. That way you can just use audio at night. We find it is too bright to have the video running all night. When you hear them and would like to see them again just press the button again to turn the picture back on. Hope this helps!'}
