{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CFWVJ5Q', 'answerTime': 'Jun 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403074800, 'question': 'Where is this made?', 'answer': 'The rubber for this product is 100% hevea natural sap from the hevea tree which comes from Malaysia. The product, design and packaging, story book and audio version are designed in Australia and the USA, and our supplier who assembled everything is from China. The product took over 1 year to design and make and our supplier is Certified ISO 90001:2008 Process-based Quality Management Standard. ISO 9001 was originally designed (1987) to set management system requirements for business quality, specifically quality in manufacturing. It was revised in 1994, 2000 and 2008 and now is used for manufacturing and services. It is now in use world-wide by over 1 million organizations in order to provide consistent quality products that are meeting customer requirements. ISO 9001:2008 is built around eight Quality Management System (QMS) principles to increase the focus on management commitment, customer satisfaction and continuous improvement.'}
