{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CM8OZ6I', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389254400, 'question': 'How do I know what size to buy? S, M+, L, XL', 'answer': 'We are the manufacturer of this product. First, measure the diameters of your nipples. If you don\'t know how to measure it, follow maymom.com/nippleruler to make yourself a nipple ruler. Knowing these data, the general rules of thumb are that the inner diameter of the breast shield should be 2-3 millimeter larger than your nipple diameter. Example: the diameter of your nipple is 23 mm, then choose the M+ (25mm) or L- (26mm) breasthields. Furthermore, please also try the following check list to find the best one for you. Center the nipple in the tunnel of the breastshield. Now begin pumping and check the following points: Is your nipple moving freely in the tunnel? Is none or only very little tissue of the areola being pulled into the tunnel of the breastshield? Do you recognize gentle, rhythmic movements in the breast at each pump cycle? Do you feel the breast emptying all over? Is your nipple free of pain? With the above check list, a mother can easily assess whether she is using the right Breastshield size. All points should be "true", then you have the right size of breastshield. A correctly fitted breastshield prevents the milk ducts from being compressed, thus enabling an optimal emptying of the breast and maximum milk output when pumping. This helps mothers to maintain their milk production and supports lactation. It also prevents chaffing and tenderness of around the nipple area.'}
