{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CP86TVY', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': 'Is this a two channel system? One camera in each room, can switch to see other child?', 'answer': "Yes. You can have up to 4 different cameras on one monitor. I have a camera in each of my boys' rooms, and i can set it to watch only one if the other isn't in bed, or have it it switch back and forth on an interval. You can also set it to sleep after a minute if the baby is quiet, and then come back on if they cry or cough or make noise."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CP86TVY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384934400, 'question': "Does the monitor have a normal charging cord? The monitor I'm replacing goes into a charging base instead of a cord, &amp; 2 of them have broken b/c of it", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It does have a plug in cord. If you don't use the video continually the battery lasts a long while. My biggest complaint is the attached stand on the monitor is very flimsy and we have broken it 3 times. The warrently replaced it twice."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CP86TVY', 'answerTime': 'May 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400655600, 'question': 'Does this have pan/ tilt/ zoom?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You can tilt the camera manually. No pan or zoom. I have two cameras for two grandchildren. It is a very nice unit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CP86TVY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': 'What kind of range do you have?', 'answer': "I have a 2400 sq ft home; the cameras are in the kids' rooms on one end of the upstairs. Our bedroom is on the other end, and we get reception all over the house. No problems. As far as outside of the house goes, i don't know yet because it has been so cold here. When it is nice, I can leave the youngest down for naps while the oldest and I go play outside or work in the garden. Don't know if this monitor will reach that far or not, yet."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CP86TVY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426402800, 'question': "Can you leave the camera function on all the time? I'd like to view my baby at all times. Also, do the cameras need to be charged?", 'answer': 'Yes you can. I leave my camera plugged into wall outlet 24/7'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CP86TVY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424419200, 'question': "Can you turn the video off and only have the sound, I'd like to do this at night while I slept.", 'answer': "You can turn the video off but when the baby starts crying it will light up. I have had to turn the face down when I don't need the video"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CP86TVY', 'answerTime': 'Feb 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422777600, 'question': 'If I use this for 2 kids, will the monitor automatically switch to the camera that senses noise, or will I have to switch channels manually?', 'answer': 'You have to switch it manually and it is a few clicks to switch it, not just one.'}
