{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CS8E0G2', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398582000, 'question': 'how easy is it to was the fabric,remove tray and fold it?', 'answer': "Cleaning the fabric is pretty easy, but there are some spots where the bottom meets the back of the seat that food can sometimes hide. Removing the fabric to do complete wash is possible, but not something that I plan on doing since it takes so long to put back on.(It's a very snug fit on the chair) I don't completely latch the tray when I put it on, because if you latch it all the way (like my husband does) it's incredibly hard to get off. But if you're sitting there with them, it stays just fine without any extra effort. Folding and unfolding is a breeze, and extremely helpful. That's the feature that sold us on this. It folds up small enough, that is can fit in the space between our couch and wall."}
