{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CXPYWCC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389686400, 'question': "So are these reuseable or you throw them away after feedings? Seems like a total waste if it's the latter, and expensive?!", 'answer': 'You throw them away. If you are going to use the whole system I feel its worth the money. The cost for 50 medela pump and freeze bags (which also get thrown away) is 15.99 for 50, the twist pouches are 17.99 for 40 so I dont feel like the cost is terrible. And I have no more dishes and no more transferring of bags and i need alot less storage since I only use 4 nipples and 2 "bottles". So for a few extra dollars, for me,the convenience and ease of using the entire twist system is worth it. If you only are using them to store, then yes they would be a waste.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CXPYWCC', 'answerTime': 'May 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400569200, 'question': 'Breast milk bottles and bags storage are covered by FSA, are these pouches FSA eligible?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This is a great question that we get from time to time. We're not accountants or tax experts, but based on the web, it looks like they should be (I found a few links that suggest this is the case) http://www.parenting.com/blogs/show-and-tell/melanie-parentingcom/irs-rules-breastfeeding-supplies-tax-deductible http://fsastore.wordpress.com/2013/08/02/flexible-spending-account-world-breastfeeding-week/ and the primary source : http://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-drop/a-11-14.pdf good luck! -kiinde support"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CXPYWCC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416729600, 'question': 'Can anyone recommend a cooler bag/pack that fits well with this system? Will need it for back to work time. Thank you!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I have been using my insulated lunch box with a reuse able ice pack in it. It has worked great so far. The bags don't leak and don't take up a whole bunch of space. I pump at lunch so the food leaves and the bags go in."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CXPYWCC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'Without purchasing the adapters, will these pouches fit a madela breast pump? Looking at the picture it looks as tho they would....', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have the madela pump and I use these pouches. They don't screw in directly but all you have to do pour it in from the madela bottle that came with the pump. It's only an additional 10 seconds. Also the measurements on these pouches aren't so good so I would recommend using the madela bottle anyway."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CXPYWCC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411542000, 'question': 'Has anyone figured out a good system for direct pumping into the pouch in regards to how much you fill the bag up with to not be wasteful of the bags?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I typically pump 4-6 oz at a time so I only hook one side up with the bag, the other I pump into a bottle then dump the bottle into the bag- saves bags and the kiddo gets a "full feeding" from one twist bag.'}
