{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CXSPL24', 'answerTime': 'May 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400050800, 'question': "If you pump into the bags, and don't get much (like an ounce), can you later reattach the bag and pump more in? Or do you need to use a new bag?", 'answer': "Maggie...you can't, because you can't add your warm breast milk to cold breast milk (so I've read). What I do if I have a bag I want to fill more is I pump into a bottle, then put that in the fridge to cool and then when they are the same temperature in the fridge, dump the contents of the bottle into the bag."}
