{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00D04R2JA', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377154800, 'question': 'Does the seat attach using the LATCH system?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It does have LATCH. However, LATCH has a 40 pound weight limit, so once your child is 40 pounds, you have to use a seat belt. Also, it has only one LATCH belt, like a typical car seat, where the Marathon, Advocate, and other Britax convertibles have two independent latch belts (one on each side attached to the steel integrated bars). This has a single strap, with a LATCH buckle on each end.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00D04R2JA', 'answerTime': 'Oct 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382598000, 'question': 'what is the exact difference between this and the frontier 90 besides the weight. can someone please explain the latch and the seat belt detail plz', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Frontier 90 has higher weight and height limits. The back raises up for a taller kid. The latch system to hook in the car is the same on both models. The hugs system on the straps ae different. The frontier had the hugs and the pioneer doesn't. The hugs are the plastic sleeves over the chest straps where it buckles on the chest. It is supposed to help in crash force absorption. I have found that it helps with the straps not getting tangled and it looks for comfortable for my son. We had it on the britax marathon we had. I didn't feel that it was worth the extra money for the frontier or those few things. I've been very happy with my choice of the pioneer. Although I do miss the hugs. Hope this helps you."}
