{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00D04R3LW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': 'What are the key differences between the Pioneer and the Frontier?', 'answer': "The Frontier has more padding and is generally a more comfortable seat, but most importantly, it has the click-tight technology whereas the Pioneer does not. I found the Pioneer very hard to install using the seat belt (which you must use instead of the latch connectors for children over 40 pounds). I could not get a secure install and it was not an easy. I returned the Pioneer the same day I tried to install it in my car. The Frontier is more expensive, but worth it. It installs in minutes, and is rock solid, doesn't move an inch. I wrote a review of the Pioneer (one star) which you can read that has more info."}
