{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00D04R2MC', 'answerTime': 'Jun 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402124400, 'question': "My car doesn't have latch. Can it still be installed if using as a car seat and not a booster seat?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You can install this seat using the car seat belt (instead of latch), and in fact the manual says that you should use the car seat belt if your child is over 40 pounds even if you do have latch. HOWEVER, I installed this seat using the seat belt in my husband's car and it was not secure at all. I actually returned the seat and got one with click tight. I highly recommend getting a Britax 90 or another model with click tight. It is very easy to install these using the seatbelt and they are extremely secure (seat dosen't budge at all!)."}
