{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00D04R2L8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415520000, 'question': 'This seat is the only booster with the secure safe guard for the belt buckle. Is it really worth while to purchase this seat for that security alone? Or are other booster seats just as safe without it?', 'answer': 'In my opinion it is of essential value in the specific instance of a thin child. It keeps the child from sliding under the lap belt in a severe accident. It keeps the lap belt positioned correctly over the hips in a minor accident. Larger and wider children would not benefit as much.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00D04R2L8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387353600, 'question': "My 27-month babygirl weighs about 35lbs and 3' tall. Does this fit for her?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'She may be a little short for this carseat. Even if it would fit her, I would highly recommend keeping her in a seat with a five point harness until she is at least 4. We started using this seat when our daughter was about 4 and a 1/2, and even then preferred the Britax seats with a five point harness because they keep her much more secure while in the seat.'}
