{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00D2JN87I', 'answerTime': 'Sep 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380351600, 'question': 'what does a shusher sound like ?any way to hear it we have been using a hair dryer', 'answer': 'It sounds like someone going "shhhhhhhhhh" in a long, drawn out way. There is a momentary pause between each "shush" so it is not a continuous sound like the hair dryer. When my baby is really upset, nothing is as effective as the hair dryer. Period. But the shusher is obviously more convenient--no cord, no blowing air, etc. I like the shusher but at this point, I use the HoMedics Sound Spa on the Go even more--the white noise function can be turned up loud and it\'s small enough to go with us anywhere. Plus, unlike the shusher, I can attach it to her car seat. And it\'s 1/3 the price. Just my two cents...'}
