{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DJPLS2W', 'answerTime': 'Feb 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392364800, 'question': 'How long can it record for on the 2GB SD card? And does anyone know if it can use a bigger SD card? Thinking about times when you have a babysitter.', 'answer': "I've never used this feature on the monitor, but if the SD card is the same size, but larger memory then I can't see why it would record for longer times. The one thing I would think would be a drawback is that the camera isn't motion activated. For instance I have my camera pointed to where I can see inside the crib. If the babysitter would go out of view of the camera, then you wouldn't be recording anything of importance. The good thing about this monitor however, is that you can have up to three cameras connect to the video monitor which will allow you more flexibility, but again if they go out of range of the camera then it won't do you much good. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DJPLS2W', 'answerTime': 'Jul 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404889200, 'question': 'Does this monitor have VOX mode? An out of range indicator? A low battery indicator?', 'answer': 'It does not have a VOX mode. When out of range, the screen goes black and the lights around the buttons will blink indicating it is out of range. When the battery is low, it will beep.'}
