{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DJPLS2W', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421827200, 'question': 'How do you put the sd card in? I have had this for a while and have never figured it out. :/', 'answer': 'Sure! In the handset remove the cover, and then the battery. You will then see the micro SD card similarly to the one in cellphones (unless you have an iphone) push against the little card and then it will spring out to easily be removed. You can buy an adapter at any walmart, walgreens...etc. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DJPLS2W', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': 'If you purchase a second camera, does this monitor scan between each camera with video and audio like the other monitors on the market? My monitor that just recently broke, would allow you to put it on a scan option and it would go back and forth every...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I recently purchased this camera, and yes, you can program the monitor to scan between each camera. For instance, I have 2 cameras, and I programmed the monitor to go back and forth between cameras. So I can view camera one for 12 or so seconds, and then it automatically goes to camera 2 for 12 or so seconds, and so on. Or I can program the monitor to be static so it views just one camera, and I can manually switch between cameras by pressing the up and down arrows. In regards to viewing both cameras on the screen at the same time, like a split screen: yes that's possible also. The only caveat here is that the Ovia gives you an option to either view one screen entirely or a four-split screen, not a two-split screen. The four-split screen is pretty small, but still works. I wish they'd have an option for a two-split screen. Hope this helps!"}
