{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DJQOREC', 'answerTime': 'Aug 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409209200, 'question': 'Does this attach to a Graco pack and play?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "These are not designed to attach to pack and plays. It attaches similar to a nut and bolt. The music box has a threaded piece that sticks out of the back and there is a piece that screws onto it, pressing against the bars of a crib in order to make a tight fit. I don't think there is a way to make it fit anything other than a crib."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DJQOREC', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399964400, 'question': 'How does it attach to the crib? Is the mechanism adjustable, able to rotate?', 'answer': 'Yes, perfect!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DJQOREC', 'answerTime': 'Apr 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396854000, 'question': 'would this work on a small crib? The size they use at a NICU?', 'answer': "No its fairly large and we had it for a week before ours would make a horrible wind in noise we switched over to the rainforest mobile by fisher price which my daughter loves and the light on it is isn't bright so it doesn't bother her when she sleeps and it comes with a remote. I hope this information helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DJQOREC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386921600, 'question': 'Will this work with rechargeable C batteries that are 1.2 volt and not the 1.5 it says it needs?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I've got 1.2v AAs in it so I'd have to assume it would run with 1.2v Cs. The performance doesn't seem downgraded at all on 3.6v total. (It uses 3 batteries.) In fact, I'm using the cheap Amazon Basics rechargeables with no issue and haven't needed to charge them yet after a month of casual use."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DMD2348', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396162800, 'question': 'Does this co sleeper come with mattress, fitted sheet etc?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi Kathy-- This cosleeper does come with a mattress and sheet, but it's worth noting that the mattress is very firm - made that way, I assume, for babies' safety. I wound up buying a snuggle wool insert, and tucking a thin cotton blanket on top of that - that way the bed is softer and warmer, but still without loose bedding. I like this cosleeper very much, but would recommend getting it set up so you can assess what tweaks would suit you before you invest in extra bedding. The sheets are not easy to remove quickly, especially if you weave all the Velcro straps through as the manufacturer seems to intend..."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DMD2348', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418112000, 'question': 'Could the bassinet mattress be used in the bottom of the play yard to make this a travel crib for an older baby?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes it can. But the crib itself is not that big. It's not exactly easy to go from the bassinet to the play yard."}
