{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DMCYENW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401865200, 'question': 'Do you roll down the side in the middle of the night to get baby? Is this difficult?', 'answer': 'The side goes down to use the unit as a "co-sleeper". As a bassinet, it\'s not easy enough that you would want to put the side up and down in the middle of the night with a crying baby; but with the side rail up, it\'s only 30" high and about 12" deep to the mattress, so it\'s much easier to get your baby out than from a full size crib.'}
