{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380956400, 'question': 'what about CROTCH DANGLER ISSUES with bjorn?', 'answer': 'oh god, it is like this rumor will never die. find me ONE peer reviewed published study that suggests the baby bjorn causes ANY type of spinal issue and you will have my undying respect. dont give me a bunch of links to zealot bloggers who want to laud their moby wraps (by the way, i love my moby wrap, but use other carriers like the baby bjorn as well). otherwise read THIS blog: http://skeptoid.com/blog/2013/01/25/will-the-babybjorn-endanger-your-infants-health/ as it summarizes my eye rolling well.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383116400, 'question': 'Biggest criticism with Baby Bjorn carrier is backache that occurs in parents using it. Does this model address this issue?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Am not sure bout the other BB carriers but this one has not given my wife or I am problems . The baby loves it and we love the fact that it's comfortable and can be used for a lot more years that the others ."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382943600, 'question': 'I have the original Bjorn Carrier and little man loves it. I do get very sore shoulders/upper back after wearing it for a while. Does this new design help alleviate this? I would think so, given the waist belt, but would appreciate feedback!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This carrier is an improvement over the original but my shoulders and back still get sore, even with the extra hip strap. But I'm very petite so I think any weight that I carry in front will hurt my shoulders and back. It's more comfortable than the original, which I also love and so did/do all my babies. I start getting sore after about a half hour of baby wearing versus almost immediately with the original."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383030000, 'question': 'Can I carry my toddler on my back facing outward?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'We own the Baby Bjorn Carrier One and we love it. it is not made to carry a baby fcing outward on the back and I have never heard of any carrier that can do this.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'Does this carrier have the option for a closed pouch-like bottom for newborns, similar to the Ergo carrier?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No. The Carrier One does not offer a closed pouch-like bottom. It does have two front-facing newborn carry positions. http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AX6-SwrN7cQ'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': 'Is it annoying that there is no hood? Does the lack of it bother sleeping babies?', 'answer': "The lack of a hood doesn't really matter. I always put a little hat on the baby's head or put her into a hooded sweatshirt before I put her into the carrier if I thought it was needed."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400137200, 'question': 'is the mesh or cotton mix cooler for hot weather?', 'answer': "This thing holds in heat fairly well, so you won't need to wrap the baby up in blankets when it is warm out. Truthfully, the main temperature problem is you. You will heat your baby up, because they will be right up against your body. We found that was sometimes a little too much warmth for extended trips when baby was 1 month old, but even at 3 months it is no longer a problem."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': "Does the flap really bend down properly and stay down or will it go in my baby's face?", 'answer': "No. I used this for my baby when she was as young as a month and didn't bother with the flap. I just made sure she had a pacifier in her mouth to be extra sure she would not suffocate."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00DNQS6PO', 'answerTime': '11 days ago', 'question': 'Is the mesh material itchy at all?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "no. it doesn't really touch your skin anyway."}
