{'answer': 'Hello Victoria, and thanks for your interest in the Maxi Cosi Mico NXT and AP base! The Mico NXT and AP were actually not manufactured in 2011; they were not manufactured until approximately 2013. So just for clarification, since there are numerous Mico models on the market, this base would not fit any of the original Mico car seat models or the brand new Mico Max 30. This base is only designed to fit the Mico NXT and AP models. If you have the original Mico car seat, you would want the base model 22517-BLK for that car seat. Conversely, the 22517-BLK will not work for the Mico NXT, AP, or Max 30. There was a design change that moved the base release handle from the base on the original Mico models to the back of the car seat itself on the NXT/AP models. The Max 30 has a rebound bar on it that is specific to that seat. That is why these bases and seats are not interchangeable. The 1 exception would be that you can purchase a Mico Max 30 base for use with the AP and NXT as they have the same base release mechanism and the Max 30 base is tested/approved for a higher rated seat (30 lb seat) so it can be used with the 22 lb. NXT and AP models. The AP/NXT bases cannot be used for the Max 30 as previously advised because they are 22 lb. bases and the Max 30 is a 30 lb. maximum weight seat. I hope this information is helpful for you. If you have any additional questions or concerns, please let us know and we will gladly help you any way we can. You may reach us via email consumer@maxicosi-us.com or phone 1-800-951-4113.', 'asin': 'B00DW2D63G', 'answerTime': '5 days ago', 'question': 'Does this base only fit the 2015 model or does it also fit the 2011 model?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
