{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E1CIGAE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389513600, 'question': 'We have the previous version for our toddler son. Will the two units interfere with eachother at all?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Nope. We use both an older model (2009) and this one with no issues.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E1CIGAE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391932800, 'question': 'in a power shortage, if I have batteries installed in the baby unit, will it continue to work?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, it should. The parent unit Sits on the charger at night, so theoretically, it should go through the night. I've had mine off the charger for up to six hours and still had over half a charge. And when it didn't have batteries, the parent unit alerts you that the other one is out, so your covered all the way around. I had the Motorola video monitor before this for two years, it cost more than this one and I like it MUCH better. I'd take this over the video monitor any day. Sorry for the super long answer. Hope it's helpful."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E1CIGAE', 'answerTime': 'Jul 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406617200, 'question': 'Is it pretty light-weight and suitable for traveling to Europe?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It is! We took it to Spain back in May, all you need is two converters, one for the charger and one for the base. The base is also battery powered which is a great help if the crib isn't by a power source."}
