{'answer': 'Hello! I can understand your concerns with a tight fit in the vehicle. The RodiFix actually has a low profile/footprint and has been very popular for its fit in many vehicles! The feature for these side wings actually accommodates growing children. The photo you see is actually with the headrest and wings in the widest and most open state you can get them in. The way this feature functions - as the headrest rises in height, the side wings will move out to accommodate older children. Therefore, the headrest can be moved up or down to the desired location as long as the midpoint of the child\'s head is in the center of the headrest. To help you with measurements, if the headrest is in the lowest setting, the width at the side wings (widest point of the seat) is approximately 17.75"W. With the headrest in the highest position (therefore the side wings in the widest position possible), the width at the side wings is approximately 20.75"W. Should you have any other questions, please let us know and we will certainly be happy to help. Have a wonderful afternoon!', 'asin': 'B00E6117FQ', 'answerTime': '17 days ago', 'question': 'We have a tight 3 across and the base here looks narrow enough/easy to buckle. Why then are there such wide side wings (it would not fit)?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
