{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394521200, 'question': "Any irritation to the baby's skin?", 'answer': "None whatsoever. It's very gentle whether you put directly on top of their skin or a shirt."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': 'Can this be used if the baby falls asleep in a swing or carseat or its only for sleeping on flat surfaces?', 'answer': "Hello MAIN, great question. While Oma/Oma+ is certainly a portable clip-on device, it does not function as designed in car seats, strollers, swings or other mobile carriers, since the sensor will detect even the tiniest external bumps or motion experienced in transit. We recommend keeping baby under your watchful eye with Oma/Oma+ clipped on to baby's diaper but deactivated to avoid false alarms when travelling. When you and baby have arrived at your destination and baby is in a motionless bed/cot, it is then safe to re-activate your monitor."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391068800, 'question': 'can this be worn under a swaddle?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yep it works just great under a swaddle blanket.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391846400, 'question': 'What is the difference between Levana and Snuza...Also, it seems to me that Snuza has better reviews? What is Your opinion/input/suggestion. Thanks!', 'answer': 'I believe the snuza was just a previous version of the Oma. It was my understanding that yet were the same. There are two versions of each though.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396162800, 'question': 'Can this be used for babies that roll onto their stomach and remain in that position for most of the night? My daughter does that and also pushes her butt up in the air...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Both our children were stomach sleepers and we had no issues with false alarms. The monitor was able to detect movement just fine while on their stomachs.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392364800, 'question': 'Will this work in the car? Or would the movement of the car make the monitor think the baby was okay?', 'answer': 'This is from the Levana website "13. Can Oma travel? Yes, this is what separates it from other monitors. As Oma requires no mains power, wires or cords (it is battery operated) it can go anywhere and everywhere you and your baby go. Please note:- Oma monitors detect all movement, including those from external sources such as a moving vehicle, pram, etc. Oma should only be relied upon when there is NO external movement present, i.e. when the vehicle, pram, etc. is stationery."'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420617600, 'question': 'Do you get the full manual in the product package? Also, does the battery already pre-placed when open the product for the first time?', 'answer': 'No the manual is online. Yes the battery is in place and ready to use.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Is the clip able to openwide enough to fit on cloth diapers?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The clip opens up to about one inch. That certainly seems like enough room to accommodate cloth diapers and rubber pants. The clip is slightly springy and has gripper teeth on it. So does the monitor, so together they both hold tight to diapers. Ours has never come off...yet. Baby isn't old enough to play with it so we're safe for awhile."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Can the vibration feature be turned off, in case it is causing unanticipated issues with sleeping?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This is taken directly from the manual, which can be found at Levana's website: NOTE: The Rouse Warning is automatically enabled each time Oma+ is switched ON. To disable this warning, ensure that OMA+ is switched ON, then press and hold the MODE button for at least 1 second until a tone is heard and the unit vibrates briefly. If you want to enable the warning again, switch Oma+ off completely (press both ON and MODE buttons simultaneously), then switch it ON again (the Vibration Alert is enabled by default when Oma+ is switched on)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E8NGRN4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425283200, 'question': 'Will this work in a swing that has been turned OFF (ie no movement) or a rock n play that is NOT rocking or vibrating?', 'answer': 'It definitely works in Rock n plays! My babies sleep in them every night wearing the monitors! I would assume it would work in a non moving swing as well.'}
