{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E9F3LZS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397199600, 'question': 'Can anyone describe the patterns in the Once Upon a Time set? Thanks!', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The one is a vine/floral pattern with a deer running through ever so often. The other is scattered flowers. If you go to the Aden and Anais website you can get a closer look. I like the colors and pattern, wish they made more products in this theme!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E9RMHD8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410937200, 'question': 'What is the support input voltage? Does it support 220V?', 'answer': "Yes! I can't speak for others, but the unit I received a couple of days ago (shipped from and sold by Amazon) came with two power adapters with 100-240V indicated on them."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E9RMHD8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393660800, 'question': 'Does the baby unit run off battery power, in addition to AC plug in?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Both units can run off battery. AA batteries. Both baby and parent units AC adapter will recharge the batteries.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E9RMHD8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409986800, 'question': "Does the talk feature work both ways? I'm considering this for a child who would need to be able to communicate back, not just parent to child.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Funny you ask that, the first time I talked to my husband he wasn't sure how to talk back. It made me laugh cause its a monitor after all you can hear everything, all the kid has to do is speak. You just have to hold the talk button on your end when you speak."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E9RMHD8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411369200, 'question': "My elderly mother's house is approximately 100 feet from my house. I want this in case she needs me and cannot get to the phone. Will this work?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'We got this for our son and daughter-in-law who have an acre and a half lot. It works fine over the entire area.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E9RMHD8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': 'I want to use this to monitor break-in for my car :p Would the battery last about 8-12hrs in the car? How loud is the parent unit?', 'answer': "The parent unit adjusts quite nicely volume-wise, from mute all the way up to being able to hear every little sound. We usually keep ours at a medium volume. I'm not sure about 12 hours, but we use ours in our room without charging overnight, so 8 hours should be fine if you start fully charged."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E9RMHD8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388822400, 'question': 'What is the amount of Watt it uses?', 'answer': 'Base says 6V DC, 500 mA. Hand unit says 5V, 1000mA'}
