{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ECG0IFA', 'answerTime': 'May 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400569200, 'question': 'Is the coupler included to attach the trailer to a bike? Does it fit most bikes?', 'answer': 'The coupler is a simple bracket that attaches to the axle of the rear wheel. Simply unbolt the rear wheel, slip over the attachment, then re-tighten the bolt. It will fit on nearly all bikes.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388217600, 'question': "How's the range?", 'answer': 'Actually pretty good, I have a small workshop outside my home and I still get three bars there with no video dropouts. I can watch and hear him while tooling around and that is with the camera in a closed room on the other side of the house at least 60 feet away with the signal going through my living room, a home office, garage, and finally on a shelf 8 feet into the workshop'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402297200, 'question': 'Can you turn the screen off but still hear sound? And can you adjust the volume?', 'answer': 'Yes you can turn the video off and still use the sound. Then just hit a button to turn the video back if you need to. Great feature to help keep the room dark while sleeping. You can also control the volume and pan the camera from the video unit.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395212400, 'question': "Is this easy to set up? I'd like to travel with it and want to make sure I won't be frustrated at the resort b/c I need a router or anything like that.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it is! We have traveled a few times with it. No issues. This was my fourth monitor. None of them compare!!! By far best one out there for picture quality.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397545200, 'question': 'Is there a way to disable the beeping sound the monitor makes when the screen turns off?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Amazon is selling the new March 2014 units, which allow you to turn the alarms off completely.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384761600, 'question': 'Is the camera able to be wall-mounted?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. The Camera has a slot on the bottom allowing you to mount it to the wall using a traditional drywall screw & anchor. We do not currently have ours mounted but likely will when the new nursery is finished.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'Can I see multi cameras streaming at the same time on the monitor unit (divided monitor space) ? Or only by switching between cameras?', 'answer': 'it switches (scans automatically or switch manually), honestly, the monitor would be too small to divide up. I can say that the scan works great for two cameras, one on a 8 week old and the other on a 3.5yo.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384329600, 'question': 'Does this unit work with 240V/50Hz power (as found in Europe)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The unit does work with 240V/50Hz power. The monitor unit can also be charged directly from a computer USB outlet.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383462000, 'question': 'How long are the power cables that come with the camera and the monitor?', 'answer': 'The power cable for the monitor is 10 ft, for the camera the cable is 8.5 ft. We put the monitor in a few places and never needed the full cord!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Oct 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413270000, 'question': "Can you see if the baby's eyes are open in the night vision?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, you can. My baby sometimes cries in her sleep, so knowing that she is just dreaming saves me from accidentally waking her up.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00ECHYTBI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398063600, 'question': 'Can anybody tell me if this monitor has encryption? If so, what kind? Security is very important to us. Thanks!', 'answer': 'These cameras do not have the capability to be viewed via WIFI, and therefore wouldn\'t be susceptible to any privacy issues that an Internet remote camera would. Instead, these cameras are "paired" by pressing a physical button on each unit. Once paired, other units wouldn\'t have the capability to "pick-up" transmissions. Unfortunately, as with all electronic devices, there are no 100% guarantees of privacy, but none of the other units use any type of encryption unless they are remote internet connection capable. I have 2 units and feel very secure. I\'ve had other units that have performed well also, but needed a system that could handle more that one camera. Great customer service folks too.'}
