{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EKNSVB8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404370800, 'question': 'Has anyone taken this stroller to Europe? Specifically, how does it handle on cobblestone? Are the wheels rubber or plastic? How big are the wheels?', 'answer': 'I have not taken this stroller overseas yet but am planning to take it to Australia in a few months. The wheels are plastic (and standard "umbrella size") and certainly not as cushy as the rubber ones on most jogging strollers but for an umbrella they are pretty decent. I took my jogging stroller to Australia last year and it was a pain in the ass during all the flights. If you are planning on a lot of flying I would highly recommend the umbrella for convenience/weight. I opted for this umbrella b/c it reclines so my son can nap in the airports during connections. It\'s not as compact as some other "super lite" strollers but it\'s light enough and folds down that you can carry it over your shoulder with the strap through airports if the baby is in another carrier. This was the lightest fully reclining umbrella I could find. It has a great sunshade compared to most other umbrellas too. So far I have only used it around town to run errands but it handles fine on paved sidewalks and I\'m really happy with it. Hope this helps you!'}
