{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EL8S9BO', 'answerTime': 'Jul 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404889200, 'question': 'I know that summer had a recall on some of their products a few months back. Do you know if this particular monitor was involved?', 'answer': "They didn't really recall the MONITORS, but they wanted to add a warning label and clips to wind the extra cord around. The reason for the recall was that babies have been strangled by the cord that is between the monitor and the wall. Apparently these parents put the monitor IN the crib, or within reach of their child and there was enough cord to wrap around the baby's neck. There is/was nothing wrong with the actual monitors. To answer your question, THIS monitor that I received did have a warning label and it DOES come with the clips so to wrap the excess cord around. This recall is a heads up to all parents/caregivers/grandparents to make sure that the monitor isn't within reach of the child being monitored, and to make sure there isn't enough slack in the cord so that the baby could become entangled in it. Kudos to Summer for calling our attention to this issue. I hope this answers your question!!"}
