{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EU5AL8W', 'answerTime': 'Apr 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397199600, 'question': 'How is the range on this product? We enjoy sitting on our patio against our house in the evenings and if the kids are in bed I want to be able to see?', 'answer': 'The range is easily a few hundred feet. My children have very early bedtimes and I use mine outside in the yard all the time! I can go about halfway into my 1 acre yard before the signal goes out.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EU5AL8W', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1420012800, 'question': 'Is it possible to have the video in split screen mode and at the same time have the audio automatically toggling between the two cameras?', 'answer': "Not that I'm aware of. If you have it in split screen mode you can pick which one you want audio on, but it doesn't toggle back and forth while on split screen."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EUV2BSE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394866800, 'question': 'is this an updated model to the one that was recalled?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. The recalled models were manufactured prior to November 2011. The jumper I received is model OJ3, which is not listed in the recall notice (visit link reference below). Since the model is listed in the label affixed to the seat I don't know if there's a way to know the model without opening the box. Luckily returns are covered with the purchase so it is worth the risk of buying it. That's what I did, if it were to be a recalled model there was not much to worry about. It just would have go back and the seller get an awful review. http://www.cpsc.gov/en/Recalls/2013/Kids-II-Recalls-Baby-Einstein-Activity-Jumpers/"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EUV2BSE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411974000, 'question': 'What do you recommend Baby Einstein Baby Neptune Activity Center or Baby Einstein Musical Motion Activity Jumper?', 'answer': "I highly recommend the Baby Einstein Jumper because it grows with your child (it has easy click height adjustments) and it collapses flat for easy transportation and storage. We purchased this jumper for our son when he was 3.5 months old and he instantly LOVED it. He's turning 9 months this week and he's still using his jumper daily, though he's already crawling everywhere and attempting to walk at this point, so this jumper doesn't keep his full attention as it did when he was younger. But we Love it! Worth every penny!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EUV2BSE', 'answerTime': 'Aug 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408086000, 'question': 'What is the start age on this', 'answer': 'Your child needs to be a support sitter. So about 4 to 5 months old.'}
