{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EUV2BSE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411369200, 'question': 'Exactly what activities are presented', 'answer': "There are three colored buttons, and three separate functions for the buttons. One is musical songs, one is shapes and colors in English, Spanish and French, and the other is a three note piano. There are otherwise the usual assortment of plastic loops and rings, brightly colored. There's an oblong rolling ball with pictures of a dog and a cat that when it spins (with tiny beads inside making noise) it changes back and forth between a photo of the animals and a cartoon drawing. There's also a dangling bird, and a sunshine flower. On one side there's a small tray that we like to use to put our daughter's rice rusk treats for her to discover."}
