{'answer': "The seat itself is one piece on the top (the green you see around the edge is rubber but seems to be molded to the top). I don't see how urine could get inside. The handle could be detached and there are 2 pieces underneath that you clip in but never have to take out again and those keep the seat in place when you put the seat on the toilet to use it -- I don't think urine would get in those places since they are at the rear of the seat. For the price, I think this is the best seat for both girls and boys. (I've raised 3 boys who are now adults and used a similar seat when they were little and am now using this Fisher-Price seat for my granddaughter. It's a simple, stable and portable seat and, in ,y opinion, easy to clean.", 'asin': 'B00F2MQ0K0', 'answerTime': '28 days ago', 'question': 'Is the seat all one piece or is there a seam somewhere where two pieces fit together? i.e. Can urine get inside anywhere and stink?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
