{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00F2MQ2BW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409036400, 'question': 'how much weight can it hold? At what point is this not good enough for a baby as our baby is 4 mths old at this point.', 'answer': 'Our son is 5 months old and about 18lbs and he still uses it all the time (and will probably continue to use for many months to come). My understanding is that this jumperoo is meant to be used all the way through their "first steps" which (in most cases) is beyond 4 and 5 months. We got this jumperoo when he was 4 months and about 15 lbs, and while he LOVED it, we could tell he was a little small for it and there was plenty of room for him to grow into it. Overall, my wife and I both agree this is one of the best purchases we\'ve made for our little man so far.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00F2MQ2BW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'how much space does it take up? how wide is it?', 'answer': 'Without it extended the side (where it extends) is about 33 inches. I measured the feet on this because that\'s the widest part. The front along the widest part(the handles because they kinda stick out) measures about 36 inches, if you jam it in the corner to keep the handles up it\'s closer to about 30. I keep it "stored" at the end of my couch and it\'s about as wide as it. Extended it\'s about 46 inches. It\'s pretty big! I almost regret buying it because we live in a smallest apartment but my baby loves it.'}
