{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00F57O766', 'answerTime': 'Aug 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407481200, 'question': 'how i chaege the battery? only with batteries or with electricity? if its with electricity? its works with 110- 240 volt?', 'answer': "Only the monitor uses batteries.... Rechargeable batteries come with the set. Two power adapters came with mine; one for the camera.... which has to run on electrical power, not batteries, and one to recharge the batteries in the hand-held monitor.... they last about 8 - 9 hours between recharging when new..... less as they age..... way less if you don't let them discharge almost completely before recharging. The two power adapters are two-blade 120 volt items that came with mine.... may be different if delivered overseas, I don't know. The monitor unit will run on alkaline batteries when you need to."}
