{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00FDUHAJG', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404198000, 'question': 'Can I mount this where one side is against a wall &amp; the other against a banister? If so does it come w/the hardware to do so?', 'answer': 'We were able to mount the gate to a banister on one side. It did not come with the hardware. We had to buy and stain a 2" x 4" piece of wood and cut to the height of the banister, then strapped it on the banister with heavy duty straps. We had cut grooves in the 2x4 to secure the straps in place. Then the gate circles (where the gate is attached to open and close it) were screwed into the wood. It sounds like a lot of work but works great in the long run.'}
