{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00FLXBHIU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415865600, 'question': "Re. traveling: is it bulky in a carry-on? I'm trying to decide between this and a BubbleBum for my 8 y/o to in rental cars when traveling. Thoughts?", 'answer': "It's wide but not bulky. Super light weight. I prefer this seat over bubble bum."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00FLXBHIU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389859200, 'question': 'Is this seat compliable with United States Standard FMVSS 213 safety standard? Thanks', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, the Incognito is compatiable with all applicable FMVSS. I was curious about this myself, as I am a car seat tech and could find no info online. They can not market the seat if it did not conform to all applicable FMVSS. I called Dorel/Safety1st and they confirmed this. The lady I talked to said she would let the appropriate people know that the FMVSS info was not in the description. She also said that the FMVSS info is on a sticker that is on the seat.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00FLXBHIU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413961200, 'question': 'what is the actual width?', 'answer': 'I\'m not sure - we have it in the backseat of a Honda Accord and it fits nicely in the seat next to the door on either side - it does not encroach onto the center seat at all. It\'s wider at the front of the seat than the back and also slightly thicker at the front. The back of the safety seat has a little "lip" that is meant to fit (I think) into the fold where the seat back meets the actual seat to help keep the booster in place. If it gets knocked askew my child just puts in back in the right position before seating. It\'s solved a major problem for us in that now the seat belt is correctly positioned across our child\'s body and not across their face/neck. This is so lightweight and not bulky, its easy to quickly move and store in the trunk if we are transporting all adults vs. children.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00FLXBHIU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414652400, 'question': 'Can I fit three of these across a back seat?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "In most back seats, yes you probably can. They aren't super narrow at the front, but most back seats are a little wider at the knee than at the hips anyway."}
