{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00FZP3E8A', 'answerTime': 'Apr 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429945200, 'question': 'Does this stroller seat recline for infant use?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "The back does recline, but it does not go flat. I think it's recommended for 3+ months. I would not put a baby under that age in there, and it works best for 6 mos and older. The back piece is just straight, so I added in a head cushion from a car seat that I wasn't using to give it more cushion when my little one fell asleep in it (and it helped out in that 4-5 month age). I really like the stroller; it pushes great through grass or trails. Side note - we had a Graco infant seat that did not latch into the stroller, but I occasionally still would set it in if we were just standing around at a park while the big kids played. You could kind if rig the straps to hold it in, but not safe for anything but a very smooth, short ride!"}
