{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00G34TIHS', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': 'Could somebody please explain the LATCH system. I have a 2006 Honda Accord and have no idea whether it can utilize that system.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The LATCH system uses latches on the car seat instead of using the vehicle seatbelts. There should be anchors in the car, basically u shaped metal rings for the latches to snap on to. The anchors are near where the seatbelt receiving buckle comes out of the crease of the seat back and seat. Check your vehicle owners guide to see if your car has the LATCH system. A 2006 Honda should. My 2007 Accord does....'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00G34TIDW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398495600, 'question': 'How easy is it to wash the covers in the event of a blowout/spilling?', 'answer': "They are very easy to remove. The tags said to hand wash, but we chanced it and used the machine. We did let it air dry and it was completely dry within 4-5 hours. My daughter vomited in her seat and you can't see or smell anything. And the cover still looks like new after washing. We were very impressed with the seat overall and cleaning it was very easy."}
