{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00G34TJWM', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'Is there a handle to use this as a baby carrier for infants? Will it work with the britax strollers?', 'answer': 'No this is not an infant carrier. This is a convertible car seat that stays in the car. It is designed for both rear facing use then transitions to forward facing and stays permanently in the car. I bought this for my then 6 month daughter as she was getting close to the height limit on her infant carrier the Britax BSafe. Most importantly she looked and acted uncomfortable in the infant carseat. I am so glad I bought this when I did as she loves it and is MUCH more comfortable. It does have 3 reclining positions although for rear facing it has to be at the most reclined postion. I did continu to use her infant carrier/carseat clicked into her stroller right until she turned 7 months now she sits just fine in her stroller. Hope this helps!'}
