{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00G34TMDI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394694000, 'question': 'I have an IS250, which I will soon be getting rid of, but in the meantime need a bigger seat for my 15 month old. Would this one fit rear facing in the back? Everything I have read says they are huge! I do not know what the next car will be, but bigger...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi Morgan, I don't think it will fit rear facing in the back. I wouldn't fit our vehicle rear facing. If we made it fit we would have to have the front seats pulled completely erect. We have it front facing and it fits. However, there isn't any shoulder room for the passengers sitting on the sides. We have 3 series bmw and the car seat takes up 60 percent of the backseat. We have it in the middle backseat and my husband can't sit in the backseat comfortably. His shoulders don't have enough room, he has to sit slanted. We don't mind, because we read in the reviews how it saved the child in an accident. We normally sit in the front seats anyway. I hope this helps you."}
