{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00G34TL6Q', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398582000, 'question': "Has anyone brought this seat onto an airplane? I'm guessing it wouldn't fit due to width but figured I would ask. Thanks!", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I have used this seat on several long distance flights and yes, it does fit. Airlines don\'t seem to like car seats placed in aisle seats unless the entire row consists of "family" (related to or traveling together). The side impact cushions do crowd ever so slightly into the next seat--really a non-issue for most though, especially if next to a family member. I am 6\'4" and about 220lbs . . . I am a little aware of the impact cushions, but not anywhere near as inconvenienced as I am by the airlines\' reduction in leg room---but I digress. Truthfully, if it keeps my daughter safer, I would endure anything . . . but this is really not an issue with this car seat . . . and if you can place this car seat in a window seat and you sit next to it, it is a non-issue.'}
