{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00G34TIKU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403938800, 'question': "Does anyone know the height limitations on this seat? I can't find it anywhere in the product details and my child is already 29 1/2 inches at 4 mo!", 'answer': 'The owners manual states 49 inches or less. Our son was almost 24 inches at birth. This seat has one of the highest height ratings we could find. I suggest visiting the Britax website for the best product descriptions. We compared a lot of seats and found the Britax line to be the best seats for the money. A friend has the Britax marathon and suggested the brand. Amazon had the best price. And free two day shipping with my Prime account. Also fits very well into all the vehicles we have put it in. Could not be happier with this car seat. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00G34TIKU', 'answerTime': 'May 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399618800, 'question': 'Does the fabric option (Onyx, Silver Birch, Sterling, Deseret Palm, etc) makes any difference to the comfort?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't think so, but I did have to buy a liner that was more breathable fabric. My daughter was very hot in this seat."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00G34TIKU', 'answerTime': 'May 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399100400, 'question': 'Are the straps difficult to adjust? Also, does it sit high while rear facing? Thanks', 'answer': "The straps are my biggest complaint. They can get tangled because of the padding surrounding them. It does sit a little higher then our graco which works well because of my small car however it doesn't look uncomfortable for wee one. I still prefer this seat over the Graco."}
