{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00G34TIKU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391328000, 'question': 'How does this compare to the Peg Perego or the Chicco Nextfit?', 'answer': 'This seat is a lot shorter lived than the nextfit because it has such a short shell.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00G34TIKU', 'answerTime': 'May 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399705200, 'question': 'With other car seats you can take the car seat out with the baby in it and go into your house or wherever are you able to do that with this carseat?', 'answer': "No this is not and infant carseat that clicks in and out. This is a stationary seat. You can adjust it to 3 different reclining levels in the rear facing position and 1 maybe 2 in the forward position. I don't recommend this for newborns. Its easier to use a carseat with a click base so you don't have to take the baby in and out however, this car seat is AMAZING when you are ready to get rid of the carrier and just put them in rear facing until a certain weight and then you can turn it around for a much heavier weight. Love this seat!"}
