{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00G34TL02', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417420800, 'question': "i'm in between the Gridlock color and black. The Gridlock material looks rough. Is it soft and cozy? The black looks hot.", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Hi Stacey. I have the black and it is very nice. I am always picking food out of it so I am so glad I got black because it still looks newish. It is not hot - it is a velour type material so it breathes. In the hot summer months Britax recommends covering up the buckles with a cloth when the car is sitting out in the sun so they don't burn your baby, but I think that would be true no matter what color you choose. Good luck - I love this seat!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00G34TL02', 'answerTime': 'Apr 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397545200, 'question': 'I live Phoenix so it gets hot in the summer, does this seat make your child sweaty?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, but our guy sweats a lot from just being a pretty active/jumping baby ... fyi, we live in San Francisco, so not sure what we'd do with him in Phoenix. It's usually just his head that comes away sweaty in the back. Not a big deal so far. The seat is solid and relatively easy to use (we have it rear-facing and it takes a little maneuvering to get him into the seat while also not bonking his head on the top of our Jeep Grand Cherokee - I think this will get harder for a little while, and then easier when we turn it around and he can climb into it himself)."}
