{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00G3XR9LG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': "Is it possible to fully pull down the canopies so the sun close to sunset doesn't distract babies?", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "The canopies can fold down to meet the seat, but the top portion (which would normally be velcroed to the frame) is exposed. I've done this before with my two month old to keep the wind from getting into the reclined seat, and then covered the exposed top portion with a blanket. But to answer your question, no. The canopy extends farther than most, but not completely without detaching from the top. Hope that helps!"}
