{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00G3XR9MU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404543600, 'question': 'Does the new 2014 version sit up/balance on its own when its folded, or do you need to lay it down flat?', 'answer': 'The handle for the fold is where the baby sits. When it folds, the seat/handle is one "end" and the wheels are the other "end". When it\'s folded, it is still several inches thick and it\'s fairly easy to lean against a wall or chair, although it cannot stand *exactly* straight up. When I\'ve leaned it against an adult-sized chair, it sticks up about 6 inches (estimated) above the seat. It doesn\'t bother me much when it\'s leaned against my chair.'}
