{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00GDKEMRI', 'answerTime': 'Apr 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398841200, 'question': 'I love the way this looks, but how breathable is the fabric? My baby is due in June and I have 2 other kids. Will we be dying of heat when we use it?', 'answer': 'I am careful not to bundle up my daughter in a heavy onesie when we wear this. The two of us can generate some heat in the moby and we keep warm. It is breathable, stretchy and comfortable fabric but the closeness of the two of you could make your child overheat if you dress baby too much. The real trouble I have with the moby is the darn thing is so long that no matter how careful I am when I need to take it off, the ends always drag on the floor and that bothers me a lot. My friend uses a sling and she loves it. I also use other carriers and alternate but I do like the moby and would recommend. Hope this helps you and best wishes on your new child.'}
