{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00GHM87GY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420876800, 'question': 'Does the seat sit up high? I am wondering if my daughter will be able to see out the window well. I am debating between this and the Clek.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Alison, This seat does sit up high! I bought this for my 7 month old grandson so he still sitting facing back. I believe in order for them to be able to see out the side windows they would have to lean forward somewhat. I got this one because #1 safety, it is very safe! #2 I had bought him the whole orbit system already. This does slip into the stroller part of it however, I find that not being able to lean it back so when the child is sleeping he/she could be more comfy in the actual stroller end of it is a flaw. As far as the height in the actual car, I found it to be a wee bit too tall and bulky. But again my main concern was the safety factor. It has great padding surrounding the head and it is a very sturdy car seat. I hope this helps! Good luck, it gets very confusing.'}
