{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00GS1H526', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': 'what is the maximum weight for using the harness?', 'answer': "Rear-Facing Requirements: Weight: 5 - 40 lbs (2.3 - 18kg), Height: 19 - 37 inches (48 - 94 cm), and Top of child's head is at least 1 inch (25 mm) below the top of the child restraint seat back. Forward-Facing Requirements: Weight: 22 - 65 lbs (10 - 29.4 kg), Height: 28 - 50 inches (71 - 127 cm), the tops of their ears are below the top of the child restraint headrest and at least one year of age. Booster Requirements: Weight: 40 - 110 lbs (18 - 49.8 kg), Height: 43.3 - 57 inches (110 - 145 cm), the tops of their ears are below the top of the child restraint headrest and at least four years of age."}
