{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00GS1H526', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397113200, 'question': 'I drive a Honda Fit, a compact 4-door hatchback. Would this seat fit well in there?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I drive a Hyundai Elantra and it fits in there. It is almost up against the front seat (my daughter is still facing backwards) so it is snug but it fits. My husband has a Toyota Tacoma truck and it fits fine in there as it is a little roomier. It doesn't seem like a huge seat- smaller than others I looked at, but it still takes up a decent amount of space in my sedan."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00GS1H526', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411369200, 'question': 'Does this seat recline in in the ff position? If so, how much. We like to do long road trips.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes Josh it reclines in the FF position. It goes from level I - sitting up, to level III @ about 45 degrees. My 18 month old daughter loves this seat. It is well padded and the construction is top notch. You will not be disappointed. We travel from Maryland to Wyoming and the child sleeps much of the time.'}
