{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00GSMU63U', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395471600, 'question': 'Also, can anyone compare/contrast with Baby Jogger City Select? It seems preferable bc it has 2 full seats, but much heavier.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'I owned the City Select for a long time when my boys were younger; now I own the VaryLight in Charcoal . The Select is a very nice stroller BUT the seats are small and my older son quickly grew out of the seat. The seat on the VaryLight has a very tall seat back and a large/tall head clearance. Both the VaryLight and the Select are easy to push and fold similarly; neither stand alone but the Joovy can lean against the wall and stand upright that way with no problem, the BJ cannot. The baskets are comparable in size and access so this is a wash in my opinon as is the fact that neither comes with a parent console which in my opinion is ridiculous with such a pricey stroller but it is what it is. The Joovy does however, come with a front child tray and one can be purchased for the rear rider (the snack tray is interchangeable from front to back) where with the BJ you have to purchase one for both seats. Also, if your child is 2.5 years or older, the jump seat on the back is a BIG hit with the sit & stand versus the double seat stroller! Really, by this age most children do not need a full seat unless you are on an ALL day outing and the child falls asleep. All in all, unless you have petite children who are very close in age or twins, I would go with the VaryLight; I LOVE mine!'}
