{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H07AZ42', 'answerTime': 'May 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400050800, 'question': 'Thinking about trying cloth diapers for the first time....what do you need to get going if using this product? 4 mo old and 4 y.o. (for night time)', 'answer': "These are pretty awesome, btw - one of the best cloth diapering inserts on the market. This product is an insert - you lay in inside a diaper cover like this bumgenious one: http://www.amazon.com/dp/B0072FRFI6?tag=blself-20 . Assuming your child has only wet the diaper, you can just pull out the wet insert and put in a dry one, reusing the cover. This means you only need one cover for ever 3 or 4 changings. When your child goes number 2, the mess will likely spread onto the inside of the cover, and you'll want to wash both. If you are serious about cloth diapering, get a diaper sprayer: http://www.amazon.com/dp/B00938R0XA?tag=blself-20 . I wouldn't do cloth diapers without one."}
