{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H6XPZN6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395298800, 'question': "Does anyone use this in a cold environment? I live in Canada and I heard that suction cup sunshades don't stick in the cold weather. Do these ones?", 'answer': 'You are right to wonder as many do have a hard time sticking and it is usually bc they are being stuck to a cold surface. If you warm the car first then stick it on it should hold through out the day but that also depends if you are talking about -5 or -30. Also it is advised to have a clean surface too. These cups are quite sticky, so please do try and if it does not work then contact Starlight and Sunny for customer support, they will make sure you are taken care of !'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSEWY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'What is the height restrictions for this seat for children who are Rear Facing?', 'answer': 'Actually, it\'s 40lbs and 1" from the red handle at the top (and that\'s the part that moves as your child grows). Nowhere in the manual does it state 32". This is one of the seats with the best/longest extended rear facing options, in terms of height.'}
