{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSK1Y', 'answerTime': 'Nov 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416556800, 'question': "I'm a first time mom so I am very confused, will this be ok to use from day one? with an infant? thx", 'answer': 'Yes. It has extra support to fit in a newborn and then remove later. Just keep in mind that it is not as easy to carry around like car seats that are designed just for newborns that will click into a stroller and have a handle so you can carry the baby around in the seat. But if you are on a budget, and just want to purchase one car seat, this will fit a newborn to 65 lbs.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MSK1Y', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424851200, 'question': 'Can you remove the crotch strap for washing?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes its removable but by instructions the straps nor crotch buckle should never be washed or submerged in water it should only be wiped with a damp cloth or baby wipe. You can use a damp cloth & dawn soap or baby shampok but never submerge in water'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MSK1Y', 'answerTime': 'Sep 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409554800, 'question': 'We live about 30 minutes from everything. Is this a comfortable seat for long car rides?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "We took at two hour ride to a theme park and my son was very comfortable in it. He fell asleep in it without any trouble. He's rear facing still and is 33 months 32 pounds and about 40 inches tall. It was a great purchase. He tells me all the time he loves it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MSK1Y', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425801600, 'question': 'I have problems with childs head falling forward in current car seat when sleeping in a rear facing position, does it happen in this one?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I don't have any problems with that happening since my child's head usually falls to the side and is caught by the side wings. Overall this is a great seat and my child always falls to asleep in it"}
