{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408950000, 'question': 'Is it possible to use the napper as the primary sleeper, or is it best to swap daily between the napper and the bassinet?', 'answer': 'I used it as a primary place for my baby to sleep up up until she was 3 months. She slept better in the backnplay bassinet then she did in her expensive crib. Just make sure baby is always properly secured.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415433600, 'question': 'Does this come with a carry bag of some sort for travel? Would the napper and changer also collapse somehow for travel?', 'answer': 'She already has one. I think it collapses.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408950000, 'question': 'How long can the napper be used for a baby comfortably? Does the vibrations work well?', 'answer': "Our son is 6 weeks old and we still use the napper. I expect it to be in use until approx 12 weeks as he is growing quickly. It probably varies with each baby, I tend to have bigger babies! Even if we only get up to 12 weeks use we will be happy. Both napper and changer have been really useful, it's been one of the best purchases we've made and of course the pack n play will get a lot of use. The music and vibrate features are great if your baby likes that sort of thing, ours doesn't much care for it!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411023600, 'question': 'Does this one have the little nightlight on the electronic module?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, it has a nightlight that can shine on the baby, up toward the ceiling, or both. I've found it is really useful when you just need to peek on baby and make sure all is well. I was doing this at least twice a night at first lol. It also helps with diaper changes without waking baby."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'Can the removable napper be used as a rocking seat by itself? Does it have the plastic legs to stand alone?', 'answer': 'Unfortunately, the napper cannot be used alone.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409382000, 'question': 'pls compare Napper to Station playard. is Station much larger? is Station suitable for older baby?', 'answer': 'I think you are asking about the napper that is on top. It is for infants up to 15 pounds. Then you transition to the mattress set at a higher level. When they start rolling and pushng up on all fours, you drop down to the lower mattress position.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415260800, 'question': 'Are the napper and changer quickly removable without disassembling and assembling the whole system?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'They are quickly removable without disassemble'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427266800, 'question': 'Ease of assembly', 'answer': 'It is pretty easy to assemble. No tools or anything are needed however, the instructions can be pretty unclear at times. It took me a good few minutes to figure some of it out. Other than confusing instructions, its pretty easy to put together.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420876800, 'question': 'Could this be used as a bassinet for a newborn once napper and changing table are removed? The top section level?', 'answer': "Yes, definitely. This is the way we will use it during the day. I am a senior who will be keeping my new granddaughter during the day. The nursery in on the second floor so I will use the Pack 'N Play during the day for our newborn."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MRDU8', 'answerTime': '12 days ago', 'question': 'Does this come with a power cord to plug into an outlet? The batteries last 3 hours, which does not seem like a long time.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "There is no power cord. It is battery only. However, The batteries in mine are still going after a month. I don't use the vibrate pack all the time, but the music is useful for soothing, and I use it for almost half of the baby's naps. Not sure where you got 3 hours, but they should last longer than that. Mine have. (Energizer if that makes a difference)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406185200, 'question': "Has anyone attempted to use this in a hatchback? We're trying to figure out if it will fit in our Toyota Prius.", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It is the most compact front-to-back convertible I have used for rear-facing. It should fit in a Prius.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405494000, 'question': 'The description for "Go Green" says the colors are grass green and chocolate brown, but the pictures look more like gray/black &amp; green. Which is it?', 'answer': "The colors are definitely gray and green. I don't know why it says brown. There is no brown on it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403679600, 'question': 'Does this car seat have a removable base? Or an additional one for purchase for another vehicle?', 'answer': 'Nope, it is all one piece'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422172800, 'question': 'What is the weight/length limit to use this rear facing? My 24 mth twins are still happy facing rear and I would like to keep them that way.', 'answer': 'Up to 40lbs for weight. Harness must be at or just below child\'s shoulders. Child\'s head must be at least 1" below the red handle. This is unique because most other seats are 1" below the outer shell. It can easily get most kids to 4 rear facing, which is exactly why we got them for both kids!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424764800, 'question': 'Does anyone know the actual rear-facing height limit? All I keep finding is "head at least 1&Prime; from the top of headrest," but what is that in inches?', 'answer': 'It allows a seated height of 26 1/2" (so sitting, bottom to top of head). It does not have a stated rear facing limit in terms of overall height as it is so tall that all kids can get to 40# weight limit before hitting that height limit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 18, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421568000, 'question': 'What is the expiration date?', 'answer': 'This seat expires 7yrs after the date of manufacture which will be listed on the box & on the seat itself'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427266800, 'question': 'i noticed that Size4Me 70 was recalled by Graco, how about this one?', 'answer': 'Mines not, it has the correct buckle on it'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426748400, 'question': 'Can a 2 month old, 12 lb baby fit securely and tightly in this?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. The seat is for 4 lbs and up, there is plenty of padding and the head support is perfect for babies without neck control. It is very easy to strap them in and adjust as they get bigger. My daughter is only 16 lbs and fits perfectly, she uses the strap covers that came with the seat comfortably.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427094000, 'question': 'is it hard to loosen the harness?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No. You can use the red handle on top to pull the straps up as baby gets taller. There is a button near where the feet are that you push and then pull the straps as long as you need them. You use the same button to pull the straps tighter.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00H8MSKAU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413961200, 'question': "How easy is it to transfer this seat between vehicles? We can't really afford 2 seats right now. The baby would ride in the other car about 1/week.", 'answer': "I don't have the latch system in my car so I use the seatbelt and tether anchor. Switching it our isn't too big of a pain but the car seat is kind of heavy and my tether anchor is a little difficult to loosen. You have to remember to pull straight with the fabric or it won't budge (might just be mine though). My scale doesn't have batteries or else I would weigh it for you."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HE2KN72', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': "You say, above that it has 3 zippers, but your only customer review, so far, says that it arrived with only one. What's up with that? Is the netting fine enough to keep out the even smaller insects like No See Ums, Midges?", 'answer': 'Indeed -that is quite correct .....on the one side, there are 3 zips which meet in the middle. "What\'s up with that" is.... (if you look closely at their picture) it shows that there are similar zips ON BOTH SIDES of the tent, with only the two ends being solid-net. The tent which arrived at my house has 3 sides of solid net, and only one side which opens. I hope that\'s a little clearer?!?! (3 zips on only 1 side) I\'m not qualified to say for sure if the net is fine enough to keep out particular bugs as I\'m not sure of their dimensions; but it is the same as another fly-net I have so I assume it\'s a standard gauge?.....looks to me like it will do the job just fine, but I can\'t guarantee anything! Hope this helps xxx'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HE2KN72', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404543600, 'question': 'Do you need a bed to set this up? Can you do it directly on the floor?', 'answer': 'No bed is needed but it will fit a bed'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HE2KN72', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396076400, 'question': 'Is there a zipper that zips the bottom part of the flaps? Or is there only a zipper for the 2 flaps that runs down the middle from the top?', 'answer': "Yes! There are a total of 3 zips - it has the zipper shown in the picture which runs from the horizontal lace trim down to the bottom of that panel, a second zip from the bottom left corner to the middle and a third from the bottom right to the middle. All 3 zips come together in the centre, the bottom panel (not shown in the picture but is UNDER the brown blanket), is one solid piece of fly screen, so it's pretty-much fully enclosed when all zips are fastened properly. Worth noting here.... the picture looks as though there is a similar entryway on the opposite side too, but one that I got has zips on only one side, and the opposite side is just sheer panel of flyscreen. I'm impressed with mine and I'm ordering another - the one that arrived had a blue trim....hoping for purple next time! I hope this answered your question! x"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398322800, 'question': 'Are the sensor pads connected to each other? If so, how long is the cord between the two sensor pads?', 'answer': 'The cord between the pads are about a foot or a foot and a half apart. Great product though.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 17, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421481600, 'question': 'Can you turn off the sensor and just use this as a sound monitor once baby is older?', 'answer': "Yep, that's how we currently use it now that our child is older. We just disabled the movement option in the parental unit and unplugged the sensor pad."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416211200, 'question': "Are two pads necessary? I'm on a budget &amp; not certain if I should buy the deluxe or the regular version of this monitor.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We had one sensor pad. Had false alarms now and then, but they decreased when we turned the sensitivity up. Also, make sure you have a piece of plywood that covers the entire area beneath the mattress so if the baby is in the crib corner, the breathing can be detected.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': '28 days ago', 'question': 'Does anyone use this with a dual-sided mattress (our mattress has an infant side &amp; toddler side) &amp; do you find that sensor sill works properly?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. I have the same mattress. Buy a wood board to put underneath from home depot... Its a reallly thin piece of wood or use something similar. And get the dual bc the single one has way too many false alarms. Love it and worth the investment'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428908400, 'question': "Can this be used in a Pack N Play? The underside of the mattress is hard plastic since the bottom isn't hard. Will it still be able to sense movement?", 'answer': 'yes, I use it also in a pack and play when I am traveling and there is no problem at all, it can still detect movement. I did however had to reduce the sensibility so it would not start the alarm all the time.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428562800, 'question': "Is there any way to turn off the alarm on the nursery unit? I don't want false alarms to wake up my baby.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you turn off the alarm then it won't sound if the baby should stop breathing so defeats the purpose of having it. Our babies always slept through the alarm which only went off when they moved off the area covered by the pad. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428044400, 'question': 'What is a "Dual Sided" mattress.We have a "dual firmness" mattress is that the same?Will it work with Moonlight Slumber Little Dreamer Dual Firmness?', 'answer': "I'd be willing to bet it would. Be sure to put a wood board under the mattress that the sensors sit on to reduce false alarms. We haven't had one... And he sleeps with pillows and blankets and all the soft cushy things that he's not supposed to yet, and the sensor still accurately picks up the breathing."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423987200, 'question': 'Will the alarm go off only if neither pad is sensing movement? Will this eliminate the false alarms we get with one pad when he rolls off?', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00HE66YU8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421827200, 'question': 'Do the movement sensors work well with a thin mattress (not standard mattress)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "We used the monitor with the bassinet mattress, which is fairly thin, and didn't have any issues with function. Just keep in mind the monitor won't work if you have a mobile running or vibration setting on your crib/bassinet. The monitor picks up the movement from the mobile rather than your baby. Easy enough fix as you just don't use the mobile when you want to the sensor pad to pick up baby's movement!"}
