{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00HTYFS0W', 'answerTime': 'Oct 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413356400, 'question': 'Is this stroller washable? Because I will like to purchase one in red color.. I need to make sure about this before to buy it.. thanks', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Dear Denisse, Thank you for your question. Yes, this stroller is washable. I worked in a Dry Cleaning Plant as the Inspector for half a decade and we always told customers to wash your carriages or strollers with a bucket of soapy water- you can use any kind of clothing detergent, but we always used Liquid Woolite with a washcloth the same or lighter color of the fabric. Squeeze the washcloth out- wash with it damp. When it's clean go over it again with just warm water- also squeezed out with a damp wash cloth. I had to clean berry juice off mine and only Palmolive Dishwashing Liquid would wash it out- and it took a while. Dishwashing Liquids don't just clean food stains off dishes- they clean food stains off many fabrics! I also cleaned off really bad mud stains from the park puddles and the damp Woolite took care of the mud stains really well. The Stroller looks new again. I hope this helps you! Maren"}
