{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00I4Y7J3K', 'answerTime': 'Jul 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404716400, 'question': 'What is the max height for the child to be able to use the harness? does it turn to a belt positioning booster after a certain height/weight?', 'answer': 'Hi Leilani; We bought the Ninja for our grandson; he is 5 yrs old and 4\'6" and about 45 pounds. He is going to be a big boy. I went to WWW.ASK.COM and this is the answer I got: http://www.target.com/p/kids-embrace-teenage-mutant-ninja-turtle-booster-seat/-/A-15007387 When he outgrows it, we will use it as a booster seat. And, Leilani, the boy just loves it. Good luck. /s/ Will The Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtle Combination Toddler/ Booster Car Seat is designed with extended-use five-point harness and larger seat. This harnessed booster seat accommodate kids 22 to 65 lbs, and when using the selt belt this booster seat accommodates children 30 to 100 lbs. Featured are an easy-to-install LATCH connectors that have a quick push-button attachment/release, a new one touch recline system, and new high harness belt slots for taller children. The TMNT Combination Booster Car Seat straps also have padded covers for added child comfort and one-handed harness adjustment - just one pull for a snug and secure fit. Included is a patented 2-position crotch strap that lengthens to accommodate growing kids, built-in belt guides, and straps also have padded covers for added child comfort. Contoured seat shell with two-position recline is shaped to support child\'s spine and legs in comfort, even on long car rides, deeper seat and deeper ""wraparound"" headrest provide superior side-impact protection and seats are equipped with high-density EPS foam which absorbs energy in the event of a collision. Seat cover can be easily removed and is machine washable. Headrest adjusts to three different positions to better fit your kids as they grow. Dual cup holders fit most Sippy cups and have an open-bottom design that won\'t collect loose objects which could be hazardous. High-impact thermoplastic seat shell is engineered with ribbing and reinforcements for added extra strength and superior protection during a collision. Patent-pending high-position top tether system controls forward movement of the child\'s head during sudden stop or collision. Features: LATCH Compatiblity, Removable Seat Pad, Armrests, Buckle Closure, Shoulder belt positioning strap, Integrated Cup Holders, Adjustable Height, Adjustable Harness Includes: Cup Holder, Shoulder belt guide, Car Seat Safety and Security Features: Adjustable safety belt, 5-Point Harness, Side Impact Protection, LATCH Equipped Car Seat Care and Cleaning: Machine Wash Forward Facing: Minimum Weight: 22 Lb., Maximum Weight: 100 Lb., 29 "; Maximum Height: 57 " Booster: Minimum Weight: 22.0 Lb., Maximum Weight: 100.0 Lb., Minimum Height: 29.0 ", Maximum Height: 57.0 " Material: Polyester Dimensions: 30.0 " H x 19.0 " W x 20.0 " D Weight: 18.0 Lb. Battery no battery used Assembly Details: assembly required, no tools needed Certifications: Meets FMVSS 213'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00I6IGF4I', 'answerTime': 'May 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401174000, 'question': 'Does the Ergo 360 have a zippered pocket to store small items (cash, chapstick etc)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Bit late, but the only zippered pocket is the one that holds the hood. It's quite small and not really designed to be a full service kind of pocket. Something as small as bills or chapstick will fit. My phone does fit in its case but that basically takes up the whole pocket."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00I6IGF4I', 'answerTime': 'Dec 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417939200, 'question': 'does it really transfer most of the weight to hips?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. I am a NICU nurse and mother of 2. I am huge on the importance of ergo-dynamics and avoiding hip issues later in life. Other carriers cause babies legs to hang which puts strain on the hips. The sitting position of the ergo carrier avoids any pulling anywhere on your baby\'s body. A friend used one of the "other brands" regularly on her youngest and she now has a lot of hip problems. Do your research. It will confirm what I am talking about. It\'s a great carrier. I leave it in the car and use it on a regular basis. It\'s so easy to go from forward facing to front facing.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00I6IGF4I', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': 'How plus size friendly is this carrier?', 'answer': "I'm a size 14 and a 38i and there is a good amount of extra strap for loosing when I wear it."}
