{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00I6IGG1A', 'answerTime': 'Jun 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403506800, 'question': "I've heard some people say the velcro is quite loud... have you found this to be an issue in quiet places or that it wakes the baby??", 'answer': "It's not unusually loud for velcro--but if you object to velcro in general, it does make the usual sound of a long, wide strip. However, if you're baby sleeps soundly enough to sleep through taking the carrier off and laid down, she probably won't be awakened by velcro. It hasn't been a problem for me (mine's more likely to wake simply by being put down in a new position--but the velcro doesn't startle her at all)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00I6IGG1A', 'answerTime': 'Aug 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407308400, 'question': 'I have the bjorn one does anyone have a comparison analysis between the Bjorn one and the Ergo 360?', 'answer': 'Please see the review written by "Mapper" on June 30, 2014. It\'s a direct comparison between the Bjorn One and Ergo 360.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00I6IGG1A', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406530800, 'question': 'Can I carry my baby through airport security checks with the Ergobaby?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes! TSA actually encourages you to leave your baby on when you go through security. Ergo baby has been a traveling lifesaver. It's super easy to use and my baby is comfortable in it."}
