{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IAVJDHC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421136000, 'question': 'I cant get the white backing off....is there a trick to it??', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you mean once you put the sticky part in the wall? It's not really a trick but you'll need a wallpaper smoother. It a plastic scraper type item you use when you want to get air bubbles out of wallpaper you put up. Before you try to take off the white so the black lettering will stay scrap over the white and press hard on the part with the lettering. Not enough to tear the paper but hard enough for the black lettering to stay. Slowly peel off the white making sure the letters stay. If the letters start to come off press the white back over it and press some more then try again."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IAVJDHC', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408690800, 'question': 'Is this easy to remove?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I'm not sure if something was going on with the decals I received, but it stuck horribly to both sides of the paper and I couldn't get it up. It was like the paper had bubbles or air in it, not smooth when arrived. It did not roll out properly, some letters stuck, some warped, I couldn't get them to straighten back out. the whole thing was a mess. I tried to place the letters on manually that remained on the paper, but they were so difficult to manipulate."}
