{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IBZ8ADK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422518400, 'question': 'What additional parts are needed to get these to work with a hygeia pump?', 'answer': "Well, it depends on which flanges (breast shields) you use... if you're using the Medela or Maymom brand breast shields, the breast shields of those brands hook directly up to the Hygeia pump, but you use these conversion rings to connect the Medela or Maymom brand breast shields to Avent brand bottles. If you're using the Hygeia brand breast shields, you probably don't need these. The Hygeia brand breast shields will screw into the Avent bottles (they're a little cross threaded, but they work - I've never had a problem doing this)."}
