{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IDHXZPY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'The description says that the blanket is 100% polyester. Is the waterproof backing also polyester? Is it coated in something that has a smell?', 'answer': 'It is all polyester but the waterproof backing has no smell.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IDHXZPY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': 'When will the product come in a different pattern?', 'answer': 'It takes 2 months to get new product in and which puts us past picnic blanket season. Once these are gone, there are no more on order until next spring.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IDHXZPY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403420400, 'question': 'Does the surface get hot or too warm out in the sun? And are the grommets (for the stakes) rust-free after repeated wash?', 'answer': "The surface is a fleece material and fleece allows air to flow between the fibers so it really shouldn't store up so much heat that it feels more than warm. The grommets are a chrome metal so they should be pretty rust proof. However, almost any metal will rust if it stays wet constantly. If you are drying the blanket thoroughly after washing before you fold it you won't have a problem. If you don't dry it you'll likely have a mold problem."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IDHXZPY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403420400, 'question': 'Does this pill easily? And if someone came out of the water and sat on this inside a tent floor, will the water seep through to the tent floor?', 'answer': "The fleece is anti-pilling and the waterproof backing works both ways so the tent floor should stay dry as long as you don't get so much water on it that it goes over the edges of the blanket."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IDHXZPY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403334000, 'question': 'is it machine washable? washing instructions?', 'answer': 'Yes it is machine washable: Machine wash, normal cycle ~105F, no chlorine bleach, do not tumble dry, do not iron, do not dry clean.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IISSKIK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422950400, 'question': 'will this work with a round or elongated built in seat such as "Bemis/Mayfair 83SLOW NextStep Child/Adult Built-in Potty Seat with Slow Close"?', 'answer': 'Not sure of that particular brand of toilet but I have 2 Splashdown Trainers installed on both round and oblong or elongated seats and it works good on both.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IISSKIK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419408000, 'question': 'Do you make them without the decal? My sons already stand when urinating. I just want something that will help keep the back of the toilet seat dry.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Absolutely! Place your order and we will ship one without the decal. Merry Christmas!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IISSKIK', 'answerTime': 'May 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400742000, 'question': 'Will this fit a child size toilet?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Unfortunately it will not fit the child/pediatric size toilets. We have preschool customers that have both sizes and use the Splashdown Trainer on the standard toilet.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IISSKIK', 'answerTime': 'May 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399964400, 'question': 'Does it come off so that you can wash it and then put it back in place?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Hi Melissa. Great question. The adhesive tape needs to stay in place. It is designed to stay in place while training. Simply clean the front and if needed wipe the area around with a sponge.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IISSKIK', 'answerTime': 'Apr 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396940400, 'question': 'Would this fit on the front of the toilet? My son sits when he pees and the urine often shoots between the seat and the toilet bowl.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Kay. Our product is designed to fit in the rear of the toilet. It may fit up front (on a round bowl) and may provide a barrier between the seat and bowl but when you raise the seat it too will rise. One of the main goals is to help your son transition from the seated position to a standing position. We have worked with pediatricians as well as preschools with a focus upon teaching the boys to "stand and go". We would love for you to purchase one but do not want you to be disappointed with trying to use it up front.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400137200, 'question': 'Is this pump compatible with other bottles?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, it is! It is compatible with all standard size bottles, so the only ones it may not fit are the wide-neck ones. I use Dr. Brown's standard bottles, and they fit perfectly."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406703600, 'question': 'Does this pump take batteries?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes they do item model number;67553.Its a 9 volt battery pack it uses 8 AA batteries.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413874800, 'question': 'I am having bcbsNE insurancee will it be covered', 'answer': 'Hi, it may be covered but not on Amazon because you need to submit a claim and I doubt if that happens here on Amazon. A friend of mine used the BCBSTX insurance to get hers from the same DME company that I used and it was covered (Aeroflow healthcare)....Google it! Hope this helps...have a blessed day :-)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426316400, 'question': 'Since this starter kit is pretty vanilla, what other Medela accessories would you recommend getting? Thanks.', 'answer': "You really don't need any. I got an extra set of everything because I get busy and don't always have time to wash and sterilize the parts every night after work, and it has worked out well."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417334400, 'question': 'Can I use this directly out of the box or will I need the 9 volt Battery Pack and 8 rechargeable batteries in order to use this?', 'answer': "Yes, The pump comes with an ac adapter that can be plugged directly into a wall outlet. The cord is not incredibly long, although it reaches across the width of my queen size bed. That's all I needed. The battery pack is sold separately, and is great for pumping when you travel or for pumping in areas with no outlet available. For example, your workplace may have a room for you to pump, but the outlet may be inconveniently placed in proximity to your chair."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': 'Is this pump compatible with Medela milk storage bags ? Can milk be pumped directly to storage bags instead of bottles?', 'answer': 'Yes. Certain packages of the storage bags come with adapters to allow you to pump directly into the bag. The storage package will say on the outside whether it includes two adapters or not.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Aug 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408690800, 'question': 'How is it different from PIS Advanced backpack http://www.amazon.com/Medela-Style-Ad...', 'answer': "It just doesn't come with the backpack or the cooler bag. It's the same exact pump. If you get the backpack, it's attached in the bottom with Velcro, so you could still take it out, but if you don't feel like spending over $100 more on an ugly black vinyl backpack and cooler, this is great. Get a cute bag for it and a free cooler bag from similac."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408258800, 'question': 'Does this need to be sterilized after every use, or can it be refrigerated or kept in a cooler until you get it home to sterilize?', 'answer': "The pump and the tubes that connect with the pump don't need to be sterilized. In terms of our sterilization/cleanliness practices, we never re-used the bottle or parts that came into contact with breast milk until they were thoroughly cleaned. We never permitted the parts to dry with breast milk on them. For each of our children, we set up a system where the infants bottles were washed by hand separately from our other dishes. We rinsed breastmilk from parts when they weren't going to go through our cleaning process right away (e.g., away from the house, daily accumulation). This is as simple as rinsing with tap water or putting them in our big soaking bowl. Our washing system was to soak the bottles in 7th Generation dish soap and scalding water for about 30 mins prior to hand washing. I don't know if you're asking this, but we were never counseled to sterilize breast milk. Refrigerate. Warm prior to serving. Which we did by placing the bottles in hot water until it warmed up. All of our children survived their parent's amateurism to make it out of infanthood. I would recommend this Medela; I think its probably the least expensive version, and it worked well for us."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405839600, 'question': "I live in South America where the Power is 220, does this breastpump support our power or I'll need to buy an adapter?", 'answer': "I live in South Korea. and Korea power is 220, too. this breastpump doesn't support 220v power. So, you have to buy an adapter. medela's orginal adapter needs 9V 1A output. if you have another adapter to support this voltage and amp value, you can use that.(under is ok, over is not ok.) I found and use an adapter for old wifi AP which has 9v 0.8A output. it works well. I hope this information help you."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IJJRVR4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 23, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422000000, 'question': 'Is this pump use battery or alternating current?', 'answer': 'It plugs into the wall. You can order a rechargeable battery pack for it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IM8G038', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': 'Is this the newest model? Newer than the Light 2?', 'answer': 'I recently order this travel crib on amazon and yes it is the newest version (newer than the travel crib light 2) it has the completely mesh sides to the base and is a wonderful product. I was worried I would get the older version when I ordered it but was pleased to see it was the newest one as seen on the baby bjorn website.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IM8G038', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428044400, 'question': 'Has anyone traveled on a plane with the crib? If yes, how did it work out? Also does the mattress fold up into the carrying case as well?', 'answer': "The case is large so it will count as a suitcase. It's sturdy. It will travel well. Whole pad folds up. It pops up in under 1 min. I know it's expensive but I'm a huge fan! Used it for two vacations. My ONLY complaint is I would not use it for a little newborn. The bottom is very sturdy and safe but not that amazing hard surface a newborn needs. I'm a little bit of a nut about my sleeping spaces but I trusted it 100% for my 9 month old."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IM8G038', 'answerTime': 'Aug 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407826800, 'question': 'Amazon says the item weight is 1 pound. Is it truly that light?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No, that must be a typo! It weighs 13 pounds, which is still pretty lightweight as travel cribs go. http://www.babybjorn.com/baby-cradle-and-travel-crib/travel-crib-light/product-specifications/ We love ours -- incredibly easy to set up and take down.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IM8G038', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423641600, 'question': 'Does the mattress seem firm enough for a newborn on this model? I read that the Travel Crib Light 2 might be unsafe for newborn due to soft mattress.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It is very thin, I wouldnt cosider it unsafe, I have had no problem with it, in fact me and my wife love this crib'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IM8G038', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410505200, 'question': 'Hello, how high is this? In terms of from where the baby sleeps to the top. Thanks!', 'answer': "Think of it this way--the mat the baby sleeps on rests on the floor. It's a great travel crib. It's big, it is easy to tote around, the sleeping mat is dense and high quality, and the baby can't hurt him/herself. The mat is low but if it is going to be set up and folded up a lot, it's worth it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IM8G038', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410505200, 'question': 'Does this item come with any sort of bassinet for a newborn?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No there is not a bassinet, however from my experience our little fella out grew the separate bassinet by week 12, probably before but we persevered that long with him waking each time he kicked. Moral of the story is if recommend splurging on a crib and not being too picky with a bassinet.'}
