{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IMOT7L4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405062000, 'question': 'What brand are they? Are they high quality? How do they compare to bum genius? The price seems too good to be true, I need help..', 'answer': 'They are Happy Flutes. Personally I have a good sized stash and love bumgenius, but all of my favorite diapers are Happy Flutes! Never had a leak, a blowout, or fit issues. And they run bigger than BG so they last longer. The quality of the materials, although many hate to admit it, is just as high as BG'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IMOT7L4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419235200, 'question': 'How do you wash these diapers?', 'answer': "There are many different wash routines which can work for these diapers, and the wash routine will depend on the type of washing and drying machines you have as well as what kind of water you have (hard, normal, soft). Generally, you pull the inserts out of the diaper before washing (they will simply bunch up in the pocket), these diapers are best with a REAL detergent such as Tide, Arm and Hammer, Free and Clear (cloth diaper detergents generally do not get the job done as they have a lot of softeners and not much detergent). A prewash with a small amount of your chosen detergent is best to start, you will get most of the dirty washed away after this wash (think about it, first wash will be potty water) and you can do a full cycle next (next wash will be clean water as you have washed the potty water away). Personally, I did an extra rinse afterwards just to be sure all of the detergent washed away as it would go on baby's bum. I dried these diapers on medium heat but they also had no issues on medium heat or air dried. I would highly suggest looking up a group called Fluff Love and CD Science on facebook; these women are experts in all of the factors in washing cloth diapers such as High Efficiency machines vs old style machines, hard water, and the best detergents for baby's needs. With a little research to find your best method, these are easy to use and easy to clean. I was very pleased as the washing aspect is the most intimidating! Good luck, I say go for it!"}
