{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00IOGIM9S', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404802800, 'question': 'is this treated with flame retardants?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I had the same question and e-mailed customer service. This is their encouraging answer! Rarely can you get a reasonably priced item without flame retardants, BPA, PVC and phthalates! The board is still MDF, but maybe it can be sealed to reduce off-gassing or left out of your home for a few days. MDF is always a concern for VOC and formaldehyde emiting. Thank you for your e-mail and interest in Inglesina. 1.) The Fast chair is not treated with any flame retardants. 2.) The Fast Dinning Tray does not contain PVC, BPA, phthalates or lead. 3.) The seat support underneath is made of Medium Density Fiber Board. The other material of the Fast is the seat fabric made of polyester, foam that is polyesther and the bag that is made by nylon. Sincerely, Joseph Consumer Manager Inglesina USA, Inc. 300 Penhorn Ave, STE 2 - Secaucus, NJ 07094 Ph: (973)244-2411 ext.23 Fax: (973)244-1190'}
