{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00IRP67MK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412492400, 'question': 'I have just bought these for a 1 month old and I can\'t get them to fit. The countless snaps are very confusing, and they are too "tall". Suggestions?', 'answer': "Here's a link to a video that explains how the rise snaps work. One Size Cloth Diapers- How Should They Fit?: http://youtu.be/tSg9RS7OoF0 You have to adjust the rise. The last three rows of snaps are for adjusting the rise. For a one month old the smallest rise setting should be used. So that means the first row and third row should meet together. Also, I found these diapers to be sort of big on my one month old but now a couple of weeks later, they fit better. They're just so little when they are newborns. If you still don't like the way the diaper fits, you could get some newborn cloth diapers. I never got the newborn cloth diapers because they grow so quickly. My son wears these diapers just fine now."}
