{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00ISS2L1W', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': 'Will this seat work for a one year old? Need a seat for a visiting child.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You "can," but I wouldn\'t. It\'s actually quite dangerous to forward face a child before 2 because their heads are disproportionately large and neck muscles are quite weak. It can cause internal decapitation as well other injuries in the event of a serious crash. A convertible Cosco would be safer (in the rear-facing position) and cheaper for the visiting child. $39 at Walmart.'}
