{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00KDKKD1I', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421308800, 'question': 'Can this pillow be washed in hot water, or is it impervious to bed bugs, dander, dust mites? Thanks.', 'answer': 'Hi. We recommend that the pillow be washed in cold water, on gentle cycle, and dried on low heat. The materials of our pillow are inherently hypoallergenic - the poly cluster fiber fill contains no known allergens. The outside covering is 100% mew cotton, which also contains no known allergens. The term hypoallergenic is usually an inherent quality and is not "made" to be hypoallergenic - otherwise chemicals would likely be used in the process (which they are NOT in our pillows). Dust mites should not be able to penetrate the fabric due to two factors: 1) the tightness of the weave, and 2) the sizing that is applied at the finishing stage. Over time (after multiple washings) that should still hold true, but there becomes a little more chance for them to get in. This is why a pillow protector could be a good combination. I would imagine that dander would also fall under this description. Alternatively, if you have bed bugs, you need a professional. I hope this helps! Thank you for your question!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': "What's included in the box?", 'answer': "Hi Leanne, Thanks for your question. In response, you'll receive the child locator watch and tracking device. Both already have batteries installed and are ready-to-be used out of the box. You'll also receive clear, easy-to-follow instructions on exactly how to use the locator on the back of the retail packaging. Hope this helps.. If you have any other questions, just let me know.. Have a blessed day, Mark"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405580400, 'question': 'Will this work on my son at a place like Disney World?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Hi Leanne, Thanks for your question. In response, yes our "Kid So Safe" child locator watch will work great for you at large theme parks like Disney World, Disney Land, 6 Flags, etc. Many of our customers are also using the watch to keep track of their small children when going to large sporting events, busy beaches, and even when going to the mall... Should work great for you.. If we can help in any other way or answer any additional questions, just let me know... Thanks, and I hope you have a blessed day, Mark'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405580400, 'question': 'What are the typical uses for this type child locator watch?', 'answer': 'Hi Leanne, thanks for your question. There are alot of different applications for this watch, however we find that most of our customers purchase to use on an upcoming trip to large theme parks like Disneyworld, Disneyland, 6 Flags, etc. We also know that our parents also love our watches and use them extensively for trips to crowded beaches, busy sporting events, trips to the mall, etc One of the biggest benefits to our child locators, and why so many people choose the "Kid So Safe" model vs all others is that 1.) Our watch is Extremely simple to use "out of the box", 2.) It works great in a variety of different locations, 3.) Kids love the look of the watch itself and its never a fight to have them wear it, 4.) It doesn\'t require an expensive monthly charge for GPS tracking vs most of our competitors, and 5.) Its a great price that\'s affordable for all parents. You can\'t put a price on your child\'s safety, and this is a great way to protect them in busy places.. I encourage you to check out one of our "Kid So Safe" child locator watches yourself and let us know what you think... I know that you\'re going to love it, just like all of our other customers.. Have a blessed day, Mark'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404975600, 'question': 'Can you set the alarm so it will start beeping after 50 feet away', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Hi Raymond, Thanks for your question. In response, its a fixed distance that's already set in the unit - typically 20-30 feet, and is not able to be modified for a specific distance. Hope this helps! Mark"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403161200, 'question': 'To what distance does this tracking device work?', 'answer': "Hi Caresse, thanks for your question. In response, we've found that the unit works best within a range of 25-30 feet from the receiver unit. The unit is very easy to use and emits loud beeping noise when your child gets outside of that range. If any other questions, just let me know. Have a blessed day, Mark"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Jun 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403334000, 'question': "Does the child trAcker watch have any safety measures so the child can't remove it?", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Hi Annette, Thanks for your question. In response, its a watch with a velcro fastening so its intended to be easy for the parent to put on and take off. We find that kids of the age this tracker is intended for, tend to enjoy having a "special" watch of their own, so they don\'t mess with it too much... If you\'d like to make it a little more difficult for them to take off, you can always just swap out the band for one thats more difficult for small fingers to open. Hope this helps, Mark'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Jul 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405926000, 'question': 'Does this watch have GPS?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Leanne, Thanks for your question. In response, the "Kid So Safe" child locator watch does NOT use GPS, which typically carries with it an additional monthly service charge. When we initially developed this locator watch, our customers told us #1 - they wanted something VERY simple to use, and #2 - they did NOT want GPS because they didn\'t want to pay that ongoing monthly fee charged by gps providers. As such, thats what we developed. A simple, easy-to-use child locator watch that your kids will love, and will give you peace of mind, with no annoying monthly GPS fees :) Hope this helps.. If you have any other questions, just let me know.. Have a blessed day, Mark'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403161200, 'question': 'Is it waterproof?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi Caresse, thanks for your question. In response, no the unit is not waterproof but we've seen it work fine in normal rainfall, etc. If any other questions, just let me know. Have a blessed day, Mark"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Aug 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407394800, 'question': "Does the child's bear make an alarm sound, or is it just the parent's receiver that sounds off an alarm?", 'answer': "Thanks for your question. In response, the parent's receiver sounds the alarm. The child's watch is a transmitter only. Hope this helps. If you have any other questions, just let us know.. Have a blessed day, Mark"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00KTK1S8Y', 'answerTime': 'Aug 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407394800, 'question': 'Is it waterproof?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Caresse, Thanks for your question. In response, the locator watch is not waterproof, but will do fine in a light rain, etc. Hope this helps. If I can be of any additional help, just let me know.. Have a blessed day, Mark'}
